        "Would Atsuki come with her?\nIf they abandoned their world together, maybe it would be bearable.\nBut she soon learned that he wouldn't.\n{color=#000}And that, though it had seemed impossible, there had always been a path toward a desirable outcome.{/color}": 'Atsuki 会和她一起走吗？\n倘若两人一同舍弃自己的世界，或许还能承受。\n但她很快便知道，他不会。\n{color=#000}而她也明白了，尽管看似毫无可能，通往理想结局的路其实一直都在。{/color}',
        "Would Atsuki come with her?\nIf they abandoned their world together, maybe it would be bearable.\nBut she soon learned that he wouldn't.\nAnd that, though it had seemed impossible, there had always been a path toward a desirable outcome.": 'Atsuki 会和她一起走吗？\n倘若两人一同舍弃自己的世界，或许还能承受。\n但她很快便知道，他不会。\n而她也明白了，尽管看似毫无可能，通往理想结局的路其实一直都在。',
        'Despite that, at almost 9:00, we were inside Ashiya Tower.': '尽管如此，快到 {time=9} 的时候，我们还是走进了芦屋塔。',
        'Despite that, at almost 9 a.m., we were inside Ashiya Tower.': '尽管如此，快到 {time=9} 的时候，我们还是走进了芦屋塔。',
        "...The reason why we were inside wasn't one I could easily put into words.": '……{w}我们为什么会在里面，我很难说清楚。',
        "We remained by the door that would open at {time=9}, simply waiting for that to happen. At our left was another door that would open at the same time, and according to what we'd been told, both led to the main floor of the tower. On that particular day, not many people seemed to care about that, as everyone who could be seen was in our same line.": '我们等在 {time=9} 会打开的那扇门前，只等它开。左边还有一扇门也会同时打开，据说两扇门都通向塔的主楼层。{w} 不过那天好像没多少人在意这一点——能看见的人全排在我们这条队里。',
        "We remained by the door that would open at 9:00, simply waiting for that to happen. At our left was another door that would open at the same time, and according to what we'd been told, both led to the main floor of the tower.{w} On that particular day, not many people seemed to care about that, as everyone who could be seen was in our same line.": '我们等在 {time=9} 会打开的那扇门前，只等它开。左边还有一扇门也会同时打开，据说两扇门都通向塔的主楼层。{w} 不过那天好像没多少人在意这一点——能看见的人全排在我们这条队里。',
        "We remained by the door that would open at 9:00, simply waiting for that to happen. At our left was another door that would open at the same time, and according to what we'd been told, both led to the main floor of the tower. On that particular day, not many people seemed to care about that, as everyone who could be seen was in our same line.": '我们等在 {time=9} 会打开的那扇门前，只等它开。左边还有一扇门也会同时打开，据说两扇门都通向塔的主楼层。{w} 不过那天好像没多少人在意这一点——能看见的人全排在我们这条队里。',
        "We remained by the door that would open at 9 a.m., simply waiting for that to happen. At our left was another door that would open at the same time, and according to what we'd been told, both led to the main floor of the tower.{w} On that particular day, not many people seemed to care about that, as everyone who could be seen was in our same line.": '我们等在 {time=9} 会打开的那扇门前，只等它开。左边还有一扇门也会同时打开，据说两扇门都通向塔的主楼层。{w} 不过那天好像没多少人在意这一点——能看见的人全排在我们这条队里。',
        "We remained by the door that would open at 9 a.m., simply waiting for that to happen. At our left was another door that would open at the same time, and according to what we'd been told, both led to the main floor of the tower. On that particular day, not many people seemed to care about that, as everyone who could be seen was in our same line.": '我们等在 {time=9} 会打开的那扇门前，只等它开。左边还有一扇门也会同时打开，据说两扇门都通向塔的主楼层。{w} 不过那天好像没多少人在意这一点——能看见的人全排在我们这条队里。',
        "Sorry for the wait, everyone. We'll now begin the group entrances. My name is Naomi. I'll be chaperoning today's guided visit.": '各位，久等了。现在开始分组入场。{w}我是 Naomi，今天的参观由我带队。',
        'As you likely already know, groups of three will move forward in turns. Each viewing is estimated to take approximately fifteen minutes. Once inside, I will personally explain what we have prepared, and I will also be available to answer questions within the specified time.': '各位大概已经知道，三人一组，依次进场。每次参观预计十五分钟左右。{w}进去之后，我会亲自为大家讲解我们准备的展品，也会在规定时间内回答大家的问题。',
        "...No, of course not. I'm seriously glad we're here. I mean it.": '……不，当然不后悔。{w}能来这里，我真的很高兴。我是认真的。',
        "It's all right. Thank you. Let's continue, though. I was the one who wanted to do this.": '没事的。谢谢你。{w}不过，我们继续走吧。当初想这么做的人是我。',
        '...Akaro. Akaro Esata.': '……{w}Akaro。{w}Akaro Esata。',
        'Naomi moved aside and placed herself before the velvet curtain. Then, she took out a keyring from her pocket as she got ready to begin the introduction.': 'Naomi 走到一旁，站到天鹅绒遮布前。{w}接着，她从口袋里掏出一串钥匙，准备开始讲解。',
        "Maybe. Liste—*cough* Listen. We'll find out what happened. Just stay there for a minute, okay? Do you feel okay?": '也许吧。听我——*咳*{w}听我说。我们会弄清楚发生了什么。你先在那儿待一会儿，好吗？你感觉还好吗？',
        "I looked around me. It was a bizarre sight, and the disgusting smell was still present after the smoke had faded. The room had been painted black. The curtain's beautiful red, the walls, the ceiling... They'd all been corrupted by an ugly, dark color, almost purple.": '我环顾四周。眼前的景象诡异至极，烟雾散去后，那股恶臭依然残留。{w}整个房间都被染成了黑色。遮布原本漂亮的红色，还有墙壁、天花板……全被一种难看的深色侵蚀，近乎发紫。',
        "Oh... What the hell happened here? It's dark in this room, but the hallway is too. The walls and ceiling are black, and I can't see anyone. The whole hallway's covered. How much smoke was there?": '噢……这里到底出了什么事？{w}房间里很暗，走廊也一样。墙壁和天花板都黑了，一个人也看不见。整条走廊都被熏遍了。这得有多少烟啊？',
        'I had no idea. Still a bit disoriented, I forced my neck to turn. The only thing in the room was the covered cabinet. However, I doubted the Sekimeiya would still be there. The easiest conclusion to reach was that the smoke had been part of an attack designed to steal it.': '我也答不上来。{w}我还有些恍惚，硬是扭过头去。房间里只有那个盖着遮布的展示柜。可我不觉得 Sekimeiya 还会在里面。最容易想到的结论是：那阵烟雾是袭击的一部分，目的就是偷走它。',
        'My headache was nearly gone, thankfully. That meant that I could start thinking things through. What had happened? Why had it happened? How was I going to find the person responsible?': '所幸头痛几乎已经消失，这意味着我可以开始把事情理清楚了。{w}发生了什么？为什么会发生？我又要怎么找出该为此负责的人？',
        "The room was empty, and it had been empty before we'd fallen unconscious. Only the cabinet had been with us, but if the smoke had come out of it, it wouldn't have surrounded us so fast. We had been stained, but not as much on the lower parts of our bodies. The ceiling was significantly darkened, the floor not so much. The smoke's density was low.": '房间里空无一物，我们昏迷之前也是这样。我们身边只有那个展示柜；可如果烟是从柜子里冒出来的，不可能这么快就把我们团团围住。{w}我们身上都沾上了烟渍，但下半身要少得多。天花板明显变黑了，地板却没有那么严重。说明烟的密度并不高。',
        'Although those points were very strange, I was still relieved that none of us had been harmed. I lay on the floor for a bit, attempting to gather more strength. When thoughts came to me, it was calming to realize that they were different from what had recently filled my head.': '这些疑点虽然十分蹊跷，但至少我们谁都没有受伤，这让我松了口气。我在原地躺了一会儿，想多攒些力气。{w}等思绪重新浮起来，我竟觉得安心——它们与近来盘踞在我脑中的东西截然不同。',
        "Once we're all out of it, he obtains the Sekimeiya. I should also consider that the smoke first arose shortly after Naomi unlocked the cabinet. This doesn't mean much, given that she could have had her key taken after she was unconscious, but if whoever did this didn't know much about the cabinet's mechanism, it makes sense they waited until it was unlocked.": '等我们都失去意识后，他就能把 Sekimeiya 弄到手。{w}另外也要考虑到，烟雾是在 Naomi 打开柜子后不久才出现的。这点本身意义不大，因为钥匙也可能是在她昏迷后才被取走的；但如果对方并不清楚展示柜的机关，那等柜子打开再动手就合理多了。',
        '...I was doing it again, almost like a coping mechanism. I had to make sure Shiroya was really okay before anything else.': '……{w}我又开始这样了，几乎像是一种自我安抚。无论如何，我得先确认 Shiroya 真的没事。',
        "...I'm afraid I don't. You were in the event room, right? Shouldn't another woman be with you?": '……这我恐怕不清楚。{w}你们当时在活动室吧？不是还有一位女士和你们在一起吗？',
        "S-So, you're right, Naomi still has to be here. And is that everyone? I get that most people were in the lobby, but if someone else entered the hallways, they couldn't have evacuated either.": '那、那么，你说得对，Naomi 肯定还在这里。{w} 在这里的人就这些了吗？大部分人当时在大厅，这我明白，可要是有人进了走廊，也一样没法撤离吧。',
        "Of course, it didn't budge at all. Shrugging a little, Sai turned back.": '当然，它纹丝不动。{w}Sai 微微耸了耸肩，转过身来。',
        '...There was something else piquing my curiosity.': '……{w}还有一件事勾起了我的好奇。',
        "Yeah. If the goal was to bring the Sekimeiya out during all the confusion, it doesn't make sense that they didn't do it here. I don't know what released the smoke. I didn't see anything in the hallways, but this is a much bigger room. It could be that whatever method they used simply wouldn't have worked here.": '是啊。如果目的是趁混乱把 Sekimeiya 带出去，那没在大厅动手就说不通。{w}我不知道烟是怎么放出来的。走廊里我没看到任何装置，而这里空间大得多。也许他们用的手段在这里根本行不通。',
        "Could it be that leaving with the Sekimeiya wasn't the goal of the plan? Or maybe that they intend to do it later? ...Is it realistic to think anyone could cause panic with the smoke, leave with this incredibly rare item, and not be caught immediately? Even if the cameras were blocked, once outside, you're still one of the last people to exit and would be searched.": '会不会带着 Sekimeiya 离开并不是计划的目的？又或者他们打算之后再动手？{w}……放烟制造混乱、带走这件稀世珍品，还能不被立刻抓住——这种事真有可能吗？就算摄像头被遮住了，到了外面，你终究是最后离场的那批人之一，照样要被搜查。',
        "There is something that comes to mind, and it's why I only asked about this floor's escape routes. The lobby was never used to escape. Now, Katei says the windows on the upper floors are sealed, but when they're open, they provide a feasible way out.": '我想到了一种可能，这也是我只问这一层逃生路线的原因。{w}大厅从来就不是逃生出口。Katei 说楼上的窗户都封死了，可只要打开，它们就是一条可行的出路。',
        "...Hm, this? It's a pendant.": '……嗯？这个？{w}是条吊坠。',
        "I know I said I hoped for this to be the case, but I'm not too sure anymore. This probably means that the culprit's plan wasn't really all that elaborate. They might just plan to spend twelve hours with us and take this thing out of here when it's time to leave.": '我确实说过希望事情如此，可现在也没那么确定了。这大概说明犯人的计划没那么周密。{w} 也许对方只打算陪我们耗上十二个小时，等该离开时再把东西带走。',
        "I'm not so sure. Hey, Katei, do you know if Naomi was aware of the existence of that alarm?": '我可没那么确定。{w} 喂，Katei，你知道 Naomi 是否知道有那道警报吗？',
        "Naomi's job was to explain everything about the Sekimeiya and make sure the exhibition happened smoothly. An alarm that's triggered when the Sekimeiya is removed is something she would know about, so thinking that she was unaware of it is pretty ridiculous. And, while her position is convenient to orchestrate this, it also makes her a very strong suspect from the get-go.": 'Naomi 的职责就是讲解 Sekimeiya 的一切，并确保展览顺利进行。Sekimeiya 被取走时会触发警报，这种事她不可能不知道；所以认为她对此毫不知情，实在很离谱。{w} 再说，她的职位虽然方便她策划这一切，却也让她从一开始就显得非常可疑。',
        "I can't be sure of this, but before the time I heard the alarm, I did hear the sound of a body falling, and given all three of us were already down on the floor, it must've been Naomi's. On top of that, the cabinet hadn't been opened, so if she opened it while I was on the floor and triggered the alarm, I think I would've heard it. Not to mention how risky this is. Surely she would've waited until all of us were definitely unconscious to get the Sekimeiya out.": '这一点我不能确定，但在我听见警报之前，确实听到了有人倒地的声响；既然我们三个当时都已经倒在地上，那多半是 Naomi。更何况，展示柜并没有被打开过。如果她是在我倒地后打开柜子、触发了警报，我想我应该会听见。{w} 更别说这有多冒险了。她肯定会等到我们全都彻底失去意识，才把 Sekimeiya 取出去。',
        'Oh... I think I see what you mean.': '哦……{w} 我好像明白你的意思了。',
        "There wasn't any other opposition. If Naomi intended to show herself to us, she would come back eventually. We worked under the assumption that she still had the cabinet key. However, if she'd ever fallen unconscious, someone could've easily grabbed it, maybe failing to recognize that the cabinet was already unlocked. If she'd woken up as that happened, the culprit might've panicked and been responsible for her disappearance.": '没人再提出反对。如果 Naomi 有意现身，迟早会回来的。{w}我们暂且认定钥匙还在她手上。不过，若她曾经失去意识，别人很容易就能把钥匙拿走，而且对方也许没发现展示柜已经解锁了。如果她恰在那时醒来，下手的人说不定会惊慌失措，那她的失踪可能就是这么造成的。',
        "Katei grabbed the doorknob, and upon turning it, he tried to push the door forward. However, it didn't budge.": '{w=0.6}Katei 握住门把，拧了一下，向前推门。门却纹丝不动。',
        "Hm... So, if one of the goals of the smoke was to disable the security cameras, they didn't use hallway C for anything.": '嗯……{w}这么说，如果放烟雾的目的之一是要让监控失效，那他们根本没打算利用 C 走廊做什么。',
        "Oh, yes. It's 9:41.": '哦，对。现在是 {time=9:41.}',
        "Oh, yes. It's 9:41 a.m.": '哦，对。现在是 {time=9:41.}',
        'As Katei said, next to the numbers that displayed the date, the current time showed 9:41. That meant the exit would unlock at approximately 21:05, in eleven hours and twenty minutes.': '正如Katei所说，日期旁边显示的当前时间正是 {time=9:41.}。也就是说，出口大约会在 {time=21:05} 解锁，距此还有十一小时二十分钟。',
        'As Katei said, next to the numbers that displayed the date, the current time showed 9:41 a.m. That meant the exit would unlock at approximately 9:05 p.m., in eleven hours and twenty minutes.': '正如Katei所说，日期旁边显示的当前时间正是 {time=9:41.}。也就是说，出口大约会在 {time=21:05} 解锁，距此还有十一小时二十分钟。',
        'They actually should be able to. ...Hello? Can anyone hear us?': '按理说应该听得见。{w}……喂？有人能听见吗？',
        "We know what occurred, yes. The Ashiya family was in contact with us, and we were informed of this communication method. Since a member of the security staff was assumed to still be in the tower, we kept this device with us expecting it to be activated at any moment. I'm a police officer. My name is Suripo.": '是的，我们清楚发生了什么。芦屋家的人联系过我们，也告知了这种联络方式。考虑到可能还有安保人员留在塔内，我们一直带着这台设备，等着它随时接通。{w}我是警察，名叫 Suripo。',
        "He was able to change all the cameras being displayed at once, making the process simple and brief. As he'd said, the only thing to be seen through a handful of them was a black screen created by the smoke. Even after the substance had solidified, there was no chance we could see well through it.": '他一下就能把显示中的摄像头全部切换掉，整个过程既简单又迅速。{w}就像他说的，有几台的画面只有一片漆黑，是被烟雾挡住的。就算烟已经凝固，隔着它也根本看不清什么。',
        'This must look odd to you all, correct? Do you know the story behind this place? This was the Ashiya family\'s residence until a decade ago. Then, its purpose changed, and work floors began to be added. This is why it\'s called a tower. The townspeople saw that floors kept being constructed, and they started to call it a tower sarcastically, as if it would never stop increasing in height. I don\'t know if Ashiya liked the name or if they officialized it to counter its negative connotations. You might\'ve also heard it called the "Ashiya skyscraper".': '你们一定觉得奇怪吧？知道这地方的来历吗？十年前，这里还是芦屋家的宅邸。后来用途变了，才开始一层层加盖办公楼层。{w}塔这个名字就是这么来的。镇上的人看着楼一直往上盖，就带着几分讥讽叫它塔，好像它会永远长下去似的。我不知道是芦屋家喜欢这个名字，还是为了压住这种贬义才正式定下这个名字。你们或许也听过「芦屋摩天楼」这种叫法。',
        'Of course, the cameras were installed after the place stopped being their residence, and they were only placed in some of the rooms before continuing was deemed unnecessary. The initial reason was to make sure it was preserved well, given that it was of great importance to the Ashiya family. They were installed with the thought of someone breaking in and expecting to find unguarded, hidden information. However, the installation process was never completed.': '当然，摄像头是在他们搬走之后才装的，只装了一部分房间，后来觉得没必要再装下去。{w}最初是为了好好保护这里，因为这里对芦屋家很重要。装摄像头，是怕有人闯进来，想找些没人看管的秘密。不过装到一半就停了。',
        "...Had such a battle actually been happening in the town I'd always lived in? I'd purposely avoided anything to do with that aspect of Yushibana, but I hadn't heard of Xyn even once. I could vaguely recall hearing about Ashiya Tower being robbed, but I'd never imagined the situation was so large scale. No one I frequently talked to had an interest in the topic, so if it was common knowledge, I'd never been told. Ashiya had always felt like a taboo, and I'd never personally researched them.": '……{w}这样的争斗，真的一直发生在我生活了这么多年的镇子上吗？关于丰花的这一面，我一向刻意回避，可即便如此，Xyn 这个名字我竟一次也没听过。芦屋塔遭劫的事，我隐约有些印象，却从没想过规模如此之大。{w}常和我来往的人里没人关心这类话题，所以就算这早已人尽皆知，也从来没人跟我提起。芦屋对我而言一直像个禁忌，我也从未主动去了解过他们。',
        "...Yes. It's possible that Xyn aren't actually involved, given the stolen gems were found. Nonetheless, the method used to get them out is still unknown. They were in one of the deepest rooms of the floor you're on.": '……是的。{w}宝石既然已经找回来了，那 Xyn 也可能根本没参与。但宝石是怎么被运出去的，我们还是不清楚。它们原本放在你们这层最深处的一间房里。',
        "What closed the exit was the alarm, which had never gone off in the past. While Ashiya are denying it, malfunctions are a possibility. The alarm was supposed to only go off whenever the Sekimeiya cabinet was forced open. If stealing the gems we found was what triggered it, it doesn't make sense that they were brought outside. And on top of that, you're telling me the Sekimeiya and the cabinet are completely fine...": '封死出口的是警报，而这种警报过去从未响过。芦屋家否认存在故障，但也不能排除这种可能。{w}按设计，只有 Sekimeiya 的展示柜被强行打开时，警报才会响。如果真是因为偷走那些宝石才触发的警报，那宝石被带到外面就说不通了。更何况，你们还说 Sekimeiya 和展示柜都完好无损……',
        "The Sekimeiya exhibition... was no more than bait they put out to lure in Xyn. That, and the alarm they secretly designed, were the main two factors of their plan. The tower is equipped with cameras and security. However, Ashiya hoped Xyn wouldn't anticipate such an abrupt jump in their measures.": 'Sekimeiya 的展览……不过是他们放出的诱饵，用来引 Xyn 上钩。这场展览，加上他们暗中设计的警报，就是整个计划的两大支柱。{w}塔内装有监控和安保人员。不过芦屋希望 Xyn 料不到他们的措施会突然升级。',
        "After the alarm, the Xyn members that got trapped inside would have no way to leave. You might've noticed the security room's door is sturdier than the others. The last function of the alarm was to lock it. Like the cabinet's lock, once the security room's door is locked, it can only be opened with the actual key, which is possessed by the security staff. Every staff member worked to put this mechanism and plan into effect, and they knew very well what they had to do. Today, only Katei Kuiji was present.": '警报启动之后，被困在里面的 Xyn 成员就再也出不去了。各位或许已经注意到，监控室的门比别处结实得多。警报的最后一项功能，就是把这扇门锁上。{w}和展示柜的锁一样，监控室的门一旦锁死，就只能用真正的钥匙打开，而钥匙在保安人员手里。所有员工都参与落实了这套装置和方案，也很清楚自己该做什么。可今天在场的，只有 Katei Kuiji 一人。',
        "No. They can't. They don't know why, but they are unable to even access the command that would let them give their approval to open the exit.": '对。他们做不到。{w}原因不明，但他们连那条批准开启出口的指令都调不出来。',
        "No. ...The attack was assumed to come during the night, but it happened this morning instead. I don't know a lot of details about this, but evidently Ashiya were going to trap at least one Xyn member inside and try to squeeze them for information over the security room microphone.": '没有。{w}……原本预计袭击会发生在夜里，结果却是在今天早上。细节我了解得不多，但看来芦屋是打算至少困住一名 Xyn 成员，再通过监控室的麦克风从他嘴里撬出情报。',
        'Since today was the last possible day, we were all anticipating Xyn to come during the night. Long before 9:00, I myself was in the tower, aware that the chances of a theft were incredibly likely. I was in contact with Ashiya staff about what the procedure would be if something were to happen.': '今天是他们能下手的最后一天，所以我们都预料 Xyn 会在夜里来。早在 {time=9} 之前我就已经在塔里了——我很清楚盗窃的可能性极高，也一直在跟芦屋的员工联系，商量万一出事该如何应对。',
        'Since today was the last possible day, we were all anticipating Xyn to come during the night. Long before 9 a.m., I myself was in the tower, aware that the chances of a theft were incredibly likely. I was in contact with Ashiya staff about what the procedure would be if something were to happen.': '今天是他们能下手的最后一天，所以我们都预料 Xyn 会在夜里来。早在 {time=9} 之前我就已经在塔里了——我很清楚盗窃的可能性极高，也一直在跟芦屋的员工联系，商量万一出事该如何应对。',
        "Was that really everything, though? Was it all just a malfunction? Was Xyn actually involved? I knew many things didn't quite add up. What the hell had happened to Naomi, on top of it all?": '可真的就只有这些吗？一切都只是故障？Xyn 真的牵涉其中吗？我知道有很多地方对不上。{w}更何况，Naomi 身上到底出了什么事？',
        'Wh-What...? What do you mean?': '什、什么……？{w}你这话是什么意思？',
        'From the beginning, when he found us. When he claimed to have searched the entire floor without finding your group. About monitoring the cameras and trying to open the exit.': '从最开始他找到我们那时。他说自己把整层都搜遍了，却没发现你们几个。{w}还有他查看监控、试图打开出口的那些话。',
        "Hm... Then I'll put it bluntly.": '嗯……{w}那我就挑明说吧。',
        '...How can you be sure...?': '……{w}你怎么能确定……？',
        'He ignored me and kept walking forward. Instead of repeating myself, I felt like being the one to ask something.': '他没理我，继续往前走。{w}我没再重复，反倒想由我来问他点什么。',
        "I couldn't quite grasp Sai's behavior, but he was also trying to piece things together and might've agreed that more than met the eye was going on. He didn't seem unintelligent, and since his approach appeared different from mine, his input was potentially useful.": '我实在摸不透 Sai 的举动，不过他也在拼凑真相，或许同样觉得事情并不简单。{w}他看上去并不笨，而且思路与我不一样，听听他的看法也许有用。',
        "Don't worry, I wouldn't do that. Let's see. In case it's not here, should we tell them?": '放心，我不会那么做的。{w}这样吧。万一东西不在这儿，我们要告诉他们吗？',
        "Of course it is. After all, if it weren't, it could only have been Naomi, and that'd be too simple.": '当然在。{w}毕竟要是不在，那就只可能是 Naomi 拿的——那也未免太简单了。',
        "...Are you sure you wouldn't want to consider the other five conspiring together and taking it while we were in the mechanical room? Then they could point the finger at us.": '……{w}你真不考虑一下吗？剩下五个人串通好，趁我们在机械室的时候把它拿走，之后再把矛头指向我们。',
        "B-But, how could this have happened? I don't understand it. The timing was too coincidental. Did Ashiya remotely power off the computer to revoke my access? All I could do with it was talk to them. Maybe the problem with the security system is a side effect of whatever happened... I will stay here for a bit, while you go. I have a couple more things to do.": '可、可这怎么会发生？我实在不明白。{w}时机也太巧了。难道是芦屋远程关掉了电脑，收回了我的权限？我只能靠它和他们通话。{w}也许安保系统的问题是那件事引起的副作用……{w}你们先走吧，我在这里待一会儿。我还有几件事要处理。',
        "I leaned against a wall, next to Shiroya. I didn't think she wanted to talk, so I kept quiet. The handrail made the position uncomfortable, but I tried not to mind it. Instead, I focused on thinking...": '我靠着墙，站在 Shiroya 旁边。我觉得她不想说话，便保持沉默。{w}扶手让这个姿势很不舒服，但我尽量不去在意，转而专心思考起来……',
        '"Shortly after that, the alarm went off, so I knew I was already trapped. During that time until I exited, I kept my eyes on the cameras. I also tried to use the computer to look up information about what had happened, but the alarm even shut down my internet connection." He\'d also said that he tried to input the command to unlock the exit.': '「紧接着警报就响了，我知道自己已经被困住。从那时到离开，我一直盯着监控画面。我也试过用电脑查发生了什么，可警报连网络都切断了。」{w}他还说过，自己试过输入解锁出口的指令。',
        "We know the alarm went off at approximately 9:05. Thanks to the time the computer displayed and that it was in sleep mode when we entered the room, if the settings perhaps showed that an hour of inactivity had been needed to enter that state, Sai could've confirmed that Katei had not been there at all.": '我们知道警报大约是在 {time=9:05.} 响起的。靠电脑上显示的时间，再加上我们进屋时它正处于睡眠模式，只要设置里显示电脑闲置一小时后才会进入睡眠模式，Sai 就能确认 Katei 根本不曾待在那里。',
        "We know the alarm went off at approximately 9:05 a.m. Thanks to the time the computer displayed and that it was in sleep mode when we entered the room, if the settings perhaps showed that an hour of inactivity had been needed to enter that state, Sai could've confirmed that Katei had not been there at all.": '我们知道警报大约是在 {time=9:05.} 响起的。靠电脑上显示的时间，再加上我们进屋时它正处于睡眠模式，只要设置里显示电脑闲置一小时后才会进入睡眠模式，Sai 就能确认 Katei 根本不曾待在那里。',
        'One thing is for sure: Sai has confirmed his theory and is now certain Katei has fed us lie after lie. And I should probably think the same.': '有一点是确定的：Sai 已经验证了自己的推论，如今确信 Katei 对我们满口谎言。{w}而我大概也该这么想。',
        "He claimed to have heard the alarm, then seen the smoke. However, just after that, he said the smoke disabled the cameras instantly. Given the alarm went off some seconds after the smoke was released, he could only have seen smoke after hearing the alarm if he had been outside the security room. It's a bit strange that he said that but was still correct in saying that the smoke disabled the cameras.": '他声称先听到警报，然后才看到烟雾。可就在这之后，他又说烟雾瞬间就让监控失效了。既然烟雾释放后过了几秒警报才响，那么他若真是在听到警报之后才看到烟雾，就只能说明他当时人在监控室外。{w}奇怪的是，他这么说，可关于烟雾让监控失效的说法又完全没错。',
        "The problem was, once again, that he didn't have any traces of smoke on him. Even if he'd changed clothes, his face and hair would've been noticeably stained. Technically, there was a way to get around that. I knew hallway B had been hit by the smoke by the point I'd noticed the lack of light under the door. However, I couldn't be sure the same thing could be said of hallway A, the third and last section that had been inundated. We'd only seen it filled with smoke after waking up.": '问题依旧在于，他身上没有任何烟雾的痕迹。就算换了衣服，脸和头发也会明显沾上。{w}严格说来，倒有一种能绕过去的可能。我注意到门缝下透不进光时，B走廊已经灌满了烟雾。可 A走廊是否同样如此，我无法确定——那是第三处、也是最后一处被烟雾淹没的区域，我们醒来之后才看到它烟雾弥漫。',
        "Considering that when we talked to Suripo, at no point was the actual time mentioned... if it wasn't actually 9:41 when we checked the time, it could all hold up.": '回想我们和 Suripo 说话时，从头到尾都没提过真实时间……如果我们查看时间的那一刻，实际并非 {time=9:41}，那么一切就都还站得住脚。',
        "Considering that when we talked to Suripo, at no point was the actual time mentioned... if it wasn't actually 9:41 a.m. when we checked the time, it could all hold up.": '回想我们和 Suripo 说话时，从头到尾都没提过真实时间……如果我们查看时间的那一刻，实际并非 {time=9:41}，那么一切就都还站得住脚。',
        "If the computer was an hour behind and the real time was 10:45, we would've been unconscious for longer than we thought, and everything could fit. Katei could have been in the security room, and enough time for the suspended state to be reached could've passed.": '如果电脑慢了一小时，真实时间是 {time=10:45}，那我们昏迷的时间就比以为的更久，所有事情也就都能对上了。Katei 完全可能待在监控室里，而且已经过了足够长的时间，让电脑进入休眠状态。',
        "If the computer was an hour behind and the real time was 10:45 a.m., we would've been unconscious for longer than we thought, and everything could fit. Katei could have been in the security room, and enough time for the suspended state to be reached could've passed.": '如果电脑慢了一小时，真实时间是 {time=10:45}，那我们昏迷的时间就比以为的更久，所有事情也就都能对上了。Katei 完全可能待在监控室里，而且已经过了足够长的时间，让电脑进入休眠状态。',
        "...Since I couldn't arrive at a conclusion, I lowered my head after being lost in thought for a while.": '……{w}想了半天也得不出结论，我最终还是低下了头。',
        "Important why? What is the higher temperature gonna do? It looks perfectly fine to me. Don't tell me: it's a real egg, right? It must be kept cold so it doesn't hatch.": '有什么重要的？温度高一点又能怎样？它看起来明明好得很。{w}别告诉我：它其实是个蛋吧？得一直冷藏，免得孵出来。',
        "Every night until today, we've been expecting Xyn's attack. Everyone was led to think Ashiya had their rarest find in a while, so as Suripo said earlier, regardless of its actual initial worth, after all the publicity, the Sekimeiya was incredibly valuable for Xyn.": '直到今天为止，每一晚我们都在提防 Xyn 来袭。{w}所有人都被引导相信，芦屋家得到了近年最稀有的发现；所以正如 Suripo 之前所说，不管 Sekimeiya 最初的实际价值如何，经过这一番宣传，它对 Xyn 而言已价值连城。',
        "A vast mountain range surrounds Yushibana, which I'm sure you see daily. On Airun, a mountain close to this building, there is a little upward path that was much more visible a few years ago. That part of the range has almost been abandoned. Over time, many fewer gemstones have been found on Airun than the others.": '丰花四周环绕着广阔的山脉，你们每天应该都看得见。离这栋楼不远的艾伦山上，有一条向上延伸的小路，几年前比现在显眼得多。{w} 那一片山区几乎已经没人去了。久而久之，在艾伦山发现的宝石也比别的山少得多。',
        'Katei pointed at the cabinet. That was all interesting and consistent with what we knew, but my mind had gone someplace else.': 'Katei 指了指展示柜。{w} 这些话都很有意思，也和我们已知的对得上，可我的思绪已经飘到了别处。',
        "It seemed pointless to think much of it; we hadn't been there for more than a decade, but back in the day, it was the perfect hidden place for us to go spend our time. Not once had we seen anyone else there, but eventually, going to the mountains just to play was seen as rude by the people who tried to make a daily living on them.": '再多想也没什么用；我们已经十多年没去过那里了，可当年，那正是我们消磨时光的绝佳藏身处。{w} 我们在那儿从没见过别人，但后来，那些靠山谋生的人渐渐觉得，只为了玩就上山是一件失礼的事。',
        "We made our way to hallway A. Finally starting to inspect the huge building was an imposing task. A lot of time had already passed, so I had no idea what to think of Naomi's disappearance. She was either incapable of reaching us... or didn't want to.": '我们来到 A走廊。终于要开始搜查这栋庞大的建筑了，这项任务可不轻松。{w} 已经过去了这么长时间，我对 Naomi 的失踪实在不知该作何感想。她要么是无法联系我们……要么是不想。',
        "While at 9:00, the floor opens to the public, it isn't until 9:10 that the showcase cabinets are uncovered. This is purely done for dramatic effect and, honestly, to give the visitors the impression that they're about to witness something very valuable.": '{time=9:00}时，这一层便向公众开放；但展示柜要到{time=9:10}才会揭开遮布。这纯粹是为了制造戏剧效果，说实话，也是为了让参观者感到自己即将见证一件极其贵重的珍宝。',
        "While at 9:00 a.m., the floor opens to the public, it isn't until 9:10 a.m. that the showcase cabinets are uncovered. This is purely done for dramatic effect and, honestly, to give the visitors the impression that they're about to witness something very valuable.": '{time=9:00}时，这一层便向公众开放；但展示柜要到{time=9:10}才会揭开遮布。这纯粹是为了制造戏剧效果，说实话，也是为了让参观者感到自己即将见证一件极其贵重的珍宝。',
        "Shortly, Katei finished with every cabinet. They had all contained gemstones of different shapes and tones. Some also had a brief explanation below them, detailing where they'd been found along with the name of who'd found them. Most were discovered in the mountains I was used to seeing in the background of Yushibana.": '很快，Katei 把所有展示柜都揭完了。{w}每个柜子里都放着形状、色泽各异的宝石。有些柜子下方还附有简短说明，写明发现地点和发现者的名字。其中大多数都是在丰花背景里那片我早已看惯的群山中发现的。',
        "The people outside think the gems were the goal and that the robbery was a failure. However, part of that relies on them not knowing the exact rooms that were covered in the smoke. I'm sure more people will conclude what I'm saying once they enter the tower. If the culprit intended to use those gems as a feint, this plan is lacking.": '外面的人认为宝石才是目标，抢劫已经失败。不过这种看法能成立，部分是因为他们并不知道烟雾究竟覆盖了哪些房间。{w} 我相信等更多人进入塔里，就会得出和我相同的结论。如果犯人本想用那些宝石作幌子，这个计划未免太不高明。',
        "You're... right. I hadn't thought of this, but I'm not convinced. Targeting both hallways still wouldn't make much sense, and most importantly, it implies her plan only worked because the alarm's effects got delayed; it would've been no so-called malfunction.": '你说得……也对。这一点我倒没想到，可还是说服不了我。{w} 而且同时袭击两条走廊仍然说不通，最重要的是，照这说法，她的计划能成全靠警报效果延迟——那可就谈不上什么「故障」了。',
        "Hm... Remember what Suripo said? If anyone was in front of the shutter as it closed, it would've stopped. It's possible it was delayed, which gave Naomi enough time to leave even though she was in the event room when the alarm played.": '嗯……{w}还记得 Suripo 说过的话吗？卷帘门下降时若有人挡在前面，就会停下来。也许它确实延迟了，于是即使警报响起时 Naomi 在活动室里，她也来得及离开。',
        "When I heard the alarm, there was another sound too, much fainter. I just realized that must've been the shutter closing, because it was pretty rough and came from the lobby. That means there was no delay, and there was a louder sound at the end when it hit the floor. I'm almost certain it went the whole time without stopping.": '听到警报的时候，我还听见另一个声音，轻得多。我刚意识到，那一定是卷帘门落下的声音——很粗重，而且是从大厅方向传来的。{w} 也就是说根本没有延迟。最后它砸到地面时，声音还更响了一些。我几乎可以确定，它全程都没停过。',
        "When we went quiet, the two people who hadn't participated in the conversation spoke. They were a bit ahead of us, so we walked up to them. After focusing on the point where they were staring, we saw what Isla had found. Next to the right wall was a small, rusty key.": '我们安静下来后，之前一直没参与讨论的两人开了口。{w} 他们就在我们前面一点，我们便走上前去。顺着他们注视的方向看去，我们看见了 Isla 发现的东西。右侧墙边躺着一把小小的、生锈的钥匙。',
        "It's impossible this belongs here. I know it's an old building and there are keys I don't possess, but it must be for something else. Keys are not prohibited items in this tower. It's possible someone dropped it and didn't realize it.": '这东西不可能属于这里。我知道这栋楼年头久了，有些钥匙不在我手上，但这把肯定是开别的东西的。{w} 塔里并不禁止携带钥匙。也许是有人掉了却没发觉。',
        "Nobody answered. He was saying that no innocent person aware of danger could've escaped through the hallway.": '没有人回答。{w} 他的意思是，任何察觉到危险的无辜者都不可能从这条走廊逃出去。',
        "If the key didn't belong to the culprit, it had to belong to someone who'd also gotten trapped and we hadn't seen. Even Naomi didn't make sense as a candidate—I'd been with her up until the alarm had sounded. If someone had fallen unconscious there, they could have dropped the key and failed to realize it upon waking up. Perhaps even the sound of it falling was obscured by the alarm, but I considered it unlikely.": '如果这把钥匙不是犯人的，那就只能是另一个同样被困住、我们却没见过的人留下的。就连 Naomi 也说不通——警报响之前，我一直和她在一起。{w} 要真有人在那儿昏了过去，钥匙可能会从他手里掉出来，而他自己醒来后也没发觉。说不定连钥匙落地的声音都被警报盖过去了，不过我觉得这种可能性不大。',
        "We didn't know for a fact the smoke in hallway A had been released at the same time as in the other two places. There was no reason to believe it hadn't been, but it also would've allowed one of Katei's claims be the truth. One part of me wanted to directly ask Katei, but I held off.": '我们并不能确定 A走廊的烟雾和另外两处是同时放出来的。虽然没有理由认为不是，但要不是同时，Katei 的某个说法就有可能是真的。{w} 我有点想直接去问 Katei，但最后忍住了。',
        "If someone had heard yells coming from the lobby or seen smoke coming through the door of the event room, they might've rushed out without stopping to retrieve their key... I recalled that I'd heard only silence when we were about to fall unconscious.": '若是有人听见大厅传来的喊声，或是看见烟雾从活动室的门缝里涌出，也许就会慌忙跑出去，顾不上取回自己的钥匙……{w} 可我记得，就在我们即将失去意识的时候，听到的只有一片寂静。',
        'We accepted that and moved on. The next room was no different from the previous. Katei went ahead and began to make sure nothing had been stolen from its cabinets.': '我们接受了这个安排，继续前进。{w} 下一个房间与之前那间并无不同。Katei 走在前面，开始逐一确认展示柜里没有东西失窃。',
        "Yeah. If someone messed with my wristwatch while I was unconscious, they could've made me falsely confirm the computer's time. Someone could have done that to frame Katei. It's too ridiculous to consider it seriously. They'd need to know that Katei would say everything he said only to turn around and disprove it with the computer's sleep mode, risking the possibility of nobody noticing it.": '对。如果有人趁我昏迷时动过我这块表，就能让我错误地确认电脑上的时间。{w} 也能借此栽赃 Katei。{w} 不过这种设想太荒唐，不值得当真。对方得先料到 Katei 会说出那套话，而这话之后又会被电脑的休眠模式推翻——而且还得赌没人会注意到。',
        "And not only that, but it's also something that only works with the people who got trapped. This wouldn't mean anything if we brought it up outside. And Katei, who didn't fall unconscious, would've said the time was wrong. It would be insane for him to create a problem for himself by changing my watch time. He also let us talk to Suripo, who could've mentioned the time at any moment.": '而且不止如此，这种做法只对被困在这里的人有效。要是我们到外面提起，根本说明不了什么。{w} 再说，Katei 并没有失去意识，大可以一口咬定时间不对。他若改了我的表，等于给自己找麻烦，实在说不通。{w} 他还让我们和 Suripo 交谈，而 Suripo 随时都可能提到时间。',
        "I still think the Sekimeiya has to be the core of all this. That has to be right. Now, don't you find it strange that a simple security member would know all that?": '我仍然认为，Sekimeiya 才是这一切的核心。这一点应该没错。{w} 那么，你不觉得奇怪吗？区区一个保安，竟然知道这么多。',
        "I'm saying he could be the the guy who originally found the Sekimeiya. He didn't know about what Suripo told us beforehand. Otherwise, he would've said it all to earn our trust. Once he knew about Suripo's factual story, he combined his own knowledge with it to make us believe he truly works in the tower.": '我是说，他很可能就是最初发现 Sekimeiya 的那个人。他事先并不知道 Suripo 告诉我们的那些事。否则，他早就全盘说出来博取信任了。{w} 等他听说了 Suripo 那套有据可查的说法之后，便把自己的见闻和它拼在一起，好让我们相信他真的在塔里工作。',
        'All right. So at approximately 8:00, I saw Katei in the lobby. The reason why I started questioning him so quickly was because when I first saw him, he was wearing normal clothes.': '好。大约在 {time=8}，我在大厅里看见了 Katei。我之所以那么快就开始质问他，是因为我第一次看见他的时候，他穿的是便服。',
        'All right. So at approximately 8 a.m., I saw Katei in the lobby. The reason why I started questioning him so quickly was because when I first saw him, he was wearing normal clothes.': '好。大约在 {time=8}，我在大厅里看见了 Katei。我之所以那么快就开始质问他，是因为我第一次看见他的时候，他穿的是便服。',
        "Xyn isn't behind this, which is why it's happening during the day. He enters the tower at 8:00 this morning. He could have somehow met with the real Katei Kuiji and learned about the alarm and emergency contact line from him.": '这事背后不是 Xyn——也正因如此，它才会发生在白天。他今天早上 {time=8:00} 进入塔内，有可能设法见到了真正的 Katei Kuiji，并从对方口中问出了警报和紧急联络线路的事。',
        "Xyn isn't behind this, which is why it's happening during the day. He enters the tower at 8:00 a.m. this morning. He could have somehow met with the real Katei Kuiji and learned about the alarm and emergency contact line from him.": '这事背后不是 Xyn——也正因如此，它才会发生在白天。他今天早上 {time=8:00} 进入塔内，有可能设法见到了真正的 Katei Kuiji，并从对方口中问出了警报和紧急联络线路的事。',
        "I don't know why he let us talk to the outside, but it's possible he had something to gain from that. Maybe he wanted everyone outside to think that Katei Kuiji really is in the tower and that everything here is going well. Maybe he wanted to make sure the bait gemstones worked and tricked Ashiya. This is so messy that it almost feels unrelated to what he did, but that can't be it.": '我不知道他为什么让我们和外界通话，但也许他能从中得到什么好处。也许他想让外面的人都相信 Katei Kuiji 确实在塔里，这里一切顺利。{w} 也许他想确认那些诱饵宝石起了作用，骗过了芦屋。整件事太乱了，简直像跟他做的事无关，但不可能只是这样。',
        "Also, one last thing. We only think that what we saw is the Sekimeiya because Katei told us so. The plan could already be further along. The real Sekimeiya could've been replaced while we were asleep. That could be another reason why Naomi's presence had to be taken care of, as she would expose that illusion.": '另外，还有最后一件事。{w} 我们之所以认定看到的就是 Sekimeiya，全是因为 Katei 这么说。计划也许早就推进得更远了——真正的 Sekimeiya 可能在我们睡着时就被换掉了。{w} 这也许也是必须处理掉 Naomi 的另一个原因，因为她会戳穿这个假象。',
        "If whatever this plan is hasn't ended, it's almost certain that a culprit must be here with us. Who would that be, and what do they intend to do next?": '如果这个计划尚未结束，那几乎可以肯定，犯人就在我们之中。{w} 会是谁？接下来又想做什么？',
        "The two staff members could have easily designed an internal attack thanks to the knowledge they possess. Katei made us think the Sekimeiya we saw was the real deal. Now, Naomi can do as she pleases since she'll be constantly covered by Katei, who will guide all of us as the most knowledgeable person here. ...Perhaps that's unlikely since he had no problem staying behind in the security room while we went to investigate.": '这两名员工凭着自己掌握的内部信息，要策划一场内部袭击并不难。Katei 让我们相信眼前的就是真正的 Sekimeiya；而 Naomi 则可以随心所欲，因为 Katei 会一直替她打掩护——作为这里最了解情况的人，他还在给我们所有人带路。{w} ……不过这也许不太可能，毕竟我们出去调查时，他一点也不介意留在监控室里。',
        "...Yes, I agree. Either him or Naomi, but with the scenario I constructed, Naomi's already taken care of. Most things are, actually. I don't know how the smoke was released, what triggered the alarm, and how Katei plans to disappear with the Sekimeiya. It's also good to note that regardless of the method, a member of security staff like him could easily design a way to release the smoke.": '……嗯，我同意。{w}不是他就是 Naomi，不过按我构建的情形来看，Naomi 那边已经处理妥当了。其实大部分环节都有着落了。烟雾是怎么放出来的、警报是什么触发的、Katei 又打算怎么带着 Sekimeiya 消失，这些我还不知道。另外还有一点值得记下：不管用什么方法，像他这样的安保人员都很容易设计出释放烟雾的手段。',
        "A bit. Aren't you? Aren't you looking forward to knowing which theory ends up being the correct one? Or maybe to find out that we were both incorrect. What if this is all bigger than we think, or just a coincidental accident?": '有一点。你不兴奋吗？{w}你就不想知道最后哪种推理才是对的？还是说，你其实希望最后发现我们两个都猜错了？万一这件事比我们想的要大得多，或者只是一场偶然的事故呢？',
        'Exactly. ...He spoke very highly of Xyn. What if he was speaking very highly of himself? The group he works for, alongside Katei?': '正是。……他对 Xyn 评价很高。{w}可万一他其实是在夸自己呢？夸的是他和 Katei 一起效力的那个组织？',
        "I see. Me, I'm just curious. I can't wait to know how this plan ends. Sadly, there's still a while until that. Maybe they need these twelve hours for something... Suripo corroborated the amount of time Katei said, so it would be strange if it turned out to be wrong.": '原来如此。{w}我嘛，只是好奇而已。我迫不及待想知道这个计划会怎么收场。可惜离那还有好一阵子。也许这十二小时他们另有用途……Suripo 也证实了 Katei 说的时间，所以这个时间要是出了错，反倒奇怪了。',
        'It was the same appearance the hallways bore. We immediately understood the smoke had also gotten into the last room. We only found it a shocking sight because of what Katei previously told us.': '走廊里也是同样的景象。我们立刻明白，烟雾也进了最后一间房。{w}只因 Katei 先前说过的话，这一幕才让我们如此震惊。',
        "You all remember what I said earlier, right? That this part of the plan didn't make a ton of sense. The gems were stolen without releasing smoke in their room, which implied that the smoke had another purpose.": '你们都记得我刚才说的吧？{w}我说这部分计划说不通。宝石被偷，却没有在它们的房间里放烟雾，这就说明烟雾另有用途。',
        "I more or less understood why Sai said that. Without inspecting every room, Katei felt confident in saying that only three different places had been hit with the smoke, but he'd been incorrect. That indicated he hadn't been behind the attack itself, since he wouldn't have made that mistake. It let Sai confront him since he no longer believed he was confronting Xyn, but a mere suspicious individual.": '我大致明白 Sai 为什么这么说。Katei 并没有逐一检查每个房间，却敢断言只有三处被烟雾波及，而他错了。{w} 这说明他并非袭击的幕后主使——若真是他，就不会犯这种错。这也让 Sai 敢于当面质问他，因为他已不再觉得自己面对的是 Xyn，而只是一个形迹可疑的人。',
        "Your assumption is mistaken. I can explain what led to that assertion. When I was in the security room, most of the cameras from this floor were being displayed. It is true that I saw the smoke appearing out of nowhere, but at that time, this room's camera was not being shown. Usually, monitoring the interior of a room isn't needed if another camera shows its door.": '你的假设不对。我可以解释我为什么会得出那个结论。{w} 我在监控室时，这一层大部分摄像头的画面都开着。我确实看到烟雾凭空冒出，但那时这间房的画面并没有显示出来。通常来说，只要另有摄像头对着房门，就不必再看房内的情况。',
        "So, all that this room's camera showed was a black screen. This means that I was unable to recognize that one of the disabled screens belonged to this room. Since both hallways possess numerous cameras, I did not notice there were one too many black screens. Later, since I looked into most of the clean rooms, I wrongly assumed that they all were the same.": '所以，这间房的摄像头画面也只是一片黑。也就是说，我没发现其中一块黑屏属于这间房。{w} 两条走廊都装了不少摄像头，我没察觉黑屏多了一块。后来，我查看过的房间大多没被烟雾波及，便错误地以为所有房间都一样。',
        "Let me be clear: I don't believe you nor intend to do so. You are full of shit. However, I don't know why you told us that only those three places had been hit, and it's pissing me off. Do you remember when you said you'd left the lobby door open? Like Atsuki pointed out, it was opened after the smoke was released since almost none went through it. Still saying that's true?": '我把话说清楚：我不信你，也不打算信你。你满嘴鬼话。可我还是想不通，你为什么要告诉我们只有那三处被烟雾波及——这让我很不痛快。{w} 你还记得你说过，大厅的门你没关吗？就像 Atsuki 指出的那样，那扇门是在烟雾放出之后才开的，因为几乎没有烟从那边透过去。你现在还坚持这个说法？',
        "Well, I don't know why that would've been done, but you can't deny it just because you find it unlikely. It could very well be that it happened after I left the security room. The rooms all look very similar, so maybe I did see this one when I looked through the cameras. Now I'm not sure. I don't know which of the two possibilities I'm presenting is the correct one.": '这个嘛，我也不知道为什么要那么做，但你不能只因为觉得不太可能就否定它。{w}完全有可能是在我离开监控室之后才发生的。这些房间看起来都差不多，说不定我看监控时确实看到了这一间。现在我也说不准了。我提出的两种可能性，到底哪一种是正确的，我自己也不知道。',
        'I mean, the curtains here were lowered when we entered. Most importantly, they were stained with the smoke. This means that during the time the smoke was released, the cabinets were covered.': '我是说，我们进来的时候，这里的遮布是放下来的。最关键的是，遮布上沾了烟雾的痕迹。{w}也就是说，放烟雾的时候，这些展示柜是遮着的。',
        "You all see what I'm saying, right? It would have been a pointless waste of time to lower them. After the smoke was released in this room, the curtains weren't moved. To put it simply, the gemstones that were once here were stolen before the smoke was released. This is why someone was able to bring them outside before the exit closed.": '你们都明白我的意思吧？再把它们放下来纯属浪费时间。这个房间放出烟雾之后，遮布就没再被动过。{w}简单来说，原本放在这里的宝石，是在烟雾放出之前就被偷走的。所以才会有人能在出口关闭之前把它们带出去。',
        "Hm, I'm not sure. We did have the chance to talk to the police, but it happened before we came here. I'm saying this was done to trick Ashiya into thinking the gems were the goal. However, I also think that the plan must somehow end by stealing the Sekimeiya, which will directly reveal that the gems were never the goal. It could definitely be that the smoke was released to trick us—the people who got trapped. It all depends on whether someone is trying to trick us.": '嗯，我也说不准。我们确实有过联系警方的机会，但那是在我们来这里之前。{w}我的意思是，他们这么做是为了让芦屋以为宝石才是目标。不过我也认为，这个计划最后必定会以偷走 Sekimeiya 收场，而那样就直接表明宝石从来不是目标。那些烟雾说不定就是为了骗我们这些被困住的人。关键在于，到底有没有人在骗我们。',
        "Who knows? If the gems were stolen during the night through some method Xyn are capable of, they'd leave the curtains lowered to prevent it from being noticed through the cameras and so that the visitors couldn't see them before 9:10.": '谁知道呢。如果宝石是在夜里被 Xyn 用某种他们办得到的手段偷走的，那他们就会让遮布一直保持放下的状态，免得被监控看出来，也让参观者在 {time=9:10.} 之前看不到里面。',
        "Who knows? If the gems were stolen during the night through some method Xyn are capable of, they'd leave the curtains lowered to prevent it from being noticed through the cameras and so that the visitors couldn't see them before 9:10 a.m.": '谁知道呢。如果宝石是在夜里被 Xyn 用某种他们办得到的手段偷走的，那他们就会让遮布一直保持放下的状态，免得被监控看出来，也让参观者在 {time=9:10.} 之前看不到里面。',
        '...Well, they were forced to leave the cabinets covered, but doing so also indicates that the gems were stolen before the doors were open to the public...': '……{w}总之，他们是不得已才让展示柜一直遮着，可这样一来，也说明宝石是在对公众开放之前就被偷走的……',
        "I don't know why. I've approached it from different angles, but I can't come up with something that makes sense. In some way, these gems must've only been a side part of the plan. Them getting stolen before the smoke was released is close to confirmation, but how everything pieces together is not as simple to figure out.": '我不知道为什么。我换了好几个角度去想，还是想不出一个说得通的解释。{w}从某种意义上看，这些宝石一定只是计划中的次要部分。它们是在烟雾放出之前就被偷走的，这几乎可以确定；但整件事怎么拼在一起，就不是那么容易想明白的了。',
        'We had all assumed that the gems were stolen before the smoke was released since the curtains had been lowered. If anyone stole the gems after the attack, there was no reason to waste their time lowering the curtains again. However, that was a very simple indicator of the time the gems had been stolen, and one that would not have been overlooked.': '遮布被放了下来，所以我们才都认定宝石是在烟雾释放之前被偷走的。若有人是在袭击之后才行窃，就没必要多此一举再把遮布放下。{w} 可这个判断失窃时间的依据实在太过简单，谁都不会忽略。',
        "I couldn't think of an immediate benefit, but deliberately misleading us about the time or reason behind an action was a potent move. That effect wouldn't have been achieved if the tower had really been robbed at night and the curtains were left down.  ...And realistically, even though Xyn could've been involved, how could they have emptied so many cabinets during the night? Hadn't the police been nearby? Hadn't the cameras been monitoring everything?": '我一时想不到这能带来什么好处，但刻意误导他人对某个举动的时间与缘由的判断，本身就是极有效的手段。若塔里真是在夜里失窃，遮布也一直垂着，就达不到这样的效果。{w} ……况且说实在的，就算 Xyn 牵涉其中，他们又怎能在夜里搬空那么多展示柜？警察难道不在附近？监控难道没有拍下一切？',
        "But we already know that. It must've been Naomi. After she did something, she must've wanted to get rid of this and didn't care about leaving it here. It makes sense that she would have disabled the security system before dropping it.": '可这一点我们早就知道了。只可能是 Naomi。{w} 她干完那件事后，肯定想把这箱子处理掉，也不在乎把它丢在这里。她多半会先关掉安保系统，再把箱子丢下，这才说得通。',
        'N-Now that you mention it, yes. I went to the mechanical room while Atsuki said he would inspect the rest of this floor.': '这、这么一说，确实有。{w} 我去了机械室，Atsuki 则说他要去查看这一层剩下的地方。',
        "Ah, no. That's not what I meant. I think you have a good reason to suspect us. Don't you remember when we got back? We said we'd gone to the bathroom, didn't we?": '啊，不，我不是那个意思。我觉得你们有充分的理由怀疑我们。{w} 你还记得我们回来的时候吗？我们说过去洗手间了，对吧？',
        "The bathrooms were empty, so we were ready to move on. Regarding the suitcase, we weren't sure what to think, but we didn't take it with us. The location where it had been discarded was the only information we had to work with. I didn't want to think too deeply into every detail, but something came to mind.": '洗手间里空无一人，我们便准备继续调查。至于那个行李箱，我们不知道该怎么判断，但也没有把它带走。{w} 唯一可供我们推敲的线索，就是它被丢弃的地点。我本不想对每个细节想得太深，可有个念头还是冒了出来。',
        "It could be that Katei was right this time. The location someone chose to leave the suitcase was one we hadn't yet been in. If the culprit left it there before we woke up, I can't think of a reason why they wouldn't have left it in one of the two main hallways. After all, the plan only involved them and the event room at a glance. At no point was it necessary to enter hallway C, which has security cameras.": '也许这一次 Katei 说对了。留下行李箱的人所选的地点，正是我们还没去过的地方。{w} 如果犯人在我们醒来之前就把它留在那里，我想不出他们为什么不干脆放在两条主走廊中的一条。毕竟表面上看，整个计划只涉及他们和活动室。根本没有必要进入装有监控摄像头的 C走廊。',
        "In addition, that spot wasn't in range of any of the cameras, so we couldn't have seen it while we'd been in the security room. ...But the trick wouldn't work on Katei, who'd already inspected the area.": '此外，那个位置不在任何摄像头的拍摄范围内，所以我们待在监控室时不可能看到它。{w} ……但这套把戏对已经检查过那片区域的 Katei 不起作用。',
        'Sai went ahead and tried to open every locker. Shortly, we confirmed that Katei was right: they were all locked tight.': 'Sai 径直上前，试着逐个打开储物柜。{w}没过多久我们就证实 Katei 说得没错：所有柜子都锁得严严实实。',
        "Yeah. It's already past 10:00. One more person is confirmed to be with us, so if she hasn't appeared yet, she must not intend to show herself.": '是啊。现在已经过了 {time=10.}。已经确认还有一个人和我们在一起，如果她还没露面，那多半是不打算现身了。',
        "Yeah. It's already past 10 a.m. One more person is confirmed to be with us, so if she hasn't appeared yet, she must not intend to show herself.": '是啊。现在已经过了 {time=10.}。已经确认还有一个人和我们在一起，如果她还没露面，那多半是不打算现身了。',
        "You won't stop trying to find ways to frame me, will you? You're wrong. They would've known I was inside the security room and must've only gone up when they saw I'd left it.": '你非要把一切都往我身上套才肯罢休，是吧？{w}你错了。他们知道我就在监控室里，一定是看见我离开了才往上走的。',
        "I don't think so, at least. If it's true that it should've been locked, by leaving it unlocked, they're telling us they possess the key. Naomi wouldn't do that purposely because it makes her suspicious. It's possible someone who's not a staff member unlocked the door.": '至少我不这么认为。假如那扇门本该锁着，他们却让它开着，就等于告诉我们：钥匙在他们手上。{w}Naomi 不会故意这么做，那只会让自己惹上嫌疑。所以，开门的也可能不是这里的工作人员。',
        "Only four of us can be inside at once. It's a fairly old elevator. The stairs really aren't so bad, so let's walk up.": '一次最多只能进四个人。这电梯有些年头了。{w}楼梯也没那么难走，我们还是走上去吧。',
        "The elevator didn't shake at all, so we only knew we were moving because of the screechy noise the ropes above us were making.": '{w=0.6}电梯没有一点晃动，我们只能靠头顶钢索发出的刺耳声响判断它在移动。',
        'They were a quiet few seconds, and since the doors to the other floors were fully opaque, they were also dim. I felt a vague sense of claustrophobia for the first time since we had awakened.': '{w=0.6}那几秒钟里一片安静，通往其他楼层的门都完全不透光，光线也很暗。醒来之后，我第一次隐约感到一阵幽闭的压迫感。',
        'Once the elevator slowed down and we were allowed to leave, I opened the door that would lead us to an unknown place.': '{w=0.6}等电梯减速停下、门可以打开时，我推开了那扇通往未知之处的门。',
        'We stepped out and looked around us. A long hallway composed of calm colors extended far ahead.': '{w=0.6}我们走出电梯，环顾四周。一条色调沉静的走廊向远处延伸。',
        'Through the door, we were able to see that, once again, the third section looked exactly like the first two. The exception was the lack of a door leading to a fourth.': '{w=0.6}透过门望进去，第三个隔间果然也和前两个一模一样。唯一的区别是，那里没有通往第四间的门。',
        "Yeah, I saw them. They do look a bit out of place. No idea what they're so paranoid about.": '嗯，我也看到了。确实显得有些突兀。{w}真不知道他们有什么好紧张的。',
        "Shiroya's and Erina's expressions told me that arguing would lead us nowhere. But I was stubborn and slightly curious about her attitude.": '从 Shiroya 和 Erina 的表情看来，争下去也不会有结果。{w}可我这人固执，对她的态度也有几分好奇。',
        '...My brain processed that line as another thoughtless remark she had made up to justify what she was saying. Only after a few seconds of silence did I fully comprehend it.': '……{w}我起初只当这是她又一句随口编出来给自己撑腰的话。沉默了几秒，我才真正明白过来。',
        '...Before answering, I kept trying to make sense of such a confusing bunch of words. I was starting to think that her story could be seen in a completely different way—a much more ominous one.': '……{w}我没有立刻回答，只是反复琢磨她那一堆让人摸不着头脑的话。我渐渐觉得，她这套说辞完全可以换个角度去理解——一个要凶险得多的角度。',
        "There's no way her friend lives with them like she said. That would mean that Xyn instructed her to lie about her friend's identity so that the actual person couldn't be found. But why the hell would they let her speak about it at all instead of telling her to keep fully quiet?": '她那位朋友绝不可能像她说的那样，和她们住在一起。也就是说，Xyn 指使她隐瞒朋友的真正身份，免得被人查到。{w} 可既然这样，他们为什么还任由她说出这些，而不是让她彻底闭嘴？',
        "However, she also said that she didn't know how long we'd stay here for. Twelve hours is the maximum time... Is it possible that depending on how some events play out, we could leave earlier?": '不过她也说过，她不知道我们会在这里待多久。{w} 十二小时是最长时间……有没有可能，随着某些事态的发展，我们能提前离开？',
        "I have no idea what any of this accomplishes, but since only some Ashiya workers should've known about the alarm's existence, only they or an attacker with inside information could've been in contact with Isla. Reasons aside, an Ashiya employee could have been relaying information to her. Two happen to come to mind, one being a man, and the other a woman.": '我完全不知道这一切有什么目的，但既然应该只有部分芦屋员工知道警报的存在，那能接触 Isla 的就只可能是他们，或者掌握内情的袭击者。{w} 先不论理由，确实可能有芦屋员工向她传递消息。我恰好想到两个人，一男一女。',
        "I see. The sound from earlier doesn't make much sense, though. We left the elevator on floor 6 and heard it moving on floor 5. Like you said, it could only have been going down.": '原来如此。{w}不过刚才那阵动静还是说不通。我们把电梯留在六楼，却在五楼听见它移动。就像你说的，它只可能是往下走。',
        "...We went to the crystal floor, but she didn't want to come back.": '……{w}我们去了水晶层，但她不肯回来。',
        "Yes. I don't know why, though. Even if she'd achieved that, it's not like she could've convinced the police. Hearing her justifications made me even more convinced that she's involved in some way. Even though she ran away, I didn't try to find her immediately since I figured there was no way she could keep hiding. She still has to be somewhere on the crystal floor.": '是。可我不知道她为什么这么做。就算说服了我，她也说服不了警察。听她那些辩解，我反而更确信她多少牵涉其中。{w} 她虽然跑了，我却没有立刻去找，因为我认定她躲不了多久。她一定还在水晶层的某个地方。',
        "...She spat out nothing but inconsistencies. She said that she'd been trying to find help since waking up. She couldn't answer why she'd gone up to the office floors instead of aiding Erina's group or staying with everyone in the event room.": '……{w}她说的话处处自相矛盾。{w} 她说自己醒来后一直在找人帮忙。可她却说不清自己为什么上到办公楼层，既不去帮 Erina 他们，也不留在活动室和大家待在一起。',
        "Someone should stay here in case Naomi tries to go up. The rest of us will split downstairs to make sure she's found. Another person will also be needed to stay on floor 2 to make sure she doesn't intend to pointlessly go hide there. Three will be enough to inspect the whole first floor. One person will stay in the lobby, the other in hallway C, and the last person will check every room in both hallways. She will not escape.": '得有人留在这里，以防 Naomi 想上楼。其余人分头去楼下，确保找到她。{w} 还需要一个人守在二楼，免得她又想着躲到那里去。检查整个一楼，三个人就够了。一个人守大厅，一个人守 C走廊，最后一个人搜查两条走廊的每个房间。她逃不掉。',
        "I'm really not sure. Anyway, how are you holding up? Sorry, I've just been trying to think about—": '我真说不准。{w}对了，你还好吗？抱歉，我一直在想——',
        "I recalled what Sai had said too late. We weren't close enough to stop it on the fourth floor. Trying to avoid wasting time, we ran toward the other side to arrive at her destination before we missed her. In our defense, we'd heard the sound when the elevator had been about to pass us by, so stopping it in time wouldn't have been possible.": '等我回想起 Sai 的叮嘱时，已经晚了。我们在四楼离得太远，根本来不及拦下。为了不浪费时间，我们朝另一侧跑去，想赶在她离开之前到达她的目的地。{w} 说句公道话，我们听见动静时电梯已经快要驶过这一层，本来也来不及拦住。',
        "We arrived on floor 5. We thought the elevator hadn't stopped there because it seemed to linger for a bit too long, but I still quickly went through the three partitions while Shiroya stayed next to the first door. As I'd thought, they were empty.": '我们到了五楼。电梯刚才似乎停得久了些，我们怀疑它在这一层停过，但我还是迅速把三个隔间查了一遍，Shiroya 则守在第一个隔间门口。{w} 果然，里面空无一人。',
        "Technically, there was just one more possibility: the attic. But you'd need a unique key for that, and Shiroya was right. The elevator only took a few seconds to arrive, indicating that there had only been a single floor of separation. By moving it, we'd also prevented Naomi from using it upstairs.": '严格说来，还剩一种可能：阁楼。{w} 但那里需要专门的钥匙，而且 Shiroya 说得对——电梯只花了几秒就到，说明它只隔了一层楼。{w} 我们把它叫下来，也让她在楼上没法再用电梯。',
        "Yeah, we experienced how slow it was. There wouldn't have been time for that. I thought that maybe this door was already unlocked or that they had the key hidden somewhere on this floor.": '是啊，我们都见识过它有多慢，根本来不及那么做。{w}我原本想，也许这扇门本就没锁，或者他们把钥匙藏在了这层楼的某处。',
        "Hm... Then the same person must've been who used it just now. It's possible they got off on floor 6 instead of the attic because they knew it would be empty and could easily reach this door. If we noticed the elevator and followed it, it would look like it was empty, but if they went directly to the attic instead, we might've noticed it went there if we called it fast enough.": '嗯……那刚才用电梯的肯定也是同一个人。他们没去阁楼，而是在六楼下了电梯，可能是因为知道这层没人，能轻易到门前。{w} 如果我们注意到电梯并追过去，看到的只会是空电梯；可要是他们直接去了阁楼，我们只要及时叫电梯，就可能发现它停到了那里。',
        "I told Akaro to go find you, and I took that time to check if it really had disappeared while the others waited here. It's gone. I stayed there a while, thinking about what could've happened, and expecting to find you two when I came back. Anyway, many of these rooms haven't been investigated yet. We stayed here until you came back to secure the only exits.": '我让 Akaro 去找你们，趁这工夫自己去确认它是不是真的不见了，其他人就守在这里。{w}确实不见了。我在那儿待了一阵，琢磨究竟是怎么回事，也盼着回来时能看见你们俩。总之，这里还有不少房间没查。我们一直守在这儿，看住仅有的出口，等你们回来。',
        "I understand... It's good that the stairs and the elevator are next to each other. Can I go see it?": '我明白了……楼梯和电梯挨在一起，这倒是好事。{w}我能去看看吗？',
        "You already tried to say this earlier, didn't you? They couldn't have done that. The way we looked through the floors would've made that impossible, and they couldn't have used the elevator since we only heard it once.": '这话你刚才就说过了吧？他们不可能做到的。{w}我们那样一层层搜过来，他们根本不可能从我们旁边过去；电梯也只响过一次，他们也没法用。',
        "That's true... Well, we can check there first if someone stays here.": '确实……{w}也罢，只要有人留在这里，我们就先去那儿查。',
        'I began looking through the opposite side of the room. There were plenty of places to hide a small object. Behind the cabinets, under the pillows that normally held gemstones... A cabinet even had empty drawers.': '我从展室另一侧开始查看。能藏下小东西的地方多得是。{w}展示柜背后、平时托放宝石的垫子下面……甚至还有一只有空抽屉的柜子。',
        'I had to get close to him, as the lack of illumination made it impossible to see what he was holding. It was nothing noteworthy; he was cupping a small, yellow gemstone on his palm.': '光线太暗，看不清他手里拿着什么，我只好凑近他。{w}也不是什么稀奇东西——他掌心里托着一颗小小的黄色宝石。',
        'Once again, he turned around and quickly left the room. I sighed and followed his steps. Outside, he was already next to the others.': '他又一次转过身，快步走出展室。{w}我叹了口气，跟了上去。到了外面，他已经站到其他人身边了。',
        "Five other rooms that met that criterion were still available: the staff room, the cleaning room, the mechanical room, the security room, and the storeroom. I looked inside the cleaning bucket, the only place in the lobby where the Sekimeiya could've been hidden from view, but it only contained soapy water.": '符合这个条件的还有五个房间：员工室、清洁间、机械室、监控室和储藏室。{w} 我看了看清洁桶，那是大厅里唯一能把 Sekimeiya 藏起来不让人看见的地方，可里面只有肥皂水。',
        "Akaro and Sai said that when they'd heard the elevator sound, Naomi had already shown up and left with Katei. If that was the case, Naomi could not have been in the attic the way I'd thought about things. To make it work, I had to slightly change it.": 'Akaro 和 Sai 说，他们听到电梯声响时，Naomi 已经出现，并和 Katei 一起离开了。{w} 若果真如此，Naomi 就不可能像我想的那样待在阁楼。要让推测成立，我得稍作修改。',
        "Shiroya, at my side, looked identical to me. The concept of death and loss had recently been changed for us. She and I hadn't experienced it until two weeks ago, when the world we'd created together crumbled down without warning.": '身旁的 Shiroya 神情与我如出一辙。对我们而言，死亡与失去的含义近来已被改写。{w} 直到两周前，我们共同构筑的世界毫无预兆地崩塌，我和她才第一次尝到这种滋味。',
        "Shiroya and I knew each other since our first year of elementary school, where we became classmates for the first time. Our parents were friends, which quickly tied us together. We would see one another during school and our parents' meetings, so we rapidly grew close. Before becoming classmates, we'd already met a few times, but we'd never really spoken.": '我和 Shiroya 从小学一年级起就认识，那一年我们第一次同班。我们的父母是朋友，这层关系很快就把我们牵到了一起。{w} 无论在学校还是父母聚会时，我们总能碰面，因此很快就熟络起来。其实在成为同班同学之前，我们已经见过几次，只是从未真正说过话。',
        "A few months later, she appeared when Shiroya and I were together, and they introduced themselves in more depth. Since then, the three of us started to become comfortable around each other after school. It was out of the ordinary for us since we were used to being alone, but we quickly took a liking to Miiya. She was a blunt and sincere girl—one who didn't seem to have many worries in life or think too hard about things. Even though she'd made her way into our lives out of the blue, we became accustomed to her presence.": '几个月后，正当我和 Shiroya 在一起时，她出现了，两人也更详细地互相介绍了一番。自那以后，放学后我们三人便渐渐熟络起来。我们早已习惯独处，这样的变化并不寻常，但我们很快就喜欢上了 Miiya。{w} 她是个直率而真诚的女孩——看上去生活里没多少烦恼，也不爱把事情想得太复杂。尽管她是不期而至地闯进了我们的生活，我们还是习惯了她的存在。',
        "The previous summer was not an easy one for us. Shiroya and I weren't sure what to do with our futures, and we knew that if our decisions differed, we might stop seeing each other. Behind everything else, that was always my biggest worry, and at the same time, Miiya was only focused on searching for a job that wanted her. I felt like I was stuck in the past, wishing that our school days could continue as always. Meanwhile, the uncertainty of the future prevented Shiroya from resting easy. That made it hard for us to keep up with each other, and even though the circumstances were perfect for a summer together, the three of us spent it alone.": '对我们来说，前一个夏天并不好过。我和 Shiroya 都不确定未来该走向何方，也明白一旦选择不同，我们或许就再也见不到彼此。在这一切背后，这始终是我最深的忧虑；而与此同时，Miiya 一心只想找到一份愿意雇她的工作。{w} 我觉得自己被困在过去，盼着学生时代能一如往常地延续下去；未来的不确定又让 Shiroya 无法安心。我们因此难以跟上彼此的步调，那个夏天明明最适合三人一起度过，我们却各自孤单地过完了它。',
        'For two or three months, my old life continued fading away. ...That was until I received a call from Miiya. She confessed to feeling a lot like I had and wanting to restore everything. I immediately called Shiroya, who sounded like she was in the same position.': '两三个月里，我旧日的生活持续褪色。{w} ……直到我接到 Miiya 的电话。她坦言自己的感受和我十分相似，也想把一切恢复原样。我立刻打给了 Shiroya，听她的语气，她也处在同样的境地。',
        "We said that we'd go back to how everything had been during the start of the year. The three of us needed it and all feared that it had ended long ago. Even though we'd settled that, there weren't many things to do during the winter in Yushibana. Hanging out and talking for hours used to work in the past, but if we were starting fresh, that might not have sufficed. That was how we came across Ashiya's advertisement; on December 15th, their biggest event to date would be held.": '我们说好，要回到年初时的那副样子。我们三人都需要它，也都害怕它早已终结。{w} 话虽如此，丰花的冬天并没有多少可做的事。过去只要凑在一起聊上几个小时便足够，但若要从头来过，那或许并不够。就在那时，我们看到了芦屋的广告：12 月 15 日，他们将举办迄今为止规模最大的一场活动。',
        'It honestly sounded like a fine idea to us. Anything the three of us could go to was good. According to the announcement, an event was held in Ashiya Tower every Thursday, each one requiring special entrance tickets.': '说实话，我们也觉得这主意不错。只要是三人能一起参加的活动，怎样都好。{w} 公告上说，芦屋塔每逢周四都会举办活动，每场都需要专门的入场券。',
        "She almost accepted immediately, but she ended up saying she'd think about it. I insisted, saying that she wouldn't be a bother, and accompanied her to her apartment. The next day, she accepted and came over for a temporary stay.": '她几乎当场就要答应，最后却说想再考虑一下。我再三坚持，说不会添麻烦，并陪她回了公寓。{w} 第二天，她答应了，搬来暂住。',
        "I didn't want to distance myself from Shiroya; facing the thought of being left alone was unbearable. That was why I'd immediately asked her to remain together for a few days. At home, we briefly saw each other every day, but no conversations aside from simple words to coordinate ourselves came from either of us. At least, she spent the days with Maxi and Umi, a dog and a cat that had lived with me for years, which I hoped made her feel less lonely. I also got to hear her voice a handful of times when she talked to her parents over the phone, but they were too busy to leave.": '我不想和 Shiroya 拉开距离；一想到要独自留下，我就无法忍受。正因如此，我才立刻请她多留几天。在家里，我们每天都会匆匆见上一面，却除了协调琐事之外谁也不开口。{w} 至少，她还有 Maxi 和 Umi 陪着——那是我养了多年的狗和猫，我希望这能让她少些孤单。她在电话里和父母说话时，我也听到过几次她的声音，可他们忙得脱不开身。',
        'We finally talked a bit before the night came. Our schedules were all over the place, and we had to wake up very early to make it to Ashiya Tower before {time=9.} As the night went on, it was clear that neither of us would be able to sleep.': '夜幕降临前，我们总算聊了一阵。我们的作息一片混乱，必须起得极早，才能在 {time=9.} 之前赶到芦屋塔。{w} 夜渐深，谁都明白我们两人都睡不着了。',
        'We finally talked a bit before the night came. Our schedules were all over the place, and we had to wake up very early to make it to Ashiya Tower before 9:00.{w} As the night went on, it was clear that neither of us would be able to sleep.': '夜幕降临前，我们总算聊了一阵。我们的作息一片混乱，必须起得极早，才能在 {time=9.} 之前赶到芦屋塔。{w} 夜渐深，谁都明白我们两人都睡不着了。',
        'We finally talked a bit before the night came. Our schedules were all over the place, and we had to wake up very early to make it to Ashiya Tower before 9:00. As the night went on, it was clear that neither of us would be able to sleep.': '夜幕降临前，我们总算聊了一阵。我们的作息一片混乱，必须起得极早，才能在 {time=9.} 之前赶到芦屋塔。{w} 夜渐深，谁都明白我们两人都睡不着了。',
        'We finally talked a bit before the night came. Our schedules were all over the place, and we had to wake up very early to make it to Ashiya Tower before 9 a.m.{w} As the night went on, it was clear that neither of us would be able to sleep.': '夜幕降临前，我们总算聊了一阵。我们的作息一片混乱，必须起得极早，才能在 {time=9.} 之前赶到芦屋塔。{w} 夜渐深，谁都明白我们两人都睡不着了。',
        'We finally talked a bit before the night came. Our schedules were all over the place, and we had to wake up very early to make it to Ashiya Tower before 9 a.m. As the night went on, it was clear that neither of us would be able to sleep.': '夜幕降临前，我们总算聊了一阵。我们的作息一片混乱，必须起得极早，才能在 {time=9.} 之前赶到芦屋塔。{w} 夜渐深，谁都明白我们两人都睡不着了。',
        "At 6:00, everything around us was covered in snow, and even though we'd grown used to the sheer cold of the mountains, staying outside for that long exceeded our limit. We walked to the entrance of the tower and were told by a guard that we could wait inside until the doors opened to the public.": '到了 {time=6}，四周的一切都覆着雪。尽管我们早已习惯山间的严寒，在外面待上那么久还是超出了极限。我们走到塔的入口，一名警卫告诉我们，可以在里面等到向公众开放的时刻。',
        "At 6 a.m., everything around us was covered in snow, and even though we'd grown used to the sheer cold of the mountains, staying outside for that long exceeded our limit. We walked to the entrance of the tower and were told by a guard that we could wait inside until the doors opened to the public.": '到了 {time=6}，四周的一切都覆着雪。尽管我们早已习惯山间的严寒，在外面待上那么久还是超出了极限。我们走到塔的入口，一名警卫告诉我们，可以在里面等到向公众开放的时刻。',
        "We were met by a lady sorting a bunch of papers behind the reception desk. Shiroya and I hadn't talked much, but staying with each other was more than enough. The only other person there was a man in the middle of the room, wearing a lost look. He glanced at us for an instant before going back to how he had been. We'd later learn his name was Akaro, and I would speak to him for the first time in the event room.": '接待台后有一位女士正在整理一叠文件，是她接待了我们。Shiroya 和我一路没说上几句话，可只要能彼此作伴，便已足够。屋里另有一个男人站在房间中央，神情茫然。他朝我们瞥了一眼，随即又恢复了先前那副模样。{w} 后来我们才知道他叫 Akaro，而我第一次同他说话，是在活动室里。',
        'No. Sure, that might also be a possibility that lets Katei not be a murderer, but Sai had an easier way all by himself. He said it earlier, right? That he went to check if the Sekimeiya had truly disappeared while you all waited next to the stairs.': '不。那种可能确实也能让 Katei 摆脱杀人嫌疑，但 Sai 一个人就有更省事的办法。{w} 他刚才说过吧？你们都在楼梯边等着的时候，他跑去确认 Sekimeiya 是不是真的消失了。',
        "That makes sense if Katei was the culprit, but if I chased Naomi here, I wouldn't have had an easy time pushing her into this wall. She would've been farther into the room than me, so I would've had to push her against one of the other three walls. Ignoring, obviously, that she would not have run into a room and cornered herself; she would've escaped from the hallway.": '如果凶手是 Katei，那确实说得通。可如果是我把 Naomi 追到这里，我想把她推到这面墙上可没那么容易。她只会比我更靠里，那我推她撞上的，就该是另外三面墙之一。{w} 更别提，她根本不会跑进一间屋子把自己逼进死角——她大可以从走廊逃走。',
        'Atsuki, stop trying to find nonexistent ways out. You are the one who killed Naomi.': 'Atsuki，别再找那些根本不存在的出路了。{w}杀死 Naomi 的人，就是你。',
        "Because I saw him! After Naomi left, when she understood that I wasn't buying it, I heard a noise. In this hallway, B, I saw Atsuki.": '因为我亲眼看见他了！{w}Naomi 走后——她明白我根本不信那套说辞——我听见了动静。就在这条 B走廊上，我看见了 Atsuki。',
        "Yes, this. Oh, it's a temperature regulator.": '嗯，这个。{w}哦，是温度调节器。',
        "I-It's here. I have no idea why, but it's here.": '它、它在这里。{w}我不知道为什么，但它就在这里。',
        'Without giving it much thought, I touched the surface of the egg-shaped object. A burst of heat flowed through my fingers, and the world broke.': '我没再多想，指尖触上了那枚蛋形物体的表面。{w}一股灼热穿过我的手指，随即，世界碎裂了。',
        "The burning sensation vanished, and I was no longer stretching out my arm. Before me was a long corridor that I'd seen before. My body froze, and I broke out in a cold sweat. A heavy cloak of confusion was cast on me as my heart took off like a rocket.": '灼烧感消失了，我的手臂也不再向前伸。眼前是一条我见过的长走廊。{w}我浑身僵住，冷汗直冒。浓重的困惑笼罩着我，心脏狂跳不止。',
        "...Was I knocked out? I had my back against the others when I reached for the Sekimeiya, but wouldn't I remember it? Wouldn't I feel pain in my head if I was hit?": '……我是被打晕了吗？{w}我伸手去够Sekimeiya的时候，背对着其他人，可要真挨了打，我总该记得吧？要是头上挨了一下，也该觉得疼啊？',
        "Then, I made my way to the offices to see if they weren't vacant for some reason. There was something I recognized in the first one.": '随后我去了办公区，看看那里是不是也空着。{w}第一间里有样我认得的东西。',
        "In the second and third partitions, my only company was a functioning camera recording my every movement. I sat on a chair and sighed deeply, unraveling at the sudden turn things had taken. Did we not have enough already? What the fuck had just happened!? My whole body hadn't stopped shaking for a second. I rejected the thought that any of it was real.": '在第二和第三个隔间里，陪着我的只有一台运转中的摄像头，记录着我的一举一动。{w}我在椅子上坐下，长长叹了口气，被这突如其来的变故弄得心乱如麻。我们遇到的麻烦还不够多吗？刚才到底他妈发生了什么！？我浑身抖个不停，一刻也没停过。我不肯相信这一切是真的。',
        'I left the offices once I felt ready to continue, but I was still hopeless. I was about to repeat my movements on the floors below when I heard a very distinguishable sound coming from my left.': '等我觉得自己能继续了，便离开办公区，可心里还是没底。{w}我正要下楼重复同样的搜索，左边忽然传来一个很容易辨认的声音。',
        'Completely unfazed, she opened the transparent door and entered the first partition. I was left outside, utterly bewildered. Without looking back, she stepped to the next door.': '她神色如常，推开那扇透明门走进了第一个隔间。我被撇在外面，彻底懵了。{w}她头也不回地走向下一扇门。',
        'There was nobody on the outer part of the fifth floor, so I looked through the partitions. The three of them were empty.': '五楼外侧空无一人，我便挨个查看隔间。{w}三间隔间里都没有人。',
        "I approached it, but I couldn't see what was behind it through the small gap. As I approached, I started to hear something. There were voices, ones that sounded shocked.": '我走近那扇门，可透过窄窄的门缝看不清里面的情形。{w}靠近时，我开始听到些动静，是说话声，语气里透着震惊。',
        "...Th-That's what it felt like.": '……{w}感、感觉就是这样。',
        "...You weren't here by that point yet, though. When I found myself in the lobby, I entered this room and only saw Naomi's body on the floor. I went up to the sixth floor to find you and eventually went back down. That's when I just found you here.": '……可那时候你们还没到这儿。等我回过神，人已经在大厅里了。我进了这个房间，只看见 Naomi 的尸体躺在地上。{w}我上六楼去找你们，后来又下来了。就是在那时，才在这里碰到你们。',
        '"To the past", right. That was the conclusion to draw from what I\'d said. Not only teleportation, but time travel too. It was a ridiculous claim even if they\'d really seen me disappear.': '「穿越到过去」，没错。按我刚才说的，只能得出这个结论。{w}不只是传送，更是时间穿越。就算他们真的亲眼看见我消失，这说法也荒唐得可笑。',
        "If I couldn't explain my own experience, did I have to assume that time traveling was possible? Had it been a factor the whole time? I thought about the full sequence of events up until that point. If they were somehow related to time travel, how were we supposed to think about that?": '既然我解释不了自己的遭遇，就非得认定时间穿越可行吗？它会不会从一开始就是整件事的一环？{w}我把此前发生的一切按顺序梳理了一遍。若这些事真与时间穿越有所牵连，我们又该怎么去看待？',
        "This cleanly holds up with what we experienced... At that point, the elevator was on the crystal floor, as it had probably arrived there when we'd heard it on the fifth. Then, when I went up to the sixth would be when Shiroya and I rushed to follow it up.": '这一点与我们经历过的完全对得上……那时电梯停在水晶层，大概是我们在五楼听见它时，它正好到了那里。{w}而 Shiroya 和我匆忙追着电梯上楼，就发生在我上到六楼的时候。',
        "...Even though I couldn't easily accept such a concept, it neatly explained many things. Was it all a ridiculous coincidence...? A trick, maybe?": '……虽然我无法轻易接受这种说法，但它确实把许多事情解释通了。{w}难道这一切都只是荒唐的巧合……？又或者，是某种把戏？',
        "But a line of reasoning that time traveling demolished was another one that it created. That was the can of worms that thinking about possibilities involving time travel opened. After all, I had randomly teleported to hallway A. Someone could've been on the same floor, killed Naomi before we'd thoroughly investigated it, and then traveled through time to an entirely different place.": '可时间穿越推翻了一条推论，却又造出了另一条。只要去设想时间穿越的种种可能，就会惹出这堆麻烦。{w} 毕竟，我是随机传送到 A走廊的。当时也许有人就在同一层，趁我们尚未彻底调查便杀了 Naomi，再穿越到完全不同的地方。',
        "Shut up. God. This is what Atsuki asked about earlier. It's a function to regulate the cabinet's temperature, is it not?": '闭嘴。天哪。{w} Atsuki 之前问的就是这个。那是用来调节展示柜温度的功能，不是吗？',
        'Holding the Sekimeiya in his hands, Sai closed the cabinet, which made a metallic sound as if it had locked automatically. Then, he left the room followed by Katei. Shiroya was still unsure of what to say, and Akaro and Erina both looked at me with uncertainty.': 'Sai 双手捧着 Sekimeiya，合上了展示柜。柜子发出金属声响，像是自动锁上了。随后他离开了房间，Katei 跟在后面。{w} Shiroya 仍不知道该说什么，Akaro 和 Erina 都带着不安看向我。',
        "We were in front of the event room. I squeezed my eyes shut and rubbed at the bridge of my nose, remembering that someone in the building had actually died. Things were moving too fast. A death, moving through time after touching a gem... But it would have been even more dangerous to stop thinking. Before I entered the room, I realized that something else went against the theory that Katei hadn't killed Naomi.": '我们站在活动室前。我闭上眼，揉了揉鼻梁，想起这栋楼里真的有人死了。事情发生得太快。一桩命案，一次触碰宝石后的穿越……{w} 可要是就此停下思考，只会更危险。进房间之前，我意识到还有一点与「Katei 没有杀 Naomi」的推论相悖。',
        "I couldn't know how it worked, but the fact that I'd seen it glowing might've indicated that nobody had traveled before me—that Katei was the only suspect. In addition, the Sekimeiya had been inside a locked cabinet. To travel and leave it inside, the culprit must've had to shut themselves inside it and then touch the Sekimeiya...": '我不知道它的原理，但我看见它发光这件事，或许说明在我之前没有人穿越过——Katei 是唯一的嫌疑人。{w} 此外，Sekimeiya 原本锁在展示柜里。凶手若想在穿越之后仍把它留在柜中，就只能把自己关进展示柜，再触碰 Sekimeiya……',
        'There was another problem, though. I didn\'t think about it until we\'d all entered the room. "Touching the Sekimeiya made me travel to the past". Ignoring how an item with such an obvious power could\'ve made it to a place where they\'d let us touch it, something directly contradicted its powers.': '不过，还有另一个问题。直到我们全都进了房间，我才想到。{w}「触碰 Sekimeiya 让我穿越到了过去」。先不说一件拥有如此明显力量的物品，怎么会出现在允许我们触碰它的地方——有一点直接与它的力量相矛盾。',
        "He handed me the gray gemstone. I felt no burn, and I remained where I was. However, I was able to appreciate the smooth surface of the Sekimeiya, which definitely hadn't disappeared with its beautiful white.": '他把那颗灰色宝石递给我。{w} 我没有感到灼痛，也没有离开原地。不过，我还能摸到 Sekimeiya 光滑的表面——它并没有随着那片漂亮的白色一起消失。',
        'I s—': '我正——{w=0.3}{nw}',
        "What are you doing? Someone look at hallway A too! The staircase is there, so we can't all leave from here.": '你们在干什么？也得有人去 A走廊看看！{w}楼梯在那边，不能所有人都走这边。',
        "Oh, my friend Atsuki? That's good. Say, did Katei look at any room all by himself?": '哦，是我的朋友 Atsuki 啊？那就好。{w}对了，有没有哪间房是 Katei 一个人查的？',
        "Erina and Isla stayed where they were. That was the safest option up until that point, but as things were, staying in an uncertain spot such as the stairs was more dangerous than moving through an empty floor. It was something Erina must not have realized, but her demeanor was clear: she wasn't leaving Isla alone. Nonetheless, the rest of us agreed and entered the event room once again.": 'Erina 和 Isla 留在了原地。在那之前，这是最稳妥的选择，但照现在的情况，待在楼梯这种情况不明的地方，反而比穿过空荡的楼层更危险。Erina 大概没意识到这一点，可她的态度很明确：她不会把 Isla 一个人留下。{w} 剩下的人也都同意，再次走进了活动室。',
        "Atsuki doesn't have a motive. Please, stop accusing him... There's so much blood, so this is where everything happened, and to do this to someone in front of a camera... You'd need to have a real reason for it. We need to find the person who did this to Naomi. They made that noise earlier... L-Look at Naomi's face. She must've been terrified, and being afraid of this happening might even be why she hid from us.": 'Atsuki 没有动机，请你别再怀疑他了……这里血这么多，说明一切就发生在这儿；而且还是在镜头前对人下这种狠手……没有充分的理由，谁做得出来。{w}我们得找到对 Naomi 下手的凶手。刚才那阵动静就是那个人弄出来的……{w}你、你看 Naomi 的脸。她当时一定怕极了；也许正因为害怕会遭这种事，她才一直躲着我们。',
        "Were we going to find anyone a second time? It must've been almost 11:00, implying that someone might've been able to remain unseen for two full hours.": '这次还能再找到人吗？时间应该快到 {time=11} 了，也就是说，有人可能整整两个小时都没被任何人看见。',
        "Were we going to find anyone a second time? It must've been almost 11 a.m., implying that someone might've been able to remain unseen for two full hours.": '这次还能再找到人吗？时间应该快到 {time=11} 了，也就是说，有人可能整整两个小时都没被任何人看见。',
        "You think so...? You definitely brought him there a few times. Maybe I left something there too. Now I want to go even more. Katei didn't mention a cabin in his story, but I'd be shocked if it was the same place. There are probably a few similar fields on that mountain.": '会吗……？你确实带他去过几次。说不定我也在那儿落下了什么。这下我更想去了。{w}Katei 讲的事里没提到木屋，不过要真是同一个地方，我可要吃惊了。那座山上大概有好几片相似的草地。',
        "...Huh? I don't know. It's kind of unbelievable... Do you think you did?": '……诶？我不知道。这事有点难以置信……{w}你自己觉得呢？',
        "If anyone else said that, I would've left it open for doubt. Someone else could deliberately lie to make me think I'd teleported when they knew what actually happened. But I had to take Shiroya's experience at face value. If I intended to think of an alternative to time travel, I had to factor in her viewpoint as well.": '换作别人这么说，我还会有所怀疑。对方也许明知真相，却故意骗我，让我以为自己被传送了。{w}但 Shiroya 的亲身经历，我不能不当真。若想找出时间穿越之外的另一种解释，我就必须把她的视角也算进去。',
        'When I went to look inside the mechanical room, Katei, Erina, and Isla were looking at hallway A. During that time, they had the chance to enter the event room. Although it would imply that they were either working together or threatened into silence.': '我去查看机械室的时候，Katei、Erina 和 Isla 正看着 A走廊。那段时间里，他们有机会进入活动室。{w}只不过这样一来，就说明他们要么是同伙，要么是被威胁封了口。',
        "So, in the end, the only possibilities are that either Katei and Erina are the culprits, worked with them, or were forced to keep quiet. ...Nobody could've hidden it in the storeroom without being seen by both of them... and Isla too, I suppose.": '也就是说，到头来只有几种可能：要么 Katei 和 Erina 就是凶手，要么他们跟凶手联手，要么他们被迫闭嘴。{w}……毕竟不管是谁，都没法在他们两人的眼皮底下把东西藏进储藏室……我想，还有 Isla。',
        "That's the only way I can think of, but it's not really possible. Technically, Sai could have hidden the Sekimeiya in his hip pack. However, we talked for a bit before he went to examine hallway A, and his back was facing us when he entered the two rooms there.": '我能想到的只有这一种，可实际上行不通。严格来说，Sai 可以把 Sekimeiya 藏进腰包里。{w}但在他去查看 A走廊之前，我们还聊了一会儿；而他走进那两个房间时，是背对着我们的。',
        "You're probably right. He wouldn't have any other way to keep it hidden. ...So the only possibility is that Katei and Erina did it while you weren't there.": '你说得大概没错。他也没有别的办法把它藏起来。{w}……那就只剩一种可能：是 Katei 和 Erina 趁你不在时动的手。',
        "I think so... They must've had the key before we found Naomi, and only Katei could've killed her. However, Katei can't be responsible just by himself since he wouldn't have been able to get the Sekimeiya before I went to the mechanical room. By that point, he was already with Erina and Isla.": '我想是的……他们一定在发现 Naomi 之前就已经有钥匙了，而能杀她的只有 Katei。{w}可是单凭 Katei 一个人不行，因为在我去机械室之前，他拿不到 Sekimeiya。那时候他已经和 Erina、Isla 在一起了。',
        "When I left the mechanical room, Erina told me that nothing had happened. So she was either working with Katei, or she was threatened to keep quiet. Nothing works involving someone from hallway B acting on their own, and the only other possibility could be an extra person threatening Erina and Katei to keep quiet. You were with your group in hallway C when you finished, so it's unlikely that person came down from a higher floor. They might've been in one of the hallway A rooms we checked.": '我离开机械室时，Erina 告诉我什么都没发生。所以，她要么和 Katei 是同伙，要么是被威胁封了口。B走廊的人单独行动怎么都说不通，唯一的另一种可能，就是有第三个人威胁 Erina 和 Katei 闭嘴。{w}你们搜查结束时，你和同伴都在 C走廊，所以那个人不太可能是从更高楼层下来的。他或许就藏在我们查过的某个 A走廊房间里。',
        "Hm... Someone else was definitely on that floor, right? So that shouldn't be impossible.": '嗯……{w}那一层确实还有别人吧？那样的话，也不算不可能。',
        "But let's assume the culprit wanted to hide it in the storeroom, whatever their reason. If they truly did it with the time travel that occurs upon touching the Sekimeiya, it follows that in the future, they'll have access to it. So someone could be ready to go to the past and hide it in the storeroom right this moment. They might intend to make it out of here with the Sekimeiya in some way.": '不过，先假设犯人出于某种理由，想把它藏进储藏室。如果真是靠触碰 Sekimeiya 时发生的时间穿越办到的，那么在未来，他们就能拿到它。{w} 也就是说，此刻可能正有人准备回到过去，把它藏进储藏室。他们或许打算以某种方式带着 Sekimeiya 离开这里。',
        "Then, they appeared inside the event room from the future. I don't know what could determine the position you teleport to, because I appeared in hallway A when I hadn't been there twenty minutes before, but if the culprit touches the Sekimeiya while holding the cabinet key, they could appear inside the event room with it.": '接着，他们从未来出现在活动室里。{w} 我不知道传送的落点由什么决定——我明明二十分钟前不在 A走廊，却还是出现在了那里；不过，如果犯人握着展示柜钥匙触碰 Sekimeiya，就有可能带着它一起出现在活动室。',
        "Once we were all in hallway C, they got out of the event room and left it in the storeroom while they hid elsewhere. If they had already lived through that portion of time, they could've known the entire sequence of events—that they would be safe in the event room until we found the Sekimeiya. But then they'd also know that it would be found right away, so why bother doing all this?": '等我们全都进了 C走廊，他们便离开活动室，把东西留在储藏室，自己躲到别处。{w} 如果他们早已经历过那段时间，就可能知道整串事件的走向——知道自己在活动室里一直安全，直到我们找到 Sekimeiya。可这样一来，他们也该知道东西马上就会被发现，那又何必费这么多功夫？',
        "But the person who lured us out of the event room would've had to go up the floors before traveling to the past, and they can't disappear from there since the Sekimeiya's still on the crystal floor. ...Once again, though, the attic makes it possible.": '可是，把我们引出活动室的人若想回到过去，必须先上楼；而既然 Sekimeiya 还在水晶层，他们就不可能从楼上消失。{w} ……不过，话又说回来，阁楼让这一切成为可能。',
        'Following the out of place sigh, he walked up to the elevator and pressed the button to call it. After a few seconds, the orange light surrounding the button told us that it had arrived, and Sai immediately grabbed the handle.': '那声突兀的叹气过后，他走到电梯前，按下呼叫按钮。{w} 几秒后，按钮周围的橙光亮起，说明电梯已经到了，Sai 立刻抓住了门把手。',
        "...I'd strongly recommend that none of you touch it. It was originally installed knowing Xyn could try to secure the elevator, but there's no point in that now, and we left up clear instructions. If you press it as the elevator is moving, it won't move again until permission is granted from outside, and given communication has been temporarily disabled, I fear nothing could be done until the exit unlocks.": '……我强烈建议你们谁都别碰它。当初设置它，是考虑到 Xyn 可能会试图控制电梯；可现在已没有那个必要，我们也留下了明确的说明。{w} 如果在电梯运行时按下它，电梯在获得外部许可前都不会再动；而通讯眼下已被暂时切断，恐怕在出口解锁之前，谁也做不了什么。',
        "No. That whole process would've taken even longer. If it wasn't on the fifth floor, the only way I could get the time I counted is if the door was open before I called it. This is kind of batshit, but if someone kept the door open upstairs and closed it a few seconds after I called it, it would've started to go down later than I expected. That would have made it seem like it was higher.": '不对。那样一来，整个过程只会更久。{w}如果它本来不在五楼，我数出的这个时间，唯一的可能就是：我按按钮之前，门就已经开着了。{w}这话听着有点离谱，但假如楼上有人一直开着门，等我按了按钮几秒后才关上，那它开始下降的时间就比我预计的要晚。这样一来，看起来就像它原本停在更高的楼层。',
        "If anyone above me used it, I wouldn't have heard them calling it. The strange thing is that I heard it three times, and I'm sure of that. This is the inconsistency here: even if someone above me used it, it would not have ended up on the fifth floor because I heard it three times.": '要是我上面有人用它，我不会听见他们按按钮的声音。可怪的是我确实听见了三次，这点我敢肯定。{w}矛盾就在这儿：即便上面有人用过它，它也不该停在五楼，因为我听见它响了三次。',
        "It couldn't have been on the fifth floor, right? It was on one of the first two. Why would someone move it like that when all it does is reveal them?": '它不可能停在五楼吧？它本来在一楼或二楼中的某一层。{w} 这么做只会暴露自己，谁会干这种事？',
        "Maybe it really was on the fifth floor... It's not completely impossible. You heard it three times, Sai, and that put it below you. When we all came back here, someone got out and sent it up to the fifth before we called it. We wouldn't have heard it no matter where it was.": '说不定它真的一直在五楼……也不是完全没可能。{w} Sai，你听见了三次，那就说明它当时在你下面。等我们都回到这里，有人出了电梯，赶在我们叫它之前把它送上了五楼。这样一来，不管它停在哪儿，我们都听不到。',
        "Nobody saw the elevator stopping on their floor, but that's fine if he stopped here. I heard it three times no matter what happened, so that means it went down at least once. Since Erina and Isla didn't see anyone coming out, the times it went down must've been to the crystal floor. Afterward, Katei took it back up, to the sixth. He knew it should've initially been on the fifth, so he sent it back there.": '没人看见电梯在自己那一层停下，不过要是他停在这一层，那也说得通。不管怎样，我听见它响了三次，说明它至少下去过一次。既然 Erina 和 Isla 都没看见有人出来，那它下去的时候一定是去了水晶层。{w} 之后，Katei 又把它开回六楼。他知道电梯原本该停在五楼，于是又把它送回了五楼。',
        "If it was someone else, there's one extremely tight explanation: unless someone is still working with the culprit, they would need to have been inside the elevator from the beginning. The elevator would've been below me and not where it was left, but then all its movements become useless.": '要是另有其人，那只有一种解释，而且条件极其苛刻：除非还有人跟犯人串通，否则那个人从一开始就得待在电梯里。{w} 可那样电梯就会一直在我下方，而不是停在原来被留下的位置；这样一来，它所有的移动就都白费了。',
        "You might just be mistaken about the goal. Yes, if they wanted to come down here, there was no reason to ever send the elevator up. There's not much reason for someone to stay down here, though. What you heard could've been someone going up to the attic. They get to hole up there and nobody sees anyone coming out.": '也许只是你把目的想错了。的确，如果那人想来这一层，就没必要把电梯往上叫。不过，也没什么理由让人待在这一层。{w} 你听见的，可能是有人上阁楼去了。只要人躲在阁楼里，就谁也不会看见有人出来。',
        "I guess so... Meaning that it's really difficult to explain this unless one of us is lying.": '大概吧……{w} 也就是说，除非我们之中有人在撒谎，否则这件事很难解释得通。',
        'I could suppose that someone was inside the elevator on the crystal floor and went to the attic. Then, the same person time traveled to the crystal floor. They wanted to go to the attic again, so they called the elevator and went back up. It had significant risk, but it was another way to justify the likely truth of being lied to.': '我可以这样假设：有人在水晶层进了电梯，上到阁楼。随后，同一个人穿越时间，回到了水晶层。因为想再去阁楼，就叫来电梯又上去了一趟。{w} 这样做风险不小，但也能从另一个角度印证：我们很可能确实被骗了。',
        'Sai looked at his watch and turned his wrist to show us the time. It was 11:20, and right above it, the date was also shown: 2011-12-15.': 'Sai 看了看表，把手腕转过来给我们看时间。上面显示 {time=11:20}，正上方还标着日期：2011-12-15。',
        'Sai looked at his watch and turned his wrist to show us the time. It was 11:20 a.m., and right above it, the date was also shown: 2011-12-15.': 'Sai 看了看表，把手腕转过来给我们看时间。上面显示 {time=11:20}，正上方还标着日期：2011-12-15。',
        "Isla didn't object. She already understood that we weren't playing around. The procedure of opening every room started once again.": 'Isla 没有反对。她早已明白，我们不是在闹着玩。{w}于是，我们又开始逐个开门检查了。',
        "We didn't relent despite quickly running out of rooms. The last time we'd gotten complacent, a body had suddenly appeared. The event room, acting as the midpoint of the hallway, still stored the Sekimeiya. ...If a culprit remained with us, they were trapped within the few last rooms.": '能查的房间很快见了底，我们却没有松劲。上次正是因为松懈，尸体才忽然出现。{w}位于走廊中段的活动室里仍存放着 Sekimeiya。……如果凶手还混在我们中间，那他就被困在最后这几间房里了。',
        "Wait... We're forgetting one place again.": '等等……{w}我们又漏掉了一个地方。',
        'Are we? ...Oh, right. The bathrooms.': '漏了吗？{w}……哦，对了，厕所。',
        'Then, Sai grabbed the opposite knob and turned it to open its door. ...He seemed to be having trouble.': '接着，Sai 握住另一扇门的把手，想要拧开。{w}{w=0.5}……他似乎拧不动。',
        "I-I suppose there must be. Hey! Open the door, you don't have any way to escape!": '大、大概吧。{w}喂！开门，你逃不掉的！',
        "Katei sighed and inserted the key. It turned, showing that he'd picked the correct one. The door made a clearly audible sound, and Katei proceeded to gently open it.": 'Katei 叹了口气，把钥匙插了进去。钥匙转动了，说明他选对了。{w} 门发出一声清晰可闻的响动，随后 Katei 轻轻把门推开。',
        "We all must've experienced a strong feeling of déjà vu. On the floor of the men's bathroom lay Naomi's unmoving body.": '我们所有人一定都产生了强烈的既视感。{w} 男洗手间的地板上，躺着 Naomi 一动不动的尸体。',
        "It felt like a pointless attempt, but I crouched to check Naomi's pulse like Sai did the first time. I felt nothing.": '我知道这多半是徒劳，但还是蹲下去探了探 Naomi 的脉搏，就像 Sai 第一次那样。{w} 我什么也没摸到。',
        "There are two more things that don't hold up. The clothes are the first. If Naomi's body traveled to the past, her clothes would've been stained with blood, just like they were at the time it traveled. And second: you all saw me vanish when it happened to me, right? If the same thing happened to Naomi, the first body should've disappeared.": '还有两点说不通。{w}第一是衣服。如果 Naomi 的尸体穿越到了过去，衣服上应该带着穿越那一刻的血迹。{w}第二：那件事发生在我身上时，你们都亲眼看到我消失了吧？如果 Naomi 也一样，那第一具尸体就该消失了。',
        '"What if the replica of the body only takes into consideration the state of the body in the past?" With the way I\'d traveled, I couldn\'t be sure whether my then-present body had teleported into the past, or if the body I\'d arrived in was identical to how it was at the point in time I appeared.': '「如果复制出的尸体只还原它在过去那一时刻的状态呢？」{w} 以我自己的穿越经历，我分不清到底是当时那具身体穿越回了过去，还是我抵达的那具身体，状态和我出现那一刻一模一样。',
        "Hm, that's interesting. She has a bump on the back of her head. It's similar to her other body, but blood's not coming out of this one.": '嗯，有意思。{w}她后脑上有一块肿包。和她另一具身体的情况相似，可这具没有流血。',
        "...Is that so? Then this body isn't the same as when she was alive despite the lack of blood.": '……是吗？{w}那么，这具尸体虽然没流血，状态却和她活着时并不一样。',
        "I won't allow that. I couldn't stop you from getting it out, but you only proved that the Sekimeiya isn't at all related to what's going on. Put it back in.": '我不允许。{w}我拦不住你们把它取出来，可你们恰恰证明了 Sekimeiya 与眼下的状况毫无干系。放回去。',
        "But I can't think we would've found someone there so easily. First, it would mean that they have another key. Second, they hid there knowing we had access to it. Third, they didn't take this key from Naomi. ...And yet the one for the cabinet was taken.": '但我不觉得我们能那么轻易就在那儿找到人。第一，那意味着他们另有一把钥匙；第二，他们明知我们能进去，却还是躲在那里；第三，他们没有从 Naomi 身上拿走这把钥匙。{w}……可展示柜的钥匙却被拿走了。',
        "If he is in danger, he will be even if we search for him. If he walked away by himself, he wouldn't let us just find him again, and if the culprit took him, they've been dodging us for quite a while. This is the first time we've been in this situation and have access to the attic, so we should go there first. Afterward, we'll move down if we haven't found him.": '他要是真有危险，就算我们去找，他也一样有危险。如果是他自己走开的，就不会让我们轻易找到；如果是凶手把他带走的，那对方已经躲了我们这么久。{w}这是我们头一回既碰上这种局面，又能进阁楼，所以该先去那儿。之后要是还没找到他，我们再往下走。',
        '...Fine. He better have a very good reason if he separated from us on purpose.': '……{w}好吧。他要是故意离开我们，最好有个像样的理由。',
        "Seriously? That's very strange... I'm not sure you understand how restricted that place is. I'm not certain we should even go.": '真的？这可太奇怪了……{w} 你们恐怕不明白那地方管得有多严。我甚至不确定我们该不该去。',
        "He closed the elevator again. We'd gotten used to the crystal floor searches, so it didn't feel like an imposing task anymore. Erina and Isla remained where they'd been while the rest of us chose individual rooms to look through, including the bathrooms and the mechanical room. Every single one of them was empty, so we reunited by the stairs.": '他重新把电梯门关上。水晶层的搜索我们已经习惯了，不再觉得是什么难事。Erina 和 Isla 留在原处，其余人各自挑了房间查看，连卫生间和机械室也没放过。{w} 每一间都是空的，我们于是回到楼梯旁会合。',
        "Without wasting time, we moved through the floors to reach the sixth. It was surreal not having Akaro with us. Naomi's second appearance eclipsed the oddity of his disappearance, but it was also something that I couldn't even begin to understand.": '我们没多耽搁，一路穿过各层，来到了六楼。{w} Akaro 不在身边，这种感觉很不真实。Naomi 的第二次出现盖过了他失踪的诡异，可那本身也是我完全无法理解的事。',
        '"The Sekimeiya didn\'t work for us earlier, so a lot of this isn\'t adding up." Sai implied that the Sekimeiya must\'ve caused Akaro\'s disappearance, but there was an important discrepancy: it was shut behind the glass. If it was involved, it worked in a way beyond what we knew.': '「方才 Sekimeiya 对我们毫无反应，所以很多地方都对不上。」{w} Sai 话里的意思是，Akaro 的失踪必定出自 Sekimeiya 之手，可这里有个重要的矛盾：它当时还锁在玻璃罩内。若它真的参与其中，那起作用的方式也超出了我们的认知。',
        "We might. I'm advising you all not to keep going. It's a restricted area, and I doubt Ashiya will be understanding even if our circumstances require this.": '也许会。我是在劝你们别再往前了。{w} 那是禁区，就算我们是迫不得已，恐怕芦屋也不会通融。',
        "Three, in fact. One more was being carried by the person holding the stolen gemstones. And no, I don't recognize it at all. More importantly, what is it doing here?": '其实有三只。还有一只由那个拿着失窃宝石的人提着。而且，我完全不认识它。{w} 更要紧的是，它怎么会在这儿？',
        "...Honestly, I have no idea. I'm not sure why they'd bring this here, no matter what its contents were. If they wanted to leave it behind, they could've done so downstairs, which is what we thought they did.": '……{w}说实话，我完全想不通。不管里面装的是什么，我都想不出他们为什么要把这东西带上来。要是想丢下它，在楼下丢掉就行——我们本来也是这么以为的。',
        "...The more I stared at the footprints, the more I doubted whether they were facing the way I was thinking. I wasn't sure anymore, but I was confident that only one pair of shoes had left them.": '……{w}脚印看得越久，我越怀疑它们的朝向是不是跟我想的一样。我已经拿不准了，但有一点我可以肯定：留下它们的只有一双鞋。',
        'Hm... Who did you steal those from?': '嗯……{w}你这是从谁那儿偷来的？',
        'Sai moved to the television and tried to power it on. Nothing happened.': 'Sai 走到电视机前，试着开机。{w}什么反应也没有。',
        "I guess this is broken, seeing as it's plugged in. ...Anyway, let's look around the area.": '插着电却开不了，看来是坏了。{w}……算了，我们在这一带看看。',
        "If this is what happened, Naomi must've traveled here while she was holding the suitcase—before we found it on the crystal floor. That would mean two Naomis have existed for quite a while, and that not only did we miss both of them, they were also killed. And let me tell you, there are some pesky contradictions down that line of thought. First, during the time Naomi could've been holding the suitcase, the Sekimeiya was in its cabinet. It wasn't locked inside, but we touched it and nothing happened to us. If that's how she time traveled up here, it again begs the question of why it worked for her.": '如果真是这样，那 Naomi 一定是拿着手提箱穿越到这里的——就在我们在水晶层发现那只手提箱之前。也就是说，有两个 Naomi 同时存在了相当长一段时间；而我们不仅两个都没撞见，她们还都被杀了。{w} 不过我得说，这条思路上有几个挺麻烦的矛盾。第一，在 Naomi 可能拿着手提箱的那段时间里，Sekimeiya 一直在展示柜里。它并没有被锁在柜子里，可我们碰过它，却什么也没发生。如果她就是那样穿越上来的，那问题又回来了：为什么偏偏对她起了作用？',
        "I'm not wrong, right? If Naomi touched it while it was out of the cabinet, we would've found it outside. The next contradiction is what we talked about earlier: Naomi would've disappeared upon traveling, so we couldn't have found her corpse and the suitcase twice.": '我没说错吧？如果 Naomi 是在它离开展示柜时碰了它，那我们本该在柜外发现它。{w} 下一个矛盾就是我们之前谈过的：Naomi 一穿越就会消失，那她的尸体和手提箱就不可能被我们发现两次。',
        'Incorrect, I think. Remember what Katei said after we got the Sekimeiya out of the cabinet?': '我觉得不对。{w} 你还记得我们把 Sekimeiya 从展示柜里拿出来之后，Katei 说了什么吗？',
        "Since the footprints are all similar, there's only one other explanation that makes sense to me: she had the key and exited the room. Either before or after all this, she entered the attic again and went straight to the hallway. But the footprints were all in similar condition, so there must not have been a lot of time between them. I'm not sure why she'd enter again only to use the elevator and go down. ...If she didn't want to be noticed, the elevator noise wouldn't do her any favors.": '既然这些脚印的状况都差不多，那在我看来，就只有另一种解释说得通了：她带着钥匙，离开了房间。在这之前或之后，她又进了阁楼，径直走向走廊。{w} 可所有脚印的新旧都相差无几，说明中间隔的时间并不长。我不明白她为什么又进来一趟，只为坐电梯下楼。……如果她不想被人发现，电梯的动静可帮不上她半点忙。',
        "She thought she'd have her keys, then...? Maybe she didn't know that much about the Sekimeiya even though she used it so early on. I think that makes the most sense. She would be the second Naomi we found. I still don't understand how we missed her if she was the one who took the elevator down, or who killed her, but the truth is that we didn't find any keys on her body.": '她以为自己还带着钥匙，结果……？也许她虽然很早就用上了 Sekimeiya，对它却了解不多。{w} 我觉得这样最说得通。她应该就是我们发现的第二个 Naomi。如果坐电梯下楼的人是她，我到现在还是想不通我们怎么会漏掉她；也还是想不通是谁杀了她。但事实就是，她身上没有钥匙。',
        "The fifth floor wasn't any different. Even though we believed that Akaro and whoever the culprit was had to be somewhere in the tower, they would never remain on an office floor if they intended to hide. Since we knew that, the most important reason why we were following that procedure was to isolate the crystal floor and be able to thoroughly look there once again.": '五楼也没什么两样。尽管我们相信 Akaro 和真凶一定还在塔里的某处，可他们若想藏身，绝不会留在办公楼层。{w} 正因为如此，我们走这套流程最重要的目的，是把水晶层隔离出来，好在那里再彻底搜查一遍。',
        "As soon as we peeked inside, we knew we'd been right: the door had been opened farther. Next to Naomi's body was the toilet, and on top of it, Akaro sat, focusing his gaze on the wall in front of him. When he noticed us, he slowly turned his head to the door and stood up.": '我们往里一探，就知道果然没错：门被推得更开了。Naomi 的尸体旁边是马桶，Akaro 就坐在上面，目光直直盯着面前的墙。{w} 察觉到我们，他缓缓把头转向门口，站了起来。',
        '...He barely reacted to our presence. ...He slowly turned his head again and spent a few seconds in silence until he acknowledged us.': '……{w}他对我们的到来几乎没有反应。{w}……他又缓缓转过头，沉默了几秒，才总算理会了我们。',
        "What? It's {time=11:36.}": '什么？{w} 现在是 {time=11:36.}。',
        "What?{w} It's 11:36.": '什么？{w} 现在是 {time=11:36.}。',
        "What? It's 11:36.": '什么？{w} 现在是 {time=11:36.}。',
        "What?{w} It's 11:36 a.m.": '什么？{w} 现在是 {time=11:36.}。',
        "What? It's 11:36 a.m.": '什么？{w} 现在是 {time=11:36.}。',
        "11:36. So it had been sixteen minutes since we'd heard the noise in the event room. It felt like more time had passed since the contents of those minutes had been dense, but it didn't seem wrong.": '{time=11:36.} 也就是说，从我们听到活动室传来声响算起，已经过了十六分钟。那段时间里发生的事太多，感觉上不止过了这么久，但细想也并不矛盾。',
        "11:36 a.m. So it had been sixteen minutes since we'd heard the noise in the event room. It felt like more time had passed since the contents of those minutes had been dense, but it didn't seem wrong.": '{time=11:36.} 也就是说，从我们听到活动室传来声响算起，已经过了十六分钟。那段时间里发生的事太多，感觉上不止过了这么久，但细想也并不矛盾。',
        "11:36, I see. Of course, it appears you were wrong, Atsuki. We didn't travel through time...": '{time=11:36}，原来如此。看来你确实弄错了，Atsuki。我们并没有时间穿越……',
        "11:36 a.m., I see. Of course, it appears you were wrong, Atsuki. We didn't travel through time...": '{time=11:36}，原来如此。看来你确实弄错了，Atsuki。我们并没有时间穿越……',
        "It doesn't make sense. I thought about it earlier. If you touched the Sekimeiya, why was it shut in the cabinet after you disappeared?": '这说不通。我之前就想过。{w}如果你碰过 Sekimeiya，那你消失之后，它为什么还锁在展示柜里？',
        "Huh...? I don't know.": '咦……？{w}我不知道。',
        "I had no idea how to interpret what he was saying. At my side, Naomi's body rested under a beautiful cloth that practically occupied the entire bathroom floor. Given the surroundings, it wasn't the most respectful thing, but we couldn't do much else for her.": '我完全不知道该如何理解他的话。{w}我身旁，Naomi 的遗体躺在一块几乎铺满整个浴室地面的漂亮遮布下。受条件所限，这算不上多么体面的做法，可我们能为她做的也只有这些了。',
        "Had Akaro really only teleported without moving through time? I kept circling around that detail. Since we knew barely anything about the mechanism behind the Sekimeiya, I couldn't definitely object. However, I estimated that I went about twenty minutes to the past. If that was variable, it was possible Akaro hadn't realized he'd gone less than a minute to the past thanks to the time on Sai's wristwatch.": 'Akaro 真的只是传送，而没有穿越时间吗？这个细节在我脑中反复打转。{w}我们对 Sekimeiya 背后的原理几乎一无所知，我自然没法断定这不可能。但按我的估计，我大约回到了二十分钟之前。不过，要是穿越的幅度并不固定，那 Akaro 也可能只是看了 Sai 手表上的时间，却没意识到自己其实只回到了不到一分钟前。',
        'Yes... I hate waking up so early. Mom made me set my alarm to 6:00.': '嗯……我最讨厌起这么早了。妈妈非要我把闹钟定在 {time=6.}。',
        'Yes... I hate waking up so early. Mom made me set my alarm to 6 a.m.': '嗯……我最讨厌起这么早了。妈妈非要我把闹钟定在 {time=6.}。',
        "I prefer them pan-seared. Why are you all on the bed? We didn't inspect this floor that thoroughly, so you should be looking for clues.": '我倒更喜欢煎的。{w}你们都赖在床上干什么？这一层我们还没仔细查过，该去找线索才对。',
        'When Shiroya pressed the "record" button, a message appeared. It said: "Delete previous recording before starting a new one". Instead of doing that, Shiroya selected the single audio track with the circle pad and pressed the play button.': 'Shiroya 按下「录音」键，屏幕上跳出一行提示：「删除已有录音后方可开始新录音」。{w} 她没有照做，而是用圆形摇杆选中了唯一的那段音频，按下播放键。',
        'A time bar appeared on the screen. Static started playing immediately, and we frowned, waiting for something else to happen. On the screen, the seconds ticked up for a while as the static went on. ...Were we hearing footsteps? Eventually, that noise was interrupted by a very loud one. It sounded as if someone had sat right next to us. Then, that person heaved a sigh, and as soon as they started speaking, we recognized who they were.': '屏幕上出现了一条时间轴。沙沙的电流声随即响起，我们皱起眉，等着别的动静。{w} 杂音持续着，屏幕上的秒数一点点往上跳。……那是脚步声吗？{w} 不久，杂音被一声巨响打断，听起来就像有人在我们旁边坐了下来。接着，那人长叹一口气，刚一开口，我们就听出那是谁。',
        '...Where am I...?': '……{w}我这是……在哪儿？',
        "Huh...? I've never... done this.": '咦……？{w}我从来没……做过这种事。',
        "I-Isla, what's gotten into you? ...What are you holding? And Erina, why aren't you doing anything!?": 'Isla，你、你这是怎么了？……你手里拿的是什么？{w} 还有 Erina，你怎么什么都不做！？',
        "With a final sob... the recording ended. The screen left us with a button to rewind the audio, and we remained motionless, with expressions we'd never worn before.": '随着最后一声啜泣……录音结束了。{w} 屏幕上只剩下一个倒回音频的按钮，我们一动不动，脸上挂着从未有过的神情。',
        'I believe we heard something else that stood out. Apart from what Isla said, the way Sai phrased it... "We might\'ve been here for more than a month." ...This "might\'ve" is very odd.': '我觉得还有一处很突兀。除了Isla说的那些，Sai的措辞……{w}「我们可能已经在这里待了一个多月。」{w}……这个「可能」很反常。',
        "...Isla, mind telling us the identity of your friend now? She could've had access to it, and somehow, she knew this incident would happen. Not only that, but she lied to you, right? About the number of people and when she said that nothing bad would happen.": '……{w}Isla，现在能告诉我们你那位朋友是谁了吗？她有可能接触过这支录音笔，而且不知怎么就知道会出事。不止如此，她还骗了你，对吧？人数上骗了你，还说不会出什么事。',
        "Holy shit, Katei. You know that you're fucked once we get out, right? You said that you work here with Naomi and that she tried to personally convince you of her innocence earlier because of that. ...But you didn't know what her job entailed?": '我靠，Katei。你知道出去以后你就完了，对吧？你说过你和Naomi在这里共事，还说她之前就是因为这个才亲自来找你、想让你相信她清白。{w}……可你竟然不知道她负责什么？',
        "The real suspect here is obviously Sai. Akaro couldn't have done anything with the key, but Sai could've unlocked the cabinet because he was outside the hallway B rooms during the search.": '这里真正可疑的显然是Sai。{w}Akaro就算拿到钥匙也做不了什么，可Sai能打开展示柜——搜查的时候，他人就在B走廊的房门外。',
        "Oh, yes. It's the key to this bedroom. The only one that remains. The other bedroom also has one, but the keys shouldn't be interchangeable.": '啊，认得。这是这间卧室的钥匙，仅剩的一把。{w}另一间卧室也有一把，不过两把钥匙应该不能通用。',
        "I wasn't sure what exactly he expected to find, but he went up the ladder. It wasn't so much that we were slacking off; rather, the recording had sapped every trace of our remaining initiative. I sat down again and blankly stared at my lap.": '我不确定他究竟指望找到什么，但他还是爬上梯子去了。我们倒也不是偷懒；那段录音把我们所剩的一点干劲都抽干了。{w}我重新坐下，茫然地望着自己的膝盖。',
        "My initial reaction was that not letting anyone else listen to the recording was the smarter choice. It would prevent fear, commotion, being suspected, and potentially falling into a trap. That just so happened to go along nicely with the way the universe seemed to function, as letting Sai or Akaro listen to the recording could've immediately made its own existence an impossibility.": '我最初的反应是，不让其他人听这段录音才是明智之举。这样能避免恐慌、骚动、被人怀疑，也能避免落入陷阱。{w}而这恰好与这个宇宙运作的方式不谋而合——一旦让Sai或Akaro听了录音，录音本身就可能立刻不复存在。',
        "I didn't want to believe it. It was a chilling thought in many ways. I had a dog and a cat to take care of. Being locked away for a month would end the worst way possible if the people outside neglected both them and us at the same time.": '我不愿相信。{w}这个念头在许多方面都叫人发寒。我家里还有一只狗和一只猫要照顾。要是被困上一个月，外面的人又同时不管它们和我们，那就真的糟透了。',
        "The first time it disappeared, the Sekimeiya was in a cabinet in the room where Naomi died. However, the cabinet in the event room hadn't been locked, so the key wasn't needed. Then, we split up between both hallways and the Sekimeiya was taken. That's when the key was used.": '它第一次消失时，Sekimeiya 就放在 Naomi 遇害那个房间的展示柜里。可活动室的展示柜当时没上锁，用不着钥匙。{w}后来我们分成两路去搜走廊，Sekimeiya 被人拿走了——那一次才用上了钥匙。',
        "...Later, when we returned from the higher floors without finding anyone, the Sekimeiya hadn't been stolen yet. It was still in the cabinet. ...And according to Sai, someone took the elevator down. I don't think the killer's intention was to take the Sekimeiya. If it had been, and they'd purposely removed the cabinet key from Naomi's set, they wouldn't have taken the Sekimeiya while we'd been searching both hallways. They would've waited for us to leave, and they wouldn't have dropped the key in your purse.": '……后来我们从楼上下来，一个人也没找到，那时 Sekimeiya 还没被拿走，仍然在展示柜里。……而且据 Sai 说，有人坐电梯下过楼。{w}我不认为凶手的目标是拿走 Sekimeiya。{w}若真是如此，对方又特意从 Naomi 的钥匙串上取下了展示柜的钥匙，就不会趁我们分头搜两条走廊的时候把 Sekimeiya 拿走。他会等我们离开，也不会把钥匙丢进你的包里。',
        "Yeah. The culprit spent time removing it from her set of keys but didn't take the attic key. All of us found Naomi's body at the same time, and even though I disappeared, you're positive nobody could've picked the key up before I came back, right?": '对。凶手花时间把钥匙从她的钥匙串上取了下来，却没有拿阁楼的钥匙。{w}我们发现 Naomi 尸体的时候大家都在场，而且就算我消失了一阵，你也很肯定在我回来之前没人能捡走那把钥匙，对吧？',
        "Akaro entered the room where Naomi died, but he couldn't have unlocked the cabinet. Sai, though, had the chance to do both things. If the search ended while one of them still had the key, they would've chosen to leave it in your purse because you were in their group. You also investigated hallway B, so if Sai hadn't denied it, you could've had a chance to get the key too.": 'Akaro 进过 Naomi 遇害的房间，但他不可能打开展示柜。Sai 却两件事都有机会做。如果搜查结束时钥匙还在他们某个人手上，他们会把钥匙留在你包里，因为你跟他们同组。{w}你也在 B走廊搜过，所以要不是 Sai 否认，你本来也有机会拿到那把钥匙。',
        "When the Sekimeiya was hidden in room B4, where we first found Naomi... It was hidden inside a temperature regulation cabinet, and that would have happened at a time where we didn't know that the cabinets had inner compartments yet.": 'Sekimeiya 最初被藏起来，是在水晶展室 B4——也就是我们第一次发现 Naomi 的地方……{w}它被藏进了一个控温展示柜，而当时我们还不知道这些柜子设有内层隔间。',
        "Anyone could've secretly known this, but think about Katei's perspective. Suripo told him that gemstones had been stolen from a room, and he didn't know which one. Therefore, he had no reason to think they had been gemstones on display instead of the ones kept in those inner compartments, right? ...But the first time we searched, he never looked in those or let us know about them.": '这事谁都可能私下知道，但站在 Katei 的立场想想。Suripo 只告诉他有间展室的宝石被偷了，却没说是哪一间。{w}那么他也没理由认为丢的是展出的宝石、而不是内层隔间里存放的那些，对吧？……可我们第一次搜查时，他从没去看过那些隔间，也没跟我们提过。',
        "...I'm already doubting what I said regarding the Sekimeiya's disappearance.": '……{w}我开始怀疑自己刚才关于 Sekimeiya 消失的那番话了。',
        "I said that if Naomi's killer took her key, they would've waited before taking the Sekimeiya; they wouldn't have done it while we were all searching the crystal floor. That's not definitely true, though. If Sai or Akaro took the key, they would've waited too.": '我说过，如果杀害 Naomi 的凶手拿走了她的钥匙，他应该会等到以后再拿 Sekimeiya，不会挑我们全都在水晶展室搜查的时候动手。{w}但这也不一定。换成 Sai 或 Akaro 拿了钥匙，他们同样会等。',
        "...Yeah. They would've kept the key until a better chance came.": '……{w}是啊。{w}{w=0.4} 他们会把钥匙留到更好的机会再动手。',
        "Right? But instead, the Sekimeiya was taken while the search was going on. Why? There has to be a reason why they didn't wait. After all, the fact that it happened during the search feels wrong, because it means that nobody who searched could've done it. How did they do it? Whoever hid the Sekimeiya took advantage of the search to appear clean—they didn't wait for a calmer opportunity.": '对吧？{w}可事实是，Sekimeiya 偏偏在搜查途中被拿走了。{w}为什么？他们之所以没等，一定有原因。{w}毕竟事情发生在搜查期间，这点很不对劲——那等于说，参与搜查的人都不可能下手。{w}那他们究竟是怎么做到的？藏起 Sekimeiya 的人借搜查洗清了自己，没有等更稳妥的时机。',
        "It's so confusing! People in both hallways could've worked together when I wasn't looking, but is that really it...? It doesn't make any sense! They rushed to hide the Sekimeiya in the storeroom, but they didn't rush to take it out of the cabinet the next time we left the crystal floor. In fact, it should still be there.": '太乱了！两条走廊上的人完全可能趁我不注意串通好，可真是这样吗……？{w}完全说不通！他们急着把 Sekimeiya 藏进储藏室，可下一次我们离开水晶展室时，他们却不急着把它从展示柜里取出来。照理说，它应该还在那儿才对。',
        "But then they wouldn't have relied on it to escape. If they used it, they must've known how to properly use it. There's still the same problem, though. The glass in the cabinet would have been down.": '可那样的话，他们就不会靠它逃走了。既然用了它，说明他们懂得怎么正确使用。{w} 不过老问题还在——展示柜的玻璃罩应该是放下来的。',
        "...No, I'd like to look for it. We were going to look through hallway B, so let's start with that. If we figure out how the Sekimeiya appeared in the storeroom, we might be able to find out who did it.": '……不用，我想找找看。{w} 我们本来就打算把 B走廊查一遍，就从那里开始吧。要是能弄清楚 Sekimeiya 是怎么出现在储藏室的，也许就能查出是谁干的。',
        'We walked to room B3 in silence... It was undeniable that staying put somewhere was much safer than being there by ourselves; someone had died, and we were up against an elusive unknown...': '我们沉默着走向水晶展室 B3……{w} 不可否认，待在原地比我们俩单独行动要安全得多。已经有人死了，而我们面对的是一个行踪难测的不明人物……',
        "After all, it made me travel through time. We hadn't spoken about it at length, but it was evident both of us wanted to understand how it worked...": '毕竟，它让我穿越了时间。{w} 这件事我们还没细谈过，但显然，我们俩都想弄明白它到底如何运作……',
        "Was another version of me... right outside the room? If we went to look and that version acted surprised to be found... assuming the past couldn't be changed and only looked at from a different perspective, it would mean that I needed to travel to the past and recreate a fake reaction.": '另一个我……就在房间外？{w} 要是我们出去查看，那个我装出被发现时很惊讶的样子……假设过去无法改变，只能换个角度去观察，那就意味着我得回到过去，把那个假反应重演一遍。',
        "Yeah. I'll wait here. I'm a little scared to touch it, but I think it's better if one of us stays here.": '嗯。{w} 我在这里等着。我有点怕碰它，不过我觉得还是留一个人待在这里比较好。',
        'I stretched my arm toward it. Hesitant at what was about to happen, Shiroya backed up while I shortened the distance between my hand and the Sekimeiya. As soon as I made the slightest physical contact with it, I felt a ridiculously painful burn on my fingers. It lasted less than a split second, and I was somewhere else.': '我朝它伸出手。Shiroya 似乎对即将发生的事有些迟疑，向后退开；我的手则一点点靠近 Sekimeiya。{w} 指尖刚触到它，一阵剧烈的灼痛便从手指上窜起。那感觉只持续了不到半瞬，下一刻，我已身在别处。',
        "It took me a few seconds to recognize where I was. In front of me were blank screens, and my surroundings were overall dim. It was the security room. My pose had also changed. I'd appeared in front of the desk and immediately fallen backward, hitting my back on the chair.": '我花了几秒钟才认出自己在哪。面前是一排黑着的屏幕，四周光线昏暗。这里是监控室。{w} 我的姿势也变了——我出现在桌前，随即向后摔倒，后背撞上了椅子。',
        'They all lit up at once, which made me squint momentarily. ...The large desktop appeared, but I only directed my eyes at the lower right side of the middle screen. {time=11:10} was the time that I saw.': '所有屏幕同时亮起，刺得我眯了眯眼。{w} ……整个桌面显现出来，我只把视线投向中间屏幕的右下角。{w} 上面显示的时间是 {time=11:10}。',
        'They all lit up at once, which made me squint momentarily.{w} ...The large desktop appeared, but I only directed my eyes at the lower right side of the middle screen.{w} 11:10 was the time that I saw.': '所有屏幕同时亮起，刺得我眯了眯眼。{w} ……整个桌面显现出来，我只把视线投向中间屏幕的右下角。{w} 上面显示的时间是 {time=11:10}。',
        'They all lit up at once, which made me squint momentarily. ...The large desktop appeared, but I only directed my eyes at the lower right side of the middle screen. 11:10 was the time that I saw.': '所有屏幕同时亮起，刺得我眯了眯眼。{w} ……整个桌面显现出来，我只把视线投向中间屏幕的右下角。{w} 上面显示的时间是 {time=11:10}。',
        'They all lit up at once, which made me squint momentarily.{w} ...The large desktop appeared, but I only directed my eyes at the lower right side of the middle screen.{w} 11:10 a.m. was the time that I saw.': '所有屏幕同时亮起，刺得我眯了眯眼。{w} ……整个桌面显现出来，我只把视线投向中间屏幕的右下角。{w} 上面显示的时间是 {time=11:10}。',
        'They all lit up at once, which made me squint momentarily. ...The large desktop appeared, but I only directed my eyes at the lower right side of the middle screen. 11:10 a.m. was the time that I saw.': '所有屏幕同时亮起，刺得我眯了眯眼。{w} ……整个桌面显现出来，我只把视线投向中间屏幕的右下角。{w} 上面显示的时间是 {time=11:10}。',
        "The last time we checked the time, Sai said it was 11:36, and he already confirmed to me that his time is the same as this computer's.": '上次看时间时，Sai 说当时是 {time=11:36}，而且他已经跟我确认过，他的时间和这台电脑一致。',
        "The last time we checked the time, Sai said it was 11:36 a.m., and he already confirmed to me that his time is the same as this computer's.": '上次看时间时，Sai 说当时是 {time=11:36}，而且他已经跟我确认过，他的时间和这台电脑一致。',
        'At this point in time, I should be on the fifth floor with Shiroya. At 11:20, we were all inside the event room after regrouping, discussing the elevator movements.': '此刻，我应该正和 Shiroya 在五楼。到了 {time=11:20}，我们已经重新会合，都在活动室里讨论电梯的异动。',
        'At this point in time, I should be on the fifth floor with Shiroya. At 11:20 a.m., we were all inside the event room after regrouping, discussing the elevator movements.': '此刻，我应该正和 Shiroya 在五楼。到了 {time=11:20}，我们已经重新会合，都在活动室里讨论电梯的异动。',
        "When we heard a noise... that's right! I can attempt to see what made it, and most importantly... what happened to Naomi.": '我们听到声响的时候……{w=0.5}对了！{w=0.4} 我可以试着去看看是什么弄出了那声响，更重要的是……{w} Naomi 到底出了什么事。',
        'Even though I was a fair distance away, I saw pure distress all over her. What had she experienced? Did she know her own body had been found? Was she aware of what would happen to her...?': '尽管隔着一段距离，我也能一眼看出她满心惶恐。她究竟经历了什么？她知不知道自己的尸体已经被发现了？{w}她清不清楚自己接下来会落得什么下场……？',
        "Naomi opened the door carefully, keeping her guard as high as it could've been. I bit my lip tightly. When the door was open, she looked inside.": 'Naomi 小心翼翼地推开门，戒备已经到了极点。{w}我用力咬住嘴唇。门一开，她就朝里面望去。',
        "Out of nowhere, Naomi's body was pulled from the inside. I felt as if my heart was pulled along with her. I couldn't see her anymore, and two people were in the bathroom, their figures hidden from me.": '冷不丁地，Naomi 的身体被从里面拽了进去。{w}我的心仿佛也跟着被拽走了。她的身影消失了，洗手间里有两个人，我却一个也看不见。',
        "The universe wouldn't allow me to change the past? That was ridiculous, and if anything, it was providing me with a way to do it. I bolted to the bathroom as fast as I could. I definitely still had time to change the past.": '宇宙不许我改变过去？荒唐。真要说的话，它反倒给了我改变过去的机会。{w}我拼尽全力冲向洗手间。我绝对还有时间改变过去。',
        "But that thought evaporated when I heard a sound in front of me. Before I could reach the bathroom, the door was forcefully shut from the inside and then locked. I recognized the sound as soon as I heard it: it was the one we'd heard from the event room.": '然而身前传来的一声响，让这个念头瞬间消散。{w}我还没跑到洗手间，门就从里面被用力关上，随后落了锁。那声音我一听就认了出来——正是我们在活动室里听到过的响动。',
        "I made it before I was spotted only because I'd reacted fast enough, but... it didn't make any sense. We were going to search through the entire floor and find no culprit.": '全靠反应够快，我才赶在被发现之前脱身，可是……这一切根本说不通。{w}我们接下来会把整层楼搜个遍，却一个凶手都找不到。',
        'Once again, I waited, watching over the stairs from afar. However, a couple minutes later, nobody had gone up. At that time, we were already next to the locked door, and we would only find Naomi inside.': '我再次等待着，远远盯着楼梯。{w}可几分钟过去了，没有一个人上来。那时我们已经站在那扇锁着的门前，而里面只会有 Naomi。',
        "So, by rushing to the door, I didn't change anything. That always happened, and yet we didn't find the person who should've been inside. Like I thought, the past won't change. As soon as I determined that I was going to do it, I was blocked off.": '也就是说，我冲向那扇门，什么也没能改变。{w}事情总是如此，可我们依然没找到那个本该在里面的人。果然，过去无法改变。我刚下定决心要动手，路就被堵死了。',
        "...But this means that something happened to the killer. Did they go back to the past before we found them? They locked the door as soon as I approached it, so they must've escaped after that point.": '……{w}可这就意味着凶手出了什么事。他们是在被我们发现之前回到过去了吗？我一靠近，门就被锁上了，所以他们一定是在那之后才逃走的。',
        '"Someone who will travel to the past". We have that person: Akaro. He\'s about to travel to the past right now, but for some reason, we won\'t find him again until later.': '「一个将要穿越回过去的人」。{w}我们正好有这么一个人：Akaro。{w}他马上就要穿越回过去了，可不知为何，我们要等到更晚些才会再次找到他。',
        "I made a plan in my head: if Akaro was responsible, he had to be the one who'd hidden the Sekimeiya while we were in the attic. We'd walk up in a few minutes, and I knew for a fact that we wouldn't look through every floor.": '我在心里盘算：如果凶手是 Akaro，那么趁我们待在阁楼的时候把 Sekimeiya 藏起来的人一定是他。{w}再过几分钟我们就会上去，而我清楚地知道，我们不会逐层搜查。',
        "As long as I hid myself in a partition, I wouldn't be seen. Afterward, I could go down again and see who'd hidden the Sekimeiya. Once more, I'd have a chance to see the murderer firsthand. And if Akaro had been telling the truth about seeing us during our inspection, I would see him for sure.": '只要躲在隔断后面，就不会被发现。之后我可以再下去一趟，看看究竟是谁藏起了 Sekimeiya。这样我又有机会亲眼见到凶手。{w}而如果 Akaro 说他在我们搜查时看见了我们，这话属实，那我就一定能看见他。',
        "We'd searched through the whole floor after that, and I could attempt to repeat that myself. I waited out the brief time until there was a safe way down.": '那之后我们把整层楼搜了一遍，我也可以试着照做。{w}我熬过那短短一阵，等到能安全下楼。',
        "When the group was gone, I slowly stepped out. Nobody had the chance to pass by after them—I'd been watching the glass from the second partition. The crystal floor was isolated, and according to Akaro, he had to be there.": '等一行人离开后，我才慢慢走出来。他们走后没人再经过——我一直从第二道隔断后面盯着玻璃。{w}水晶层是封闭的，而按 Akaro 的说法，他一定就在那里。',
        "I began looking through every room. I'd seen other people do it, but I'd never personally been the one to inspect. Investigating like that felt a bit paradoxical: if Akaro was in one of the rooms, he would see me even though he'd never mentioned it to us. Despite that, I continued.": '我开始逐间查看。以前都是看别人这么做，自己从没亲手查过。{w} 这样查总觉得有点矛盾：假如 Akaro 就在某个房间里，他会看到我，可这件事他从没跟我们提过。尽管如此，我还是继续查了下去。',
        "After the mechanical room, I began the hallway A search. A few minutes later, I'd confirmed that it was fully vacant.": '查完机械室，我开始搜 A走廊。{w} 几分钟后，我确认那里一个人也没有。',
        "Had he seen me all by myself and avoided me? If so, he would know that I was about to travel to the past when he saw me and Shiroya heading downstairs—we'd told him that we all stayed together the whole time... If he'd hidden the Sekimeiya, he would be aware that we were about to find it. And despite that, he hadn't stopped or questioned us.": '难道他看到我独自一人，就故意避开？如果真是这样，那他看见我和 Shiroya 下楼时，就该知道我们马上要穿越到过去——我们跟他说过，大家一直待在一起……{w} 如果他藏起了 Sekimeiya，也清楚我们即将找到它。可他并没有拦下我们，也没有多问。',
        'Unable to piece together what was happening, I stood still, waiting for what was bound to occur. At the point Akaro asked Sai for the time, it was 11:36.': '我怎么也理不清正在发生什么，只好站在原地，等待注定要发生的事。Akaro 向 Sai 问时间时，是 {time=11:36.}',
        'Unable to piece together what was happening, I stood still, waiting for what was bound to occur. At the point Akaro asked Sai for the time, it was 11:36 a.m.': '我怎么也理不清正在发生什么，只好站在原地，等待注定要发生的事。Akaro 向 Sai 问时间时，是 {time=11:36.}',
        "After my past self went to check the Sekimeiya, everyone but Akaro left. I saw Isla's and Shiroya's purses, and they were oblivious of what they were carrying. No matter how much I thought about the abnormal death of the second Naomi, the recording that the four of us were about to hear had remained in the back of my mind.": '过去的我去确认 Sekimeiya 之后，除了 Akaro，其他人都离开了。{w} 我看到了 Isla 和 Shiroya 的手提包，而她们对自己带着什么毫不知情。无论我怎么琢磨第二个 Naomi 那场不寻常的死亡，我们四人即将听到的那段录音始终盘踞在我脑海深处。',
        'The culprit had used the Sekimeiya and possessed knowledge of it. I\'d been pretty sure of that already, but seeing them vanish from the bathroom was a stark confirmation. They knew what they were doing, and they were consciously escaping from us. While it was possible that a ninth person was present, thanks to the Sekimeiya, it wasn\'t necessarily the case. Everything that the "culprit" had done could\'ve been done by one of us as long as they had knowledge of the Sekimeiya\'s mechanics.': '犯人使用过 Sekimeiya，也了解它。这一点我早就很有把握；而亲眼看到对方从卫生间消失，更是确凿的印证。那人清楚自己在做什么，也有意识地躲避我们。{w} 借助 Sekimeiya，确实可能存在第九个人，但也未必如此。只要掌握了 Sekimeiya 的运作原理，「犯人」做过的一切，我们当中任何人都能做到。',
        'So then, who were they? What was their purpose? I never stopped asking myself that last question. Why did they need to kill Naomi? Did their bizarre plan involve trapping us inside the building for the next few weeks...?': '那么，那人是谁？目的又是什么？我一直在不停地问自己最后那个问题。为什么非要杀掉 Naomi？{w} 难道那人荒唐的计划，就是把我们关在这栋楼里好几个星期……？',
        'I reassured myself that there was no way they could accomplish that... However, it was undeniable that the cameras recorded them. They surely intended to prevent anyone outside from viewing the recordings. We\'d already seen an "Access Denied" message, after all.': '我安慰自己，这种事他们绝不可能办到……{w} 可监控摄像头拍下了他们，这一点无可否认。他们一定打算阻止外面的人看到这些录像。毕竟，我们已经见过「拒绝访问」的提示了。',
        "I continued waiting. At around 11:50, I'd travel to the past, and before that, the Sekimeiya would be stolen and Akaro would leave. At least I was safe where I was—I knew Shiroya and I hadn't entered the cleaning room.": '我继续等待。大约 {time=11:50}，我会穿越到过去；在那之前，Sekimeiya 会被偷走，Akaro 也会离开。至少我待的地方是安全的——我清楚我和 Shiroya 没有进过清洁间。',
        "I continued waiting. At around 11:50 a.m., I'd travel to the past, and before that, the Sekimeiya would be stolen and Akaro would leave. At least I was safe where I was—I knew Shiroya and I hadn't entered the cleaning room.": '我继续等待。大约 {time=11:50}，我会穿越到过去；在那之前，Sekimeiya 会被偷走，Akaro 也会离开。至少我待的地方是安全的——我清楚我和 Shiroya 没有进过清洁间。',
        "A few more minutes passed; our past selves were occupied with listening to the recording.  There wasn't a lot more time left until we'd appear, but I knew for sure that Akaro would first exit the bathroom.": '又过了几分钟，过去的我们正忙着听录音。{w} 距离我们出现已经没有多少时间了，但我确信 Akaro 会先从卫生间出来。',
        "He looked tired and still a bit groggy. After breathing deeply, he walked off toward the stairs and disappeared from my field of vision. We'd told him the elevator wasn't functional, so he went up by foot. That meant Shiroya and I were about to head down.": '他看上去很疲惫，还带着几分昏沉。深吸一口气后，他朝楼梯走去，从我的视野里消失。{w} 我们告诉过他电梯不能用，所以他只能走上去。这也意味着，我和 Shiroya 马上就要下楼了。',
        "Once the group moved to the attic, I'd quickly come back from the second floor and opened the door to see if Akaro was present. There were a few seconds around then where someone could've tampered with the bathroom's interior, but since we'd just searched through the entire floor, they needed to have traveled from the future... I could justify it like that, but there was hardly any chance of it.": '那伙人一去阁楼，我便立刻从二楼折返，打开门确认 Akaro 在不在。就在那前后几秒里，确实可能有人对卫生间内部动过手脚；可我们刚把整层搜过一遍，那人就必须是从未来穿越过来的……{w} 这样解释也说得通，但几乎没有这种可能。',
        '...Could the key to what happened have been removed by Akaro? Whatever it was, had he left the bathroom with it just then...?': '……{w}难道解开那件事的关键，被 Akaro 拿走了？不管那是什么，他刚才离开卫生间时，是不是就把它带在身上……？',
        "Trying not to announce my presence, I observed the hallway, knowing that it couldn't yet have been me and Shiroya. Nobody appeared to be there, which was odd. Shortly after, I heard another sound come from the opposite hallway.": '我尽量不暴露自己，只静静观察着走廊。那个时间点，弄出动静的不可能是我和 Shiroya。可那里似乎空无一人，这就怪了。{w} 没过多久，对面的走廊又传来一声响动。',
        "It was Sai... He had made the sound and was in front of the event room... However, that shouldn't have been possible. At that moment, he was in the attic. We'd left him in the bedroom after he climbed the ladder to look around.": '是 Sai……{w} 声音是他弄出来的，人就站在活动室前……可这根本不可能。那一刻，他明明在阁楼。他爬上梯子四处看过之后，我们就把他留在了卧室里。',
        '...Um. Hey, Atsuki. How are you doing?': '……呃。{w=0.4} 那个，{w=0.3} Atsuki。{w=0.4} 你还好吗？',
        "...Let's go to the lobby.": '……{w}去大厅吧。',
        '...The past Shiroya and I had surely already arrived. We went to the bathroom first, and then to the event room. ...So if Sai had the Sekimeiya, had I interrupted his actions, thereby changing the past?': '……过去的 Shiroya 和过去的我肯定已经到这里了。我们先去了洗手间，然后才到活动室。{w} ……那么，既然 Sekimeiya 在 Sai 手上，是不是我打断了他的行动，把过去给改变了？',
        'Hm... Yeah, I did see the Sekimeiya disappeared. Was it Akaro, or was it you?': '嗯……{w} 对，我确实看见 Sekimeiya 不见了。拿走它的是 Akaro，还是你？',
        "If that had happened, it meant that the Sekimeiya traveled with him too, but what would the reason for that be? ...And even then, who hid the Sekimeiya from the cabinet? It was a fact that we'd seen it empty, but I didn't notice anyone entering the room where Shiroya found it.": '若真是那样，就说明 Sekimeiya 也跟着他一起穿越了——可这又是出于什么缘由？{w} ……再说，究竟是谁把 Sekimeiya 从展示柜里拿走的？我们确实亲眼见过展示柜是空的，可我也没见有人进过 Shiroya 找到它的那个房间。',
        "...I didn't respond, but he wouldn't break the silence before I did.": '……{w}我没有回答。只要我不开口，他也不会先打破沉默。',
        'That one, huh? Sure thing. Give me a second, though. This is my self-reflection moment of the day.': '那个啊？行。{w}不过等我一下。这是我今天的自我反省时间。',
        '...I should have already disappeared, assuming things happened as I remember them. Shiroya must be waiting. Follow me. Got it?': '……{w}如果一切都按我记忆中的发生，那我现在本该已经消失了。Shiroya 一定还在等。跟我来，明白吗？',
        'He touched my arm with his sleeve. It was hot.': '他用袖子碰了碰我的手臂。{w}很烫。',
        'I walked forward to see the time displayed on the computer. It said it was 11:57.': '我走上前去看电脑上显示的时间。上面显示的是 {time=11:57.}',
        'I walked forward to see the time displayed on the computer. It said it was 11:57 a.m.': '我走上前去看电脑上显示的时间。上面显示的是 {time=11:57.}',
        "I used this computer 47 minutes ago, at 11:10. You determined that Katei wasn't in this room during the attack thanks to the sleep timer, so it must be more than 45 minutes.": '我四十七分钟前用过这台电脑，那时是 {time=11:10.}。你之前靠休眠计时推断出袭击发生时 Katei 不在这个房间里，所以间隔一定超过四十五分钟。',
        "I used this computer 47 minutes ago, at 11:10 a.m. You determined that Katei wasn't in this room during the attack thanks to the sleep timer, so it must be more than 45 minutes.": '我四十七分钟前用过这台电脑，那时是 {time=11:10.}。你之前靠休眠计时推断出袭击发生时 Katei 不在这个房间里，所以间隔一定超过四十五分钟。',
        "So you remember. Good. Despite that, it was open a little bit just now. Someone must have come in here. This door isn't loose, and it won't open all by itself.": '看来你记得。很好。{w}可刚才那扇门却开了一条缝。一定是有人进来过。这扇门并不松，不会自己开的。',
        "Because it might reveal your lie. Let's say you traveled from {time=12:10.} It's possible the time displayed would now be something like {time=12:20.}": '因为它也许能揭穿你的谎话。{w}假设你是从 {time=12:10.} 穿越过来的，那表上现在显示的时间很可能就是 {time=12:20.} 之类。',
