        "This watch doesn't receive the time from a satellite. You sounded pretty convincing earlier when you said that you didn't know how to edit the time. Maybe you just didn't foresee this at all and the battery actually stopped working. If the battery ran out when the displayed time was, say, 12:10 p.m., it could pick up from there when we put in a new one—watches like that exist. Also, this watch was working just earlier, when you said it was 11:36 a.m. Let's see what happens when we insert a new battery.": '这块表不是靠卫星对时的。你刚才说自己不会调时间，听起来倒挺像那么回事。也许你根本没料到这一步，电池是真的耗尽了。{w}如果电池耗尽时，表上显示的是 {time=12:10} 这样的时间，那换上新电池后，它可能会从那里继续走——市面上确实有这种表。而且，刚才你说时间是 {time=11:36.} 的时候，这块表还在正常走着。我们换上电池，看看会怎么样。',
        "I bet I know why. You're up there and we'd see your past self. Additionally, you don't remember anyone going up. Where did you stay? We could just avoid anyone else.": '我大概知道原因。你就在上面，我们一上去就会遇见过去的你。再说，你也不记得有人上去过。{w}你当时待在哪里？我们避开其他人就行。',
        'We circled through every floor without finding her. The attic was unlocked, so we went up the last, narrow staircase and entered the living room.': '我们把每一层都转了一遍，还是没有找到她。{w}阁楼没有上锁，我们便沿最后那段窄楼梯上去，走进了客厅。',
        'The four digits displaying the time showed a "--:--", which most likely indicated that no time had been set. I would have assumed that the battery removal reset the internal system if not for what was above the time.': '显示时间的四个数字变成了“--:--”，多半表示还没有设定时间。{w}要不是时间上方还显示着别的，我本会以为拆电池把内部系统重置了。',
        'The time began displaying numbers, and Sai set it to 4:00.': '时间重新显示出数字，Sai 把它调成了 {time=4:00.}',
        'The time began displaying numbers, and Sai set it to 4:00 a.m.': '时间重新显示出数字，Sai 把它调成了 {time=4:00.}',
        "You have a watch, so you would've looked at it to find out how far back you went. Did you do that?": '你带着手表，肯定会看一眼，好知道自己回到了多久以前。{w}你看了吗？',
        "...I didn't. However, I didn't travel to the past either, so your question is pretty pointless.": '……{w}没有。{w}不过我根本没穿越到过去，你这个问题毫无意义。',
        "They were all empty, and I didn't bother searching too deeply into them. I understood what Sai's business on that floor was. He needed us to go there to have a chance at escaping—he had no way of dodging me on the upper floors.": '里面全是空的，我也没心思一间间细查。{w}我明白 Sai 为什么要在这层动手脚了：他需要我们来到这一层，才有机会脱身——在楼上，他根本甩不开我。',
        "I went to look at the computer's time, which read {time=12:18.} I sat on the chair and sighed in exasperation for a few seconds. There were plenty of things to think about, but instead my mind went to something that continued to gnaw at me.": '我去看了一眼电脑上的时间，上面显示 {time=12:18.}{w} 我在椅子上坐下，懊恼地叹了好一会儿气。该想的事多得是，我的思绪却偏偏飘向那件一直耿耿于怀的事。',
        "I went to look at the computer's time, which read 12:18.{w} I sat on the chair and sighed in exasperation for a few seconds. There were plenty of things to think about, but instead my mind went to something that continued to gnaw at me.": '我去看了一眼电脑上的时间，上面显示 {time=12:18.}{w} 我在椅子上坐下，懊恼地叹了好一会儿气。该想的事多得是，我的思绪却偏偏飘向那件一直耿耿于怀的事。',
