        '"9999-12-31" hints at that even further. It\'s the highest date the watch could display, so it could be linked to another common concept related to time travel: loops.': '「9999-12-31」更是加深了这个猜想。{w}那是手表能显示的最大日期，因此可能与时间穿越的另一常见概念有关——循环。',
        "For example, if the watch is in the process of traveling from 12:20 to the past, until it reaches the travel point, the time displayed would increase per travel. If that's repeated infinite times, the date would eventually hit its maximum value and stay there.": '举例来说，如果手表正从 {time=12:20} 向过去穿越，那么在抵达穿越点之前，每穿越一次，显示的时间就会增长。如此重复无数次，日期终会达到最大值，并停在那里。',
        "For example, if the watch is in the process of traveling from 12:20 p.m. to the past, until it reaches the travel point, the time displayed would increase per travel. If that's repeated infinite times, the date would eventually hit its maximum value and stay there.": '举例来说，如果手表正从 {time=12:20} 向过去穿越，那么在抵达穿越点之前，每穿越一次，显示的时间就会增长。如此重复无数次，日期终会达到最大值，并停在那里。',
        "So, assuming something of the sort is what happened, is it a coincidence that I just so happened to experience the loop in which the battery had to be replaced? There would be times in which the watch would appear functional and ones in which the date wouldn't have reached the year 9,999 yet. All of those would have to reach the same loop point, which contradicts the way I thought this worked, because traveling to the past would end up modifying it in different manners.": '那么，假设事情正是如此，我恰好碰上需要更换电池的那一轮循环，难道只是巧合？{w}有时手表看上去还正常，有时日期尚未走到9999年。这些情况最终都得汇入同一个循环点，这与我设想的运作方式相矛盾——毕竟穿越回过去，会以各不相同的方式改变它。',
        "That isn't all. Naturally, I'm thinking about this to justify the watch's date, but there's no apparent reason why Sai would travel back to the same spot more than once. And if he somehow could circumvent aging, it'd mean that after the point he traveled from, he couldn't exist anymore; if there is a point in time in which he always travels back, he could never make it past that point. Despite that, I'm sure that if I go to the attic right now, I'll see him.": '还不止这些。我这样推想，自然是为了解释手表上的日期，可 Sai 根本没有理由一次又一次回到同一个时间点。{w}而就算他有办法绕开衰老，那也意味着他从某个时间点穿越离开后，在那之后便无法继续存在；倘若存在一个他总会穿越回去的时刻，他就永远越不过那一刻。尽管如此，我确信此刻回到阁楼，仍能见到他。',
        "The facts are as follows: Sai probably only traveled once because countless versions of himself didn't exist at the same time. The watch can't be in a regular time loop because the Sekimeiya doesn't work like that and because the watch would physically degrade before reaching the year 9,999. And yet the date reached its highest possible value. I really feel that something of significance might be the cause behind it...": '事实如下：Sai 大概只穿越过一次，因为并不存在无数个同时并存的他自己。手表也不可能处在寻常的时间循环里，一来 Sekimeiya 不是那样运作的，二来手表在抵达9999年之前就会先一步损耗殆尽。{w}可日期偏偏走到了它的最大值。我总觉得，背后或许有什么要紧的东西在作祟……',
        "One last important thing I can take from this is that if the watch's status was caused by Sai traveling to the past, adding that he was surprised to see it disabled and that it was working at 11:36, it's possible that he hadn't yet traveled by that time.": '最后还有一点值得留意：倘若手表的状态是 Sai 穿越回过去造成的，再考虑到他看见手表停摆时的惊讶，以及 {time=11:36} 时它还正常运转，那么他到那个时刻为止，或许还没有穿越过。',
        "One last important thing I can take from this is that if the watch's status was caused by Sai traveling to the past, adding that he was surprised to see it disabled and that it was working at 11:36 a.m., it's possible that he hadn't yet traveled by that time.": '最后还有一点值得留意：倘若手表的状态是 Sai 穿越回过去造成的，再考虑到他看见手表停摆时的惊讶，以及 {time=11:36} 时它还正常运转，那么他到那个时刻为止，或许还没有穿越过。',
        'Next, I pressed "Initialize Camera Monitoring", but as before, I was met with a message box containing the "Couldn\'t detect video footage" text. Trying to look at the archived footage yielded no result either. In the lower right corner was a button that read "Power system off", but it was grayed out.': '接着我按下「初始化摄像头监控」，可和之前一样，弹出的仍是一个写着「未检测到视频画面」的提示框。想查看存档录像同样毫无结果。{w}右下角有个「电源系统关闭」的按钮，却是灰色的，无法点击。',
        'I kept looking, but to no avail. I performed a thorough search for the word "Archived", but none of the results interested me. The time had been passing fast, and I didn\'t want to waste any more of it. The computer displayed 12:31.': '我继续翻找，依旧一无所获。我把「Archived」这个词彻底搜了一遍，可搜出来的结果没有一条让我感兴趣。时间过得飞快，我不想再浪费下去。电脑上显示的时间是 {time=12:31.}',
        'I kept looking, but to no avail. I performed a thorough search for the word "Archived", but none of the results interested me. The time had been passing fast, and I didn\'t want to waste any more of it. The computer displayed 12:31 p.m.': '我继续翻找，依旧一无所获。我把「Archived」这个词彻底搜了一遍，可搜出来的结果没有一条让我感兴趣。时间过得飞快，我不想再浪费下去。电脑上显示的时间是 {time=12:31.}',
        '...Those words came as a surprise, so I forced my breathing to remain normal.': '……{w}这话出乎我的意料，我竭力让呼吸保持平稳。',
        'You traveled too? At the same time...? Why did I never see you, then?': '你也穿越了？同一时间……？{w}那为什么我一直没见到你？',
        "So you opened the door to the security room... We both traveled the same amount of time, then. I-I see... I was in the cleaning room when you came down, so we didn't see each other.": '所以监控室的门是你打开的……那我们俩穿越的时间一样。{w}我、我明白了……你下来的时候我在清洁间，所以我们才没碰面。',
        "Hm... The others returned and then went up again. I knew they were going to the attic, so I followed them to see if everything was actually repeating. I didn't go up immediately, so when I got there, Sai and Katei were already in the bedroom. I entered and listened from the hallway, and they were saying the same things as before.": '嗯……{w}其他人回来后，又上去了。我知道他们要去阁楼，就跟上去看看一切是不是真的在重演。{w}我没有立刻上去，所以等我到的时候，Sai 和 Katei 已经在卧室里了。我进了阁楼，在走廊里听着，他们说的和之前一模一样。',
        "Probably, but I didn't try to touch it again. I closed the cabinet before I looked around this floor briefly, and I thought that you might be back in the attic. I went there, but not much had seemed to change. I stayed in the hallway to listen to the conversation going on in the bedroom. Even if they'd seen me, it wouldn't have mattered much since we had just left from their perspective.": '大概吧，不过我没敢再碰它。我先关上展示柜，把这一层大致看了一圈，然后想你可能已经回阁楼了。我上去后，发现似乎没多少变化。{w}我留在走廊里听卧室里的谈话。就算被他们看见，也没什么大不了的，因为从他们的角度看，我们才刚刚离开。',
        'He kept saying it. He never left, and the elevator was still there with the door open. The conversation started winding down, and when they talked about going to the bathroom, I left right away so nobody would see me. I stayed in the living room for a couple minutes with the doors closed, but I think that they all took that time to go to the bathroom, so I started going down again to find you. I looked through every floor until I saw you right as I was about to start with this one.': '他反复这么说。他一直没离开，电梯也还停在那里，门开着。谈话渐渐接近尾声，他们提到要去洗手间时，我立刻离开，免得被人看见。{w} 我关着门在客厅里待了几分钟，但我想他们就是趁那段时间一起去了洗手间，于是我又往下走去找你。我一层层找下来，正要从这一层开始找时，就看见了你。',
        "Hm... I suppose it makes sense we never saw each other. Five minutes before the point we traveled from, I saw Sai on this floor. I thought he traveled from the future because he was supposed to still be upstairs. If he actually was there during that time, I had to be right in some way. He escaped from me more than ten minutes ago, so I'm not sure where he is right now.": '嗯……{w}我们一直没碰面，倒也说得通。在我们穿越回来的五分钟前，我在这一层看见了 Sai。我以为他是从未来穿越回来的，因为他本来应该还在楼上。{w}如果他当时真的在那里，那我的某个判断应该没错。他十几分钟前从我眼前逃走了，所以我现在不知道他在哪里。',
        "Yeah... It could be that it chooses random nearby locations, but that might be a bit of a stretch. It would mean that we could keep trying it until we appear outside the tower, but that recording didn't seem to indicate that will be possible. There's no way it was real, though...": '是啊……也许它会在附近随机选择位置，但这有点牵强。那样的话，我们只要不断尝试，直到出现在塔外就行；可那段录像似乎并不表示有这种可能。{w}不过，那怎么可能是真的……',
        "Well, even though you were picked up too, it's not like the people in the attic traveled. There's a specific distance from the Sekimeiya in which people can travel if it's activated. The first time, it was smaller, which is why Sai didn't travel.": '这个嘛，就算你也被卷了进去，阁楼里的人却没有时间穿越。Sekimeiya 周围有一个特定范围，它启动时，范围内的人就能时间穿越。{w}第一次那个范围更小，所以 Sai 没有时间穿越。',
        "That was my first thought too. The first time, I went twenty minutes into the past, and Sai, who was a few steps behind me, wasn't within range. This time, I went forty minutes into the past, and you went too despite being a bit farther away. Both times before traveling, I felt a painful burn on my fingers for a split second. The Sekimeiya was searing. I believe the second time it was even hotter, so that could be tied to this as well. Inside its cabinet, the Sekimeiya is kept cold. Once it's removed, it begins to get progressively hotter at an unnatural rate. Sai brought up something like this earlier.": '我起初也这么想。第一次我回到了二十分钟前，而落后我几步的 Sai 不在范围内。这次我回到了四十分钟前，你离得稍远些，却也一起时间穿越了。{w}两次时间穿越前，我的手指都有一瞬间像被灼伤般刺痛。Sekimeiya 烫得厉害。我觉得第二次甚至更烫，所以这也许也有关联。{w}放在展示柜里时，Sekimeiya 是冷的。一旦取出，它就会以不自然的速度逐渐变热。Sai 之前提过类似的事。',
        "I was in front of the bathroom when it was locked, so if that was when the culprit disappeared, it would've teleported me as well alongside the others in the event room, assuming that was the source. After we heard the sound, we first searched through hallway A. During that time, is it possible that someone used the Sekimeiya and the range encompassed the culprit in the bathroom? Given that we still found it inside the cabinet after finding the second Naomi, that doesn't seem feasible.": '上锁的时候，我就站在洗手间门前。假如犯人正是在那一刻消失的，那么传送的源头应该就在这里。若果真如此，我就该和活动室里的其他人一样被一并传走才对。{w}听到那声响后，我们最先搜查的是 A走廊。在这段时间里，会不会有人动用了 Sekimeiya，而范围恰好把洗手间里的犯人也圈了进去？可我们找到第二个 Naomi 之后，Sekimeiya 依旧在展示柜里，这么想来又说不通。',
        'But... there might be one way. According to Shiroya, she returned to room B3 and found the Sekimeiya in the cabinet where I\'d activated it, and at that point, Sai had a disabled Sekimeiya in his hip pack. Was there a second Sekimeiya at the same time as another? While the culprit was locked in the bathroom, could it be that someone made them escape with another Sekimeiya? ...Someone who remained in hallway B, maybe? Could it have happened from the second floor? And then, did both that person and the culprit escape to the past? If so, where the hell have they been all this time? This concept of "range" must start to explain what happened...': '可是……或许还有一种可能。据 Shiroya 说，她回到 B3房间，发现 Sekimeiya 就在我启动它的那个展示柜里；而在那一刻，Sai 腰包里装着一个已经停用的 Sekimeiya。也就是说，同一时间存在两个 Sekimeiya？{w}犯人在洗手间被锁住的时候，会不会有人用另一个 Sekimeiya 把他带走了？……会不会是某个留在 B走廊的人？还是从二楼动的手？{w}然后，那个人和犯人一起逃到了过去？若真是如此，他们这段时间究竟躲在什么地方？看来，得靠「范围」这个概念来解释这一切了……',
        "I can't think of anything. But right now, more than one Sekimeiya might exist. If you had two, you could bring one to the past. You just need to be holding one while you touch the other. I really don't think that can be the answer. The second one would've spawned out of nowhere.": '我想不出来。但现在，世上也许不止一个 Sekimeiya。{w}只要有两个，就能把其中一个带到过去——手里握着一个，再去触碰另一个就行。{w}可我实在不觉得这能成立。第二个总不可能凭空冒出来。',
        "I went ahead and grabbed it. It didn't take me long to confirm that nothing was below it.": '我干脆伸手把坐垫拿了起来。{w}很快就确认了下面什么都没有。',
        "What? Do you wanna know the time? It's 12:37.": '干嘛？想知道几点了？现在是 {time=12:37.}',
        "What? Do you wanna know the time? It's 12:37 p.m.": '干嘛？想知道几点了？现在是 {time=12:37.}',
        "I'm sorry, but that won't happen. You've said that you spotted me in hallway A, so if I ever go back to the past, I'll avoid being seen. It's that simple. You've told me what happened, so you've made sure I won't ever let it occur. If I travel to the past, I'll quickly check my hip pack, so there's no way I won't know I had the Sekimeiya there. This proves you're just making it all up.": '很遗憾，那不可能发生。你说过在 A走廊看见我，那只要我真回到过去，就一定会避开你的视线。{w} 就这么简单。你已经把会发生的事告诉我，也就等于确保了我不会让那一幕发生。要是我穿越回过去，第一时间就会检查腰包，不可能不知道自己带着 Sekimeiya。这足以证明，你说的全是编的。',
        "Had two Sekimeiya ever existed at the same time? Was that still the case? And if so, how had it happened? I hoped we'd quickly have a better idea of all that, but in the meantime, I continued running through my previous thoughts. We were only four hours into our imprisonment, and we were already dealing with a seemingly incomprehensible pile of questions.": '是否真的同时存在过两个 Sekimeiya？现在是否仍然如此？若是，又是怎么发生的？{w} 我希望我们能尽快弄清这些，但在那之前，我仍在反复梳理先前的思绪。我们被困在这里才四个小时，眼前却已经堆满了看似无法理解的问题。',
        "Remember what we thought earlier? That the time traveled is dependent on the amount of time the Sekimeiya's not in the cold? That might remain consistent. I'd say we traveled at approximately {time=12:40.} The one before this was at {time=11:50}, and after that, you saw the Sekimeiya had powered off. That Sekimeiya shouldn't have been put in the cabinet again, so if it's the one you activated, it was out of the cabinet for a long time.": '还记得我们之前的推测吗？穿越的时间长短，取决于 Sekimeiya 离开低温环境多久。这一点或许仍然成立。{w} 我们大概是在 {time=12:40.} 穿越的。上一次是在 {time=11:50}，之后你看到 Sekimeiya 已经断电了。它应该没有再被放回展示柜，所以如果你激活的就是它，那它离开展示柜已经很久了。',
        "Remember what we thought earlier? That the time traveled is dependent on the amount of time the Sekimeiya's not in the cold? That might remain consistent.{w} I'd say we traveled at approximately 12:40. The one before this was at 11:50, and after that, you saw the Sekimeiya had powered off. That Sekimeiya shouldn't have been put in the cabinet again, so if it's the one you activated, it was out of the cabinet for a long time.": '还记得我们之前的推测吗？穿越的时间长短，取决于 Sekimeiya 离开低温环境多久。这一点或许仍然成立。{w} 我们大概是在 {time=12:40.} 穿越的。上一次是在 {time=11:50}，之后你看到 Sekimeiya 已经断电了。它应该没有再被放回展示柜，所以如果你激活的就是它，那它离开展示柜已经很久了。',
        "Remember what we thought earlier? That the time traveled is dependent on the amount of time the Sekimeiya's not in the cold? That might remain consistent. I'd say we traveled at approximately 12:40. The one before this was at 11:50, and after that, you saw the Sekimeiya had powered off. That Sekimeiya shouldn't have been put in the cabinet again, so if it's the one you activated, it was out of the cabinet for a long time.": '还记得我们之前的推测吗？穿越的时间长短，取决于 Sekimeiya 离开低温环境多久。这一点或许仍然成立。{w} 我们大概是在 {time=12:40.} 穿越的。上一次是在 {time=11:50}，之后你看到 Sekimeiya 已经断电了。它应该没有再被放回展示柜，所以如果你激活的就是它，那它离开展示柜已经很久了。',
        "Remember what we thought earlier? That the time traveled is dependent on the amount of time the Sekimeiya's not in the cold? That might remain consistent.{w} I'd say we traveled at approximately 12:40 p.m. The one before this was at 11:50 a.m., and after that, you saw the Sekimeiya had powered off. That Sekimeiya shouldn't have been put in the cabinet again, so if it's the one you activated, it was out of the cabinet for a long time.": '还记得我们之前的推测吗？穿越的时间长短，取决于 Sekimeiya 离开低温环境多久。这一点或许仍然成立。{w} 我们大概是在 {time=12:40.} 穿越的。上一次是在 {time=11:50}，之后你看到 Sekimeiya 已经断电了。它应该没有再被放回展示柜，所以如果你激活的就是它，那它离开展示柜已经很久了。',
        "Remember what we thought earlier? That the time traveled is dependent on the amount of time the Sekimeiya's not in the cold? That might remain consistent. I'd say we traveled at approximately 12:40 p.m. The one before this was at 11:50 a.m., and after that, you saw the Sekimeiya had powered off. That Sekimeiya shouldn't have been put in the cabinet again, so if it's the one you activated, it was out of the cabinet for a long time.": '还记得我们之前的推测吗？穿越的时间长短，取决于 Sekimeiya 离开低温环境多久。这一点或许仍然成立。{w} 我们大概是在 {time=12:40.} 穿越的。上一次是在 {time=11:50}，之后你看到 Sekimeiya 已经断电了。它应该没有再被放回展示柜，所以如果你激活的就是它，那它离开展示柜已经很久了。',
        "Can't he just go back to the past after 12:40?": '他就不能在 {time=12:40} 之后再穿越回过去吗？',
        "Can't he just go back to the past after 12:40 p.m.?": '他就不能在 {time=12:40} 之后再穿越回过去吗？',
        "Hm... Well, there's still the Sekimeiya he had in his hip pack, right? Maybe he traveled using that one.": '嗯……{w} 对了，他腰包里不是还放着一个 Sekimeiya 吗？也许他是用那个穿越的。',
        'Huh? Definitely not an hour before we traveled, right? At that point, we were all in the other bedroom. Oh, you mean later?': '咦？总不会是穿越前一小时吧？那时候我们都在另一间卧室里。{w} 哦，你是指之后？',
        'Oh... So where we appeared might be related. We went an hour to the past, and at around 12:10 both of us were in the attic, right?': '哦……那我们出现的地方也许与此有关。我们回到了一小时前，而在 {time=12:10} 前后，我们两个都在阁楼，对吧？',
        'Oh... So where we appeared might be related. We went an hour to the past, and at around 12:10 p.m. both of us were in the attic, right?': '哦……那我们出现的地方也许与此有关。我们回到了一小时前，而在 {time=12:10} 前后，我们两个都在阁楼，对吧？',
        'Well, you said we traveled at around 12:40, so to 11:40. That means 12:10 was the middle point.': '你说我们是在 {time=12:40} 左右穿越的，回到了 {time=11:40.} 那 {time=12:10} 正好是中间点。',
        'Well, you said we traveled at around 12:40 p.m., so to 11:40 a.m. That means 12:10 p.m. was the middle point.': '你说我们是在 {time=12:40} 左右穿越的，回到了 {time=11:40.} 那 {time=12:10} 正好是中间点。',
        'We traveled from 11:50 to 11:10, and during those forty minutes, I was never in the security room. We just found the second Naomi and moved back and forth between the attic and the crystal floor.': '我们从 {time=11:50} 穿越到 {time=11:10}，而那四十分钟里，我从没进过监控室。我们只是发现了第二个 Naomi，然后在阁楼和水晶层之间来回跑。',
        'We traveled from 11:50 a.m. to 11:10 a.m., and during those forty minutes, I was never in the security room. We just found the second Naomi and moved back and forth between the attic and the crystal floor.': '我们从 {time=11:50} 穿越到 {time=11:10}，而那四十分钟里，我从没进过监控室。我们只是发现了第二个 Naomi，然后在阁楼和水晶层之间来回跑。',
        "So we can't get anywhere with this. Appearing where both of us were at 12:10 could be a coincidence, but if it isn't, I have no idea what determined it.": '我们各自出现在 {time=12:10} 时所在的位置，也许只是巧合；可如果不是巧合，我完全想不出是什么决定了这一点。',
        "So we can't get anywhere with this. Appearing where both of us were at 12:10 p.m. could be a coincidence, but if it isn't, I have no idea what determined it.": '我们各自出现在 {time=12:10} 时所在的位置，也许只是巧合；可如果不是巧合，我完全想不出是什么决定了这一点。',
        "We were dealing with Sai and a culprit who had traveled with the Sekimeiya. If the place you appeared somehow depended on a previous location, we could know exactly where someone had been in the past if we knew the location they'd appeared in, effectively drawing information out of them. I couldn't apply it to Sai, since I hadn't seen him appearing anywhere, but it was something to keep in mind in the future.": '我们面对的是 Sai，以及一个曾与 Sekimeiya 一同穿越的犯人。假如出现的地点与先前所在的位置存在某种关联，那么只要知道某人出现的位置，就能准确推断他过去去过哪里，等于从他身上套出情报。{w} 我没法把这套推断用在 Sai 身上，因为我没见他出现在任何地方；不过往后可以留意这一点。',
        '"Can I not go back to the past, save Miiya, and threaten the forensic technicians to say that they\'ve found her jaw?" Something like that was a complete delusion. Had I already saved Miiya? Of course not. I often used to be optimistic as I fell asleep, and I\'d realize how foolish I\'d been immediately after waking up.': '「我难道不能回到过去，救下 Miiya，再威胁法医，让他们声称找到了她的下颌吗？」{w} 这种念头纯属妄想。我已经救下 Miiya 了吗？当然没有。我过去常在入睡前盲目乐观，醒来后立刻意识到自己有多愚蠢。',
        '...I fell asleep.': '{w=0.5}……我睡着了。',
        'We walked carefully through the hallway. Having no sense of time was a peculiar feeling, but our surroundings were fully silent. If people were still in the other bedroom, the door was perfectly hiding their presence. Once we got to the living room, we identified a slight change.': '我们小心翼翼地穿过走廊。失去时间感是种异样的感觉，但四周一片死寂。如果另一间卧室里还有人，那扇门也把他们的存在掩藏得严严实实。{w} 到了客厅后，我们察觉到了一处细微的变化。',
        "I'd looked at the cleaning cart a few times before. Underneath and around it, there were three buckets storing scourers and chemicals like bleach. ...Those hadn't moved.": '我之前看过那辆清洁推车好几次。车底和车旁摆着三只水桶，里面装着清洁海绵和漂白剂之类的化学用品。{w}……那几只桶却纹丝没动。',
        "...Are you serious? That can't be it, you were touching the cabinet when you traveled for the first time. How come it didn't disappear?": '……你不是认真的吧？{w}这说不通啊，你第一次穿越的时候明明碰着展示柜。它怎么就没消失？',
        "...Th-That's true. I supported my body on it with my left hand, so I was touching the cabinet. That's strange. If this cart disappeared when we traveled, did it appear somewhere else...?": '……确、确实。我当时用左手撑着身子，是碰着展示柜没错。{w}那就怪了。要是这辆推车在我们穿越时消失了，它是不是跑到别的地方去了……？',
        "...M-Maybe you're right.": '……{w}也、也许你说得对。',
        "I wanted to test it, and I got close to Shiroya so that if it worked, the range would encompass her too. Perhaps it was a bad idea since nothing assured us we'd appear together, but it was better to try it like that. Without overthinking it, I placed my entire left hand on top of the Sekimeiya. After a full second, nothing had happened.": '我想试一试，就靠近了 Shiroya，这样万一奏效，她也能落在范围内。这或许不是什么好主意，毕竟谁也不能保证我们会一起出现，但那样试总归更好一些。{w}我没再多想，把整只左手覆在 Sekimeiya 上。{w}整整一秒过去，什么也没发生。',
        "That's strange... Can you think of why?": '这就怪了……{w}你能想到是什么原因吗？',
        'Not at all. At least not if it stays consistent with the previous events. If the mechanics are completely random, it can just be that it takes a random amount of time until it starts to get hot. However, minutes after the Sekimeiya that Sai had in his pack turned white, it was already really hot.': '完全想不到。至少按它之前的表现来推，我是想不出原因。假如运作机制完全随机，那也可能只是要过一段随机的时间，它才会开始发烫。{w}可 Sai 背包里那个 Sekimeiya 变白之后才过几分钟，就已经烫得厉害了。',
        "This time, let's be the ones to hide it. Later, we'll be able to see if anything has changed and hopefully understand how it functions a bit better. We have a chance since, for some reason, nobody appears to be here...": '这次，换我们来藏它。{w}之后就能看看有没有什么变化，运气好的话，还能更了解它的运作规律。机会难得——不知为何，这里好像一个人都没有……',
        "So, I have two suggestions. One is inside a computer tower. I saw screwdrivers in the attic. If we open up a computer tower and hide the Sekimeiya inside it, it's hard to think anyone will easily find it. It requires thinking about it and unscrewing every other tower until you find it.": '所以我有两个提议。第一个是藏进电脑主机里。{w}我在阁楼见过螺丝刀。只要拆开一台主机，把 Sekimeiya 藏进去，很难想象有人能轻易找到。得先想到这种可能，再一台台拧开其他主机，才能找到它。',
        "I thought of it earlier... the last key in Naomi's keyring. It's likely it belonged to her locker, given that every staff member has one, and the size of the key seemed appropriate for it.": '我之前就想到了……Naomi 钥匙圈上的最后一把钥匙。{w}它多半就是她储物柜的钥匙——每个员工都有一个，那把钥匙的大小也正合适。',
        "But the specter of the voice recorder haunted us; we'd found something that implied we'd be there for a whole month. For the first time, that sounded just a bit desirable, as it would've given us more time to comprehend what was going on and how to use the Sekimeiya. It was possible someone was angling to trap us for a month just to accomplish that, but I couldn't begin to imagine how the rest of the plan would unfold in that case.": '可录音笔的阴影始终挥之不去：我们发现的东西暗示，我们会在这里待上整整一个月。{w}这个念头头一次让人觉得还有几分可取之处，因为那会给我们更多时间去弄清究竟发生了什么，以及如何使用 Sekimeiya。或许有人正是为了这个目的才想把我们困上一个月；但若真是如此，我完全想象不出计划的其余部分会如何展开。',
        "We entered B4, the room with the first Naomi. I remembered where the keys were, so I found them easily. Two keys remained: the small one I wanted and the one for the door in the first staircase. I took the smaller one off the keyring; otherwise, it was too large to keep on my person, and it might've made noise.": '我们走进水晶展室 B4，也就是第一个 Naomi 所在的房间。我记得钥匙放在哪里，所以很轻松就找到了。{w}钥匙圈上只剩两把：我想要的那把小钥匙，以及第一段楼梯处那扇门的钥匙。我把小的那把从钥匙圈上取了下来；不然整串太大，带在身上不方便，还可能发出声响。',
        "Then, we moved to the staff room. I inserted the key into a locker—I'd once again been correct about the purpose of a key.": '随后我们去了员工室。{w}我把钥匙插进一个储物柜——我又一次猜对了这把钥匙的用途。',
        "I placed the Sekimeiya in the smaller one and took the coat out. I felt through the pockets, but they were all empty aside from a single handkerchief that I left alone. I put the coat back inside. It was a bit disappointing that we hadn't found anything substantial, but I hadn't expected to.": '我把 Sekimeiya 放进上面那格，取出外套，逐一摸过口袋。里面都是空的，只有一条手帕，我没有动它。{w}随后我把外套挂了回去。什么像样的线索都没找到，多少有些失望，不过这本来也在意料之中。',
        "By the way, regarding the cart disappearing... I think it makes more sense than not. What's really strange is that apparently nobody noticed the Sekimeiya after it fell.": '对了，关于推车消失的事……{w}我倒觉得这样才说得通。真正奇怪的是，Sekimeiya 掉下来之后，居然没有人注意到它。',
        "I was stepping on my shoes, so they teleported. My shoes were stepping on the floor, though, so why didn't the floor teleport? It's probably just because my clothes were under my possession, while the floor wasn't.": '我脚上穿着鞋，所以鞋也传送了。可鞋踩在地板上，地板为什么没有传送？{w}大概只因为衣服算我的所有物，而地板不算。',
        "Remember the suitcase in the attic? Something similar must've happened. Naomi traveled holding it, so it traveled along too. We didn't find it strange at all since it's natural to imagine it'd happen, but your purse has traveled both times when it was only touching your clothes. It has to be because it's recognized as part of your whole entity when you travel.": '还记得阁楼里的手提箱吗？应该也是同样的道理。Naomi 传送时提着它，它便跟着一起传送了。{w}我们丝毫不觉得奇怪，因为理所当然地认为会这样；可你的手提包两次都只是贴着衣服，却也跟着传送了。这只能是因为传送时，它被认定为你这个整体的一部分。',
        "Pretty much. Even though it's what allows you to travel in the first place, it should've been included in your possessions. That wasn't necessarily the case in the previous travels—I wasn't holding the cabinets in the same sense. The Sekimeiya must exclude itself when it comes to what it makes travel. And lastly, even if it had traveled, it's unlikely we would've appeared with it, which is what I speculated happened with the Sekimeiya in Sai's hip pack. Since the cart didn't appear with us in the attic, the Sekimeiya probably wouldn't have either.": '差不多吧。虽然正是它让你能够穿越，它本身也该算在你的随身物品里。之前那几次穿越就未必如此了——那时我算不上真正「拿着」展示柜。{w} Sekimeiya 在让物体穿越时，必然要把自己排除在外。最后，就算它真的穿越了，我们也不太可能和它一起出现——我先前推测 Sai 腰包里的 Sekimeiya 就是这种情况。既然推车没有和我们一起出现在阁楼，Sekimeiya 多半也不会。',
        "I guess you're right... This clears a few things up. We should probably try to get an idea of what happened here, though.": '大概吧……这样一来，有几件事就说得通了。{w} 不过，我们最好还是先弄清楚这里究竟发生了什么。',
        'To cross to the opposite hallway, we went through the lobby, knowing that the mechanical room was also on our way. Unexpectedly, our search came to an abrupt stop when we stepped into the large hall.': '为了到对面的走廊去，我们穿过大厅，顺路也能看看机械室。{w} 没想到，刚一踏进那座宽阔的厅堂，搜索就戛然而止。',
        "We fell asleep and lost track of time. Did something happen? Where's Isla?": '我们睡着了，没注意时间。出什么事了吗？{w} Isla 呢？',
        'Sai, showing the strongest reaction, approached the room while letting out a conspicuous grunt. He opened the door and stayed still for some time. Then, he entered the small space. Before the others had time to wonder what he was doing, he exited and told them that it was empty.': '反应最大的是 Sai，他闷哼一声，走向那间房。{w} 他推开门，在门口一动不动地站了好一会儿，随后才走进那个狭小的空间。其他人还没来得及琢磨他在做什么，他就已经出来，说里面空无一人。',
        "As they put that into practice, Sai continued yelling out Katei's name. He wasn't being drawn to the noise, so it followed that he wasn't nearby. Drawing a zigzag pattern, Akaro and Sai met in the lobby after looking through every room in their respective hallways. In the meantime, Isla observed next to her mother. Despite her initial optimism, she was aware of what the situation had become. Sai put an end to the search by concluding that the mechanical room was empty.": '方案付诸实施，Sai 一边搜一边继续高喊 Katei 的名字。他没有循声而来，可见并不在附近。{w} Akaro 和 Sai 走着之字形路线，搜完各自走廊的每个房间后在大厅会合。这期间，Isla 在母亲身旁看着。她起初虽抱着乐观，此刻也明白局面变成了什么样。{w} Sai 断定机械室是空的，结束了这次搜索。',
        "She sat on the stairs. She was tired and had to bear the constant burden of bringing her daughter into danger. They were locked up in a huge building with a murderer, and the people she wanted to trust had accepted that time travel was an ongoing factor they'd used to explain the mysteries pressing down on them.": '她在楼梯上坐下。{w}她累了，还不得不一直背负着把女儿带入险境的压力。他们被困在一栋巨大的建筑里，里面还有杀人凶手；而她本想信任的那些人，早已把时间穿越当成反复出现的一环，用它来解释压在众人头上的种种谜团。',
        'Isla had left the door open, so Erina was the first one to see the interior. Just as she remembered, it was dirtied by a purplish black color, and almost no brightness penetrated the coating on the ceiling. The light leaking in from hallway C was the main source of illumination. It took her a second to spot Isla with how dark it was; she was putting all of the force she could into opening up a cabinet. Unbeknownst to Erina, what would then occur would not leave her memories until they all faded away.': 'Isla 没关门，Erina 便成了第一个看清室内的人。正如她记忆中那样，里面被一层紫黑色污迹浸染，天花板上的涂层几乎透不进半点光。{w}主要的光源，是从 C走廊漏进来的微光。光线太暗，她花了一秒才找到 Isla——那孩子正用尽全身力气去掀开一个展示柜。Erina 并不知道，接下来发生的事，将一直盘踞在她的记忆里，直到一切褪色。',
        "As Erina rushed inside, Isla's instincts told her to get out of the position she'd put herself in. However, due to jumping upward, the front of the cabinet had suspended her in midair, painfully pressing into her stomach and preventing her legs from reaching the floor. The only way she could move was by leaning forward.": 'Erina 冲进房间时，Isla 本能地想从自己摆出的姿势里挣脱出来。可她是往上跳的，柜子的前壁把她悬在半空，硬生生压进她的肚子，疼得厉害，双腿也够不到地面。{w}她唯一能动的方向，就是往前倾。',
        'Erina let out a cry and ran as fast as she could. Meanwhile, Sai and Akaro looked on from the door. When Erina reopened the lid and leaned in, she finally saw what the ominous cabinet contained.': 'Erina 惊叫一声，拼了命地跑过去。与此同时，Sai 和 Akaro 在门口看着。{w}等 Erina 重新掀开柜盖、俯身探入，她终于看清了那个不祥的展示柜里装着什么。',
        "Nothing. Erina didn't see anything but the five faces of the cabinet, covered by a velvet texture that, while untainted by the smoke, appeared black due to the lack of light.": '什么都没有。{w}Erina 看到的只有柜子的五面内壁，覆着天鹅绒般的材质；那材质虽没被烟雾侵蚀，却因光线不足而显得漆黑。',
        'They had realized that the room was empty. Isla had suddenly disappeared without leaving a trace. Even though disappearances had become commonplace, they\'d thought that the Sekimeiya had to be directly involved for one to occur. Despite that, they\'d found it in the cleaning room and left it there. Furthermore, Atsuki\'s earlier explanation of the "range" emitted by the Sekimeiya couldn\'t explain what had occurred, as nobody else nearby had disappeared along with Isla.': '他们这才意识到，房间里已空无一人。Isla 骤然消失，没留下半点痕迹。虽说消失这种事早已见怪不怪，他们却一直以为，发生这种事时 Sekimeiya 必定直接参与其中。{w}可实际上，他们明明是在清洁间找到 Sekimeiya 的，后来又把它留在了那里。况且，Atsuki 先前解释过 Sekimeiya 会散发某种「范围」，这也无法解释眼前的事——因为 Isla 消失时，附近并没有其他人一起不见。',
        "The silence had continued uninterrupted since they'd set foot on the crystal floor, but the three of them had been thinking about drastically different things. It was an outside sound that finally breached the empty air, coming from hallway A.": '自从踏上水晶层，四周的寂静便一直延续，未曾中断，可三个人心里想的却是天差地别的事。{w} 最终打破这片空寂的，是 A走廊方向传来的一声响动。',
        'He gripped the lower part of the lid with his right arm and lifted it. As soon as the smallest gap appeared, he peeked inside. Even though there was very little light, he frowned.': '他右手抓住柜盖下沿，向上抬起。刚露出一丝缝隙，他就朝里看去。{w} 光线虽暗，他的眉头却皱了起来。',
        "However, as soon as she entered the huge and overwhelming lobby, her body gave out under the full weight of her daughter's death. She wouldn't be able to find her killer, and most likely, she would never begin to understand what had happened to her. Suffering from the ultimate feeling of emptiness, she slumped on a wall and slowly slid to the ground.": '然而，一走进那空旷而令人窒息的大厅，女儿的死便如山压顶，她的身体再也撑不住了。她找不到凶手，多半也永远弄不明白女儿遭遇了什么。{w} 被极致的空虚吞没，她靠到墙边，缓缓滑坐在地上。',
        'They approached her slowly and remained at her side. A loud noise resounded through the entire floor... and they understood what it had been.': '他们缓缓走近，守在她身旁。{w} 一声巨响在整个楼层回荡……他们明白那是什么声音。',
        "Nobody chose to leave the lobby. They knew that gravity, a simple law of the universe, had closed Isla's coffin by itself. However, they didn't know the true consequences that sound had brought, and spent the time unaware until the hallway B door opened.": '谁也没有离开大厅。他们知道，是重力这条再简单不过的宇宙法则，自行合上了 Isla 的棺盖。{w} 可他们并不知道那声响真正带来了什么后果，就这样毫无察觉地待着，直到 B走廊的门打开。',
        "Shiroya looked crushed. She couldn't believe such a sudden and tragic story had unfolded while she'd slept. I began to feel guilty about my recent actions, ones I'd taken in ignorance.": 'Shiroya 神情黯然，几乎垮了。她无法相信，就在自己睡着的时候，竟发生了这样突然而惨烈的事。{w} 我开始为自己近来的举动感到愧疚——那些事都是我在毫不知情时做下的。',
        "And if that was what had happened, the source of the range had to have been outside the cabinet, or else the Sekimeiya would've remained inside it. If the range came from the Sekimeiya in the cleaning room, Erina, by the entrance to room A5, should've traveled as well. Sai and Akaro saw Isla falling into the cabinet, so Katei, who had just disappeared, could've been who'd activated it. In that case, nobody would have noticed he'd traveled too.": '如果真是这样，那么范围的源头就只能位于展示柜之外，否则 Sekimeiya 应该仍留在柜中。{w}倘若范围源自清洁间的 Sekimeiya，那么守在 A5 展室入口旁的 Erina 也该被传送走才对。Sai 和 Akaro 亲眼看见 Isla 倒进展示柜，那么刚刚消失的 Katei，或许正是启动它的人。若果真如此，谁也不会注意到他也被传送了。',
        "However, the crystal floor had just been searched, so if Katei's range had encompassed the whole cabinet... it might have come from floor 2. If the range went through solid objects and Katei was above the room, the ceiling was no obstacle.": '不过，水晶层才刚刚被搜寻过；如果 Katei 的范围覆盖了整个展示柜……那源头或许来自二楼。{w}如果范围能穿透实体，而 Katei 就在展室上方，那么天花板也构不成阻碍。',
        "After Isla's disappearance, the group searched through the whole building and didn't find Katei. If he activated the travel from floor 2, he could appear on the crystal floor, escaping the search. However, it was important to note that they never found me and Shiroya, so their search wasn't perfect. That theory explained Katei's and Isla's disappearances along with the lack of the Sekimeiya in the cabinet. ...Would it mean that it was all just a very unfortunate coincidence, though?": 'Isla 失踪后，众人搜遍了整栋楼，也没找到 Katei。如果他是在二楼启动传送的，就可能出现在水晶层，从而躲过搜索。{w}不过有一点值得留意：他们始终没发现我和 Shiroya，可见搜索并不彻底。{w}这套推断能解释 Katei 与 Isla 的失踪，也能解释展示柜里为何没有 Sekimeiya。……可这难道意味着，一切只是极为不幸的巧合？',
        "W-Wait... This isn't what you said.": '等、等等……{w}这跟你说的不一样啊。',
        "The others all got closer. They saw Isla resting face-up with her knees folded. However, my own tiny wish had been denied by the Sekimeiya beside her, emitting a faint light which illuminated her more than I'd wanted.": '其余人也纷纷凑近，看见 Isla 仰面躺着，双膝蜷曲。{w}然而，我那个小小的愿望却被她身旁的 Sekimeiya 打破了——它散发着微弱的光，把她的样子照得比我期望的更清楚。',
        "What? I-It shouldn't be here... I haven't gone to the cleaning room myself, but I'm certain that when I saw her, there was nothing else here. I didn't find it appropriate to blame them for leaving the Sekimeiya out of the cabinet since Isla had disappeared, but none of us could have moved it.": '什么？它、它不该在这里……{w}我虽然没亲自去过清洁间，但我很确定，我见到她的时候，这里没有别的东西。Isla 失踪之后，他们没把 Sekimeiya 收回展示柜，我不好因此责怪他们，可我们之中谁都不可能挪动过它。',
        'What the...? Oh, right, you said the cleaning cart disappeared after our travel.': '搞什么……？{w}啊，对了，你说过我们传送之后，清洁推车就不见了。',
        "...Don't be stupid. I used the other one too.": '……{w}别犯傻了。另一个洗手间我也用过了。',
        '...Something Sai had said bothered me: "the culprit". He was implying that what happened to Isla was someone\'s fault, and one who had orchestrated everything deliberately. I wasn\'t so convinced about that, so we moved again to where Isla lay to determine an important fact: the cause of her death.': '……Sai 有句话让我耿耿于怀：「犯人」。{w}他言下之意，Isla 的遭遇是某人的过错，而且是有人刻意安排好了一切。我并不那么确信，于是我们再次回到 Isla 躺着的地方，要弄清一件要紧的事——她的死因。',
        "I covered my hand with my sleeve and reached in to grab it. I underestimated the depth of the cabinet, and my fingers brushed the Sekimeiya, causing it to roll and contact Isla's face. Frowning, I retrieved it properly and stood up straight.": '我用袖子裹住手，探进去拿它。我低估了展示柜的深度，指尖擦到了 Sekimeiya，它滚了一下，碰到了 Isla 的脸。{w}我皱起眉，重新把它拿好，直起身子。',
        'For the first time, and with a slight frown, I reached my hand out to touch her. However, any doubts I had were wiped away by contacting her lifeless skin. Even though nothing indicated how it had happened, Isla was not alive.': '我微微皱眉，第一次伸手去碰她。{w}可一碰到她那毫无生气的皮肤，我心中的疑虑便烟消云散。尽管没有任何迹象说明事情是如何发生的，Isla 确实已经死去。',
        "How had the leap from life to death happened? I had no good guess. I spoke in a faint voice so that Erina wouldn't hear me. Two weeks prior, a death had destroyed my life, but that was almost minuscule compared to how Erina must have felt. If I had any answers for her, they needed to be certain.": '从生到死的这一步究竟是如何发生的？我毫无头绪。{w}我压低声音，不让 Erina 听见。两周前，一场死亡毁掉了我的生活，但和 Erina 此刻的感受相比，那几乎微不足道。如果我要给她答案，那答案就必须确凿无疑。',
        "I don't know. If someone did this to her, sure, but in terms of natural deaths, not many things would apply. Children don't really have their hearts suddenly fail very often.": '我不知道。{w}如果有人害了她，那倒是有可能；但如果是自然死亡，能对得上的情况并不多。小孩子心脏突然衰竭，毕竟不常见。',
        "Yeah. ...What if traveling is what caused this to begin with? When she disappeared, she traveled through time and appeared somewhere else. If she couldn't have existed at that point, it's possible she appeared in this state. Even though she reminds me of the second Naomi, that body had a head wound. ...I can't see any such thing here, though.": '嗯。……如果一开始就是时间穿越造成的呢？她消失的时候穿越了时间，出现在别处。如果她在那个时间点本不可能存在，那她以这种状态出现也有可能。{w}虽然她让我想起第二个 Naomi，但那具尸体头上有伤。……不过，这里看不到那样的伤。',
        "...I doubt it. It's true that something was up with this cabinet, but that'd require her to spend a long time inside, and there's no reason why she wouldn't have gotten out. That would take a lot less time than dehydration, but it's still considerable. Let's say that she couldn't escape, though. The way she'd die would be from carbon dioxide intoxication, not from lack of oxygen. Even in a small space like this, I think it'd take six or seven hours. Maybe even more since a child would breathe less.": '……{w}我不这么认为。展示柜确实有些不对劲，可要真是这样，她就得在里面待上很长时间，而她没理由不出来。这虽然比脱水致死快得多，但也相当久了。{w}就算她真的逃不出来，死因也会是二氧化碳中毒，而不是缺氧。即便在这么小的空间里，我想也要六七个小时。孩子呼吸量小，也许还更久。',
        "There was another reason why I believed something like that might've happened, and it was Isla's yell. If she'd traveled to the past and spent time in the cabinet, it meant that Isla screamed because she saw her own body. However, that same travel would've made two bodies travel back, multiplying the number every time. That couldn't be right, and it also meant that the body she saw was alive.": '我之所以觉得可能发生过那样的事，还有一个理由：Isla 的喊叫声。如果她穿越到了过去，又在展示柜里待过一段时间，那就说明 Isla 之所以尖叫，是因为看见了自己的尸体。{w}可同一次穿越会让两具身体一起回到过去，而且每经历一次，数量还会翻倍。这说不通；这也意味着她看见的那具身体当时还活着。',
        "...What I'd just said replayed in my mind: probably six or seven hours would've been needed for her to suffocate inside the cabinet. That time could be cut in half if two Islas had been in the cabinet, breathing twice as much air...": '……{w}我刚才说的话在脑中回放：她要在展示柜里窒息，大概需要六七个小时。可如果有两个 Isla 待在柜子里，呼吸量翻倍，这个时间就会缩短一半……',
        "I recalled the recording that told us Isla would be alive in a month. How to treat it, I had no idea, but it had ironically become a last hope. Could the Sekimeiya have the power to bring a person back to life? It wasn't that crazy of a thought depending on how it worked, so the recording coming true at the cost of spending a month in the tower was the best-case scenario.": '我想起那段录音，它告诉我们 Isla 一个月后还会活着。我不知道该怎么看待它，可讽刺的是，它竟成了我们最后的希望。{w}Sekimeiya 难道有让人复活的力量？这想法有多荒唐，要看它究竟怎么运作——但也不是完全不可能。所以，如果代价是在塔里待上一个月，却能让录音成真，那已经是最好的结果了。',
        "If one thing was certain, it was that some kind of plan existed behind it. Out of everyone there, the recorder had appeared inside Isla's purse. Not only that, the audio on it was downright bizarre. In a few hours, at 21:00, we'd have a much better understanding of its veracity. Although we hadn't checked, it was very likely within that mysterious cabinet, still inside Isla's purse.": '有一点可以肯定：这背后肯定藏着某种计划。在场的人里，录音笔偏偏出现在 Isla 的手提包中。不止如此，里面的录音简直诡异至极。再过几个小时，到 {time=21}，我们就能更清楚地判断它是真是假。虽然还没去确认，但它很可能还在那个神秘的展示柜里，仍旧放在 Isla 的包里。',
        "If one thing was certain, it was that some kind of plan existed behind it. Out of everyone there, the recorder had appeared inside Isla's purse. Not only that, the audio on it was downright bizarre. In a few hours, at 9 p.m., we'd have a much better understanding of its veracity. Although we hadn't checked, it was very likely within that mysterious cabinet, still inside Isla's purse.": '有一点可以肯定：这背后肯定藏着某种计划。在场的人里，录音笔偏偏出现在 Isla 的手提包中。不止如此，里面的录音简直诡异至极。再过几个小时，到 {time=21}，我们就能更清楚地判断它是真是假。虽然还没去确认，但它很可能还在那个神秘的展示柜里，仍旧放在 Isla 的包里。',
        'After giving the flashlight back to Katei, he brought it to the security room. Once again, we moved to the lobby due to its proximity to the outside world and how spacious it was. Shiroya, Katei, and I sat on the couch. There were chairs next to the reception desk, but everyone else chose to sit on the floor in silence, leaning against a wall. Every speck of motivation within me had been crushed. While I wanted to know what was going on even more, I only had the energy to think to myself.': '我把手电筒还给了 Katei，他把它送回了监控室。我们又一次回到大厅——这里离外界最近，地方也宽敞。{w} Shiroya、Katei 和我坐在沙发上。接待台旁摆着椅子，其他人却都默不作声地靠墙坐在地上。{w} 我仅剩的一点干劲也彻底消失了。我虽然更想知道究竟出了什么事，却只剩下一个人胡思乱想的力气。',
        "My intent was to eventually check on the Sekimeiya that we had, so I had to eventually decide what to do regarding that. We were all sitting down, letting the time pass and waiting for our release. If I didn't do anything, it was possible the police would find the key on me, giving away that I'd been the one to hide the Sekimeiya. I would have to discard it before it was too late.": '我迟早得去看看我们手里的那个 Sekimeiya，所以终究得决定拿它怎么办。{w} 我们全都坐着，任时间流逝，等着有人来放我们出去。如果我什么也不做，警察说不定会在搜身时找到那把钥匙，从而发现藏起 Sekimeiya 的人就是我。我得在被发现之前把它处理掉。',
        "It's impossible to feel sure about this, but hours ago, I tried to save Naomi. As soon as I became determined to change the past, and just when it seemed possible, the universe put a barrier in front of me and made everything occur as it had. Even though it might have already been too late to save Naomi when I ran to the bathroom, I had already decided not to let her killer escape. Even that was seamlessly denied.": '这一点无法完全确定。但几个小时前，我试图去救 Naomi。就在我下定决心要改变过去、眼看就要成功的那一刻，宇宙在我面前立起了一道墙，让一切照原样发生。{w} 我冲向洗手间时，也许已经来不及救 Naomi 了，但我当时已经决定绝不让凶手逃走。就连这一点，也被无声无息地否定了。',
        "I knew nothing good would come from that, but at least seeing Miiya again was a vague possibility. However, the Sekimeiya hadn't appeared to work when we hid it, so we simply had to hope it would start working again before doing anything. ...To go back far enough, the time traveled couldn't be less than or equal to the time stored, but I didn't think was the case.": '我知道那样做不会有任何好处，但至少，再见到 Miiya 还存着一线模糊的可能。{w} 可是我们把它藏起来时，Sekimeiya 似乎已经不再起作用；所以在动手之前，我们只能盼着它重新恢复。……若要回到足够远的过去，穿越的时间就不能小于或等于蓄能的时间——但我觉得并不是那样。',
        "I thought about something. Why had the Sekimeiya not worked when we stored it in the locker? Could the universe have prevented it from working? What if, after traveling, we would've been guaranteed to change what had already occurred? Maybe the Sekimeiya would disallow any travel that was going to lead into an impossibility.": '我想到了一件事。{w} 我们把 Sekimeiya 放进储物柜时，它为什么不运作？会不会是宇宙阻止了它？假如穿越之后，我们必定会改变已经发生的事呢？也许，凡是会引发不可能情况的穿越，Sekimeiya 都不允许。',
        '...Someone in that silent room with me could have had the intention to trap us for an entire month. Potentially so that they could achieve a very far travel. As I thought about it, I cemented more and more how important it was to fully understand the Sekimeiya.': '……和我一起待在这间寂静房间里的人当中，也许就有人打算把我们困上整整一个月，好完成一次距离极远的穿越。{w} 越想下去，我越发确信：彻底弄清 Sekimeiya 的机制有多么重要。',
        "Sai was the one who first presented the draft of a theory I was using—that the time the Sekimeiya spent outside of its cabinet was what determined the amount of time traveled. If that was the fundamental motive of our extended imprisonment, Sai was the best candidate to suspect. He had never listened to the audio. However, that same recording also made it sound as if we'd been abandoned by the world outside, so it was potentially foolish to blame someone in the building instead.": '我此刻用的那套理论——Sekimeiya 离开展示柜的时间决定穿越的时间——最初的雏形正是 Sai 提出的。{w} 如果这就是我们被长期困住的根本动机，那 Sai 是最值得怀疑的人选。他从未听过那段录音。可那段录音听起来也像是我们被外面的世界抛弃了，因此一味怀疑楼里的某个人，也许是愚蠢的。',
        "But the reality was that we were most likely still sharing space with a murderer who had killed anywhere from one to three times. The death of the second Naomi had almost certainly been a normal homicide, but I wasn't sure if the case was the same with Isla. The culprit's actions had been linked to the Sekimeiya from the beginning, and they had managed to escape us so far. It was strange how they'd known about the Sekimeiya's powers straight away, and it had begun to seem like they were from the far future.": '但现实是，我们仍然很可能与一名杀过一人、甚至三人的凶手共处一室。第二个 Naomi 的死几乎可以肯定是普通的凶杀，至于 Isla，我就说不准了。{w} 凶手的行动从一开始就与 Sekimeiya 有关，而我们至今没能抓住对方。对方一上来就了解 Sekimeiya 的力量，这一点很蹊跷，渐渐地，我甚至觉得他们来自遥远的未来。',
        "...We could all easily have been in the middle of their process. All of us had learned about the Sekimeiya's powers. Then, someone decided to trap us for an entire month and would actually accomplish it somehow. In the future, once the required time passed, they would travel back and exist at the start of the day's events with a full understanding of the Sekimeiya.": '……我们很可能正处在对方计划的中间阶段。{w} 我们所有人都了解了 Sekimeiya 的力量。接着，某个人决定把我们困上整整一个月，而且真的会以某种方式办到。{w} 到了未来，等所需的时间一过，那个人就会穿越回来，以对 Sekimeiya 了如指掌的状态，出现在这一天的事件开始之时。',
        "They would cause what they'd once seen, which meant that at that moment, a future version of one of us existed somewhere. It was a bit paradoxical too, but depending on how they would replicate the events they'd experienced, it might've made sense. It was like the first time I'd traveled to the past, when Shiroya hadn't realized that I was from the future. What if we had already found the culprit in one of our searches but didn't realize it? Could they have impersonated their past self at some point?": '他们会促成自己曾经见过的那些事，也就是说，在这一刻，我们之中某人的未来版本正存在于某处。这同样带来些许悖论，但要看他们如何重现自己经历过的那些事件，也许就说得通。{w} 就像我第一次回到过去时，Shiroya 根本没意识到我来自未来。{w} 万一我们在某次搜索中已经找到了凶手，却没能察觉呢？对方会不会在某个时刻冒充了过去的自己？',
        "Inside, we had access to the computer that managed the security system—altering the alarm's functions was well in reach. It wasn't that simple, though. Even if one of us permanently locked the exit, the outside would have to get us out in less than a month, as it would become a life or death situation.": '从内部，我们能接触到管理安保系统的电脑——改动警报的功能并非难事。{w} 但事情没那么简单。即使我们当中有人把出口彻底锁死，外界也必须在不到一个月内把我们救出去，否则就成了生死攸关的问题。',
        "They had said that blowing off the shutters wasn't viable, but there had to be something they could do if it came down to it. An underground passage, for example; there was no way shutters alone would keep us trapped for a month. And regarding the motive, I didn't think I was being unrealistic. It might've been to use the Sekimeiya in a specific way, and I couldn't think of anything else. That would confirm that the time traveled wasn't determined with a 1:1 ratio.": '他们说过炸开卷帘门行不通，但真到那一步，总该有别的办法。比如地下通道——光靠几道卷帘门，绝不可能把我们困上一个月。{w} 至于动机，我不觉得自己是在空想。也许就是为了以某种特定方式使用 Sekimeiya，除此之外我想不出别的。那样一来，也就证实了穿越的时间并非按一比一的比例决定。',
        "When I thought of that, I came to a pretty unsettling realization. If that was the motive of someone's grand plan, the Sekimeiya would have stored a great deal of time after a month—at least one month back, probably more. We'd reached the conclusions that the range was likely proportional to the time traveled and that it most likely went through solid objects.": '想到这里，我得出了一个相当令人不安的结论。{w} 如果那就是某人宏大计划的动机，那一个月后，Sekimeiya 就会蓄下大量时间——至少能回到一个月前，恐怕还不止。我们已经推断出：重叠范围很可能与穿越的时间成正比，而且它多半能穿过固体。',
        "The minutes continued to pass, and the mutual silence remained broken. I went back over everything I'd considered, but ultimately, we would have to wait to decide further on any theory. At the very least, considering all those options would prepare me for whatever would end up happening.": '时间一分一分地过去，谁也没有开口。{w} 我把想过的一切又理了一遍，但说到底，任何理论都得等事情有了眉目才能再作判断。至少，把这些可能都想一遍，能让我对接下来无论发生什么都有所准备。',
        "We remained frozen like that for a long time, during which we all must've been thinking about Isla, Naomi, the Sekimeiya, and the culprit behind it all. The sound that resumed time's march came from one of us. We turned our blank faces and saw Katei standing up, stretching his arms a little.": '我们就那样僵坐着，过了很久。在那段时间里，每个人想必都在想着 Isla、Naomi、Sekimeiya，以及这一切背后的凶手。{w} 打破这片凝滞的声响，来自我们中的一个人。我们木然转过头，看见 Katei 站了起来，稍稍伸展着手臂。',
        "...It didn't change what I thought: they couldn't go back to the past. Shiroya and I looked at each other, but we decided to ignore them and wait.": '……这不会改变我的判断：他们回不到过去。{w} Shiroya 和我对视一眼，但我们决定不予理会，继续等下去。',
        "It was a little strange that Sai had left right after Katei. Perhaps he was still wary of him and wanted to see what he'd gone to do. I thought further on it: was the possibility of one of them going considerably back to the past truly something I could rule out? If everything was as we thought, yes. I'd personally put the Sekimeiya in its cabinet, and at that moment, I felt the cold temperature. After that, nobody had entered the room. It wouldn't have been possible for anyone to unplug the cabinet or take the Sekimeiya out later...": 'Sai 紧跟着 Katei 出去，这有点奇怪。也许他仍对 Katei 心存戒备，想看看他到底去做什么。{w} 我又往下想：他们中的一个回到相当远的过去的可能性，我真的能排除吗？{w} 如果一切都如我们所想，那确实能排除。Sekimeiya 是我亲手放进展示柜的，当时我还摸到了那股低温。那之后，没有人进过那个房间。谁也不可能事后再拔掉展示柜的电源，或者把 Sekimeiya 取出来……',
        "We remained on the floor, waiting for Katei and Sai to come back as we kept every thought to ourselves. The atmosphere had suddenly become a lot more uneasy as soon as one of us departed. Akaro kept looking at the door Katei had disappeared through, visibly doubting him. Erina, on the other hand, hadn't reacted to Sai's movements in the slightest.": '我们仍坐在地上，等着 Katei 和 Sai 回来，各自把心思藏在心里。有人一离开，气氛顿时变得紧张起来。{w} Akaro 一直盯着 Katei 消失的那扇门，显然在怀疑他。而 Erina 对 Sai 的举动毫无反应。',
        "The first room we entered was the storeroom, continuing with our backward order. It was one of the smallest rooms on the entire floor, and its purpose was still a bit unclear, as it wasn't storing anything that was particularly useful. Given how small it was, we should've left it immediately, but Shiroya noticed something that prolonged our stay.": '我们继续按倒序，先进了储藏室。这里是整层最小的房间之一，用途至今不太明确，也没存放什么特别有用的东西。{w} 地方这么小，本来看一眼就该走，可Shiroya发现了什么，让我们多留了一阵。',
        'On one of the squares touching the left wall, Shiroya had seen a slight lack of dust, which was otherwise present over every surface of the room. Even though the poor illumination made it hard to see, what seemed to be fingerprints existed on it. Not only that, but its close surroundings were a bit cleaner than the rest of the walls.': '在贴着左墙的一个方格上，Shiroya发现那里的积灰比别处少——这房间的每处表面原本都落着灰。{w} 虽然光线昏暗难以看清，但上面似乎留着指纹。不止如此，那一带也比墙面其余部分干净一些。',
        "I suppose so... But I doubt it means anything, and we can't even be sure it happened today.": '大概吧……{w} 不过我看这未必说明什么，而且也没法确定就是今天弄的。',
        '...Huh? Wh-What...?': '……{w}咦？{w}什、什么……？',
        "...All right, let's settle this quickly. Katei is lying. I was up there, and he never showed up.": '……{w}行了，这事赶紧说清楚。Katei 在撒谎。我上去过，他根本没露面。',
        "Now look at this. Someone removed the keyhole from this door to prevent us from opening it. Hm... Not only that, but the inner mechanism was broken too. This won't allow for a new handle to be inserted.": '看看这个。有人把门上的锁孔整个拆掉了，好让我们打不开。{w}嗯……不止如此，里面的机关也被弄坏了，就算想装个新把手也装不上。',
        'Yes. This entire corridor now stretches farther than the crystal rooms. I think it might extend far enough to reach outside.': '对。{w}整条走廊现在延伸得比水晶展室还远。我觉得它够长，说不定一直通到了楼外。',
        "The gaps aren't big enough to let light pass, or the door is wider than it seems. Just think about it, though. Why would this secret passage exist? If they had something to hide in it, they wouldn't have another locked door past it. They would just hide it in the secret passage itself. Otherwise, this door wouldn't be here or be locked. This passage is the secret itself. It's hidden because this door leads outside. If the middle wall didn't exist, the length of the room would reveal it.": '缝隙太窄，光透不过来；也可能是这扇门比看上去更宽。可你们想一想，这条暗道为什么会存在？{w}如果里面藏了什么，他们不必在尽头再设一道上锁的门，直接把东西藏在暗道里就行。否则，这扇门根本不必有，更不必上锁。{w}这条暗道本身就是秘密。它之所以被藏起来，是因为这扇门通向外面。要是没有中间那道墙，房间的长度就会把它露出来。',
        "Don't get me wrong. I'm not worried. I'm just intrigued. How is it even remotely possible the Sekimeiya exists? How did it make it here without anyone finding out about its powers? These big picture questions are what I'm most lost about.": '别误会。我不是担心，只是好奇。{w}Sekimeiya 这种东西究竟怎么可能存在？它又是怎么一路来到这儿，却没有一个人察觉它的能力？我最想不通的，就是这些大方向上的问题。',
        'I thought something was noteworthy. Even though a perfect hiding spot existed, the Sekimeiya had never been hidden in it. ...Why? Earlier, it had been hidden in the storeroom. Therefore, the person who hid it there was probably not aware of the movable wall.': '我觉得有件事值得留意。明明有这样一处绝佳的藏匿之所，Sekimeiya 却从未被藏在那里。{w}……为什么？先前它是被藏在储藏室里的。也就是说，把它藏起来的那个人，多半并不知道这面可以移动的墙。',
        "What about the lobby? The hallway doors are locked until 9:00, isn't that right?": '大厅呢？走廊的门不是要等到 {time=9} 才开吗？',
        "What about the lobby? The hallway doors are locked until 9 a.m., isn't that right?": '大厅呢？走廊的门不是要等到 {time=9} 才开吗？',
        "With a brief sigh indicating that he wasn't fond of my proposition, Sai turned his wrist. I looked at his watch and saw that the displayed time was 14:56.": 'Sai 轻叹一声，显然并不赞同我的提议，随即转动手腕。我看向他的手表，上面显示的时间是 {time=14:56.}。',
        "With a brief sigh indicating that he wasn't fond of my proposition, Sai turned his wrist. I looked at his watch and saw that the displayed time was 2:56 p.m.": 'Sai 轻叹一声，显然并不赞同我的提议，随即转动手腕。我看向他的手表，上面显示的时间是 {time=14:56.}。',
        "Almost 15:00, I see. We're past the halfway point, so with all that's happened, let's spend the last six hours calmly until the police enter and we can have a better understanding of what's been going on.": '都快 {time=15} 了啊。时间已经过半，既然发生了这么多事，剩下的六个小时就安静度过吧，等警察进来，我们也好更清楚地弄明白到底出了什么状况。',
        "Almost 3 p.m., I see. We're past the halfway point, so with all that's happened, let's spend the last six hours calmly until the police enter and we can have a better understanding of what's been going on.": '都快 {time=15} 了啊。时间已经过半，既然发生了这么多事，剩下的六个小时就安静度过吧，等警察进来，我们也好更清楚地弄明白到底出了什么状况。',
        "Sai and Katei rolled their eyes, but they kept quiet. If we were alone with both Sekimeiya locked in place as well, nobody could use them. Everyone looked uncertain, and Sai seemed depressed. He'd made it obvious he was enjoying his time in the tower, and instead of having another six hours to play with a time travel device, it was already over.": 'Sai 和 Katei 翻了个白眼，但都没作声。只要我们单独待在这里，两个 Sekimeiya 也都锁在原处，谁也没法使用它们。{w}众人神色犹疑，Sai 则显得颇为沮丧。他之前明显很享受在塔里的时光；本来还有六个小时能摆弄时间穿越装置，现在就这么结束了。',
        "The four main possibilities are: the culprit isn't one of us and we kept missing them. The Sekimeiya teleported there randomly. The culprit made the Sekimeiya teleport there without touching it. One of us will go back to the past after spending six hours here.": '主要可能性有四种：犯人并不在我们之中，只是我们一直没撞见对方。{w} Sekimeiya 随机传送到了那里。{w} 犯人没有触碰 Sekimeiya，却让它传送到了那里。{w} 我们中的某个人会在这里待满六小时后回到过去。',
        "No matter which one is right, before we lock ourselves away, we need to thoroughly inspect this bedroom. Both levels. If a Sekimeiya's already here, the imprisonment wouldn't mean anything, as anyone could leave at any time after making sure nobody else is in range. A key would do the trick too, and we've seen that some kind of replication has occurred. We found two identical suitcases and two Naomis.": '不管哪一种才是真的，在把自己关起来之前，我们都得把这间卧室彻底检查一遍。上下两层都要查。{w}如果这里已经有一个 Sekimeiya，那我们把自己关起来就毫无意义——只要确认没有其他人在重叠范围内，谁都能随时离开。一把钥匙也能达到同样的效果，而我们已经见过某种复制现象：两个一模一样的行李箱，还有两个 Naomi。',
        "Searching for an extra key to this bedroom might sound paranoid since nothing indicates it exists, but it's necessary. If we ignore these precautions, we're leaving a potential escape route for the culprit that can be used at any time. They have higher knowledge of the Sekimeiya than we do, so we have no guarantee that they couldn't obtain a key they would hide later, use it to escape, go back to the past, and preemptively hide a replicated key inside knowing we'd lock ourselves in here.": '现在去找这间卧室的备用钥匙，听起来或许有些疑神疑鬼，毕竟没有任何迹象表明它存在，但这一步是必要的。要是忽略这些防范，就等于给犯人留下一条随时能用的退路。{w}对方对 Sekimeiya 的了解远胜于我们，所以我们无法保证他们不会弄到一把钥匙：他们可以先把钥匙藏好，再用它逃出去，回到过去，然后提前在这间房里藏下一把复制钥匙——毕竟他们知道我们会把自己锁在这里。',
        "...Yeah. Our intention is to be safe in here, so let's search around beforehand.": '……{w}是啊。我们就是想在这里确保安全，所以先搜一遍吧。',
        "I wouldn't say they'd have an easy time of it, but let's see... Hey, jackass, if you're actually here, we're gonna lock ourselves in this room for six hours. If you intend to kill us to continue with your plan at some point, hurry up and do it now before you need to deal with breaking the door down.": '我倒不觉得他们能轻松得手，不过……走着瞧吧。{w}喂，混账东西，你要是真在这儿，我们接下来会把自己锁在这间房里六个小时。{w}如果你打算之后杀了我们，好继续你的计划，那就趁现在赶紧动手，省得到时候还得费劲破门。',
        "That seemed to assuage Akaro's worries. The six of us went to the upper section of the bedroom to inspect it. I used that time to try to prevent something really bad from happening, as Sai's insistence made me realize something else was to come.": '这番话似乎打消了 Akaro 的顾虑。{w}我们六个人来到卧室上层检查。我趁那段时间设法阻止真正糟糕的事发生，因为 Sai 的坚持让我意识到，后面还有别的变故。',
        "When we were up top, I made sure nobody had the funny idea of leaving anything hidden for later. I am very sure that, right now, both sections of this bedroom don't contain anything the culprit has deliberately left here. I'll begin.": '我们在上面时，我已经确认过，没人动歪脑筋把东西提前藏起来。现在我可以肯定，这间卧室的上下两层都没有犯人故意留下的东西。{w}我先来。',
        "My objection had a reason behind it. That method of showing we didn't possess anything was highly disadvantageous for me. Even though letting them find my key wouldn't have been the worst, Shiroya and I would've become very suspicious, and if anyone realized what the key was for, they would all see the Sekimeiya in the locker. Furthermore, it'd bring back the commotion Erina had been trying to eliminate. That was why I took the single chance I believed I had.": '我出言反对，是有原因的。{w}那种证明我们身上没藏东西的做法，对我极为不利。就算被他们搜出我的钥匙还不算最糟，我和 Shiroya 也会立刻成为重点怀疑对象；而一旦有人想明白那把钥匙是开什么的，所有人就会看到储物柜里的 Sekimeiya。更何况，那还会重新掀起 Erina 一直在设法消除的骚动。所以我才抓住了自认为唯一的一次机会。',
        "I immediately knew that I had sounded a little off. It was intentional, to set the expectation that nothing would be found on me. As such, when he got to the right pocket of my pants, he looked at me with a frown, noticing that I'd been incorrect.": '话一出口，我就知道自己语气有点不对。那是我故意的，好让他以为我身上什么都搜不出来。{w}所以，当他摸到我裤子右边口袋时，皱着眉看向我——他发觉我方才说错了。',
        "...Okay, you're clean too. Katei, mind being next?": '……好，你也没问题。{w}Katei，下一个你来？',
        "Before going up the ladder, I'd thought that I had only one way to avoid being found out; I would've been easily noticed if I attempted to leave the key somewhere. Taking advantage of the fact that I also had the cabinet key and that it was slightly bigger, I'd removed the locker key from my back pocket and slid it into the same pocket as the cabinet's. Until that point, I'd avoided keeping both together so that I didn't produce metallic noises as I walked.": '上梯子之前我就想过，要避免被识破，我只有一条路可走。若想把钥匙藏在别处，必定会被人轻易发现。{w}幸好我身上还带着展示柜的钥匙，而且比储物柜那把稍大一些；我便把储物柜钥匙从后裤袋取出，塞进装展示柜钥匙的同一个口袋。此前我一直刻意不让两把钥匙放在一起，免得走路时发出金属碰撞的声音。',
        "The locker key was small. I'd purposely put it horizontally behind the cabinet's so that Sai would press his hand on it and only notice the bigger shape at the front. Fortunately, I'd been able to abuse his minor surprise by taking out the cabinet key and leaving the smaller one inside. When the body inspection proceeded, he assumed the right pocket was clean and didn't check it again.": '储物柜的钥匙很小。我故意把它横着塞在展示柜钥匙后面，这样 Sai 摸到时，只会注意到前面那个更大的轮廓。{w}幸好我趁着他那一瞬间的惊讶，把展示柜钥匙取了出来，小钥匙仍留在口袋里。之后继续搜身时，他便以为右边口袋已经查过，没有再检查一遍。',
        'After staring at it, Sai put the key back in. In the next pocket, he found something else. For the third time in a row, they were keys.': 'Sai 盯着它看了半晌，把钥匙放了回去。{w}他又在下一个口袋里摸到了别的东西。这已经是连续第三次摸到钥匙了。',
        "They don't work. You're done, then.": '都开不了。{w}那你也查完了。',
        "You're right... Maybe they wanted to avoid every possibility of being spotted and didn't want to step into hallway A. The fingerprints that you saw... Are they clear enough to be useful? If the police can figure out who they belong to, that could be a path to the culprit.": '你说得对……也许他们想杜绝一切被人看到的可能，所以不愿意踏进 A走廊。{w}你看到的那些指纹……清晰到能派上用场吗？如果警方能查出指纹属于谁，那或许就是追到犯人的一条线索。',
        "Yeah. There's one more thing, too. When we discovered the secret door, my first thought was that someone bypassed our searches by hiding there.": '嗯。还有一点。{w}我们发现那扇暗门时，我首先想到的是，有人藏在那里，躲过了我们的搜查。',
        "Huh... I suppose they could've used the Sekimeiya to teleport inside without opening the wall, but that doesn't sound likely. Anyway, who's next?": '唔……{w}他们也可能用 Sekimeiya 直接传送进去，根本不用开墙，不过这听起来不太可能。{w}总之，下一个是谁？',
        "Shiroya volunteered. In her case, nothing was found in her clothes. Her purse was almost empty and only contained a wallet, two of the three tickets we'd bought for the event, our personal identification to match the tickets, and the key to my house.": 'Shiroya 主动上前。{w}她身上什么都没搜出来。她的手提包里几乎空无一物，只有一只钱包、我们为活动买的三张票中的两张、用来核对门票的身份证件，以及我家的钥匙。',
        "She moved ahead. Usually, it would've been worth considering that the person who proposed the arrangement had a secret reason, but I knew Erina was genuine. Sai gently made sure she hadn't been concealing anything, and by letting us know that her purse was clean as well, he put an end to our last measure. Personal keys and identification had also been found in her purse. We were specifically searching for hidden keys, so even though it was normal we all possessed ours, Sai made sure to confirm that their shape didn't match the bedroom door's.": '她走上前。按理说，该想一想提出这个办法的人是不是另有隐情，但我知道 Erina 是真心实意的。Sai 不紧不慢地确认她没藏任何东西，又告诉我们她的手提包也没有问题，我们最后一道措施到此结束。{w}她的包里同样只有她自己的钥匙和身份证明。我们要找的正是藏起来的钥匙，因此虽然人人带着自己的钥匙再正常不过，Sai 还是逐一确认了它们的形状与卧室门锁不符。',
        "I feel like under the bathroom carpet is good enough. Like you said, it's not too important. Regarding the handle, no great spot comes to mind, but it doesn't matter anyway. The attic's full of removable handles, so someone outside could probably unscrew one to use it on the door if they really wanted to open it. In case that happens, we have the chain to rely on.": '我觉得藏在卫生间地毯下面就可以了。就像你说的，这本来也不太重要。{w}至于外把手，我一时想不出什么好地方，不过反正无所谓。阁楼里可拆的把手多得是，外面的人若真想开门，卸一个下来装上去就行。真到那一步，还有门链拦着。',
        "I unscrewed the outer handle too and left both of them under the bed in the opposite bedroom. In the door, only one hole became visible, as the keyhole wasn't found on the handles themselves. I made sure that the door couldn't be opened through the hole. A very short metal cylinder was poking out, but it was incredibly tight; we weren't going to turn it from the inside. When I was certain, I asked one last time.": '外侧的把手我也一并卸下，两个都放到对面卧室的床底。{w}门上只露出一个孔，因为锁孔并不在把手上。我确认过，光凭这个孔打不开门。孔里探出一小截金属圆柱，但卡得极紧，从内侧根本拧不动。确认无误后，我最后问了一次。',
        'Hm, 15:08.': '嗯，{time=15:08.}',
        'Hm, 3:08 p.m.': '嗯，{time=15:08.}',
        "Erina was sitting on a bed. She didn't pay much attention to our presence, so we silently sat on the opposite one. Although six hours still had to pass, I promptly realized that I was still exhausted. It was possible I could sleep and fast-forward to {time=21.}": 'Erina 坐在一张床上，没怎么理会我们，我们便默默坐到对面那张床上。{w}虽说还有六个小时要熬，我很快意识到自己依旧疲惫不堪。说不定睡一觉，就能直接睡到 {time=21.}。',
        "Erina was sitting on a bed. She didn't pay much attention to our presence, so we silently sat on the opposite one.{w} Although six hours still had to pass, I promptly realized that I was still exhausted. It was possible I could sleep and fast-forward to 21:00.": 'Erina 坐在一张床上，没怎么理会我们，我们便默默坐到对面那张床上。{w}虽说还有六个小时要熬，我很快意识到自己依旧疲惫不堪。说不定睡一觉，就能直接睡到 {time=21.}。',
        "Erina was sitting on a bed. She didn't pay much attention to our presence, so we silently sat on the opposite one. Although six hours still had to pass, I promptly realized that I was still exhausted. It was possible I could sleep and fast-forward to 21:00.": 'Erina 坐在一张床上，没怎么理会我们，我们便默默坐到对面那张床上。{w}虽说还有六个小时要熬，我很快意识到自己依旧疲惫不堪。说不定睡一觉，就能直接睡到 {time=21.}。',
        "Erina was sitting on a bed. She didn't pay much attention to our presence, so we silently sat on the opposite one.{w} Although six hours still had to pass, I promptly realized that I was still exhausted. It was possible I could sleep and fast-forward to 9 p.m.": 'Erina 坐在一张床上，没怎么理会我们，我们便默默坐到对面那张床上。{w}虽说还有六个小时要熬，我很快意识到自己依旧疲惫不堪。说不定睡一觉，就能直接睡到 {time=21.}。',
        "Erina was sitting on a bed. She didn't pay much attention to our presence, so we silently sat on the opposite one. Although six hours still had to pass, I promptly realized that I was still exhausted. It was possible I could sleep and fast-forward to 9 p.m.": 'Erina 坐在一张床上，没怎么理会我们，我们便默默坐到对面那张床上。{w}虽说还有六个小时要熬，我很快意识到自己依旧疲惫不堪。说不定睡一觉，就能直接睡到 {time=21.}。',
        "It was time to disconnect. I'd been actively trying to piece everything together, but after choosing to abandon that, only time would force me to go back, in the case that something horrible awaited us at the end of the road. At least, that was what I'd been ready to accept.": '我该停止想这些了。我一直在努力想拼凑出全貌，但既然选择放手，就只有时间能逼我重新面对——假如路的尽头真有什么可怕的东西在等着我们。{w}至少，我已经准备好接受这一点了。',
        "It was no accident. Isla saw something inside that cabinet, so she must've been lured there. Katei could've made her disappear; he's known about the Sekimeiya for longer than anyone else. Then, he showed up after he left Isla's body in the cabinet... You two have experienced what the Sekimeiya does, but I don't know how to think about it.": '那不是意外。Isla 在展示柜里看见了什么，所以一定是被人引过去的。Katei 可能让她消失了；他了解 Sekimeiya 的时间比任何人都长。{w} 然后，他把 Isla 的遗体留在展示柜里，自己又现身了……你们俩已经见识过 Sekimeiya 的作用，可我不知道该怎么看待这件事。',
        'It was clear that Erina was attaching herself to the slightest gleam of hope that still persisted. The recording "proved" that Isla would be alive in the future, so Erina needed the time to pass to know if there was any trust left to be placed in it. She must\'ve suggested waiting in the room in the hope of nothing occurring at 21:00.': '看得出来，Erina 正紧紧抓住最后一丝尚存的希望。那段录音「证明」了 Isla 在未来会活着，所以 Erina 需要等时间过去，才能知道它是否还值得相信。一定是她提议在房间里等到 {time=21.}，盼着那时什么都不会发生。',
        'It was clear that Erina was attaching herself to the slightest gleam of hope that still persisted. The recording "proved" that Isla would be alive in the future, so Erina needed the time to pass to know if there was any trust left to be placed in it. She must\'ve suggested waiting in the room in the hope of nothing occurring at 9 p.m.': '看得出来，Erina 正紧紧抓住最后一丝尚存的希望。那段录音「证明」了 Isla 在未来会活着，所以 Erina 需要等时间过去，才能知道它是否还值得相信。一定是她提议在房间里等到 {time=21.}，盼着那时什么都不会发生。',
        "At least, that was what I thought until I remembered that the two Naomi bodies defied that belief. I believed that no matter what had happened to Isla, being dead inside the cabinet had to be the end of her path. However, two identical corpses hinted that the Sekimeiya could have some sway even after death. That was the actual hope Erina had to rely on—the recording didn't guarantee a bright future even if it turned out to be legitimate.": '至少，我原本是这么想的——直到我记起那两具 Naomi 的遗体，这个念头才被推翻。{w} 我曾相信，无论 Isla 遭遇了什么，死在展示柜里都必然是她这条路的终点。然而，两具一模一样的尸体暗示着，Sekimeiya 在死后仍可能施加某种影响。那才是 Erina 真正能依靠的希望——即使那段录音是真的，也并不能保证一个光明的未来。',
        "In that instant, I felt a bubble of hope growing in my head. The Sekimeiya hadn't caused any apparent effect when it touched Isla's dead body, even though we might not have seen it immediately. If that had created a living version of her at an earlier point in time like I speculated with Naomi... My thoughts were directed to Miiya once again.": '那一瞬间，我脑中仿佛有一个希望的泡沫正在膨胀。{w} Sekimeiya 触碰到 Isla 的遗体时，并没有造成任何明显的效果——尽管我们也许没能立刻看出来。如果它像我对 Naomi 的推测那样，在更早的时间点创造出了一个活着的她……我的思绪又一次转向了 Miiya。',
        "...With that sentence, the huge but simple possibility opened up in my mind. I hadn't considered it at all since I'd been blinded by conspiracies, but I immediately understood why Shiroya reached that idea.": '……{w}听到这话，一个巨大却简单的可能性出现在我脑中。此前我完全没想到，因为我一直被种种阴谋猜测蒙住了眼，但我立刻明白了 Shiroya 为什么会想到这一点。',
        '...I didn\'t want to deny it, but it wasn\'t that simple. In fact, nothing about her fate had changed. I could assemble things the following way: "when Isla disappeared from the cabinet, she went far into the past. The range should\'ve been a lot bigger, but we might be wrong about that part. In a month, that Isla will somehow enter the tower".': '……我并不想否认，可事情没那么简单。{w} 事实上，她的命运丝毫没有改变。{w} 我只能这样拼凑：「Isla 从展示柜里消失时，回到了很久以前。重叠范围本该大得多，不过这一点也许是我们弄错了。一个月后，那个 Isla 会以某种方式进入塔里。」',
        'Tragically, no matter what I thought up, the following step had to be: "Isla travels to the past and ends up dead in the cabinet". There was no way to end it differently. However, even though the voice recorder had appeared in Isla\'s purse, the origin of it was still unexplained with that theory.': '可悲的是，无论我怎么设想，下一步都只能是：「Isla 回到过去，最后死在展示柜里。」没有别的可能。{w} 然而，尽管录音笔出现在 Isla 的包里，这个说法仍然解释不了它的来历。',
        "Isla said they'd been hanging out a lot, so as I said, conceptually, it's incredibly unreasonable to think that she spent the time as her friend knowing how everything would play out. You saw her once when she hadn't gone to school, which should be an impossibility since she would've known you would see her, and she would've avoided that.": 'Isla 说她们经常一起玩。所以就像我说的，从道理上讲，她明知一切会怎么发展，却还以朋友的身份度过那段时间，实在说不通。{w} 有一次你看见她没去上学，这本来不可能发生——她明知会被你撞见，就该避开才对。',
        "Instead of continuing, Erina turned around and lay on the bed while Shiroya and I looked lost. Her idea had a lot of promise, but it appeared ultimately impossible until we had more information. I'd usually been able to create a patchwork design out of the loose ends of a theory, but in that case, I couldn't think of anything else. Needless to say, I didn't think any part of my memory had been erased upon traveling—although, to be fair, perhaps I wouldn't have realized it.": 'Erina 没有再说下去，转身躺倒在床上，我和 Shiroya 则愣在原地。她的设想很有希望，但在掌握更多线索之前，似乎终究行不通。{w} 换作平时，我总能把理论里那些散落的线头拼成一个勉强自洽的轮廓，可这一次，我再也想不出别的了。不用说，我并不认为自己在穿越时丢失了某段记忆——不过话说回来，就算真丢了，我大概也不会察觉。',
        "I breathed deeply, but anxiety began to crawl up my back, exacerbated by my own lack of knowledge. I hated exploring all sorts of options without knowing if I'd ever find the truth. Isla's bleak ending had already been revealed to us, making the process of putting together its outline all the more draining.": '我深深吸了口气，焦虑却沿着脊背爬上来。因为对真相一无所知，这份焦虑越发强烈。{w} 我讨厌在不知道能否找到真相的情况下，把所有可能性都试一遍。Isla 凄惨的结局已经摆在我们眼前，要把它的轮廓拼出来，就更让人心力交瘁。',
        '...Hm? ...Wh-What...?': '……嗯？{w}……什、什么……？',
        'Atsuki! Did you really think you could get out of this with simple threats? Those will not work on me, so once we make it out, you can say goodbye to your normal life.': 'Atsuki！{w} 你以为靠几句威胁就能脱身？我可不怕这一套。等我们出去，你就跟正常生活告别吧。',
        'And then... Isla died. You were behind that, right? You tried to make us believe that you were sleeping as it happened! How did I swallow that lie...? Shiroya found the hidden passage in the storeroom? How was I so stupid...? You were about to use it...!': '然后……Isla 死了。那也是你干的吧？你还想让我们相信，事发时你正在睡觉！我怎么就信了这种鬼话……？{w} Shiroya 在储藏室里找到了暗门？我怎么这么蠢……？你本来就要用那扇门……！',
        '...Are you just fucking around, or are you really this dumb?': '……{w}你他妈是在耍我，还是真就蠢到这个地步？',
        "I suppose you're not going to give up. You two are the culprits behind this incident. Why were you in the first group of the guided visit when you've shown no interest in the gems? Now that I've learned about it, you must confess. I know you didn't attempt to threaten me individually since I work here and there's no way I'd give in to you.": '看来你是不会认了。这件事就是你们俩干的。{w}你对宝石一直没什么兴趣，为什么偏偏排在参观的第一批？既然我已经查清了，你就老实交代吧。我知道你没单独来威胁我——我在这里工作，绝不可能向你低头。',
        "Sai and Akaro weren't there. From the hatch, I could see the entire lower bedroom devoid of any human presence.": 'Sai 和 Akaro 不在那里。{w}透过活板门望下去，下面整间卧室里不见半个人影。',
        "I went down the ladder. They weren't in the wardrobe or under the bed. Countless questions hammered from inside my head, but I immediately went to check the door.": '我顺着梯子下去。{w}衣橱里没有，床底下也没有。{w}无数疑问在脑中翻腾，可我还是先去查看房门。',
        "It had to be around 15:30. I doubted we'd been in the bedroom for more than 25 minutes. No matter what had happened, it was clear that calmness wasn't what awaited us.": '那时应该差不多是{time=15:30.}了。我们在卧室里待的时间，想必不超过二十五分钟。无论发生了什么，有一点很清楚：等着我们的绝不是平静。',
        "It had to be around 3:30 p.m. I doubted we'd been in the bedroom for more than 25 minutes. No matter what had happened, it was clear that calmness wasn't what awaited us.": '那时应该差不多是{time=15:30.}了。我们在卧室里待的时间，想必不超过二十五分钟。无论发生了什么，有一点很清楚：等着我们的绝不是平静。',
        "I don't want to. I'm not sure what Akaro's deal is, but if Sai was the only one to escape, I would've thought that his motive was to make us chase after him to undo the bedroom lock. If they're still in the tower, there's not much they can do. They can go to the past or hide the Sekimeiya, but they'd still be trapped in here. Even if they went far back enough to exit the tower, there's no reason for us to chase them.": '我不想走。Akaro 到底想干什么我不清楚，但如果只有 Sai 一个人逃了，我会以为他的动机是引我们去追，好让我们从里面解开卧室的锁。{w} 他们若还留在塔里，能做的不多。回到过去也好，把 Sekimeiya 藏起来也好，终究还是困在这里。就算他们回到足够早的时候离开这座塔，我们也没有追上去的理由。',
        '"Why is the culprit hiding the Sekimeiya if we\'ll be able to find it?" That recurring question felt similar to our present situation. What could they have wanted to achieve by making it out? Unless they wanted to experiment with the Sekimeiya or hide it, the only reason I could produce was that they\'d needed to go back in time to finish something off.': '「既然我们迟早能找到，犯人为什么要藏起 Sekimeiya？」这个反复出现的问题，与眼前的处境颇为相似。{w} 他们逃出去究竟想达成什么？除非是为了试验 Sekimeiya 或者把它藏起来，我能想到的唯一理由，就是他们需要回到过去，了结某件事。',
        "To open the door, the key would have been needed. There was no other way to accomplish it. However, we knew it couldn't have been inside the bedroom. As I'd thought earlier, the only way to undo the lock was by using the key from the outside and then unsetting the chain from the inside.": '要开门就必须用钥匙，没有别的办法。可我们知道，钥匙不可能在卧室里。{w} 正如我之前想的，唯一能打开这把锁的办法，是从外面用钥匙开锁，再从里面摘掉门链。',
        'With my eyes closed and without giving it much thought, I could reach a very easy explanation, similar to what Sai proposed before we\'d locked ourselves in the bedroom: "they left through the door and went to the past with the Sekimeiya. Then, they opened the bedroom\'s door with the key that we hid under the bathroom carpet. To escape, they simply pulled the door open from the inside, which would\'ve been slightly open".': '我闭上眼，几乎不用多想，就找到了一个极简单的解释，跟 Sai 在我们把自己锁进卧室前的说法差不多：{w}「他们从门离开，带着 Sekimeiya 回到过去。然后用我们藏在浴室地毯下的钥匙打开了卧室的门。要出去，只需从里面把门拉开——那时的门应该已经开了一条缝。」',
        "Their escape method, though, had a real origin. Sai's and Akaro's thoughts.": '然而他们的逃脱方式却有着真实的起源：{w} Sai 和 Akaro 的念头。',
        "There was a slight problem: unlocking the door from the outside would make a bit of noise. If it happened before they thought of the concept, the loop would have no origin, as the noise itself would tell them what to do. I couldn't think of a way to circumvent it easily. If the key could fit under the door, their future selves could've slid it inside. However, the gap wasn't big enough, or else we would've simply locked ourselves in and slid it out of the bedroom.": '但有个小问题：从外面开锁会发出一点声响。如果这声响在他们想到这个主意之前就已经出现，循环就没有起点，因为那声响本身就会告诉他们该怎么做。{w} 我一时想不出能轻易绕开这一点的办法。要是钥匙能从门缝底下塞进去，未来的他们就可以把钥匙送进来。可惜门缝不够宽——否则我们只要把自己锁进卧室，从门缝把钥匙推出去就行了。',
        "Beyond that concept, I felt that Katei's story was iffy. As likely as it was that Sai and Akaro could've conspired together, nothing told us Katei hadn't been in on it too. They could've spent half an hour unlocking the door and then made it seem as if they'd magically escaped. Katei immediately suggested unlocking the bedroom to us, making for a simple motive if all three of them were secretly against Erina's request.": '除此之外，我还觉得 Katei 的说法有些可疑。Sai 和 Akaro 合谋的可能性固然不小，可也没有任何证据能说明 Katei 没有参与其中。{w} 他们大可花上半个小时慢慢开锁，再装作是凭空逃了出去。而 Katei 立刻提议我们打开卧室门——若这三人暗地里都反对 Erina 的要求，动机就再简单不过了。',
        'Wait, wh-who...? What the fuck happened to this handle...?': '等等，谁、谁啊……？{w}这门把手怎么他妈搞成这样……？',
        'Katei? Is that his name? Where should I remember him from?': 'Katei？他叫这个名字？{w}我怎么会记得他？',
        "Even if the chain can be ignored from the outside, we'll easily hear it if someone tries to force it open again. I was probably wrong before. We should've kept the key inside to avoid all this. I'll keep it with me. This way, if Sai comes, he won't be able to enter or let anyone leave easily.": '就算外面的人能无视链条，只要有人再想硬撬，我们很容易就能听见。{w}之前是我错了。钥匙本该留在里面，也就不会有这些事。钥匙我来保管。这样，就算 Sai 来了，他也进不来，也没法轻易把谁放出去。',
        "I have no idea, but I don't think it's 16:00 yet.": '我不知道，但我想还没到 {time=16}。',
        "I have no idea, but I don't think it's 4 p.m. yet.": '我不知道，但我想还没到 {time=16}。',
        "I understood why Katei didn't want me to humor Akaro, but not too long ago, I'd considered the possibility that the Sekimeiya could cause memory loss. I wanted to know if that was possible, as it could've let Isla's story occur as we'd imagined it. If Akaro had traveled through time after escaping, it could have been the direct cause of the state he was in.": '我明白 Katei 为什么不想让我顺着 Akaro 的话说。可就在不久前，我还考虑过 Sekimeiya 会不会造成记忆缺失。我想确认这种可能，因为若真如此，Isla 的说法就有可能像我们设想的那样成立。{w}如果 Akaro 是在逃出去之后穿越了时间，那很可能就是他现在这副样子的直接原因。',
        "Huh... I don't know how to answer this. I sympathize with you two, as I've already said. That's why it's surprising to see you lying like this.": '嗯……{w}我不知道该怎么回答。我说过了，我同情你们俩。也正因如此，看到你们这样撒谎，我才会觉得意外。',
        "...Are you out of your mind? Why the hell would we tell you anything about us? No, I get it, the Sekimeiya must've inserted false memories into your head, right? Is that what you're going to say next?": '……你脑子有问题吗？我们凭什么要把自己的事告诉你？{w}不，我明白了，一定是 Sekimeiya 往你脑子里塞了假记忆，对吧？你接下来是不是就要这么说？',
        "...I could tell you weren't serious, but why did you mention the Sekimeiya?": '……{w}我听得出来你不是认真的，可你为什么要提 Sekimeiya？',
        "...I'm not sure.": '……{w}我也不清楚。',
        'Wha... Isla? Isla!': '什……Isla？{w} Isla！',
        'All of a sudden, Erina snapped. Her whole face shifted into the most desperate expression a human could make, and she dashed toward the door, slamming into it. Ignoring that she had the right key and that the chain was set, she tried to pull it open frantically until her motions abruptly stopped.': 'Erina 忽然失控了。她整张脸扭曲成了一个人所能露出的最绝望的样子，朝门口冲去，一头撞在门上。{w}她明明手里有钥匙，门链也还挂着，却发疯似的想把门拉开，动作却突然停住了。',
        "She was suffering... I could hear her yell. She's here, outside this door. There. You all hear her too... right?": '她很难受……我听见她在喊。她就在这儿，就在门外。{w}听，你们也都听见了吧……？',
        "He knew what time it was and didn't remember touching the Sekimeiya even once... If he was being honest, it indicated that he hadn't traveled far through time. His internal clock would've differed from ours if he had, and if he'd looked at the time, he would've known it was earlier than it should've been, as he didn't remember the exact moment of the travel. ...So if his memory issues were caused by the Sekimeiya, it was unlikely it was due to traveling farther than I had yet.": '他知道现在是几点，却完全不记得自己碰过 Sekimeiya……{w}如果他说的是实话，就说明他穿越的时间跨度并不大。要是跨得远，他的时间感就会和我们不同；只要他看过一眼钟，就该发现时间比他以为的要早——毕竟他并不记得自己穿越的那一刻。{w}……所以，就算他的记忆问题是 Sekimeiya 造成的，原因也不太可能是他穿越得比我更远。',
        "Lastly, there's a much easier solution: that there was always someone else inside the building who we missed. Just now, Erina acted like she heard Isla outside the bedroom. Even though nobody else heard anything, if it truly happened, she could've opened the door for Akaro and Sai if her existence there wasn't in any capacity derived from their escape.": '最后，还有一个简单得多的解释：这栋楼里一直有另一个人，只是我们漏掉了。{w} 刚才 Erina 那副样子，就像她在卧室外听见了 Isla 的声音。虽然其他人都没听见，但若真有此事，而且她出现在那里与 Akaro 和 Sai 的逃脱无关，那她就有可能替他们打开了门。',
        "I tried to calm Erina down by saying that nobody was outside, and I thought that it was impossible. However, it shouldn't be. It follows Shiroya's theory from earlier, in fact. If Isla went weeks back in time, dying in the cabinet must be the final step of her travels. However, she said that her friend would wait for her outside the tower, meaning that there can be a living Isla somewhere right now.": '我安慰 Erina 说外面没有人，当时也认定那不可能。可仔细想想，未必不可能。事实上，这正合 Shiroya 先前的推论。{w} 如果 Isla 回到了几周之前，那么死在展示柜里就该是她这趟穿越的终点。可她说她的朋友会在塔外等她——也就是说，此刻在某处，很可能还有一个活着的 Isla。',
        "...Okay. As long as you don't run off with it or anything.": '……{w}好吧。只要你别拿着它跑掉就行。',
        "Hence, my idea had to be shifted a little bit. I would go down and attempt to open the door. If it was open, it'd mean that the loop could be completed. I'd leave, and on the crystal floor, I would unlock Naomi's locker and activate the Sekimeiya. It was likely I would go back far enough, given how long the Sekimeiya had already been there. Then, when the time came, I would unlock the door from the outside with the key Erina had handed me, allowing the loop to be created.": '所以，我的计划得稍微改一改。{w} 我先下楼试着开门。如果门开着，就说明这个循环能够成立。我会离开房间，到水晶层打开 Naomi 的储物柜，启动 Sekimeiya。{w} 考虑到 Sekimeiya 已经在那里放了那么久，我多半会被送回到足够早的时间。然后，等时候到了，我再用 Erina 交给我的钥匙从外面开门，让这个循环得以形成。',
        "Could such a thing really not occur...? I sighed, slightly disappointed, and set the chain again. Figuring the trick out would've felt like good progress toward understanding the Sekimeiya, so it was unfortunate that I couldn't know the reason why it hadn't functioned.": '这种事真的不可能发生吗……？我有些失望地叹了口气，重新扣上门链。{w} 若能看破其中的诀窍，对理解 Sekimeiya 来说该是很大的进展；可惜我弄不清它为什么没有奏效。',
        "This is really frustrating... There's no way to know why it didn't work. While it's easy to assume that the existence of this kind of loop is impossible, or perhaps willingly creating one is... I can't draw a single conclusion. There are too many factors that could've stopped the loop from reaching its end, effectively denying its existence.": '真是让人心烦……根本无从得知它为什么没有成功。{w} 大可以简单认定这种循环不可能存在，或者说，凭人的意志去制造一个循环本就不可能……可我连一个确定的结论都下不了。有太多因素都可能让循环走不到终点，也就等于否定了它的存在。',
        "For example, what if Akaro is lying to us? He became cautious of my presence as soon as I approached the door, so if I'd gotten it to open, he might've restrained me if what he's after is preventing us from leaving and allowing Sai to roam freely. That could be why he prompted the four of us to go up top.": '比如，万一 Akaro 在骗我们呢？{w} 我一靠近门，他就对我起了戒心。要是我真把门弄开了，而他所图的正是阻止我们离开、让 Sai 在外自由行动，那他也许会当场制住我。他之所以鼓动我们四个人到上面去，原因或许就在这里。',
        "If he did that, I couldn't proceed, so the door would never have been open. Similarly, what if Sai took the Sekimeiya out of Naomi's locker? Downstairs, I couldn't have used it to go back to the past, yet again cutting off the loop.": '如果他真那么做，我就没法继续下去，那扇门也永远不会被打开。{w} 同理，要是 Sai 把 Sekimeiya 从 Naomi 的储物柜里拿走了呢？我在楼下就没法用它回到过去，循环同样会断掉。',
        "Right... When Shiroya and I traveled from the cleaning room, even though the cart disappeared, it didn't appear in the attic with us, as the bodies we appeared in were most likely identical to how they had been at 12:10, when both of us were in the attic in those same locations...": '对了……我和 Shiroya 从清洁间穿越时，推车虽然消失了，却没有和我们一起出现在阁楼。因为我们现身时所用的身体，多半与 {time=12:10} 时的我们完全相同——那时我和 Shiroya 都在阁楼里，而且就在相同的位置……',
        "Right... When Shiroya and I traveled from the cleaning room, even though the cart disappeared, it didn't appear in the attic with us, as the bodies we appeared in were most likely identical to how they had been at 12:10 p.m., when both of us were in the attic in those same locations...": '对了……我和 Shiroya 从清洁间穿越时，推车虽然消失了，却没有和我们一起出现在阁楼。因为我们现身时所用的身体，多半与 {time=12:10} 时的我们完全相同——那时我和 Shiroya 都在阁楼里，而且就在相同的位置……',
        "This means that if I had traveled holding the bedroom key, chances are I wouldn't have appeared with it in the past. Akaro and Sai wouldn't have encountered that problem since, for them, the key would've always been under the bathroom's carpet. But... no, that shouldn't have been a problem. I could've used one of the handles we left under the beds. There might've been another screwdriver in the opposite bedroom, and even if there wasn't, putting in screws without a screwdriver isn't too hard. Could it be that wasn't possible because it wasn't part of the loop I'd thought of...? Or maybe I just wouldn't have been able to do it without alerting Akaro.": '这意味着，如果我拿着卧室钥匙穿越，多半不会带着钥匙一起出现在过去。Akaro 和 Sai 就不会遇上这种问题，因为对他们来说，钥匙一直就在浴室地毯下面。{w} 可是……不，那本来不该成为问题。我可以用我们留在床下的其中一个把手。对面卧室里也许还有另一把螺丝刀；就算没有，不用螺丝刀把螺丝拧上去也不算太难。难道这种办法行不通，是因为它不在我设想的循环里……？又或者，我只是没法在不惊动 Akaro 的情况下做到？',
        "Even if I appeared with the key, that would cause a situation that I never experienced. Going to the past would've immediately changed things, overwriting the way in which I'd gone to the past in the first place. The loop would've become impossible if this happened, resulting in my failed attempt. ...And Akaro and Sai, who spent less time in the bedroom and most likely used a different Sekimeiya, might not have faced this issue either.": '即便我带着钥匙现身，也会造成一种我从未经历过的局面。回到过去会立刻改变现状，把我原本回到过去的方式覆盖掉。若真如此，循环就不可能成立，我的尝试也会以失败告终。{w} ……而 Akaro 和 Sai 在卧室里待的时间更短，多半用的也是另一个 Sekimeiya，他们或许同样不会遇到这个问题。',
        'If you look where you\'ll leave a mark and find it, you\'ll know that arrangement of doors and movements will work. If the mark isn\'t there, you\'ll know you would die midway, rendering you unable to leave the mark. You can keep thinking of different arrangements until the mark appears. Since you\'ll only move forth once you see the mark, it\'s an effective bootstrap—the end result is what allows it to happen. But despite being a "paradox", there\'s actually an origin to it.': '你去查看自己打算留记号的位置。如果记号已经在那里，就说明那套门和走法行得通；如果记号不在，就说明你会中途丧命，没法留下记号。{w} 你可以不断设想不同的组合，直到记号出现。既然你只有看到记号才会真正行动，这就形成了一种有效的自举——是结果本身让它得以发生。虽说它被称为「悖论」，其实仍然有源头。',
        'Even though this is an extreme situation, it can apply in any circumstance because it removes the generalized risk associated with going back to the past. Regardless of the circumstances, you can think something up in your head. If it\'ll work, you\'ll see the successful result, and if it won\'t, nothing will happen. You would be guaranteed to never fail, no matter what you attempt. The killer could\'ve used this method before killing Naomi; "if I move this specific way after killing her and I\'m not seen, I\'ll let my current self know by leaving a drawer in the next room open", for example.': '这虽然是极端情形，却能适用于任何情况，因为它消除了回到过去时通常伴随的风险。{w} 无论处境如何，你都可以先在脑中设想。若行得通，你就会看到成功的结果；若行不通，就什么也不会发生。这样一来，无论尝试什么，你都能保证自己不会失败。{w} 凶手在杀害 Naomi 之前，也可能用过这个方法；比如：「如果我在杀了她之后按这种特定方式行动，而且没有被看见，我就把隔壁房间的抽屉打开，好让当下的我知道。」',
        "Another big advantage is that you'd be able to make any move that's currently hard to accomplish by deciding it to occur retroactively. At some point, the killer might have wanted to prevent us from entering a room. However, they couldn't go and lock it, or they would've been seen.": '另一个巨大优势是，任何眼下难以完成的行动，你都可以决定让它在过去发生，借此完成。{w} 某个时候，凶手也许想阻止我们进入某个房间。可他们不能直接去上锁，否则就会被看见。',
        "The final step is one I'm not willing to accept: could you witness a very smoothly committed crime, decide that you were the perpetrator, and go back to the past to replicate it?": '最后一步我不愿接受：{w} 你能目睹一桩实施得天衣无缝的罪行，认定自己就是凶手，然后回到过去将它重演吗？',
        'For now, I\'ll ignore it. Would I send the recorder back in time to reproduce everything instead of writing a note that details it all thoroughly purely because "I didn\'t live that"? That\'s ridiculous.': '眼下，我先不去管它。{w} 难道仅仅因为「那段经历不是我亲身度过的」，我就要把录音笔送回过去、重现一切，而不是写一张把所有细节都交代清楚的便条？太荒唐了。',
        "Even though level 1 appears to have endless applications, there should be a daunting barrier to cross: the memories of the person who thinks of the loop. Someone who did this would always have to work around the past that they remember. Let's say the culprit wanted to kill someone in the event room and then had to choose between hallways A and B to escape.": '第一层看似用途无穷，但应该有一道难以逾越的障碍：设想出循环之人的记忆。做过这种事的人，永远得设法绕开自己记忆中的过去。{w} 假设凶手想在活动室杀掉某人，之后必须从A走廊和B走廊中选一条逃走。',
        "These loops always entail going back to the past. If the culprit had seen hallway A empty after the point Naomi would be killed, later, when they thought that they had to create the loop, they'd know they couldn't use hallway A. If they'd seen both hallways A and B empty instead, they would've put themselves into a corner and would be unable to create a loop in which they escaped successfully.": '这类循环总意味着要回到过去。如果凶手在 Naomi 将被杀的那个时间点之后看见A走廊空无一人，那么后来当他们意识到必须创造循环时，就会知道自己不能用A走廊。{w} 可要是他们看见A走廊和B走廊都空着，反而会把自己逼进死角，无法创造出成功逃脱的循环。',
        'It sounds a bit crazy; "it doesn\'t matter if they saw these hallways empty—if they hadn\'t looked at them, they still would\'ve been empty". That\'s not the case, though. That logic clashes with the most important part of this concept: that the origin of the loop is the mind of the person who will execute it.': '这听起来有点疯狂：「他们看见这些走廊空着也无所谓——就算不看，走廊也还是空的。」{w} 可事实并非如此。这种逻辑和这个概念最关键的一点相冲突：循环的源头，在于将来执行它的人的脑中。',
        'Both hallways were empty. Why hadn\'t the culprit seen their future self escaping through one of them? The reason is that seeing their escape route would\'ve told them about the plan they\'d later think of, and the origin would\'ve disappeared. So one would never see a result of a future loop before having thought of it, as that could induce or highly influence its creation, resulting in the classic bootstrap "they thought of the loop because they had experienced it".': '两条走廊都空着。凶手为什么没看见未来的自己从其中一条逃出去？因为看见自己的逃脱路线，就等于知道了自己之后才会想出的计划，源头便会消失。{w} 所以，在想到某个循环之前，人绝不会先看见它的结果；否则，那可能诱发或极大地影响循环的诞生，最终变成经典的自举情形：「他们之所以想到这个循环，是因为他们经历过它。」',
        "If the culprit is operating under this knowledge, that'd be a very good reason to stay hidden. If they spent all their time in front of the security screens observing what occurred in real time across the building, whenever they needed to make a retroactive move, their own memories of all the empty places would be the one thing preventing them from accomplishing it. Of course, this is also because the past can't be changed, so if they observed too much, they would make any future loop impossible, as they would never see a loop in action before thinking of it.": '如果凶手也明白这一点，那便是隐藏行踪的绝佳理由。要是他们把所有时间都花在监控屏幕前，实时观察整栋楼里发生的一切，那么每当需要做出回溯性行动时，自己对那些空无一人的场景的记忆，反而会成为阻止他们成功的唯一障碍。{w} 当然，这也是因为过去无法改变；观察得太多，就会让任何未来的循环都变得不可能，因为他们不可能在想到某个循环之前，先看到它正在发生。',
        "It was a very intriguing concept, but nothing assured me it was applicable. I was still a bit upset that I had no indication of why my plan hadn't worked... Would it work if I could slide the key under the door and wait a few minutes before trying to leave?": '这个概念非常耐人寻味，可没有任何东西能保证它适用。{w} 我仍然有些烦躁：自己的计划为何没有成功，竟连一点线索都没有……如果我先把钥匙从门底塞出去，等上几分钟再尝试离开，会不会就行得通？',
        "That would've matched Akaro's and Sai's circumstances more closely, but it could've led into even more reasons behind the failure. For example, Sai could've taken the key from under the door if he'd been nearby. ...I wasn't sure what to do or think.": '那样会更接近 Akaro 和 Sai 的处境，却也可能引出更多导致失败的原因。比如，Sai 若就在附近，完全可能把门下的钥匙拿走。{w} ……我不知道该怎么做，也不知道该怎么想。',
        "From room B4, I traveled twenty minutes to the past. I didn't know what had happened, so I ended up taking the elevator to the sixth floor. That action made our original selves follow the elevator up, and eventually, it all led into me traveling through time.": '我从B4房间穿越到了二十分钟前。当时我不知道发生了什么，结果乘电梯上了六楼。{w} 这个举动让原本的我们跟着电梯上了楼，而最终，这一切又让我穿越了时间。',
        "In short, if I hadn't gone up, it's possible I wouldn't have ended up traveling to the past. Therefore, traveling to the past is, in a way, what led me to traveling to the past. I'm not sure it was a bootstrap, but what's certain is that I didn't intend for it to occur; by traveling, I merely finished up the past that had already taken place.": '简而言之，如果我没有上楼，我或许就不会穿越到过去。所以，从某种意义上说，正是穿越到过去这件事，导致了我穿越到过去。{w} 我不确定这算不算自举，但可以肯定的是，我并非有意让它发生；我所做的穿越，不过是补完了早已发生的过去。',
        "We were facing a dilemma regarding Sai. We knew he was probably still down there, but we didn't know whether following him was what he wanted. His intent was unclear whether it was disrupting the peace, experimenting with the Sekimeiya, or following along with his bigger plan. Ultimately, we had once again decided to continue staying locked up because of Erina's input.": '我们在 Sai 的问题上陷入了两难。我们知道他多半还在楼下，却不知道跟上去是否正合他的心意。他的意图并不明确：是想制造混乱，是想试验 Sekimeiya，还是在推进自己更大的计划。{w} 最终，因为 Erina 的意见，我们再次决定继续闭门不出。',
        "He didn't insist further before closing his eyes again. I thought he had given up, but not long after, he opened his mouth again.": '他没再坚持，又闭上了眼睛。{w}我以为他已经放弃，谁知没过多久，他又开了口。',
        'What the...? What a joke. Atsuki! Come here!': '「搞什么……？开什么玩笑。{w}Atsuki！你过来！」',
        "Anyway, this is more than enough. We're leaving. Atsuki, this time, that camera clearly recorded your actions when you let Akaro escape. Don't think this will go unpunished.": '「总之，这已经够了。我们要走了。{w}Atsuki，这回摄像头可把你的所作所为拍得清清楚楚——是你放走了 Akaro。别以为这事会不了了之。」',
        'Then, Shiroya and I exchanged looks. She gave me a bitter smile that I replied to with a long sigh. I estimated it was around {time=16:20}, meaning that less than five hours remained until our scheduled freedom. We stayed still for a few seconds, contemplating the open door in front of us that symbolized our utter failure to keep everyone in one place.': '随后，Shiroya 和我对视了一眼。她冲我苦笑，我回以一声长叹。{w}我估摸现在大约是 {time=16:20}，距离约定重获自由的时刻已不足五个小时。我们静静站了几秒，望着眼前敞开的大门——它象征着我们彻底没能把所有人留在一处。',
        'Then, Shiroya and I exchanged looks. She gave me a bitter smile that I replied to with a long sigh.{w} I estimated it was around 16:20, meaning that less than five hours remained until our scheduled freedom. We stayed still for a few seconds, contemplating the open door in front of us that symbolized our utter failure to keep everyone in one place.': '随后，Shiroya 和我对视了一眼。她冲我苦笑，我回以一声长叹。{w}我估摸现在大约是 {time=16:20}，距离约定重获自由的时刻已不足五个小时。我们静静站了几秒，望着眼前敞开的大门——它象征着我们彻底没能把所有人留在一处。',
        'Then, Shiroya and I exchanged looks. She gave me a bitter smile that I replied to with a long sigh. I estimated it was around 16:20, meaning that less than five hours remained until our scheduled freedom. We stayed still for a few seconds, contemplating the open door in front of us that symbolized our utter failure to keep everyone in one place.': '随后，Shiroya 和我对视了一眼。她冲我苦笑，我回以一声长叹。{w}我估摸现在大约是 {time=16:20}，距离约定重获自由的时刻已不足五个小时。我们静静站了几秒，望着眼前敞开的大门——它象征着我们彻底没能把所有人留在一处。',
        'Then, Shiroya and I exchanged looks. She gave me a bitter smile that I replied to with a long sigh.{w} I estimated it was around 4:20 p.m., meaning that less than five hours remained until our scheduled freedom. We stayed still for a few seconds, contemplating the open door in front of us that symbolized our utter failure to keep everyone in one place.': '随后，Shiroya 和我对视了一眼。她冲我苦笑，我回以一声长叹。{w}我估摸现在大约是 {time=16:20}，距离约定重获自由的时刻已不足五个小时。我们静静站了几秒，望着眼前敞开的大门——它象征着我们彻底没能把所有人留在一处。',
        'Then, Shiroya and I exchanged looks. She gave me a bitter smile that I replied to with a long sigh. I estimated it was around 4:20 p.m., meaning that less than five hours remained until our scheduled freedom. We stayed still for a few seconds, contemplating the open door in front of us that symbolized our utter failure to keep everyone in one place.': '随后，Shiroya 和我对视了一眼。她冲我苦笑，我回以一声长叹。{w}我估摸现在大约是 {time=16:20}，距离约定重获自由的时刻已不足五个小时。我们静静站了几秒，望着眼前敞开的大门——它象征着我们彻底没能把所有人留在一处。',
        "Oh, what the...? You're right, no way this is drinkable.": '「哦，搞什么……？{w}你说得对，这玩意儿根本没法喝。」',
        "I grimaced at the taste. Not much water had flowed out of the tap, but although it was pretty transparent, it wasn't something I could drink. It had slightly alleviated the dryness, at least.": '尝到那味道，我皱起了眉。水龙头只流出一点水，看着倒也清澈，却根本不能喝。{w}不过至少稍稍缓解了口干。',
        "Look at this. I can see different pairs of footprints going between the entrance and the hallway, and there are many more under them that have degraded a lot. It's too hard to conclude anything from them, though.": '「看看这个。玄关和走廊之间有好几组不同的脚印，下面还有许多已经严重模糊的脚印。{w}不过，光凭这些实在难以下结论。」',
        "H-Huh... A-Are these Isla's? They can't be, right? And I think they're a bit too big.": '「呃、呃……{w}这、这些是 Isla 的吗？不可能吧？而且我觉得尺寸有点太大了。」',
        "I wish the button would light up when the elevator's moving. I doubt Erina and Katei would've used it already, no matter the reason. I'd say it was probably someone else.": '「电梯运行的时候，按钮要是会亮就好了。{w}不管出于什么原因，我都不觉得 Erina 和 Katei 会这么快就用电梯。要我说，多半是别人。」',
        "There was no revealing sight that immediately met our eyes. The floor spread out in front of us exactly as we remembered it. In hallway A, the light had begun to find a path through the dark coating and bounced off the walls more than it had the last time I'd been there. The strange smell hadn't faded since we'd been in the attic, and it had started to seem like the natural scent of the tower. It wasn't unpleasant, only intriguing, as I couldn't associate it to anything I'd ever smelled, and we couldn't identify its source.": '眼前并没有什么能说明问题的景象。这一层在我们面前铺展开来，与记忆里别无二致。{w} A走廊里，光线已开始在黑色涂层中找到通路，映在墙上的反光也比上次来时更多。那股怪味从我们在阁楼时起就没散过，如今倒像是这座塔本来就有的气味。算不上难闻，只让人好奇——我实在想不起在哪里闻过类似的味道，我们也查不出它的来源。',
        "...No. I can't wait to find Sai and hear the excuses he'll come up with.": '……不在。{w} 我已经等不及找到 Sai，听听他能编出什么借口了。',
        "It wasn't storing anything. Its interior contained nothing but an empty space waiting to be filled. ...My dumbfounded look persisted until the realization fully sank in.": '那层里什么都没有。{w} 柜内空无一物，只余一个等着被填满的空位。……我愣在那里，直到这个事实彻底沉进心里。',
        "If it did, we might know when. We've never seen two Sekimeiya exist at the same time, but it should've happened when one supposedly appeared in Sai's hip pack, right?": '如果真是这样，我们也许能推算出是什么时候。{w} 我们从没见过两颗 Sekimeiya 同时存在，但据说有一颗出现在 Sai 的腰包里——那时候应该就发生过这种情况，对吧？',
        "It could've traveled to the past, to Sai's hip pack. I get Sai's own existence is another mystery, though. ...After that, he hid it in the cleaning room.": '它也可能穿越到了过去，落进 Sai 的腰包。不过 Sai 的存在本身就是另一个谜。{w}……之后，他把它藏进了清洁间。',
        "Next, we hid it in this locker, but at some point, the same thing happened. It teleported to the hallway A cabinet, with Isla... This time, it didn't even have to go to the past. It could've simply teleported.": '接着，我们把它藏进了这个储物柜，可不知什么时候，同样的事又发生了。它传送到了 A走廊的展示柜，出现在 Isla 旁边……{w}这一次，它甚至不用回到过去，可能只是单纯传送了一下。',
        "So, is it disappearing randomly? There are a couple things I'm not sure about. Even though it could have teleported to the storeroom, the cabinet in the event room was unlocked, so I think one of us moved it... I suppose it's possible someone hid it in hallway B and it teleported to the storeroom, but that's hard to believe.": '那么，它是在随机消失吗？{w}有几处我还不太确定。它确实可能传送到了储藏室，但活动室的展示柜当时没上锁，所以我觉得是我们中的某个人把它挪走了……{w}也有可能有人把它藏在 B走廊，然后它传送到了储藏室，只是这实在难以相信。',
        "And there's one unexplained thing I can think of: the first time Isla disappeared from the cabinet, before appearing again. Nothing was found inside it, so the Sekimeiya couldn't have teleported from this locker yet.": '还有一件事我想不通：Isla 第一次从展示柜里消失，之后又重新出现在那里。{w}可当时柜里什么都没找到，所以 Sekimeiya 那时不可能已经从储物柜传送过去。',
        "That's one way to put it together. I think everything holds up. Anyway, if the Sekimeiya was actually taken from here by someone, it's very possible they put it inside Isla's cabinet. Honestly, it feels out of place to think that it's been teleporting itself through time at random intervals.": '这么拼也说得通，我觉得前后都对得上。{w}总之，如果 Sekimeiya 真是被人从这里拿走的，那很可能就是被放进了 Isla 的展示柜。说实话，要认为它自己在随机的时间间隔里反复传送，总觉得不太对劲。',
        "The door was still locked, so I highly doubt the lock was picked and then set again. Only one thing would've been needed to get the Sekimeiya out of here if it never disappeared all by itself: the key. Duplication can be easily achieved by traveling to the past since two versions of yourself exist at the same time. I'm still not sure about everything you can do with it, but it can work with objects, like how we're replicating our clothes after traveling.": '门当时还锁着，所以我不认为有人撬过锁之后又把它重新锁好。如果 Sekimeiya 不是自己凭空消失的，那要把它从这里带走，只需要一样东西：钥匙。{w}只要回到过去，就能轻松复制出一把——毕竟同一时刻会存在两个自己。时间穿越到底能做到哪些事，我还没完全弄明白，但它对物品同样有效，就像我们穿越之后，衣服也会被复制一样。',
        "But that's not necessarily the truth. The main reason why I think that is because of the initial footprints in the attic and because her keys weren't removed from her first body. Maybe the reason for that is the killer had a replica of Naomi's keyring from the start. It's even possible an entirely different person killed the second Naomi and grabbed her keys...": '但这未必就是真相。我这么判断，主要是因为阁楼里最初的那些脚印，还有她的钥匙并没有从她第一具身体上被取走。也许是因为凶手从一开始就有一串复制出来的 Naomi 钥匙。{w}甚至有可能，杀死第二个 Naomi 并取走钥匙的，完全是另一个人……',
        'No, we could have. We have the key, so we could go back to the past and unlock it.': '不，我们能打开。{w}钥匙在我们手上，只要回到过去就能把锁打开。',
        "No, I'm saying that, right now, there's likely only one: someone else will grab this key, go back to the past, and use it to unlock the locker.": '不，我是说，眼下大概只剩一种可能：{w}有别的人会拿走这把钥匙，回到过去，用它打开储物柜。',
        "Yeah, it seems I was wrong. Perhaps I'm taking myself too seriously. The universe didn't break, and I doubt the past changed.": '嗯，看来我错了。也许是我太把自己当回事了。{w}宇宙没有崩坏，过去大概也没被改变。',
        "I'd left it unlocked, so it opened. Once again, the winter coat was the only thing inside. I brushed my hand through the higher compartment just to make sure that it wasn't actually going invisible or anything. I shrugged and closed the locker, unable to lock it anymore.": '我之前没上锁，柜门应声而开。里面依旧只有那件冬季外套。{w}我把手伸进上层隔间扫了一遍，确认它并不是真的隐身了之类的。我耸耸肩，关上柜门——已经没法再锁上了。',
        'After the longest time, we put into action the usual procedure. We began with the cleaning room at our side. Next was the crystal room B6, found on the opposite side.': '隔了这么久，我们终于又照例行动起来。{w}先从身旁的清洁间开始，接着是对面的水晶展室 B6。',
        "I'd been about to move to the next room when Shiroya's casual voice stopped me in place. I turned around slowly to see her nodding at my disbelief. I approached the door and looked through it.": '我正要走向下一个房间，Shiroya 随口一句让我停住了脚步。我慢慢转过身，看见她正点着头，像是在回应我这副难以置信的表情。{w}我走到门边，透过门看进去。',
        "Given what happened while we were in the attic, it seems likely that whoever took the Sekimeiya was the main culprit behind everything. Despite that, they simply left it here, probably after using it. They haven't come back for it, so maybe that's a hint to their goal—or their failure. Regardless, it was probably activated recently, so we shouldn't go too far back, just enough to understand what went down while we were in the attic. Also, I don't think it's as hot as it was in the past, so depending on how far back we go, we could confirm that correlation.": '从我们在阁楼时发生的事来看，拿走 Sekimeiya 的人很可能就是这一切的主谋。可即便如此，他们还是把它留在了这里，大概是在用过之后。他们没有回来取，这或许暗示了他们的目的——又或者是他们的失败。{w} 无论如何，它多半是最近才被启动的，所以我们不该回到太远的过去，只要刚好能弄清我们在阁楼时发生了什么就行。{w} 另外，我觉得它没有以前那么烫了，所以根据我们回到多远的过去，也许就能证实这一点。',
        "I don't know, but I can come up with a bit of an idea. We had the key, and the chain was left set. That makes it likely that he teleported out. ...I thought that perhaps Sai did that. Maybe he traveled next to the door to encompass Akaro and make him escape since neither of them could open the door. It could be that he made us go to the upper bedroom so that we wouldn't travel with him. I don't know why they'd do any of that, but there's not much else I can think of.": '我不知道，不过我大概能想到一种可能。{w} 钥匙在我们手里，门链却还扣着，所以他多半是传送出去的。……我想，也许是 Sai 做的。{w} 也许他穿越到门边，把 Akaro 也纳入范围，好让他一起逃出去，毕竟他们谁都打不开那扇门。他让我们去楼上卧室，也许就是为了不让我们跟他一起穿越。我不知道他们为什么要做这些，但除此之外我也想不出别的可能。',
        "Actually, no, Akaro could've escaped all by himself and left the chain set. Maybe he suddenly disappeared from the room, traveling to the past. Then, in the past, he activated the Sekimeiya to encompass the bed on which he was sitting; it wasn't necessary for Sai to do that as long as Akaro had thought of it.": '不对，Akaro 也可能全靠自己逃出去，离开时门链依旧扣着。{w} 也许他突然从房间里消失，穿越到了过去。然后在过去启动 Sekimeiya，把当时自己坐着的床也纳入范围；只要 Akaro 自己能想到，就不必由 Sai 来做。',
        "And if Akaro never actually escaped the way I said, it's possible they went very far into the past. We spent a long time in the bedroom, so there was a lot of time for the Sekimeiya to store energy. You know, this could've been what Akaro and Sai worked together to accomplish. The stored time was originally Sai's idea.": '而且，如果 Akaro 根本不是照我说的那种方式逃走的，他们也可能穿越到了很久以前。我们在卧室里待了那么长时间，Sekimeiya 有足够的时间蓄能。{w} 你想想，这也许正是 Akaro 和 Sai 联手做成的事。蓄能这个点子本来就是 Sai 提出来的。',
        "Hm... And they couldn't simply have waited more before escaping the bedroom because the Sekimeiya was chilled. There's still the disappearing Sekimeiya in the locker to explain, but that'd be the only thing.": '嗯……而且他们不能在逃出卧室前多等一会儿，因为 Sekimeiya 已经凉了下来。{w} 这样一来，唯一还需要解释的就是储物柜里消失的 Sekimeiya，不过也就只剩这一件事了。',
        "Yeah. Sai seemed to be having fun, so exiting the tower doesn't seem like something he'd want to do. However, they did this right after discovering the storeroom's secret exit. As soon as they saw that, they probably realized they could go back many hours in time, find that door from the outside, and try to enter and exit with the Sekimeiya. They might be about to try coming back in since doing it earlier would've made their own travel impossible.": '嗯。{w} Sai 看起来玩得挺开心，不像是会想离开塔的人。可他们偏偏是在发现储藏室那条秘密出口之后立刻行动的。{w} 一看到那个出口，他们大概就意识到，自己可以回到许多小时前，从外面找到那扇门，再带着 Sekimeiya 进出。他们也许正准备试着回到塔内，因为要是更早行动，他们自己就没法穿越了。',
        "According to her, she called it without realizing that she was about to cause the noise we'd already heard. The belief that every event had an origin point was reinforced once more, as she'd unconsciously reenacted the past. Us hearing the elevator had derived into traveling to the past, but the action of calling the elevator had an organic origin. Not only that, we'd explained the single sign of life we'd experienced, so we had to seriously wonder what happened to Sai, Akaro, Erina, and Katei.": '按她的说法，她按电梯时并没有意识到，自己正要弄出我们早就听到的那个声音。每个事件都有个起点，这个想法又得到了一次印证，因为她无意中重演了过去。我们是因为听到电梯声才穿越回过去的；而按电梯这个动作本身，却有个自然的起因。{w} 不光如此，我们之前察觉到的唯一一点生命迹象，现在也解释通了，于是我们不得不认真去想：Sai、Akaro、Erina 和 Katei 到底出了什么事。',
        "And that probably happened a bit more than ten minutes before we touched the Sekimeiya. After that, we discussed whether to leave, placed the handles back on the door, walked down to the crystal floor, and talked about the Sekimeiya vanishing. We appeared in the bedroom before the time we'd heard the elevator... We might've appeared where we'd been ten minutes prior to traveling while only going back five. It's the opposite of what I thought before. It swapped the two points, although I'm not sure if the times fit that well.": '而那大概是在我们碰触 Sekimeiya 之前十多分钟。之后我们商量要不要离开，把门把手装回门上，下到水晶层，又聊起 Sekimeiya 消失的事。{w} 可我们出现在卧室的时间，却在听见电梯之前……也许我们只回溯了五分钟，出现的地点却是穿越前十分钟所在的位置。这和我先前的推测正好相反。两个时点掉了个个儿，只是时间上对不对得上，我还没有把握。',
        "From when we were locked up in the attic. Blood dripped off someone... Akaro didn't look injured when he came back, but that doesn't mean much.": '是我们被关在阁楼那阵子留下的。血是从某人身上滴下来的……{w} Akaro 回来的时候看不出受伤，可那也说明不了什么。',
        "I stared at the single drop of blood. Something about it was intriguing—while it wasn't a puddle, it was fairly wide. It wasn't a single drop that would come out of an innocuous scratch. Despite that, there was only one mark. Since any wound that produced a drop of that size would keep bleeding, it was likely it had been covered to prevent further blood loss.": '我盯着那一滴血。{w} 这滴血有些耐人寻味——它虽没有积成一摊，却铺得相当开。这样的大小，不像是无关痛痒的擦伤能滴出来的。可地上就只有这一处痕迹。{w} 能滴出这么大一滴血的伤口，必然会继续流血，所以多半是用什么东西按住了伤口止血。',
        "Erina and Katei must be somewhere, but they can't have anything to do with this. Even though Akaro didn't appear injured, it's possible he dripped blood before traveling to the past, and time traveling could have undone a recent injury.": 'Erina 和 Katei 应该也在某处，可这事跟他们不会有关系。{w} 就算 Akaro 看起来没受伤，也可能是在穿越回过去之前滴的血——时间穿越会把新近的伤一并抹去。',
        "Escaping alive was our main goal at the start. Then, escaping with a time travel device had begun to sound like an achievable goal that some of us probably shared. However, Shiroya and I had internally sought an unreachable peak while we'd been taunted by such inconsequential time travel. That was saving our friend who'd died two weeks earlier.": '起初，活着逃出去是我们主要的目标。后来，带着时间穿越装置逃出去，也渐渐成了触手可及的事，我们之中大概有人抱着同样的打算。{w} 可在这种只能挪动些许时间的穿越一次次撩拨之下，Shiroya 和我心里真正盯着的，却是一座够不着的山巅——救回两周前死去的朋友。',
        "Even though it had appeared impossible regardless of the approach, concluding that last detail might've opened the first real path to it, no matter how vague or improbable. If we could understand what determined the exact amount of time to be traveled, and most importantly, the appearing location... If there had been a time in which I'd been touching Miiya, and I could replicate that body...": '无论怎么尝试都显得不可能，可最后那个结论，也许已经为我们打开了第一条真正的路，哪怕它多么模糊、多么渺茫。{w} 只要弄清是什么决定了穿越的确切时长，尤其是出现的位置……{w} 只要我曾有过触碰 Miiya 的时刻，而我又能复现那具身体……',
        'My past body and my possessions of the past could be replicated, but Miiya might not have counted if I\'d simply been "touching her". But what if I could think of a time where I\'d been holding her hand or her shirt? None immediately came to mind, but they could apply.': '过去的身体和当时随身的东西都能被复现，可如果我仅仅是「碰到她」，Miiya 未必算数。{w} 但若我能想起某个曾握着她的手、或是抓着她衣角的时刻呢？一时想不起来，可这样的时刻未必没有。',
        "I might have jumped the gun by minimizing the fact that Miiya is a human. While I thought that we couldn't rule this out without attempting it, I see a big problem that might just reveal its impossibility.": '我可能太急着下结论，忽略了 Miiya 是人类这一点。{w} 我原以为不实际试一试就不能排除这种可能，但现在我看出一个大问题，它可能恰恰说明这条路走不通。',
        'In the bedroom, our past bodies were recreated, and we appeared within them. The locker key is proof enough of that. However, what happened to the brain? If our past bodies were recreated, the brain belonged to a past version of us. Despite that, we possessed memories and knowledge obtained after the recreated point.': '在卧室里，我们过去的身体被重新造出，而我们现身其中。储物柜钥匙足以证明这一点。{w} 可是，大脑又是怎么回事？既然被复现的是我们过去的身体，大脑自然也该属于过去的我们。然而我们却拥有复现时点之后的记忆与知识。',
        "But I can't know whether I'm overwriting my past consciousness every time I replicate my body or if it's merely not being replicated and I'm occupying an empty spot. After all, the Sekimeiya touched Isla's dead body and she didn't travel. That's probably because there was no longer a consciousness present within her.": '可我无从判断：每次复现身体时，是我覆盖了过去的意识，还是过去的意识根本未被复制，我只是占据了一个空位。{w} 毕竟，Sekimeiya 曾碰到 Isla 的遗体，她却没有穿越。那大概是因为她体内已不剩任何意识。',
        "But the second step—the amount of distance traveled—appears to operate under a consistent rule: the longer the Sekimeiya spends storing energy, the farther we travel. ...Meanwhile, the replicated location has differed with each travel, and there's no clear rule to draw. Nonetheless, it's hard to think only one thing would be consistent.": '可第二步——穿越的距离——似乎遵循着一条稳定的规律：Sekimeiya 蓄能越久，我们走得越远。{w} ……相比之下，复现的位置每次都不同，找不出明确的规则。不过，很难相信其中只有一项是有规律的。',
        "The core of replicating a past location is purely teleportation. We're teleporting to a coordinate of space we were once at. However, how is the Sekimeiya working with that coordinate? While the answer could be that its powers are simply magical, there's more depth to it than I first thought.": '复现过去位置的核心，说到底就是传送。我们被传送到自己曾经待过的某个空间坐标。{w} 可是，Sekimeiya 究竟如何处理这个坐标？答案或许只是「它的力量本就近乎魔法」，但其中牵涉的东西比我最初想的要深。',
        'The easiest concept of teleportation to grasp consists of two containers and matter teleporting from one to the other. The teleportation point is "the other container" because it exists and can be accessed. We aren\'t appearing inside designated and fixed containers, though, so let\'s assume that the coordinate of the bedroom, where I appeared, can be measured with a number.': '最简单的传送概念，就是两个容器：物质从一边传到另一边。传送点就是「另一个容器」，因为它存在、可以抵达。{w} 但我们并不是出现在某个被指定好的固定容器里，所以不妨假设：我现身的那间卧室的坐标，可以用一个数值来表示。',
        'Hm... Nobody else ever held that key, right? Could someone go back in time and replicate a position where they were holding it?': '嗯……{w} 没有别人拿过那把钥匙吧？有没有可能，有人回到过去，复制出自己握着钥匙时的位置？',
        'My mind had gone pretty deep into it: what if someone replicated a position in which they\'d been "holding" me? Had that ever happened? ...If that would create a lifeless body of mine, it could appear holding the key.': '我越想越深：如果有人复制出自己正「抱着」我时的位置呢？这种事发生过吗？{w}……如果那会造出一个没有生命的我，那个我说不定会握着钥匙出现。',
        'I looked all around me and shook my head. Then, I continued circling the room with my eyes until I noticed an oddity.': '我环顾四周，摇了摇头。{w} 接着，我继续用目光扫视房间，终于发现一处异样。',
        "I walked up to it, unsure if it was anything important. When Shiroya saw what I was staring at, she also realized what was off. Upon closer examination, even though the difference was minimal, my observation was proven correct: the lowest drawer of a cabinet wasn't fully closed. Before I could reach it, Shiroya spoke about a detail I'd missed.": '我走上前，不确定那是否值得留意。Shiroya 看见我盯着的东西，也看出是哪里不对劲。{w} 我凑近细看，尽管差别微乎其微，我的判断还是得到证实：一个展示柜最下层的抽屉没有完全合上。我还没伸手，Shiroya 就说起一个我漏掉的细节。',
        'Which meant that, most likely, the person who left the Sekimeiya behind also opened the drawer. I extended my arm and pulled the drawer toward me. Immediately, an object within rolled around the narrow interior, making dry noises as it hit the wood.': '也就是说，留下 Sekimeiya 的人很可能也打开过抽屉。{w} 我伸出手，把抽屉拉向自己。里面立刻有东西在狭窄的空间中滚动，撞上木板，发出干涩的声响。',
        "I looked at Shiroya and was met with a bitter expression. She'd already made up her mind. Touching it could have brought us out of the tower, but it also had the chance to considerably drag out our stay while we'd be unable to have any impact on a history which had already occurred. I nodded and began thinking about how to move it without burning myself.": '我看向 Shiroya，她一脸苦涩。她显然已经下定决心。{w} 碰到它也许能让我们离开这座塔，但也可能大大延长我们滞留的时间，而且我们仍无法对已经发生的历史产生任何影响。我点了点头，开始琢磨怎么搬动它才不会烫伤自己。',
        "I think we should just stop altogether... Let's just wait until we can leave. We can travel through time, which is still insane to think about, but there's no point to it, right? At most, it can help us understand what's going on, but there are cameras all over the place, and the police are probably a few hours away from entering. We don't even know how the Sekimeiya got inside the drawer, and it's clear that we don't understand anything about what we got caught up in. Touching it again could just be dangerous, so there's no point in risking it...": '我看，我们干脆别再折腾了……就等到能离开的时候吧。{w} 我们能穿越时间，这事想起来仍然很离谱，可这又有什么意义呢？顶多帮我们弄明白发生了什么，但这里到处是摄像头，警察大概再过几个小时就会进来。{w} 我们连 Sekimeiya 怎么进了抽屉都不知道，显然也完全没弄懂自己卷进了什么。再碰它可能只会带来危险，所以没必要冒这个险……',
        "As I felt a breaking wave of emotions, I managed to give her a nod. I'd let the desire to escape become a background goal, while it should've been the only thing to strive for. It had been sudden, but after all those dreamlike hours, Shiroya brought me back to reality—Miiya's death was irreversible. I breathed deeply, trying to keep myself balanced.": '一阵翻涌的情绪几乎将我淹没，我还是勉强朝她点了点头。我竟把逃出去的念头降成了次要目标，而它本该是我唯一该争取的事。一切来得突然，可在那几个如梦似幻的小时之后，Shiroya 把我拉回了现实——Miiya 的死无法逆转。{w} 我深吸一口气，努力让自己镇定下来。',
        "A-All right... I agree. Let's wait patiently and ignore whatever the hell the others are doing. At {time=21}, the front door has to open.": '好、好吧……我同意。{w} 我们就耐心等着，别管其他人到底在搞什么。到了 {time=21}，前门一定会打开。',
        "A-All right... I agree.{w} Let's wait patiently and ignore whatever the hell the others are doing. At 21:00, the front door has to open.": '好、好吧……我同意。{w} 我们就耐心等着，别管其他人到底在搞什么。到了 {time=21}，前门一定会打开。',
        "A-All right... I agree. Let's wait patiently and ignore whatever the hell the others are doing. At 21:00, the front door has to open.": '好、好吧……我同意。{w} 我们就耐心等着，别管其他人到底在搞什么。到了 {time=21}，前门一定会打开。',
        "A-All right... I agree.{w} Let's wait patiently and ignore whatever the hell the others are doing. At 9 p.m., the front door has to open.": '好、好吧……我同意。{w} 我们就耐心等着，别管其他人到底在搞什么。到了 {time=21}，前门一定会打开。',
        "A-All right... I agree. Let's wait patiently and ignore whatever the hell the others are doing. At 9 p.m., the front door has to open.": '好、好吧……我同意。{w} 我们就耐心等着，别管其他人到底在搞什么。到了 {time=21}，前门一定会打开。',
        'The world froze. However, strangely, movement was still within.': '世界静止了。{w} 然而奇怪的是，静止之中仍有东西在动。',
        "Atsuki and Shiroya were in front of the event room. Unbeknownst to them, instead of deftly weaving their way through myriad, tangled threads, those very same strings took hold of their own bodies. Atsuki's hand reached for the Sekimeiya, and as his brain was informed of the most painful burn he'd ever felt, his eyes took in the sudden darkness that appeared around him.": 'Atsuki 和 Shiroya 站在活动室门前。他们并不知道，自己并非在灵巧地穿行于无数纠缠的丝线之间；恰恰相反，是那些丝线攫住了他们的身体。{w} Atsuki 的手伸向 Sekimeiya，一阵从未有过的剧烈灼痛随即传进他的大脑，同时他眼前骤然一暗，四周陷入黑暗。',
        'However, he knew the layout and began to move forward. Even though he was lost in time, his movements hinted at a goal. After a few steps, his motion was halted by a sound that echoed off the walls.': '不过他熟悉布局，便继续往前走。虽然他在时间中迷失了方向，举动却像是有明确的目标。{w} 没走几步，一阵在墙壁间回荡的声音让他停住了脚。',
        "After a few steps, no new message reverberated. He looked up and saw a distant and faint green light. It belonged to a security camera, but he couldn't know if it was working.": '走了几步，没有新的声音回荡。{w} 他抬起头，看见远处一点微弱的绿光。那是监控摄像头，但它是否在运作，他无从得知。',
        "He shortly spotted a door and took hold of its knob. Then, he felt an alien pain in his hand that startled him. Confused, he tried with his other hand and pushed open the door with ease. To comprehend where he was, he reached for the closest wall. After recognizing the shape of a locker, he knew he'd picked the correct door and had arrived in the staff room.": '很快他摸到一扇门，握住门把手。随即，手上传来一阵陌生的疼痛，令他吃了一惊。他满心疑惑，换成另一只手，轻轻一推，门就开了。{w} 为了弄清自己在哪儿，他摸向最近的墙壁。认出储物柜的形状后，他知道自己选对了门——这里是员工室。',
        "Without warning, the lights turned on, emitting no noise. Instead of being startled, Atsuki shut his eyes forcibly, attacked by the intense illumination. After a few attempts at reopening them, his vision finally adapted, and he looked around the room where he'd spent so much time. He confirmed that it was the staff room, looking exactly as he'd thought.": '毫无预兆地，灯亮了，却没有一点声响。Atsuki 没有被吓到，反倒被刺目的光逼得紧紧闭上眼。{w} 他试了几次才重新睁开，视线终于适应，于是环顾这个他待了许久的房间。他确认这里就是员工室，和他想象的一模一样。',
        '"Wh-What the fuck are you doing?" Those were the first words Atsuki heard in more than an hour. He didn\'t know how to reply, so he moved forward, drawn in by the scenery behind the man.': '「你、你他妈在干什么？」这是 Atsuki 一个多小时以来听到的第一句话。{w} 他不知该怎么回答，只是被那人身后的景象吸引，向前迈了一步。',
        '"What\'s that suitcase for?" The man\'s expression instantly morphed again. Those cold words were interpreted as a clear and sudden attack, but he tried to hide his reaction.': '「那只手提箱是做什么用的？」{w} 那人的表情立刻又变了。他把这句冷冰冰的话当成了明摆着的突然挑衅，却还是竭力掩饰自己的反应。',
        "On the floor, Atsuki spent the last seconds of his life facing up, unable to move any part of his body. Resembling a hallucination, he saw his killer being startled by the knob's movement. When the door completed its arc and bounced on the wall, three more figures entered Atsuki's sight, but he couldn't distinguish their expressions. In front of him, he saw four people.": 'Atsuki 仰面躺在地上，身体任何部位都动弹不得，就这样度过生命最后的几秒。恍如幻觉一般，他看见凶手被门把的转动惊了一下。门扇划开弧线、撞在墙上弹回，又有三个人影进入他的视野，可他辨不清他们的神情。{w} 他眼前，站着四个人。',
        "But when I opened the door, I was met with a sudden and unexpected sight. My mind reeled as I stared at it, too stunned to react differently. I abruptly turned to face Shiroya, who responded to me with a plain expression. I yelled at her to come over, and she sprinted toward me. Not only had I seen something that put an end to the search, but I also knew that Shiroya and I absolutely couldn't be separated.": '可我一推开门，骤然撞见一幅完全出乎意料的景象。{w}我怔怔地望着，脑中一片混乱，惊得做不出别的反应。我猛地转头看向 Shiroya，她神情平淡地回望我。{w}我朝她大喊，让她过来，她便向我奔来。我不只看到了足以终结这场搜寻的东西，也清楚我和 Shiroya 绝对不能分开。',
        "Once again, Shiroya looked down at the pool of blood. It was natural for a head injury to bleed so much, and what I'd observed didn't reveal much. For all we knew, it was an accident. The way I imagined it, if he'd fallen back, he would've hit his head against the desk, ended up under it, and pushed the chair away. Despite how much blood covered the floor, there were no bloody footprints leaving the room.": 'Shiroya 又一次低头看向那摊血。头部受伤流这么多血本就正常，而我看到的情况也提供不了多少线索。就目前所知，这也许只是一场意外。{w}照我的设想，他若是向后倒下，头撞在桌沿，身体滑到桌下，椅子也会被撞开——现场就会是这样。尽管地板上到处是血，却没有带血的脚印通向房间外。',
        "However, the gruesome scenery obligated us to think that someone could've done it. Pushing Katei would've achieved the same result. Vast pools of blood would take a long time to dry, so I easily spotted smaller drops on the sides of the desk. Those were much closer to drying up, reminding me of the one in the event room.": '可眼前的惨状，也让我们不得不考虑另一种可能：有人下了手。只要推 Katei 一把，也能造成同样的结果。{w}大片血迹要很久才会干，所以桌边那些细小的血滴格外显眼。它们已经快要干透，让我想起活动室里的那一滴。',
        '"10:04: Camera(s) disabled and associated footage erased".': '「{time=10:04}：摄像头已停用，相关录像已删除」。',
        '"10:04 a.m.: Camera(s) disabled and associated footage erased".': '「{time=10:04}：摄像头已停用，相关录像已删除」。',
        'Oh, what...? At 10:04?': '啊，什么……？是在 {time=10:04}？',
        'Oh, what...? At 10:04 a.m.?': '啊，什么……？是在 {time=10:04}？',
        "That must've been when Katei was here alone. We checked the time at 9:41... Twenty minutes later was when we left, and he stayed behind, trying to fix the system.": '那应该是 Katei 独自留在这里的时候。我们在 {time=9:41.} 看过时间……二十分钟后我们离开，他留下来想修好系统。',
        "That must've been when Katei was here alone. We checked the time at 9:41 a.m... Twenty minutes later was when we left, and he stayed behind, trying to fix the system.": '那应该是 Katei 独自留在这里的时候。我们在 {time=9:41.} 看过时间……二十分钟后我们离开，他留下来想修好系统。',
        "The most conspicuous hint, a message left on the computer, was potential proof that Katei had been the culprit we were trying to ferret out. I reached for the mouse and dragged the message aside. Behind it, the program Katei had attempted to display the footage with was the only thing seen on the screen. It had a list of all the cameras, but they were useless if they'd actually been disabled.": '电脑上留下的那条消息，是最显眼的线索，也可能证明 Katei 就是我们要揪出的犯人。我伸手握住鼠标，把消息拖到一旁。{w}消息后面，屏幕上只剩下 Katei 原本用来播放录像的程序。程序里列着所有摄像头，可如果它们真被停用了，那也毫无用处。',
        'I lowered my eyes. The taskbar contained the single clock we had at our disposal. As soon as I glanced at it, the numbers switched from 16:59 to 17:00.': '我垂下目光。任务栏上显示着我们唯一能参照的时钟。我刚看过去，数字便从 {time=16:59} 跳到了 {time=17:00.}。',
        'I lowered my eyes. The taskbar contained the single clock we had at our disposal. As soon as I glanced at it, the numbers switched from 4:59 p.m. to 5:00 p.m.': '我垂下目光。任务栏上显示着我们唯一能参照的时钟。我刚看过去，数字便从 {time=16:59} 跳到了 {time=17:00.}。',
        "It's 17:00. Only four hours are left.": '已经 {time=17.} 了。只剩四个小时。',
        "It's 5 p.m. Only four hours are left.": '已经 {time=17.} 了。只剩四个小时。',
        "I'd forgotten about that... You're right. However... it was Katei who told us what the green light meant. We can't be certain about it.": '我都忘了这回事……你说得对。{w}不过……绿灯的含义是 Katei 告诉我们的。我们没法确定他说的是不是真的。',
        "They haven't stopped flickering, and I'm sure they also were before 10:00, so if the cameras really aren't recording, the lights must simply indicate that they're powered on.": '它们一直在闪，我敢肯定 {time=10} 之前也是这样。所以，如果摄像头真的没在录像，这些灯就只能说明它们通着电。',
        "They haven't stopped flickering, and I'm sure they also were before 10 a.m., so if the cameras really aren't recording, the lights must simply indicate that they're powered on.": '它们一直在闪，我敢肯定 {time=10} 之前也是这样。所以，如果摄像头真的没在录像，这些灯就只能说明它们通着电。',
        "I'm not sure, but thinking about it more, there's no way this was an accident... If Katei fell backward and hit his head against the desk, it means he was exiting the room. Why would he try to leave with that message being shown on the screen? Another person had to be involved somehow.": '我不确定，但再仔细想想，这绝不可能是意外……{w}如果 Katei 是向后倒下、头撞上桌沿，那就说明他当时正要离开房间。屏幕上还显示着那条消息，他为什么要在这时候离开？一定有另一个人以某种方式牵涉其中。',
        'Because at her right, Erina lay, her clothes tinted maroon by all the blood on them. Shiroya looked at me with the clear wish to deny reality. It hit us like a truck: Erina was dead too, and the only people remaining with us were dangers who we wanted to avoid.': '因为就在她右侧，Erina 躺在那里，衣服被血染成了暗红。{w} Shiroya 望着我，眼神里分明盼着这一切不是真的。这个事实如重锤砸下：Erina 也死了，而还留在我们身边的，尽是些我们避之不及的危险人物。',
        "I went back to the small theory I'd put together. If she had traveled to the past and confronted Akaro and Sai while the rest of us were in the bedroom, that could have given them a motive for her death... Even though they were the only suspects, they hadn't shown back up, so it was appropriate to think that they might never intend to.": '我又想起自己拼凑出的那个小推测。如果她穿越回过去，在我们其余人还待在卧室时与 Akaro 和 Sai 撞上，这可能就成了他们杀害她的动机……{w} 虽然他们是仅有的嫌疑人，却始终没再露面，想来他们也许根本不打算再出现。',
        'I dashed to hallway B. It was empty. My mind still reeling, I reentered the event room.': '我冲向 B走廊。那里空无一人。{w}我脑子仍乱成一团，又回到了活动室。',
        "I rushed out of the room and ran to hallway C. It was empty as well. Had it been a hallucination? There was no way—I was sure of what I'd seen.": '我冲出房间，跑向 C走廊。那里同样空无一人。{w} 难道是我的错觉？不可能——我很确定自己看见了。',
        "It was Sai's dilemma all over again. I had just explained what I saw to Shiroya, so if she ever did travel to the past and repeat what I'd told her, she would be completing a loop with no origin. It couldn't be that she purposely let me see her just because I said so. If Shiroya ever traveled again, she'd immediately recognize that the situation I described could come at any time. There was no chance for it to happen without foreknowledge, like when she'd called the elevator in the attic...": '这又成了 Sai 当初的困境。我刚把自己看到的事告诉 Shiroya；如果她日后真的穿越回过去，做出我描述的那些举动，那她就等于补全了一个没有源头的循环。她不可能只因为我说过这些话，就故意让我看见她。{w} 如果 Shiroya 再穿越一次，她立刻就会明白，我描述的情形随时都可能发生。没有预知，这一幕根本不可能出现——就像她在阁楼里叫来电梯那次……',
        'The state of the security room was unchanged. I saw some drops of blood had fully dried up, which was consistent with the time displayed on the computer: {time=17:29.}': '监控室仍保持原样。我注意到几滴血已经完全干涸，这与电脑上显示的时间相符：{w} {time=17:29.}',
        'The state of the security room was unchanged. I saw some drops of blood had fully dried up, which was consistent with the time displayed on the computer:{w} 17:29.': '监控室仍保持原样。我注意到几滴血已经完全干涸，这与电脑上显示的时间相符：{w} {time=17:29.}',
        'The state of the security room was unchanged. I saw some drops of blood had fully dried up, which was consistent with the time displayed on the computer: 17:29.': '监控室仍保持原样。我注意到几滴血已经完全干涸，这与电脑上显示的时间相符：{w} {time=17:29.}',
        'The state of the security room was unchanged. I saw some drops of blood had fully dried up, which was consistent with the time displayed on the computer:{w} 5:29 p.m.': '监控室仍保持原样。我注意到几滴血已经完全干涸，这与电脑上显示的时间相符：{w} {time=17:29.}',
        'The state of the security room was unchanged. I saw some drops of blood had fully dried up, which was consistent with the time displayed on the computer: 5:29 p.m.': '监控室仍保持原样。我注意到几滴血已经完全干涸，这与电脑上显示的时间相符：{w} {time=17:29.}',
        "Both of us wanted to stay in the event room until 21:00, but it was a different Shiroya who made us leave. What if whatever's about to happen leads into Shiroya traveling and she experiences her side of what I just saw?": '我们俩本来都想在活动室待到 {time=21}，可把我们叫走的是另一个 Shiroya。假如接下来要发生的事，最终会让 Shiroya 穿越时间，去经历我刚看到的那一幕中属于她的视角呢？',
        "Both of us wanted to stay in the event room until 9 p.m., but it was a different Shiroya who made us leave. What if whatever's about to happen leads into Shiroya traveling and she experiences her side of what I just saw?": '我们俩本来都想在活动室待到 {time=21}，可把我们叫走的是另一个 Shiroya。假如接下来要发生的事，最终会让 Shiroya 穿越时间，去经历我刚看到的那一幕中属于她的视角呢？',
        "However, that had already happened, and I'd told her about it. So what possibilities remained? What could the masked answer have been? ...Reason. That was what I needed to locate.": '可那件事已经发生，我也告诉过她了。那还剩哪些可能？那个被藏起来的答案究竟是什么？{w}……是理由。我要找的就是理由。',
        "Naomi's body appeared dead twice. Sai existed both in the attic and on the crystal floor, and simple time travel couldn't explain it. What about the Akaro who had different memories? Isla and Erina have died despite the fact they're supposed to be alive in the future. Now, a Shiroya that's very hard to explain with pure time travel has suddenly shown herself.": 'Naomi 的尸体出现了两次。Sai 同时存在于阁楼和水晶层，单纯的时间穿越解释不通。那个记忆不同的 Akaro 又该怎么解释？{w}Isla 和 Erina 已经死了，可她们在未来本该活着。如今又突然出现了一个很难单用时间穿越解释的 Shiroya。',
        "He didn't know who Katei was... but he knew me.": '他不知道 Katei 是谁……{w}却认得我。',
        "Could something else have been the answer? I thought about that first. I'd just put together how unlikely it was that anyone had entered the attic recently. That meant the Shiroya I'd seen probably hadn't hurried up to the attic and returned those clothes to the wardrobe.": '会不会另有答案？我首先想到的就是这个可能。{w}我刚推断出，最近几乎不可能有人进过阁楼；也就是说，我见到的那个 Shiroya 应该没有匆匆跑上阁楼，把这些衣服放回衣柜。',
        "...Even though they look the same, I'm willing to assume these clothes aren't the exact same ones I saw you wearing. Meaning that two identical sets exist at the moment, if your other self is still here somewhere.": '……{w}虽然看着一样，但我觉得这身不是我见你穿过的那一套。也就是说，如果你的另一个自己此刻还在这栋楼里某处，那眼下就有两套一模一样的衣服。',
        "Just like I'd thought when we were locked in the bedrooms, there was a way to place the origin of the loop inside Shiroya's mind. If she'd created a plan downstairs in the event room where a future self of hers would lure us out to accomplish something, and she'd later travel to make that happen, I'd begin to accept it as possible. Since it had happened to Shiroya, though, I wasn't able to reason it out like that.": '就像我们被关在卧室里时我想过的那样，有一种办法能把循环的起点放进 Shiroya 的头脑里。{w}如果她早在楼下的活动室里定下计划——让未来的自己把我们引出去、达成某件事——而她后来真的穿越回去促成此事，那我或许还能接受这种可能。可事情落到 Shiroya 自己身上，我就没法这么推想了。',
        "If we ever see that version of you again and you're wearing these clothes, I'll check this spot. If the mark is there, it'll mean that you traveled from the future with it somehow. If it's not, that'll tell us the truth is different.": '要是我们再见到那个你，而她穿着这身衣服，我就检查这里。{w}如果有记号，就说明她是带着这身衣服从未来穿越来的。如果没有，那就说明真相并非如此。',
        "However, the door didn't immediately open. The only explanation was that someone had called it from the third floor, but they weren't getting in. I cautiously reached forward and pushed the door.": '可门并没有立刻打开。唯一的解释是有人在三楼叫了电梯，却又不进来。{w}我小心翼翼地伸手推开了门。',
        '...Okay.': '……{w}好吧。',
        "Out of nowhere, I saw a hand gripping a knife swing toward me. My heart didn't have time to stop before I began to see the motion slowly. Without being able to give it any thought, I turned my whole body around as fast as possible.": '一只握着刀的手不知从何处朝我劈来。{w}我的心甚至来不及一惊，眼前的动作就开始慢了下来。顾不上思考，我用尽全力扭转身子。',
        "Even though the bathrooms could be locked from the inside, Katei said that his key opened all of them. We were most definitely being chased by his killer, who could've picked it up or could go back to the security room to do so. Entering the partitions would only doom us too. Instead, with the distance between us and our attacker beginning to extend, we did our best not to slow down for even a second.": '卫生间的门虽然可以从里面反锁，但 Katei 说过，他的钥匙能打开每一间。追我们的十有八九就是杀他的凶手——那把钥匙，对方可能已经捡走，也可能回监控室去取。{w}躲进隔间只会让我们也送命。眼下我们和对方的距离正渐渐拉开，我们拼尽全力，一秒也不敢放慢。',
        "I stepped up the stairs, unable to match our prior pace. Our bodies couldn't withstand much more. As much as I tried to keep up for just a few more seconds, my legs were barely responding. Seeing how the same thing was happening to Shiroya, I feared that our lack of sleep would finally catch up to us.": '我迈上楼梯，却已经跟不上先前的速度。我们的身体撑不了多久了。{w} 我拼命想再撑几秒，双腿却几乎不听使唤。看到 Shiroya 也是同样的样子，我担心睡眠不足终于要拖垮我们。',
        "I'm... not sure. If this is the same culprit who's been using the Sekimeiya all this time, I'm certain they'd have a way to replicate the key even if we have it with us. If it's Sai, he could go back to the past and replicate his body during a time he was holding it.": '我……没把握。如果对方就是一直使用 Sekimeiya 的那个凶手，那就算钥匙在我们手上，他多半也有办法复制一把。{w} 要是 Sai 的话，他只要回到过去，在自己还拿着钥匙的时候复制身体就行了。',
        'I truly hoped that, at 21:00, the police would come. I needed to get out with Shiroya at that time. There was no way I could make it even a second longer without breaking down.': '我真心盼着{time=21}警察能来。我必须在那时和 Shiroya 一起离开这里。再多撑一秒，我都会崩溃。',
        'I truly hoped that, at 9 p.m., the police would come. I needed to get out with Shiroya at that time. There was no way I could make it even a second longer without breaking down.': '我真心盼着{time=21}警察能来。我必须在那时和 Shiroya 一起离开这里。再多撑一秒，我都会崩溃。',
        "What!? It's not here!": '什么！？{w} 不在这儿！',
        "No, we can't rush out. We might be going up against Sai, and he wouldn't let us escape like this. If he entered the attic with another key, he could be luring us to the staircase.": '不，不能就这么冲出去。{w} 对手也许是 Sai，他不会让我们这样轻易脱身。他要是用另一把钥匙进了阁楼，那多半是想把我们引到楼梯口。',
        "Trying to leave through the main door didn't sound right, but we might've already been done for. The only other way out, the elevator, was no guarantee either. The person behind us had waited a couple minutes before making their entrance, so if they'd used that time to disable the elevator below us, we were completely trapped.": '从大门出去似乎行不通，可我们或许早已无路可走。另一个出口就只有电梯，同样未必靠得住。{w}身后那人等了几分钟才现身，要是他们利用那段时间弄停了我们下面的电梯，我们就彻底被困死了。',
        "But a different thought came to me. If they recognized the footprints and anticipated our actions, they could wait in the hallway, knowing we'd immediately leave. It was too late, as I'd already grabbed Shiroya's hand, and I wasn't able to stop mine from turning the handle of the door.": '可我又想到另一种可能。如果对方认出了脚印，料准了我们的行动，就会守在走廊里，等着我们自投罗网。{w}已经太迟了——我早已抓住 Shiroya 的手，也来不及阻止自己转动门把手。',
        "We had the chain, but it was unreliable. We'd seen how Akaro burst through it in five seconds. Not only that, but even though we were supposed to possess the single key to the attic, someone had managed to make their way in. The same thing could repeat in the bedroom. Earlier, Akaro and Sai had escaped with its key, and we knew they'd then activated the Sekimeiya in some way. It was possible they'd produced a spare key already.": '我们有门链，但那靠不住。我们都见过 Akaro 只用五秒就撞断了它。更何况，阁楼的钥匙本该只有一把，而且就在我们手里，却还是有人闯了进去。同样的事也可能在卧室重演。{w}先前 Akaro 和 Sai 带着卧室的钥匙逃走，而我们知道他们随后以某种方式启动了 Sekimeiya。说不定他们早已配出了一把备用钥匙。',
        "If we find it, we can choose a place to stay hidden until we're unavoidably found. Then, we can activate it. If we go far into the past, we won't be able to think of ambushing the culprit knowing where they'll be since it'd contradict them finding us, but we could make it outside the tower if we're lucky enough. If we travel to the recent past, we could find a new place to hide that this person had just looked at. It'd only be buying us more time, but it's better than having to confront someone with a knife or keep exhausting ourselves.": '找到它，我们就能选个地方藏起来，一直撑到不得不被发现为止，然后再启动它。{w}若是回到很久以前，我们就不能靠知道凶手的行踪去埋伏——那样就和他们找到我们这件事相矛盾了，不过运气好的话，也许能跑到塔外去。{w}若是回到不久前，我们就能另找一处他刚刚搜过的地方藏身。那也不过是多拖些时间，但总好过跟一个拿着刀的人正面相对，或者把自己累垮。',
        "N-No. I remembered how this all started when I stopped myself. We were going down with the elevator and stopped on floor 3 because someone called it knowing we were inside. No matter who this is, at this point, they must've thought of disabling the elevator under us so that we can't use it to escape.": '不、不行。我刚要动，就想起了这一切是怎么开始的。{w}当时我们乘电梯下行，却在三楼停下，因为有人明知我们在里面，还是按了电梯。不管对方是谁，到了这一步，他们一定已经想到，要让我们下面的电梯停住，叫我们没法靠它逃跑。',
        "If we called the elevator anyway and it came, it would definitely be a trap and they intend to do the same thing as before. As soon as we go down, they could call it. The last time, they waited next to the offices, but this time, I'm sure they'd be right outside to make sure we can't continue moving. Think about it, it's also possible we're dealing with both Akaro and Sai. If one of them is on a floor under us, they could be hoping we take the elevator and lose any way out.": '就算我们按了，电梯真的上来，那也一定是个陷阱，他们打算故技重施。我们一旦下去，他们就能把电梯叫走。{w}上次他们守在办公室旁边，这一次，我敢肯定他们会直接守在门外，确保我们没法再移动。{w}你想想，对手也可能是 Akaro 和 Sai 两个人。只要其中一人在我们下面的楼层，他们就可能巴不得我们坐电梯，好让我们彻底断了退路。',
        "I was experiencing the most unsettling silence possible. Waiting in the storeroom wasn't an option, so I could only find three: trying to use the elevator to go down, trying to lock ourselves in a bedroom, and trying to leave the attic through the main door.": '我从未体会过如此令人不安的寂静。守在储藏室不是办法，我能想到的只有三条路：{w}乘电梯下楼，躲进卧室反锁房门，或者从正门离开阁楼。',
        "Why would they have stopped searching for us when it's certain we're in the attic? ...It could mean they're working alone. If they quit looking and want to ambush us instead, it could mean nobody is working with them. Their partner would've taken care of that while the other kept trying to find us.": '明知我们就在阁楼里，他们为什么停止搜索了？{w}……也许说明他们只有一个人。如果对方不再找人，转而打算伏击我们，那就可能没有同伙。若有同伙，本该一个继续搜，另一个去准备伏击。',
        'I thought about going to a bedroom to pick up a screwdriver. It was the only weapon I could think of, but I abandoned the thought. It was no match against a knife, and the more I thought about it, the more I felt that going back to a bedroom was a bad idea. Furthermore, if the person chasing us had taken the key, they would probably have taken such an obvious weapon as well.': '我想过去卧室拿螺丝刀。那是我唯一能想到的武器，但很快打消了这个念头。它敌不过刀，而且越想越觉得，折回卧室不是个好主意。{w}再说，追我们的人既然拿走了钥匙，多半也不会漏掉这么显眼的武器。',
        'The same knife, the same breeze at my side... After leaving the partitions, as if the culprit had teleported behind me, I saw another missed swing that was incredibly close to taking my life. It had happened again—a sudden ambush.': '{w=0.6}又是那把刀，又是身侧那阵风……绕过隔板后，犯人仿佛传送到了我身后，我又一次看见挥空的刀锋，离夺走我的性命只差毫厘。又来了——又一次突袭。',
        '"Atsuki! You son of a bitch!"': '{w=0.7}「Atsuki！{w=0.5}你这王八蛋！」{w=1.1}{nw}',
        'The chase resumed. Shiroya and I sprinted as fast as we could toward the staircase to floor 3 while I reeled at the fact that it had actually been Sai. Why... and why then? His face had made it clear that trying to ask would be our end.': '追逐再次开始。我和Shiroya拼命朝通往3楼的楼梯跑去，而我的脑中仍嗡嗡作响：追来的人竟然真的是Sai。{w}为什么……又为什么偏偏是那时候？他的表情已经说明，开口去问就是死路一条。',
        "The way it happened, I imagined Sai was hiding inside the first partition, waiting for us to pass by. We began to speed down the stairs while I tried to decide on what to do. Sai hadn't started to chase us until he'd yelled my name, which had created enough distance between us to seriously consider the elevator.": '从当时的情形看，我想Sai是躲在第一道隔板后，等我们经过。{w}我们加快脚步下楼，我一边盘算接下来该怎么办。Sai直到喊出我的名字才开始追，这也让我们之间拉开了足够的距离，能认真考虑走电梯这条路。',
        '"Stop!" Shiroya cried again, but anything she could say was meaningless to Sai, who was certain of her fate.': '“住手！”{w}Shiroya再次喊道，可她说什么对Sai都已毫无意义——他早已认定她难逃一死。',
        "Mercilessly, he moved his arm in an arc, drawing a long horizontal cut through Shiroya's chest. Inwardly, Atsuki cried in anguish. But Sai frowned. After instinctively reacting to Shiroya's attempt at aiding Atsuki, he looked at his second victim in disbelief.": '他毫不留情地挥臂划出一道弧线，在Shiroya胸前横着划开一道长长的口子。Atsuki在心里痛苦地嘶喊。{w}可Sai却皱起了眉。他本能地对Shiroya救助Atsuki的举动做出反应，随后难以置信地看向自己的第二个受害者。',
        'And then a third, and a fourth... All of them felt much more painful, but he couldn\'t move. "You brought this on yourself, you fucking idiot!" Those words were received as static noise. An irreversible cloudiness began to fill Atsuki\'s consciousness, and eventually, his brain stopped interpreting the splashes of blood that every stab produced, shortly cutting off forever.': '接着是第三刀、第四刀……每一刀都比之前疼得多，可他已经动弹不得。“这是你自找的，你这该死的蠢货！”{w}那些话落进他耳中，只剩一片杂音。不可逆转的混沌开始充满Atsuki的意识；最终，他的大脑不再去辨认每一刀溅起的血，很快便彻底停止了运作。',
        "Shiroya's eyes widened in amazement. Both of them had failed to recall its existence. They thought back on Katei's words. He'd told them that if the button was pressed while the elevator was moving, only an entity from outside the tower could enable it again.": 'Shiroya惊讶地睁大了眼睛。两人都忘了还有这个按钮。{w}他们回想起Katei的话。他说过，如果电梯运行时按下那个按钮，就只有塔外的人才可能让它重新启动。',
        "Shiroya had been living in Atsuki's house for a week, and they'd never set an end date. She hoped she could stay with him for a little bit longer without being a bother. In the meantime, Atsuki's mind kept going to what they'd talked about hours previously. It had been so long since they'd visited their old cabin that he really felt a strong desire to go back there with her.": 'Shiroya 已经在 Atsuki 家住了一个星期，两人却从未定下期限。她希望能再多留一阵子，又不至于给他添麻烦。{w} 与此同时，Atsuki 的思绪一直绕着几小时前他们谈过的事打转。他们已经太久没去过那座旧小屋了，他实在很想再和她回去看看。',
        "When he'd made the rushed decision of activating the emergency stop function of the elevator, he hadn't thought of it. If it was legitimate, nobody was going to let them out. When the thought came to him, Atsuki's heart began to speed up again.": '他匆忙决定按下电梯的紧急停止按钮时，并没有想到这一点。如果那段录音是真的，就没人会放他们出去。{w} 这个念头一冒出来，Atsuki 的心脏又开始狂跳。',
        "How long until 21:00? If they could be sure that point in time would mark the end to their suffering, reaching it wouldn't be an issue. As soon as Atsuki had thought of the not-unlikely worst scenario, though, every second had begun to feel unbearable.": '距离 {time=21} 还有多久？如果能确定那个时刻就是痛苦的终点，熬到那时也不成问题。然而，Atsuki 一想到最坏的情况并非不可能发生，每一秒都开始变得难以忍受。',
        "How long until 9 p.m.? If they could be sure that point in time would mark the end to their suffering, reaching it wouldn't be an issue. As soon as Atsuki had thought of the not-unlikely worst scenario, though, every second had begun to feel unbearable.": '距离 {time=21} 还有多久？如果能确定那个时刻就是痛苦的终点，熬到那时也不成问题。然而，Atsuki 一想到最坏的情况并非不可能发生，每一秒都开始变得难以忍受。',
        "He wasn't sure how much longer they had to wait for... Perhaps they'd been inside for half an hour. As much as he wanted the time to pass, he knew an inevitable time would come: almost 21:00.": '他不确定他们还要等多久……也许他们已经在里面待了半个小时。他虽盼着时间快点过去，却也知道那个无可避免的时刻终将到来：将近 {time=21.}。',
        "He wasn't sure how much longer they had to wait for... Perhaps they'd been inside for half an hour. As much as he wanted the time to pass, he knew an inevitable time would come: almost 9 p.m.": '他不确定他们还要等多久……也许他们已经在里面待了半个小时。他虽盼着时间快点过去，却也知道那个无可避免的时刻终将到来：将近 {time=21.}。',
        'The uncertain period of time in which nothing would be known. Was it past 21:00, and they were already doomed? Was the way out about to unlock? ...How could they know?': '在那段时间里，什么都无法确定。是不是已经过了 {time=21}，他们早就没救了？出口是不是马上就要打开？……可他们又怎么会知道？',
        'The uncertain period of time in which nothing would be known. Was it past 9 p.m., and they were already doomed? Was the way out about to unlock? ...How could they know?': '在那段时间里，什么都无法确定。是不是已经过了 {time=21}，他们早就没救了？出口是不是马上就要打开？……可他们又怎么会知道？',
        "And it wouldn't occur. He had spent the past few minutes with his eyes closed when he opened them after a sudden noise.": '而这一切并没有发生。{w} 过去几分钟他一直闭着眼睛，直到一声突如其来的响动让他睁开眼。',
        "Shiroya didn't react to what I said, but we continued to make our way through the floor. There was another reason we had to target the event room: if Sai was our only attacker, for as long as we circled in and out of it, we wouldn't be caught. Of course, we couldn't do that for the remaining three hours, but it was better than putting ourselves in a corner.": 'Shiroya 没有回应我的话，但我们继续穿过这一层。{w} 我们非去活动室不可，还有另一个原因：如果袭击者只有 Sai，那么只要我们在活动室里外绕圈子，就不会被他抓住。当然，剩下三个小时不可能一直这样，但总比把自己逼进角落要好。',
        '...There we go. You two were starting to really tire me out.': '……找到了。{w=0.5} 你们俩还真让我费了不少劲。',
        "As soon as we tried to leave, Sai's body collided with mine at full speed. I was knocked down and fell by his feet. When his terrifying voice made me look up, I saw the knife we'd been running from, pointed right in front of my face.": '我们刚要离开，Sai 整个人便全速撞了上来。我被撞倒在地，摔在他脚边。{w} 听到他那骇人的声音，我抬起头，随即看见我们一路躲避的那把刀，正对着我的脸。',
        "I thought so... Have you stopped trying to kill me...? I don't understand what you're doing.": '我想也是……{w}你不打算杀我了吗……？我不明白你在做什么。',
        'Uh... Right now... it should be around 17:40.': '呃……现在……应该是 {time=17:40.} 左右。',
        'Uh... Right now... it should be around 5:40 p.m.': '呃……现在……应该是 {time=17:40.} 左右。',
        "You're right. My watch says it's 17:41, and I'm sure it's correct.": '你说得没错。我的表显示 {time=17:41}，而且我确定它走得准。',
        "You're right. My watch says it's 5:41 p.m., and I'm sure it's correct.": '你说得没错。我的表显示 {time=17:41}，而且我确定它走得准。',
        "What the fuck? Don't tell me you believed him. I knew he could try to enter from the storeroom door, but I haven't guarded it the entire time.": '搞什么？{w}别告诉我你信了他。我早知道他会试着从储藏室的门进来，可我不可能一直守着那儿。',
        '...Was it in the farthest back room in hallway B? B6?': '……{w}是在 B走廊最里面那间？B6？',
        '...Huh. I see. It teleported there after you used it... I get it.': '……{w}哼，原来如此。{w}你们用过之后，它传送到了那里……我明白了。',
        "Don't lie. You have a knife which was definitely used to kill Erina. You're trying to trick us, aren't you? You used the Sekimeiya to escape the tower, and then you entered again through the storeroom with that knife that you brought from the outside. You traveled from the hallway B room, which is how you knew we found the Sekimeiya there. The state we saw Akaro in... did you do that?": '少骗人。你手里那把刀，分明就是杀死 Erina 的凶器。{w}你想骗我们，对吧？你用 Sekimeiya 逃出了塔，然后带着从外面弄来的那把刀，从储藏室重新进来。{w}你是从B走廊那间房穿越回来的——所以你才知道我们在那里找到了 Sekimeiya。{w}我们看到 Akaro 时他那副样子……也是你干的？',
        "What you two just said... is wrong. However, I didn't have to get rid of any clothes, seeing as I didn't kill anyone.": '你们俩刚才说的……都错了。{w}不过，我根本不需要处理什么衣服，因为我没杀过人。',
        "Were we wrong? ...About what? His clothes still had very faint traces of the smoke on them. If he had traveled outside the tower and then entered from the storeroom, there would've been no smoke on them. ...Was that wrong as well?": '我们错了？……错在哪儿？{w}他衣服上还残留着极淡的烟味。如果他先前去过塔外，再从储藏室进来，衣服上就不该沾着烟味。……这一点也错了吗？',
        "Regardless, it was still shut, so nobody could have traveled after leaving the Sekimeiya there. The window for that explanation was incredibly tight—it had to have happened before that point or after the present time if the Sai we were talking to was the result of an upcoming time travel. We also couldn't rule out the possibility that someone took the Sekimeiya out of the cabinet, used it, and placed it back inside.": '不管怎样，抽屉当时是关着的，所以把 Sekimeiya 留在抽屉里之后，就不可能再有人穿越离开。能解释得通的时间范围窄得惊人：要么发生在那之前；要么，如果我们面前这个 Sai 是未来某次穿越的结果，就得发生在我们当下之后。{w}另外，也不能排除有人把 Sekimeiya 从展示柜里取出来用过、又放回去的可能。',
        "Sai's lips curved into a grin. Then, he kneeled and left the knife on the floor.": 'Sai 嘴角一弯，笑了。{w}随后他蹲下身，把刀放在了地上。',
        "You two don't understand anything. You think you do, and it's laughable. Right. I don't want to use my knife because overpowering you physically right now would be a loss. I'll have to go one step further and show you how pathetic your resistance is.": '你们俩什么都不懂，却自以为都懂，真是可笑。{w}没错，我不想动刀，是因为现在靠武力制服你们反而是我输。我得再进一步，让你们看看自己的抵抗有多可悲。',
        "I didn't understand anything, but Sai had a plan. Given what had happened the previous time, I hesitated to chase after him, but I immediately realized that was a mistake. To prevent him from completely leaving our line of sight, I sprinted toward the door and looked down the hallway.": '我完全摸不着头脑，但 Sai 一定有计划。想起上次发生的事，我迟疑着不敢追上去，可随即意识到这是错的。{w}为了不让他彻底脱离视线，我冲向门口，望向走廊。',
        "It seems he understands how the Sekimeiya works better than us... and it's still possible another one exists. If he entered the room where he knew the other Sekimeiya was, he could've gone back to the past. Maybe he thought both of us would chase behind him and he could immediately enter the event room from hallway A. That's why it should be fine if you stay here, looking at the hallway. I'll open the doors while you make sure Sai doesn't leave and nobody enters from the other side.": '他似乎比我们更清楚 Sekimeiya 的运作方式……而且，很可能还有另一个。{w}如果他进了自己知道放着另一个 Sekimeiya 的房间，就能回到过去。他也许以为我们俩都会追在他身后，这样他就能立刻从A走廊进入活动室。{w}所以，你留在这里盯着走廊就好。我来开门，你负责看住 Sai，别让他跑掉，也别让任何人从另一头进来。',
        'Before moving on, I saw something. On top of one shelf, there was a key.': '正要离开时，我瞥见了什么。{w} 有个架子的顶上放着一把钥匙。',
        'Not here either... Unless he used the Sekimeiya and then it teleported itself away like he said happened earlier...': '这里也没有……{w} 除非他用了 Sekimeiya，然后它像他先前说的那样自己传送走了……',
        "Next, I entered room B4. It exuded a sinister aura, exhibiting Naomi's and Erina's deaths. Trying to ignore my sudden heartache, I inspected every cabinet where Sai or the Sekimeiya could be. As usual, they were all empty.": '接着我走进 B4房间。这里透着一股不祥的气息，Naomi 和 Erina 就死在此处。我强压下心头骤然的刺痛，把 Sai 或 Sekimeiya 可能藏身的展示柜一一查过。{w} 和之前一样，全是空的。',
        "We need to search hallway A, but the lobby and hallway C are a problem. Wait here, watching over this hallway and the other door like you were doing. I'll be back in a second.": 'A走廊得搜一遍，可大厅和 C走廊是个麻烦。{w} 你守在这儿，照刚才那样看着这条走廊和另一扇门。我很快就回来。',
        "So, if he's still on this floor, he has to be inside a room in this hallway. We'll do the same thing, then.": '那么，只要他还在这一层，就只可能藏在这条走廊的某个房间里。{w}那就照老办法再来一遍。',
        'All right. What are you doing over there? Searching for me?': '好吧。{w}你们在那头做什么？找我？',
        "You just jumped ten steps too far, Atsuki. It's baffling how easy it is to trick you. I really just relied on a trick I felt could work, which you might discover eventually.": 'Atsuki，你这步子迈得太大了。骗你竟然这么容易，真让人吃惊。{w}我不过是靠了一个自认为行得通的把戏，你最终也许能想明白。',
        "*sigh* Aren't you missing a really easy way I could've escaped?": '唉……{w}你们是不是没想到，我本来有个特别简单的办法能脱身？',
        "Sorry, Shiroya, I'm nullifying our deal. Atsuki deserves to know what happened. It was simple. Atsuki, the first room you went to was the cleaning room, right? You were close—I was in the staff room. The moment you entered it, I left. In the hallway, Shiroya winked at me and let me escape. I feel awful keeping you in the dark, honestly.": '抱歉，Shiroya，我们的交易作废。Atsuki有资格知道真相。{w}事情很简单。Atsuki，你最先去的是清洁间，对吧？只差一点——我当时在员工室。{w}你进门的那一刻，我就离开了。在走廊里，Shiroya朝我眨了眨眼，放我走了。说真的，一直把你蒙在鼓里，我心里过意不去。',
        "Right. I'm so smart that I turn myself on. That's true, though. I suppose it's not fair if I won't answer anything. Remember at the beginning? I had no issues sharing my thoughts with you, but that changed at one point. There's no way you're dense enough to not know when.": '没错，我聪明得连自己都要迷上自己了。不过这也是事实。要是什么都不回答，确实不太公平。{w}还记得一开始吗？那时我很乐意把自己的想法告诉你们，但后来某个时候变了。你们总不至于迟钝到连这都看不出来吧。',
        "We found out we were next to a time travel device, yes. Then, keeping everything to myself became the smarter option. I did not in any way suspect what the Sekimeiya would be capable of, but I was expecting something to occur. I thought I'd have to be very perceptive to understand whatever could be going on, but everything happened in front of our eyes.": '是啊，我们发现身边就是一台时间穿越装置。从那之后，把一切藏在心里就成了更聪明的选择。{w}我完全没有想到 Sekimeiya 会有这种能力，但也预感到会出事。我原以为必须非常敏锐才能弄懂到底发生了什么，结果一切就明明白白地发生在眼前。',
        "You have no idea what I'm talking about. I understand, and it's great. I promise there's some meaning behind that, but don't think I'll be stupid enough to tell you anything undesirable. Now, explain something for me. I thought about it a little, and I don't understand what you said regarding Akaro. He came back up to the bedroom and opened the door with the key, which was later left in the original drawer—": '你完全不知道我在说什么。我明白，这很好。我保证这话自有含义，但别以为我会蠢到把不该说的都告诉你们。{w}现在，给我解释一件事。我想了想，还是没搞懂你说的关于 Akaro 的事。{w}他回到楼上的卧室，用钥匙开了门，而那把钥匙后来被留在了原来的抽屉里——',
        "How intriguing. I just glossed over it when you mentioned his reappearance, but I'm not certain what to think anymore. When you let him enter, you made sure he didn't have a key on his person, right?": '真有意思。你提到他重新出现时，我没怎么细想，现在却不知道该怎么想了。{w}你们放他进来时，确认过他本人身上没有钥匙，对吧？',
        "Hm... I'm just finishing off your ignorance.": '嗯……{w}我只是来结束你们的无知。',
        '...Who killed Katei?': '……{w}是谁杀了 Katei？',
        "The culprit? Don't be silly. And I'm not sure why you're asking me this when I recall saying over and over that Katei did it.": '凶手？别傻了。{w}我记得自己反复说过，是 Katei 干的，真不明白你为什么还要问我。',
        "Because I have eyes. That might sound unfair, though—you do too, but you don't understand. That's what I don't quite get. Regardless, that's it. I'll touch the Sekimeiya and immediately appear from hallway B. I'll see you.": '因为我有眼睛。这话听着或许不公平——你也有眼睛，只是看不懂。这一点我倒是真不明白。{w}总之，就到这里。我去碰 Sekimeiya，然后立刻从B走廊出现。回见。',
        'I turned to my side. Nobody was there.': '我转头看向身旁。{w}空无一人。',
        'What the fuck...? Did the range reach her? Why her but not me?': '怎么回事……？{w}范围波及到她了吗？{w}为什么是她，不是我？',
        "That was what Sai had said: a version of himself might've been waiting in hallway B. I approached the door and looked through it. I saw a handful of open doors that I'd left that way, but no sign of life.": 'Sai 是这么说的：另一个他也许正等在 B走廊。{w}我走到门边，透过门看进去。有几扇门还像我离开时那样敞着，却不见半点人影。',
        "However, nothing was changing. I was getting worried, but I didn't know what to do. After some minutes of standing up, I started to feel uncertain.": '可是，一切毫无变化。我越来越不安，却不知该如何是好。{w}站了几分钟后，我心里开始没底。',
        "I was just trying to reinforce the thought that I wasn't alone, acting as if it was impossible. What if she'd appeared outside the tower, entered through the storeroom from the outside, and left the door open to leave after placing the Sekimeiya in the cabinet? It looked like motives behind actions had stopped mattering, so being sure about any detail had started to feel impossible.": '我只是在反复说服自己并非孤身一人，装作那根本不可能。{w}可万一她真的出现在塔外，从外面经储藏室进来，把 Sekimeiya 放进展示柜后又敞着门离开呢？行动背后的动机似乎早已不重要，任何细节都变得无法确定。',
        "When I entered hallway A, I became convinced of it: Sai and Shiroya had escaped. That had to have been the meaning behind Sai's words, but it was impossible to know if I'd see them again before 21:00.": '走进 A走廊时，我总算确信了：Sai 和 Shiroya 已经脱身。Sai 那番话的意思必定如此，只是我无从知道，在 {time=21.} 之前还能不能再见到他们。',
        "When I entered hallway A, I became convinced of it: Sai and Shiroya had escaped. That had to have been the meaning behind Sai's words, but it was impossible to know if I'd see them again before 9 p.m.": '走进 A走廊时，我总算确信了：Sai 和 Shiroya 已经脱身。Sai 那番话的意思必定如此，只是我无从知道，在 {time=21.} 之前还能不能再见到他们。',
        "...Out of the blue, I recalled something else. Awkwardly, I put my free left hand in my right pocket and took out a key. I'd found it in the cleaning room just earlier, high on a shelf.": '……{w}忽然，我又想起了另一件事。{w}我用空着的左手别扭地伸进右边口袋，掏出一把钥匙。那是我刚才在清洁间找到的，就放在架子高处。',
        "I shut myself in the staff room with the Sekimeiya since I wanted it to spend a few minutes out of the cabinet. I knew which locker was Naomi's, and as I thought, it was open. I attempted to insert the key in the keyhole, but it didn't fully go in.": '我带着 Sekimeiya 进了员工室，关上门，好让它在展示柜外待上几分钟。我知道哪个是 Naomi 的储物柜，过去一看，果然开着。{w}我试着把钥匙插进锁孔，却插不到底。',
        "I knew that I'd found the key in the cleaning room, but something still felt iffy about that, preventing me from jumping to conclusions. I folded the pants and put them inside before I grabbed the heavy coat.": '我知道钥匙是在清洁间找到的，可这件事总让我觉得哪里不对劲，不敢贸然下结论。{w}我把裤子叠好放回柜中，又拿起那件厚重的外套。',
        'It was pretty big, so I began to run my hand over its surface in search of anything I could find. Almost immediately, I took something from a pocket.': '外套相当大，我开始用手在表面摸索，想找出些什么。{w}几乎立刻，我就从口袋里掏出了一样东西。',
        "I kept going over the same spot until I was sure that I'd been right. Something very hard to notice was there. Intrigued, I turned the cloth around and saw that part of the neck area was covered by a different type of material. I put my finger under it and found that the two layers allowed for a narrow cavity.": '我反复摸同一个地方，直到确信自己没弄错。那里确实有样极难察觉的东西。{w}我来了兴趣，翻开布料，发现领口有一块覆着另一种材质。我把手指探到下面，发现两层布料之间留着一道狭窄的空隙。',
        "A bug. That was what it looked like. I'd never personally seen one, but it had a very similar shape to the ones I'd seen in television shows. It was circular, and on its surface was what looked like a microchip. By adding the location where I'd found it, I could only recognize it as a spying bug.": '窃听器。看上去就是那种东西。{w}我从没亲眼见过，但它的外形和电视节目里出现的非常相似。它是圆形的，表面有个像微型芯片的东西。再结合发现它的位置，我只能认定这是窃听器。',
        "No, that doesn't make a ton of sense. They wouldn't plant it on clothes that are always left in this locker. Could it be the inverse, then? Did Ashiya suspect they were part of Xyn?": '不，这不太说得通。他们不会把窃听器装在这种一直留在柜子里的衣服上。{w}那么，反过来呢？难道是芦屋怀疑这名员工是 Xyn 的人？',
        'I had no idea, but thinking that Sai was the killer didn\'t fit very well either. Why had he spared my life earlier? Could he really have found a hidden knife we all missed? He even said it was poorly hidden and that he\'d overstepped... What the hell did that mean? "Heh... That\'s wrong." Sai\'s voice played in my head. "What you two just said... is wrong."': '我毫无头绪，可认为 Sai 是凶手也同样说不通。他之前为什么放我一条生路？他真的找到了我们都没发现的藏刀吗？他甚至说那把刀藏得很拙劣，还说自己越界了……那到底是什么意思？{w}「呵……不对。」Sai 的声音在我脑中响起。{w}「你们俩刚才说的……错了。」',
        'Should I take his word at face value and accept that he knows better than us? What exactly is wrong about that? I can think of three different things.': '我该不该就这么信了他的话，承认他比我们更清楚内情？{w} 可我们刚才说的究竟哪里错了？我能想到三处。',
        "He might've been referring to the part where his clothes would disappear forever. Perhaps they would appear somewhere, but that doesn't sound too likely. Maybe he really meant that the Sekimeiya couldn't have achieved that, but there's no way we were wrong. We know such a thing could've occurred because the key to Naomi's locker was reconstructed in my pocket by traveling. Did he maybe mean that he never could've achieved that under his own circumstances? Maybe he figured out what determines the replicated location, and he knew that given the way it works, the Sekimeiya would never have replicated a point in which his clothes were clean. Could that be it...?": '他指的也许是衣服会永远消失那件事。那些衣服或许会出现在别的地方，但这听起来不太可能。{w} 又或者他真正的意思是，Sekimeiya 根本做不到这种事——可我们绝不可能弄错。钥匙就是证据：Naomi 储物柜的钥匙，正是在穿越中从我口袋里复现出来的。{w} 难道他想说的是，换作他自己的处境，他绝无可能做到？也许他已经弄清是什么决定了复现位置，并且知道按这套机制，Sekimeiya 绝不会复现出他衣服干净的那个时间点。会是这样吗……？',
        "Oh, right, when I appeared in the security room and fell backward because the chair wasn't properly positioned for me to sit on it. The position where I appeared indicated that the replicated location was of me sitting on that chair, but I had never done that. Oh, and the recording too. Of course, if it's legitimate, we assumed it was brought from the future. While there isn't a big issue, the way we were thinking the Sekimeiya worked doesn't make it that simple.": '哦，对了——那次我出现在监控室，椅子没摆在我坐下去的位置，我整个人向后摔倒。我出现的位置表明，复现位置对应的是我坐在那把椅子上的样子，可我从没那样坐过。{w} 还有那段录音。当然，如果它是真的，我们之前一直推测它是从未来带回来的。这本身倒不是什么大问题，但按照我们原先对 Sekimeiya 运作方式的理解，事情没这么简单。',
        "In a month from now, someone would have to hold the voice recorder. Then, farther in the future, that same person would have to go all the way back to today and have the time in which they held it as the replicated location. It's not reasonable to rule that out, but it complicates everything a lot more. But I can't just abandon that way of thinking about it. It can't be that you can bring any item you have to the past, or else the cleaning cart would've appeared with Shiroya in the attic.": '一个月后，得有人拿着那支录音笔。然后在更远的未来，同一个人还得一路回到今天，把他拿着录音笔的那段时间作为复现位置。{w} 这固然不能排除，但会让一切都复杂得多。{w} 可我也不能就此放弃这种思路。总不至于身上的任何东西都能带回过去吧——否则清洁车早该跟着 Shiroya 一起出现在阁楼里了。',
        "How can we be wrong? There's no way we are...! We appeared in the attic exactly where we'd been prior to that point. That position was definitely based on a previous one, so we can't be completely wrong. However, there's the security room instance... Like I thought back then, that can't be a random location... Sitting in front of the computer... Could it have been influenced by Katei's past position? He was the one who sat on that chair a while before our travel, but why would this have mattered!?": '我们怎么会错？绝不可能……！我们出现在阁楼时，位置正是之前待过的地方。那个位置绝对是基于先前的经历，所以我们的想法不可能全盘皆错。可监控室那一次……{w} 就像我当时想的，那不可能是个随意的位置……坐在电脑前……难道是被 Katei 之前的位置影响了？{w} 在我们穿越前不久，坐过那把椅子的人正是他，可这又有什么关系！？',
        "I saw my own back, walking away. I immediately understood where I'd gone. Definitely more than fifteen minutes back, to the point where I'd circled around the crystal floor hallways.": '我看到了自己的背影，正朝远处走去。{w} 我立刻明白自己回到了哪段时间。绝对不止十五分钟，而是回到了我在水晶层走廊来回打转的时候。',
        "I forcibly expelled that thought from my mind. There was no way Shiroya could suddenly die like that. ...But as much as I tried to reassure myself of that, Miiya's abrupt end pressed down on the back of my head.": '我强行把这个念头赶出脑海。Shiroya 怎么可能就这么突然死了。{w} ……可无论我怎样安慰自己，Miiya 那突如其来的死始终压在我心头。',
        "I instantly understood that I had forgotten a crucial detail. I couldn't open the door since Shiroya had recently locked it. Not only that, she'd kept the key.": '{w=1.6}我立刻明白，自己遗漏了一个关键的细节。{w} 门打不开了——Shiroya 不久前刚把阁楼锁上，而且钥匙还留在她手上。',
        'Was it a confirmation that someone else was still with me? Sai and the other Shiroya were the two likely candidates to have done it... I was more confused than surprised. Why would someone have opened that cabinet... and left it open?': '这是否说明还有别人和我一起待在这座塔里？最有可能动手的就是 Sai 和另一个 Shiroya……{w} 比起惊讶，我更觉得困惑。为什么会有人打开那个展示柜……还让它就这么敞着？',
        "I moved the chair and looked at the computer, which displayed 18:24. I felt that going back to the staff room at 18:30 was appropriate, but I didn't want to risk being too early.": '我挪开椅子，看向电脑，屏幕上显示着 {time=18:24.}。我觉得 {time=18:30} 再回员工室正合适，可又不想回去得太早。',
        "I moved the chair and looked at the computer, which displayed 6:24 p.m. I felt that going back to the staff room at 6:30 p.m. was appropriate, but I didn't want to risk being too early.": '我挪开椅子，看向电脑，屏幕上显示着 {time=18:24.}。我觉得 {time=18:30} 再回员工室正合适，可又不想回去得太早。',
        "...Until I remembered the chase from earlier. I kneeled beside Katei and put my hand in the pocket where he'd kept most of his keys.": '……直到我想起先前的那场追逐。{w} 我在 Katei 身边跪下，把手伸进他平时放大部分钥匙的口袋。',
        "They also took that old-looking key... Was the person who originally dropped it in hallway A responsible for this? Maybe that's not it. I've been thinking that someone could enter the tower through the storeroom, but if that key belonged to that door, maybe they'd need it from the outside. I'm not sure they would try picking it up to appear in the past with it because their replicated locations holding the key would all be inside the tower...": '那把旧模样的钥匙也被拿走了……难道当初把它掉在 A走廊的人就是这一切的元凶？{w} 也许不是。我一直在想，有人可以从储藏室进入这座塔；可如果那把钥匙是开那扇门的，他们也许得从外面用它开门。我不确定他们会不会特意捡起那把钥匙、带着它回到过去——因为这样一来，他们所有拿着钥匙的复制位置就都落在塔里了……',
        "Unless I go back to thinking about thought-up loops, I guess. There could be something that would work. The person who killed Katei took that rusty key and walked out of the tower through the storeroom door, which was open. That created a location outside the tower where they were holding the key that could be replicated. Then, they reentered and used the Sekimeiya to go back in time. In the past, they appeared outside the tower holding the key, so they were able to unlock the door and reenter with something they'd obtained outside—like a knife. They left the door open so that their past self could exit with the key and create the replicated location.": '除非我又回头去琢磨那种假想出来的循环。说不定真有办法行得通。{w} 杀死 Katei 的人拿起那把生锈的钥匙，从敞开的储藏室门走出塔外。这样一来，就出现了一个位于塔外、他们手里握着钥匙的位置，而这个位置可以被复制。接着，他们重新进塔，用 Sekimeiya 回到过去。在过去，他们握着钥匙出现在塔外，因此能打开那扇门，带着从外面弄到的东西——比如一把刀——再回来。他们故意没关门，好让过去的自己带着钥匙出去，复制出那个地点。',
        "The computer's screen is lit, meaning that someone used it in the past fifty minutes. It was exactly 17:00 when we found Katei's body, so it's been far more than that.": '电脑屏幕亮着，说明过去五十分钟里有人用过它。我们发现 Katei 的尸体时正好是 {time=17}，到现在早就超过五十分钟了。',
        "The computer's screen is lit, meaning that someone used it in the past fifty minutes. It was exactly 5 p.m. when we found Katei's body, so it's been far more than that.": '电脑屏幕亮着，说明过去五十分钟里有人用过它。我们发现 Katei 的尸体时正好是 {time=17}，到现在早就超过五十分钟了。',
        'What I found most strange was that the three screens looked identical to how they had at 17:00.': '最让我觉得奇怪的是，三块屏幕的样子和 {time=17.} 时一模一样。',
        'What I found most strange was that the three screens looked identical to how they had at 5 p.m.': '最让我觉得奇怪的是，三块屏幕的样子和 {time=17.} 时一模一样。',
        '"10:04: Camera(s) disabled and associated footage erased". That same message was on the side I\'d dragged it to, and behind it was the security camera program.': '「{time=10:04}: 摄像头已停用，相关录像已删除」。这条提示还停在我先前把它拖到的位置，后面就是监控摄像头的程序。',
        '"10:04 a.m.: Camera(s) disabled and associated footage erased". That same message was on the side I\'d dragged it to, and behind it was the security camera program.': '「{time=10:04}: 摄像头已停用，相关录像已删除」。这条提示还停在我先前把它拖到的位置，后面就是监控摄像头的程序。',
        'But an error sound played, accompanied by the same message. "10:04: {tip=camera}Camera(s) disabled and associated footage erased{/tip}".': '可随即响起一声报错音，跳出的仍是那条提示。「{time=10:04}: {tip=camera}摄像头已停用，相关录像已删除{/tip}」。',
        'But an error sound played, accompanied by the same message. "10:04 a.m.: {tip=camera}Camera(s) disabled and associated footage erased{/tip}".': '可随即响起一声报错音，跳出的仍是那条提示。「{time=10:04}: {tip=camera}摄像头已停用，相关录像已删除{/tip}」。',
        'At 18:30, I left the room. It was time to reunite with the Sekimeiya, so I went to hallway B through the event room.': '{time=18:30}，我离开房间。该去取回 Sekimeiya 了，于是我穿过活动室前往 B走廊。',
        'At 6:30 p.m., I left the room. It was time to reunite with the Sekimeiya, so I went to hallway B through the event room.': '{time=18:30}，我离开房间。该去取回 Sekimeiya 了，于是我穿过活动室前往 B走廊。',
        'I pushed the door open and saw the gray Sekimeiya on the floor. Since everything had gone as expected, I entered, reclaiming my place as the sole Atsuki.': '我推开门，看见灰色 Sekimeiya 躺在地上。{w} 一切都在预料之中，我走了进去，重新做回唯一的我。',
        "That was a routine they were happy with and felt lucky to share. The boy let his mind relax, looking at the sky as it began to darken. It would soon be the winter, and the temperature would attempt to hinder those moments. That was why he did as much as he could to enjoy the scenery he'd been granted, hoping the girl at his side was doing the same.": '这样的日常让他们心满意足，也庆幸能一同分享。男孩放松下来，望着天色渐暗。冬天很快就要到了，气温会试图夺走这样的时刻。{w} 所以他尽可能多地去享受眼前这片景色，也希望身旁的女孩同样如此。',
        'They were about to stretch their limbs when an overwhelming light took over their sight. They lost control of their bodies and felt as if they were about to faint. When they next opened their eyes, they were unable to recognize their surroundings.': '他们正要伸展四肢，一道铺天盖地的光吞没了视野。身体失去了掌控，仿佛随时会昏过去。{w} 等他们再次睁眼，四周已全然陌生。',
        'Instead of laughing at it, the boy tried it out. The way he attempted it was by thinking about the object he wanted to create. Instantly, in midair, a red ball appeared. After gravity made it bounce on the floor a few times, he was left speechless by the result of his thought.': '男孩没有把它当笑话，反而试着照做。他只是在脑中想象要造出的东西。{w} 半空中立刻出现了一个红球。重力让它在地上弹了几下，他望着自己念头化出的实物，一时说不出话。',
        "They'd agreed they would trade off on deciding an object per day, but they quickly found that they didn't have many good ideas. The girl had always wanted a spinning egg chair, so she thought of one big enough to put her whole body in. It turned out to be exactly as she'd wanted it, so she spent the full 24 hours inside with a joyful expression.": '两人说好每天轮流决定一件物品，可很快就发现彼此都没什么好点子。女孩一直想要一张旋转蛋椅，于是想了一张大到足以容下她整个身体的。{w} 它果然和她想要的一模一样，她便满脸欢喜地在里面待了整整二十四个小时。',
        "For that reason, the first time he let his emotions burst out, they had automatically taken the form of those simple words. While he'd been wanting to say them for a long time, he wasn't scared the reception might've been negative. He'd simply never been able to bring himself to do it, justifying it as being disconnected. As soon as their new reality had been presented to them, he'd understood that he couldn't spend all that time suppressing his honest and natural feelings.": '所以，当他第一次任由情感倾泻而出时，那份情感自然而然化成了那句简单的话。这句话他想说很久了，倒不怕会被拒绝。他只是始终迈不出那一步，只以「彼此还没到那一步」为由搪塞过去。{w} 而当新的现实摆在眼前，他便明白，自己不能在那漫长岁月里一直压抑这份坦率而自然的心意。',
        '"...Really? I definitely didn\'t think so. That\'s surprising." She had a smile on her face and looked genuinely happy. Looking down and seeing it, the boy sighed in relief, knowing that no matter what would happen, he wouldn\'t regret having said it.': '「……真的吗？我可一点都没看出来。真叫人意外。」{w} 她脸上带着笑，看上去是真心高兴。看见那笑容，男孩松了口气——他知道，无论之后会怎样，他都不会后悔说出口。',
        'But as it turned out, that wasn\'t the end of it. "I\'ve liked you for a long time too. I was pretty scared to say it." Keeping the same smile, she let him know his feelings were shared.': '可事情并没有就此结束。{w}「我也早就喜欢上你了。一直怕得不敢说。」{w} 她带着同样的笑容，让他知道自己并非单相思。',
        "They managed to start up a conversation so that the mood didn't fade. There were many things they wanted to say and many questions to ask. Since when, how much...? The girl knew her chair would soon disappear, so she left it for her bed, where they kept talking until they fell asleep.": '他们好不容易才重新聊了起来，好让气氛不至于冷下去。想说的话很多，想问的事也有很多。{w}从什么时候开始，又有多深……？女孩知道那把椅子很快就要消失，便从椅子上下来，爬上了床，两人一直聊到沉沉睡去。',
        "The chair kept getting brought back every so often. One day, the boy tried it and understood why the girl liked it so much. Glad to see his liking of it, she joined him inside. They hadn't ever felt as close as that, but the relaxing sensation let them spend an entire silent day together, content to be living in the moment. At one point, the girl got confused, thinking the 24 hours must've passed, but she realized that the boy had already silently prolonged the duration, so she continued resting her face next to his.": '那把椅子时不时就会被重新变出来。有一天，男孩也坐了上去，终于明白女孩为什么那么喜欢它。{w}见他喜欢，女孩高兴地钻进椅子里，和他挤在一起。两人从未感到如此亲密。而那种放松的感觉让他们安安静静地一起度过了一整天，谁也没有说话，满足于活在当下。{w}某一刻，女孩糊涂了，以为二十四个小时早已过去，随即发现男孩已经悄悄把时限延长了，便继续把脸贴在他旁边。',
        "Since he'd broken out of his old mold, the boy had grown used to only voicing his true thoughts, like he'd always wanted to do. Some days, they would try to materialize new objects. When it was his turn, he created a huge trampoline. He'd always found them fun, and he'd thought of generating one for a while. They let themselves loose and used it for hours, as if their bodies couldn't wear out.": '摆脱旧日的壳之后，男孩渐渐习惯只把真实的想法说出口——这正是他一直想做的事。{w}有些日子，他们会试着变出新的东西。轮到他时，他变出了一张巨大的蹦床。他向来觉得蹦床有趣，也早就想造一个。两人放开手脚玩了起来，在蹦床上跳了好几个小时，仿佛身体永远不会疲惫。',
        "At one point, they stopped creating new objects, knowing they could just be in the egg chair. They were happy to live like that, but they knew there was a detail they'd barely talked about.": '到了某个时候，他们不再变出新的东西，因为只要待在蛋形椅里就足够了。{w}就这样过下去，他们很幸福，但他们清楚，有个细节，两人几乎从未谈起过。',
        'The girl responded quickly. "...Yes, but it\'ll be okay. We know how long we\'ve liked each other for in the real world, so whoever remembers will just tell the other about it. There are so many things I want to do with you once we\'re back. Since one of us will remember, we can do all of them and more."': '女孩很快答道。{w}「……怕。不过没关系的。我们在现实世界里喜欢了对方多久，彼此都清楚，所以无论谁记得，只要告诉另一个人就好。回去之后，我想和你做的事多得很。既然总有一人会记得，那些事就都能做，还能做更多。」',
        '"All right. Whoever keeps these memories will confess to the other as soon as we come back." Then, they would live the life they\'d been talking about for so long.': '「好。不管是谁留下了这些记忆，回去之后都要立刻向对方表白。」{w}然后，他们就要去过谈论了那么久的那种生活。',
        "And, once again, time went on. They didn't get tired of talking, of thinking, of caressing, and of living. They spent every second as if no time was passing.": '而时间，又一次向前流去。{w}谈话、思索、抚触、相伴度日——这些他们从不厌倦。每一秒都过得仿佛时间并未流逝。',
        '"Whoever keeps these memories will confess to the other as soon as we come back." What? No... he couldn\'t do that.': '「不管是谁留下了这些记忆，回去之后都要立刻向对方表白。」{w}什么？不……他做不到。',
        'She approached him with a worried face. "Are you okay?" He wasn\'t confused about what had happened. He understood it perfectly well, and the only thing he felt was emptiness. After nodding, he continued walking.': '她满脸担忧地凑近。「你没事吧？」{w}对发生的事，他并不困惑。他完全明白，心里只剩下空茫。他点了点头，继续往前走。',
        "The two same barriers had come back: himself, and uncertainty. Not a second of those hundred years had mattered. No, of course that was wrong. He'd have to cherish and remember the times they'd spent in that intimate room... because, in the real world, they would never happen.": '同样的两道屏障又回来了：他自己，以及不确定。那百年之中的每一秒都毫无意义。{w}不，当然不是这样。他必须珍惜并记住他们在那间亲密小室里度过的时光……因为在现实世界里，那些时光永远不会发生。',
        'Looking a little sad, the girl smiled and waved. Then, as they always did, both of them took different paths. ...And yet again, only one of them found it significant.': '女孩带着几分落寞笑了笑，挥了挥手。{w}随后，两人一如既往地各自走向不同的方向。……然而这一次，依旧只有一个人觉得这意味深长。',
        "I'd always been prone to letting my imagination run wild, and sometimes I'd make up full little stories. Unable to sleep one night, I'd thought of that one.": '我向来容易让想象信马由缰，有时还会编出完整的小故事来。{w}某个睡不着的夜里，我想到的便是这一个。',
        '"I need to say it. I\'ve always wanted to, and I can\'t believe I never will. I love you."': '「我必须说出来。{w}我一直都想说，怎么也想不到竟会再没有机会。{w}我爱你。」',
        "But it couldn't be. I'd never written that, and I never would. However, I knew very well the single thing that could've ever made that note a reality. A voice played in my mind.": '可这不可能。我从没写过那样的东西，也绝不会写。然而我比谁都清楚，唯一能让那张纸条成真的，会是什么。{w} 一个声音在脑海里响起。',
        '"Shiroya\'s fate is death."': '「Shiroya 的命运是死亡。」{w=2.8}{nw}',
        "No—it wouldn't happen. That note had my handwriting, but it didn't mean anything. I would never write it. Even if the worst happened at a later point, I wouldn't. But... it existed. I had it in my hands.": '不——不会的。那张纸条上虽是我的字迹，却说明不了什么。我绝不会写下它。哪怕往后真出了最坏的事，我也不会写。{w} 可是……它确实存在。就在我手里。',
        "Soon, my voice started to crack as I realized how close I was to the reality in which my oldest friend had died. Sai had spoken it like it was an absolute, and I'd found a note I wished I'd never read. I kept telling myself that there had to be another meaning, but my shouts devolved into hopeless crying until I fell to my knees in the middle of the hallway.": '很快，我的嗓音开始嘶哑，因为我意识到自己离那个现实有多近——那个现实里，我最好的朋友已经死了。Sai 说出那话时犹如宣判，而我又捡到了一张宁愿从未读过的纸条。{w} 我不断告诉自己那一定另有含义，可呼喊渐渐变成绝望的哭嚎，最后我跪倒在走廊中央。',
        "There, I saw a slender figure looking at me. It was Shiroya, her face near the breaking point. However, she wasn't the one I'd been thinking of. Her clothes were from the attic, and despite her expression, she felt wrong in a way I couldn't define.": '在那里，我看见一个纤细的身影正望着我。{w} 是 Shiroya，她脸上的神情几近崩溃。可她并不是我一直在找的那个人。她穿着阁楼里的衣服，尽管表情如此，她身上却有种说不清的不对劲。',
        "Wh-Where were you? What's with those clothes? Are you the same person who disappeared with Sai?": '你、你刚才在哪儿？这身衣服是怎么回事？{w} 你就是和 Sai 一起消失的那个人吗？',
        'You guess so? What do you mean? You remember everything, right?': '你是猜的？{w} 你什么意思？你什么都记得吧？',
        "I'm glad to see you two are safe. I was a bit worried... Wh-What's with those clothes? You weren't wearing them earlier, were you...?": '看到你们俩平安无事，我就放心了。我原本还有点担心……{w} 这、这身衣服是怎么回事？你们先前穿的不是这个吧……？',
        "She nodded. If that was the case, it was painfully simple, and I'd failed to think about it because of all the overlapping thoughts I'd had on the matter. I'd been thinking about a replicated body who'd shared the stained blood but not any wound, while, sure enough, we'd never actually confirmed there'd been one. And, of course, the blood. If it wasn't hers, there was another very clear candidate to consider.": '她点了点头。{w}若真是如此，答案简单得近乎残酷，我却因为心里翻来覆去的种种推测，始终没往这上面想。我一直在设想那是一具复制出来的身体，沾着同样的血迹，却没有任何伤口，可事实上，我们从未真正确认过她身上有伤。{w}还有那些血。既然不是她的，那就还有一个再明显不过的人选。',
        "A-Are you serious...? Were you playing dead, then? Or just unconscious? It doesn't look like you feel very well.": '你、你说真的……？{w}那你是在装死？还是只是昏过去了？你的脸色看起来很差。',
        'The Sekimeiya... does it really make you travel through time? How does it work?': 'Sekimeiya……它真的能让人穿越时间吗？{w}是怎么做到的？',
        "...Neither of us knew how to answer. We'd concluded the past couldn't be altered, so that shouldn't have been possible.": '……{w}我们两人都不知道该如何回答。我们早已得出结论：过去无法改变，所以那本该是做不到的。',
        "I don't know why I didn't think of it earlier. Someone killed her a few hours ago, so I just have to go to that time and prevent it. But I couldn't find the Sekimeiya. I kept looking at Isla's face for a very long time, and she told me that she could be saved. Then, I saw a girl, and after that I heard you shouting.": '我不知道自己为什么没早点想到。她几小时前被人杀了，那我只要回到那个时间点阻止那件事就行了。{w}可我找不到 Sekimeiya。我盯着 Isla 的脸看了很久很久，她告诉我，她还有救。接着，我看见了一个女孩，之后便听到了你的喊声。',
        "Um... I guess it couldn't have been anyone else. ...It must have been Shiroya.": '嗯……{w}我想那也不可能是别人。{w}……一定是 Shiroya。',
        "...It couldn't have been an accident. But anyway, the Sekimeiya's not in the event room.": '……那不可能是意外。{w}不过话说回来，Sekimeiya 不在活动室。',
        'Are you sure...? Do you know where it could be? I really need to find it.': '你确定……？{w}你知道它可能在哪儿吗？我真的必须找到它。',
        '...Are you lying?': '……{w}你在说谎吗？',
        'Sai... where the fuck did you go? Were you in the attic? Do you know where Shiroya went? I saw her disappear with you.': 'Sai……你他妈到底去哪儿了？你刚才在阁楼里？{w}你知道 Shiroya 去哪儿了吗？我看见她和你一起消失了。',
        "I see, they're definitely an improvement for you. And just ignore me, Atsuki. I was busy sorting something out.": '原来如此，穿在你身上确实顺眼多了。{w}还有，别管我，Atsuki。我刚才正忙着理清一些事。',
        "More moments of silence followed. Erina still showed no signs of reconsideration, and we couldn't forcefully take the Sekimeiya from her. Sai had nonchalantly said that fifteen minutes would be enough to go many hours back when I'd just traveled approximately twenty minutes after storing that amount of time. I looked at Erina's purse, where the Sekimeiya was getting hotter and hotter.": '随后又是一阵沉默。Erina 丝毫没有回心转意的迹象，我们也不能硬从她手里抢走 Sekimeiya。{w}Sai 轻描淡写地说，等上十五分钟就足以回到好几个小时之前；可我才刚蓄能十五分钟，却只穿越了大约二十分钟。我望向 Erina 的手袋，里面的 Sekimeiya 正越来越烫。',
        'You look pretty nervous. I saw something written there. You were pretty in control of things when you pulled off that trick with the key earlier, so why is this getting you all worked up? Do you wanna hide it that badly?': '你看起来挺紧张的。我可看见上面写着字。{w}刚才你耍钥匙那套把戏时，还一副胸有成竹的样子，怎么现在反倒急成这样？你就那么想把它藏起来？',
        "...It's just a personal paper. It has nothing to do with you or the Sekimeiya.": '……{w}只是一张私人纸条，和你、和 Sekimeiya 都没有关系。',
        'What... the fuck is going on?': '这……{w}他妈到底是怎么回事？',
        "What's with that reaction? Don't you see she's just delirious? She didn't die, but I have a pretty good idea of what happened to her. Say, did you hallucinate someone?": '你这是什么反应？看不出来她只是在说胡话吗？{w}她没死，不过她身上发生了什么，我大致猜得到。话说回来，你是不是产生了幻觉，看见了某个人？',
        'Oh? Is she dead? ...Wait, Miiya, you said...?': '哦？她死了？{w}……等等，你刚才说 Miiya……？',
        "Miiya's hair... was red. I recalled Akaro's voice from the time he'd lost some of his memories. What he'd said almost implied that he knew what happened to Miiya and what we'd gone through.": 'Miiya 的头发……是红色的。{w}我想起了 Akaro 失去部分记忆时的声音。他当时说的话，几乎暗示他知道 Miiya 遭遇了什么，也知道我们经历了什么。',
        'Did Erina just lie...? How would she know about her? And why would she do that?': '难道是 Erina 在撒谎……？{w}她怎么会知道 Miiya？又为什么要撒这种谎？',
        'She died at around 14:00, right? It should be enough, yes.': '她是在 {time=14} 前后死的吧？那应该够了。',
        'She died at around 2 p.m., right? It should be enough, yes.': '她是在 {time=14} 前后死的吧？那应该够了。',
        "That's strange. Once again, if she's about to travel to the past, how come her past self hasn't already appeared? Of course, seeing her future self should be an impossibility, but why would she have decided not to show herself?": '奇怪。还是那个问题，如果她马上就要穿越回过去，那过去的她为什么还没出现？{w}当然，她不可能见到未来的自己，可她为什么决定不露面呢？',
        "Earlier, Sai had traveled after storing energy for fifteen minutes—the same amount. At that time, I hadn't traveled despite being next to Shiroya, so I knew how big the range would be. I stepped back too to be sure I wasn't included and wouldn't travel away from Shiroya.": '先前 Sai 蓄能十五分钟——同样长的时间——之后便穿越了。{w}那时我就在 Shiroya 身边，却没有被一起传走，所以我知道范围有多大。我也退开了几步，确保自己不在范围内，不会从 Shiroya 身边被传送走。',
        "Why didn't it work!? Did Sai disappear? Was everything that he said a lie...?": '为什么没有生效！？Sai 消失了吗？{w} 难道他说的一切都是谎话……？',
        'In fact, the teleportation probably caused the illusion from the start... The "other" Sekimeiya. I\'m not sure how it happened, but I bet it was the same one every time.': '实际上，那个假象很可能从一开始就是传送造成的……那个「另一个」Sekimeiya。{w} 我不清楚是怎么做到的，但我敢打赌，每次出现的都是同一个。',
        "The second is the most confusing one. Erina, Shiroya, and I haven't traveled. There's no way we weren't included in the range, is there? At least not Erina, who touched the Sekimeiya... But it only worked for Sai... There has to be a reason why we were excluded, but is it reasonable to think I can figure it out?": '第二个疑问最令人费解。Erina、Shiroya 和我都没有穿越。我们不可能不在范围内吧？至少碰过 Sekimeiya 的 Erina 不会不在……{w} 可生效的偏偏只有 Sai……我们被排除在外一定有其原因，但我真能想明白吗？',
        "Can I... not save Isla? Why did it not work...? Oh, of course. What was I even thinking? Traveling to the past isn't possible. You lied about it since the beginning, right? That's why it didn't work: it can't happen. I actually fell for it.": '我……救不了 Isla 吗？为什么没有生效……？{w} 啊，当然了。{w} 我到底在想什么？回到过去根本不可能。{w} 你从一开始就在骗我，对不对？所以才会失败：那根本不可能发生。我居然真的上当了。',
        "The Sekimeiya wasn't there. Only the pants and the coat remained inside. I closed the door and locked it again.": 'Sekimeiya 不在里面。柜中只剩下裤子和外套。{w}我关上门，重新上了锁。',
        '"So many hours". Right, she thinks Sai went back to before Isla died. In reality, he went back about twenty minutes, if that\'s consistent. ...Although she just went from saying time travel isn\'t possible to thinking it is again. She\'s more unstable than I thought.': '「这么多小时」……没错，她以为 Sai 回到了 Isla 死前的时候。可实际上，如果规律没变，他只回溯了二十分钟左右。{w}……不过她刚才还说时间穿越不可能，转眼又觉得确有其事。她比我想的还要不稳定。',
        '...! Wh-Who the fuck are you? How are you here?': '……！{w}你、你他妈是谁？怎么会在这儿？',
        "Well... No. Of course we do. Aren't you... dead?": '呃……不认识。{w}不对，当然认识。{w}你不是……死了吗？',
        "Uh... it's {time=18:43.}": '呃……{w} 现在是 {time=18:43.}。',
        "Uh...{w} it's 18:43.": '呃……{w} 现在是 {time=18:43.}。',
        "Uh... it's 18:43.": '呃……{w} 现在是 {time=18:43.}。',
        "Uh...{w} it's 6:43 p.m.": '呃……{w} 现在是 {time=18:43.}。',
        "Uh... it's 6:43 p.m.": '呃……{w} 现在是 {time=18:43.}。',
        "{time=18:43.}.. That was about twenty minutes behind the real time I estimated. That meant Sai's replicated location after traveling had been twenty minutes prior, and his watch hadn't stopped working.": '{time=18:43.}……{w}这比我估算的真实时间慢了大约二十分钟。也就是说，Sai 穿越后出现的位置，其实是二十分钟前的位置；而他的手表并没有停走。',
        "18:43...{w} That was about twenty minutes behind the real time I estimated. That meant Sai's replicated location after traveling had been twenty minutes prior, and his watch hadn't stopped working.": '{time=18:43.}……{w}这比我估算的真实时间慢了大约二十分钟。也就是说，Sai 穿越后出现的位置，其实是二十分钟前的位置；而他的手表并没有停走。',
        "18:43... That was about twenty minutes behind the real time I estimated. That meant Sai's replicated location after traveling had been twenty minutes prior, and his watch hadn't stopped working.": '{time=18:43.}……{w}这比我估算的真实时间慢了大约二十分钟。也就是说，Sai 穿越后出现的位置，其实是二十分钟前的位置；而他的手表并没有停走。',
        "6:43 p.m...{w} That was about twenty minutes behind the real time I estimated. That meant Sai's replicated location after traveling had been twenty minutes prior, and his watch hadn't stopped working.": '{time=18:43.}……{w}这比我估算的真实时间慢了大约二十分钟。也就是说，Sai 穿越后出现的位置，其实是二十分钟前的位置；而他的手表并没有停走。',
        "6:43 p.m... That was about twenty minutes behind the real time I estimated. That meant Sai's replicated location after traveling had been twenty minutes prior, and his watch hadn't stopped working.": '{time=18:43.}……{w}这比我估算的真实时间慢了大约二十分钟。也就是说，Sai 穿越后出现的位置，其实是二十分钟前的位置；而他的手表并没有停走。',
        'Hold on, though... Your name... I think I might actually remember that. Shi... roya, was it? My memories are a little foggy.': '不过，等等……你的名字……我好像还真有印象。{w}Shi……roya，对吧？我的记忆有点模糊。',
        "I've been with you since 9:00, Sai.": 'Sai，从 {time=9} 起，我就一直和你们在一起。',
        "I've been with you since 9 a.m., Sai.": 'Sai，从 {time=9} 起，我就一直和你们在一起。',
        "...I do, and she's telling the truth.": '……{w}我认识，而且她说的是实话。',
        'The entire time? Not even you have been here since 9:00!': '一直都在？从 {time=9} 起，连你都不在这里啊！',
        'The entire time? Not even you have been here since 9 a.m.!': '一直都在？从 {time=9} 起，连你都不在这里啊！',
        '...Oh...!': '……{w}啊……！',
        '...I... need to go somewhere.': '……{w}我……得去个地方。',
        '"Please, don\'t follow me." Why...? Why did she want to go alone...? I was sure I looked devastated, but I was only trying to decipher the sudden change of behavior my oldest friend had undergone.': '「请你别跟来。」为什么……？她为什么非要一个人去……？{w}我当时一定显得很受打击，可我只是想弄明白，我认识最久的那位朋友为什么会突然变成这样。',
        "You can stop trying already. Since you sided with that girl, you made it clear you'll only spit out bullshit. I don't know what you're trying to pull, but you look pathetic. She'll come back whenever she feels like, if she doesn't die in the process. Meanwhile, let's keep waiting for the shutter to open. I'd appreciate it if you told the truth, though. How did she get in?": '省省吧。你既然站在那女孩那边，就已经表明你只会满嘴胡扯。我不知道你想耍什么花样，但你看起来真可悲。{w}只要她没死在半路，想回来时自然会回来。在这之前，我们继续等卷帘门打开吧。不过，你要是肯说实话，我会很感激。她是怎么进来的？',
        "That's false. Since she seems to be with you, I really doubt you were stupid enough to make her enter through the storeroom. That's what's strange, but perhaps you did. Let me see.": '不对。她看起来是和你一起的，所以我实在不觉得你会蠢到让她从储藏室进来。奇怪就奇怪在这里，不过也许你真这么做了。{w}让我看看。',
        'Instead of answering, he entered the storeroom. Seconds later, he returned.': '他没有回答，径直走进储藏室。{w}几秒后，又折了回来。',
        "That's harsh. I suppose that's the only way you can defend yourself. We'll see what your plan amounts to soon. Maybe not, actually. Maybe we'll just never see that girl again. At least not alive, of course.": '真狠啊。看来你也只能靠这种方式自保了。很快就能知道你的计划究竟能走到哪一步。{w}不过，也许根本等不到那时候。也许我们再也不会见到那女孩了。当然，至少不会活着见到她。',
        "...I don't know.": '……{w}我不知道。',
        'There were too many things I needed to understand. Questions had barraged me since 9:00, and each one was more complex than the last. With the little time we had left, there was no way I could be optimistic and think that everything was magically going to be resolved.': '需要弄明白的事太多了。自从{time=9}起，疑问就接二连三地压过来，而且一个比一个复杂。剩下的时间如此有限，我根本无法乐观地相信一切会奇迹般迎刃而解。',
        'There were too many things I needed to understand. Questions had barraged me since 9 a.m., and each one was more complex than the last. With the little time we had left, there was no way I could be optimistic and think that everything was magically going to be resolved.': '需要弄明白的事太多了。自从{time=9}起，疑问就接二连三地压过来，而且一个比一个复杂。剩下的时间如此有限，我根本无法乐观地相信一切会奇迹般迎刃而解。',
        "The way she looked at me... It was like she was telling me that if I followed her, I would hinder whatever she wanted to do. But she was already in hallway C. If she really wanted me not to come along, all she had to do was use the elevator up to the attic and I'd have no way to chase her.": '她看我的眼神……像是在告诉我，如果我跟上去，就会妨碍她想做的事。{w}可她已经到了 C走廊。如果她真不想我跟着，只要乘电梯上阁楼，我根本没法追上去。',
        "Is this all the time you needed to give her? Let me see... It's {time=19:08.}": '你给她留的时间就这么点？{w}我看看……现在是{time=19:08.}',
        "Is this all the time you needed to give her?{w} Let me see... It's 19:08.": '你给她留的时间就这么点？{w}我看看……现在是{time=19:08.}',
        "Is this all the time you needed to give her? Let me see... It's 19:08.": '你给她留的时间就这么点？{w}我看看……现在是{time=19:08.}',
        "Is this all the time you needed to give her?{w} Let me see... It's 7:08 p.m.": '你给她留的时间就这么点？{w}我看看……现在是{time=19:08.}',
        "Is this all the time you needed to give her? Let me see... It's 7:08 p.m.": '你给她留的时间就这么点？{w}我看看……现在是{time=19:08.}',
        'Ah!': '啊！{nw}',
        'W—': '什——{nw}',
        "Nobody's here! I... didn't press the button either! We need to... stop the bleeding. We could use something from the attic!": '这里没人！我……我也没按过按钮！{w}我们得先……止血。阁楼里应该有能用的东西！',
        "But desperately searching by myself sounded overwhelming. I wouldn't stop losing blood any time soon, making me more and more tired. The pain wasn't going to suddenly fade, and there was no way I would be able to tolerate it until 21:00 on top of everything else.": '可要独自一人拼命寻找，光是想想就让人吃不消。血一时止不住，我只会越来越疲惫。疼痛也不会忽然消退，何况我还得一直忍到 {time=21}——我根本撑不住。',
        "But desperately searching by myself sounded overwhelming. I wouldn't stop losing blood any time soon, making me more and more tired. The pain wasn't going to suddenly fade, and there was no way I would be able to tolerate it until 9 p.m. on top of everything else.": '可要独自一人拼命寻找，光是想想就让人吃不消。血一时止不住，我只会越来越疲惫。疼痛也不会忽然消退，何况我还得一直忍到 {time=21}——我根本撑不住。',
        "The second thing was a thought. I knew I looked just like Erina had previously, so I found myself suddenly coming back to something she'd recently said.": '第二样，是一个念头。{w}我知道自己现在的模样，就和先前的 Erina 一样，于是忽然想起她前不久说过的话。',
        "18:54, precisely what I'd estimated. For a short time, at least, I could try to experiment and gain some form of knowledge, no matter how small. Feeling like I could trust my judgment a bit better than before, I stepped out and went over what I'd been thinking.": '{time=18:54}，与我的估算分毫不差。至少在这一小段时间里，我可以试着做些验证，获取些情报，哪怕再微不足道。我觉得自己比先前更能信任自己的判断了，于是走出门，重新梳理此前的想法。',
        "6:54 p.m., precisely what I'd estimated. For a short time, at least, I could try to experiment and gain some form of knowledge, no matter how small. Feeling like I could trust my judgment a bit better than before, I stepped out and went over what I'd been thinking.": '{time=18:54}，与我的估算分毫不差。至少在这一小段时间里，我可以试着做些验证，获取些情报，哪怕再微不足道。我觉得自己比先前更能信任自己的判断了，于是走出门，重新梳理此前的想法。',
        "So, I had an idea: a sound. To start off, I could produce a loud sound I knew I hadn't heard. If I managed to make it happen, the past could be changed.": '于是，我有了个主意：制造一声响动。{w} 一开始，我可以先弄出一声我确定自己从未听过的巨响。只要能做到，就说明过去可以被改变。',
        "I twisted the knob on the door and pushed it open. It was fully in my reach: I could slam the door and generate a considerably loud sound that hadn't previously existed. Was the universe about to black out? I'd shortly find out, as I really intended to do it.": '我拧开门把，推开门。这完全做得到：只要摔上门，就能造出一声此前从未有过的巨响。{w} 宇宙会就此陷入黑暗吗？很快便见分晓——我真的打算这么做。',
        "I ran toward the stairs and quickly disappeared from view. I hadn't edited my memories at all. I still remembered the reality in which no sound had played. It was a potentially massive problem; I could've created a reality in which two versions of myself existed permanently. If I'd separated myself from my past version who was on the crystal floor, he wouldn't ever travel and leave his place for me to occupy like what had been happening so far.": '我朝楼梯跑去，转眼便脱离了视线。我的记忆丝毫未变。我依然记得那个没有响起任何声音的现实。{w} 这或许是个大问题：我可能造出了一个两个我永久并存的现实。若我与留在水晶层的那个过去的我分开，他就永远不会穿越，也不会像至今这样腾出位置让我顶替。',
        "I felt a piercing pain and looked at my hand. Running with clenched fists had slightly reopened the wound, and a small amount of blood was dribbling out. If I'd left some behind, it would create a trail to find my whereabouts. I looked at the staircase and saw very little blood.": '一阵刺痛袭来，我看向自己的手。握拳奔跑让伤口又微微裂开，渗出一点血来。要是这样一路滴下去，就会留下追查我下落的血迹。{w} 我朝楼梯看了一眼，只看到很少的血迹。',
        "Less than two hours remained until {time=21.} The alarm had gone off at about {time=9:05}, and the automatic unlock was rapidly approaching. Was it enough time to try putting things into practice? I still didn't know what consequences would truly come out of my change. Would I permanently have differing memories from the people around me? Would I have to coexist with another Atsuki?": '距离 {time=21.} 还剩不到两个小时。警报大约在 {time=9:05} 响过，自动解锁的时刻正迅速逼近。这些时间够不够我试着付诸实践？{w}我仍不知道自己的改变究竟会带来什么后果。我会永远和身边的人拥有不同的记忆吗？我是不是必须和另一个 Atsuki 共存？',
        "Less than two hours remained until 21:00. The alarm had gone off at about 9:05, and the automatic unlock was rapidly approaching. Was it enough time to try putting things into practice?{w} I still didn't know what consequences would truly come out of my change. Would I permanently have differing memories from the people around me? Would I have to coexist with another Atsuki?": '距离 {time=21.} 还剩不到两个小时。警报大约在 {time=9:05} 响过，自动解锁的时刻正迅速逼近。这些时间够不够我试着付诸实践？{w}我仍不知道自己的改变究竟会带来什么后果。我会永远和身边的人拥有不同的记忆吗？我是不是必须和另一个 Atsuki 共存？',
        "Less than two hours remained until 21:00. The alarm had gone off at about 9:05, and the automatic unlock was rapidly approaching. Was it enough time to try putting things into practice? I still didn't know what consequences would truly come out of my change. Would I permanently have differing memories from the people around me? Would I have to coexist with another Atsuki?": '距离 {time=21.} 还剩不到两个小时。警报大约在 {time=9:05} 响过，自动解锁的时刻正迅速逼近。这些时间够不够我试着付诸实践？{w}我仍不知道自己的改变究竟会带来什么后果。我会永远和身边的人拥有不同的记忆吗？我是不是必须和另一个 Atsuki 共存？',
        "Less than two hours remained until 9 p.m. The alarm had gone off at about 9:05 a.m., and the automatic unlock was rapidly approaching. Was it enough time to try putting things into practice?{w} I still didn't know what consequences would truly come out of my change. Would I permanently have differing memories from the people around me? Would I have to coexist with another Atsuki?": '距离 {time=21.} 还剩不到两个小时。警报大约在 {time=9:05} 响过，自动解锁的时刻正迅速逼近。这些时间够不够我试着付诸实践？{w}我仍不知道自己的改变究竟会带来什么后果。我会永远和身边的人拥有不同的记忆吗？我是不是必须和另一个 Atsuki 共存？',
        "Less than two hours remained until 9 p.m. The alarm had gone off at about 9:05 a.m., and the automatic unlock was rapidly approaching. Was it enough time to try putting things into practice? I still didn't know what consequences would truly come out of my change. Would I permanently have differing memories from the people around me? Would I have to coexist with another Atsuki?": '距离 {time=21.} 还剩不到两个小时。警报大约在 {time=9:05} 响过，自动解锁的时刻正迅速逼近。这些时间够不够我试着付诸实践？{w}我仍不知道自己的改变究竟会带来什么后果。我会永远和身边的人拥有不同的记忆吗？我是不是必须和另一个 Atsuki 共存？',
        'Two hours remain until the front door presumably opens. In about thirty minutes is when I traveled to the past, but that might not happen anymore. This means that I could have the chance to let the Sekimeiya gather power until 21:05.': '距离前门开启大概还有两个小时。我原本会在三十分钟后穿越回过去，但如今那件事或许不会再发生。也就是说，我或许有机会让 Sekimeiya 一直蓄能到 {time=21:05.}',
        'Two hours remain until the front door presumably opens. In about thirty minutes is when I traveled to the past, but that might not happen anymore. This means that I could have the chance to let the Sekimeiya gather power until 9:05 p.m.': '距离前门开启大概还有两个小时。我原本会在三十分钟后穿越回过去，但如今那件事或许不会再发生。也就是说，我或许有机会让 Sekimeiya 一直蓄能到 {time=21:05.}',
        "I went back to a distant thought. Could it be that the shutter wasn't going to move at 21:00 so that the Sekimeiya would store enough time to grant a lengthy travel?": '我又想起了先前的一个念头。卷帘门在 {time=21} 时不会动，会不会就是为了让 Sekimeiya 积蓄足够的时间，从而换来一次长距离的穿越？',
        "I went back to a distant thought. Could it be that the shutter wasn't going to move at 9 p.m. so that the Sekimeiya would store enough time to grant a lengthy travel?": '我又想起了先前的一个念头。卷帘门在 {time=21} 时不会动，会不会就是为了让 Sekimeiya 积蓄足够的时间，从而换来一次长距离的穿越？',
        "That's me... and Erina, as well. I remember those movements.": '那是我……{w}还有 Erina。那些动作我记得。',
        'Yes... Should we keep going up?': '嗯……{w}要继续往上走吗？',
        '...When, exactly?': '……{w}具体是什么时候？',
        "Uh... I... don't know. My head is still a bit foggy, but I don't remember that.": '呃……{w}我……不知道。脑子还有点迷糊，可我不记得有过这回事。',
        "Erina's above us. By the way, about 35 minutes ago, did you hear the sound of a door closing coming from hallway A?": 'Erina 在上面。{w}对了，大概三十五分钟前，你有没有听到从 A走廊传来的关门声？',
        'What? What kind of question is that?': '啊？{w}这算什么问题？',
        '...{tip=lie}Yes{/tip}, why?': '……{w}{tip=lie}听到了{/tip}，怎么了？',
        "When Erina and I had taken the elevator, those drops hadn't existed. There were too many of them to think I hadn't seen them. Sai was definitely living in the reality I'd changed, but I wasn't sure the same could be said for Erina.": '我和 Erina 乘电梯经过时，那里还没有这些血迹。数量不少，我不可能没看见。{w}Sai 无疑活在我改变过的现实里，但 Erina 是否也一样，我就说不准了。',
        "...Excuse me? I don't have the key, no. You can search me if you want. I don't have it.": '……你说什么？我没有钥匙。{w}不信可以搜我的身，我没有。',
        "...Let's go up, then. Shiroya might actually be in the attic.": '……{w}那就上去看看吧。Shiroya 说不定真在阁楼里。',
        "I told you. It's locked. Do you not have the key?": '我说过了，门锁着。{w}你没带钥匙？',
        'Hey! Shiroya! Are you inside? Why would you lock yourself in like this!?': '喂！Shiroya！你在里面吗？{w}干嘛把自己锁在这种地方啊！？',
        "...! You're all right!": '……！{w}你们没事！',
        "O-Oh! Thank God, and sorry... What's with the blood, though?": '啊、啊啊！太好了……抱歉。{w}不过，你身上的血是怎么回事？',
        "Hm... It's 19:40.": '嗯……现在是 {time=19:40.}',
        "Hm... It's 7:40 p.m.": '嗯……现在是 {time=19:40.}',
        "However, one thing is strange. Sai's watch reads 19:40, which I'm pretty sure is the real time. That must mean he's synced it properly.": '不过，有一件事很奇怪。Sai 的表显示 {time=19:40}，我基本可以确定这正是真实时间。也就是说，他已经把表校准好了。',
        "However, one thing is strange. Sai's watch reads 7:40 p.m., which I'm pretty sure is the real time. That must mean he's synced it properly.": '不过，有一件事很奇怪。Sai 的表显示 {time=19:40}，我基本可以确定这正是真实时间。也就是说，他已经把表校准好了。',
        "If we go to the past, I'm pretty sure we could drastically change the way things played out. It's possible some people would still remember this reality, but the change should persist. It's possible two realities just converged, but the real one comes from my change. It overlapped the last one despite some people potentially still remembering it.": '只要回到过去，我们肯定能大幅改变事情的走向。也许有些人仍会记得这个现实，但改动本身应该会保留下来。{w}两个现实也可能就这样交汇了。不过真正的现实来自我的改动，它覆盖了上一个现实，尽管有些人可能还记得那一个。',
        "The things I was saying sounded complicated, but in practice, all they meant was that the past could be changed if we consciously wanted it to. Lingering memories might've been an issue for unaffected people, making them think they were in the wrong reality, but that was a minor issue given what we could accomplish. Of course, I wasn't fully aware of how it worked. I didn't know why some memories could remain or what determined the people who kept them, but factually altering history was all that mattered.": '我说的那些听起来复杂，实际上不过是——只要我们有意识地去做，过去就可以被改变。残留的记忆或许会给未受影响的人带来困扰，让他们以为自己身处错误的现实；但比起我们能达成的事，这只是小问题。{w}当然，我并不完全清楚其中的原理。我不知道为什么有些记忆会留存，也不清楚是什么决定了哪些人保留记忆；但只要事实上能改写历史，其他都无关紧要。',
        "...! It's gone.": '……！{w} 不见了。',
        "It would've been easy, but I'm not completely sure. The door doesn't look like it moved, so it also could've teleported. While you were in the attic, we saw that happen. I definitely witnessed the Sekimeiya teleport to its cabinet. But Sai could've easily grabbed it. Akaro as well. I saw him, and he should still be here somewhere. It was before I changed the past, but all I did was draw attention to hallway A. There's no way that was enough to overwrite Akaro's existence.": '那本来很容易得手，但我也说不准。柜门看上去不像动过，所以它也可能是自己传送走的。{w}你在阁楼那会儿，我们见过这种事。我确实亲眼看见 Sekimeiya 传送进了它的展示柜。{w}但 Sai 完全可以顺手把它拿走，Akaro 也一样。我见过他，他应该还在这栋楼的某处。我看到他是在我改变过去之前，可我只是把注意力引到了 A走廊。那点影响绝不可能抹掉 Akaro 的存在。',
        "Who knows? I couldn't find it, but why do you care? Akaro might be responsible, and he could have taken it outside. If that happened, there's nothing we can do. However, if it's still inside, the police will find it immediately, right? It can be hidden from us, but not from them.": '谁知道呢。反正我没找到。不过这跟你有什么关系？{w}说不定是 Akaro 干的，他可能已经把它带到外面去了。如果真是那样，我们也没办法。{w}不过，它要是还在楼里，警察一进来就能找到，不是吗？它能瞒过我们，却瞒不过他们。',
        "You're free to enlighten me. If I knew where it was, what would my endgame be? Hoping the police don't find it? There's no way that would happen. Someone took it when we weren't around. That must mean they have the means to conceal it from both us and the police. Otherwise, hiding it is pointless.": '那你不妨告诉我。如果我知道它在哪儿，我到底图什么？指望警察找不到它？那绝不可能。{w}有人趁我们不在时拿走了它。那说明对方有办法把它藏得让我们和警察都找不到，否则藏起来根本没有意义。',
        "Are you even listening to yourself? You think I want to steal the Sekimeiya? Sure, I wouldn't say no to having it, but that's not gonna work out. First of all, they'd simply appear in the past. If a bunch of people time travel, the panic would ruin any kind of plan like that. At least a few people have to know what the Sekimeiya is capable of too, right? Why would they send the police to grab it if they know what touching it would do?": '你自己听听你说的这叫什么话？你觉得我想偷 Sekimeiya？是，我不介意把它弄到手，可那根本行不通。{w}首先，他们只会出现在过去。那么多人一起时间穿越，引发的恐慌足以毁掉这种计划。再说，总该有几个人知道 Sekimeiya 有什么能耐吧？他们若知道一碰它会发生什么，又怎么会派警察去拿？',
        "...All right. I agree, so let's just wait.": '……{w}好吧。我同意，那就等着吧。',
        "Okay, let's sit around and wait. I'm exhausted and just want to get out, so I hope nothing else happens. Whatever Xyn or the culprit are up to is no concern of ours anymore... I have no idea what happened to Akaro, but I don't care. If he's behind this whole mess, he'll face the consequences.": '好了，我们就坐着等吧。我已经累坏了，只想出去，所以希望别再出什么事。Xyn 或者真凶想做什么，都跟我们无关了……{w}我不知道 Akaro 出了什么事，也不在乎。如果这一团乱麻是他搞出来的，他自会承担后果。',
        'Nonetheless, if the time truly was 19:50, the end of the lengthy tunnel was near. Would freedom really be found at its exit, or would a new stretch of confinement begin? We were approaching the time where the truth behind the supposed month-away recording would be settled.': '话虽如此，如果此刻真的是 {time=19:50}，那这条漫长的隧道也快到头了。出口处等着的真是自由吗？还是说，新的囚禁才刚要开始？那段号称过了一个月的录音，其真相也快水落石出了。',
        'Nonetheless, if the time truly was 7:50 p.m., the end of the lengthy tunnel was near. Would freedom really be found at its exit, or would a new stretch of confinement begin? We were approaching the time where the truth behind the supposed month-away recording would be settled.': '话虽如此，如果此刻真的是 {time=19:50}，那这条漫长的隧道也快到头了。出口处等着的真是自由吗？还是说，新的囚禁才刚要开始？那段号称过了一个月的录音，其真相也快水落石出了。',
        "He'd used a knife against me once. If he opposed us, it was only fair to return the favor. Sai hadn't been wrong in suspecting Katei at the start, seeing through his myriad lies. However, he was insane if he thought he'd done a good job of hiding his own. The overconfidence he'd sheltered himself behind would prove useless if it was seen through.": '他对我动过一次刀。若他站在我们的对立面，那我们以牙还牙也理所当然。{w}Sai 一开始就怀疑 Katei，看穿了他形形色色的谎言，这一点并没错。可他要是以为自己的谎瞒得漂亮，那简直是疯了。他拿过度自信当掩护，而那份自信一旦被看穿，就毫无用处。',
        "...She'd better come back quickly.": '……{w}她最好快点回来。',
        "...Erina, it would be really bad if we searched for the Sekimeiya. It's... difficult to say it, but if we do that, you'll begin to hope your daughter will be saved. I know it's harsh to hear, but it won't end well. We won't find it.": '……{w}Erina，我们要是去找 Sekimeiya，那可就糟透了。{w}这话……很难说出口，可一旦去找，你就会开始指望你女儿能得救。我知道听着残忍，但不会有好结果的。我们找不到的。',
        '...What? You had to have traveled as well, right?': '……{w}什么？{w}你们肯定也穿越了吧？',
        "...That... doesn't make any sense, though. Are you telling the truth?": '……{w}可这……根本说不通。你们说的是真话？',
        "...But the real one hadn't come back after more than five minutes. In addition, the other one had claimed to be the very same person, indicating that her origin point could still have been coming...": '……{w}可真正的 Shiroya 过了五分多钟还没回来。{w}而且另一个她自称是同一个人，也就是说，她出发的时间点或许还没到……',
        "Maybe you're right. After all, she could just use this time to search on her own. And nobody else is around... There's no danger to fear. By which I mean, she didn't want to go to the bathroom. She had something else in mind. Are you telling me you don't know what it is?": '也许你说得对。毕竟，她完全可以趁这段时间自己去找。{w}而且周围没有别人……也没什么好担心的。{w}我是说，她根本不是要去洗手间。她另有打算。你是想告诉我，你不知道那是什么？',
        "What, then? Akaro came back out of nowhere and did something to her? Did she go to the past even though the Sekimeiya's probably gone? Why? And shouldn't she have come back if that had happened? I told you I was hoping for a calm end to all this. Were you two the ones who hid the Sekimeiya after all?": '那到底是怎么回事？Akaro 凭空冒出来，对她做了什么？还是说，Sekimeiya 明明很可能已经不在了，她却跑到了过去？为什么？真要是那样，她不是早该回来了吗？{w}我说过，我希望这一切能平平静静地收场。该不会，Sekimeiya 其实是你们两个藏起来的吧？',
        'From his point of view, Akaro has been missing for hours, ever since they escaped from the bedroom together. Is that it, though? ...Or am I being tricked?': '在他看来，两人一起逃出卧室之后，Akaro 已经失踪了好几个小时。{w}可真是这样吗？……还是说，我被人耍了？',
        "In the reality where Akaro appeared, Sai didn't seem surprised to see him. ...There were plenty of other things that had to be different, though.": '在 Akaro 出现的那段现实里，Sai 见到他时似乎并不惊讶。{w}……不过，肯定还有许多别的不同之处。',
        "Who could've guessed? ...That's fine. If she's still here, we'll find her.": '谁能想到呢？……算了。{w}如果她还在这栋楼里，我们会找到她的。',
        "...I don't know if you have something in mind, but you two will stay together, making sure nobody can sneak past. Not Shiroya, not Akaro, and not someone who's hiding.": '……{w}我不知道你心里在打什么主意，不过你们两个待在一起，别让任何人溜过去。不管是 Shiroya、Akaro，还是哪个躲起来的家伙。',
        "...Sure. But do understand that the Sekimeiya exists somewhere. Using it, it's possible to bypass any regular search by teleporting back to a recently inspected place. I doubt we have to worry about that, though.": '……行。{w}不过你要清楚，Sekimeiya 就在某个地方。用它传送回刚查过的地方，就能绕过任何常规搜查。但我想，这种事应该用不着担心。',
        "W-Wait. You said Shiroya wasn't in the women's bathroom, but you didn't mention this.": '等、等等。{w}你说 Shiroya 不在女洗手间里，可你没提这个。',
        "Not me. I honestly thought it must've left the building some time ago. I wonder why anyone would hide it. However, it seems Shiroya activated it and went to the past. Maybe she knew where it would be if she hid it herself. It doesn't make a lot of sense that she's not here, though.": '不是我。{w}说实话，我以为它早就被带出这栋楼了。真不明白谁会把它藏起来。{w}不过，看来是 Shiroya 启动了它，回到了过去。如果是她自己藏的，她或许知道它会出现在哪里。可她却不在，这就说不通了。',
        "...We still haven't searched the whole floor. I'll go leave the Sekimeiya in the event room, and we won't move it again.": '……{w}这一层还没搜完。我去把 Sekimeiya 放到活动室，之后谁都不再动它。',
        '...Just keep waiting here.': '……{w}你就在这儿等着吧。',
        "Hello. I just wanted to see what you were doing. I'll be outside this room to make sure you don't do anything with the Sekimeiya. Don't think Shiroya's actions aren't suspicious. I don't want her to come from the other hallway and grab it or something. Don't worry, either. I'll stay in the hallway, and I won't get it out myself.": '你好啊。我只是想看看你在做什么。我会守在门外，确保你不会对 Sekimeiya 动什么手脚。别以为 Shiroya 的举动就没有可疑之处。我可不想让她从另一条走廊过来，把它抢走之类的。{w}你也不用担心，我会待在走廊里，不会自己去把它拿出来。',
        "...I don't know...": '……{w}我不知道……',
        "It's 20:37.": '现在是 {time=20:37.}。',
        "It's 8:37 p.m.": '现在是 {time=20:37.}。',
        "What plan, Sai? Do you think we did this to find the Sekimeiya you didn't want us to find? You understand that doesn't make any sense, right? She found it in the bathroom. What's the point of forcing a search to find it if she already identified where it was?": '什么计划，Sai？你觉得我们做这些，是为了找出你不想让我们找到的 Sekimeiya？{w} 你自己也明白这说不通吧？她是在洗手间里发现它的。既然她已经确定了它在哪儿，那还强行搜查做什么？',
        '...Why is she faking, then?': '……{w}那她为什么要装？',
        "Yeah. You traveled through time. Do you think you might've changed anything?": '嗯。{w}你穿越过时间。你觉得有没有可能改变过什么？',
        "We might be able to change the past. If we travel together, we'll keep our memories of this reality. I'm not sure how it works yet, but I thought of something. Sai's definitely suspicious of us, so I doubt he'll let us just waltz on in and take the Sekimeiya. Obviously, given the time left, it's very unlikely we'll go back far enough even if the Sekimeiya stores energy the whole time.": '我们或许能改变过去。只要一起穿越，我们就会保留这个现实的记忆。具体原理我还没弄明白，不过我想到了一个办法。{w}Sai 肯定在怀疑我们，他不可能就这么让我们大摇大摆地进去拿走 Sekimeiya。再说以剩下的时间来看，就算 Sekimeiya 一直在蓄能，我们也不可能回到足够远的过去。',
        'How do we store thirty minutes without Sai noticing? I feel like this is feasible. Remember how the cabinet works? We could unplug the cord, which would stop the temperature regulation.': '怎么才能瞒过 Sai 蓄满三十分钟？我觉得这事可行。{w}还记得展示柜的原理吗？只要拔掉电源线，温度调节就会停下。',
        "...You don't want to try it...?": '……{w}你不想试试吗……？',
        "But... we'll regret it. If we don't even try it, the time will come when we'll hate not having tried it.": '可是……{w}我们会后悔的。要是连试都不试，总有一天会恨自己当初为什么没试。',
        "I know... I just thought about it more. Let's wait until the time is up. We can end everything now. We've been here for too long... I just want to get out. Believe me, there's no need to do anything else.": '我知道……我只是又多想了一会儿。{w} 等到时间结束吧。我们现在就可以把一切做个了结。{w} 我们在这里待得太久了……我只想离开。{w} 相信我，没有必要再做别的了。',
        "...To tell you the truth, I'm not even sure I'd want to do it even if we could.": '……{w}说实话，就算真能做到，我也说不准自己还想不想做。',
        "Most importantly, I just want to leave this place. We have to keep going with what we've got, and I'm sure it'll be fine. This isn't a world where Miiya survives, so let's keep living the best we can.": '最重要的是，我只想离开这里。我们只能靠手头这些继续走下去，我相信不会有事的。{w} 这不是 Miiya 能活下来的世界，我们就尽力活下去吧。',
        "I know it might sound shallow, but it'll be fine. If Isla is fated to be alive in the future, she will be no matter what you do. You'll see her again, right? That's what the recording predicted. Now, you just have to wait until that happens.": '我知道这话听起来可能很空泛，但会没事的。{w} 如果 Isla 注定在未来还活着，那不管你做什么，她都会活着。你还会再见到她，对吧？录音里就是这么预测的。现在，你只要等到那一天就好。',
        "At this point, why aren't we doing more than doubting him? There's been a culprit among us the whole time. Now, only four of us are left, and we didn't find Akaro. It can only be him, right? Of us, he's the only one missing. I think he disappeared on purpose. I need to find him.": '都到这一步了，我们为什么还只是怀疑他，不行动？犯人一直就在我们当中。如今只剩四个人，却找不到 Akaro。除了他还能是谁？{w}我们当中只有他不见了。我觉得他是故意消失的，我必须找到他。',
        "Shiroya and I looked at each other, hesitant to react. We'd agreed to wait until 21:05, so Erina's abrupt departure wasn't enough to disrupt that.": '我和 Shiroya 对视一眼，一时都没有动作。我们说好要等到 {time=21:05}，所以 Erina 忽然离开，也不足以让我们改变计划。',
        "Shiroya and I looked at each other, hesitant to react. We'd agreed to wait until 9:05 p.m., so Erina's abrupt departure wasn't enough to disrupt that.": '我和 Shiroya 对视一眼，一时都没有动作。我们说好要等到 {time=21:05}，所以 Erina 忽然离开，也不足以让我们改变计划。',
        '...Hm...': '……{w}嗯……',
        '...How much time is left? Less than twenty minutes, right?': '……{w}还剩多少时间？不到二十分钟了吧？',
        '...Oh, I see.': '……{w}{w=0.7}哦，原来如此。',
        '...Wh-What?': '……{w}怎、怎么了？',
        'N-No. Sorry to ask like this, but what time is it?': '没、没有。{w}抱歉突然这么问，现在几点了？',
        "...I'm sorry?": '……{w}抱歉，你说什么？',
        'It should be 20:50 soon.': '应该快到 {time=20:50} 了。',
        'It should be 8:50 p.m. soon.': '应该快到 {time=20:50} 了。',
        '...R-Really...? Okay.': '……{w}真、真的吗……？好。',
        'I closed the glass. Erina had been gone for about five minutes. If she had actually traveled, a version of her that was still to touch the Sekimeiya existed somewhere.': '我合上了玻璃罩。{w}Erina 离开了大约五分钟。如果她真的穿越了，那么某个地方一定还有一个尚未触碰 Sekimeiya 的她。',
        "Did that happen? It's 20:51. Let's go to the lobby.": '有这回事？现在 {time=20:51.}，去大厅吧。',
        "Did that happen? It's 8:51 p.m. Let's go to the lobby.": '有这回事？现在 {time=20:51.}，去大厅吧。',
        '...Huh? ...O-Oh.': '……哎？{w}……啊、哦。',
        '...Where is it?': '……{w}刀呢？',
        "The computer screens were suspended, so I pressed a key to light them up, trying not to step on all the blood. The time displayed was 20:55, which matched Sai's.": '电脑屏幕都黑着，我按了个键把它们点亮，同时尽量不踩到满地血迹。屏幕上显示的时间是 {time=20:55}，和 Sai 说的一致。',
        "The computer screens were suspended, so I pressed a key to light them up, trying not to step on all the blood. The time displayed was 8:55 p.m., which matched Sai's.": '电脑屏幕都黑着，我按了个键把它们点亮，同时尽量不踩到满地血迹。屏幕上显示的时间是 {time=20:55}，和 Sai 说的一致。',
        '...You did it. Happy now?': '……{w}你找到了。满意了？',
        "Not at all. Why would it be? Oh, you still think I hid the Sekimeiya myself. Now you can see you're wrong. Let's go to the lobby, as I've been saying.": '当然不会。能有什么问题？{w}哦，你还以为是我把 Sekimeiya 藏起来的吧。现在你该明白自己错了。就像我一直说的，去大厅吧。',
        '...All right.': '……{w}好吧。',
        '...Hm? ...Is anything wrong?': '……{w}嗯？……有什么事吗？',
        '...21:00. Only these last five minutes are left.': '……{time=21:00.}只剩最后五分钟了。',
        '...9:00 p.m. Only these last five minutes are left.': '……{time=21:00.}只剩最后五分钟了。',
        "...What? Where's Erina?": '……{w}什么？{w} Erina 呢？',
        "Don't forget what I said... I meant all of it. Now stay here, and don't follow me.": '别忘了我刚才说的话……每一句我都是认真的。{w}现在待在这里，别跟过来。',
        "The knife wasn't there... That's fine. That doesn't mean anything.": '刀不在里面……{w}没关系。那说明不了什么。',
        '...What time is it?': '……{w}现在几点了？',
        "It could be about to open. We don't know exactly the time the alarm went off. Maybe it was at 9:06.": '也许马上就会开了。警报究竟是在什么时候响的，我们并不清楚。说不定就是 {time=9:06.} 响的。',
        "It could be about to open. We don't know exactly the time the alarm went off. Maybe it was at 9:06 a.m.": '也许马上就会开了。警报究竟是在什么时候响的，我们并不清楚。说不定就是 {time=9:06.} 响的。',
        'Erina kept silent, but we could hear her breathing. Letting our hearts hammer our chests, we kept facing the sealed entrance, our promised freedom slipping away.': 'Erina 沉默不语，可我们能听见她的呼吸。{w} 我们的心脏在胸腔里狂跳，却只能继续面对紧闭的入口，眼看着说好的自由一点点溜走。',
        '21:08. What the fuck? Why is it still closed!?': '{time=21:08.} 他妈的怎么回事？怎么还关着！？',
        '9:08 p.m. What the fuck? Why is it still closed!?': '{time=21:08.} 他妈的怎么回事？怎么还关着！？',
        "It's 21:10! There's no way the time is wrong...! Why is this still going?": '都已经 {time=21:10} 了！时间不可能有错……！为什么还在继续？',
        "It's 9:10 p.m.! There's no way the time is wrong...! Why is this still going?": '都已经 {time=21:10} 了！时间不可能有错……！为什么还在继续？',
        '"Hey." After a long few seconds, Miiya put on a smile and made her way in.': '「嘿。」{w=0.5}沉默了好几秒，Miiya 才挂上笑容，迈步走进来。',
        'Make sure not to miss it, as we will show the rarest gemstone to have been found in recent years. Like every Thursday, the special visit will start at 9:00.': '届时将展出近年来发现的最稀有宝石，敬请不要错过。与每个星期四一样，特别参观将于 {time=9.} 开始。',
        'Make sure not to miss it, as we will show the rarest gemstone to have been found in recent years. Like every Thursday, the special visit will start at 9 a.m.': '届时将展出近年来发现的最稀有宝石，敬请不要错过。与每个星期四一样，特别参观将于 {time=9.} 开始。',
        "Atsuki's heater, once turned on, was comfortable, so they spent the entire time in his house until it felt appropriate to leave. Miiya's parents informed her they'd made dinner for her, and Shiroya took it as her cue as well. After saying their goodbyes, Atsuki saw both girls leaving on different paths.": 'Atsuki 家的暖气一开就很舒服，他们便一直待在他家里，直到该告辞的时候。{w} Miiya 的父母说给她做了晚饭，Shiroya 也顺势起身告辞。道别之后，Atsuki 目送两个女孩走向不同的方向。',
        "Me...? I doubt it, yeah. I stopped considering that when I was twelve. That's so much school just to get your foot in the door. It's not like I want to end up being some boring office worker or something, but I want to have time for myself too...": '我……？嗯，我看不会。我十二岁就不再考虑那条路了。{w}光是为了入行，就得读那么多年书。我也不是想最后变成什么无聊的上班族，可我也想要自己的时间啊……',
        "Eventually, their coats were no longer able to protect them from the icy air. The short winter day came to an end as the sky began to darken. Colliding with her own misty breath, Miiya stood up and asked whether they'd like to walk around to warm themselves up.": '终于，外套也挡不住刺骨的寒气。天色渐暗，短暂的冬日走到了尽头。{w}Miiya 站起身，呼出的白雾扑在脸上，问她们要不要走一走，暖暖身子。',
        'Shiroya took out her phone and looked at the time: 20:27. Aimlessly walking, they noticed the falling snow was getting lighter. People were entering their homes for the night, and some tire tracks had recently been carved into the snow.': 'Shiroya 掏出手机看了看时间：{time=20:27.} 他们漫无目的地走着，注意到雪渐渐小了。人们陆续归家歇息，雪地上还新轧出了几道车辙。',
        'Shiroya took out her phone and looked at the time: 8:27 p.m. Aimlessly walking, they noticed the falling snow was getting lighter. People were entering their homes for the night, and some tire tracks had recently been carved into the snow.': 'Shiroya 掏出手机看了看时间：{time=20:27.} 他们漫无目的地走着，注意到雪渐渐小了。人们陆续归家歇息，雪地上还新轧出了几道车辙。',
        "Oh! Hello, it's not usual I get a late visit. Are you searching for anything in particular?": '哦！{w=0.4}你们好，这么晚还有客人上门，倒是少见。几位想找点什么吗？',
        "Given the size of the explosion, that must've happened before the smoke had been released. Then, as everyone had fallen unconscious, nobody had been able to recognize the artificial smell of the gas and ventilate the area, causing it to build up. At {time=21}, when the lights had been turned on, the small spark had ignited that gas. The two people farthest from the center of the blast hadn't been critically harmed, but they'd been sent to the hospital. One girl had entered a coma after falling through the broken floor and hitting her head, and the last girl, who'd been the closest to the heater, had died instantly.": '从爆炸的规模来看，燃气泄漏应该发生在烟雾释放之前。之后所有人都昏迷过去，没人辨得出燃气里添加的那股气味，也没人能够通风，燃气便越积越多。{w} 到了 {time=21}，灯光亮起的一刻，一点微小的火花就引燃了燃气。{w} 离爆炸中心最远的两个人没有受到致命伤害，但都被送进了医院。一个女孩从破裂的地板坠落，撞到头部，陷入昏迷；最后一个女孩离取暖器最近，当场身亡。',
