        "...Oh. I'm glad to see you're back. I hope you enjoy the event.": '……哦。{w} 很高兴看到你回来。希望你玩得愉快。',
        "There was still more than an hour left until 9:00, when the front door would open. I'd stopped being curious about what we'd be shown as a result of the overbearing mixture of tiredness and coldness. I'd been paying attention to the brief conversations I could hear to stave off boredom, and they all kept detailing how strange the whole event was.": '距离正门在 {time=9} 打开还有一个多小时。疲惫和寒冷交织在一起，压得人没了脾气，我已经不再好奇他们究竟要给我们看些什么了。为了打发时间，我一直留意着周围零星的谈话，而那些话无一不在说这场活动有多奇怪。',
        "There was still more than an hour left until 9 a.m., when the front door would open. I'd stopped being curious about what we'd be shown as a result of the overbearing mixture of tiredness and coldness. I'd been paying attention to the brief conversations I could hear to stave off boredom, and they all kept detailing how strange the whole event was.": '距离正门在 {time=9} 打开还有一个多小时。疲惫和寒冷交织在一起，压得人没了脾气，我已经不再好奇他们究竟要给我们看些什么了。为了打发时间，我一直留意着周围零星的谈话，而那些话无一不在说这场活动有多奇怪。',
        "It must've already been 9:00, because we were told we could advance through the left door if we weren't part of the event. Nobody did, though—everyone present was gathered behind us.": '应该已经 {time=9} 了，因为有人告诉我们，不参加活动的人可以从左边那扇门进去。可没人动身——在场的人都聚在我们身后。',
        "It must've already been 9 a.m., because we were told we could advance through the left door if we weren't part of the event. Nobody did, though—everyone present was gathered behind us.": '应该已经 {time=9} 了，因为有人告诉我们，不参加活动的人可以从左边那扇门进去。可没人动身——在场的人都聚在我们身后。',
        "Uh, y— *cough* *cough* *cough* Wh-What happened? We're still here?": '呃，对——*咳*{w} *咳* *咳*{w} 怎、怎么了？我们还在这儿？',
        'Hh— ...What the fuck is this...?': '呃——{w}……这他妈是什么情况……？',
        "You're right. That's the Sekimeiya. In case Naomi didn't warn you, the Sekimeiya must never be taken out of its cabinet. The temperature provided to it is essential to maintain it well. Did you keep it shut inside?": '你说得对，那就是 Sekimeiya。{w} 万一 Naomi 没提醒过你们——Sekimeiya 绝对不能从展示柜里拿出来。保存它需要恒定的温度。你们一直把它关在柜子里吧？',
        "What...? Why can't we leave?": '什么……？{w} 为什么我们不能离开？',
        "We were rightfully frustrated, as it seemed all of us had gotten innocently trapped, and we weren't even sure why. Thankfully, though, everyone was keeping calm. I was quite tired, which might have watered down my reaction to everything. It was hard to believe what I was experiencing was real, but I would most likely fall asleep somewhere well before the deadline.": '我们自然很烦躁——所有人似乎都无辜被困，连原因都不清楚。所幸大家还都保持冷静。{w} 我相当累，或许也因此对这一切反应迟钝。我很难相信眼前经历的一切是真的；不过离截止时间还早，我很可能在那之前就睡着了。',
        "We repeated the same process and concluded there was nothing to be found on it. Katei didn't have the login information for the computers, so our single way to measure the time was Sai's wristwatch. According to that, the time was 9:50.": '我们照同样的流程查了一遍，断定这层也一无所获。Katei 不知道电脑的登录信息，唯一能看时间的就只有 Sai 的手表。据表上显示，此刻是{time=9:50.}',
        "We repeated the same process and concluded there was nothing to be found on it. Katei didn't have the login information for the computers, so our single way to measure the time was Sai's wristwatch. According to that, the time was 9:50 a.m.": '我们照同样的流程查了一遍，断定这层也一无所获。Katei 不知道电脑的登录信息，唯一能看时间的就只有 Sai 的手表。据表上显示，此刻是{time=9:50.}',
        "And if this really opens the security room, it could confirm that. Wasn't Katei in front of us all this time, checking the floor as if he was looking for something?": '「如果这真能打开监控室，就能证实这一点。{w}这一路 Katei 不都走在最前面，像是在找什么东西似的四处查看吗？」',
        "Huh? It enters all the way, but it's not unlocking it.": '咦？{w} 能整个插进去，锁却打不开。',
        "You're right... What the hell? It wasn't even locked. This was the right key, though...": '你说得对……搞什么？门压根没锁。{w} 可这把钥匙明明是对的……',
        'From the hallway, we saw many lit screens in front of us illuminating a dim space. It seemed like a bit of smoke had leaked through the gaps of the door. Slowly, we made our way in, wondering whether Katei had purposely lied or simply been incorrect.': '从走廊里望去，前方许多亮着的屏幕照亮了一间昏暗的屋子。似乎有些烟雾从门缝里渗了出来。{w} 我们慢慢走进去，心里琢磨 Katei 究竟是在故意撒谎，还是单纯说错了。',
        'We got closer to them. There was a single chair in front of the middle screen that Atsuki gripped the back of. He was going to sit on it, but he stopped short.': '我们走近了些。中间屏幕前只有一把椅子，Atsuki 握住了椅背。{w} 他正要坐下，却停住了。',
        "Did someone clean it off? I doubt anyone paid attention to this camera when we were here before, so we can't know how long it's been like this.": '有人擦过吗？{w} 之前我们在这儿的时候，恐怕没人注意过这台摄像头，所以也无从知道它这样多久了。',
        "...I-I'm confused. Why did you not wait for us? Did you actually open the security room?": '……我、我有点糊涂了。{w}你们怎么不等我们？监控室的门真的打开了？',
        "Oh, here you are! Where the hell did you go? And where's Katei?": '哦，你们在这儿！你们到底跑哪儿去了？{w}Katei 呢？',
        "I suddenly saw you were all gone and didn't know if you'd walked down or toward the offices, but I figured I hadn't noticed you'd gone down the stairs. ...I didn't find anyone when I went all the way down. I was gonna search through the first floor until I heard a sound coming from the stairs that I followed up here.": '我一转眼就发现你们全不见了，也拿不准你们是下楼了还是去了办公室那边。我猜是自己没注意到你们下了楼。{w}……我一路走到下面，谁也没找到。本来打算把一楼搜一遍，后来听见楼梯那边有动静，就顺着声音上来了。',
        "...Excuse me? That's not how it was programmed to work. Regardless, is that why you suddenly left? To see if you could open the security room?": '……{w}你说什么？{w}程序可不是这么设定的。{w}话说回来，你们突然离开，就是为了试试能不能打开监控室？',
        "What? What is wrong with what I've said? And that must've been a malfunction in the alarm. I had no way to confirm the lock was set when I left since the inner knob undoes it by itself, and I didn't check behind me to see if it locked automatically. It should have, but it appears it didn't.": '什么？{w}我说的话有什么问题？{w}那一定是警报出了故障。因为内侧的旋钮会自动开锁，我离开时没法确认门锁上了没有；我也没有回头确认它是否自动锁上了。本该锁上的，看来并没有。',
        "I see. You don't get it. You're claiming these are yours, am I right? You didn't just come across Naomi whatsoever.": '我明白了，你还没搞懂。{w}你是说这串钥匙本来就是你的，对吧？你根本没碰见过 Naomi。',
        'I picked the key that seemed to fit and inserted it into the keyhole. After a turn, the door was unlocked. Sai wasted no time in opening it and looking within.': '我挑了那把看起来对得上的钥匙，插进锁孔。一转，锁便开了。{w}Sai 毫不迟疑地推门张望。',
        "You don't say. If the Sekimeiya's there, someone had to have just brought it up. Oh, that could be really bad...! It needs to be put in its cabinet immediately! Please, step aside.": '那还用说。Sekimeiya 要是在那儿，肯定是有人刚把它搬上来的。{w}哎呀，那可就糟了……！得马上把它放回展示柜！请让一让。',
        '...Do you think these footprints make any sense?': '……{w}你们觉得这些脚印说得通吗？',
        'He looked at the two of us. I stared at the floor, trying to understand what he was getting at. A few seconds later, neither of us had responded.': '他看向我们两人。{w}我低头盯着地板，想弄清他究竟在指什么。几秒过去，我们谁也没有答话。',
        "Neither of us, probably. To get the Sekimeiya here, I would've had to go to the crystal floor, up to the attic, and then back down. All without taking the elevator, and you all remember I appeared from below where you were. There's no way I would've had enough time. Are you forgetting Naomi? She's the only person who could have left these footprints unless she gave her key to someone else. I can't believe she'd leave the Sekimeiya here. She knew full well about the cold it needs.": '我们俩多半都进不来。要把 Sekimeiya 搬到这儿，我得先去水晶层，再上到阁楼，然后再下来。全程还不能坐电梯——你们都记得吧，我是从你们下面那一层上来的。我根本不可能有那么多时间。{w}你们把 Naomi 忘了？除非她把钥匙交给了别人，否则这些脚印只可能是她留下的。我不信她会把 Sekimeiya 丢在这里。它需要低温，她比谁都清楚。',
        "...It's still visible: under the more recent footprints, there are other ones, much harder to notice and smaller in size. Like the rest, they go from the entrance to the sofa, where the Sekimeiya is.": '……{w}还看得出来：较新的脚印下面还压着别的脚印，更淡，也更小。和其余的脚印一样，它们从入口一直走到放着 Sekimeiya 的沙发。',
        "I would assume they're from when the Sekimeiya was left on the sofa, but that can't be it. It should have still been on the crystal floor then. What bugs me is they don't seem to continue. Once they get to the sofa, they don't go anywhere else. I don't believe they go back to the door either, but I might be missing the returning ones. Now that Katei walked over them, it's even harder to tell. It's still somewhat possible to distinguish the size and direction they're facing. Without a doubt, they don't belong to the same person who left the other ones. That's Katei, if you were wondering.": '我本来以为，这些脚印是 Sekimeiya 被放到沙发上时留下的，可这说不通。那时候它应该还在水晶展室。{w}让我在意的是，这串脚印似乎没有延续下去。到了沙发之后，它们就没再往别处去。我觉得它们也没有回到门口，不过折返的那几枚也许被我漏掉了。何况 Katei 刚踩过一遍，现在更难分辨。{w}不过勉强还能看出大小和朝向。毫无疑问，它们和留下另外那些脚印的人不是同一个——顺带一提，那些是 Katei 的。',
        "...By the way, what's this smell?": '……{w}话说回来，这是什么味道？',
        "Hm... I feel like I've smelled it before, but I don't know where.": '嗯……{w}总觉得在哪儿闻过，可就是想不起来。',
        "You're right. It's bizarre, but only because of the footprints I pointed out. You have Naomi's keyring, so you must know where she is. In addition, it seems like your own footprints did the same as hers at least one of the times they went from the entrance to the sofa.": '你说得对。事情确实蹊跷，但蹊跷之处只在于我指出的那些脚印。{w}Naomi 的钥匙串在你手上，你不可能不知道她在哪儿。而且你自己的脚印也和她的一样，至少有一次从玄关走到沙发后就断了。',
        "This doesn't make any sense. Unless I misinterpreted it, the person who left the footprints should still be here. Maybe even two people. Was it a trick in case we noticed them? What if the first person stayed on the sofa, and when Katei came, they exited through the main door, stepping over his footprints and taking advantage of the bigger shoe size?": '这根本说不通。除非我看错了，否则留下脚印的人现在应该还在这里。也许还不止一个人。{w}难道那是为了防我们注意到脚印而设的障眼法？假设第一个人在沙发上没动，等 Katei 进来，他才从大门出去，利用 Katei 鞋码更大这一点，踩着他的脚印走。',
        '...Of course. They just left with the elevator. It has to be that. Katei!': '……原来如此。他们就是坐电梯走的。只能是这么回事。{w}Katei！',
        'I will choose to stop playing along with you. However, if the elevator is really working, I can only think of one explanation that makes sense. ...That it was just enabled, minutes or seconds ago, while we were all here.': '我决定不再配合你了。不过，如果电梯真的能用，我只能想到一个说得通的解释。{w}……它是几分钟、甚至几秒前才刚被启用的，就在我们所有人都在场的时候。',
        "...You're so stupid.": '……{w}你真是蠢得可以。',
        "You're on a wrong streak. We already determined earlier that the alarm underwent an error and didn't lock the security room after I left, did we not? Why would I assume that it worked after they closed it? I figured the error probably repeated, and the door wouldn't have locked itself even if they closed it.": '你真是错得离谱。我们之前不是已经确认过，警报出了故障，我离开后监控室并没有上锁吗？{w}我凭什么以为他们关上门之后它就会正常上锁？我觉得故障多半会再犯，就算他们关了门，门也不会自己锁上。',
        'Wh— Was it like this when you came?': '什——{w} 你们来的时候就是这样？',
        "...If it's true that the alarm should've locked it after leaving, sure. But even if it did malfunction, the only reason why we didn't enter before was because you'd left your key inside, right? Normally, she would've expected you to bring it out and be able to open the door whenever. It doesn't make sense to say she cared about us using the computer because we should've been able to get in here right away, while it was still working.": '……如果警报本该在我们离开后把门锁上，那倒说得通。{w}可就算它真出了故障，我们之前没进来，唯一的原因也是你把钥匙落在了里面，对吧？{w}正常情况下，她会以为你把钥匙带出来了，随时都能开门。既然我们本来随时都能进来，而且那时候电脑还能用，那说她会在意我们使用电脑，就说不通了。',
        "Sure. We still haven't looked through this entire floor. If we can't find Naomi here, we'll have to search the entire building in more depth. Oh, there's something else I meant to ask you. Inside the elevator, there's a stop button that's supposed to enable communication with the outside. Would that help us?": '好。这一层我们还没搜完。要是在这儿找不到 Naomi，就只能把整栋楼再仔细搜一遍了。{w}对了，我还想问你一件事。电梯里有个停止按钮，按说能让里面的人与外界联络。那个能帮上忙吗？',
        "No, it won't. The alarm's effects may not have worked perfectly, but one of them was to disable that connection. If you press the button, you'll get locked inside until 21:00, so I'd advise you not to do it.": '不，没用。警报的效果也许并不完美，但其中之一就是切断那种联络。你一旦按下按钮，就会被关在里面直到 {time=21}，所以我劝你别按。',
        "No, it won't. The alarm's effects may not have worked perfectly, but one of them was to disable that connection. If you press the button, you'll get locked inside until 9 p.m., so I'd advise you not to do it.": '不，没用。警报的效果也许并不完美，但其中之一就是切断那种联络。你一旦按下按钮，就会被关在里面直到 {time=21}，所以我劝你别按。',
        "And there should be no problem with that. You said Naomi was gonna let you do it, but Katei made sure nobody would touch it. You all understand he's been lying, don't you? And the Sekimeiya was brought to the attic, either by him or Naomi—the two people who should've known a higher temperature could be damaging.": '那就更没问题了。你说过 Naomi 本来要让你摸的，可 Katei 却非要确保没人碰得到它。{w} 你们都清楚他一直在撒谎了吧？而且，Sekimeiya 是被搬进阁楼的——不是他，就是 Naomi；而这两个人本来最该知道温度太高会弄坏它。',
        'I just... traveled to the past.': '我刚刚……{w}回到了过去。',
        "Nobody could accuse Katei of a trick, as we'd all seen him disappear. He was breathing heavily, and he started to move his arms, checking that his body worked as usual.": '没人能说 Katei 是在耍把戏，他消失的样子我们都亲眼看见了。{w}他呼吸粗重，抬了抬手臂，像是在确认身体还和往常一样听使唤。',
        "I know how it sounds, but that's what it felt like. No... what the hell just happened? It did feel like I went back a few seconds, to when I was walking from the security room to the event room.": '我知道这话听着荒唐，可当时的感觉就是这样。不……刚才到底是怎么回事？{w}我确实觉得自己回到了几秒之前，回到我从监控室走向活动室的那一刻。',
        'Wh-What the hell? It turned white again.': '这、这是怎么回事？{w}它又变白了。',
        "What the fuck...? He did it again! Does he think we're idiots? He walked away from a stone that made him teleport and didn't demand the keys!": '搞什么……？他又来这一套！{w}他当我们是傻子吗？被一块石头传送走了，居然扭头就走，连钥匙都不要回去！',
        "...I felt slight traces of tension for a second. Was it really possible he was about to travel through time? I didn't think I could really take that seriously, but seeing him about to try made me uncomfortable. It was almost laughable how all of us looked on in anticipation, trying to confirm whether we'd lost our minds or not. His hand got closer and closer to the gem until no distance separated it from him.": '……有一瞬间，我隐隐感到一阵紧张。他真的就要穿越时间了吗？我原以为自己不会当真，可亲眼见他准备尝试，心里还是不安起来。我们所有人都满怀期待地望着，想确认自己究竟是不是疯了——那副样子几乎有些可笑。{w}他的手一点点靠近宝石，直到中间再没有一丝距离。',
        "Um... Y-Yes. I suppose so. I can't... I can't believe it, though.": '嗯……是、是的。应该是吧。{w}可我……我还是不敢相信。',
        "Hm... I don't think I traveled a few seconds through time, but actually minutes. About twenty, I'd say.": '嗯……{w}我想我穿越的不只是几秒，而是好几分钟。大概二十分钟吧。',
        "It's not doing anything, and it's cold. ...It must do nothing when it's this color. It's just a thought, but maybe I traveled farther because it spent more time out of the cabinet. When Katei touched it, it had barely been out for any time at all.": '它毫无反应，还是凉的。……变成这种颜色时，它应该就什么也做不了。{w}只是我的猜测——也许是因为它在展示柜外放的时间更长，我才穿越得更远。Katei 碰它的时候，它才刚从柜子里拿出来没多久。',
        "...Oh, I haven't been able to fix anything. I apologize. I am completely lost; I don't even know what the issue is. Everything is properly arranged and connected, so unless no electricity is reaching the outlets, I'm out of ideas.": '……唉，我什么也没修好，实在抱歉。{w}我完全摸不着头绪，连问题出在哪都不知道。所有线路都排布妥当、连接完好，除非是插座根本没通电，否则我也没辙了。',
        '...Is there anything... Oh, the elevator?': '……有什么……{w}咦，电梯？',
        'Me neither. ...Wait, I just remembered the hallway B camera. The one that had its lens completely clean.': '我也没注意。{w}……等等，我想起 B走廊那台监控了，就是镜头干干净净的那台。',
        "...After looking at each other, we let him know we'd recently lost track of Sai. Before Katei could get too alarmed, Akaro cut in.": '……{w}我们面面相觑，告诉他我们不久前就跟丢了 Sai。还不等 Katei 过于惊慌，Akaro 就插了话。',
        '...The duct tape, remember? Sai took out my keyring, and it had a piece of duct tape attached to it. That piece had smoke residue on it.': '……{w}胶带，记得吗？Sai 拿出我的钥匙串时，上面粘着一截胶带。那截胶带上留着烟熏的痕迹。',
        "...When I walked down to the crystal floor, searching for you, I found it hidden behind a handrail and put it in my pocket to inquire about it. That's when it got stuck to the keyring.": '……{w}我下到水晶层找你们的时候，发现它被藏在扶手后面，就收进了口袋，打算之后再问清楚；也就是在那时，它粘到了钥匙串上。',
        "What the hell is Naomi doing...? We can't even use the computer to figure anything out. Do you all think Sai ran away on his own? Now we need to find both of them.": 'Naomi 到底在搞什么……？连电脑都用不了，什么都查不出来。{w}你们真觉得 Sai 是自己跑掉的？现在两个人全得找。',
        "...Huh? Sorry, I don't know. I just can't believe it. I really traveled through time.": '……啊？{w}抱歉，我也不知道。我只是……实在无法相信。我真的经历了时间穿越。',
        "Well, I can't believe it either. ...Are you sure you don't want to do it again?": '其实我也无法相信。{w}……你确定不想再来一次？',
        'Am I wrong? He traveled to the past with the Sekimeiya—that much I know. Then, he simply reunited with you guys. Am I missing something?': '我说错了吗？他用 Sekimeiya 穿越回了过去——这点我知道。{w}然后，他就这么和你们会合了。我是不是漏掉了什么？',
        "If I'm not missing anything, I don't know. However, he is hiding something, and apparently even from you. I'm sure he'll want to use the Sekimeiya again, so if he doesn't tell you that, assume that he's lying and try to stop him.": '如果我没漏掉什么，那我也不知道。不过，他确实藏着事，而且显然连你也瞒着。{w}我敢肯定他还想再用 Sekimeiya，所以如果他没把那件事告诉你们，就认定他在撒谎，想办法拦住他。',
        "I'm not sure it'd work anyway. If the exit closed as the alarm went off and she's hiding somewhere, she must be confident she won't be found. And if she's working with Katei, he's definitely confident we won't find her. We've already been everywhere in this building, so I don't think it's essential that we keep looking for her. If she can be found, it'll happen eventually.": '反正我也不确定那样做有没有用。警报响起时出口已经关了，她既然正躲在某处，就一定有把握不会被人找到。要是她和 Katei 是一伙的，那 Katei 肯定也确信我们找不到她。{w}这栋楼里我们都已经找遍了，所以我觉得没必要继续找她。如果她真的能被找到，迟早也会找到。',
        "That makes sense. ...And it's still here.": '说得通。{w}……而且它还停在这儿。',
        'No, did he...? Or did I just poke it when I stood up?': '不对，难道他……？{w}还是我起身时不小心碰到的？',
        "Atsuki and I should've been alone in the attic, which had both of its entrances locked. I suddenly wasn't sensing my tiredness anymore. I grabbed my purse and approached the hatch.": '阁楼的两个入口都锁着，这里本该只有我和 Atsuki。{w}我忽然感觉不到倦意了。我抓起手提包，走向阁楼口。',
        "Uh, yes... I only slept for a few minutes and couldn't do it again.": '呃，{w=0.4}嗯……{w=0.5}我只睡了几分钟，后来就睡不着了。',
        "*yawn* Yeah, and I don't think it'll happen. Are you still tired?": '*哈欠*{w}对啊，不过我看是睡不着了。你还困吗？',
        '...Yeah, sure.': '……{w}嗯，走吧。',
        'Nobody crossed this carpet. I can hardly see the footprints anymore. ...You have the key with you, right?': '没人踩过这块地毯，脚印都快看不清了。{w}……钥匙你带着吧？',
        "Atsuki was resembling Katei more and more to me, and I didn't know if I could trust him. Behind him was the red stop button, which Katei claimed would confine us inside until the alarm's effects automatically reverted.": 'Atsuki 越来越像 Katei，我不知该不该信他。{w}他身后是红色的停止按钮，据 Katei 说，一旦按下，我们就会被关在里面，直到警报效果自动解除。',
        'In the top right corner, "13:16" was displayed in black digits.': '右上角用黑色数字显示着「{time=13:16}」。',
        'In the top right corner, "1:16 p.m." was displayed in black digits.': '右上角用黑色数字显示着「{time=13:16}」。',
        'Oh, 13:00 already. I guess I did sleep for over two hours.': '「哦，都 {time=13} 了啊。看来我真的睡了两个多小时。」',
        'Oh, 1 p.m. already. I guess I did sleep for over two hours.': '「哦，都 {time=13} 了啊。看来我真的睡了两个多小时。」',
        "Atsuki, after appearing in the kitchen, would not have been able to leave the attic. He couldn't have left through the staircase before us, because there were no footprints that started from the kitchen.": 'Atsuki 出现在厨房之后，不可能离开阁楼。{w}他也无法赶在我们之前从楼梯离开，因为没有任何脚印是从厨房那边开始的。',
        "I don't know; I wasn't able to change anything the last time. I have no idea how this will work. I'll disappear from this room and appear somewhere else. If I try to change what I experienced, I don't know how the universe will react. Perhaps you won't notice any difference and I'll branch the world. Maybe this reality will instantly morph into the one I'm making.": '我不知道；上一次我什么也没能改变。这次会怎样，我完全没把握。{w}我会从这个房间消失，出现在别处。如果我试图改变自己经历过的事，我不知道宇宙会如何反应。也许你察觉不到任何异样，而我会让世界分岔；也许这个现实会瞬间变成我正在塑造的那一个。',
        "...It teleported you as well? How come that didn't happen the other times? And both of us appeared here...": '……{w}它把你也传送了？为什么之前几次没发生这种事？{w}而且我们两个都出现在这里……',
        '...Excuse me? Was Katei not with you?': '……等等？{w}Katei 没和你们在一起吗？',
        '...What the fuck, then!?': '……{w}那他妈的到底是怎么回事！？',
        "No idea, but I saw him not too long ago. He's been here the whole time. Do you still have the key to the attic?": '不知道，不过刚才我还见过他。他一直都在这儿。{w}阁楼的钥匙还在你们手上吗？',
        '...Oh, right, what time is it?': '……{w}对了，现在几点了？',
        "...Hm, it's {time=13:19.}": '……嗯，{w}现在是 {time=13:19.}。',
        "...Hm,{w} it's 13:19.": '……嗯，{w}现在是 {time=13:19.}。',
        "...Hm, it's 13:19.": '……嗯，{w}现在是 {time=13:19.}。',
        "...Hm,{w} it's 1:19 p.m.": '……嗯，{w}现在是 {time=13:19.}。',
        "...Hm, it's 1:19 p.m.": '……嗯，{w}现在是 {time=13:19.}。',
        "Everyone present was surprised at the same time. While Akaro hadn't expected to see me and Atsuki, we hadn't expected to see who he was with either.": '在场的人同时愣住了。{w}Akaro 没想到会见到我和 Atsuki，而我们也同样没想到他身边站着的是谁。',
        "...I've been here. *sigh*": '……我一直在这儿。{w}（叹气）',
        "You're a fucking liar! You haven't been here for hours! Where the fuck were you, and why are you back? The computer doesn't work, and I'm the only one with a watch. How did you accurately say that you've been gone for three hours!? Hey, did Naomi have a watch? Does anyone remember?": '你他妈在撒谎！你已经好几个小时不在这儿了！你到底去了哪儿，又为什么回来？电脑用不了，有手表的只有我一个。你怎么可能准确说出自己已经离开三个小时了！？{w}喂，Naomi 有手表吗？有人记得吗？',
        'Who... is this?': '这……{w}这是谁？',
        "We dashed to the door. ...When we looked through it, we immediately realized that wasn't the only question to ask.": '我们冲到门口。{w}……往门里一看，便立刻明白，该问的远不止这一句。',
        "There was no meaning to be found. No smell of blood, no identity of the corpse, but a death that defied reason. Furthermore, the past had changed. Not because of the appearance of a body, but because of Erina's yell, which had spread throughout the crystal floor—a yell we hadn't heard while we'd been downstairs. I immediately understood that someone had been killed. I'd gone over the concept of death many times in my mind, so I simply stared at that dreamlike scene before I was pushed aside.": '这一切毫无道理可言。没有血腥味，也辨不清死者的身份，只有一桩违背常理的死亡。而且，过去已经变了。改变的原因不是这具尸体的出现，而是 Erina 的那声喊叫——它传遍了水晶层，而我们在楼下时，谁也没有听见。{w}我立刻明白，有人被杀了。死亡这件事，我早就在心里翻来覆去想过很多次，所以只是怔怔地望着那如梦似幻的一幕，直到被人推开。',
        "I don't know. You remember the Sekimeiya, right? As you said, it's not in the cabinet right now, and you're an excellent candidate to have taken it out. It's possible this man entered the tower after it was locked down, and if you did so too, your disappearance, your knowledge of the time, and this knife you're talking about... would all make sense.": '我不知道。你还记得 Sekimeiya 吧？就像你说的，它现在不在展示柜里，而最可能把它拿走的人就是你。{w}这个人可能是封锁之后才进塔的；如果你也一样，那你失踪的那段时间、你对时间的了解，还有你说的那把刀……就全都说得通了。',
        "Yes, look at this! This is why I thought it must've been a knife. It was his own! He still has his baton, but his knife is gone. I personally saw that he had a knife right here a few days ago.": '对，你们看这里！我就是因为这个才认定凶器是刀。那是他自己的刀！{w}警棍还在，刀却不见了。几天前我亲眼看见，他的刀就挂在这个位置。',
        "So the killer did this to prevent us from talking to people outside once again. I have to assume that you still have not found Naomi, so instead of blaming me, consider that it's very possible this person has been here since we got trapped, and we didn't find him just like we couldn't find Naomi.": '所以凶手这么做，是为了再一次切断我们和外面的联系。{w}我只能认为你们还是没找到 Naomi——与其在这里怪我，不如想想：这个人很可能从我们被困起就一直待在塔里，我们找不到他，就像找不到 Naomi 一样。',
        "...Don't say stuff like that. I didn't do this.": '……{w}别乱说话。人不是我杀的。',
        '...Stop. Akaro, is what you said earlier true? That you found Katei ten minutes before coming to the event room?': '……等等。{w}Akaro，你刚才说的是真的吗？你说你是在来活动室前十分钟找到 Katei 的？',
        '...Is that so? You two were talking in hallway A. Did you look at the lobby? I recall the door was shut.': '……{w}是吗？你们俩当时在 A走廊说话。你们看过大厅吗？我记得那扇门是关着的。',
        "At 13:17, we'd walked down to the mechanical room, which meant that the man had died while we'd been under him.": '{time=13:17}，我们已经下到机械室，也就是说，那个男人死的时候，我们就在他脚下。',
        "At 1:17 p.m., we'd walked down to the mechanical room, which meant that the man had died while we'd been under him.": '{time=13:17}，我们已经下到机械室，也就是说，那个男人死的时候，我们就在他脚下。',
        "...If you're not lying, then forget what I said. Everyone has an alibi, unless two or more people did it. You two were together, Katei and Akaro were together, and me, Erina, and Isla were together.": '……如果你们没说谎，那就当我没说过。所有人都有不在场证明——除非凶手是两个人以上。{w}你们俩在一起，Katei 和 Akaro 在一起，而我、Erina 和 Isla 在一起。',
        "I'm not sure how they took his knife or how we didn't hear a fight. In fact, I have no clue what happened. None of us have blood on our clothes, which I suppose doesn't mean anything since it doesn't seem like much blood sprayed out, but I'll remind you all again that the Sekimeiya was hidden a while ago. All of us go back to having no alibi when everyone is able to go to the past.": '我不知道对方是怎么夺走他的刀的，也不知道我们为什么没听到打斗声。说实话，我完全不明白发生了什么。{w}我们身上都没有血迹——不过这大概说明不了什么，毕竟看起来并没有溅出多少血。但我要再提醒各位一次：Sekimeiya 早就被藏起来了。只要所有人都能回到过去，我们每个人的不在场证明就都不成立了。',
        'That\'s right, which forces me to point out the topic you were discussing in hallway A. "I touched the Sekimeiya a second ago." Didn\'t those words come out of your mouth?': '没错，所以我不得不提一提你们在 A走廊聊的那件事。{w}「我刚才碰了一下 Sekimeiya。」——这话不是从你嘴里说出来的吗？',
        'And you were about to say "no, both of them traveled". However, given the knowledge of the Sekimeiya you should have, that shouldn\'t be possible. After touching it, the Sekimeiya would power off, and it would take a while before anyone could activate it again. Does that mean that you knew that was possible? You haven\'t explained much about what you did during the time we were in the attic.': '而你刚才差点说出「不，他们两个都穿越了」。可按你对 Sekimeiya 本该有的了解，这应该不可能才对。碰过之后，Sekimeiya 就会关闭，要过一段时间才能再次启动。{w}难道说，你早就知道那种情况可能发生？我们在阁楼那段时间里你做了什么，你可没怎么解释过。',
        "This? Sure. Do you think I have it...? I'm being serious. I didn't find it, but it's possible I missed it. Go look.": '这个？行啊。你觉得东西在我身上……？{w}我说真的。我没找到，但也许是我漏看了。自己去看吧。',
        "Someone... killed him... and it's not easy for any of us to have done it. Finally, the Sekimeiya isn't where it should be. Added to the fact that Naomi hasn't been found, you can't possibly think we did this, right?": '有人……杀了他……而我们谁都不容易做到。还有，Sekimeiya 也不在该在的地方。{w}再加上 Naomi 至今不见踪影，你总不可能觉得这是我们干的吧？',
        "There's n-no way. I think Naomi's the first person to suspect. Not only has she managed to remain hidden, but she also might have the same keys that we have. There are no cameras here, but we don't know if they're recording in the first place... You said you didn't inspect the whole building because you thought we were in the attic, right? We have to be missing something that the culprit is aware of. Could there be a place we're ignoring?": '绝、绝对不可能。我觉得头号嫌疑人就是 Naomi。她不但一直藏得好好的，手里可能还有和我们一样的钥匙。{w}这里没有摄像头，可我们连它们有没有在录像都不知道……你说过，你以为我们在阁楼，所以没把整栋楼查遍，对吧？我们一定漏掉了什么，而凶手知道那是什么。会不会有个地方一直被我们忽略了？',
        "If it's neither of those, there's still an answer with the Sekimeiya. This policeman could've come from the future if he touched the Sekimeiya after 21:00, and Naomi could've left the tower by going far to the past. We found the Sekimeiya in the attic and don't know where it is now.": '如果这两者都不是，那还有 Sekimeiya 这个可能。这个警察若是在 {time=21} 之后碰过 Sekimeiya，就可能是从未来来的；Naomi 也可能穿越到遥远的过去，就此离开了这座塔。我们在阁楼找到了 Sekimeiya，如今却不知道它在哪儿。',
        "If it's neither of those, there's still an answer with the Sekimeiya. This policeman could've come from the future if he touched the Sekimeiya after 9 p.m., and Naomi could've left the tower by going far to the past. We found the Sekimeiya in the attic and don't know where it is now.": '如果这两者都不是，那还有 Sekimeiya 这个可能。这个警察若是在 {time=21} 之后碰过 Sekimeiya，就可能是从未来来的；Naomi 也可能穿越到遥远的过去，就此离开了这座塔。我们在阁楼找到了 Sekimeiya，如今却不知道它在哪儿。',
        'He disappeared from our sight. Soon, we began to hear the same sound of doors opening coming from hallway B.': '他从我们视野里消失了。{w}很快，B走廊那边又传来了同样的开门声。',
        "I kept doing so for many seconds, gripping the door's handle with my right hand. One of the many thoughts that crossed my mind was if I should move.": '我就这样看了好几秒，右手始终握着门把手。{w} 脑中掠过许多念头，其中之一是：我该不该动。',
        '...Huh? Yes.': '……咦？{w} 嗯。',
        "I didn't voice any complaints. I just gave him a tiny nod. Outside, I kept glancing left and right until Atsuki was done.": '我没有出声反对，只是轻轻朝他点了点头。{w} 到了外面，我一直左顾右盼，直到 Atsuki 查看完毕。',
        '...You have the key, right?': '……{w}钥匙在你身上吧？',
        "...I don't get it. Was Naomi never with us? How is this possible? I know we've already been here for a long time, but that doesn't make it any less confusing. Where the hell is the Sekimeiya, also?": '……{w}我搞不懂了。Naomi 难道从来就没跟我们在一起过？{w}这怎么可能？我知道我们在这儿已经待了很久，可我还是想不通。还有，Sekimeiya 到底在哪儿？',
        "Let's just go back down. I hope they trust what we tell them. ...We can't even take the elevator, damn it.": '先下去吧。希望他们会相信我们说的话。{w}……该死，连电梯都坐不了。',
        "I don't know. I had no idea it existed.": '我不知道。{w}我根本不知道还有这么个地方。',
        '...Can we not do anything to open it?': '……{w}我们就不能想办法打开它吗？',
        "...Well, this door might lead outside, and Katei keeps assuring us he didn't know about it. Even if he's lying, it must be a secret door that's hard to find. There's grass on the sides of the tower, meaning that if this door opened outwardly, it would leave conspicuous marks on the grass and could be noticed. It probably opens inward instead.": '……{w}这扇门也许通向外面，而 Katei 一直坚称自己不知道有这扇门。就算他在撒谎，这扇门也必定很难被发现。{w}塔的两侧长着草，也就是说，如果这扇门向外开，就会在草地上留下明显的痕迹，容易被人察觉。所以它多半是向内开的。',
        "...Now a few things make sense, at least. As you said, nobody was found, so Naomi must've been here at some point.": '……{w}至少现在有几件事说得通了。就像你说的，到处都没找到人影，所以 Naomi 一定来过这里。',
        "Yes, yes. I'd like to advise you all on something. I've made sure that if this door is opened again, I'll be able to tell.": '对，对。我想提醒各位一件事。{w}我已经做好了安排，只要这扇门再次被打开，我就能知道。',
        "...In the off chance Naomi's still in the tower, she's up there, being covered by the three of you. I want to go see it by myself, and I'm sure Akaro and Erina aren't content with your words alone.": '……{w}万一 Naomi 还在塔里，那她就在上面，正被你们三个包庇着。我要亲自去看看；而且我敢肯定，光凭你几句话，Akaro 和 Erina 也不会满意。',
        'When Akaro and Katei arrived, they went with Sai, curious to see if anything was to be found. The attic was composed of only a few rooms, so they made quick work of inspecting them.': 'Akaro 和 Katei 到了之后，和 Sai 一起去查看，都想看看能不能找到什么。{w}阁楼只有几个房间，很快就查完了。',
        "Hmhm. I suppose we might as well stay here if we're gonna remain in one place.": '嗯哼。{w}反正总得待在一个地方，那就在这里吧。',
        "Me? No, not at all. If it's not outside, it must be hidden pretty well...": '我？不，完全没头绪。{w} 要是它不在外面，那一定藏得相当隐蔽……',
        '...I think we should. I doubt he knew where the Sekimeiya was since he was searching in this room as well, but nobody from the other room has followed him.': '……{w}我觉得该去。他刚才也在这屋里找过，应该不知道 Sekimeiya 在哪儿；可另一个房间的人也没有谁跟上去。',
        "To prevent that, the structure could be partially frozen. But that wasn't all. It could also be reshaped.": '为避免这种情况，可以先将结构局部冻结。{w} 不过，还不止这些。它也能被重新塑形。',
        "Sai wasn't there. However, on the sofa, a recognizable shining egg lay, next to the many footprints that indicated someone had walked on that floor very recently.": 'Sai 并不在那里。{w}可沙发上却放着一个眼熟的发光的蛋，旁边还有许多脚印，显然不久前有人在这块地板上走过。',
        "The Sekimeiya... Whatever it is, it can do much more than making one travel through time. I don't think I should just explain to you two. I've had time to learn how it functions, and it's incredible.": 'Sekimeiya……不管它是什么，它能做到的都远不止让人穿越时间。{w}我觉得不该只靠口头解释。我已经花时间摸清了它的运作方式，而它实在不可思议。',
        "It isn't. It stopped working earlier, unfortunately, so we won't be able to measure the time. Anyway, I'm glad you're all following along. Now, Isla, mind telling me a number?": '确实不走了。很遗憾，它早些时候就停了，所以我们没法计时。{w}总之，你们能跟得上就好。那么，Isla，能说一个数字吗？',
        'Huh...? C.': '哎……？{w}C。',
        "Actually, I'm not completely sure myself. It can do anything, so we'll see. Some time from now, it will make a sound. That'll tell us it's worked.": '说实话，我自己也不完全确定。它什么都能做，所以等着看吧。{w}过一阵子，它会发出一点声响。那就说明它起作用了。',
        '"There it is." A metallic sound startled everyone but Sai. They stared at the locked door, as it had come from behind it.': '「来了。」{w}一声金属轻响，除 Sai 外所有人都被吓了一跳。他们盯着那扇锁着的门——声音正是从门后传来的。',
        "You're all wondering where the Sekimeiya is, right? Don't worry, I'll tell you. After it does something that requires more power than usual, it teleports to its cabinet. I'm not sure why yet, but it's what I learned. You'll see. Follow me.": '你们都在想 Sekimeiya 到哪儿去了吧？别急，我告诉你们。{w}它完成一件比平时需要更多力量的事之后，就会传送到自己的展示柜里。原因我还不清楚，但这是我查到的。{w}你们看就知道了。跟我来。',
        "Isn't it obvious? Now, all you have to do is activate the Sekimeiya. If you really understand how it works, you can make it send you to the past and to the locked bedroom. There, you'll leave the piece of paper and make the noise we heard. Before we enter, you'll touch the Sekimeiya and vanish from the room, once again to the past. That could be why you locked the door, so that we wouldn't open it immediately after hearing the noise. You definitely didn't prove that the Sekimeiya is able to materialize a piece of paper. ...It's true that it might've teleported from the attic to this cabinet after that. That's the most believable part of what you're claiming, though.": '这不是明摆着的吗？现在你只要激活 Sekimeiya 就行。{w}如果你真懂它的原理，就能让它把你送回过去，送到那间上锁的卧室。你在那里留下纸条，弄出我们听到的声响。趁我们还没进门，你碰一下 Sekimeiya，从房间里消失，再次回到过去。{w}你锁门大概就是这个缘故——免得我们一听见声音就立刻开门。你根本没有证明 Sekimeiya 能凭空变出一张纸。{w}……在那之后，它确实有可能从阁楼传送到这个展示柜里。不过，这也是你那些说法里最可信的一点。',
        "No, no. You don't understand. I will never travel to the past again. Everything's already over, and the Sekimeiya did it all. Listen, Atsuki. I can prove that what you said didn't happen. If it had, another version of myself would have to be somewhere in the tower right now. Let's confirm that version of me doesn't exist.": '不不，你没明白。我不会再穿越到过去了。一切都已经结束，都是 Sekimeiya 干的。{w}听好了，Atsuki。我可以证明你说的那些没有发生。如果真发生了，此刻塔里某处就该有另一个我。我们去确认一下，那个我并不存在。',
        '"Wait." Shiroya objected. "I can think of another way, if we\'re supposed to believe what you\'re saying now."': '「等等。」Shiroya 提出了异议。{w}「如果照你现在说的，我还能想出另一种可能。」',
        'It\'s possible you\'ll really never travel to the past again, but another version of you could. I remember when you made Atsuki and me go to the living room. Back then, you weren\'t there, and you appeared from the hallway. What if that was already another version of you? If you lured us out of the bedroom, your original version could go in there to hide under the bed. From there, you heard what we were talking about in the hallway, "9C". That version of you will travel to the past and appear inside the bedroom, where you\'ll leave the note. Then, you\'ll use the Sekimeiya to go back to the past again, and you\'ll appear before us in the living room to play out the rest.': '也许你真的不会再穿越了，但另一个你却可以。{w}我记得你让 Atsuki 和我去客厅那次。当时你不在，是从走廊里出现的。那说不定已经是另一个你了？{w}要是你把我们引出了卧室，原本的你就能进屋，躲到床底下。你在那里听见了我们在走廊里说的「9C」。{w}那个你会穿越到过去，出现在卧室里，留下字条。然后你再用 Sekimeiya 回到过去，在客厅里出现在我们面前，把剩下的戏演完。',
        "Like I said, what I could believe is that the Sekimeiya can teleport itself. If you really came to understand how that works... I remember when you claimed you forgot about the key to the other bedroom, but I don't believe you really did. That could've easily been an excuse to disappear from our sight. After all, you asked to be searched, but only before you entered the other bedroom. It's possible you got both keys from that room and initially only showed us one. However, it's also possible the Sekimeiya had teleported there. You touched it and went to the past, to the right bedroom. You placed the note and touched the Sekimeiya before it teleported away. You went back in time and appeared in the second level of the left bedroom. This way, as soon as you entered it, the version of yours who'd already placed the note got out, and you showed us the wrong key when you'd already done everything.": '就像我说的，我能接受的是——Sekimeiya 能传送自己。如果你真的弄懂了它的运作方式……{w}我记得你说过忘了另一间卧室的钥匙，可我不信你真忘了。那很可能只是个借口，好从我们眼前消失。毕竟你主动让我们搜身，却偏偏是在进那间卧室之前。{w}你完全可能从那个房间里拿到两把钥匙，起初只拿出一把给我们看。不过，也有可能是 Sekimeiya 传送到了那里。{w}你碰了它，回到过去，到了右边那间卧室。你放下字条，趁 Sekimeiya 还没传送走，又碰了它。你回到过去，出现在左边卧室的二层。这样一来，你一走进卧室，那个已经放好字条的你便出来了；而你给我们看那把错钥匙的时候，其实一切都已经做完了。',
        "Oh, I see. ...I said you traveled to the past before the Sekimeiya teleported away, which must have been before we heard the noise. However, there are two ways around this. One, the Sekimeiya teleported itself to the past after you made the noise. That would solve it, if it's possible. Two, the Sekimeiya teleported itself to the opposite bedroom and then back to the initial one. That's how you could've stayed there for longer and made the sound.": '哦，我明白了。{w}……我刚说你在 Sekimeiya 传送离开之前回到了过去，而那一定发生在我们听到声响之前。不过，这一点有两种绕开的办法。{w}其一，Sekimeiya 是在你弄出声响之后才把自己传送到过去的。只要这能做到，问题就解决了。{w}其二，Sekimeiya 先把自己传送到对面那间卧室，再传回原来那间。这样你就能在那里多待一阵，把声音弄出来。',
        "...How about this? That didn't happen either. You're just wrong. In fact, I really did overlook that the other bedroom had a key as well. That was not part of what I intended to do.": '……那这样吧。那些也没发生。你就是想错了。{w}事实上，我确实没注意到另一间卧室也有钥匙。那并不在我原本的计划之内。',
        "I bet the way you locked the room from the inside was part of your trick too. You set the chain and then locked the door with the key. That created the illusion that the Sekimeiya removed the chain, but it could've been as simple as you taking it out right after locking the door. It's not like we would've noticed.": '我敢说，你从里面锁门的手法也是把戏的一部分。你先挂上门链，再用钥匙锁门。{w}这样就造成了 Sekimeiya 取下门链的假象，可实际上，你完全可能只是锁完门之后把链子摘了下来。我们反正也注意不到。',
        "...I actually didn't think about that. However, I didn't do it.": '……这一点我倒真没想到。{w}不过，我没有那么做。',
        "At some point, after having written the note, he would touch the Sekimeiya and go minutes back to the past. He would appear somewhere in the attic and claim he'd just set the chain and traveled out of the room, when in reality he would have already left the note. Then, he would ask for the specific number and wait out the time he'd spent in the bedroom before opening the door and finding the note.": '写好纸条之后，他会再碰一下 Sekimeiya，回到几分钟前。他会出现在阁楼的某处，声称自己刚挂好链条、从房间里穿越出来——可实际上，那时纸条早就放好了。{w}接着，他会问出那个具体数字，再等够他之前在卧室里待的那段时间，然后开门发现纸条。',
        "Sai took two steps into the room, but his shadow was still acting as a barrier for the ceiling light. Atsuki wanted to verify Sai's bluff and quickly turn the light back on. He was certain that a future version of him was nearby after already placing the note. If he could know what Atsuki was doing, it was possible his idea would retroactively fail. However, Atsuki was confident that'd still prevent Sai from completing his setup without a hole.": 'Sai 往房里走了两步，影子依旧挡着顶灯的光。Atsuki 想验证他是不是在虚张声势，便迅速把灯重新打开。他确信，未来的 Sai 已经放好纸条，人就在附近。{w}如果那个未来的 Sai 能知道 Atsuki 正在做什么，他的计划就有可能被反过来推翻。不过 Atsuki 相信，即便如此，也足以让 Sai 的布置留下破绽。',
        "It had not been a deception. Right after setting the chain and locking the door, Sai had touched the Sekimeiya and traveled to the past, outside the bedroom. By doing that, he'd left both levels of the bedroom truly devoid of life. That was why Atsuki's very first solution had been that Sai would, in the future, travel to the past again and appear inside the right bedroom after it had been locked.": '那并不是骗局。挂好链条、锁上门之后，Sai 立刻碰了 Sekimeiya，穿越到过去，落在卧室门外。这样一来，卧室的上下两层就真的空无一人。{w}正因如此，Atsuki 最先想到的解法是：Sai 会在之后再次穿越回过去，出现在上锁后的右边卧室里。',
        "Don't worry. This time, I won't go anywhere. Let's do what we did before, then. Isla, give me three numbers from one to nine.": '放心，这次我哪儿也不会去。那就照之前那样做吧。{w} Isla，从一到九里给我三个数。',
        '...Oh, certainly, Atsuki. We can do it like this.': '……{w}哦，当然可以，Atsuki。{w}那就这么办。',
        '...57, 58, 59...': '……57、58、59……{w=0.9}{nw}',
        "Seventeen minutes. 2 + 6 + 9. Remember when you said I'd waited an arbitrary amount of time to time everything properly? I'm glad I can now be certain I understand exactly how to use the Sekimeiya.": '十七分钟。2 + 6 + 9。{w}你还记得吗？你说过我是随便等了一段时间，好把每一步的时机都掐准。好在我现在可以确定，自己已经彻底弄清 Sekimeiya 该怎么用了。',
        "Was it you? Are you my accomplice who helped me do this? If not, I'm open to alternatives.": '是你吗？{w}你是帮我做成那件事的共犯吗？要不是，我也愿意听听别的解释。',
        "My wristwatch doesn't work anymore, and I don't know if I can fix it. We have no other way to look at the time. It'll be hard, but we'll spend every minute left together so that I can't go to the past and explain this your way.": '我的手表不走了，也不知道能不能修好。{w}我们没别的办法看时间了。这会很辛苦，但剩下的每一分钟我们都要待在一起，这样我就没法回到过去，用你们说的那种方式解释这一切。',
        "There were no tricks left. The few times anyone had to go to the bathroom, it was made sure nothing else happened. Finally, they'd managed to wait until 21:00, keeping the cold in the cabinet sealed.": '再没有别的花招了。有几次有人要去洗手间，大家也都确保没出别的事。最后，他们总算熬到了 {time=21}，始终把寒气封在展示柜里。',
        "There were no tricks left. The few times anyone had to go to the bathroom, it was made sure nothing else happened. Finally, they'd managed to wait until 9 p.m., keeping the cold in the cabinet sealed.": '再没有别的花招了。有几次有人要去洗手间，大家也都确保没出别的事。最后，他们总算熬到了 {time=21}，始终把寒气封在展示柜里。',
        'Y—! You scared the fuck out of me! Holy shit! What the fuck are you doing!? You almost hit me with the door!': '哇——！吓死我了！{w} 搞什么啊！你到底在干什么！？门差点砸到我身上！',
        "...I didn't lie, though. I really didn't find the Sekimeiya when I looked for it.": '……{w}可我没有说谎。我找的时候，真的没找到 Sekimeiya。',
        'Huh, how bizarre. Are we supposed to look for it now? What the hell. At least we know not to let Atsuki do it.': '哈，真是怪事。{w}难道现在还得我们去找？搞什么鬼。至少我们知道不能让 Atsuki 去做。',
        '...Oh, give me the key.': '……{w=0.7}对了，把钥匙给我。',
        '...Excuse me?': '……{w}等等。',
        "There's one place we definitely need to check: the storeroom. I'll see if the door was opened. The Sekimeiya disappeared out of nowhere, but who knows what else happened with that; your footprints were erased from the living room.": '有个地方必须查——储藏室。我去看看那扇门有没有被打开过。{w}Sekimeiya 凭空消失了，可谁知道除此之外还发生了什么。你们的脚印在客厅里被抹掉了。',
        "I looked at his wristwatch, and it said it's 13:44. I want to look at the computer's, though.": '我看了一下他的手表，上面显示 {time=13:44.} 不过我想再看看电脑上的时间。',
        "I looked at his wristwatch, and it said it's 1:44 p.m. I want to look at the computer's, though.": '我看了一下他的手表，上面显示 {time=13:44.} 不过我想再看看电脑上的时间。',
        "It seems like nobody is following us... What if this was done to keep the Sekimeiya inside the elevator, for example? That's kind of flawed, because they'd have to stop the elevator between two floors and then touch the Sekimeiya to do it. But doing it like that, it'd be stuck inside, and not even the buttons would help you. And even if it could be called with the buttons, we'd have to find them first. That would make the Sekimeiya simply hidden there instead.": '看起来没人跟上来……{w}比方说，如果这么做是为了把 Sekimeiya 留在电梯里呢？可这说不通——他们得先把电梯停在两层之间，再碰到 Sekimeiya 才行。可那样一来，东西就困在电梯里了，就算有按钮也没用。{w}而且，就算用按钮能把电梯叫过来，我们也得先找到那些按钮才行。那样的话，Sekimeiya 就只是被藏在那儿罢了。',
        "I found the key in one of the staircases and we came here, but the door was unlocked to begin with. Then, Katei said his key he'd left inside wasn't there... We assumed it was the same one, but maybe that was wrong. Maybe there were two keys, and one belonged to another employee. I'm not really sure it's that, though. It felt to me like Katei was scanning the floor for something. That's how I found the key in the first place.": '我是在一段楼梯上捡到那把钥匙的。后来我们来了这里，可那扇门本来就没锁。之后 Katei 说，他留在里面的钥匙不见了……{w}我们以为那是同一把，但也许想错了。也许有两把钥匙，其中一把属于别的员工。不过我也不太确定是不是这样。当时我觉得，Katei 像是在地上找什么东西——我最初能找到那把钥匙，就是因为看到了他那副样子。',
        "Wait, y-you're right...! I left some of them open, didn't I?": '等等，你、你说得对……！{w}我明明留了几扇没关，对吧？',
        "Hold on, is this normal? Katei said it was burning when he was holding it, and it was hot when I had it too. Now it's not, though.": '等等，这正常吗？{w}Katei 说他拿着的时候，它烫得像在烧，我拿着时也很烫。可现在不烫了。',
        "...I'd rather not. Let's leave it in the cabinet.": '……{w}还是算了。就把它留在展示柜里吧。',
        "...But when I got here, you were in front of the storeroom. Does that mean you'd already tried to open the security room? Why was that your priority?": '……{w}可我来的时候，你站在储藏室前面。这么说，你已经试过打开监控室了？为什么要先去那里？',
        "Because our footprints disappeared? I'm not sure I follow that logic. Anyway, it's 13:50.": '就因为我们的脚印消失了？这个逻辑我可不太明白。总之，现在是 {time=13:50.}。',
        "Because our footprints disappeared? I'm not sure I follow that logic. Anyway, it's 1:50 p.m.": '就因为我们的脚印消失了？这个逻辑我可不太明白。总之，现在是 {time=13:50.}。',
        "What if someone's hiding inside? Naomi...? Mind coming out?": '要是有人躲在里面呢？{w}Naomi……？能出来一下吗？',
        "I can't see anything through these gaps, but I mean, Katei's got a point; why would anyone lock this room? The computer doesn't work, so unless it was done to prevent us from fixing it, I can't think of much else. There aren't that many more rooms to lock yourself up in. I can think of the bathrooms and the bedrooms, but I'm sure you'd feel much more secure behind this sturdy door.": '从这些缝隙里什么也看不清。不过，Katei 说得有道理——为什么会有人把这间房锁上？{w}电脑坏了，除非是为了不让我们修好它，否则我想不出别的理由。能把自己反锁起来的地方也没剩几处。洗手间和卧室倒是可以，可躲在这扇结实的门后，想必会安心得多吧。',
        'Wait. Is it me, or are we very stupid?': '等等。{w}是我多心，还是我们真的很蠢？',
        "...You haven't, though. At least not on this floor.": '……{w}可你没试过。至少这一层没试。',
        "As Atsuki gripped the handle, I noticed that the door was closed. He had previously left it open to disable the elevator before searching through the higher floors. When he tugged on it, the door didn't budge.": 'Atsuki 握住门把手时，我才注意到门是关着的。他先前为了让电梯停运，特意把门敞着，然后才去搜查楼上几层。{w}他用力一拉，门却纹丝不动。',
        '...Akaro attempted to cross the wires, but nothing happened.': '……{w}Akaro 试着把电线接在一起，但什么也没发生。',
        'We all stared at the door in shock. It was locked.': '{w=1.3}我们全都震惊地盯着那扇门。门锁着。',
        "Wh-Wh...!? It won't open!": '什、什么……！？{w=0.5} 打不开！',
        'This is insane, then! How are we supposed to get in here? Is Naomi really in the attic? How does she keep doing this!?': '那这简直荒唐透顶！我们到底要怎么进去？{w} Naomi 真的在阁楼里吗？她到底是怎么一次次做到的！？',
        'One, you wanted to keep the idea of checking them to yourself. Two, one of the previous doors had already opened, so you had no reason to keep checking them after that.': '其一，你不想让别人也想到去检查电梯门。{w} 其二，之前已经有一扇门打开过，从那以后你自然没理由再继续检查。',
        "*sigh* Okay, sure. If there's currently someone in the attic, they might want to take the elevator down and back up at some point, so it's not a bad idea to keep confirming that it can't be accessed.": '唉……{w} 好吧，随你。如果现在真有人躲在阁楼里，他说不定什么时候会想坐电梯下来再上去，所以继续确认电梯没法用，倒也不是坏主意。',
        '"Isla! Don\'t look!"': '{w=0.7}「I{w=0.1}s{w=0.1}l{w=0.1}a{w=0.1}！{w=0.5}千{w=0.1}{w=0.1}万{w=0.1}{w=0.1}别{w=0.1}{w=0.1}看{w=0.1}{w=0.1}{w=0.1}」{w=1}{nw}',
        'Immediately, Atsuki crouched. He softly grabbed an arm and pressed his finger to its wrist. His own arm lost its strength and released its grip.': 'Atsuki 立刻蹲下。他轻轻抓住一只手臂，把手指按在手腕上。{w} 他的手却一下子没了力气，松开了。',
        "Of course? Someone just locked the attic as well, right? We're still missing the person who did this. Someone killed Naomi. I have no idea what happened to this girl, but look behind Naomi's head and at the blood on the floor. Most of it is dry. She's been dead for a while; it wasn't her we were looking for.": '这有什么不能信的？刚刚不也有人把阁楼锁上了吗？做出这些事的人，我们还没找到。{w} Naomi 是被人杀的。这女孩身上发生过什么，我完全不清楚，可你看看 Naomi 的后脑，再看看地上的血——大部分都干了。她死了有一阵子了，我们要找的人根本不是她。',
        'O-Oh! I completely ignored that. ...Also, what I told you earlier was true. Naomi did have another copy of the keys.': '啊、哦！我完全没想到这一点。{w}……还有，我之前说的没错，Naomi 确实另有一套钥匙。',
        'They closed the door and let the elevator bring them to the attic, the place the person we were searching for had sealed off. I turned back and saw Atsuki walking to the lobby.': '他们关上电梯门，任由电梯把他们送上阁楼——那地方被我们要追查的人封锁了。{w}我回过头，看见 Atsuki 正朝大厅走去。',
        "...It's still not working...! Wh-Why not? I'm doing the same thing.": '……还是不行……！{w}为、为什么？我明明做的是同样的事。',
        "Th-There's no way. ...Should I bring her to the lobby?": '怎、怎么可能。{w}……要不要把她带到大厅去？',
        'Sai is right. This wasn\'t an accident, and I heard it. I-I was in the first partition of the second floor when I heard Erina. Her voice hardly reached me, but the words I picked up were enough to understand what was happening. "Don\'t lie! It can only be you. You killed them."': 'Sai 说得对。这不是意外，我亲耳听到了。我、我当时在二楼的第一个隔间里，听见了 Erina 的声音。{w}她的声音传到我这里已经很微弱，但我听到的那几句，足以让我明白发生了什么。「别骗人了！只可能是你。是你杀了他们。」',
        '...Is this true, Atsuki?': '……{w}这是真的吗，Atsuki？',
        "...It's because of this thread that I detached from the curtain earlier.": '……{w}因为我之前从遮布上拆下了这根线。',
        "It's true that we can't be sure nobody's currently in the security room, but it's unlikely. They can't keep shut in there after 21:00.": '确实不能保证此刻监控室里没人，但这不太可能。都过了{time=21.}，他们不可能还一直把自己关在里面。',
        "It's true that we can't be sure nobody's currently in the security room, but it's unlikely. They can't keep shut in there after 9 p.m.": '确实不能保证此刻监控室里没人，但这不太可能。都过了{time=21.}，他们不可能还一直把自己关在里面。',
        "You heard what Isla said, right? Before dying, Erina told her to stay in that room. She knew she was gonna confront the person she believed to be the killer, and she didn't want Isla to see it or interfere. So now tell us, Atsuki: why did you say that none of us could've done it?": '你们都听见 Isla 的话了吧？Erina 临死前让她待在那间房里。她知道要去质问那个自己认定的凶手，也不想让 Isla 看见，或者插手。{w}那么，Atsuki，你来说说：你为什么说我们之中没人做得到？',
        "Because I left the attic first. I walked down, but I... couldn't really bring myself to go to the crystal floor. That's why I stayed in the first partition of the second floor, thinking to myself... From there, I would've seen anyone moving through floor 2.": '因为我最先离开阁楼。我往下走，可是……实在没勇气去水晶层。所以我留在二楼最前面那一段，心里想着……{w}从那里，二楼有谁走动我都能看见。',
        "In addition, the panels haven't been attached yet, so there was no way to call it from here. The floor 1 button was pressed from the attic. Which leaves the following way possible: someone took the elevator with Erina and Isla. That's how the killer could've gotten to the crystal floor without being seen. Did anyone see both of them taking the elevator?": '另外，按键面板还没装回去，没法从这里叫电梯。一楼按钮是在阁楼按下的。{w}于是只剩下一种可能：有人和 Erina、Isla 一同乘了电梯。凶手就是这样避开众人视线，来到了水晶层。有谁亲眼看到她们两个上电梯吗？',
        '"I\'ll repeat what I did. I was the first to leave the attic, and I went to the second floor. I spent several minutes there, during which I heard the elevator once."\n\n"Then, Erina\'s voice echoed to me, but it was very muddled. All I recognized was "Don\'t lie! It can only be you. You killed them.""\n\n"I ran down the staircase and found her dead. I didn\'t see or hear anyone else, so I ran back up to find you all."': '{w=0.7}「我再说一遍我做了什么。我第一个离开阁楼，去了二楼。在那里待了几分钟，其间听到过一次电梯的动静。」{w}\n\n「后来，Erina 的声音传了过来，但很模糊。我只听清了『别撒谎！只可能是你。是你杀了他们。』」\n\n「我顺着楼梯跑下去，发现她已经死了。我没看见也没听见其他人，于是又跑上来找你们。」',
        '"Right. He found me first since I was on the third floor. I left the attic later than him and walked through the floors until I stayed on the third."\n\n"I just wanted to be alone for a bit, but I didn\'t feel like staying put somewhere. However, I ended up spending the most time on the third floor, where I heard the elevator. I spent some time in the offices and some outside."\n\n"Some minutes later, Atsuki came running from below."': '{w=0.4}「对。我在三楼，所以他先找到了我。我比他晚离开阁楼，一路走过几层，最后停在了三楼。」{w}\n\n「我只是想一个人待一会儿，又不想一直守在同一个地方。结果三楼成了我待得最久的地方，我就是在那里听见电梯的。我先在办公室里待了一阵，又到外面待了一阵。」{w}\n\n「几分钟后，Atsuki 从楼下跑了上来。」',
        '"So, you\'re already unable to prove you didn\'t take the elevator with Erina and Isla. Did anyone see you leaving through the main door?"': '{w=0.4}「也就是说，你没法证明自己没有和 Erina、Isla 一起乘电梯了。有人看见你从正门出去吗？」',
        '"Can you prove you didn\'t go down with them?"': '{w=0.4}「你能证明自己没有和她们一起下去吗？」',
        '"No, but Atsuki saw me on the third floor immediately after he saw Erina."': '{w=0.4}「不能。不过 Atsuki 看到 Erina 之后，紧接着就在三楼看见了我。」',
        '"I don\'t think accomplices came into play, because it seems like Erina was killed after she accused someone of being the culprit. However, since you and Atsuki know each other, he could be covering for you."\n\n"Also, if you took the elevator with Erina and Isla, you could\'ve used it to reach the third floor after killing her and sent it back to the crystal floor from there."\n\n"Remember when we sent it from the sixth floor to the crystal floor? We heard no noise. If at that point, Atsuki was already running down the staircase, he might not have heard you. Did you check the elevator when you found Erina?"': '{w=0.4}「我不认为有共犯。Erina 是在指认凶手之后才被杀的。不过，你和 Atsuki 彼此认识，他有可能在替你遮掩。」{w}\n\n「还有，如果你和 Erina、Isla 一起乘了电梯，你完全可以在杀了她之后坐电梯去三楼，再把电梯送回水晶层。」{w}\n\n「还记得我们从六楼把电梯送到水晶层那回吗？我们什么都没听见。如果那时 Atsuki 已经在往楼下跑，他也许就听不到你的动静。你发现 Erina 的时候，检查过电梯吗？」',
        '"That doesn\'t matter. I can confirm that she didn\'t take the elevator."': '{w=0.4}「那不重要。我可以确认，她没有乘电梯。」',
        '"You can, Katei?"': '{w=0.4}「Katei，你能确认？」',
        '"Yes. That\'s because when I left the attic, only Erina, Isla, and Akaro remained. Everyone else had already left."\n\n"I looked everywhere to see who had left, and I also opened the elevator in the attic, as I thought of using it. However, I ended up walking out through the main door. Only Akaro could\'ve taken the elevator with Erina and Isla."': '{w=0.4}「能。因为我离开阁楼时，留在里面的只剩 Erina、Isla 和 Akaro，其他人都已经走了。」{w}\n\n「我把各处看了一遍，确认谁已经离开，还打开了阁楼的电梯，因为我当时想过要乘它。可最后我还是从正门走了出去。能和 Erina、Isla 一起乘电梯的，只可能是 Akaro。」',
        '"I see. Well then, what did you do? I recall we found you on the fifth floor."': '{w=0.4}「原来如此。那么你做了什么？我记得我们是在五楼找到你的。」',
        '"Precisely. That\'s where I was the entire time."\n\n"In the attic, I spent a few minutes in one of the bedrooms with Akaro. Soon, I noticed some people had left, so I checked to see who remained."\n\n"I was a bit angry people were entering and leaving the attic without my consent, so I went to find the people who had left."\n\n"However, I reached the fifth floor and recalled the two dead bodies. Most importantly, that a killer was around. That\'s what made me stop."\n\n"I had thousands of things to think about, and that\'s what I did. I went over the incident to see if there was any conclusion I could get to, but ultimately, I didn\'t move from there. I heard the elevator once, which was the only sound that reached my ears until you guys came."': '{w=0.4}「正是。我一直在那里。」{w}\n\n「在阁楼时，我和 Akaro 在其中一个房间里待了几分钟。不久我发觉有人离开了，就去确认还剩哪些人。」{w}\n\n「有人不经我允许就在阁楼里进进出出，我有些恼火，便去找那些离开的人。」{w}\n\n「可走到五楼，我又想起了那两具尸体，更重要的是，想起了凶手还在附近。我因此停下了脚步。」{w}\n\n「我要想的事太多了，就站在那里想。我把整件事从头到尾过了一遍，看能不能得出什么结论，但最终一步也没有挪。其间我听到过一次电梯的声音，那也是你们赶来之前我听到的唯一声响。」',
        '"That\'s fine by me, and I can confirm it: he\'s telling the truth."\n\n"The reason why I stayed on the fourth floor was different from everyone else\'s. It was because I quickly began to hear noise coming from the floor above me. More specifically, footsteps that I now know belonged to Katei."\n\n"I paid attention to see if there was anything I could figure out from them, but they simply kept going in circles, so it gave the impression that whoever was walking above me was either lost in thought or fairly nervous."\n\n"For most of the time, the sound of footsteps came directly from the third partition. However, during the last few minutes, they left it and started to come from outside the offices."\n\n"When I heard the elevator, I thought the person above me would come down. That never happened, though, and the footsteps never ceased. There was no time for Katei to do anything."': '{w=0.4}「我没意见，而且我可以作证：他说的是实话。」{w}\n\n「我留在四楼的理由和各位不同：我很快就听见楼上传来动静，准确地说，是脚步声——现在我知道那是 Katei 的。」{w}\n\n「我留心去听，想从中听出些什么，可那脚步声只是来回打转，给人的感觉是，楼上那个人不是在出神，就是相当紧张。」{w}\n\n「大部分时间里，脚步声都直接从第三个隔间那边传来。不过在最后几分钟，它离开了那里，开始从办公室外传来。」{w}\n\n「听到电梯时，我以为楼上的人会下来。可那人始终没下来，脚步声也一直没停。Katei 根本没有时间做别的事。」',
        '"I\'m glad we settled this quickly. This also confirms that Sai is telling the truth. Everything that he said is correct, which means that he was on the fourth floor the whole time."': '{w=0.4}「这么快就说清楚了，很好。这也证实了 Sai 说的是实话。他说的每一点都对得上，也就是说，他一直都在四楼。」',
        '"Akaro, it\'s you left, and you understand your position, right?"': '{w=0.4}「Akaro，剩下的人就是你了，你也明白自己的处境吧？」',
        '"Yes, but I don\'t have much to say. I left the attic when Erina and Isla were still sitting on the sofa. I\'m pretty sure Katei is right and they were the two people remaining in the attic."\n\n"I knew most people had left, but the sixth floor was completely desolate. I also had quite a few things to think about, so I eventually sat where you found me and spent the whole time there. I actually didn\'t hear the elevator, but I was pretty far from it and not paying much attention."': '{w=0.4}「明白，不过我也没什么好说的。我离开阁楼时，Erina 和 Isla 还坐在沙发上。我想 Katei 说得没错，留在阁楼里的就是她们两个。」{w}\n\n「我知道大多数人都走了，六楼又空荡荡的。我也有不少事要想，最后就坐在你们找到我的地方，一直待到你们来。其实我没听见电梯的声音，不过我离得远，也没怎么留意。」',
        '"I have a question. Why didn\'t I hear your footsteps if I was directly below you?"': '{w=0.4}「我有个问题。我就在你正下方，为什么没听见你的脚步声？」',
        '"That I can answer. Haven\'t you noticed? Akaro doesn\'t make much sound when he walks."': '{w=0.4}「这个我能回答。你没注意到吗？Akaro 走路几乎没什么声音。」',
        '"I know what you\'re all thinking—I could\'ve gone to the crystal floor with Erina and Isla. Of course, Isla could verify that didn\'t happen, but even if I\'d managed to make it to the crystal floor, I couldn\'t have been found on the sixth."\n\n"According to Sai, Katei spent the last few minutes outside the offices, one floor below me. So if I\'d killed Erina, I needed to either use the elevator or walk up to reach the sixth floor. Doing that without being found or heard would\'ve been impossible."': '{w=0.4}「我知道你们在想什么——我可能和 Erina、Isla 一起去了水晶层。当然，Isla 可以证明没这回事；可就算我真到了水晶层，也不可能在六楼被发现。」{w}\n\n「按 Sai 的说法，最后几分钟 Katei 一直在办公室外，就在我下面一层。那么，如果是我杀了 Erina，我要么坐电梯，要么走楼梯上六楼。无论哪种，都不可能不被人看见或听见。」',
        '"Is that it, then? Was Atsuki right? None of us could\'ve done it?"\n\n"I\'m not sure I can think of a way out that doesn\'t involve the Sekimeiya. We\'ll get there, though."': '{w=0.4}「那就是这样了？Atsuki 说对了？我们当中谁都做不到？」{w}\n\n「不借助 Sekimeiya 的话，我一时想不出别的解释。不过总会弄明白的。」',
        '"I can think of one, I suppose."': '{w=0.4}「我倒能想出一个。」',
        '"I\'m just saying that Sai and Katei could technically have done it, right? Their versions of events are just covering each other."': '{w=0.4}「我只是说，从道理上讲，Sai 和 Katei 也有可能是凶手，不是吗？他们各自的说法不过是互相打掩护。」',
        '"That\'s not true. Did you not hear what Akaro said? He said that when he left the attic, Erina and Isla were the only two people left. That means that Katei and I couldn\'t have gone to the crystal floor."': '{w=0.4}「不对。你没听见 Akaro 说的吗？他离开阁楼时，里面只剩 Erina 和 Isla 两个人。也就是说，Katei 和我根本不可能去水晶层。」',
        '"You could have. Erina and Isla used the elevator alone, from the attic. However, they got off on floor 4 or 5, where you two were. That way, you could\'ve gotten to the crystal floor with a single elevator trip."\n\n"I don\'t mean to say I believe it to be the case, but I\'m answering what you asked. Then, you could\'ve taken the elevator back up while Atsuki and I were on the crystal floor, which we wouldn\'t have heard."': '{w=0.4}「有可能。Erina 和 Isla 从阁楼单独乘了电梯，但她们在四楼或五楼——也就是你们两人所在的地方——下了电梯。这样，你们乘一趟电梯就能到水晶层。」{w}\n\n「我不是说我相信事情就是这样，只是在回答你的问题。然后，趁 Atsuki 和我在水晶层的时候，你们可以再乘电梯上去，我们不会听见。」',
        '"I see. So then you could have also done this."': '{w=0.4}「原来如此。那么你也可能用同样的手法。」',
        '"Yes, which is why we should ask Isla. Once we rule that out, it seems like all of us have some sort of alibi."': '{w=0.4}「对，所以该去问 Isla。排除这种可能之后，我们每个人似乎都有不在场证明了。」',
        'Then, the final method. Using the Sekimeiya in the future.': '那么，就剩最后一种手法了。{w}在未来使用 Sekimeiya。',
        "That's good. I have a question. When you came from the attic, you used the elevator, right? Were you and Erina alone?": '那就好。我有个问题。{w}你们从阁楼下来时乘的是电梯，对吧？当时只有你和 Erina 两个人吗？',
        'This is a very important question. Who do you think the killer is?': '这个问题非常重要。{w}你认为凶手是谁？',
        "Yes, that's what I mean. I have no clue how this would work, though, or why she'd travel to the past. I suppose that tells us the Sekimeiya is bound to be used again in the future. Technically, all Erina needs to do to be safe is not travel to the past. But she has to... or else what happened makes no sense.": '对，我就是这个意思。不过我想不通这到底是怎么做到的，也想不通她为什么要穿越到过去。我想，这至少说明未来一定还会有人使用 Sekimeiya。{w} 严格来说，Erina 只要不穿越到过去就能平安无事。可她非去不可……否则已经发生的事就说不通了。',
        "Oh, no, actually. I meant to suspect Erina herself since she's another person who could've technically done this. Wouldn't that be just nuts? Suicide via murdering yourself. Before you ask, I don't believe that happened, no, but it's a little strange.": '啊，不，其实不是。我是想说，Erina 本人也有嫌疑，毕竟严格来讲，她也是能做到那件事的人之一。那岂不是太荒唐了？自己杀自己？这算哪门子自杀。{w} 先别问，我也不信真有这种事，不过确实有点奇怪。',
        'That could be it. Isla nodded when I asked her "So you haven\'t moved from here?" She probably thought "you" meant her and Erina, so by answering yes, she meant neither of them left the room.': '有可能就是这样。{w} 我问她「你没离开过这里吧？」的时候，她点了点头。{w} 她大概把这句话里的「你」当成了她和 Erina 两个人，所以点头的意思是她们谁都没离开房间。',
        "...I don't think you did anything to Erina, and so far the four deaths could have a motive in common. The policeman could've entered through the storeroom, and then he was killed because he was a direct threat.": '……{w}我觉得 Erina 的事不是你做的。而且到目前为止，四起死亡可能出于同一个动机。那个警察也许是从储藏室进来的，随后因为构成直接威胁而被杀。',
        "The two in the elevator could have the very same motive: they were seen as threats. Both of them could've gone through the storeroom door as well since they weren't found until much later. Finally, Erina might've confronted the killer. It could be that the four dead people were all seen as threats by the same person.": '电梯里那两个人也可能是出于同一个动机：他们被视为威胁。而且他们俩也可能是从储藏室的门进出的，毕竟过了很久才发现。{w} 最后，Erina 也许是当面撞上了凶手。或许这四名死者，全都是被同一个人视为威胁的人。',
        "If we rule out those last two options, our choices will diminish greatly, and it's possible we can, like I said earlier. If someone traveled from the future and killed Erina, either they're still here or they left through the storeroom. Basically, if we can't find anyone and I confirm that the storeroom door didn't open, we can remove those possibilities.": '如果排除最后两种可能，范围就会大大缩小，而且就像我刚才说的，我们也许真能做到。{w} 如果有人从未来穿越回来杀了 Erina，那这个人要么还在这里，要么已经从储藏室离开了。总之，如果我们找不到任何人，而我又能确认储藏室的门没有开过，这些可能性就可以排除。',
        "No, I have it here. It was in the, um... wardrobe. I knew I wasn't allowed to touch it, so I had to cover it with this.": '不对，它就在我这儿。它原本在，那个……衣柜里。{w} 我知道我不能碰它，所以只好用这个把它裹起来。',
        "I see, you're right. Let's do what we were talking about on the way down. If we have the Sekimeiya while we search every floor, there's no way it'll be used to bypass us.": '原来如此，你说得对。{w}就照下楼时说的那样做。我们带着 Sekimeiya 逐层搜过去，就不可能有人用它绕过我们。',
        "It doesn't matter. Do not press it. Someone is guaranteed to have been on the crystal floor, and their only way out is the storeroom. Just in case, we shouldn't bring the elevator here.": '无所谓。别按。{w}水晶层上肯定有人，而他们唯一的出口就是储藏室。为防万一，不能把电梯叫过来。',
        "Erina dashed ahead of her and opened the door herself. It didn't seem like there was anything inside.": 'Erina 抢在她前面冲了过去，亲手推开门。{w}里面似乎什么也没有。',
        "That doesn't make sense. It really doesn't—the cabinet is locked. That would mean that whoever took the Sekimeiya out locked the cabinet while it was empty. I have another idea. Let me take the Sekimeiya. Akaro and Katei, you watch the stairs.": '这说不通。{w}真的说不通——展示柜一直锁着。照这么说，拿走 Sekimeiya 的人还得在柜子空着的时候把它锁上。{w}我还有个想法。Sekimeiya 由我来拿。Akaro、Katei，你们盯着楼梯。',
        "The sheet disappeared. Between Sai's hands, not only had the sheet vanished, but also the Sekimeiya.": '那块布消失了。{w}Sai 两手之间，消失的不只是那块布，还有 Sekimeiya。',
        'Wh—! Oh my God, I almost had a heart attack!': '什——！{w}天啊，我差点心脏停跳！',
        "This is going way beyond me. If there's someone on this floor, let's just fucking find them. I have no idea if we were right. Maybe if the Sekimeiya overheats, it teleports away, but only this time it happened when it was touched.": '这已经远远超出我的理解范围了。这层要是真有人，就他妈把人揪出来。{w}我根本不知道我们猜得对不对。也许 Sekimeiya 过热后就会传送离开，只是这一次，它是在被碰到时才传送的。',
        "Fuck... Let's hurry. The Sekimeiya might've appeared on this floor. I didn't think this through. If someone's actually here, there's a chance it'll allow them to escape.": '妈的……动作快点。Sekimeiya 可能已经出现在这层了。{w}是我考虑不周。要是真有人在这儿，说不定反而会让对方有机会逃走。',
        "I know it looks like she vanished, but I think there's more to it. Naomi and the policeman are still here, but do you remember when I brought both bodies to the lobby? I don't think the policeman was here.": '我知道她看起来像是凭空消失了，但我觉得没这么简单。{w} Naomi 和那名警察现在还在这里。不过你们还记得我把两具尸体搬来大厅的时候吗？我印象里，那名警察当时并不在这儿。',
        "So, the policeman disappeared and reappeared...? Let's make sure we can't find the other bodies before I go insane. ...Oh wait, look at Naomi's head.": '也就是说，那名警察消失后又出现了……？先确认确实找不到其他尸体吧，免得我发疯。{w}……哦，等等，看 Naomi 的头。',
        "The elevator was in the attic when we left, but I didn't count on the buttons getting reattached. I can think of one escape route. We saw that the call button was there on the second floor. When we were inspecting the offices, perhaps they called the elevator. If it came from the attic, we wouldn't have heard it since we were on the same floor as the elevator. Similarly, if they immediately took it to escape to another floor, we wouldn't have heard that either.": '我们离开的时候，电梯停在阁楼，可我没料到按键会被装回去。我倒是能想到一条逃跑路线。{w}在二楼那会儿，我们看见呼叫按钮还在。我们检查办公室的时候，对方也许叫了电梯。如果它是从阁楼下来的，我们跟电梯在同一层，不会听见动静。{w}同样，如果对方立刻乘电梯逃去了别的楼层，我们也一样听不到。',
        "Wh-What? You're... right.": '什、什么？{w}你说得……没错。',
        "There's nothing. All the buttons are gone. Even the blood is. But I see what you mean. The elevator had to be here with the door open since we arrived, so if the culprit took it on the second floor, they got off here.": '什么都没有。按键全没了，连血迹也没了。{w}不过我明白你的意思。我们到这里时，电梯就已经停在这里，门也开着；那么如果凶手是在二楼搭上电梯的，他们就是在这层下的。',
        "I guess there's one way. The Sekimeiya disappeared from the sheet Isla was carrying, right? And we found it inside the cabinet in the event room. Even if the killer was here, they couldn't have escaped with the Sekimeiya because they would've left the cabinet glass open. I guess it's possible they found it somewhere else, and it teleported to the cabinet after they touched it. That's all I can think.": '我想，倒是有一种可能。{w}Isla 拿着的那张纸上，Sekimeiya 不是消失了吗？后来我们却在活动室的展示柜里找到了它。{w}就算凶手当时就在这层，也没法带着 Sekimeiya 逃出去，因为那样展示柜的玻璃就会是开着的。说不定他是在别处找到它的，一碰到，它就传送回了展示柜。我能想到的只有这些。',
        'I had the chance to go to the security room and saw Atsuki was already there. The time displayed on the BIOS was 15:45, which was five minutes after locking up the Sekimeiya.': '我趁机去了趟监控室，Atsuki 已经在那里了。BIOS 上显示的时间是 {time=15:45}，距离我们锁上 Sekimeiya 已经过了五分钟。',
        'I had the chance to go to the security room and saw Atsuki was already there. The time displayed on the BIOS was 3:45 p.m., which was five minutes after locking up the Sekimeiya.': '我趁机去了趟监控室，Atsuki 已经在那里了。BIOS 上显示的时间是 {time=15:45}，距离我们锁上 Sekimeiya 已经过了五分钟。',
        "Sai and Akaro were in the lobby, avoiding the sight of the blood flowing out of Naomi's head. Atsuki sat on the staircase in hallway C. ...I roamed around the floor a couple of times, and none of those positions changed.": 'Sai 和 Akaro 待在大厅，不去看 Naomi 头部流出的那片血迹。Atsuki 坐在 C走廊的楼梯上。{w}……我在这一层转了两圈，他们谁都没有挪动过位置。',
        "There were five hours left until 21:00, and I'd never been good at waiting around. It didn't seem like anyone had more business with the Sekimeiya or any interest in continuing to argue. While that was the ideal scenario, having to simply wait began to stress me out.": '距离 {time=21} 还有五个小时，而我一向不擅长干等。看来没人再要动 Sekimeiya，也没人想继续争执下去。这本该是最好的局面，可只能干等着，反倒让我越来越烦躁。',
        "There were five hours left until 9 p.m., and I'd never been good at waiting around. It didn't seem like anyone had more business with the Sekimeiya or any interest in continuing to argue. While that was the ideal scenario, having to simply wait began to stress me out.": '距离 {time=21} 还有五个小时，而我一向不擅长干等。看来没人再要动 Sekimeiya，也没人想继续争执下去。这本该是最好的局面，可只能干等着，反倒让我越来越烦躁。',
        '"Are you awake?" It was Atsuki\'s voice.': '「你醒了吗？」{w}是 Atsuki 的声音。',
        'Someone had gone up the ladder. I tried not to mind it and keep sleeping.': '有人顺着梯子爬上去了。{w}我努力不去在意，继续睡。',
        '...Did you do that? Are you Atsuki?': '……{w}是你开的？你是 Atsuki 吗？',
        'I gripped the handle and tried to open the door. It was locked.': '我握住门把手，试着开门。{w}门锁着。',
        'Then, I fell to the floor immediately after appearing.': '{w=1.0}可我刚一现身，便立刻跌倒在地。',
        'When I pressed a key, the three screens lit up, and on the middle one, I saw a message. "{time=10:04}: Camera(s) disabled and associated footage erased".': '我按下一个键，三块屏幕亮了起来，中间那块屏幕上显示出一行字。{w}「{time=10:04}：摄像头已停用，相关录像已删除」。',
        'When I pressed a key, the three screens lit up, and on the middle one, I saw a message.{w} "10:04: Camera(s) disabled and associated footage erased".': '我按下一个键，三块屏幕亮了起来，中间那块屏幕上显示出一行字。{w}「{time=10:04}：摄像头已停用，相关录像已删除」。',
        'When I pressed a key, the three screens lit up, and on the middle one, I saw a message. "10:04: Camera(s) disabled and associated footage erased".': '我按下一个键，三块屏幕亮了起来，中间那块屏幕上显示出一行字。{w}「{time=10:04}：摄像头已停用，相关录像已删除」。',
        'When I pressed a key, the three screens lit up, and on the middle one, I saw a message.{w} "10:04 a.m.: Camera(s) disabled and associated footage erased".': '我按下一个键，三块屏幕亮了起来，中间那块屏幕上显示出一行字。{w}「{time=10:04}：摄像头已停用，相关录像已删除」。',
        'When I pressed a key, the three screens lit up, and on the middle one, I saw a message. "10:04 a.m.: Camera(s) disabled and associated footage erased".': '我按下一个键，三块屏幕亮了起来，中间那块屏幕上显示出一行字。{w}「{time=10:04}：摄像头已停用，相关录像已删除」。',
        '...At 10:04, the recordings were erased...?': '……{time=10:04}，录像被删除了……？',
        '...At 10:04 a.m., the recordings were erased...?': '……{time=10:04}，录像被删除了……？',
        "The screen also showed the time: 18:21. Directly below it was Katei's head—the epicenter of all the blood. It was beyond doubt that he had been killed as well.": '屏幕上还显示着时间：{time=18:21.} 正下方就是 Katei 的头——一切血迹的中心。毫无疑问，他也已经遇害了。',
        "The screen also showed the time: 6:21 p.m. Directly below it was Katei's head—the epicenter of all the blood. It was beyond doubt that he had been killed as well.": '屏幕上还显示着时间：{time=18:21.} 正下方就是 Katei 的头——一切血迹的中心。毫无疑问，他也已经遇害了。',
        "E-Erina...! You scared me. Wh-What's with all that blood? Wait, who am I? {tip=miiya}A-Are you...?{/tip}": 'Erina……！你吓死我了。你、你身上怎么这么多血？{w}等等，我是谁？{tip=miiya}你、你是……？{/tip}',
        "M-Miiya...? My head hurts a lot... I don't remember you.": 'Miiya……？{w}我头很痛……我不记得你。',
        "I reached into the cabinet and picked up the Sekimeiya up without directly touching it. It was considerably cold. I didn't think that touching it would send me far through time, but as it could've made me stay trapped in the building for longer, I decided I wouldn't do it again.": '我把手伸进展示柜，没让皮肤直接碰到 Sekimeiya，把它拿了起来。{w}它相当冰凉。我并不认为碰一下就会把我送到很远的过去，可那样有可能让我被困在这栋楼里更久，所以我决定不再碰它。',
        '...Oh, right...! It can send you to the past.': '……{w}哦，对了……！它能把人送到过去。',
        "...That's not true. You're mistaken. It couldn't have been more than three hours ago.": '……{w}不对。你记错了。最多也就是三个小时前的事。',
        'Wha—!? What are you doing!?': '什——！？{w=0.3}你干什么！？',
        'These keys... Why do you have them? Is this one for the cabi—': '这些钥匙……你怎么会有？{w}这一把是展示柜的——',
        'Atsuki...! Did he see her?': 'Atsuki……！{w}他看到她了吗？',
        "Erina even accused me of not being here previously, so why didn't she say that to her too? She's the one who hasn't been here, and earlier, it sounded like she was locked in the attic. Did the person above me do that? And that still has yet to happen...": 'Erina 刚才还一口咬定我之前不在这里，那她怎么不对那个人也这么说？{w}明明不在场的是她，而且听刚才那番话，她像是被锁在阁楼里。是楼上那个人干的吗？而那件事到现在也还没发生……',
        "...I wish I could explain everything to you, but I still don't really know what happened. But, yes. I'm really glad to see you again.": '……我也希望能把一切都解释给你听，可我自己也还不太清楚发生了什么。{w}不过，没错。能再见到你，我真的很高兴。',
        '...fuck— ...ing here? ...succ— ...plan of—': '……妈的——……在这儿？{w=0.4}……成功——……计划——',
        "For as long as I stayed there, I didn't comprehend anything. I knew I could be found out easily, but I wasn't against that. In fact, I considered opening the door, but I would listen from a distance for as long as I could.": '我在那儿待着的这段时间里，一句话也没听懂。{w}我知道自己很容易被发现，却并不抗拒。我甚至考虑过推门进去，但还是想尽量隔着距离多听一会儿。',
        'Dead...? Are they really talking about me?': '死了……？{w}他们真的在说我吗？',
        "...Wait! Where did it go!? It's not here!": '……等等！它去哪了！？{w} 它不在这里！',
        'Oh... Oh...!': '啊……{w} 啊……！',
        "...! It's closed...! I didn't close it.": '……！{w} 门关上了……！可我没关过啊。',
        '...Then were you above me... in the bedroom?': '……{w}那你刚才是在我楼上的卧室里？',
        'I see. ...It should already be pretty late, but you still have the cabinet key, right?': '这样啊。{w} ……时间应该已经不早了，不过展示柜的钥匙还在你那儿吧？',
        "Would it work like this...? It might. The proof that she's dead doesn't exist anymore.": '会这样奏效吗……？{w}也许吧。能证明她死了的证据，如今已经不存在了。',
        "And at some point, it will happen again. We're supposed to hear the elevator two more times. That means it'll end up in the attic again.": '而且过一会儿，同样的事还会再发生一次。{w}我们还要再听到两次电梯声，也就是说，它最后还是会停在阁楼。',
        "...I don't know. It doesn't make any sense, does it? The flow of time wouldn't work like that. It's impossible. ...Also, he told us to wait safely and get out of the tower. There's no way I'll be able to use the Sekimeiya once we're outside, and that still wouldn't make any sense. Nothing does.": '……{w}我不知道。{w}这根本说不通，不是吗？时间的流动不会是这样的。不可能。{w}……还有，他让我们安心等着，然后离开这座塔。可一旦到了外面，我根本用不了 Sekimeiya，那样也还是说不通。没有一件事说得通。',
        "He's right. But she's on the crystal floor, alongside a third Atsuki. It can't be that the world was changed so that she never died, because that Atsuki was surprised to see her too. One of them was probably who went up to the attic, but what will come out of this? Will different versions of us remain? The other Atsuki didn't make it sound like that.": '他说得没错。可她就在水晶层，身边还有第三个 Atsuki。世界不可能被改写成她从未死过——那个 Atsuki 见到她时，同样一脸惊讶。{w}上楼去阁楼的，多半就是他们当中的一个，可这样又能得出什么结果？我们这些不同的版本会同时留下来吗？另一个 Atsuki 的说法听起来并不是这样。',
        'It had teleported to the attic, so if nothing else happened, the state of the world would stay as it was. But there were so many things to iron out. Three Atsukis existed at once. She had appeared out of nowhere in front of one of them. Not all the disappeared corpses had reappeared alive.': '它传送到了阁楼，所以只要别的什么都没发生，世界的状态就会维持原样。{w}可需要理顺的地方太多了。三个 Atsuki 同时存在；她凭空出现在其中一个面前；消失的尸体也并非全都活着回来了。',
        "Hm? No, I didn't. I'm confused by what you mean. I came down, and it seemed like you weren't there because I couldn't hear you. I did turn on the light to confirm it, but you were already gone. Is that what you meant?": '嗯？没有。你这么说我倒糊涂了。{w}我下楼的时候听不到你的声音，以为你不在。我确实开灯确认过，可你已经走了。你问的是这个吗？',
        '...Yes, sorry. I thought someone might have turned it on after you came.': '……{w}对，抱歉。我以为你下来之后，有人开过灯。',
        "I don't even know if turning off the light in the upper bedroom would've turned it off where I was anyway. This doesn't make any sense...!": '我甚至不确定，关掉楼上卧室的灯，会不会也把我那边的灯关掉。{w}这根本说不通……！',
        'Wait... ...Is it not here?': '等等……{w}……不在这里？',
        'Wait, no. I bet I know what happened.': '等等，不对。{w}我想我知道是怎么回事了。',
        "Holy shit, man. Will this attitude stop? Why were you waiting here? You knew we'd go up, right? Was your idea to make us chase you to then touch the Sekimeiya and wait here to sneak back down?": '我靠，你这副态度有完没完？{w} 你守在这儿做什么？你早知道我们要上去吧？你是想引我们追过来，自己碰一下 Sekimeiya，然后守在这儿，好偷偷溜下去？',
        "Me...? I don't even know what you're talking about.": '我……？{w} 我根本不知道你在说什么。',
        "...What? I'm being serious. I have absolutely no idea what you're talking about. What girl?": '……什么？{w} 我是认真的。我完全不知道你在说什么。什么女孩？',
        '...Answer me. What girl?': '……{w} 回答我。什么女孩？',
        '...Hm. ...Shiroya, right?': '……嗯。{w} ……Shiroya，对吧？',
        "...We should put the Sekimeiya in the cabinet and stay on the crystal floor. That's what we were told.": '……{w}照之前说的，我们得把 Sekimeiya 放进展示柜，待在水晶层。',
        'We ran behind Akaro. I looked down and saw that there was still no blood on the floor or the staircase.': '我们跟在 Akaro 后面跑。{w} 我低头看去，地板和楼梯上依旧没有血迹。',
        "...I don't know. I can't just assume you're lying after all that's happened.": '……我不知道。{w} 出了这么多事，我也不能就这么认定你在说谎。',
        'Wait, is that it...? Could it be that they were genuinely brought back to life? But, no... If another version of me existed, it must be something completely different.': '等等，难道说……？难不成她们是真的死而复生了？{w} 不对……如果真有另一个我，那一定完全是另一回事。',
        "...That's what happened. Did you really not find anyone? Aren't you the one who says that I took the elevator up?": '……事情就是这样。{w} 你真的一个人都没找到？不是你说我乘电梯上去了吗？',
        "Yes. I'm only one person, though, so I couldn't really search optimally. But it is possible there was nobody to find if the three people who should've been there merely traveled with the Sekimeiya, which, again, you happened to have.": '没错。可我只有一个人，没法搜得面面俱到。{w} 不过，要是本该在那里的三个人只是带着 Sekimeiya 走了——而它偏偏又在你手里——那找不到人也说得通。',
        "...I'm accusing you of trying to execute a plan that might involve getting the Sekimeiya out of the tower. Of lying openly, and of working with that girl you know who didn't get trapped with us.": '……{w} 我是在指责你：你想执行一个把 Sekimeiya 弄出塔的计划；你公然撒谎；还跟那个你认识、但没跟我们困在一起的女孩串通。',
        "...I'm sorry, but I can't really take you seriously. I woke up a few minutes ago and have no idea what any of this is about. Since Akaro is backing you up, I guess it's true that the two missing bodies reappeared, but it seems they're gone again, right? Erina is with Isla two rooms over, and she looks totally okay. Also, I already said that I don't want to take the Sekimeiya out of here again.": '……抱歉，我实在没法把你的话当真。我几分钟前才醒过来，根本不知道这些事是怎么回事。既然 Akaro 也站在你那边，那两具消失的尸体确实重新出现过，我承认；可她们似乎又不见了，对吧？Erina 就在隔了两个房间的地方和 Isla 待着，看上去一点事都没有。{w} 再说，我已经说过，我不想再把它带出去了。',
        "However, if it's true that I was here and said things that didn't make sense... You're right, I know that girl, Shiroya. She's an old friend of mine who... died two weeks ago. I don't have any idea why she was here today or how that's possible.": '不过，如果我当时真在这里，还说了些莫名其妙的话……{w}你说得对，我认识那个女孩，Shiroya。她是我的老朋友，两周前……去世了。我不知道她今天为什么会出现在这里，也不知道这怎么可能。',
        "It's currently 19:32. There's no need to search for them, but don't worry—they'll be found as soon as the police enter the building. If you really do want that, you're not opposed, right?": '现在是{time=19:32.} 没必要去找她们，不过你放心——警察一进大楼，她们就会被找到。如果你真的希望那样，应该也不会反对吧？',
        "It's currently 7:32 p.m. There's no need to search for them, but don't worry—they'll be found as soon as the police enter the building. If you really do want that, you're not opposed, right?": '现在是{time=19:32.} 没必要去找她们，不过你放心——警察一进大楼，她们就会被找到。如果你真的希望那样，应该也不会反对吧？',
        "...! I still think we should find them because I want to understand what happened. If we find them, you'll believe all that I'm saying.": '……！{w}我还是觉得应该去找她们，因为我想弄明白到底发生了什么。找到她们，你就会相信我说的一切了。',
        "I see. Then we'll go ahead and believe it after 21:00, when two versions of you are found.": '是吗。那就等{time=21}，等找到两个你之后，我们再相信。',
        "I see. Then we'll go ahead and believe it after 9 p.m., when two versions of you are found.": '是吗。那就等{time=21}，等找到两个你之后，我们再相信。',
        "However, 21:00 kept approaching at a steady pace, and nobody seemed against that. I wanted to get rid of the note in my purse, but I couldn't go to the bathroom to flush it away. When no one was looking at me, I stuffed it inside one of my shoes. The police would probably search us after we left, so my purse wasn't a good place to hide it.": '然而{time=21}仍在稳步逼近，似乎没有人反对。我想处理掉包里的那张纸条，却不能去洗手间把它冲掉。趁没人注意我，我把它塞进了一只鞋里。离开之后警察多半会搜身，放在包里并不稳妥。',
        "However, 9 p.m. kept approaching at a steady pace, and nobody seemed against that. I wanted to get rid of the note in my purse, but I couldn't go to the bathroom to flush it away. When no one was looking at me, I stuffed it inside one of my shoes. The police would probably search us after we left, so my purse wasn't a good place to hide it.": '然而{time=21}仍在稳步逼近，似乎没有人反对。我想处理掉包里的那张纸条，却不能去洗手间把它冲掉。趁没人注意我，我把它塞进了一只鞋里。离开之后警察多半会搜身，放在包里并不稳妥。',
        "Sai's voice didn't reach Miiya, who had disappeared to the second floor. Everyone ran behind her, hesitant to go up, as her goal could've been to lure them away. Meanwhile, Atsuki was lost and began to feel a despicable anxiety building up. Why was Miiya objecting to the only thing they had to do?": 'Miiya 已经跑上二楼不见踪影，Sai 的喊声没能传到她耳中。众人跟着追了过去，却迟迟不敢上楼——她说不定就是想把他们引开。{w} 另一边，Atsuki 茫然无措，心底渐渐涌起一股令自己都感到卑劣的焦躁。那明明是唯一该做的事，Miiya 为什么要反对？',
        "In hallway C, Miiya's. On the first staircase, Katei's. Close to them, thrown on the floor, was a screwdriver covered in more than one person's blood.": 'C走廊里躺着 Miiya 的尸体。{w}第一段楼梯上躺着 Katei 的尸体。{w}在他们附近，地板上扔着一把螺丝刀，沾着不止一个人的血。',
        "All of them were dead. In addition, it was confirmed that all of them had died instantly. That meant that they couldn't have killed each other. However, the police raided the whole building and didn't find anyone else.": '所有人都死了。而且，经确认所有人都是当场死亡。这意味着他们不可能互相残杀。{w}然而，警方搜遍了整栋楼，没有发现其他人。',
        'It was 20:00. The unbelievable day was coming to an end, but there was still something we were missing.': '已经是 {time=20.}。这难以置信的一天即将结束，可我们还有件事没弄明白。',
        'It was 8 p.m. The unbelievable day was coming to an end, but there was still something we were missing.': '已经是 {time=20.}。这难以置信的一天即将结束，可我们还有件事没弄明白。',
        "...It's 20:33.": '……现在是 {time=20:33.}',
        "...It's 8:33 p.m.": '……现在是 {time=20:33.}',
        '...Akaro, do you remember Erina? Do you think she had all her buttons?': '……{w}Akaro，你还记得 Erina 吗？你觉得她当时脑子还正常吗？',
        "...I didn't lie about anything.": '……{w}我没有说过一句谎。',
        '...I suppose.': '……{w}说得也是。',
        "Y-You...! You're a murderer! And you! ...You're behind this attack!": '你、你……！你是凶手！{w}还有你！……这场袭击是你策划的！',
        "Suripo was indecisive. If Vaisude had known about Xyn's attack, why had he only warned them that it would occur? He hadn't accomplished anything, as it had already been a well-known possibility. And even if he'd been involved with Xyn in some way, the same question had to be asked.": 'Suripo 犹豫不决。如果 Vaisude 早就知道 Xyn 会发动袭击，为什么他只是警告说袭击会发生？这毫无用处，因为那本来就是大家都知道可能发生的事。{w} 就算他与 Xyn 有什么牵连，同样的问题还是得问。',
        'Confident that those questions would be answered in the future, Suripo walked back to the shutter to continue waiting for 21:04, when the entrance would open.': 'Suripo 相信这些问题日后总有答案，便走回卷帘门前，继续等待 {time=21:04}，到那时入口就会开启。',
        'Confident that those questions would be answered in the future, Suripo walked back to the shutter to continue waiting for 9:04 p.m., when the entrance would open.': 'Suripo 相信这些问题日后总有答案，便走回卷帘门前，继续等待 {time=21:04}，到那时入口就会开启。',
        "Lei wasn't a blood relative of Ashiya, but she'd been sent as their representative, speaking on their behalf, and had been giving the police any essential information. From the get-go, she had stated that the process of stealing the Sekimeiya was underway despite Ashiya's public declarations, which were that Xyn's plan had immediately failed.": 'Lei 并非芦屋家的血亲，但她是作为芦屋家的代表被派来的，替他们发言，也一直向警方提供必要的信息。{w} 她从一开始就说，盗取 Sekimeiya 的行动已经展开——尽管芦屋对外宣称 Xyn 的计划当场就被挫败了。',
        "It was almost 21:00, and the winter sky had long ago darkened, bringing a sheer cold to everyone who'd kept waiting to witness the resolution of a long day.": '时间将近 {time=21}，冬日的天色早已黑透，彻骨的寒意笼罩着每一个仍在等着看这漫长一天如何收场的人。',
        "It was almost 9 p.m., and the winter sky had long ago darkened, bringing a sheer cold to everyone who'd kept waiting to witness the resolution of a long day.": '时间将近 {time=21}，冬日的天色早已黑透，彻骨的寒意笼罩着每一个仍在等着看这漫长一天如何收场的人。',
        '21:00 came. The crowd was kept back by the group of policemen in front of the tower, but even the officials were partially curious how the shutter would withdraw.': '{time=21} 到了。塔前的一队警察拦住了人群，可就连这些警员也多少有些好奇：那卷帘门究竟会怎么收起。',
        '9 p.m. came. The crowd was kept back by the group of policemen in front of the tower, but even the officials were partially curious how the shutter would withdraw.': '{time=21} 到了。塔前的一队警察拦住了人群，可就连这些警员也多少有些好奇：那卷帘门究竟会怎么收起。',
        'There were only a few seconds left. Nobody knew the exact time the shutter had closed, but they had determined it had been right about 9:04.': '只剩最后几秒。没人知道卷帘门关闭的确切时刻，但推算下来，大约就在 {time=9:04.}',
        'There were only a few seconds left. Nobody knew the exact time the shutter had closed, but they had determined it had been right about 9:04 a.m.': '只剩最后几秒。没人知道卷帘门关闭的确切时刻，但推算下来，大约就在 {time=9:04.}',
        "Twelve hours earlier, unidentified smoke had been released on the first floor of the tower. Right away, the possibility of it being poisonous had been presented. However, they'd abandoned it as soon as the safety of the trapped individuals had been confirmed less than an hour later. Nonetheless, they'd prepared equipment such as masks just to be careful.": '十二小时前，塔的一层曾释放出不明烟雾，当时立刻有人提出它可能有毒。{w} 然而，不到一小时后被困者的安全得到确认，这个可能性便被搁置了。尽管如此，为稳妥起见，他们还是备好了口罩之类的装备。',
        "One man confirmed that the mechanical room was barren and rushed back up to enter hallway B, its walls nearly as dark. There, an old friend of his frantically tried to find the people who should've been trapped inside. A great deal of blood was on the floor toward the end of the hallway, which only compounded the officers' uneasiness.": '一名警员确认机械室里空无一物，便急忙折回，进入 B走廊，墙壁几乎同样漆黑。{w} 那里，他的一位老友正拼命寻找本该被困在里面的人。走廊尽头的地面上有大片血迹，令警员们越发不安。',
        "In the opposite hallway was a longer trail of blood. The security room was the first place to be opened, so they didn't have to wait long to have their fears confirmed. Then, in a deeper room, they saw an even more wretched nightmare.": '对面的走廊上，血迹拖得更长。监控室是最先被打开的房间，因此他们的恐惧没过多久便得到证实。{w} 随后，在更深处的一间房里，他们看见了更加凄惨的噩梦。',
        'They walked up the first staircase and saw a person standing there. It was a girl with blue hair who looked a little disoriented.': '他们走上第一段楼梯，看见那里站着一个人。{w} 是个蓝头发的女孩，神情有些恍惚。',
        '"...Are you okay?" Suripo asked. The girl nodded faintly and looked away from him.': '「……你还好吗？」Suripo 问道。{w} 女孩轻轻点了点头，随即将视线移开。',
        "Suripo remembered the voice of the child he'd heard at the start of that long day after looking at her face. The pictures also encompassed all the blood found in the hallways and elevator. Two of the bodies had the same face and clothing, which was incredibly odd, as nothing like that had been mentioned during the brief period of communication with those inside.": '看到她的脸，Suripo 想起了漫长的一天开始时听到的那个孩子的声音。照片里也拍下了走廊和电梯中所有的血迹。{w} 其中两具尸体面容与衣着完全相同，这怪异得离谱——先前与楼内的人短暂联络时，谁也没提过这样的事。',
        "These bodies must be taken out. We don't know what happened or what this gas is, but it's in the entire building. A proper investigation might not be able to occur for a while with these circumstances. However, the security cameras have been recording since this all started. Save all the footage to a drive.": '这些尸体必须搬出来。我们既不知道发生了什么，也不知道这气体究竟是什么，可它弥漫了整栋楼。这样的情况之下，正式调查恐怕一时半会儿没法展开。{w} 不过，从事情开始到现在，监控一直在录。把所有录像都存进硬盘。',
        "I need to say it. I've always wanted to, and I can't believe I never will. I love you.": '我必须说出来。{w} 我一直都想说，却怎么也没料到，最后竟再没有机会。{w} 我爱你。',
        "She didn't know the exact time, but her job hadn't ended yet. She stepped up to her own shoulders and grabbed them. After lifting herself, she began to back up.": '她不知道确切的时间，但自己的任务还没有结束。{w} 她走上前，抓住另一个自己的双肩。扶起对方之后，她开始向后退去。',
        'There was no time to react. During the instants before the light came back on, the girl closed her eyes and attempted to cover her face with her arms.': '已经来不及反应。{w} 在灯光重新亮起前的那几瞬，女孩闭上眼，试图用双臂护住脸。',
        "But reality had hit me way harder just the next day. I'd finally decided on something, and it was rejected. Why had Miiya died? It wasn't fair. The three of us were so happy that day, so why had it been Miiya's last?": '可现实在第二天就给了我更沉重的一击。我好不容易做出了决定，却被生生驳回。{w} Miiya 为什么会死？这不公平。那天我们三个人那么开心，为什么那偏偏成了 Miiya 的最后一天？',
        "It's all right. Thank you. Let's continue, though. I was the one who wanted to come.": '没事的。谢谢你。{w}不过，我们继续走吧。当初想来的那个人是我。',
        "And that was what we'd most needed. We hadn't talked about anything because we didn't have the strength to say what we wanted. The situation we ended up in forced us to talk to each other again. When I noticed that we were speaking normally, I was grateful that coming to the tower had given us what we'd been looking for.": '而这正是我们最需要的。之前我们什么都没谈，是因为连说出心里话的力气都没有。我们最终陷入的处境逼得我们又说起话来。{w} 当我发觉我们像平常一样交谈时，不禁心生感激：来到这座塔，竟让我们得到了苦苦寻求的东西。',
        "Trapped with us was a killer—a person who'd produced the same pain we'd felt before. There had to be justice for Naomi, but we were unable to figure out the truth behind her death.": '与我们一同被困的还有一名凶手——一个曾让我们体会过同样痛苦的人。{w} 必须为 Naomi 讨回公道，可我们却查不出她死亡的真相。',
        "And soon, we came across the bathrooms on the lowest floor. Inside the men's was Naomi's body. Not the one we'd already found, but a different one. That confirmed what we'd all already imagined: in the tower with us, while the world couldn't see it, something beyond the bounds of possibility was taking place.": '不久，我们来到了最底层的洗手间。男洗手间里躺着 Naomi 的尸体。{w} 不是我们已经发现的那一具，而是另一具。这证实了我们所有人早已隐约想到的事：就在这座塔里，在我们身边，正发生着某种超乎常理的事，而外界对此一无所知。',
        "Through an exhausting chase, we heard the voice of our attacker. It was Sai, one of the people who'd been with us since that morning. What had we done to be chased with a knife? His voice conveyed that attempting to ask that would be fatal.": '一场追逐耗尽了我们力气，我们也听清了追来者的声音——是 Sai，从那天早上起就一直和我们同行的人之一。{w} 我们究竟做了什么，竟招来持刀追杀？他的语气明明白白告诉我们：这话一旦问出口，就是死路一条。',
        "In front of me was Sai. Both of us had appeared in the right-hand bedroom of the attic. When Sai's eyes met mine, he raised his eyebrows, hesitant to move.": '站在我面前的是 Sai。我们两人都出现在了阁楼右侧的卧室里。{w} Sai 与我目光相接，眉头一挑，迟迟没有动作。',
        "That sent a chill through my body. He really had tried to kill Atsuki, and he was willing to kill me. What we wanted was to leave the building safely, and by keeping Sai locked away, I'd intended to prevent more things from happening. ...I began to worry about my decision.": '我浑身一凉。他真的对 Atsuki 动过杀心，也真的愿意杀我。{w}我们只想安全离开这栋楼，我把 Sai 关起来，本是为了防止再出别的事。……想到这里，我开始怀疑自己的决定。',
        "You remember what I said, right? You will die—that's a guarantee. Because I pretty much know it for a fact, I'm wondering whether I should make it happen myself. Since I have confirmation of your death, it's very likely that if I try to push you into a wall, I'll kill you. I have no reason to think I'll end up safe, though. That knife you have is pretty scary, and I wouldn't want to be recorded.": '你还记得我说过的话吧？你会死——这是板上钉钉的事。我几乎可以肯定这一点，所以在想，要不要亲手让它成真。{w}既然我已经知道你会死，那只要我把你往墙上一推，很可能就真能要了你的命。不过我也没理由认为自己会平安无事。你手里那把刀挺吓人的，而且我不想被录下来。',
        "Then we go back to what I already said. I know what I'm saying for certain, but the details of it are a mystery to me. I do feel bad for you. You were in a coma for a while, right? If I remember correctly, the name that was put out was yours. It's unfortunate that you'll die here after surviving that.": '那就回到我刚才说的。我很确定自己在说什么，可细节对我来说仍是个谜。{w}我确实有点同情你。你昏迷过一阵子吧？如果我没记错，当时对外公布的名单上写的是你的名字。好不容易挺过来，却要死在这里，实在可惜。',
        "I couldn't decide. It was very possible that the force behind most of what had happened throughout the day was Sai. There wasn't a lot of time left until 21:00, and if I could seclude him during that last stretch, we had the chance to leave safely.": '我拿不定主意。这一天里大半的事，背后很可能都是 Sai 在推动。离 {time=21} 已经不远，只要最后这段时间能把他隔离起来，我们就有机会平安离开。',
        "I couldn't decide. It was very possible that the force behind most of what had happened throughout the day was Sai. There wasn't a lot of time left until 9 p.m., and if I could seclude him during that last stretch, we had the chance to leave safely.": '我拿不定主意。这一天里大半的事，背后很可能都是 Sai 在推动。离 {time=21} 已经不远，只要最后这段时间能把他隔离起来，我们就有机会平安离开。',
        "If he's been lying recently... Why would he say that I'll die or that the blood in the lobby is mine? That's impossible. That blood can't be mine, so why would he say it? It matches with the recording because I wasn't mentioned once in it. Could it be that he's consistently trying follow a story that he's set up?": '如果他最近一直在撒谎……那他为什么说我会死，说大厅里的血是我的？这不可能。那血不可能是我的，他为什么要这么说？{w}这一点倒是和录音对得上——录音里一次都没提到我。难道他一直在照着自己编好的剧本走？',
        "I can't decide. ...Because if Sai isn't the culprit, then it's Akaro, who could be anywhere, and then Atsuki would be up against him alone. Both Akaro and Sai have acted suspicious in their own ways, and Sai sounded hostile toward him earlier. ...But that could easily be a trick since they escaped the bedroom together.": '我下不了决心。……因为如果凶手不是 Sai，那就是 Akaro；他可能在任何地方，而 Atsuki 就得独自面对他。{w}Akaro 和 Sai 各有各的可疑之处，Sai 之前对他也挺敌视的。……可他们是一起逃出卧室的，那点敌意很可能只是演戏。',
        "...I won't move.": '……{w}我不会走的。',
        "You shouldn't try it. Also, I don't think the cameras are recording.": '你最好别试。{w}再说，我看那些摄像头根本没在录。',
        '...Is this how you and Akaro escaped the bedroom the last time? That was what Atsuki suspected.': '……{w}上次你和 Akaro 就是这么从卧室逃出去的？Atsuki 是这么怀疑的。',
        "...You remember what you asked earlier, right? Yes, if you get close to me again, I will use the knife. Don't move again.": '……{w}你还记得刚才问过我什么吧？对，你要是再靠近我，我就用刀。别再动了。',
        "He repositioned his face on the pillow and closed his eyes. ...A couple of minutes later, he hadn't moved at all.": '他把脸在枕头上挪了挪，闭上眼睛。{w}……好几分钟过去了，他纹丝不动。',
        'There was no response. The attic felt just as desolate as when Sai had been there. I noticed that I still had the knife in my hand. I slid it through the gap of the door, trying to push open the latch.': '没有回应。阁楼和 Sai 在时一样冷清。{w}我这才发觉手里还握着刀，便把它从门缝里探进去，想顶开门闩。',
        "Did I really travel to this goddamn bedroom? That's just unfortunate. What's with that look? You're still here? How long has it been? ...I guess I just trapped myself.": '我还真穿越到这种鬼卧室来了？真是倒霉透顶。{w}你那是什么表情？你还在这儿？过了多久了？……看来我是把自己给困住了。',
        '...The key? No. Answer my question. How long has it been since I left?': '……钥匙？没有。{w}先回答我。我离开之后过了多久？',
        "Don't you get that it's impossible I still have the key? It's like you said a while ago. I just appeared in the middle of this bedroom, looking at the door. Obviously, that coordinate is from the time you were in front of the door, pointing the knife at me. At that point, I didn't have the key yet.": '你还不明白吗，我不可能还拿着那把钥匙。就像你刚才说的。{w}我一出现就在这间卧室中央，面朝门口。显然，那个坐标对应的是你站在门口拿刀指着我的时候。那时候我还没拿到钥匙。',
        "That's the key to the other bedroom. Take your hand out of the pocket.": '那是另一间卧室的钥匙。{w}把手从口袋里拿出来。',
        'Hesitantly, he did so. One last key remained inside.': '他犹豫着照做了。{w}里面还剩最后一把钥匙。',
        "Yeah, I also have the attic key, but I guess that doesn't matter much to you. Are you happy now? Do you think I might have it in my hair? It's pretty messy today. Maybe in one of my shoes? Don't worry, I left it up top.": '没错，阁楼的钥匙也在我这儿，不过这对你大概没什么意义吧。{w}现在满意了？你觉得我会把钥匙藏在头发里？我今天头发确实挺乱的。说不定在鞋里？{w}放心，我把它留在上面了。',
        "...You're lying.": '……{w}你在骗人。',
        "When he appeared in the middle of the bedroom... Of course, he even said it. That location belonged to the time I'd been blocking his path to the door. That's how he escaped the first time. At that point, the key to the bedroom was already in his pocket, which is why he had it when he appeared from the future. Atsuki said it too, that he grabbed it when he was chasing us. But, for some reason, there was another key in the drawer. At some point, the key got duplicated.": '他出现在卧室中央的时候……对，他自己也说过。{w}那个坐标对应的，是我挡住他去路、不让他靠近门口的那段时间。{w}他第一次就是这样逃出去的。那时卧室的钥匙已经在他口袋里，所以他从未来出现时才会带着钥匙。Atsuki 也说过，他追我们的时候把钥匙抢走了。{w}可是不知为何，抽屉里还有另一把钥匙。就在某个时刻，钥匙变成了两把。',
        "I couldn't look at Sai anymore. No matter whether he was the person behind everything, I hated him and the unquestionable malice behind his actions. However, 21:00 was very close, and creating more conflicts would only be a problem.": '我再也无法直视 Sai。不管他是不是这一切的幕后之人，我都厌恶他，也厌恶他所作所为背后那份不容置疑的恶意。可距离 {time=21} 已经很近了，再起冲突只会徒增麻烦。',
        "I couldn't look at Sai anymore. No matter whether he was the person behind everything, I hated him and the unquestionable malice behind his actions. However, 9 p.m. was very close, and creating more conflicts would only be a problem.": '我再也无法直视 Sai。不管他是不是这一切的幕后之人，我都厌恶他，也厌恶他所作所为背后那份不容置疑的恶意。可距离 {time=21} 已经很近了，再起冲突只会徒增麻烦。',
        "I... see. We didn't check Erina's pulse, remember...?": '原来……如此。{w}我们当时没确认 Erina 的脉搏，你还记得吧……？',
        "It's possible what I changed only affected some people. I definitely went back in time and altered the events I'd experienced. Sai recognizes the change, but I'm not sure Erina does. It felt like both realities met, leading into differing memories. That could be what happened to Akaro, when his version of events contradicted ours. Maybe someone made some change that didn't affect us, or maybe it didn't affect Akaro.": '我的改动也许只影响了部分人。我确实回到了过去，改动了我们经历过的事。Sai 记得这个变化，Erina 却未必。{w} 感觉就像两个现实交汇在一起，记忆也随之分岔。Akaro 那时大概也是这样——他记忆中的经过和我们不一样。也许有人做了某种改变，却没有波及我们，也可能只是没有波及 Akaro。',
        "Let's keep going. I last traveled from the staff room. Let's go there.": '继续走吧。{w} 我上一次是从员工室穿越的。就去那儿。',
        "You're free to enlighten me. If I knew where it was, what would my endgame be? Hoping the police don't find it? There's no way that would happen. Someone took it when we weren't around. That must mean they have the means to keep it out of ours and the police's sights. Otherwise, hiding it is pointless.": '那就请你说给我听听。要是我知道它在哪儿，我图的是什么？指望警察找不到？那根本不可能。{w} 有人趁我们不在的时候把它拿走了。这说明对方有办法让它既躲过我们，也躲过警察。否则，藏起来毫无意义。',
        "...Atsuki wanted to find the Sekimeiya and change the past. If I told him, I knew he would activate it. However, I wasn't sure I wanted that.": '……{w}Atsuki 想找到 Sekimeiya，改变过去。我若告诉他，他一定会启动它。可我并不确定自己是否想这样。',
        '—Wha— ...Ow. Where... is this?': '——什——{w=1} ……好痛。{w=0.8} 这里……是哪儿？',
        'It was my phone. The time displayed was 21:10, but I only wanted to look at the date. I navigated deeper into the settings menu to access the current date. Then, I stared at the screen, reading it over and over.': '是我的手机。屏幕上的时间显示为 {time=21:10}，但我只想看日期。我往设置菜单更深处翻，找出当前日期，然后盯着屏幕，一遍又一遍地看。',
        'It was my phone. The time displayed was 9:10 p.m., but I only wanted to look at the date. I navigated deeper into the settings menu to access the current date. Then, I stared at the screen, reading it over and over.': '是我的手机。屏幕上的时间显示为 {time=21:10}，但我只想看日期。我往设置菜单更深处翻，找出当前日期，然后盯着屏幕，一遍又一遍地看。',
        'My senses dulled—the world darkened—my coat tightly enveloped me— And then it was gone. The cold and pain disappeared too, leaving me floating in the middle of nowhere.': '我的感官渐渐迟钝——世界暗了下去——外套紧紧裹住我——{w} 然后，那一切都消失了。{w} 寒冷与疼痛也一并退去，只剩我漂浮在虚无之中。',
        "That's... me. ...And there's Atsuki. Not from now, but when we were still children. Laughing. Playing. Having fun.": '那是我……{w} ……还有 Atsuki。{w} 不是现在，而是我们还小的时候。笑着，玩着，那么开心。',
        "He took the flower off the toy and began fidgeting with my shirt. When he was done, I couldn't help but smile.": '他把花从玩偶头上取下来，在我衣襟上摆弄起来。{w} 等他弄完，我忍不住笑了。',
        'Seamlessly, the world changed. We were riding on our bikes down the streets of Yushibana. ...And then we were drinking hot chocolate after playing in the snow. One after another, fond memories played in my vision, and I once again became a child.': '世界悄然变换，衔接得毫无痕迹。我们骑着自行车，穿行在丰花的街道上。{w} ……转眼间，又变成我们玩过雪后一起喝着热巧克力。那些温暖的回忆一幕接一幕在眼前浮现，我又变回了孩子。',
        "...Miiya. I liked her as a friend, but... When did it get so complicated? She was gone. But even when she was alive, things didn't feel completely right. Myriad moments of before her death flowed into my mind. We were smiling and laughing in all of them, but as I watched us from above, I just wondered if she'd ever actually considered me a friend. We had spent time together, but I wasn't sure what it had meant.": '……Miiya。{w} 我对她的喜欢，是朋友之间的那种，可是……{w} 事情是什么时候变得这么复杂的？{w} 她已经不在了。可就算她活着的时候，一切也并非全然对劲。她生前的无数瞬间涌入脑海。每一个瞬间里，我们都在笑；可当我从上方望着我们时，我只想知道，她究竟有没有真正把我当成朋友。我们曾一起度过许多时光，可那究竟意味着什么，我并不确定。',
        'We had access to a time travel device. We had no idea how it worked, but could we use it to rescue her? Did I... even want to rescue her?': '我们手上有时间穿越装置。我们完全不知道它如何运作，但能不能用它救她？{w} 我……真的想救她吗？',
        'The sensation of possessing a body gradually came back to me. My limbs existed again. In an instant, I became acutely aware of a pain in my cheek. I was resting on a pebble.': '拥有身体的感觉渐渐回来了。我的四肢重新有了实感。{w} 刹那间，我清楚地感到脸颊一阵疼痛——原来我正压在一颗小石子上。',
        "I exhaled deeply, pulling myself together. That dream, if it could be called that, was almost like the coma I'd been in once already, a haze of half-concepts. It was almost frightening how lost I'd gotten in it. I remembered fragments of it, but the question of whether I wanted to save Miiya was still vividly present in my mind.": '我深深呼出一口气，让自己镇定下来。那场梦——如果那也能叫梦的话——几乎像我此前经历过的那次昏迷，是一团由半成形念头组成的迷雾。我在其中迷失得如此之深，事后想来几乎有些后怕。{w} 我只记得一些碎片，但「我是否想救 Miiya」这个问题，仍鲜明地留在脑海中。',
        'I rested for a bit longer, trying to drive off those intrusive thoughts, until I was eventually able to sit up. I was still lost in the dark, so I pulled out my phone and looked at the time. It was 21:34.': '我又歇了一会儿，试图驱散那些侵入脑中的念头，直到终于能坐起身。四周仍是一片黑暗，我辨不清方向，只好掏出手机看时间。屏幕上显示 {time=21:34.}。',
        'I rested for a bit longer, trying to drive off those intrusive thoughts, until I was eventually able to sit up. I was still lost in the dark, so I pulled out my phone and looked at the time. It was 9:34 p.m.': '我又歇了一会儿，试图驱散那些侵入脑中的念头，直到终于能坐起身。四周仍是一片黑暗，我辨不清方向，只好掏出手机看时间。屏幕上显示 {time=21:34.}。',
        "...The darkness had become absolute. On that day, the Sekimeiya must've been somewhere. As Ashiya's announcement had already been made public, they were probably keeping it somewhere in the tower.": '……{w}黑暗已彻底吞没了一切。那一天，Sekimeiya 一定就在某处。既然芦屋的声明早已公开，他们多半把它存放在塔内的某个地方。',
        "These belong to my apartment. They're not Atsuki's. ...The tickets aren't here either.": '这些是我公寓的钥匙，不是 Atsuki 的。{w}……门票也不在。',
        "My phone showed 21:48, and I was behind my school, where I'd rarely ever been at such a time.": '手机显示{time=21:48}，我正站在学校后面——这个时间，我几乎从未来过这里。',
        "My phone showed 9:48 p.m., and I was behind my school, where I'd rarely ever been at such a time.": '手机显示{time=21:48}，我正站在学校后面——这个时间，我几乎从未来过这里。',
        "But then what? Should I try to make us not go to the tower? How would I attempt to prevent the attack from happening? Even if Atsuki and I don't go, there are people who will die. And in both cases, I'm giving up on going to the past again to save Miiya. If the past can be changed, I can't just leave her to die.": '可那之后呢？难不成要设法让我们别去那座塔？我又要怎么阻止那场袭击？就算我和 Atsuki 不去，也还是会有人死。{w} 无论走哪条路，我都等于放弃再次回到过去救 Miiya。既然过去可以改变，我就不能眼睁睁看着她死去。',
        "But this is still really scary. At the time I change the past, I'll be stuck in a world with another self of mine, and I won't be the original. The me that Atsuki saw in the event room... will it really be me? Will I decide that I don't want to change the past just so that I keep living in a world where I'm the only version of myself? I wouldn't do that, would I?": '可这仍然叫人心惊。等我改变过去的那一刻，我就会被困在一个还有另一个自己的世界里，不再是原来的那一个。{w} Atsuki 在活动室看到的那个我……真的会是我吗？我会不会为了继续待在一个只有我这个版本的世界里，就决定不去改变过去？我不会做出这种事吧？',
        "It was the same modest apartment I'd always lived in, but it seemed like I'd last been there a very long time in the past. I'd left a trail of slick, snowy footprints, so I went to the entrance and dropped my boots beside the door.": '这还是我住惯的那间朴素公寓，可上一次待在这里，仿佛已是极为遥远的过去了。{w} 我留下一串湿滑的雪脚印，于是回到玄关，把靴子脱在门边。',
        'I sat up and looked at my phone. It was {time=1:06.} When I looked behind me, I saw the large screen of glass turning orange momentarily, reflecting the distant light.': '我坐起身，看了眼手机。时间是{time=1:06.}{w}回头望去，只见那面巨大的玻璃屏一瞬间染上橘色，映着远方的光。',
        'I sat up and looked at my phone. It was 1:06.{w} When I looked behind me, I saw the large screen of glass turning orange momentarily, reflecting the distant light.': '我坐起身，看了眼手机。时间是{time=1:06.}{w}回头望去，只见那面巨大的玻璃屏一瞬间染上橘色，映着远方的光。',
        'I sat up and looked at my phone. It was 1:06. When I looked behind me, I saw the large screen of glass turning orange momentarily, reflecting the distant light.': '我坐起身，看了眼手机。时间是{time=1:06.}{w}回头望去，只见那面巨大的玻璃屏一瞬间染上橘色，映着远方的光。',
        'I sat up and looked at my phone. It was 1:06 a.m.{w} When I looked behind me, I saw the large screen of glass turning orange momentarily, reflecting the distant light.': '我坐起身，看了眼手机。时间是{time=1:06.}{w}回头望去，只见那面巨大的玻璃屏一瞬间染上橘色，映着远方的光。',
        'I sat up and looked at my phone. It was 1:06 a.m. When I looked behind me, I saw the large screen of glass turning orange momentarily, reflecting the distant light.': '我坐起身，看了眼手机。时间是{time=1:06.}{w}回头望去，只见那面巨大的玻璃屏一瞬间染上橘色，映着远方的光。',
        "The first day of December... Miiya's not here anymore, I'm in the hospital, and Atsuki's probably at his house. Or, I guess I'm actually in my bed.": '十二月一号……{w}Miiya 已经不在了，我在医院，Atsuki 大概在他家。{w}不对，我现在其实躺在自己床上。',
        "Out of nowhere, I realized I'd been lying in bed for a while without doing anything. ...It had happened so quickly. It felt like just minutes ago I'd been waiting with everyone in the lobby.": '不知怎的，我忽然发觉自己已经躺了好一阵，什么都没做。{w}……事情发生得太快了。仿佛几分钟前，我还在大厅里和大家一起等着。',
        "{time=12:43.}.. It's late.": '{time=12:43.}……{w}都这么晚了。',
        "12:43...{w} It's late.": '{time=12:43.}……{w}都这么晚了。',
        "12:43... It's late.": '{time=12:43.}……{w}都这么晚了。',
        "12:43 p.m...{w} It's late.": '{time=12:43.}……{w}都这么晚了。',
        "12:43 p.m... It's late.": '{time=12:43.}……{w}都这么晚了。',
        '...And now what?': '……{w}那么，接下来呢？',
        "Even if the main entrance of the building is locked, assuming the storeroom door did lead to the outside, I could maybe enter through it. ...There's no way I could take the entire cabinet out without triggering the alarm. Someone would be looking at the cameras, and I don't even know where the cabinet is.": '就算大楼正门锁着，假如储藏室的门真能通到外面，我也许还能从那里进去。{w}……可我不可能不触发警报就把整个展示柜搬出去。总会有人盯着监控，何况我连展示柜在哪儿都不知道。',
        "I guess I don't have to go anywhere. I could just come back when I get tired. This is only for today, though. I seriously need to decide on what to do.": '算了，也不必非去哪里。累了直接回来就好。{w}不过仅限今天。我确实得认真想好接下来该怎么办。',
        '...Should I go to the tower? What would I even do? And what else is there in town? The library? How long has it been since I went there? Too long, honestly...': '……要去塔那边吗？去了又能做什么？{w}再说镇上还有别的地方可去吗？图书馆？我多久没去过了？老实说，真的太久了……',
        '...Thank you.': '……{w}谢谢你。',
        '"The incident occurred when an unknown individual released smoke that caused four people inside to lose consciousness. The other two were too far from the range to receive any serious injuries. While everyone was unconscious, a heater depleted its surrounding oxygen after its flame went out, and when a visitor turned on the lights, an immediate explosion of short radius but intense force occurred. It killed the first victim instantly and broke the floor of the shop. The second girl, Mirana, was protected by the furniture next to her but fell through the broken floor."': '「事发时，一名身份不明者释放烟雾，致使店内四人失去意识。其余两人距离较远，未受重伤。众人昏迷期间，一台取暖器在火焰熄灭后耗尽了周围的氧气；一名来客开灯时，随即发生了爆炸，波及范围不大，威力却极强。{w} 第一名遇难者当场死亡，店铺的地板也被炸裂。另一名女孩 Mirana 因身旁家具的遮挡而免于冲击，却从破裂的地板坠落。」',
        "And it doesn't even say why the incident happened. ...Right, on the 15th, when smoke knocked us out for the second time, I thought that both incidents must have been caused by the same people. That would be Xyn.": '而且报道里根本没提事故的原因。{w} ……对了，十五号那天，烟雾第二次把我们熏晕时，我就觉得这两起事件一定是同一伙人干的。那应该就是 Xyn。',
        "...Wait, it actually is this. I'm not wrong. It was caused by Xyn. That's why no further details got published. That's what Katei told us. Xyn had already tried to steal the Sekimeiya once, but they failed. They almost caught the person behind it, but since they ended up escaping, it wasn't published that they'd been from Xyn.": '……{w}等等，原来就是这个。我没记错。{w} 的确是 Xyn 造成的。所以才没有公布更多细节。{w} 这是 Katei 告诉我们的。Xyn 早就试图偷走 Sekimeiya 一次，但失败了。他们差点抓到幕后的人，可对方最后还是逃了，所以报道里没有说这是 Xyn 所为。',
        "Oh, of course... In the attic, I knew I recognized that smell. I smelled it in that shop. ...That's what happened there. Xyn tried to steal the Sekimeiya before it was brought to Ashiya Tower. The Sekimeiya was in the shop, and for some reason, Xyn didn't succeed.": '啊，原来如此……在阁楼里，我就觉得那股气味在哪儿闻过。我在那家店里闻到过。……那里发生的就是这么回事。Sekimeiya 被送进芦屋塔之前，Xyn 就想把它偷走。{w} 当时 Sekimeiya 就在那家店里，而不知为何，Xyn 没能得手。',
        'I huffed, deeply frustrated. I began to drink the coffee, and as I scanned the pages, more concise articles came into view.': '我重重吐了口气，满心烦躁。{w} 我一边喝着咖啡，一边扫视报纸，更多简短的报道映入眼帘。',
        '"Unknown Man Escapes from Prison Cell". Intrigued by the premise, I read the body of the article.': '「不明男子逃离牢房」。{w}这个标题勾起了我的兴趣，我接着往下读正文。',
        "What...? Is it talking about a prison here? I don't think there's a proper one in Yushibana, so maybe it's just talking about holding cells in the police department.": '什么……？说的是这里的监狱吗？{w}丰花应该没有正规的监狱，大概指的是警局里的拘留室吧。',
        '"The identity of that person remains unknown. They were dressed as a prisoner, but no footage shows who they were or how they ended up in that cell. The corridor they were in was unprotected, as nobody should\'ve been inside the cell. By the time the footage recording them was noticed, they\'d already disappeared. The cell itself was unlocked, supposedly due to being vacant. There was no security in that area, so it is possible the individual left the entire building. Their identity and the way they got to that cell are under investigation, but no method to reach it such as a hidden passage between cells was found to exist."': '「该人物的身份至今不明。其人身着囚服，但没有任何影像拍到此人是谁，又是如何进入那间牢房的。此人所在的走廊无人看管，因为那间牢房本不该有人。等到拍下此人的录像被人注意到时，他早已不见踪影。{w}牢房本身没有上锁，据称是因为当时空置。那一带没有任何安保措施，因此此人有可能已经离开整栋建筑。关于其身份以及进入牢房的方式仍在调查中，但并未发现牢房之间存在暗道之类的进入途径。」',
        "What the hell? I never heard about this. I guess I don't really watch or read the news.": '怎么回事？{w}我从没听说过这件事。也难怪，我本来就不怎么看新闻。',
        "I nodded and left the shop. Did I look like a person burying a lot of pain? To be talking casually and smiling only one day after Miiya's death, I assumed that was the only explanation to Darfee.": '我点点头，离开了店里。{w}我看起来像是个把痛苦深埋心底的人吗？Miiya 才去世一天，我就能谈笑自如——在 Darfee 眼里，恐怕也只有这一个解释吧。',
        "It was Sunday, so it made sense that most places were closed. I'd thought of going to the tower earlier, but that wasn't even possible, as it closed on Sundays. While I thought about what to do next, my legs automatically turned me toward a branching street.": '今天是周日，多数店铺关门也理所当然。我本打算早些去芦屋塔，可那根本行不通，因为塔周日不开放。{w}我一边想着接下来做什么，双腿却已经自行把我带向了一条岔路。',
        "If nothing changes, what will happen on the 15th? I still don't understand what was up with the recording. Could it really be that the exit will be locked for a month? If so, the police should take care of these two, right...?": '如果什么都没改变，15号那天会怎么样？我到现在还是不明白那段录音到底是怎么回事。{w}出口真的会被锁上一个月吗？真是那样的话，警察总该会照顾这两个家伙吧……？',
        "...I don't know enough about what happened these days to do something and actually be sure I've changed the past. At least not in a non-drastic way, like by speaking to Atsuki. I could go to my hospital room and draw something on my face that I didn't wake up with...": '……{w}这些天发生的事，我了解得太少，就算做了什么，也没法确定自己真的改变了过去。至少没法靠跟 Atsuki 说句话这种不痛不痒的办法来确认。我可以回病房，在脸上画点醒来时本来没有的东西……',
        '"The Sekimeiya". It was a flyer marked by the touch of many snowflakes. I\'d seen it before, but I didn\'t want to look at it.': '「The Sekimeiya」。{w}那是一张传单，上面留着不少雪花落过的痕迹。我以前见过它，却不愿去看。',
        'I took the phone from my purse and looked at the screen. It was almost 15:00.': '我从手提包里取出手机，看了看屏幕。时间快到 {time=15.} 了。',
        'I took the phone from my purse and looked at the screen. It was almost 3 p.m.': '我从手提包里取出手机，看了看屏幕。时间快到 {time=15.} 了。',
        "Shiroya...! How are you!? I'm so glad you called! We were so worried!": 'Shiroya……！你怎么样！？{w}你能打来真是太好了！我们担心死了！',
        "...Why did I travel so many days back? That doesn't make sense. Were we wrong, and the time the Sekimeiya spent out of the cabinet wasn't what influenced the time traveled?": '……{w}为什么我会回到这么多天以前？说不通。难道我们弄错了，影响穿越时长的并不是 Sekimeiya 离开展示柜的时间？',
        "There'll be the attack, and people will fall unconscious, probably except the attacker. If that period of time isn't enough, I'll have twelve hours to use it, during which people will get trapped again. If it comes down to it, I might have to think of how to take advantage of what happened. When the smoke went off, there were many places that weren't hit...": '到时候会发生袭击，除袭击者之外的人大概都会失去意识。如果那段时间还不够，我还有十二个小时可以利用，那期间人们会再次被困住。{w}真到了那一步，我或许得想想怎么利用当时发生的事。烟雾弹炸开的时候，还有很多地方没有被波及……',
        'A bit of meat remained in a plastic tray. I really only kept buying it because my parents used to. I grabbed it and looked at my side. Thankfully, the frying pan was clean.': '塑料托盘里还剩一点肉。我之所以一直买它，只是因为父母以前常买。{w}我端起托盘，又看了看旁边。还好，平底锅是干净的。',
        "I appeared late on November 30th, where I'd been on that day. When we were in the tower, we thought about going ten minutes back but appearing where we'd been five minutes before traveling. Did something like that happen again? Maybe I appeared at {time=21:10} where I'd been at {time=21:00}, so my old self wasn't there anymore. If I showed up exactly where I was at the time, I would've replaced my old self, and now I know that didn't happen.": '我是在十一月三十日晚上出现的，位置是当天自己待过的地方。我们在塔里的时候曾推测，穿越回十分钟前，却会出现在穿越前五分钟所在的位置。{w}难道这次也是这样？也许我在 {time=21:10} 出现在自己 {time=21:00} 待过的地方，所以原来的我已经不在那里了。如果我恰好出现在当时自己所在的位置，就会取代过去的我——而现在我知道，并没有发生这种事。',
        "I appeared late on November 30th, where I'd been on that day. When we were in the tower, we thought about going ten minutes back but appearing where we'd been five minutes before traveling.{w} Did something like that happen again? Maybe I appeared at 21:10 where I'd been at 21:00, so my old self wasn't there anymore. If I showed up exactly where I was at the time, I would've replaced my old self, and now I know that didn't happen.": '我是在十一月三十日晚上出现的，位置是当天自己待过的地方。我们在塔里的时候曾推测，穿越回十分钟前，却会出现在穿越前五分钟所在的位置。{w}难道这次也是这样？也许我在 {time=21:10} 出现在自己 {time=21:00} 待过的地方，所以原来的我已经不在那里了。如果我恰好出现在当时自己所在的位置，就会取代过去的我——而现在我知道，并没有发生这种事。',
        "I appeared late on November 30th, where I'd been on that day. When we were in the tower, we thought about going ten minutes back but appearing where we'd been five minutes before traveling. Did something like that happen again? Maybe I appeared at 21:10 where I'd been at 21:00, so my old self wasn't there anymore. If I showed up exactly where I was at the time, I would've replaced my old self, and now I know that didn't happen.": '我是在十一月三十日晚上出现的，位置是当天自己待过的地方。我们在塔里的时候曾推测，穿越回十分钟前，却会出现在穿越前五分钟所在的位置。{w}难道这次也是这样？也许我在 {time=21:10} 出现在自己 {time=21:00} 待过的地方，所以原来的我已经不在那里了。如果我恰好出现在当时自己所在的位置，就会取代过去的我——而现在我知道，并没有发生这种事。',
        "I appeared late on November 30th, where I'd been on that day. When we were in the tower, we thought about going ten minutes back but appearing where we'd been five minutes before traveling.{w} Did something like that happen again? Maybe I appeared at 9:10 p.m. where I'd been at 9:00 p.m., so my old self wasn't there anymore. If I showed up exactly where I was at the time, I would've replaced my old self, and now I know that didn't happen.": '我是在十一月三十日晚上出现的，位置是当天自己待过的地方。我们在塔里的时候曾推测，穿越回十分钟前，却会出现在穿越前五分钟所在的位置。{w}难道这次也是这样？也许我在 {time=21:10} 出现在自己 {time=21:00} 待过的地方，所以原来的我已经不在那里了。如果我恰好出现在当时自己所在的位置，就会取代过去的我——而现在我知道，并没有发生这种事。',
        "I appeared late on November 30th, where I'd been on that day. When we were in the tower, we thought about going ten minutes back but appearing where we'd been five minutes before traveling. Did something like that happen again? Maybe I appeared at 9:10 p.m. where I'd been at 9:00 p.m., so my old self wasn't there anymore. If I showed up exactly where I was at the time, I would've replaced my old self, and now I know that didn't happen.": '我是在十一月三十日晚上出现的，位置是当天自己待过的地方。我们在塔里的时候曾推测，穿越回十分钟前，却会出现在穿越前五分钟所在的位置。{w}难道这次也是这样？也许我在 {time=21:10} 出现在自己 {time=21:00} 待过的地方，所以原来的我已经不在那里了。如果我恰好出现在当时自己所在的位置，就会取代过去的我——而现在我知道，并没有发生这种事。',
        "...If Sai also traveled, there's no way he won't try to steal the Sekimeiya before then, when nobody else seemed aware of its powers. I didn't consider that more people could be here with the same intentions that I have, aside from the original Xyn plan.": '……{w}如果 Sai 也穿越了，在那之前还没有旁人知道 Sekimeiya 的力量，他绝不会放过偷走它的机会。除了 Xyn 原本的计划之外，我从没想过还会有别人抱着和我一样的打算来到这里。',
        '...I finally got up, supporting my body with one arm. As I did so, I realized what that had been.': '……{w}我终于用一只手臂撑起身子。就在起身的时候，我明白那是什么了。',
        '"Today at {time=9:51}, a deposit of ¥20,000 was transferred into your bank account. This will be reflected in 3 to 4 business days." The time showed {time=17:57.}': '「今天 {time=9:51}，你的银行账户存入 ¥20,000。此笔款项将在 3 至 4 个工作日内到账。」{w} 屏幕上的时间是 {time=17:57.}。',
        '"Today at 9:51, a deposit of ¥20,000 was transferred into your bank account. This will be reflected in 3 to 4 business days."{w} The time showed 17:57.': '「今天 {time=9:51}，你的银行账户存入 ¥20,000。此笔款项将在 3 至 4 个工作日内到账。」{w} 屏幕上的时间是 {time=17:57.}。',
        '"Today at 9:51, a deposit of ¥20,000 was transferred into your bank account. This will be reflected in 3 to 4 business days." The time showed 17:57.': '「今天 {time=9:51}，你的银行账户存入 ¥20,000。此笔款项将在 3 至 4 个工作日内到账。」{w} 屏幕上的时间是 {time=17:57.}。',
        '"Today at 9:51 a.m., a deposit of ¥20,000 was transferred into your bank account. This will be reflected in 3 to 4 business days."{w} The time showed 5:57 p.m.': '「今天 {time=9:51}，你的银行账户存入 ¥20,000。此笔款项将在 3 至 4 个工作日内到账。」{w} 屏幕上的时间是 {time=17:57.}。',
        '"Today at 9:51 a.m., a deposit of ¥20,000 was transferred into your bank account. This will be reflected in 3 to 4 business days." The time showed 5:57 p.m.': '「今天 {time=9:51}，你的银行账户存入 ¥20,000。此笔款项将在 3 至 4 个工作日内到账。」{w} 屏幕上的时间是 {time=17:57.}。',
        'As always, I left my phone on the bedside table next to me so that I could check the time after waking up or to set an alarm. I hugged the pillow and closed my eyes.': '和往常一样，我把手机放在床头柜上，方便醒来后看时间或设闹钟。{w}我抱住枕头，闭上眼睛。',
        "Those days were bound to end. I'd eventually have to find a job or study far from home. The weeks without obligations were ideal, but the feeling of wasting them was what made them stressful. I'd rarely been able to feel so calm, even though I still had very serious concerns on my mind. I hated thinking about it, but what would I do in the future? My parents wouldn't keep sending me money for many more months, so what job could I find? I was only a little interested in studying medicine, but I didn't want to move, and I'd have to spend years and years pursuing it. Of course, it was expensive too, so I felt I had to completely discard the idea.": '这样的日子终究会结束。我迟早得去找工作，或者离家去读书。无所事事的几周本该是理想的，可那种虚度光阴的感觉反倒让人心焦。我很少能像这样平静，尽管心里仍压着极重的顾虑。{w}我一想到这些就厌烦，可将来到底要做什么呢？父母不会再连着几个月给我汇钱了，那我能找到什么工作？我对学医只有那么一点兴趣，却又不想搬家，而且要为此耗上好几年。当然，学费也很贵，所以我觉得只能彻底打消这个念头。',
        "...I have to assume that's how it'd work. It's the most logical answer, isn't it? Neither of us would blink out of existence.": '……{w}只能这么想了吧。这是最合逻辑的答案，不是吗？我们谁都不会凭空消失。',
        "I reached for my phone to look at the time. It showed {time=9:07}, confirming how long I'd slept.": '我伸手拿起手机看时间。{w}屏幕上显示 {time=9:07}，看来我这一觉睡了很久。',
        "I reached for my phone to look at the time.{w} It showed 9:07, confirming how long I'd slept.": '我伸手拿起手机看时间。{w}屏幕上显示 {time=9:07}，看来我这一觉睡了很久。',
        "I reached for my phone to look at the time. It showed 9:07, confirming how long I'd slept.": '我伸手拿起手机看时间。{w}屏幕上显示 {time=9:07}，看来我这一觉睡了很久。',
        "I reached for my phone to look at the time.{w} It showed 9:07 a.m., confirming how long I'd slept.": '我伸手拿起手机看时间。{w}屏幕上显示 {time=9:07}，看来我这一觉睡了很久。',
        "I reached for my phone to look at the time. It showed 9:07 a.m., confirming how long I'd slept.": '我伸手拿起手机看时间。{w}屏幕上显示 {time=9:07}，看来我这一觉睡了很久。',
        "...Wait, what's this? ...The Sekimeiya incident might happen soon...?": '……等等，这是什么？{w}……Sekimeiya 事件或许即将发生……？',
        "...Who is this? There's no way it's from the people who organized the attack. The Sekimeiya hadn't been given to Ashiya yet, and they wouldn't know people will get trapped since the alarm's existence was supposed to be a secret.": '……{w}这是谁？{w}这绝不可能是策划那场袭击的人发的。Sekimeiya 当时还没交到芦屋手上，而且警报的存在本该是秘密，他们不可能知道有人会被困在里面。',
        "...There's no way. This can only be one thing. ...Someone who traveled from the future—from the 15th. If it's not that, whoever posted this knew about the Sekimeiya's powers.": '……不可能。那就只剩下一种解释。{w}……有人从未来穿越回来——来自15号。若非如此，发帖的人就是知道 Sekimeiya 的力量。',
        '"Some people even got trapped inside, but I don\'t know what happened to them." ...If I\'m right, this person must have been outside of the tower. They knew some of us had gotten trapped, but not what was happening inside. Then, before {time=21}, they traveled to the past.': '「有人甚至被困在了里面，可他们后来怎么样，我不知道。」{w}……如果我猜得没错，这个人当时就在塔外。他知道我们中有人被困住了，却不知道里面发生了什么。然后在 {time=21} 之前，他穿越回了过去。',
        '"Some people even got trapped inside, but I don\'t know what happened to them."{w} ...If I\'m right, this person must have been outside of the tower. They knew some of us had gotten trapped, but not what was happening inside. Then, before 21:00, they traveled to the past.': '「有人甚至被困在了里面，可他们后来怎么样，我不知道。」{w}……如果我猜得没错，这个人当时就在塔外。他知道我们中有人被困住了，却不知道里面发生了什么。然后在 {time=21} 之前，他穿越回了过去。',
        '"Some people even got trapped inside, but I don\'t know what happened to them." ...If I\'m right, this person must have been outside of the tower. They knew some of us had gotten trapped, but not what was happening inside. Then, before 21:00, they traveled to the past.': '「有人甚至被困在了里面，可他们后来怎么样，我不知道。」{w}……如果我猜得没错，这个人当时就在塔外。他知道我们中有人被困住了，却不知道里面发生了什么。然后在 {time=21} 之前，他穿越回了过去。',
        '"Some people even got trapped inside, but I don\'t know what happened to them."{w} ...If I\'m right, this person must have been outside of the tower. They knew some of us had gotten trapped, but not what was happening inside. Then, before 9 p.m., they traveled to the past.': '「有人甚至被困在了里面，可他们后来怎么样，我不知道。」{w}……如果我猜得没错，这个人当时就在塔外。他知道我们中有人被困住了，却不知道里面发生了什么。然后在 {time=21} 之前，他穿越回了过去。',
        '"Some people even got trapped inside, but I don\'t know what happened to them." ...If I\'m right, this person must have been outside of the tower. They knew some of us had gotten trapped, but not what was happening inside. Then, before 9 p.m., they traveled to the past.': '「有人甚至被困在了里面，可他们后来怎么样，我不知道。」{w}……如果我猜得没错，这个人当时就在塔外。他知道我们中有人被困住了，却不知道里面发生了什么。然后在 {time=21} 之前，他穿越回了过去。',
        "If they were outside the tower and suddenly traveled, did people see that? Did someone from inside the building travel to the 24th and bring this person with them? That can't be, right? It's the same thing I thought about regarding my own travel. It would've had an immense range, and it would've picked up so many more people, including me.": '如果他在塔外突然穿越，会被人看见吗？会不会是楼里的人穿越到24号时，把他一起带了过去？{w}不可能吧？我对自己那次穿越也是这么想的。那样的话，范围会大得离谱，还会把更多人卷进来，包括我在内。',
        "Maybe I have this wrong. If the recording was genuine, the exit wouldn't have unlocked after 21:00. That could be why this person doesn't know what happened to us, and they could've traveled after the 15th. Maybe when they did, nobody else was outside the tower, and that's why only one person traveled.": '也许是我弄错了。如果那段录音是真的，出口在 {time=21.} 之后就不会解锁。这或许就是这个人不知道我们遭遇了什么的原因，而他可能是在15号之后才穿越的。也许他穿越的时候，塔外再没有别人，所以才只有他一个人穿越。',
        "Maybe I have this wrong. If the recording was genuine, the exit wouldn't have unlocked after 9 p.m. That could be why this person doesn't know what happened to us, and they could've traveled after the 15th. Maybe when they did, nobody else was outside the tower, and that's why only one person traveled.": '也许是我弄错了。如果那段录音是真的，出口在 {time=21.} 之后就不会解锁。这或许就是这个人不知道我们遭遇了什么的原因，而他可能是在15号之后才穿越的。也许他穿越的时候，塔外再没有别人，所以才只有他一个人穿越。',
        "But if that's it, who made that travel happen? Whoever did would've disappeared from the tower. ...Was it Akaro? When we left the attic's bedroom, we found the Sekimeiya powered off in a hallway B room. After that time, I didn't see Akaro again, and he could've touched it. ...Also, the rest of us but Sai were in the attic, so maybe that's why we didn't travel alongside Akaro.": '可若真是这样，那次穿越又是谁触发的？触发穿越的人本该从塔里消失。{w}……是 Akaro 吗？{w}我们离开阁楼那间卧室时，发现 Sekimeiya 已经关机，放在 B走廊的一个房间里。那之后我就再没见过 Akaro，他有机会碰到它。……而且，除了 Sai，我们几个当时都在阁楼里，也许正因如此才没跟着 Akaro 一起被传送走。',
        "But... much later, Atsuki said that he'd seen him. ...Maybe I'm wrong. If the range isn't an obstacle, anyone could've gone so far back. Then, they either could've reentered through the storeroom or been inside since that morning.": '可是……很久之后，Atsuki 说他见过那个人。{w}……也许我错了。如果范围不是障碍，那谁都有可能回到那么早的过去。那样的话，这个人要么是从储藏室重新进来的，要么从那天早上起就一直待在楼里。',
        "...If this person was outside the tower and went to the past alongside someone who activated the Sekimeiya, would they have thought that they'd experienced a hyperrealistic dream? That sounds pretty strange, but I suppose there aren't many more interpretations. They don't exactly seem to have a record of being mentally stable...": '……{w}如果这个人当时在塔外，而有人启动了 Sekimeiya，他跟着一起回到了过去，那他会不会以为自己做了一场无比真实的梦？这听起来很荒唐，但除此之外恐怕也没有多少解释。毕竟从帖子里看，他的精神状态本来就算不上稳定……',
        'Below the initial post was a short reply. "Yeah, right? If you can see the future, do me a favor and PM me tomorrow\'s lottery numbers. That\'d be sick. I\'d make a nice long reservation at that comfy Damski resort place, always wanted to go."': '原帖下面是一条简短的回复。{w}「可不是嘛？你要是能看见未来，就帮个忙，把明天的彩票号码私信给我。那可太爽了。我要在 Damski 那家舒服的度假村订个长住，我一直想去。」',
        'The next reply had been posted one day later. Below it, the dated entry showed it had been sent on the 25th of November, at 20:00.': '下一条回复是一天后发的。下面的日期显示，发送时间是11月25日 {time=20.}。',
        'The next reply had been posted one day later. Below it, the dated entry showed it had been sent on the 25th of November, at 8 p.m.': '下一条回复是一天后发的。下面的日期显示，发送时间是11月25日 {time=20.}。',
        "It wasn't snowing that day either, and my street seemed empty. I went down the stairs and walked ahead. The direction was the same I'd taken the previous day, but Sidnoc was located before the center of Yushibana.": '那天也没有下雪，我那条街看上去空无一人。{w}我走下楼梯，继续往前走。方向跟昨天一样，不过 Sidnoc 在到丰花中心之前。',
        "I grabbed my wallet, but I knew I barely didn't have enough cash to pay for everything. I took out my credit card instead and handed it to her.": '我掏出钱包，可我知道身上的现金差一点点不够付全款。{w}于是我改拿信用卡，递给她。',
        '1991. I pressed "okay" and waited a few seconds.': '1{w=0.4}9{w=0.2}9{w=0.3}1.{w=0.3} 我按下「确认」，等了几秒。',
        "The angle was from a little high up, so it was likely taken through an apartment window. In Yushibana, most apartments didn't have different floors, so it was likely that if I simply found the place it'd been taken from, I could also find out who lived there.": '拍摄角度略高，很可能是透过某间公寓的窗户拍的。{w}丰花的大多数公寓都只有一层，所以只要找到拍摄地点，或许就能查出住在那里的住户。',
        "There's also the chance the person who posted the thread is someone I know. Assuming I manage to travel back in time again, it's definitely possible that they'll still go all the way back as long as the incident occurs. It shouldn't even matter if Atsuki and I don't go. I'll definitely have to go to the tower before the 15th. I guess the best I can hope for is that I'll be able to touch the Sekimeiya and go far enough back to save Miiya. Most likely, the biggest issue right now is not knowing how to make myself go so far back again.": '发帖人也可能是我认识的人。假设我还能再次穿越回过去，那么只要那起事件发生，对方仍有可能照样一路回到过去。即使我和 Atsuki 不去，应该也无所谓。{w}我无论如何都得在15号之前去一趟芦屋塔。我能指望的最好结果，大概就是碰触 Sekimeiya，并回到足够早的过去救下 Miiya。眼下最大的问题，恐怕是我不知道怎样才能让自己再次回到那么早的过去。',
        "Oh, actually, it should be simple. When I woke up in the hospital, it was the afternoon of the 8th, and Atsuki was there. So I know for a fact that he'll be out at that time.": '啊，其实应该很简单。{w}我在医院醒来时是8号下午，Atsuki 就在那里。所以我确定，那个时间他不在家。',
        "I bit my lip and tried to keep walking. I'd already thought of the negative implications of that, but I had to start seriously worrying about them.": '我咬住嘴唇，继续往前走。{w}那些糟糕的可能我早就想到过，只是如今不得不认真对待了。',
        "Does this pretty much mean that I have to go to the tower as soon as possible, find the Sekimeiya, and somehow activate it to go days back? That could easily go wrong in so many ways...! What if I stay in front of the tower permanently to see what Xyn do with the Sekimeiya once they steal it? This could also very easily end up being a mistake, and there's no way I could do it.": '这基本上就是说，我得尽快赶到塔里，找到 Sekimeiya，然后想办法启动它，回到几天前？{w}这中间随便哪个环节都可能出岔子……！{w}又或者，我干脆一直守在塔前，看 Xyn 偷走 Sekimeiya 之后会拿它做什么？{w}这同样极可能是个错误的决定，而且我根本做不到。',
        'I took my phone out and looked at its screen. Then, I peered into the distance, toward the tower.': '我掏出手机看了看屏幕。{w}随后抬眼望向远处的塔。',
        'Hm... Around here?': '嗯……{w}就在这附近？',
        'Should I try to ring the bell...? It could be any of the four. If the person from the forum is someone I know, maybe I could recognize their voice.': '要不要按门铃试试……？四户里哪一户都有可能。{w}如果论坛上那个人是我认识的，说不定能听出声音。',
        'Still holding the phone, I pressed the call button and dialed the numbers on the wall. 1989-1815-251... I started to hear the high-pitched beeps.': '我仍拿着手机，按下通话键，拨出墙上写的那串号码。{w} 1989-1815-251……{w=0.6} 听筒里响起尖锐的提示音。',
        "Oh, hey. ...I'm calling for an apartment I see for sale at Ampla.": '哦，你好。{w}……我是想问问在 Ampla 看到的那套出售的房子。',
        "That's great. ...Are you perhaps at the address right now?": '那太好了。{w}……你现在是不是就在房子那儿？',
        "I didn't have to wait long for a door farther back to open. A middle-aged man came out and shuffled up to me.": '没过多久，靠里的一扇门开了。{w}一个中年男人走出来，拖着步子来到我面前。',
        'He had two keys on his palm and used one to unlock the entrance. I saw a gray hall with stairs leading up.': '他掌心里握着两把钥匙，用其中一把打开了大门。{w}我看见一个灰色的大厅，里面有通往楼上的楼梯。',
        'He stopped in front of the first door, which had an "A" above it. Instead of unlocking it himself, he rang the bell.': '他在第一扇门前停下，门上标着「A」。{w}他没有自己开锁，而是按响了门铃。',
        "Ah, good morning. ...Well, I guess it's close to noon already. Are you coming to see my apartment?": '啊，早上好。{w}……不过看样子都快中午了。{w}你是来看房的吗？',
        "The furniture won't be taken away. You'll notice the heating is working just fine, but sunlight makes it inside all day too. You might've noticed that there's no elevator below, but fortunately, you only have to go up a single set of stairs.": '家具不会搬走。你会发现暖气运行良好，而且一整天都有阳光照进来。{w}你可能已经注意到楼下没有电梯，不过好在只需要爬一段楼梯。',
        'The room was pretty messy, and it stored different kinds of objects and old devices. My attention was quickly directed to a framed picture.': '房间里相当杂乱，堆着各式各样的物件和旧设备。{w}我的目光很快被一个相框吸引过去。',
        "I know we haven't spoken about price—I can be a bit flexible. Right now, the set price is ¥42,000 a month, but you'll need to make an initial deposit of ¥126,000. How does that sound?": '我知道我们还没谈过价钱——这方面我可以稍微通融。目前的定价是每月 ¥42,000，不过首次需要缴纳 ¥126,000 的押金。{w}你觉得怎么样？',
        "Hm... I certainly liked this place. It's a big decision, though... I'll have to think about it.": '嗯……我确实挺喜欢这里。不过这是个大决定……{w}我得再考虑考虑。',
        "As soon as I turned around, I was met with the same sensation. The door to the outside closed, and I saw a man walking up the stairs. The look he gave muddled my mind, instantly making me doubt everything I'd just determined.": '刚一转身，同样的感觉又袭了上来。{w}通往外面的门关上，我看见一个男人正走上楼梯。他投来的目光搅乱了我的心绪，让我瞬间怀疑起刚才得出的所有结论。',
        "It was the very same look as the other man's, down to the piercing pause. When time continued, he stepped up and unlocked the opposite door, quietly shutting it behind him without saying a word.": '那眼神和另一个男人如出一辙，连那令人窒息的停顿都分毫不差。{w}时间恢复流动，他走上前，打开对面那扇门的锁，一言不发地轻轻带上。',
        'Lost in thought, I arrived at Ramon. In contrast to the early morning, the street was fairly busy, partially thanks to the good weather. I recognized a group of kids years younger than me, so I avoided even looking at them.': '我一路想着，不知不觉到了拉蒙街。{w}和清晨不同，这条街相当热闹，多半是因为天气好。我认出几个比我小好几岁的孩子，索性连看都不往那边看。',
        "I wandered around slowly, hoping something would come to mind. ...Knowing that the future I was envisioning could have been destroyed at any moment caused a hollow anxiety to form in my chest. It was the same one I'd felt after Miiya died.": '我缓缓地四处闲逛，盼着能想到些什么。{w}……一想到自己所设想的未来随时可能被摧毁，胸口便涌起一阵空洞的不安。那感觉，和 Miiya 死后我曾有过的一模一样。',
        "I thought that on the 30th, I appeared underground at 21:10 where I'd been only minutes prior. Plenty of travels that happened in the tower can fit that idea, but there were already some that didn't, and neither does this one.": '我原以为，30号那天我在{time=21:10}出现在地下，而那正是我几分钟前待过的地方。塔里发生的许多次穿越都能套用这个说法，但已经有些对不上，这一例同样不符。',
        "I thought that on the 30th, I appeared underground at 9:10 p.m. where I'd been only minutes prior. Plenty of travels that happened in the tower can fit that idea, but there were already some that didn't, and neither does this one.": '我原以为，30号那天我在{time=21:10}出现在地下，而那正是我几分钟前待过的地方。塔里发生的许多次穿越都能套用这个说法，但已经有些对不上，这一例同样不符。',
        "If his parents said that he shouldn't have been there on the 24th, it can't be that it was a coordinate mere minutes away from the point he appeared. But of course, his parents' house isn't a random position. It definitely had to have been based on one from his past.": '既然他父母说他24号本不该在那里，那它就不可能是他出现前几分钟所在的地点。{w}不过话说回来，他父母家也并非随意选定的位置。那必定是基于他过去的某个地点。',
        "Ahead of me, I saw something I recognized. The very same stare I'd just been given.": '前方，我看见了似曾相识的一幕。{w}正是方才落在我身上的那种眼神。',
        "I spun around me, and after a full circle, my heart hammered once. All around, I'd seen people fixing their eyes on me.": '我原地转了一圈，整整一圈之后，心脏猛地一跳。{w}四周的人，全都直勾勾地盯着我。',
        "I moved to the end of the street. There, the atmosphere was completely calm, similar to how things had been that morning. Slightly ahead of me was the school I'd always gone to, in front of the end of the mountain range.": '我走到街的尽头。那里一片宁静，和今早的情形很像。{w}前方不远处就是我念了多年的学校，学校后面便是山脉的尽头。',
        "I could see people in the distance, too tiny to recognize. I'd pretty much circled around Yushibana, and it was fairly smaller than the perception of it I'd always had.": '远处能望见人影，小得辨不清面容。{w}我几乎绕着丰花走了一圈，它比我向来以为的要小上不少。',
        "I could make it home without crossing the center again, so I headed toward the path I'd often taken after classes. However, I abruptly forced my legs to stop.": '不必再穿过镇中心也能到家，于是我走向放学后常走的那条路。{w}然而，我猛地停下脚步。',
        'I kept walking, shrugging off whatever was up with me. But I soon had to stop again.': '我甩开心里那点莫名的异样，继续走着。{w}可没过多久，又不得不停下。',
        "Nobody seemed to be behind me, but something inside me told me otherwise. The first time, I'd turned around after stopping and hadn't seen anyone. The second, I hadn't sensed anything, but I wanted to make sure.": '身后似乎没有人，可我心里总觉得不对劲。{w}第一次，我停下脚步回头，谁也没看见。第二次，我什么都没察觉到，却还是想确认一下。',
        "Footprints. They weren't mine, and I hadn't seen them seconds earlier. They came from the park hugging the edge and then disappeared toward faraway trees.": '脚印。{w}不是我的，几秒前我还没看见。它们从公园边缘一路延伸出来，然后消失在远处的树丛间。',
        "The path was mostly straight until my apartment. It wasn't too cold, so I didn't slow down. On the way, I crossed paths with a neighbor of mine. Naturally, her footprints didn't match the ones I'd seen...": '回公寓的路大部分是直路。天不算太冷，我也就没有放慢脚步。{w}路上，我遇见了住在附近的邻居。她的脚印自然和我看见的那些对不上……',
        "...Why would anyone follow me? To confirm that it was me because I should be in the hospital? ...It wouldn't be to hurt me, right? ...If it was someone from Xyn who traveled to the past, would I actually be seen as a threat to them? If they know I should be in the hospital, they could figure out that there are two of me and I came from the future.": '……为什么会有人跟踪我？{w}是因为我本该待在医院，所以来确认我的身份？……应该不会是来伤害我的吧？{w}……如果对方是来自 Xyn 的时间穿越者，我会被他们当成威胁吗？只要他们知道我本该住院，就能推断出有两个我，而且我是从未来来的。',
        '...I dried it with a hanging towel and put it on the burner with the food. I knew not to turn the intensity all the way up or it would burn easily. I stood in front of the pan, focusing only on evenly heating the meat.': '……我用挂着的毛巾把锅擦干，放到炉灶上，再放入肉。{w}我知道火不能开到最大，否则很容易烧焦。我站在锅前，只专心把肉均匀加热。',
        "...I should just try not to think about it too much. Even if I was being followed, what's most important is still that the Sekimeiya could be taken before the 15th.": '……{w}还是别想太多了。就算真有人跟踪我，最重要的仍然是：Sekimeiya 可能会在 15号之前被夺走。',
        "...And if I try to enter the tower during the night and I'm caught before I can trigger the alarm, it could all fail. My main two worries are not knowing where the Sekimeiya is and not knowing how to travel a lot of days back in time.": '……再说，要是我夜里进塔，还没触发警报就被抓住，整个计划就可能失败。{w}我最担心的两点，一是不知道 Sekimeiya 在哪里，二是不知道怎么回到许多天之前。',
        "I could go to the tower during the day and try to find the cabinet. If it's there, I know the mechanism behind the alarm will already be working, so I could try to consciously change the past the following night by entering the tower and forcing the cabinet open. I suppose it's possible it already is in the event room if nobody's allowed in for now. There wasn't a camera in the storeroom, so maybe I could see if the handle of the hidden door is still there and if it really leads outside. Using that hidden section is my best bet to make it to the tower during the night. I could either try to enter it from the outside or wait behind the movable wall during the day, where I won't be found before the tower closes.": '我可以白天先去塔里，试着找到展示柜。如果它还在，我就知道警报背后的机关已经启动了，那么第二天夜里，我就能有意识地改变过去——进塔，强行撬开展示柜。既然现在不许人进入，展示柜也可能已经被移到活动室了。{w}储藏室里没有摄像头，所以我可以去看看暗门的把手还在不在，以及那扇门是否真的通向外面。{w}我要进塔，最靠谱的办法就是利用那个隐蔽区域。要么从外面设法进去，要么白天躲在可移动墙壁后面——这样在塔关闭之前，不会有人发现我。',
        "There, assuming the person in the security room doesn't leave, I could try to mess with the Sekimeiya. Maybe I'll touch it and appear somewhere that's being recorded, though. If that's seen from the security room and I don't reply to whatever I'm told by the guard, it's incredibly likely they'll go ahead and unlock the exit.": '在那里，只要监控室里的人不离开，我就能试着摆弄 Sekimeiya。不过，也许我一碰它，就会出现在有摄像头的地方。{w}如果监控室看到了这一幕，而我又对守卫的喊话毫无回应，他们极有可能直接去打开出口。',
        "But if I see that I can open the door, it's possible I'll have a good way out. During the night, I could enter the tower through that door and quickly go to the Sekimeiya cabinet to trigger the alarm. Then, as soon as possible, I could leave with the Sekimeiya through the storeroom.": '但如果我确认自己能打开那扇门，说不定就有了一条很好的退路。{w}夜里，我可以从那扇门进塔，迅速赶到放 Sekimeiya 的展示柜前触发警报。然后，尽快带着 Sekimeiya 从储藏室离开。',
        '...But did that bring serious risks? Even if I was later found outside, I could touch the Sekimeiya and go to the past before my identity was given away. Although I would lose the Sekimeiya.': '……{w}可这样做真就没有严重风险吗？就算之后在外面被人发现，我也能赶在身份暴露之前碰到 Sekimeiya，回到过去。代价是会失去 Sekimeiya。',
        'Wait... there might be a way to solve the problem of not being able to figure out why I went so many days to the past.': '等等……{w}我一直想不通自己为什么会回到那么多天前，可这个问题或许有办法解决。',
        "If I can't open the storeroom door, I could still make it inside the tower during the night if I wait in the section past the movable wall, assuming someone else who knows about it doesn't check it. After that, I could activate the alarm and leave the Sekimeiya out of its cabinet for a really long time.": '要是打不开储藏室的门，我也能趁夜里留在塔内——只要躲在活动墙后面那块区域，前提是其他知道这块区域的人不会来查看。{w}之后触发警报，让 Sekimeiya 长时间留在展示柜外就行了。',
        "How would I prevent the exit from opening early? I'd be talked to from the security room, so maybe I could reply and act as if I really am from Xyn. Could I try to negotiate for hours or somehow convince them not to open the exit prematurely?": '怎么才能阻止出口被人提前打开？监控室那边一定会跟我通话，我或许可以答话，装成 Xyn 的人。{w}能不能设法拖上几个小时，或者想办法说服他们不要提前开门？',
        'If I could think of something to say so that they keep me there, I could be in hallway A all the time. Assuming twelve hours pass, I could run to touch the Sekimeiya just before the deadline. And if at least one stored minute means two minutes traveled, I would go 24 hours into the past. As long as I can make it to the previous night, to a time before the tower is open to the public, I could change the past and repeat the process. I could progressively go days back without understanding how to travel such a long distance at once.': '只要能想出说辞把他们拖住，我就能一直待在 A走廊。{w}等快到十二个小时的时候，赶在时限前跑回去碰 Sekimeiya。如果蓄能一分钟至少能穿越两分钟，我就能回到二十四小时之前。只要回到前一晚、回到塔还没对外开放的时刻，我就能改变过去，再把这套流程重来一遍。{w}这样一天天往回退，哪怕我始终不明白怎样才能一次穿越那么长的距离。',
        "There are issues too. The person in the security room could see that the Sekimeiya's outside the cabinet and demand that I put it back, knowing that the refrigeration is essential to keep it safe. And if one minute stored doesn't come out to two or more minutes traveled, I could appear during daytime, so I couldn't repeat the process until the same night I started from in the first place.": '问题也不少。监控室的人一看到 Sekimeiya 不在展示柜里，就会明白制冷对它有多要紧，然后要我把东西放回去。{w}而且，万一蓄能一分钟换不来两分钟以上的穿越时间，我就会出现在白天，那样非得等到与出发时同样的夜晚，才能再走一遍流程。',
        '...What would even happen if I went back to the 30th and could save Miiya? Where would I stay?': '……{w}就算我真回到 30 号、救下了 Miiya，之后又会怎样？我住哪儿？',
        "Since the past would greatly change, the current version of me who traveled from the 15th would very likely be overwritten. Even if my original self still goes to the hospital on the 30th, that me wouldn't go to live with Atsuki, so I'd instantly have to figure out what to do in a world with two versions of myself.": '过去会被大幅改写，从 15 号穿越而来的这个我多半也会被覆盖掉。{w}即便原本的我在 30 号仍会去医院，那个我也不会再去和 Atsuki 同住，于是我立刻就得在一个有两个我的世界里想好该怎么办。',
        "...Oh, I don't actually think this can work. If the Sekimeiya really was in that shop on the 30th, as long as it wasn't immediately brought to the tower, there could be a point where I couldn't keep progressively going one day back at a time. There'd eventually be no Sekimeiya in the tower to travel with.": '……唔，这办法恐怕行不通。{w}如果 30 号那天 Sekimeiya 确实还在那家店里，只要它没有立刻被送进塔里，我迟早会退到某个时间点——那时塔里根本没有 Sekimeiya 可以用来穿越。',
        "If I can only go one day back at a time, I'll eventually reach Sunday, when the tower is closed and I can't get in. The last possible night where I could do this would be Monday—tonight. ...So Miiya died on a Saturday, and I can't save her if I don't figure out why I went so far back.": '一次只能往回退一天的话，迟早会退到星期日——那天塔闭馆，我根本进不去。我还能动手的最后一晚就是星期一，也就是今晚。{w}……也就是说，Miiya 死在星期六，而我要是弄不清自己为什么回到那么久以前，就救不了她。',
        'In the end, no matter how much I thought in the living room of my house, I had to go to the tower. During the day, I had to try to find the Sekimeiya and check the status of the storeroom door so that I could determine the best course of action.': '说到底，我坐在自家客厅里想得再多，也还是得去一趟塔。{w}白天我必须设法找到 Sekimeiya，再看看储藏室那扇门的情况，才能定下最妥当的做法。',
        'I heard a faint sound. After suddenly raising my head, I noticed it was coming from next to me.': '我听见一点细微的声响。{w}猛地抬起头，才发现声音是从旁边传来的。',
        'O-Oh, you picked up. Good. Hey there.': '啊……你接了，太好了。{w}那个，你好。',
        '...December 15th? What are you talking about?': '……{w}12 月 15 号？你在说什么？',
        '...I do, yeah. I was there.': '……{w}是啊，我知道。我就在现场。',
        'Wh— R-Really...!? So that is what happened! How, though!?': '什——真、真的吗……！？{w} 原来是这么回事！可到底是怎么做到的！？',
        "S-So, time traveling really is possible...! I was so scared I'd lost it completely! Do you really not know anything about what happened?": '那、那么说，时间穿越真的存在……！我还一直怕是自己彻底疯了！{w} 你对当时发生的事，真的一点都不知道吗？',
        "Yeah, I'm sorry... I didn't know what to say. It was hard to ask out of nowhere if you'd traveled through time.": '嗯，抱歉……我不知道该怎么开口。{w} 突然问你有没有经历时间穿越，这话实在很难说出口。',
        "...So, are you okay now? I figure getting caught in that attack and suddenly traveling through time was hard on you. I know I didn't take it well.": '……{w}那么，你现在还好吗？被卷进那场袭击，又突然穿越了时间，我想这对你来说一定很难熬。我自己当时就受不了。',
        "I am. Don't worry about me. But I do have a question. Did you let your past self see you?": '我还好。不用为我担心。{w} 不过我有个问题。你有没有让过去的自己看到你？',
        "My past self? No... I didn't, but I-I did see him. I came back to my place on the 25th of November, and in the afternoon, I saw myself coming back from work. I got scared when I heard the sound, so I escaped without being seen. When I started to understand what had happened to me, I managed to avoid problems pretty easily by staying at home before the evening or at my parents'.": '过去的我？没有……我没让他看见，倒是我、我确实看见了他。{w} 我是在十一月二十五日回到自己住处的，那天下午，我看见自己下班回来。听到动静时我吓坏了，趁没被发现赶紧躲开。{w} 等渐渐弄明白自己身上发生了什么，我只要在傍晚前待在家里，或者去父母那边，就能很轻松地避开麻烦。',
        "Yes, but I'm afraid I won't work there much longer. ...Honestly, I have been told in the past I'm not always mentally stable. I'm relieved that it's not at the point I'd feared, but staying at my job would be very irresponsible... and dangerous. ...I didn't share it at first, but I think that just made it worse, so I've already accepted my condition.": '是的，不过恐怕我在那里也干不了多久了。{w}……说实话，以前就有人说过，我的精神状态有时不太稳定。我很庆幸情况还没到我所害怕的地步，但继续留在那个岗位上会非常不负责任……也很危险。……我一开始没把这件事说出来，可我觉得那样反而更糟，所以我已经接受了自己的状况。',
        "Oh, I'm sorry. I don't know anything. It was a highly entertained possibility that Xyn could've been planning something, but I don't know anything beyond that.": '哦，抱歉。我什么都不知道。{w}当时局里确实认真考虑过 Xyn 可能在谋划什么，但除此之外我也没听说别的。',
        'Uh... yes. Do you know exactly when you traveled through time on the 15th?': '呃……{w}有。{w}你知道自己15号是几点穿越的吗？',
        "The time? ...It might've been close to 16:00, I think.": '时间？……我想，大概快到{time=16}的时候吧。',
        "The time? ...It might've been close to 4 p.m., I think.": '时间？……我想，大概快到{time=16}的时候吧。',
        "Hm... I don't know, then. I traveled hours later, so I don't know what to think.": '嗯……{w}那我就不知道了。我是在几个小时后才穿越的，实在想不明白。',
        "...I don't think so, no.": '……{w}没有了，我想不到。',
        "I left my phone on the floor and rested my head back on the pillow. I'd briefly looked at the time, which had shown 16:58.": '我把手机搁在地板上，又把头靠回枕头。刚才我瞥过一眼时间，显示是{time=16:58.}。',
        "I left my phone on the floor and rested my head back on the pillow. I'd briefly looked at the time, which had shown 4:58 p.m.": '我把手机搁在地板上，又把头靠回枕头。刚才我瞥过一眼时间，显示是{time=16:58.}。',
        "I'm glad all that makes more sense now. ...It's probably fine that I revealed I traveled through time. At {time=16} we were in the attic, and I think Sai and Akaro had already escaped from the bedroom... I might've been right with what I thought before.": '现在总算理清了不少，我也安心了。……我透露了自己穿越过时间，应该没关系吧。{w}在{time=16}的时候，我们还在阁楼里，我记得 Sai 和 Akaro 已经逃出卧室了……我之前想的说不定没错。',
        "I'm glad all that makes more sense now. ...It's probably fine that I revealed I traveled through time.{w} At 16:00 we were in the attic, and I think Sai and Akaro had already escaped from the bedroom... I might've been right with what I thought before.": '现在总算理清了不少，我也安心了。……我透露了自己穿越过时间，应该没关系吧。{w}在{time=16}的时候，我们还在阁楼里，我记得 Sai 和 Akaro 已经逃出卧室了……我之前想的说不定没错。',
        "I'm glad all that makes more sense now. ...It's probably fine that I revealed I traveled through time. At 16:00 we were in the attic, and I think Sai and Akaro had already escaped from the bedroom... I might've been right with what I thought before.": '现在总算理清了不少，我也安心了。……我透露了自己穿越过时间，应该没关系吧。{w}在{time=16}的时候，我们还在阁楼里，我记得 Sai 和 Akaro 已经逃出卧室了……我之前想的说不定没错。',
        "I'm glad all that makes more sense now. ...It's probably fine that I revealed I traveled through time.{w} At 4 p.m. we were in the attic, and I think Sai and Akaro had already escaped from the bedroom... I might've been right with what I thought before.": '现在总算理清了不少，我也安心了。……我透露了自己穿越过时间，应该没关系吧。{w}在{time=16}的时候，我们还在阁楼里，我记得 Sai 和 Akaro 已经逃出卧室了……我之前想的说不定没错。',
        "I'm glad all that makes more sense now. ...It's probably fine that I revealed I traveled through time. At 4 p.m. we were in the attic, and I think Sai and Akaro had already escaped from the bedroom... I might've been right with what I thought before.": '现在总算理清了不少，我也安心了。……我透露了自己穿越过时间，应该没关系吧。{w}在{time=16}的时候，我们还在阁楼里，我记得 Sai 和 Akaro 已经逃出卧室了……我之前想的说不定没错。',
        "How much time had I spent there? I'd tried to keep my mind empty, but it wasn't easy, especially after Vaisude's call. As usual, the bath had been relaxing, but it also made me more tired.": '我在里面待了多久？我试着什么都不去想，可这并不是件容易事，尤其是 Vaisude 那通电话之后。{w}和平时一样，泡澡让人放松，却也让我更疲惫了。',
        "No sunlight was left. I approached my phone and glanced at the time. {time=19:19.} The previous day, I'd gone to sleep very early, so my body was demanding that I repeat the schedule.": '外面已经没有日光。我走到手机旁看了一眼时间。{w}{time=19:19.} 前一天我睡得很早，身体似乎正催着我照同样的作息再来一遍。',
        "No sunlight was left. I approached my phone and glanced at the time.{w} 19:19. The previous day, I'd gone to sleep very early, so my body was demanding that I repeat the schedule.": '外面已经没有日光。我走到手机旁看了一眼时间。{w}{time=19:19.} 前一天我睡得很早，身体似乎正催着我照同样的作息再来一遍。',
