        "The time was 7:45 a.m.{w} I set the phone back on the table while a glimpse of the dream I'd just had returned to me.": '时间已是{time=7:45.}{w}我把手机放回桌上，方才梦中的些许片段又浮上心头。',
        "The time was 7:45 a.m. I set the phone back on the table while a glimpse of the dream I'd just had returned to me.": '时间已是{time=7:45.}{w}我把手机放回桌上，方才梦中的些许片段又浮上心头。',
        "I didn't want to turn around so soon, so I kept going down, taking a few uncertain steps. There was nobody outside. I was the only person I could see being hit by the falling snow.": '我不想这么快就折返回去，便继续往下走，脚步有些迟疑。{w}外面空无一人。放眼望去，被落雪打着的只有我一个人。',
        "Would I only go when I'd made up my mind? If so, that would never happen. My whole life, I'd always avoided getting near that building. After the hellish day I'd spent there, that resistant part of me had only gotten stronger.": '我难道非得等下定决心了才会去吗？要真是这样，就永远去不成了。{w}我这一辈子都在避开那栋建筑。我在那里熬过地狱般的一天后，心里抗拒的那一面只会更强。',
        "Last night, I decided I'd go today, though. I really should... I should, because if I don't, Miiya's fate could be set in stone at any time.": '不过昨晚我已经决定，今天就去。我确实该去……{w}必须去，否则 Miiya 的命运随时都可能再无转圜余地。',
        "Am I just afraid of being alone in a world where Miiya's alive? I don't even think I'm that concerned about getting caught by the police. Right now, I'm all by myself, and I don't dislike it like I have in the past. ...It's probably because I know it's not indefinite, though.": '我难道只是害怕独自待在这个 Miiya 还活着的世界里吗？我甚至不觉得自己有多担心被警察抓到。{w}此刻我孤身一人，却不像过去那样讨厌这种感觉。……不过这大概是因为我知道，这种状态不会一直持续下去。',
        "A foggy Ramon street extended far ahead of me, but only a handful of people were walking, covering their heads due to the snow. I had never seen it so devoid of life. The entire area had begun to be coated by a thin layer of whiteness. I'd gotten there early enough to witness it before it was manually removed.": '雾气弥漫的拉蒙街在眼前延伸开去，路上只有零星几个人，因为下雪都遮着头。我从没见过这里如此人烟稀少。{w}整片街区已经覆上了一层薄薄的白色。我到得够早，才赶在有人清扫之前见到这一幕。',
        "I got more and more confused. ...Was the lack of people normal? Perhaps the few memories I had of my morning trips to school were mistaken. I was sure of one thing, though. When I'd taken Ramon street to go to classes, it had been to stop by Ina and eat something. While I couldn't be sure about the other places, I knew that not once had Ina been closed.": '我越来越困惑。……街上没人，是正常的吗？也许我早上上学的那点记忆本来就不可靠。{w} 但有一件事我很肯定。我走拉蒙街去上课，是为了顺路去伊娜吃点东西。别的地方我不敢说，可伊娜从来没有关过一天门。',
        '...I took my phone out and looked at the time. It was 7:59.': '……我掏出手机看了看时间。{time=7:59.}',
        '...I took my phone out and looked at the time. It was 7:59 a.m.': '……我掏出手机看了看时间。{time=7:59.}',
        "The classes started at {time=8:00}, and I'd always been under the impression that Ina opened half an hour earlier. I stepped under a thin stone roof to shield myself from the snow.": '上课时间是 {time=8:00}，而在我印象里，Ina 总是提前半小时开门。{w} 我站到一道窄窄的石檐下躲雪。',
        "The classes started at 8:00, and I'd always been under the impression that Ina opened half an hour earlier.{w} I stepped under a thin stone roof to shield myself from the snow.": '上课时间是 {time=8:00}，而在我印象里，Ina 总是提前半小时开门。{w} 我站到一道窄窄的石檐下躲雪。',
        "The classes started at 8:00, and I'd always been under the impression that Ina opened half an hour earlier. I stepped under a thin stone roof to shield myself from the snow.": '上课时间是 {time=8:00}，而在我印象里，Ina 总是提前半小时开门。{w} 我站到一道窄窄的石檐下躲雪。',
        "The classes started at 8:00 a.m., and I'd always been under the impression that Ina opened half an hour earlier.{w} I stepped under a thin stone roof to shield myself from the snow.": '上课时间是 {time=8:00}，而在我印象里，Ina 总是提前半小时开门。{w} 我站到一道窄窄的石檐下躲雪。',
        "The classes started at 8:00 a.m., and I'd always been under the impression that Ina opened half an hour earlier. I stepped under a thin stone roof to shield myself from the snow.": '上课时间是 {time=8:00}，而在我印象里，Ina 总是提前半小时开门。{w} 我站到一道窄窄的石檐下躲雪。',
        "...Wait. There's nobody here. Why did I not see anyone going to school?": '……等等。这里一个人都没有。{w} 我怎么没看见有人去上学？',
        'I turned abruptly to a nearby sound. An old man was walking toward me from the wider street.': '身旁传来响动，我猛地转过头。{w} 一位老人正从宽阔的街道那边朝我走来。',
        '"Oh?" He suddenly noticed I\'d addressed him and focused his expression, trying to hear my voice.': '「哦？」{w} 他这才注意到我在跟他说话，神情一紧，侧过耳朵想听清我的声音。',
        "I've never been there, but it's true that it's usually open. You think it should be?": '我没进去过，不过那家店平常确实开着。{w} 你觉得它现在该开门了？',
        "Yes. I think so. It's not only Ina, though. Everything's closed.": '是的，我想是这样。{w}不过不止Ina，所有店都关着门。',
        "...Maybe I'm wrong. ...It's just the impression I got.": '……{w}也许是我弄错了。……只是我有这种感觉罢了。',
        'Darfee was inside with a ring of keys in his hand. He unlocked the door and pushed the shutter all the way up. I approached nervously before he noticed me.': 'Darfee 就在里面，手里拿着一串钥匙。他打开门锁，把卷帘门一直推到了顶。{w}我趁他还没注意到我，忐忑地走上前去。',
        '...! Shiroya! What are you doing here so early?': '……！{w}Shiroya！你怎么这么早就来了？',
        '...I was waiting for you to open. I really wanted to go somewhere, for some reason. I thought you opened at {time=7:30}, though.': '……我在等你开门。不知怎么的，今天特别想出门。{w}不过我记着你 {time=7:30} 开门才对。',
        '...I was waiting for you to open. I really wanted to go somewhere, for some reason.{w} I thought you opened at 7:30, though.': '……我在等你开门。不知怎么的，今天特别想出门。{w}不过我记着你 {time=7:30} 开门才对。',
        '...I was waiting for you to open. I really wanted to go somewhere, for some reason. I thought you opened at 7:30, though.': '……我在等你开门。不知怎么的，今天特别想出门。{w}不过我记着你 {time=7:30} 开门才对。',
        '...I was waiting for you to open. I really wanted to go somewhere, for some reason.{w} I thought you opened at 7:30 a.m., though.': '……我在等你开门。不知怎么的，今天特别想出门。{w}不过我记着你 {time=7:30} 开门才对。',
        '...I was waiting for you to open. I really wanted to go somewhere, for some reason. I thought you opened at 7:30 a.m., though.': '……我在等你开门。不知怎么的，今天特别想出门。{w}不过我记着你 {time=7:30} 开门才对。',
        "I'd felt completely rested after waking up, but that had drastically changed. Staring at the wood, I kept biting the pastry, its warmth permeating my body.": '刚起床时我还觉得精神十足，如今却已大不相同。{w}我盯着木纹桌面，一口口咬着糕点，暖意渐渐渗进身体。',
        'I sat on one of the two chairs, its angle allowing Ramon to be seen. ...What had I been going on about? There were a number of pedestrians walking with an umbrella above them.': '我在两把椅子中的一把上坐下，这个角度正好能望见拉蒙街。{w}……我刚才都在胡思乱想些什么？路上有不少行人，头顶撑着伞。',
        "...! It's burning. It's a lot less hot when I make it at home.": '……！{w=0.5}烫死了。{w}我自己在家冲的，可没这么烫。',
        'I finished it in a few sips. Seconds later, I began to notice a faint headache, a frequent side effect coffee had on me.': '几口便见了底。{w}不过几秒，一阵隐隐的头痛就泛了上来——这是咖啡常给我带来的副作用。',
        'The man nodded, and Darfee packed both loaves into a thin bag that he handed over. "What else?"': '男人点点头，Darfee 把两条面包装进一只薄袋子递过去。{w}「还要别的吗？」',
        "It was hard to believe the place would evolve throughout the day, becoming a bar in the evening. Everyone had instantly left without sitting anywhere, as the chairs and stools were primarily used later in the day. The café was open the entire day on every day of the week. However, even though Darfee was the main person behind it, I'd frequently seen members of his family behind the counter. He couldn't do it all himself.": '很难想象这地方会在一天里变样，到了傍晚就成了酒吧。客人都是买完就走，谁也没坐下——椅子凳子多半是留给晚些时候用的。{w}咖啡馆一周七天，整天营业。可虽说这里主要靠 Darfee 操持，我也常看见他的家人站在柜台后。他一个人忙不过来。',
        "...Hm. I don't think so. I'm still hungry, but I don't really want another pastry.": '……嗯。{w}不用了。{w}我还饿着，可实在不想再吃一块点心。',
        "That's fine. ...Have you talked to your parents?": '也好。{w}……跟你父母联系过了吗？',
        "...Yeah, I called my mom the other day. ...We talked a bit, but they're gonna stay where they are. I already mentioned that's also what I prefer.": '……嗯，前几天给我妈打过电话。{w}……聊了几句，他们还是打算留在那边。我也说过，这样正合我意。',
        '...I think I prefer being alone, at least at home.': '……{w}我想我还是更喜欢一个人，至少在家里是这样。',
        "Oh, right, I guess he isn't aware that I'm still in the hospital. There's no reason he would know that without calling my parents. Will he find out on the 8th...? I don't know what I'll say if he does.": '啊，对了，他大概还不知道我还在住院。他又没给我父母打过电话，本来也没理由知道。{w}到了 8 号，他会知道吗……？到时候我该说什么，自己也不知道。',
        "...Not much. I went to Atsuki's house yesterday, and I was there for a while.": '……{w}没做什么。昨天去了 Atsuki 家，待了好一阵子。',
        "I don't want to put any pressure on you, but I'm curious if you have an idea about what you'll do. Last I heard, you were considering studying medicine, right? ...Sorry, maybe this isn't a good time to ask these questions.": '我不想给你压力，只是想知道你心里有没有个打算。上次听你说，你在考虑学医，对吧？{w}……抱歉，也许现在不该问这些。',
        "Don't worry... I don't know, though. I don't even know anything about medicine. It's just one of the few areas I think I could find interesting, but I'm not sure I want to keep studying. I think it's a lot more likely I'll try to find a job.": '别在意……不过，我自己也没想好。{w}我对医学本来就一无所知，只觉得那大概是我少数几个能提起兴趣的领域，可要不要继续读书，我也说不准。更有可能的是，我会去找份工作。',
        "Um... I don't know. Maybe. I'll think about it. Can I? I really appreciate it, though.": '呃……我不知道。{w}也许吧。{w}让我想想，可以吗？不过真的很谢谢你。',
        "Admittedly, if that had been proposed to me before December, I might've accepted immediately, as I'd been desperately lacking an actual path to take. But part of me just wanted the days to continue. It was a selfish and impossible wish, but the two days of December I'd redone had possessed a calmness I'd rarely known despite my own paranoia.": '说实话，这话要是放在十二月之前对我说，我大概会一口答应——那时的我正急需一条实实在在的路。{w}可我心里有一部分，只盼着这样的日子能一直延续下去。这个愿望自私，也不可能实现；而在我重新度过的那两天里，尽管满心猜疑，却有一种我极少体会过的安宁。',
        "Technically, at the moment, none of that mattered anymore. Studying medicine, moving away, getting a job... All of that would be irrelevant if I traveled to the past again or if I modified history. It would all have been for nothing. I would strive to prevent the death of a friend, isolating myself in a world where not a single thing of what I'd constantly worried about would occur.": '严格来说，此刻这些都已经无关紧要。学医、搬走、找工作……只要我再次回到过去、改写历史，这一切就都没有意义。{w}全都白费了。我会拼尽全力阻止朋友死去，把自己封闭在一个我担心的那些事统统不会发生的世界里。',
        "Before that, there was only an optional step. It was deciding. I still had the ability to choose. It wasn't true that going to the tower was essential for that.": '在那之前，只剩下一个可做可不做的步骤——做决定。{w}我仍然有权选择。去塔里并不是做决定的必要条件。',
        "No matter what I'd find there, deciding whether to change the past or not was possible, even though I'd done my best to believe that I'd never choose the latter. After all, I'd touched the Sekimeiya to change the past, and it would've been for nothing if I later decided not to.": '无论在那里发现什么，我仍然可以决定要不要改变过去——尽管我一直拼命让自己相信，我绝不会选择不改变。{w}毕竟，我碰 Sekimeiya 就是为了改变过去；如果最后决定不改，那一切不就白费了吗？',
        "...What would actually happen if I step aside and choose not to go to the tower again? I don't think that'd actually be so simple either. Late on the 15th, I disappeared from the tower, leaving the others behind. If everything happens as it did, Atsuki will try to travel to the past himself, and the problem of the recording will come back in full force.": '……如果我抽身而退，选择不再去那座塔，究竟会发生什么？我想事情也不会那么简单。{w}15日深夜，我从塔里消失，把其他人留在那里。若一切照旧发生，Atsuki 就会自己尝试穿越回过去，而录音的问题也会卷土重来。',
        "Even though I'd changed the past by calling my mother, that wouldn't necessarily prevent the events of the 15th from occurring—the version of me in the hospital at that moment could still travel back in time the same way I had. I knew that could be wrong. If I still went back in time after my mom told me about the call she got when I was in the hospital, I wouldn't ever try to change the past by calling her. The distinction between that Shiroya and me already somewhat existed.": '即便我曾给母亲打过电话、改动了过去，也未必能阻止15日的事件发生——那一刻躺在医院里的那个我，仍可能像我当初一样回到过去。{w}但我知道这也未必。如果母亲告诉过我，我住院时她接到过那通电话，而我仍然回到了过去，那我就绝不会再试图通过给她打电话改变过去。那个 Shiroya 与我之间，某种程度上已经有所不同。',
        "Then yes, of course, there was a way to prevent that from happening. Upon changing the past, the problematic variable was solely the other version of myself. Therefore, by removing that variable, I'd have everything I wanted. ...But that wasn't something I could seriously consider. That possibility simply didn't exist.": '那么，当然，确实有办法阻止这件事发生。{w}一旦改变过去，唯一成问题的变量就是另一个自己。也就是说，只要把这个变量消除掉，我想要的一切就都能得到。{w}……但这种事我不可能认真去考虑。{w}那种可能根本不存在。{w=0.8}{nw}',
        "That's mean... It's ¥300.": '真伤人……{w}300日元。',
        "I walked directly to Ramon street. In the distance, I had recognized a purse. ...After staring at it for a few seconds, I knew exactly where I'd seen it.": '我径直走向拉蒙街。远处，我认出了一只手提包。{w}……盯着它看了几秒，我便想起在哪儿见过它。',
        "I couldn't see anyone. There were multiple doors on both sides and more branching paths farther ahead.": '我看不到任何人。{w}两侧有好几扇门，前方还有更多岔路。',
        'I don\'t know what happened to me this morning, but today\'s definitely a school day. ...If that was really Isla, it could\'ve actually been her "friend", right? Was I correct, and her identity was Isla herself?': '不知道今天早上我到底是怎么了，可今天明明是上学的日子。……如果那真是 Isla，那会不会其实是她的「朋友」？{w}也就是说，我猜对了——那个人就是 Isla 本人？',
        "That thought had seemed a little strange in the tower for a number of reasons. She couldn't have gone back in time to repeat exactly what she'd lived through, but I had since learned that a long travel like that could've happened without needing to store energy for a month.": '在塔里时，这个念头因为种种原因显得有些奇怪。{w}她不可能回到过去，把经历过的事原样重演一遍；但后来我才知道，那样的长途穿越并不需要蓄能一个月也能完成。',
        "I went all the way down the street, where the footprints turned to the right. Once again, I was close to Atsuki's house, but the marks on the ground deviated from it. There was still no indication of them ending, and I wasn't able to see anyone farther ahead.": '我一路沿着街道走到尽头，脚印在那里向右拐去。{w} 我又一次来到 Atsuki 家附近，可地上的痕迹却偏离了那里。脚印仍没有到头的迹象，前方也望不见半个人影。',
        'Does Isla live here? ...Should I ring the bell?': '这里是 Isla 的家吗？{w} ……我该按门铃吗？',
        'Should I just watch from here and try to observe who the friend is? Maybe I should just leave. I know where Isla lives now, so I can try to prevent them from going to the tower on the 15th. That might be best.': '还是说，我该在这里守着，看看那位朋友究竟是谁？{w} 也许我干脆离开算了。我已经知道 Isla 住在哪里，可以设法阻止她们在十五号那天去塔里。{w} 那样或许最好。',
        "If I were to do that, and Isla's friend is really herself, she'd end up in the same situation as me, stuck in a world with two versions of her. What will happen after that? How would the world even take it? If they don't go to the tower, Isla won't be able to travel to the past. Will that simply not matter, and both of them will continue to live? If her existence gets overwritten, mine will be too, right?": '可要是我真那么做，而 Isla 的朋友确实就是她自己，那她就会落到和我一样的境地——被困在一个同时存在两个自己的世界里。{w} 之后会怎样？世界又承受得住吗？如果她们不去那座塔，Isla 就无法穿越到过去。难道这根本无关紧要，两个人都能继续活下去？{w} 可要是她的存在被覆盖，我的存在不也会一样吗？',
        "It shouldn't be, right? Even if I don't like any of the choices, there has to be one I prefer. If they're all equally bad, then I can just choose one to stick to, can't I? I can just decide my entire life like that.": '不该如此吧？就算没有哪个选项让我满意，总该有一个我更中意的。{w} 要是它们一样糟，那我随便挑一个坚持到底不就行了？我的人生就可以这样定下来。',
        "I looked at the way I'd come from. Nobody was there.": '我回头望向来路。{w} 空无一人。',
        "I had felt the same sensation as the day before. I didn't know if I'd noticed a sound or a movement, but my head had suddenly turned to that corner. I looked at the ground, but many footprints were there, and due to the falling snow, it was hard to tell which were recent.": '我又有了和昨天相同的感觉。我分不清自己是听见了声响还是看到了动静，头却猛地转向了那个角落。{w} 我低头看地面，那里脚印杂乱，加上落雪不停，很难分辨哪些是新的。',
        "Is it just me? ...It's not, right? Yesterday, someone was definitely following me. Did I only imagine it this time?": '是我的错觉吗？……不是吧？{w} 昨天确实有人在跟踪我。这一次难道只是我多心了？',
        'Could it be Isla...? No, the footprints I saw yesterday belonged to an adult.': '会是 Isla 吗……？{w} 不对，昨天我看到的脚印分明属于一个成年人。',
        "I was still fairly hungry and far from my apartment, but if I went home in a straight line, I'd have to go through all the deserted streets before getting back to the center. I didn't want to do that if someone was observing me in secret.": '我还挺饿的，离家又远，可要是径直回家，就得先穿过那一整片冷清的街巷，才能回到市中心。{w} 若真有人在暗中窥视我，我可不想走那条路。',
        'The wind was noticeably stronger higher up. The terrain there was plain, and the way branched out. Higher still was the entrance to the caves, whereas the path to the right would take me close to home.': '越往高处，风明显越强。那里地势平坦，道路分了岔。{w}再往上便是洞穴入口，而右边的路则能通到我家附近。',
        "I didn't know if I could accomplish it, but the choice was about whether to try it. I could be caught by the police or be beaten to the punch by someone else from the future. If the latter happened, I was letting it happen by not acting. It was my own fault. It was all a mess, and there was no way not to make it one. I wanted to talk to Miiya again, but even if I saved her, that wouldn't happen. She hadn't deserved to die, so I could trade positions with her. I wouldn't even be doing it for some twisted form of recognition, as nobody would know what had happened—my other self would exist in my place, and I'd step aside.": '我不知道自己能否做到，但这个选择的关键只在于要不要去尝试。我可能被警察抓住，也可能被另一个来自未来的人抢先一步。若是后者，那就等于我袖手旁观、任由它发生，是我自己的错。{w}一切都乱成一团，而且无论如何都注定会乱。我想再和 Miiya 说说话，可就算救了她，这也办不到。{w}她本不该死，那么我可以和她互换位置。我这么做甚至不是为了某种扭曲的认可——没有人会知道发生了什么；另一个我会取代我的位置，而我退到一旁。',
        'I looked at the tower, knowing the Sekimeiya was inside. Who else in that town knew about what had happened on the 15th? I wished I could know that.': '我望着那座塔，知道 Sekimeiya 就在里面。{w}这座镇子上，还有谁知道15号那天发生了什么？我真希望能知道。',
        "What that meant was that she had a few days for herself. Immediately after that, Shiroya didn't know what shape the future would take, but she believed that she and Atsuki would get through it. Her goal was solely to enjoy the remaining time she had. Despite that, seeing a bustling street while she walked down the mountain, she only felt empty.": '这意味着，她还有几天属于自己的时间。之后会变成什么样，Shiroya 无从知晓，但她相信自己和 Atsuki 能撑过去。她的目标只是好好享受剩下的时光。{w}然而，下山途中望着熙熙攘攘的街道，她心里却只觉得空落落的。',
        'She turned around and saw a still car in the middle of the road. Its driver burst out and dashed to the front. "Oh my God! Are you okay!? Hey...!"': '她回过头，只见路中央停着一辆一动不动的车。司机冲下车，直奔车头。{w}「天哪！你没事吧！？喂……！」',
        '"What the fuck!? I barely tapped him! Don\'t fucking tell me...!" What had happened wasn\'t a mystery; Shiroya was stunned into immobility. As a handful of bystanders ran to the car, she desperately wished that no one\'s life had been lost.': '「妈的！？我不过轻轻撞了他一下！别他妈告诉我……！」{w}出了什么事并不难猜；Shiroya 吓得动弹不得。几个路人朝车边跑去，她拼命祈祷没有人因此丧命。',
        'Hey! ...Say something! Come on! Say something!': '「喂！……说句话啊！{w}拜托，说句话啊！」',
        "You've gotta be fucking kidding! ...Hey! Wake up! Man! He just ran out in front of me! There was no way I could've stopped in time! Come on, say something! Please!": '「你他妈开什么玩笑！……喂！醒醒啊！{w}老天，是他自己冲到车前的！我根本来不及刹车！{w}快啊，说句话！求你了！」',
        "H-He's right, I saw it too. He suddenly crossed the road. It looked like he started running when he saw her.": '「他、他说得对，我也看见了。那个人突然横穿马路。{w}好像一看见她就跑了起来。」',
        'Soon, an ambulance came, but everyone was already aware it was futile. The body was quickly placed on a stretcher and injected with a substance. Losing no time, he was brought in through the rear door of the vehicle, and it sped away.': '不久，救护车赶到了，但所有人都明白已经无济于事。{w} 遗体很快被抬上担架，注射了某种药剂。救护人员片刻不停，从车尾门把遗体送进车内，车子随即疾驰而去。',
        "She had recently been forced to accept the cruelty of reality, but she hadn't been prepared for the same thing to happen again. She denied it. She told herself that she'd mistaken his face or that everyone had failed to notice he'd still been alive. ...If everything was a dream, it would resolve all of her problems at once.": '近来她已经被迫接受了现实的残酷，却还没准备好面对同样的事再次发生。{w} 她不愿承认。她告诉自己，是她认错了他的脸，或是所有人都没发现他其实还活着。……如果这一切都是梦，那她的所有问题便能一并解决。',
        '...Sh-Shiroya. Mirana.': '「……Sh、Shiroya。{w}Mirana。」',
        "The incident of the 15th had already occurred, and in the distance, she could see Ashiya Tower. It had been a while ago when she'd touched the Sekimeiya in the bathroom, but she hadn't set foot in that building again.": '15日的事件早已发生，远处能望见芦屋塔。{w} 她在洗手间触碰到 Sekimeiya 已是许久之前的事，自那以后，她再没有踏进过那栋楼。',
        'At 21:00, the main shutter had unlocked. However, nobody had been found alive inside.': '{time=21}，主卷帘门解锁了。然而，里面没有发现任何生还者。',
        'At 9 p.m., the main shutter had unlocked. However, nobody had been found alive inside.': '{time=21}，主卷帘门解锁了。然而，里面没有发现任何生还者。',
        "Two people had been found dead. Their names were Naomi Cabca and Isla Majutsu. Drops of blood that hadn't belonged to them had been found on the floor, but the whereabouts of the remaining people were a mystery. After raiding the building, the police had failed to find them.": '有两具尸体被发现，分别是 Naomi Cabca 和 Isla Majutsu。{w} 地板上还找到了不属于她们的血迹，但其余人的下落仍是个谜。警方突入大楼搜查后，始终没能找到他们。',
        "It had been soon confirmed that more people should've been there. Counting everyone who'd scanned their tickets in the entrance, the names of the people who hadn't evacuated were Atsuki Hakutoki, Shiroya Mirana, Sai Yomiya, Akaro Esata, and Erina Majutsu. What had happened to them? It was impossible they had left the building during their twelve hours of imprisonment, as the whole structure had been observed from the outside since that morning.": '很快便确认，本该有更多人在里面。根据入口处所有验票记录，未撤离者分别是 Atsuki Hakutoki、Shiroya Mirana、Sai Yomiya、Akaro Esata 和 Erina Majutsu。{w} 他们究竟遭遇了什么？从那天早晨起，整栋建筑便一直处于外部监视之下，因此他们不可能在被困的十二小时里离开大楼。',
        'The police concluded that Isla Majutsu, the second victim, had died many hours after {time=9.} Yet, they had very few clues as to what had occurred. Almost all the recorded footage had been erased, and what remained was useless. The belongings of the two victims contained nothing of importance, and neither did any place in the building. That only made things more confusing, because despite the belief of many citizens, nothing else had been stolen beyond the gemstones that had been found in the morning.': '警方断定，第二名死者 Isla Majutsu 是在 {time=9.} 之后数小时才死去的。{w} 然而，关于究竟发生了什么，他们掌握的线索寥寥无几。几乎所有监控录像都被抹去，剩下的也毫无用处。两名死者的遗物中没有重要物品，大楼各处也同样一无所获。{w} 这反而让事情更加扑朔迷离：许多市民相信失窃的不只是宝石，但除了早上发现的那批宝石之外，并没有其他东西失窃。',
        'The police concluded that Isla Majutsu, the second victim, had died many hours after 9:00.{w} Yet, they had very few clues as to what had occurred. Almost all the recorded footage had been erased, and what remained was useless. The belongings of the two victims contained nothing of importance, and neither did any place in the building.{w} That only made things more confusing, because despite the belief of many citizens, nothing else had been stolen beyond the gemstones that had been found in the morning.': '警方断定，第二名死者 Isla Majutsu 是在 {time=9.} 之后数小时才死去的。{w} 然而，关于究竟发生了什么，他们掌握的线索寥寥无几。几乎所有监控录像都被抹去，剩下的也毫无用处。两名死者的遗物中没有重要物品，大楼各处也同样一无所获。{w} 这反而让事情更加扑朔迷离：许多市民相信失窃的不只是宝石，但除了早上发现的那批宝石之外，并没有其他东西失窃。',
        'The police concluded that Isla Majutsu, the second victim, had died many hours after 9:00. Yet, they had very few clues as to what had occurred. Almost all the recorded footage had been erased, and what remained was useless. The belongings of the two victims contained nothing of importance, and neither did any place in the building. That only made things more confusing, because despite the belief of many citizens, nothing else had been stolen beyond the gemstones that had been found in the morning.': '警方断定，第二名死者 Isla Majutsu 是在 {time=9.} 之后数小时才死去的。{w} 然而，关于究竟发生了什么，他们掌握的线索寥寥无几。几乎所有监控录像都被抹去，剩下的也毫无用处。两名死者的遗物中没有重要物品，大楼各处也同样一无所获。{w} 这反而让事情更加扑朔迷离：许多市民相信失窃的不只是宝石，但除了早上发现的那批宝石之外，并没有其他东西失窃。',
        'The police concluded that Isla Majutsu, the second victim, had died many hours after 9 a.m.{w} Yet, they had very few clues as to what had occurred. Almost all the recorded footage had been erased, and what remained was useless. The belongings of the two victims contained nothing of importance, and neither did any place in the building.{w} That only made things more confusing, because despite the belief of many citizens, nothing else had been stolen beyond the gemstones that had been found in the morning.': '警方断定，第二名死者 Isla Majutsu 是在 {time=9.} 之后数小时才死去的。{w} 然而，关于究竟发生了什么，他们掌握的线索寥寥无几。几乎所有监控录像都被抹去，剩下的也毫无用处。两名死者的遗物中没有重要物品，大楼各处也同样一无所获。{w} 这反而让事情更加扑朔迷离：许多市民相信失窃的不只是宝石，但除了早上发现的那批宝石之外，并没有其他东西失窃。',
        'The police concluded that Isla Majutsu, the second victim, had died many hours after 9 a.m. Yet, they had very few clues as to what had occurred. Almost all the recorded footage had been erased, and what remained was useless. The belongings of the two victims contained nothing of importance, and neither did any place in the building. That only made things more confusing, because despite the belief of many citizens, nothing else had been stolen beyond the gemstones that had been found in the morning.': '警方断定，第二名死者 Isla Majutsu 是在 {time=9.} 之后数小时才死去的。{w} 然而，关于究竟发生了什么，他们掌握的线索寥寥无几。几乎所有监控录像都被抹去，剩下的也毫无用处。两名死者的遗物中没有重要物品，大楼各处也同样一无所获。{w} 这反而让事情更加扑朔迷离：许多市民相信失窃的不只是宝石，但除了早上发现的那批宝石之外，并没有其他东西失窃。',
        'This was the first public statement: "Five people who were trapped in Ashiya Tower on the 15th are still to be found. The deaths of Naomi Cabca and Isla Majutsu are being investigated. However, access to Ashiya Tower is strictly prohibited, as a potentially dangerous gas was found within it in high quantities. While investigating the motive behind the attack is not the highest priority, aside from the gemstones found immediately after the authorities secured the situation, no other valuable items were found to be missing, indicating that theft may not have been the goal."': '这是首次公开声明：{w}「15日被困在芦屋塔的五人至今下落不明。Naomi Cabca 与 Isla Majutsu 的死亡正在调查中。然而，由于楼内发现了大量可能具有危险性的气体，芦屋塔严禁进入。{w} 虽然查清袭击动机并非当务之急，但除了当局控制现场后立即发现的宝石之外，没有发现其他贵重物品失窃，这表明盗窃或许并非目的。」',
        "It was the next day. She had slept and eaten, but it couldn't be said she'd done so for any particular reason. The miserable way she felt... it was all too familiar to her, but the difference in potency was immense.": '已是第二天。她睡过，也吃过东西，却很难说这是为了什么。{w} 那种凄惨的心境……她再熟悉不过，只是这一次强烈得远非往日可比。',
        "That was the fundamental dispute in Yushibana. The older citizens, aware of the way Ashiya had once been, were becoming outnumbered by the recent influx of people Ashiya had brought, who supported the now-corporation due to financial reasons and were ignorant of its roots. After the 15th of December, the backlash Ashiya had received had been enormous. Through their poor security measures, they'd let two people be killed, and they hadn't publicly responded well to the ordeal, blinded by their battle against Xyn.": '这正是丰花最根本的矛盾。熟知芦屋昔日作风的老一辈市民，正逐渐在人数上被芦屋近来引入的大批外来者超过；这些外来者出于经济上的理由支持如今这家企业，却对其根源一无所知。{w} 12月15日之后，芦屋遭到猛烈声讨。由于安保措施不力，他们让两人丢了性命；又因为被与 Xyn 的争斗蒙蔽了双眼，面对这场变故也没能在公众面前妥善应对。',
        'All Ashiya kept saying was that they were still investigating what had happened—that they would find the missing people and expose those working as part of Xyn. Then, the tower would quickly open again. However, everyone knew that nobody had entered that building since the 15th due to the unknown gas, so those statements were seen as a haphazard, lacking defense.': '芦屋只是一再声称，他们仍在调查发生了什么，会找到失踪者，也会把为 Xyn 效力的人揪出来。随后，塔会很快重新开放。{w} 然而人人都知道，自15日以来，由于不明气体，没人进过那栋楼，因此这些说辞被视为草率而站不住脚的辩解。',
        "Where were the remaining people? Why had they not been in the tower? One of them had died in a car accident, and another one had been unable to explain anything to the police. It didn't make sense; they should've been in the tower, late on the 15th. ...And what about the other three? They hadn't been found anywhere.": '其余的人在哪里？他们为什么不在塔里？{w} 其中一人死于车祸，另一人对警方什么也解释不了。这说不通——15日深夜，他们本该在塔里。……那另外三人呢？到处都找不到他们。',
        "Alone in her apartment, she didn't look away until the signal resolved. When it did, someone else was speaking about the same topic, but very far from the tower.": '她独自待在公寓里，直到信号恢复才移开视线。{w} 信号恢复后，电视里是另一个人在谈同一件事，但那人离塔楼很远。',
        "It became known that someone had offered to buy the tower from Ashiya, and they had accepted due to their awful position. In the blink of an eye, Ashiya, which had been seen as a source of power and wealth within Yushibana, had entirely vanished. Who had been the buyer, however? It didn't seem that information was widely available.": '人们后来得知，有人提出要向芦屋买下这座塔，而芦屋因为处境糟糕便答应了。转眼之间，曾在丰花被视为权势与财富象征的芦屋就彻底消失了。{w} 可买家到底是谁？这个消息似乎并没有多少人知道。',
        'After so long, there was a reason why Shiroya and her cat had their heads out their window. It was October 4th, and the sight they were beholding would no longer exist the following day.': '过了这么久，Shiroya 和她的猫之所以把头探出窗外，是有原因的。{w} 今天是10月4日，而他们眼前的景象，到了明天就不复存在了。',
        "At {time=12}, the demolition would begin. There'd been no correspondence from Ashiya in months. The facts behind the unknown gas and the deaths within the tower were still shrouded in darkness. The interior of the building had been investigated a few times after the 15th, but nothing useful had been figured out. Ashiya had removed everything of value, so after it was verified by the new owner, the demolition seemed to pose no risk aside from the dust it would scatter across the hill behind the tower.": '到了{time=12}，拆除便会开始。芦屋已经几个月没有任何联络。不明气体与塔内死亡事件背后的真相，仍笼罩在黑暗之中。{w} 15日之后，楼内被调查过几次，却始终没能查出什么有用的东西。芦屋已将值钱之物尽数搬走，经新主人确认后，此次拆除除了会让尘土散落到塔后的山丘上，似乎不会造成其他风险。',
        "At 12:00, the demolition would begin. There'd been no correspondence from Ashiya in months. The facts behind the unknown gas and the deaths within the tower were still shrouded in darkness.{w} The interior of the building had been investigated a few times after the 15th, but nothing useful had been figured out. Ashiya had removed everything of value, so after it was verified by the new owner, the demolition seemed to pose no risk aside from the dust it would scatter across the hill behind the tower.": '到了{time=12}，拆除便会开始。芦屋已经几个月没有任何联络。不明气体与塔内死亡事件背后的真相，仍笼罩在黑暗之中。{w} 15日之后，楼内被调查过几次，却始终没能查出什么有用的东西。芦屋已将值钱之物尽数搬走，经新主人确认后，此次拆除除了会让尘土散落到塔后的山丘上，似乎不会造成其他风险。',
