        "At 12 p.m., the demolition would begin. There'd been no correspondence from Ashiya in months. The facts behind the unknown gas and the deaths within the tower were still shrouded in darkness. The interior of the building had been investigated a few times after the 15th, but nothing useful had been figured out. Ashiya had removed everything of value, so after it was verified by the new owner, the demolition seemed to pose no risk aside from the dust it would scatter across the hill behind the tower.": '到了{time=12}，拆除便会开始。芦屋已经几个月没有任何联络。不明气体与塔内死亡事件背后的真相，仍笼罩在黑暗之中。{w} 15日之后，楼内被调查过几次，却始终没能查出什么有用的东西。芦屋已将值钱之物尽数搬走，经新主人确认后，此次拆除除了会让尘土散落到塔后的山丘上，似乎不会造成其他风险。',
        'She raised her entire body next. On the screen was a man speaking into a microphone. She grabbed the remote and increased the volume, staring at the text beneath him.': '她随即直起了身子。屏幕上是一个对着话筒讲话的男人。{w}她抓起遥控器调高音量，目光落在男人下方的文字上。',
        "Another one was quickly found afterward, belonging to Sai Yomiya. Finally, when almost all the debris had been removed, Erina Majutsu's body was found. The three bodies were heavily crushed, and it's believed some parts of them weren't found.": '「紧接着又发现了另一具，属于 Sai Yomiya。最后，当瓦砾几乎清理殆尽时，Erina Majutsu 的遗体也被找到了。{w}三具遗体都严重压毁，据信还有部分残骸未能找到。」',
        "As of now, what happened is unknown. While the bodies were severely smashed, they were not fully decomposed. It has been determined that they died the day of the demolition. However, the possibility of the demolition itself causing their deaths has been thoroughly refuted. It was properly verified that nobody was in the building before the impact, and that's not the only reason. The three bodies were below all the rubble. If the building had really fallen on them, their condition would be even worse. Strangely, some of the body parts that were recovered are practically intact, despite the state of most others. There was no dust discovered on the bodies—neither inside their clothes nor in their mouths. For this reason, the situation is being handled very carefully, as the truth behind it might be appalling. It has been considered that the bodies were disposed of within the rubble following the demolition since they couldn't have been directly hit by it. However, given how deep they were and the absence of blood around them, that was immediately discarded as well. Even though the abundance of the unidentified old gas has disappeared, around the three bodies was where the last remaining traces were found. This is an extremely delicate case that has carried unsolved questions with it all year. Now that everyone who was trapped in the building has been found, the authorities will do all they can to figure out what happened on that day.": '「截至目前，事情经过仍不清楚。遗体虽然严重损毁，却并未完全腐烂。现已确定他们死于拆除当天。{w}不过，拆除本身导致他们死亡的可能性已被彻底排除。事前已经确认，爆破前建筑物里没有人，而且这还不是唯一的理由。{w}三具遗体位于所有瓦砾之下。若建筑物真的压在他们身上，遗体的状况只会更糟。奇怪的是，尽管大部分残骸损毁严重，找到的部分肢体却几乎完好无损。{w}遗体上没有发现灰尘——衣服里、嘴里都没有。正因为如此，这起案件才被处理得如此谨慎，因为背后的真相可能令人震惊。{w}有人推测，既然遗体不可能是被直接砸中的，那就是在拆除之后被人丢进瓦砾堆里的。然而考虑到遗体埋藏之深、周围又没有血迹，这一推测也立即被排除了。{w}尽管大量来源不明的陈旧气体已经消散，最后残留的痕迹正是在这三具遗体周围发现的。{w}这桩极其棘手的案件，整整一年都悬而未决。如今被困于建筑物内的人已全部找到，当局将竭尽全力查明那一天究竟发生了什么。」',
        'Thursday was two days away. Every Thursday morning, an event would be held in the tower. That was the day I chose to step into the building for the second time and find the Sekimeiya that was surely confined inside.': '距离周四还有两天。{w}每逢周四上午，塔里都会举办活动。我选中了那一天，第二次踏进那栋大楼，去找必定被关在里面的 Sekimeiya。',
        "I tried to breathe properly. If I wasn't beaten to it, I only had one more day that I'd chosen to give myself, hopelessly refusing to let them end so soon. And the very next one, I'd go to the tower in the morning and think about the best way to act. Then, I'd put that into effect that very night.": '我试着让呼吸平稳下来。如果没人抢在前头，我给自己留下的日子就只剩一天了——我还在徒劳地不肯让它们这么快结束。{w}第二天，我会一早就去那座塔，琢磨最合适的行动方式。然后当天晚上就付诸行动。',
        'At last, I saw the absence of brown at my right. As I thought, it extended all the way down, leading to a dirt road close to my home.': '终于，我看到右侧有一片地方不再是褐色。{w}果然，那条路一直向下延伸，通往我家附近的一条土路。',
        'I started to feel a little nervous. Had I actually felt someone behind me once more, or was it paranoia...? I just needed to go home. I looked by my feet.': '我开始有些不安。究竟是真的又感觉到身后有人，还是我多心了……？我只要回家就好。{w}我低头看了看脚边。',
        '...I was close to the end of the street, where it curved into another one. If someone was watching me from behind at that moment, they had to be in eyeshot.': '……{w}我快到街尾了，街道在那里拐向另一条路。此刻若有人从身后盯着我，就一定在我的视野里。',
        "It immediately became visible. It was a police officer. ...But that wasn't all, so I didn't stop.": '那一抹蓝色立刻清晰起来。是一名警察。{w}……但还不止如此，所以我没有停下脚步。',
        '...I... was feeling like someone was following me just now. Could it have been this person?': '……{w}我……刚才一直觉得有人在跟着我。会不会就是这个人？',
        "Mine...? ...It's Shiroya Mirana.": '我的……？{w}……我叫 Shiroya Mirana。',
        'He looked at me and silently wrote on the paper. Then, he suddenly smiled, completely shifting his expression.': '他看了我一眼，默默在纸上写着什么。{w}随后忽然露出笑容，神情为之一变。',
        'These are mine. I looked at the ground earlier specifically for this. ...And these were definitely not here before.': '这些是我的。我之前特意看过地面，就是为了这个。{w}……而这些印子，之前绝对没有。',
        'It must be these since they end where the car was. They also resemble the ones I saw yesterday.': '一定是这些——脚印正好停在车子原先停着的地方。{w}而且和我昨天见过的很像。',
        "I kept following them in reverse, hoping they would lead somewhere. However, I immediately realized that wouldn't work. The more I walked, the more the footprints faded due to the falling snow. Soon, I could hardly even make out their shape.": '我顺着脚印一路往回追，希望能追到什么地方。可很快就明白这行不通。{w}雪还在下，我越往前走，脚印就越淡，没多久便几乎辨不出形状。',
        '16:00 already... I was outside for so many hours.': '都已经 {time=16} 了啊……我在外面待了那么多个小时。',
        '4 p.m. already... I was outside for so many hours.': '都已经 {time=16} 了啊……我在外面待了那么多个小时。',
        "The person who was just arrested... Could they have been from Xyn? If so, that's a new occurrence, because we were told that no members had been caught yet.": '刚才被捕的那个人……会不会是 Xyn 的人？{w} 要真是，那倒是新情况，因为我们听说还没有成员落网。',
        "I'll change the past drastically for the first time by going to Atsuki's house and taking the tickets we bought. Later, I can go to Isla's house and either attempt to talk with whoever her friend really is or try to prevent them from going on the 15th in the same way.": '这将是我第一次大幅改变过去：去 Atsuki 家，把我们买好的票取走。{w} 之后我再去 Isla 家，试着和她那位朋友——不管对方到底是谁——谈谈；或者用同样的办法，阻止她们在 15 号去那里。',
        "Right now, the 15th is the failsafe in case I can't find the Sekimeiya beforehand. If I let everything repeat, I'll be able to touch it again on that day. Hell, I could see where the recorder even came from, or even stay there for a month, depending on whether it's real or not.": '眼下，万一我事先找不到 Sekimeiya，15 号就是最后的保险。只要让一切照旧重演，我那天就能再次碰到它。{w} 说不定还能弄清录音笔到底从哪儿来，甚至在那里待上一个月——就看录音是不是真的了。',
        "But if Atsuki, Isla, Erina, and I don't go to the event, it will all be considerably different. What if something causes the attack to fail? What if Katei and Ashiya are able to unlock the exit this time?": '可要是 Atsuki、Isla、Erina 和我都不去参加活动，一切就会大不相同。{w} 万一某个变故让袭击失败了呢？{w} 万一这次 Katei 和芦屋能打开出口呢？',
        "That would get rid of the only guaranteed time where getting the Sekimeiya again will be possible. So, if I don't find it anywhere on Thursday, maybe waiting until the 15th is the best call.": '那样一来，唯一能确定再次拿到 Sekimeiya 的时机就没了。{w} 所以，如果周四我哪儿都找不到它，也许等到 15 号才是上策。',
        'Now I know something very important. At close to {time=16}, a very long travel took place, and it reached through the walls of the tower... Could I place myself in that range, or would I be arrested?': '现在我知道了一件非常重要的事。接近 {time=16} 时，发生过一次跨度极大的穿越，其范围甚至穿过了塔的墙壁……{w} 我能让自己也进入那个范围吗？还是说我会被抓起来？',
        'Now I know something very important. At close to 16:00, a very long travel took place, and it reached through the walls of the tower...{w} Could I place myself in that range, or would I be arrested?': '现在我知道了一件非常重要的事。接近 {time=16} 时，发生过一次跨度极大的穿越，其范围甚至穿过了塔的墙壁……{w} 我能让自己也进入那个范围吗？还是说我会被抓起来？',
        'Now I know something very important. At close to 16:00, a very long travel took place, and it reached through the walls of the tower... Could I place myself in that range, or would I be arrested?': '现在我知道了一件非常重要的事。接近 {time=16} 时，发生过一次跨度极大的穿越，其范围甚至穿过了塔的墙壁……{w} 我能让自己也进入那个范围吗？还是说我会被抓起来？',
        'Now I know something very important. At close to 4 p.m., a very long travel took place, and it reached through the walls of the tower...{w} Could I place myself in that range, or would I be arrested?': '现在我知道了一件非常重要的事。接近 {time=16} 时，发生过一次跨度极大的穿越，其范围甚至穿过了塔的墙壁……{w} 我能让自己也进入那个范围吗？还是说我会被抓起来？',
        'Now I know something very important. At close to 4 p.m., a very long travel took place, and it reached through the walls of the tower... Could I place myself in that range, or would I be arrested?': '现在我知道了一件非常重要的事。接近 {time=16} 时，发生过一次跨度极大的穿越，其范围甚至穿过了塔的墙壁……{w} 我能让自己也进入那个范围吗？还是说我会被抓起来？',
        "Even though everyone close to the building will know that someone with my name is inside, would they recognize my face? All I'd have to do would be spot Vaisude and get very close to him at 16:00.": '虽说靠近大楼的人都会知道有个和我同名的人在里面，可他们认得我的脸吗？我只需找到 Vaisude，在 {time=16.} 时贴近他就行了。',
        "Even though everyone close to the building will know that someone with my name is inside, would they recognize my face? All I'd have to do would be spot Vaisude and get very close to him at 4 p.m.": '虽说靠近大楼的人都会知道有个和我同名的人在里面，可他们认得我的脸吗？我只需找到 Vaisude，在 {time=16.} 时贴近他就行了。',
        "That would make me travel to the 24th of November. This would be the best possible outcome. I'd make it far enough to be the first person to find the Sekimeiya in the mountains, stop all of this at the source, and save everyone.": '那样我就会穿越到 11 月 24 日。这将是再好不过的结果。{w} 我能回到足够早的时候，成为第一个在山里找到 Sekimeiya 的人，从源头阻止这一切，救下所有人。',
        "I didn't think Vaisude had lied, but I'd somewhat changed history when I'd called my mom, and I didn't know what extra changes that implied. Furthermore, I had no idea if someone else would change the past differently; the butterfly effect could've easily prevented the 16:00 travel from happening.": '我不觉得 Vaisude 撒了谎，可我给妈妈打电话时已经多少改变了历史，不知道这还牵连出哪些变化。更何况，我根本不清楚别人会不会以别的方式改变过去；蝴蝶效应轻而易举就能让 {time=16} 的那次穿越不再发生。',
        "I didn't think Vaisude had lied, but I'd somewhat changed history when I'd called my mom, and I didn't know what extra changes that implied. Furthermore, I had no idea if someone else would change the past differently; the butterfly effect could've easily prevented the 4 p.m. travel from happening.": '我不觉得 Vaisude 撒了谎，可我给妈妈打电话时已经多少改变了历史，不知道这还牵连出哪些变化。更何况，我根本不清楚别人会不会以别的方式改变过去；蝴蝶效应轻而易举就能让 {time=16} 的那次穿越不再发生。',
        "I had been going to sleep very early, so I was pretty tired. However, there was something I had to do that I didn't want to leave for the next day. I'd been yawning and stretching on the floor, but I felt I had a bit of time before going to bed.": '最近我睡得很早，所以这会儿已经相当疲倦。可有件事我必须去做，不想拖到第二天。{w} 我躺在地板上打着哈欠、伸着懒腰，不过感觉离上床还有一点时间。',
        'The sky had gotten a lot darker, and the icy air almost changed my mind. I quickly put my coat and boots back on, checked that everything was in my purse, and stepped out after turning off the lights.': '天色已暗了许多，冰冷的空气差点让我打退堂鼓。{w} 我赶紧重新穿上外套和靴子，确认包里的东西都在，关灯后出了门。',
        "Oh, it's still valid, don't worry. They last a whole year. Anyway, December 1st? Let me see.": '哦，还来得及，不用担心，有效期整整一年。{w} 话说回来，十二月一日是吧？我看看。',
        "I hadn't been sure what day to say, but I hadn't wanted to ask for the previous day's. If I went back to November, I'd change the past in a considerable way. Then, the butterfly effect could affect what I was doing. I knew each digit of a winning lottery number was manually drawn every time, so if I changed the past and made it back to the same day, it was entirely possible the latest winning number would differ. A mere millisecond of difference could result in a different draw. I'd chosen December 1st because it was the next day after Miiya's death, and I didn't know how far back I'd end up being able to go.": '我拿不准该报哪一天，却又不愿问前一天的开奖结果。若回到十一月，过去就会被大幅改动，随之而来的蝴蝶效应也可能波及我眼下要做的事。{w} 我知道中奖号码的每一位都是人工摇出来的，所以只要改动过去、再回到同一天，最新的中奖号码完全可能变掉——哪怕只差一毫秒，摇出的结果也会不同。我选十二月一日，是因为那是 Miiya 死后的第二天，而我不清楚自己究竟能回到多久以前。',
        "I see. That's unfortunate. Do you want to try again?": '这样啊，那真是可惜。{w} 你要再买一组吗？',
        'All right. How much would I have won if all the digits matched?': '好的。{w} 要是数字全对，能中多少钱？',
        "Let me see... The main prize money of December 1st was ¥917,999,011. It's even higher now. Nobody's won the jackpot in a while.": '我看看……{w} 十二月一日的头奖金额是 917,999,011 日元。{w} 现在更高了，已经有一阵子没人中头奖。',
        '30-05-12-31-15-26--24... 30-05-12-31-15-26--24...': '30-05-12{w=0.3}-31-15-26{w=0.4}--24……{w=1} 30-05-12-31-15-26{w=0.3}--24……',
        "Yes, but only before 17:00. You don't have to worry about this today since the next Lotus-6 will be held on the 5th, this Thursday.": '可以，不过得在 {time=17.} 之前买。今天不用着急，下一期 Lotus-6 是这周四（5号）开奖。',
        "Yes, but only before 5 p.m. You don't have to worry about this today since the next Lotus-6 will be held on the 5th, this Thursday.": '可以，不过得在 {time=17.} 之前买。今天不用着急，下一期 Lotus-6 是这周四（5号）开奖。',
        "Me too. I'm sorry for having so many questions, but if I won, would my identity have to be revealed?": '我也希望如此。{w} 抱歉问了这么多，不过如果我中了奖，身份会被公开吗？',
        "For that, I'd have to duplicate my bank card or try to take it out of the other me's purse. What would I do if I saw that so much money was added and immediately taken from my account? If it was investigated, security cameras would probably see me in the bank.": '为此，我得复制一张银行卡，或者设法从另一个我的钱包里把卡拿出来。{w} 要是我看到账户里突然多了一大笔钱、转眼又被人取走，我会怎么做？要是有人查起来，监控多半会拍到我在银行里的身影。',
        "30-05-12-31-15-26--24... I'm pretty sure that was it.": '30{w=0.2}-05{w=0.1}-12{w=0.2}-31{w=0.4}-15{w=0.1}-26{w=0.8}--24……{w} 应该就是这个。',
        'My phone showed 9:57. I had no plans for the day, but it was a very special one. Like usual, I stepped to the bathroom and rubbed my eyes.': '手机显示 {time=9:57.} 今天没有任何安排，却是格外特殊的一天。我照常走进卫生间，揉了揉眼睛。',
        'My phone showed 9:57 a.m. I had no plans for the day, but it was a very special one. Like usual, I stepped to the bathroom and rubbed my eyes.': '手机显示 {time=9:57.} 今天没有任何安排，却是格外特殊的一天。我照常走进卫生间，揉了揉眼睛。',
        "I'd been nervously pacing as I ate them and stopped myself as soon as I realized it. I didn't have anything to do, and repeatedly going over the same thoughts was only stressful. I'd decided to spend my final free day in as relaxing of a manner as I could manage, but I couldn't let myself keep worrying about losing precious time.": '吃着吃着，我才察觉自己一直不安地来回踱步，便立刻停住。{w} 我无事可做，反复琢磨同一件事只会徒增压力。我早已决定，最后一个自由的日子要尽量过得轻松，可又没法不去担心白白耗掉时间。',
        "I stared at what I had. I'd been selecting random clothes for the past few days, but I found myself thinking a little harder about it. I had a blue hoodie that I really liked in mind, but I couldn't find it, so I ended up grabbing a long-sleeved orange shirt instead.": '我盯着衣柜里的衣服。这几天我都是随手抓一件，这回却不由得挑得更仔细了些。{w} 我想起一件很喜欢的蓝色连帽衫，可怎么也找不到，只好拿了件橙色长袖衬衫。',
        "They weren't too wet, so I kept crouching and using as few of my scarce clothespins as possible. I took out a pretty blue and white shirt. I figured that I was still pretty tired since I thought I'd left it out of the washer due to the bad memories it brought, but I still hung it properly and kept going.": '衣服不算太湿，我便一直蹲着，尽量少用那些本就不多的衣夹。{w} 我取出一件漂亮的蓝白衬衫。我大概还是很累，竟以为自己是因为它带来的那些糟糕回忆，才没把它放进洗衣机。但我还是把它好好挂上，继续干活。',
        'I turned to the table he was pointing to. As I spun, something caught my eye.': '我朝他指的那张桌子转过身去。{w}就在转身的一瞬，有什么东西映入了我的眼帘。',
        'There was a TV close to the entrance. It was muted, but I could see a reporter speaking into a microphone. I recalled the words of the police officer.': '入口附近有台电视，没开声音，但能看见一名记者正对着话筒讲话。{w}我想起了那名警察说过的话。',
        'The voice of the reporter began to reach us, and when it did, the image had transitioned once again. For a second, it had been a short video recorded from a security camera. It showed a prison cell and a person in prison clothing hard to recognize due to the high angle.': '记者的声音开始传进我们耳中，也就在这时，画面再一次切换了。{w}刚才短暂闪过的，是一段监控摄像头录下的短片：画面里是一间牢房，还有一个穿着囚服的人。由于拍摄角度很高，很难辨认出那个人。',
        "I never learned about this... On November 24th, a prisoner escaped from a cell. But Xyn isn't mentioned here even though they also said the identity of the person wasn't known. ...How's that possible? They don't know the identity of someone they arrested?": '这件事我从没听说过……11 月 24 日，一名囚犯从牢房里逃走了。{w}可这里没提到 Xyn，尽管同样说此人的身份不明。{w}……这怎么可能？人都抓到了，还不知道是谁？',
        "What the hell was going on, then? Could they have been the same person? A few days earlier, they'd appeared in that cell. The previous day, they'd been arrested. What kind of coincidence was that? Had he been sent to the same cell? Had the police not realized that he was the person who'd escaped on the 24th? And why was his identity unknown if they thought he was a Xyn member?": '那么，究竟发生了什么？会不会是同一个人？几天前，那人出现在那间牢房里；而昨天，他又被捕了。{w}这算什么样的巧合？他是被关进了同一间牢房吗？警方难道没发现，他就是24日逃掉的那个人？可既然他们认为他是Xyn成员，为什么又不知道他的身份？',
        "Xyn had attempted to steal the Sekimeiya once before the 15th. They failed, and while the police had the chance to catch a Xyn member, they escaped. I couldn't remember the exact way it was phrased, but that had happened once before the 15th...": 'Xyn曾在15日之前试图偷走Sekimeiya。他们失败了，警方本有机会抓住一名Xyn成员，却还是让对方逃掉了。{w}我记不清原话是怎么说的，但15日之前确实发生过这样一件事……',
        "They caught a Xyn member for the first time. ...But they'll escape before the 15th. Katei and the article prove that.": '他们第一次抓住了一名Xyn成员。{w}……但在15日之前，那人会逃掉。Katei和那篇报道都能证明这一点。',
        "There's something crucial that I can't ignore. In both cases, someone ended up in a prison cell. I don't know if the same person was caught both times, but it's very likely they came from the future. So, anything regarding them could differ from the reality I know.": '有一点至关重要，我不能忽略。{w}两起事件里，都有人被关进了牢房。我不知道两次被抓的是不是同一个人，但那人极有可能来自未来。所以，任何与他有关的事，都可能和我所知道的现实不同。',
        "...Trying to work it all out, I'd locked up.": '……{w}我试图理清这一切，脑子却僵住了。',
        "Doesn't this fit all too well with the article? If both events are connected, the fact that the person in the cell was a Xyn member must match as well. However, in the article, that wasn't revealed. ...Could that be the original event that Katei told us about? That person escaped and managed to get to the tower. After that, they traveled to the past and got caught again when they were following me. Somehow, the police still didn't know their identity, but this time it was revealed that they were a Xyn member.": '这和那篇报道未免也太吻合了吧？如果两件事有关联，那么牢房里那人是Xyn成员这一点也应该对得上。可报道里并没有提到这一点。……Katei说过的原本那起事件，会不会就是这个？{w}那个人逃掉后设法到了塔里，之后又穿越回过去，在跟踪我时再次被抓。不知为何，警方仍然不知道他的身份，但这一次，他是Xyn成员的事被公开了。',
        "If whoever that person was traveled to the cell from the 15th, they couldn't have been the same person to be caught yesterday, because the second arrest must be a new event. Could it be that history was changed, but I still remember the one that both I and that man came from because I also traveled from it?": '不管那人是谁，既然他是从15日穿越到牢房的，他就不可能是昨天被抓的同一人，因为第二次逮捕必定是新增的事件。{w}难道说，历史真的被改写了，而我和那个男人都来自原来的历史——因为我也是从那里穿越来的，所以还记得它？',
        "Hm... I did wonder before why he appeared in a jail cell on the 24th. From the 15th, it's very likely he'd appear somewhere he'd been before in the past.": '嗯……我之前就纳闷过，他为什么会在24日出现在牢房里。{w}从15日穿越的话，他极有可能出现在自己过去曾待过的地方。',
        "What's iffy about this? That their identity was unknown, that the cell could've been the same one...? The fact that they appeared in a cell on the 24th might also be a contradiction—they wouldn't have been there before traveling. I feel like there are more problems, but I don't know how to identify them.": '这套说法哪里有问题？他的身份不明，那间牢房又可能是同一间……？{w}他24日出现在牢房里这一点也可能自相矛盾——穿越之前，他根本不可能在那里。我感觉还有更多问题，却说不清具体是什么。',
        "...But if this is what happened, Xyn must be in disarray. Someone from their group was arrested when they're all still free. Could this make them rethink their attack? That could be bad. Maybe Ashiya won't care about using the Sekimeiya as bait now that a Xyn member's been caught, but the event should still happen...": '……可如果事情真是这样，Xyn内部一定乱作一团。他们组里有人被抓，其他人却还都逍遥法外。这会不会让他们重新考虑袭击计划？那就糟了。{w}如今有Xyn成员被捕，芦屋也许不会再在意拿Sekimeiya当诱饵，但那件事仍然应该会发生……',
        "Oh, one thing definitely is strange, though. On the 24th, the police weren't able to identify the person who appeared in the cell. But he was arrested in the street yesterday, and that policeman almost seemed like he knew that it was a good arrest to make. That doesn't make any sense. That man was in the tower on the 15th, so if the police were fine with arresting him yesterday, it follows they would've also arrested him immediately on the morning of the 15th.": '哦，不过有一点确实很奇怪。{w}24日，警方没能查明出现在牢房里的人的身份。可他昨天在街上被捕，那名警察几乎像是知道这次抓对了人。{w}这完全说不通。那个男人15日就在塔里，如果警方昨天愿意逮捕他，那他们15日一早也该立刻逮捕他才对。',
        "After all, if it got too late, I'd have to ring the bell and face him. ...I didn't think I could do that.": '毕竟，要是拖得太晚，我就得按门铃去面对他。{w}……我想我做不到。',
        '...Would I really never enter it again? Could I really have been mere minutes away from going in and out of that door for the last time?': '……我真的再也不会踏入那栋房子了吗？{w}难道我离最后一次进出那扇门，真的只差几分钟了吗？',
        '...I decided against that again.': '……{w}我再次打消了这个念头。',
        '...Should I just wait here...?': '……{w}难道真要在这里一直等下去……？',
        'I hid myself and leaned against the dark, cold wall. Suddenly, I recognized what I was looking at.': '我藏好身子，靠在昏暗冰冷的墙边。{w}忽然，我认出了眼前的景象。',
        "...I considered two important facts: in the attic, Erina had implied they'd bought the tickets pretty early. That meant they were likely to already have them.": '……{w}我想到两个要紧的事实。在阁楼里，Erina曾暗示她们的票买得相当早。也就是说，票多半已经在她们手上了。',
        "Isla! Are you here...!? It's me, Shiroya!": 'Isla！你在吗……！？{w}是我，Shiroya！',
        "But I'd seen her from the café during school hours. That had to be an Isla who'd traveled from the future. Why had she been out of her house? I figured she wouldn't have wanted to show herself anywhere, which was why she wasn't opening the door.": '可是，我在上课时间从咖啡馆里看见过她。那一定是从未来穿越而来的Isla。{w}她为什么会走出家门？我猜想，她不愿在任何地方露面，所以才不肯开门。',
        "I'd grabbed the handle to make some noise, and I'd accidentally pushed forward. I didn't move. I kept staring inside until I was sure it was vacant. Then, I lightly pushed the door a bit more and took a careful step in.": '我本来只是握住门把手想弄出点声响，却一不小心把它推开了。{w}我没有动，只盯着屋里看，直到确定里面空无一人。然后，我又轻轻把门推开一些，小心翼翼地迈了进去。',
        "I opened the entryway closet in search of the purse and was faced with a few women's and girls' jackets. Scattered in the closet were clothes you wouldn't typically see when visiting someone's house. An apron with the name of a local restaurant, a uniform for a factory worker, and a cap branded with the logo of a convenience store.": '我打开玄关的柜子找那只手提包，看到的却是几件女式和女童外套。柜子里还零散挂着几件平时去别人家做客不会见到的衣服。{w}一条印着本地餐馆名字的围裙、一套工厂工人的制服，还有一顶印着便利店标志的帽子。',
        "...Tomorrow, I'll definitely have to take our tickets, no matter how. It might not be as much of a priority as I thought, though. If I find the Sekimeiya in the tower and enter it during the night, I'll either travel through time or be caught by the police. If I travel through time, taking our tickets won't matter since I'll change the past. ...And if I get caught by the police, there's no way Atsuki won't learn about it. I'm not sure what would happen to my other self, but I doubt she and Atsuki would just go to the tower on the 15th.": '……明天，我无论如何都得把我们的门票拿到手。不过，这件事也许没有我以为的那么要紧。{w}如果我在塔里找到 Sekimeiya，并在夜里进入其中，要么完成时间穿越，要么被警察抓住。若能穿越成功，拿门票也就没有意义，因为我会改变过去。……而要是被警察抓住，Atsuki 不可能不知道。我不清楚另一个我会怎样，但我不觉得她会在 15 号那天和 Atsuki 一起去塔里。',
        'I looked at my phone. It was {time=14:04.} There was nothing else I wanted to do for the day, so I went to the kitchen after a long pause.': '我看了一眼手机，时间显示 {time=14:04.}{w} 今天已经没有别的事想做了，过了好一会儿，我才走向厨房。',
        'I looked at my phone. It was 14:04.{w} There was nothing else I wanted to do for the day, so I went to the kitchen after a long pause.': '我看了一眼手机，时间显示 {time=14:04.}{w} 今天已经没有别的事想做了，过了好一会儿，我才走向厨房。',
        'I looked at my phone. It was 14:04. There was nothing else I wanted to do for the day, so I went to the kitchen after a long pause.': '我看了一眼手机，时间显示 {time=14:04.}{w} 今天已经没有别的事想做了，过了好一会儿，我才走向厨房。',
        'I looked at my phone. It was 2:04 p.m.{w} There was nothing else I wanted to do for the day, so I went to the kitchen after a long pause.': '我看了一眼手机，时间显示 {time=14:04.}{w} 今天已经没有别的事想做了，过了好一会儿，我才走向厨房。',
        'I looked at my phone. It was 2:04 p.m. There was nothing else I wanted to do for the day, so I went to the kitchen after a long pause.': '我看了一眼手机，时间显示 {time=14:04.}{w} 今天已经没有别的事想做了，过了好一会儿，我才走向厨房。',
        "I wonder what would happen if I revealed what the Sekimeiya can do. They'd have to believe me due to my existence. And then what? Would they let me go with no real identity of my own? Would the Sekimeiya be kept a secret? If so, there's no chance I'd be able to live anything akin to a normal life. Honestly, maybe getting caught by the police would be better... Or, if I'm able to save Miiya, I could reveal myself, and they'd decide what to do.": '如果我说出 Sekimeiya 能做到什么，会怎么样？我的存在本身就是证据，他们不信也得信。{w}然后呢？他们会让我这个没有真正身份的人离开吗？Sekimeiya 的事会被保密吗？如果是那样，我根本不可能过上任何正常生活。{w}说实话，也许被警察抓住反而更好……或者，如果我能救下 Miiya，我可以自己现身，让他们决定怎么处置我。',
        "...I realized I'd just thought that and pitied myself. I'd been feeling sporadic senses of liberty the past few days after being shut away for so long, so the fact that I'd seen an outcome deprived of any freedom as acceptable was just disheartening.": '……{w}我意识到自己刚冒出这种念头，便不由得可怜起自己来。被关了那么久之后，这几天我偶尔能感到一点自由；可即便如此，我居然觉得一个毫无自由可言的结局也可以接受，这实在令人心灰意冷。',
        '...What the hell was I thinking?': '……{w}我到底在想什么？',
        "I took Isla's and Erina's tickets to prevent them from going to the tower on the 15th. It sounded like a good idea because they could've sold out quickly... I completely ignored that they could simply print them out again. ...I don't think they'd have to buy new ones.": '我拿走了 Isla 和 Erina 的票，是为了阻止她们在15号去芦屋塔。当时觉得这主意不错，因为票很可能很快售罄……{w} 却完全忽略了她们只要重新打印一份就行。……我想她们应该不用再买新票。',
        "How the hell do I do this, then? Unless Erina and Isla don't notice that their tickets are gone until they're in the tower, they can just go anyway. At least in the case of Atsuki and myself, it was seeing our tickets that made us decide to go through with attending the event, so we might actually not go if I do take them.": '那我到底该怎么做？除非 Erina 和 Isla 一直到进了芦屋塔才发现票没了，否则她们照样可以去。{w} 至少对我和 Atsuki 来说，是看到票之后才决定去参加活动的，所以如果我把票拿走，我们说不定真就不会去了。',
        'I grabbed my phone again. It was 5:30.': '我又拿起手机。时间是 {time=5:30.}',
        'I grabbed my phone again. It was 5:30 a.m.': '我又拿起手机。时间是 {time=5:30.}',
        "It was doubtful I'd be able to sleep after coming back, when I'd finally be aware of the crucial details I needed. But since it was likely Atsuki wouldn't be at home late in the day, I didn't think it was a terrible idea.": '等我回来时，已经弄清了那些关键细节，恐怕就更睡不着了。{w}不过，Atsuki 今天晚些时候多半不在家，所以这主意也不算太糟。',
        "More than three hours remained until 9:00, when the tower's halls would open to the public. On the 15th, though, Atsuki and I had been in the lobby since much earlier.": '距离塔内对外开放的 {time=9} 还有三个多小时。可15号那天，我和 Atsuki 早得多就在大厅里了。',
        "More than three hours remained until 9 a.m., when the tower's halls would open to the public. On the 15th, though, Atsuki and I had been in the lobby since much earlier.": '距离塔内对外开放的 {time=9} 还有三个多小时。可15号那天，我和 Atsuki 早得多就在大厅里了。',
        "It wasn't very far, and despite the eerie scenery, I was glad I'd left my apartment. I had to be in the tower in the morning, and I knew its entrance opened far before 9:00. A receptionist had been there when we'd arrived, so I could try to buy tickets for the event and think about questions I wanted to ask.": '路并不远。四周景色虽然有些诡异，我还是庆幸自己出了公寓。早上我得进塔，而且知道入口在 {time=9.} 之前很早就开放。我们到的时候，前台已经有人，所以我可以试着买活动门票，再想想想问的问题。',
        "It wasn't very far, and despite the eerie scenery, I was glad I'd left my apartment. I had to be in the tower in the morning, and I knew its entrance opened far before 9 a.m. A receptionist had been there when we'd arrived, so I could try to buy tickets for the event and think about questions I wanted to ask.": '路并不远。四周景色虽然有些诡异，我还是庆幸自己出了公寓。早上我得进塔，而且知道入口在 {time=9.} 之前很早就开放。我们到的时候，前台已经有人，所以我可以试着买活动门票，再想想想问的问题。',
        'Instead of putting my hand back in my pocket, I grabbed my phone. The screen displayed {time=5:48.} Then, I hesitantly gripped the handle of the door and tried to open it. Like it seemed, it was locked.': '我没有把手放回口袋，而是掏出手机。屏幕上显示 {time=5:48.}。随后，我迟疑地握住门把手，试着开门。{w}果然，门锁着。',
        'Instead of putting my hand back in my pocket, I grabbed my phone. The screen displayed 5:48. Then, I hesitantly gripped the handle of the door and tried to open it.{w} Like it seemed, it was locked.': '我没有把手放回口袋，而是掏出手机。屏幕上显示 {time=5:48.}。随后，我迟疑地握住门把手，试着开门。{w}果然，门锁着。',
        'Instead of putting my hand back in my pocket, I grabbed my phone. The screen displayed 5:48. Then, I hesitantly gripped the handle of the door and tried to open it. Like it seemed, it was locked.': '我没有把手放回口袋，而是掏出手机。屏幕上显示 {time=5:48.}。随后，我迟疑地握住门把手，试着开门。{w}果然，门锁着。',
        'Instead of putting my hand back in my pocket, I grabbed my phone. The screen displayed 5:48 a.m. Then, I hesitantly gripped the handle of the door and tried to open it.{w} Like it seemed, it was locked.': '我没有把手放回口袋，而是掏出手机。屏幕上显示 {time=5:48.}。随后，我迟疑地握住门把手，试着开门。{w}果然，门锁着。',
        'Instead of putting my hand back in my pocket, I grabbed my phone. The screen displayed 5:48 a.m. Then, I hesitantly gripped the handle of the door and tried to open it. Like it seemed, it was locked.': '我没有把手放回口袋，而是掏出手机。屏幕上显示 {time=5:48.}。随后，我迟疑地握住门把手，试着开门。{w}果然，门锁着。',
        'I stepped back carefully, trying to get a feel for my surroundings. ...And all I determined was that I was completely alone.': '我小心地后退几步，想感受一下周围的环境。{w}……结果只确定了一件事：我完全是一个人。',
        "On the 15th, that door had been highlighted by the warm light behind it, and we'd entered it at 6:00.": '15日那天，那扇门被背后的暖光照亮，我们是在 {time=6.} 进去的。',
        "On the 15th, that door had been highlighted by the warm light behind it, and we'd entered it at 6 a.m.": '15日那天，那扇门被背后的暖光照亮，我们是在 {time=6.} 进去的。',
        "That time was very close, but I began to wonder whether that had been a special occasion. Maybe they'd anticipated people would come very early and that was why the tower had been open at 6:00.": '那个时间已经很近了，但我开始怀疑那天是不是特殊情况。也许他们预料到会有人很早就来，所以塔才在 {time=6.} 就开了门。',
        "That time was very close, but I began to wonder whether that had been a special occasion. Maybe they'd anticipated people would come very early and that was why the tower had been open at 6 a.m.": '那个时间已经很近了，但我开始怀疑那天是不是特殊情况。也许他们预料到会有人很早就来，所以塔才在 {time=6.} 就开了门。',
        "...Over three hours were left until 9:00. When would the entrance open? I had no way to know how long I'd have to wait.": '……距离 {time=9.} 还有三个多小时。入口什么时候才会开？我根本不知道要等多久。',
        "...Over three hours were left until 9 a.m. When would the entrance open? I had no way to know how long I'd have to wait.": '……距离 {time=9.} 还有三个多小时。入口什么时候才会开？我根本不知道要等多久。',
        '{time=6:03.}.. It had only been a few minutes, and the words "No service" were still there.': '{time=6:03.}..{w}才过了几分钟，屏幕上依旧显示着「无服务」。',
        '6:03...{w} It had only been a few minutes, and the words "No service" were still there.': '{time=6:03.}..{w}才过了几分钟，屏幕上依旧显示着「无服务」。',
        '6:03... It had only been a few minutes, and the words "No service" were still there.': '{time=6:03.}..{w}才过了几分钟，屏幕上依旧显示着「无服务」。',
        '6:03 a.m...{w} It had only been a few minutes, and the words "No service" were still there.': '{time=6:03.}..{w}才过了几分钟，屏幕上依旧显示着「无服务」。',
        '6:03 a.m... It had only been a few minutes, and the words "No service" were still there.': '{time=6:03.}..{w}才过了几分钟，屏幕上依旧显示着「无服务」。',
        "I'd also looked at my phone on the 15th, before we'd been asked to leave them behind with the guards. By 6:03, we'd already been allowed to step in.": '15日那天，在他们要求我们把手机交给警卫保管之前，我也看过手机。到 {time=6:03} 时，我们已经获准进去了。',
        "I'd also looked at my phone on the 15th, before we'd been asked to leave them behind with the guards. By 6:03 a.m., we'd already been allowed to step in.": '15日那天，在他们要求我们把手机交给警卫保管之前，我也看过手机。到 {time=6:03} 时，我们已经获准进去了。',
        'How much longer do I have to be here...? Is the tower not going to open until 9:00?': '我还要在这里待多久……？塔难道要等到 {time=9} 才开门吗？',
        'How much longer do I have to be here...? Is the tower not going to open until 9 a.m.?': '我还要在这里待多久……？塔难道要等到 {time=9} 才开门吗？',
        'When I looked at the time again, it was 6:28. Once more, it seemed as if the last half hour had happened in an instant, while the next one would last an eternity.': '我再看时间，已经是 {time=6:28.}。又一次，过去半小时仿佛只在一瞬，而接下来的半小时却会漫长得像永远。',
        'When I looked at the time again, it was 6:28 a.m. Once more, it seemed as if the last half hour had happened in an instant, while the next one would last an eternity.': '我再看时间，已经是 {time=6:28.}。又一次，过去半小时仿佛只在一瞬，而接下来的半小时却会漫长得像永远。',
        "Oh, Katei too. ...He said he'd been taking the daily shifts recently. Uh... did he say when he started? ...It should also be well before {time=9.}": '对了，还有 Katei。……他说自己最近每天都在值班。{w}呃……他说过几点开始吗？……应该也远早于 {time=9.}。',
        "Oh, Katei too. ...He said he'd been taking the daily shifts recently.{w} Uh... did he say when he started? ...It should also be well before 9:00.": '对了，还有 Katei。……他说自己最近每天都在值班。{w}呃……他说过几点开始吗？……应该也远早于 {time=9.}。',
        "Oh, Katei too. ...He said he'd been taking the daily shifts recently. Uh... did he say when he started? ...It should also be well before 9:00.": '对了，还有 Katei。……他说自己最近每天都在值班。{w}呃……他说过几点开始吗？……应该也远早于 {time=9.}。',
        "Oh, Katei too. ...He said he'd been taking the daily shifts recently.{w} Uh... did he say when he started? ...It should also be well before 9 a.m.": '对了，还有 Katei。……他说自己最近每天都在值班。{w}呃……他说过几点开始吗？……应该也远早于 {time=9.}。',
        "Oh, Katei too. ...He said he'd been taking the daily shifts recently. Uh... did he say when he started? ...It should also be well before 9 a.m.": '对了，还有 Katei。……他说自己最近每天都在值班。{w}呃……他说过几点开始吗？……应该也远早于 {time=9.}。',
        "The same wait continued until 7:00 came. The time I'd spent could've been summarized in a blink, as each second had been identical.": '同样的等待一直持续到 {time=7}。这段时光几乎一眨眼就能概括，因为每一秒都没有任何分别。',
        "The same wait continued until 7 a.m. came. The time I'd spent could've been summarized in a blink, as each second had been identical.": '同样的等待一直持续到 {time=7}。这段时光几乎一眨眼就能概括，因为每一秒都没有任何分别。',
        "...I looked up, but I couldn't see anything past the dark, monolithic slab of the building. I hadn't moved in so long that turning my head was painful. I had to do it slowly, but I managed to see the stars.": '……{w}我抬起头，视线却被那栋黑色巨碑般的建筑挡得严严实实。{w}我太久没动，连转头都疼。我慢慢转过头，终于看见了星星。',
        '...Wait... Am I crazy...?': '……等等……{w}我是不是疯了……？',
        "What...? This doesn't make any sense. Where's... the sun?": '什么……？这根本说不通。{w}太阳……{w}去哪了？',
        'Then, speechless, I looked back at my phone. {time=7:04.}': '随后，我无言地低头看向手机。{w} {time=7:04.}',
        'Then, speechless, I looked back at my phone.{w} 7:04.': '随后，我无言地低头看向手机。{w} {time=7:04.}',
        'Then, speechless, I looked back at my phone. 7:04.': '随后，我无言地低头看向手机。{w} {time=7:04.}',
        'Then, speechless, I looked back at my phone.{w} 7:04 a.m.': '随后，我无言地低头看向手机。{w} {time=7:04.}',
        'Then, speechless, I looked back at my phone. 7:04 a.m.': '随后，我无言地低头看向手机。{w} {time=7:04.}',
        "I don't understand... It's like the world has stopped moving. No service... Why? Why does my phone have no service!?": '我不明白……就好像整个世界都停止运转了。{w}没有信号……为什么？手机为什么没有信号！？',
        "I'd witnessed the sun rising from behind the mountains countless times. But at that moment, no hint of light peeked out from over them. It was 7:00 already, so why was Yushibana still covered in darkness?": '我曾无数次见过太阳从山后升起。可此刻，山际没有透出一丝光亮。明明已经 {time=7} 了，丰花为什么还笼罩在黑暗里？',
        "I'd witnessed the sun rising from behind the mountains countless times. But at that moment, no hint of light peeked out from over them. It was 7 a.m. already, so why was Yushibana still covered in darkness?": '我曾无数次见过太阳从山后升起。可此刻，山际没有透出一丝光亮。明明已经 {time=7} 了，丰花为什么还笼罩在黑暗里？',
        "I'd felt that time might not have been passing since I'd leaned on that streetlight. Astonished, I forced myself to step forward and spun. Nothing at all had changed.": '从我靠上那盏路灯起，我就觉得时间也许没有在流动。我惊愕不已，强迫自己迈步向前，又转过身去。{w}一切都没有丝毫改变。',
        "What was I waiting for? The tower should've opened already. Without a doubt, the sun should've begun to rise already. ...Waiting had become my only protest, but time staunchly refused to advance to the next day.": '我究竟在等什么？塔早就该开了。太阳也早该升起了，绝不会有错。{w}……等待成了我唯一能做的抗争，可时间顽固地不肯走到第二天。',
        "I hugged my body even tighter. I'd been convinced the cold would end at some point, but it continued without end, eroding me. Would 9:00 be no different? I could no longer tell myself it was impossible.": '我把身体抱得更紧了。我原本相信寒冷总会有尽头，可它无休无止地延续，不断侵蚀着我。{time=9} 到来时，难道也会一样吗？我已经无法再对自己说那不可能。',
        "I hugged my body even tighter. I'd been convinced the cold would end at some point, but it continued without end, eroding me. Would 9 a.m. be no different? I could no longer tell myself it was impossible.": '我把身体抱得更紧了。我原本相信寒冷总会有尽头，可它无休无止地延续，不断侵蚀着我。{time=9} 到来时，难道也会一样吗？我已经无法再对自己说那不可能。',
        '{time=7:30.}.. "{tip=phone}No service{/tip}". That time, I slowly moved my finger up to the call button. It was freezing, but it still registered my touch. The moment I pressed it, I called my mother\'s number.': '{time=7:30.}……{w}「{tip=phone}无服务{/tip}」。{w}这一次，我慢慢把手指移向通话键。{w}我的手指冻得发僵，屏幕却仍能感应到触碰。我按下去的瞬间，拨出了母亲的号码。',
        '7:30...{w} "{tip=phone}No service{/tip}".{w} That time, I slowly moved my finger up to the call button.{w} It was freezing, but it still registered my touch. The moment I pressed it, I called my mother\'s number.': '{time=7:30.}……{w}「{tip=phone}无服务{/tip}」。{w}这一次，我慢慢把手指移向通话键。{w}我的手指冻得发僵，屏幕却仍能感应到触碰。我按下去的瞬间，拨出了母亲的号码。',
        '7:30... "{tip=phone}No service{/tip}". That time, I slowly moved my finger up to the call button. It was freezing, but it still registered my touch. The moment I pressed it, I called my mother\'s number.': '{time=7:30.}……{w}「{tip=phone}无服务{/tip}」。{w}这一次，我慢慢把手指移向通话键。{w}我的手指冻得发僵，屏幕却仍能感应到触碰。我按下去的瞬间，拨出了母亲的号码。',
        '7:30 a.m...{w} "{tip=phone}No service{/tip}".{w} That time, I slowly moved my finger up to the call button.{w} It was freezing, but it still registered my touch. The moment I pressed it, I called my mother\'s number.': '{time=7:30.}……{w}「{tip=phone}无服务{/tip}」。{w}这一次，我慢慢把手指移向通话键。{w}我的手指冻得发僵，屏幕却仍能感应到触碰。我按下去的瞬间，拨出了母亲的号码。',
        '7:30 a.m... "{tip=phone}No service{/tip}". That time, I slowly moved my finger up to the call button. It was freezing, but it still registered my touch. The moment I pressed it, I called my mother\'s number.': '{time=7:30.}……{w}「{tip=phone}无服务{/tip}」。{w}这一次，我慢慢把手指移向通话键。{w}我的手指冻得发僵，屏幕却仍能感应到触碰。我按下去的瞬间，拨出了母亲的号码。',
        '...A quiet, robotic voice came out of the speaker.': '……{w}听筒里传来一道平静而机械的声音。',
        'Still gripping my phone, I took it out again. According to it, time had definitely been passing, as it showed 7:35.': '我仍紧攥着手机，又把它拿了出来。屏幕上显示 {time=7:35.}，看来时间确实一直在流逝。',
        'Still gripping my phone, I took it out again. According to it, time had definitely been passing, as it showed 7:35 a.m.': '我仍紧攥着手机，又把它拿了出来。屏幕上显示 {time=7:35.}，看来时间确实一直在流逝。',
        "But I suddenly stopped when I remembered something from the day we'd been inside that immense building. If that door had really led to the wall I was at, there was a way I could find it.": '但我忽然停下脚步，因为我想起那天待在那座巨大建筑里时发生的一件事。{w}如果那扇门真的通到我面前的这面墙，我就有办法找到它。',
        "If a door was there, it must've been made or covered with the same bricks as everywhere else. However, when we'd been in the storeroom, we had shaken the door from the inside, and it had made a rattling sound. ...If the other side was the wall, then shaking it from the outside would produce the same sound.": '如果那里真有一扇门，它一定和其他地方一样，用同样的砖块砌成或覆盖着。不过，我们待在储藏室里的时候，曾从里面摇晃过那扇门，它发出了咔嗒咔嗒的响动。{w}……如果门的外侧就是这面墙，那么从外面摇晃它，应该也会发出同样的声音。',
        'The sound I heard was different. Speechless, I extended my arm to the wall and pushed. When I did, I felt it move.': '这次听到的声音不一样。{w}我一时说不出话，伸手抵住墙面一推，竟感觉到它动了。',
        'After so long, that was what made my heart speed up. I felt the edges and confirmed the outline of a door. Akaro had been right after all. That door in the storeroom was the only thing blocking our way out.': '折腾了这么久，让我心跳骤然加快的竟是这一点。我摸到边缘，确认了门的轮廓。{w}Akaro 果然没说错。储藏室里那扇门，正是挡住我们出路的唯一障碍。',
        "...I'd gotten it to open easily just by pushing it. However, it had opened inwardly, which was why we hadn't been able to do it in the storeroom.": '……{w}我只轻轻一推，门就开了。可它是朝内开的，所以我们在储藏室里才打不开。',
        "I walked deeper into the narrow entrance, leaving it open. There hadn't been much wind outside, so I didn't think it would close on its own. Immediately, I hit another wall. It was what concealed the area I was in.": '我任由门开着，沿着狭窄的入口往里走。外面风不大，我想它应该不会自己关上。{w}紧接着，我又撞上了一面墙。正是它遮住了我所在的这片区域。',
        "...I didn't know what to do. Of course, there had to be someone in the security room, but there simultaneously couldn't be—the world had frozen. What would happen if I was seen? I couldn't claim to have randomly found the hidden door.": '……{w}我不知道该怎么办。按理说，监控室里一定有人；可与此同时，又不可能有人——世界已经静止了。{w}要是被人看见，会怎么样？我总不能说自己碰巧发现了暗门。',
        "I couldn't see hallway A, but I knew I was there. I was immediately certain that I wasn't in a dream due to my senses. It was the smell. The same strange smell that had characterized the building on that long day tinged the air again.": '我看不见 A走廊，却知道自己正站在那里。感官让我立刻确信，这不是梦。{w}是那股气味。在那个漫长的一天里，弥漫整栋楼的奇异气味，此刻又飘散在空气里。',
        "But I knew it wasn't the scent of the building itself. On the evening of the 15th, I'd identified the real source. The Sekimeiya. When we'd been close to it, the smell had strengthened, and when we'd been farther from it, it had always been weaker.": '可我知道，那并非建筑本身的气味。15日傍晚，我已经找出了真正的源头。{w}是 Sekimeiya。我们靠近它时，气味就变浓；离得远了，便总是淡下去。',
        "I hit the wall at my side, failing to walk in a straight line. Carefully, I continued to move until I felt a doorknob. It was the security room's, so I gently gripped it.": '我走不直，撞上了身侧的墙。我谨慎地继续摸索，直到碰到一个门把。{w}那是监控室的门把，我轻轻握住了它。',
        'Oh... This is...!': '哦……{w}这是……！',
        'Glancing at the many open drawers, I saw something next to a pile of files. I pulled the heavy compartment open and tried to reach the bottom with a finger.': '我扫了一眼那些半开的抽屉，在一叠文件旁看到了什么。{w}我拉开那个沉重的抽屉，伸手往最里面探去。',
        "I could see a red light by the reception desk, but it wasn't enough to illuminate the lobby, even with the streetlights shining faintly from beyond the glass. I questioned it again. Why was the entire floor dark when I'd been able to turn on the computer?": '前台那边有一点红光，可即便玻璃外透进微弱的路灯光，也照不亮大厅。{w}我又一次起了疑。既然我能打开电脑，为什么整层楼都是暗的？',
        "There was a room below me. There'd been nothing in the storeroom, so the mechanical room was a rational place to store the cabinet. But more importantly, I knew that the light breakers were there. There were no switches on the walls, so if the breakers were on, I would have no idea why the tower was still dark.": '我下方还有一个房间。储藏室里空无一物，那么把展示柜放在机械室也合情合理。{w}但更重要的是，我知道照明电闸就在那里。墙上没有任何开关，所以如果电闸是开着的，我就更不明白这座塔为何仍是黑的。',
        '{tip=keys}Two more keys{/tip}. Once they were illuminated, I recognized them as well.': '{tip=keys}又是两把钥匙{/tip}。{w} 灯光一照，我也认出了它们。',
        "After I'd taken a few steps, I turned around. Through the door, I was peering back into the lobby.": '走了几步，我回过头。{w} 隔着门，我朝大厅里张望。',
        "I could see nothing but darkness, and that didn't make any sense... Because from there, I should've been able to see the lights of the reception desk.": '除了黑暗，我什么都看不见，这根本说不通……{w} 因为站在这里，本该能看见前台那边的灯光。',
        'It was... cold. As soon as I took a step in, I perceived a decrease in temperature.': '很……冷。{w} 我刚踏进一步，就感到温度降了下来。',
        'Wh—': '什——{w=0.3}{nw}',
        'Is that the alarm...!? Why!? Did I just break it!?': '是警报……！？为什么！？{w} 难道是我弄坏的！？',
        "I'd never heard that sound, but it had to be the same one that played when we were trapped. I started to lose control of my nerves. What was happening? I'd triggered it after doing something to the cabinet, and I couldn't see what.": '我从没听过这个声音，但那一定是当初我们被困时响起的同一个。{w} 我渐渐慌了神。到底出了什么事？我动了展示柜，警报才响的，可我看不清自己到底动了什么。',
        "I stood still, praying for the sound to disappear. I was being locked in, but nobody was in the security room, and I'd left the storeroom door open. As I stood, I perceived a fainter and rougher sound coming from the lobby. It was the shutter, closing automatically.": '我僵在原地，盼着那声音快点消失。我正被关在里面，可监控室里没人，储藏室的门我也一直敞着。{w} 就在我站着的时候，大厅方向传来一阵更微弱、更粗重的响声。是卷帘门，正在自动落下。',
        "Wait...! Does this mean that I can travel really far back again? Why, though...!? The cabinet shouldn't allow it.": '等等……！{w} 这么说，我又能穿越到很久以前了？{w} 可为什么……！？这个展示柜不该有这种力量。',
        "...I touched the white stain on the cushion and knew I hadn't been mistaken; something was there.": '……{w}我摸到衬垫上的白色污渍，知道自己没看错；那里确实沾着东西。',
        'What the hell is this...? A card?': '这到底是什么……？{w} 一张卡片？',
        'My hand, cold as it was, began to burn painfully. I was so close to the Sekimeiya and to leaving behind yet another reality. I shut my eyes, mustering up the will to move my hand farther. I expected that by the next time I opened them, my surroundings would have morphed entirely.': '我的手本就冰凉，此刻却开始灼痛。Sekimeiya 近在咫尺，我又要把一个现实抛在身后了。{w}我闭上眼，硬起心肠把手再往前探。我以为，等我再次睁眼时，周遭的一切定已彻底换了模样。',
        'H— You...!': 'H——{w}你……！',
        "I felt my body and noticed my heart skip a beat. I was wearing different clothes, ones I'd washed the day before. As soon as the world had unfrozen, so had I. I could move my hand without it cramping, as if the time I'd spent outside had been erased. ...And when I did, I realized I wasn't tired anymore.": '我低头看了看自己，心跳漏了一拍。身上换成了另一套衣服，是前一天刚洗过的那身。{w}世界一解冻，我也随之解冻了。手能活动，不再僵得抽筋，仿佛我在冻结中度过的那些时间已被一笔勾销。……而等我活动起手脚，才发现疲惫感也一并消失了。',
        "I followed his eyes toward the hallway B door. When I gave it a closer look, I saw the crucial detail I'd missed. Its edges were dark. I'd seen it before, so I didn't have to wonder what it meant.": '我顺着他的视线望向B走廊的门。再仔细一看，我才发现了先前漏掉的关键之处。{w}门边发黑。这景象我见过，不必再猜它意味着什么。',
        "H-Huh? A lot of things! Do you remember everything? Late into the day, we were in the lobby, and I went to the bathroom. There, I activated the Sekimeiya and appeared on the 30th of November, below that gem shop. Then... a few days later, I entered the tower and touched the Sekimeiya. That's how I just appeared here.": '啊？很、很多事！你全都记得吗？那天很晚了，我们在大厅，我去了洗手间。就在那儿，我启动了 Sekimeiya，出现在11月30日，就在那家宝石店的下方。{w}然后……过了几天，我进了塔，碰到了 Sekimeiya。于是我就出现在了这里。',
        "...Are you really... the real Shiroya? I don't really understand what you're telling me.": '……{w}你真的是……Shiroya本人吗？你说的话我实在听不明白。',
        "...I didn't know what to say, but he was the Atsuki I'd been with that day. How was I talking to him? Hadn't his existence been overwritten...?": '……{w}我不知道该说什么。可他确实是那天陪在我身边的 Atsuki。我怎么可能还在跟他说话？他的存在不是已经被覆盖了吗……？',
        "I don't...! I just told you. I appeared on the 30th of November. I stayed at my apartment while my past self was in the hospital, and a few days later, I entered the tower. I have no idea what happened there, though. The Sekimeiya was already in the cabinet, and I touched it since nobody was in the security room. After that, I appeared in the lobby with you. Now we're here.": '我不知道……！我不是刚说过吗。我是在11月30日出现的。{w}过去的我还在住院时，我一直待在自己的公寓里；几天后，我进了芦屋塔。{w}不过塔里发生了什么，我完全不清楚。Sekimeiya 那时已经在展示柜里了。我看监控室里没人，就伸手碰了它。之后，我便和你一起出现在大厅里。再然后，就是现在这里。',
        "...Then I'm not sure it would help if I told you what happened after you left. Another version of you was there, but it wasn't you, right?": '……那我不确定，把在你离开之后发生的事告诉你有没有用。{w}当时还有另一个你也在场，但那不是你，对吧？',
        "Well, we weren't able to leave when the time came. I'm not sure what happened, why, or how, but the lights went off, and we couldn't get out. ...You remember the recording, right? It was real.": '结果，时间一到，我们却没能离开。发生了什么、为什么会这样、又到底是怎么发生的，我都不清楚，但灯灭了，我们也出不去。{w}……你还记得那段录音吧？{w}那是真的。',
        "Yes, it did happen. It wasn't a trick. It still doesn't make any sense, though. I can't wrap my head around what happened. You said that you touched the Sekimeiya in the event room days before the 15th, right?": '对，那确实发生过。不是骗人的把戏。{w}可我还是完全想不通，怎么也理不清发生了什么。{w}你说过，15日的前几天，你在活动室里碰过 Sekimeiya，对吧？',
        "I see. What the fuck, then...? I don't get anything. I thought I got caught up in your travel and both of us appeared in front of the hallway B door, the location where we were on the morning of the 15th.": '我明白了。那他妈到底是怎么回事……？我完全搞不懂。{w}我本来以为，自己被卷进了你的时间穿越，两个人才会一起出现在 B走廊的门前——也就是15日早上我们所在的地方。',
        "Wh-What? I... don't get it.": '什、什么？{w}我……{w}不明白。',
        "Sorry, when I touched it in the bathroom, its surroundings were incredibly hot. ...I can feel the heat, but it's nothing like then. Do you know more about how the Sekimeiya works?": '抱歉，我在浴室里碰到它的时候，它周围烫得吓人。……现在也能感觉到热，但和那时完全不能比。{w} 关于 Sekimeiya 的原理，你还知道些什么吗？',
        "When his hand touched it, the Sekimeiya disappeared. That was all I'd wanted. However, nothing else did.": '他的手一碰到，Sekimeiya 便消失了。{w} 这正是我唯一所求。可除此之外，什么也没有发生。',
        "That had escaped my mind a long time ago. ...The Sekimeiya's teleportation. What caused it...!? Would it sometimes reject a travel? If so, why had it happened then...!?": '这件事我早就抛到脑后了。……Sekimeiya 的传送。{w} 究竟是什么触发了它……！？难道它有时会拒绝时间穿越？若真是如此，那当时又为什么发生了传送……！？',
        "I shook my head. The lid that Atsuki had just opened... The instant the Sekimeiya disappeared, it had closed without producing a sound. And that wasn't all. Over it, the velvet curtain covered it perfectly, making the cabinet look like every other one in the room.": '我摇了摇头。{w} Atsuki 刚刚打开的那个盖子……就在 Sekimeiya 消失的瞬间，无声无息地合上了。而且不止如此。天鹅绒遮布严严实实地罩着它，让那展示柜看上去和房间里其他柜子一模一样。',
        "I couldn't believe I was circling those floors once more, but as I did, my mind went back to the door to the lobby. After leaving the crystal room, it had looked more open than before. That was strange, because as Atsuki said, the way we'd left it was just like how it was that morning, before Sai opened it all the way.": '没想到我竟又一次在这些楼层里打转。一路跑着，我的思绪却回到了通往大厅的那扇门上。离开水晶展室时，它看上去比先前敞得更开。{w} 这很奇怪，因为正如 Atsuki 所说，我们离开时它的样子，就和那天早上 Sai 把它完全推开之前一模一样。',
        "However, the most important detail was higher up, above the three sleeping bodies. I hadn't been able to give it a good look, but the camera's lens had seemed to reflect the light of the crystal room. Then, I'd looked at the other lenses and thought that they more clearly had smoke on them.": '不过，最关键的一处细节在更高处，就在那三个熟睡的人上方。当时我没能看仔细，但那台摄像头的镜片似乎映着水晶展室的光。{w} 后来我又看了看其他镜头，觉得它们上面的烟迹更明显一些。',
        "Atsuki once told me he'd seen it teleport to its cabinet. That seemed to resolve the doubt from earlier—it had just teleported to the event room, which was why it was there when we woke up. The important question was what else the disappearance implied. The cabinet's reversion to its previous state revealed a secondary effect.": 'Atsuki 曾说过，他见过它传送回自己的展示柜里。这似乎解开了先前的疑问——它只是传送到了活动室，所以我们醒来时它才会在那里。{w} 真正重要的是，这次消失还意味着什么。展示柜恢复成先前的样子，说明另有一重附带效应。',
        "...What exactly was I hearing? The footsteps ahead, mine, and Atsuki's. Why did it sound as if there were more? The echo could've been messing with me, but it seemed as if another pair of footsteps was running just behind us.": '……我到底听到了什么？前面的脚步声、我自己的脚步声，还有 Atsuki 的。{w} 可为什么听上去不止这些？{w} 也许是回音在作弄我，但仿佛另有一双脚步，正紧跟我们身后奔跑。',
        "It didn't make any sense, but I could open the attic. I inserted the key into the keyhole without wasting any more time. When it unlocked, I slowly pushed the door open.": '这毫无道理，可我确实能打开阁楼。我不再耽搁，把钥匙插进锁孔。{w} 锁一开，我缓缓推开了门。',
        'Then, I saw who was there. Naomi.': '接着，我看清了里面的人。{w}是 Naomi。',
        "...It didn't make any sense. It was ridiculous to think that it could. However, the door was locked.": '……{w}这说不通。指望它说得通，本身就荒唐。可门确实锁上了。',
        "I kept circling the floor, carefully scanning it. He couldn't have faded out of existence just like that—the door proved something else had happened.": '我在这一层来回走动，仔细扫视每个角落。{w}他不可能就这样凭空消失——那扇锁上的门说明另有蹊跷。',
        "Those events should've been erased completely, so why were they repeating? ...Maybe it didn't matter if I really had returned to my world. I would soon learn if everything I'd experienced would happen again.": '那些事本该被彻底抹去，为什么又在重演？{w}……也许不管我是不是真的回到了自己的世界，都已经不重要了。我很快就能知道，自己经历过的一切会不会再来一遍。',
        '...Wait!': '……{w}等等！',
        "...Why isn't my phone here? Why...? I had it when I touched the Sekimeiya, and the keys that I found in the mechanical room are still here with the one for my apartment. Why the hell is only my phone gone!?": '……我的手机怎么不在这里？{w}为什么……？我触碰 Sekimeiya 的时候它还在，机械室里找到的钥匙和我公寓的钥匙也都还在这里。为什么偏偏只有手机不见了！？',
        "Wait, that's not right. Not all the keys are here. I have the attic's and the rusty key, but not the cabinet's. Why? Why didn't that one travel with me!?": '等等，不对。钥匙并没有全在这里。{w}阁楼的钥匙和那把生锈的钥匙都在，唯独没有展示柜的钥匙。为什么？为什么偏偏那一把没有跟着我一起过来！？',
        "But wait. Where's Katei...?": '可是等等。{w}Katei人呢……？',
        "Then... this isn't the start of the day we know. Everything is bound to differ. ...Could Katei have seen me here, which made him hesitant to show himself?": '那么……这就不是我们所知道的那一天的开始了。一切肯定会变得不一样。{w}……会不会是Katei看见我在这里，才迟迟不肯现身？',
        'I\'d had a fairly absurd thought. "I can enter the attic, so what if I put on the clothes from up there and make up an excuse like being too cold or that my clothes were itchy due to the smoke?"': '我冒出一个相当荒唐的念头。{w}「既然我能进阁楼，那不如换上那边的衣服，再编个借口，比如太冷了，或者说烟尘弄得衣服发痒？」',
        "It was me who unlocked it. On the 15th, we couldn't get it to open when we came across it because Naomi had shut herself inside. ...Since it hasn't been locked again, she must not have left yet.": '锁是我打开的。15号那天，我们走到这里时打不开门，因为 Naomi 把自己关在了里面。{w}……既然门没有再被锁上，说明她还没有离开。',
        "I couldn't fathom the sight. Why was there another Sekimeiya next to it? I knew from what Atsuki told me that two had existed at one point...": '我无法理解眼前的景象。为什么它旁边还有另一个 Sekimeiya？{w} 听 Atsuki 说过，曾经有过两个……',
        'When we all entered the attic, her footprints began at the suitcase. Now, they end at it, and I already mixed mine with hers.': '我们大家一起进阁楼时，她的脚印是从行李箱那里开始的。{w} 现在却止于行李箱，而且我的脚印已经和她的混在一起了。',
        'Keeping my hands off the gem, I opened the wardrobe. Once I looked inside, I remembered the two pieces of clothing Atsuki had pointed at. They were a white shirt and a dark gray pair of pants, larger than what I usually wore. There was nothing else to put on.': '我没碰那颗宝石，打开了衣柜。往里一看，想起了 Atsuki 指过的那两件衣服。{w} 一件白衬衫，一条深灰色长裤，尺码都比我平时穿的大。除此之外没别的可穿。',
        'The door to the attic was still unlocked, so I had to hurry. I took off my coat and grabbed both pieces of clothing, sensing a bizarre surrealness as I put them on. Would that mere action guarantee my return to that world? There was nothing else I could do to aim for that. ...Had the me that Atsuki had seen really been me after all?': '阁楼的门还没上锁，我必须抓紧。我脱下外套，抓起那两件衣服换上，隐约觉得这一切荒诞得不真实。仅仅这样做，就能保证我回到那个世界吗？除此之外，我再没有别的办法可以尝试。{w}……Atsuki 见到的那个我，到底真的是我吗？',
        "The other Sekimeiya still sat on the sofa. What would happen to it? Would anyone find it before the rest entered the attic? We had only been able to come in thanks to the keys on Naomi's dead body. Someone in the tower had to be plotting her death right then, so I needed to find her and see if I could prevent that.": '另一个 Sekimeiya 仍放在沙发上。它会怎么样？会不会在其他人进阁楼之前就被发现？{w} 我们能进来，全靠 Naomi 尸体上的钥匙。塔里此刻一定有人在密谋取她性命，所以我必须找到她，看看能否阻止。',
        "He claimed the recording was real. What the hell did that even mean? Did they really spend an entire month here? There's no way.": '他硬说那段录音是真的。{w} 那到底是什么意思？他们真的在这里待了整整一个月？绝不可能。',
        "Katei's still not with them. There's no way they talked to the outside. Why is Katei not showing himself? He still has to be here, doesn't he...?": 'Katei 还是没跟他们在一起。{w}他们绝不可能跟外界联系过。{w}可 Katei 为什么迟迟不现身？他一定还在这里，不是吗……？',
        'Where could Atsuki be!? Is it possible he went to the past and was teleported outside the tower? ...Even if that happened, would he not have entered it again? I suppose not if the incident had already started.': 'Atsuki 到底在哪里！？会不会是他去了过去，结果被传送到了塔外？{w}……就算真是那样，他难道不会重新进去吗？除非那时事件已经开始了。',
        '...Atsuki? Are you here...? Atsuki!': '……Atsuki？{w}你在这儿吗……？{w}Atsuki！',
        '...What...?': '……{w}什么……？',
        "Puzzled, I tried to understand why stepping out of the building was possible. ...On the 15th, the handle had been taken off. When I'd entered the tower during the night, it had already been gone. So how could it possibly have been attached right then?": '我满腹疑惑，想弄清为什么此刻竟能走出这栋楼。{w}……15 号那天，把手已经被拆掉了。我夜里进塔的时候，它早就不在了。既然如此，它此刻怎么会还装在上面？',
        'There was a line of reasoning that made a bit of sense. In the morning of that day, we had found a rusty key on the floor of hallway A. ...It was a key I had in my purse at that very moment.': '有一条思路勉强说得通。{w}那天早上，我们在 A走廊的地上捡到过一把生锈的钥匙。……而此刻，那把钥匙正躺在我的手包里。',
        "Why would it have been removed so early? Of course, to prevent us from leaving. ...But how would anyone have done that? After all, the alarm was supposed to be a secret. We didn't even learn what really triggered it.": '何必那么早就把它拆掉？当然是为了不让我们离开。{w}……可这到底是怎么做到的？毕竟警报本该是秘密，我们连它到底是怎么被触发的都没弄明白。',
        "I see. ...The handle was removed days before the 15th, but this didn't repeat this time, so the door is unlocked. Someone who traveled far to the past must have removed the handle, aware of the alarm and secret door thanks to their future knowledge. But... did they see the handle removed before they traveled and then remove it in the past, making it a loop with no start...?": '原来如此。……那个世界的把手早在15日的好几天前就被拆掉了，这次却没有重演，所以门才没锁。一定是有人穿越到很久以前，拆下了把手——他凭着来自未来的知识，知道警报，也知道暗门。{w}可是……会不会是他穿越前见过把手被拆，于是回到过去亲手拆掉了它，这样就形成了一个没有起点的循环……？',
        "...Katei's absence. I don't think he's in the building right now. In the past, I found the key for this door in his security room. On the 15th, we found it in hallway A, where I bet he dropped it. ...I wonder why he didn't go back for it. Was Katei responsible for all this? That doesn't make a ton of sense, but he had this key. He was ready to leave through this door because he knew the alarm would go off and block every other method of escape. If someone hadn't removed the handle in the past, we might never have even seen him.": '……Katei 不在了。我想他现在并不在这栋楼里。{w}在那个世界，我是在他的监控室里找到这扇门的钥匙的。15日那天，我们在 A走廊捡到了它，我猜是他掉在那里的。……不知他为什么没有回去捡。{w}这一切都是 Katei 做的吗？这么说不太说得通，可钥匙确实在他手上。他早就准备从这扇门离开，因为他知道警报会响，其他所有逃路都会被封死。若不是有人在过去拆掉了把手，我们恐怕根本见不到他。',
        "It was possible the world would morph as the hours went on. People would learn about time travel and eventually go back in time. Upon altering the past, the world's status would shift. It was a mystery how the changes were applied, but I didn't think it was impossible that I could get to where I wanted merely by letting the hours pass.": '随着时间推移，世界也许会发生变化。人们会得知时间穿越，最终回到过去。一旦过去被改写，世界的状态也会随之改变。{w}这些变化是怎么生效的，至今仍是个谜，不过我想，也许光等着时间过去，我就能到达自己想去的地方。',
        "I turned around and walked toward the wall. ...I thought I'd heard a sound coming from the hallway.": '我转过身，朝墙走去。{w}……我好像听见走廊那边有动静。',
        "I had to rush out of the storeroom. That yell was full of nothing but despair, and someone was still there. I wanted to deny I'd even heard it, but I forced myself to move.": '我必须立刻冲出储藏室。那声喊叫里只有绝望，而那个人还在外面。{w}我恨不得当作自己什么都没听见，却还是逼着自己动了起来。',
        "...On the floor was my own body, facing me with blank eyes. It had been my own anguished yell that I'd heard. Next to it was Naomi, her head dripping blood beneath one of my arms.": '……地板上躺着我自己的尸体，空洞的双眼正对着我。刚才那声痛苦的喊叫，原来是我自己发出的。{w}旁边是 Naomi，她的头就在我一条手臂下面，鲜血不断滴落。',
        "I had to calm myself down. The world I was in wouldn't remain. It would be entirely modified until it warped into the day I'd lived through. That would erase my death.": '我必须冷静下来。我所在的这个世界不会一直这样。{w}它会被彻底改写，直到变成我经历过的那个日子。那样一来，我的死就会被抹去。',
        "I was unbearably terrified, so I froze behind the wall. Paralyzed by fear, I was unable to leave that place. I had to go to the event room and move the bodies to where I was so that they wouldn't be found. If the killer noticed me, however, everything would be over.": '我害怕得几乎无法承受，整个人僵在墙后。恐惧令我动弹不得，我无法离开那个地方。{w}我必须去活动室，把尸体搬到我这里来，免得被人发现。可一旦凶手注意到我，一切就完了。',
        "It had been a few minutes. Suddenly, faint voices came from the hallway. I immediately knew the group had returned. I couldn't even hesitate. Without wasting time, someone ran past, toward the event room. Then, a voice came from there.": '过了几分钟，走廊里忽然传来隐约的人声。我立刻明白，是他们回来了。{w}我连犹豫都来不及。有人马上跑了过去，奔向活动室。紧接着，那边传来了声音。',
        "It was Sai. It appeared the storeroom door, being lower quality than the rest, let sound pass easily. But Sai's words weren't the ones I'd expected. Upon hearing that, everyone else ran to the room.": '是 Sai。看来储藏室的门比别处单薄，声音很容易透过来。可 Sai 说的话出乎我的意料。{w}其他人一听到，全都朝活动室跑去。',
        '...What? Have they not seen the bodies? "The three of them". Naomi, myself, and someone else went down at some point. This third person must be the killer...': '……什么？他们没看到尸体吗？{w}「他们三个人」。Naomi、我，还有另一个人，都在某个时候下过楼。这第三个人，一定就是凶手……',
        '...That voice was Isla\'s. Puzzled, I still managed to comprehend what had happened. The bodies had been removed, but the Sekimeiya had been taken. They didn\'t seem to have noticed any blood on the floor, so it had been quickly cleaned as well. However, something didn\'t make sense. "The three of them must\'ve taken it!" Erina said that. If only those three were possible suspects, the whole group saw the Sekimeiya in the cabinet before going up. ...How was that possible? I had just seen two in the attic...': '……那是 Isla 的声音。我满心困惑，却还是勉强理清了状况。尸体被移走了，Sekimeiya 也被拿走了。他们似乎没注意到地板上有血，看来是被人迅速清理干净了。{w}可是有一点说不通。{w}「肯定是他们三个人拿走的！」这话是 Erina 说的。如果只有那三个人有嫌疑，那就意味着大家上楼之前，都看到了展示柜里的 Sekimeiya。{w}……这怎么可能？我明明才刚在阁楼里看到两个……',
        "Shiroya isn't doing anything! It has to be Naomi! Shiroya! If you're here, please come out!": 'Shiroya什么都没做！一定是Naomi！{w}Shiroya！你要是在这儿，就出来吧！',
        "...es, they have to be on the Ashiya floor. That's why this was done. The elevator wasn't working earlier, so they prevented us from using it as soon as it was up and running again.": '……没错，他们一定在芦屋层。所以他们才搞了这一出。{w}电梯之前一直不能用，他们就是不想让电梯一恢复就被我们用上。',
        '...Was Akaro the killer? When he proposed staying somewhere, an idea came to mind.': '……{w}难道Akaro就是凶手？他一提找个地方待着，我心里就浮起一个念头。',
        "It didn't seem like the bodies could've been in the attic, so it was possible Atsuki would find them if he searched hard enough. He was against staying in a room with everyone before finding me. That was one of the reasons I abandoned my hiding spot. I couldn't leave him alone, even if I wished the world would change. If he couldn't find me, he would suffer alone for hours. ...Even so, as I saw the hallway, I kept trembling. I really wanted to talk to him as if nothing had happened.": '那两具尸体应该不在阁楼里，只要 Atsuki 找得够仔细，说不定就会发现。在找到我之前，他不肯和大家一起待在房间里。这也是我放弃藏身之处的原因之一。{w}我没法把他一个人丢下，哪怕我心里盼着世界就此改变。要是他找不到我，就会独自煎熬好几个小时。……可即便如此，一望见走廊，我还是止不住发抖。我真的很想装作什么都没发生，去和他说说话。',
        "Nobody heard the sound of my steps. Who had killed me and Naomi? That question also brought me to leave the storeroom. If it wasn't anyone in hallway B, I wouldn't be safe staying by myself. If it was one of them, I would be safe as long as we were all together, and it was possible I could determine who was responsible. As long as nothing tricky happened, we would remain in one place. If I made sure that continued, it was a good way to let the time advance until the afternoon. It would almost guarantee that the interior of the tower remained calm.": '没有人听见我的脚步声。究竟是谁杀了我和 Naomi？这个问题也促使我离开了储藏室。{w}若凶手不在 B走廊这些人里，我独自待着并不安全；若凶手就在他们之中，只要大家待在一起，我就没事，说不定还能查出是谁下的手。{w}只要不出什么岔子，我们就会一直待在同一个地方。我若能盯住这一点，正好可以让时间一点点推进到下午，几乎就能保证塔里平安无事。',
        'In his hands was a glowing Sekimeiya. However, I immediately saw something I assumed nobody had realized. His sleeve was between it and his skin. He was purposely avoiding contact with it.': '他手里握着一个发光的 Sekimeiya。然而，我立刻发现了一处大概谁都没注意到的细节。{w}他的袖子隔在它和自己的皮肤之间——他是故意不去碰它。',
        'Wait, wh-what? No. We never went there. In the attic, she gave me these, and when we left, she suddenly ran back and locked herself inside.': '等等，你、你说什么？没有。我们根本没去过那里。{w}在阁楼里，她把这些给了我，我们出来之后，她突然又跑回去，把自己锁在了里面。',
        "...When we saw that the Sekimeiya was gone, Akaro told us to run upstairs. He'd been searching for you two, and we missed him when he was in the offices. On the fourth floor, the panel had been ripped off. We went up and saw that they were gone on the fifth and sixth as well. Sai tried to open the doors, but the elevator wasn't there. By the time we ran all the way down, it had happened on the first three floors too, and the elevator wasn't there either.": '……我们发现 Sekimeiya 不见了之后，Akaro 就叫我们往楼上跑。他一直在找你们俩，我们在办公室那一带和他错过了。{w}四楼的面板已经被撬了下来。我们再往上，五楼、六楼也一样。Sai 试着开门，可电梯不在那里。{w}等我们一路跑到楼下，底下三层也成了这样，电梯同样不在。',
        "Finally, Akaro spoke. From the storeroom, I'd noticed his voice sounded rougher and sharper than I remembered, but that seemed to have disappeared. When I looked at him, he turned around and walked to that room.": 'Akaro 终于开口了。我在储藏室里就注意到，他的嗓音比我记忆中更粗更尖，可这会儿那种感觉似乎已经消失了。{w}我看向他时，他转过身，朝那间屋子走去。',
        "He had knowledge of the Sekimeiya—the way he held it was the giveaway. He had to be the one who had stolen it, not just the killer. Atsuki and I had seen the temperature set to 0 °C more than once, and Akaro specifically set it to 5 °C, so there was no way he didn't know about that requirement. ...The temperature of the Sekimeiya's display cabinet wasn't visible, so I wondered what it was.": '他了解 Sekimeiya——看他拿它的手法就明白了。他一定就是偷走它的人，而不只是凶手。我和 Atsuki 不止一次见过温度被设在 0 °C，而 Akaro 特意把它设成 5 °C，他不可能不知道这个要求。{w}……Sekimeiya 展示柜的温度从外面看不到，我有些在意那究竟是多少。',
        "Lastly, when I least expected it, Akaro approached us. ...I glanced at him, but his eyes didn't meet mine. Then, he sat to my right, between me and the cabinet containing the Sekimeiya.": '最后，在我最没料到的时候，Akaro 朝我们走来。……我瞥了他一眼，他却没有与我对视。{w}随后他在我右边坐下，就坐在我和放着 Sekimeiya 的展示柜之间。',
        "The last time, all of us had looked at the gems, so the situation clearly differed. Atsuki hadn't so much as shifted one of his legs since we'd come in. I'd wanted to talk to him, but I hadn't expected he would act that way. Before entering the tower, he and I had spoken very little. That gradually changed during the day, but the Atsuki next to me looked just like he had at his house.": '上一次来的时候，我们所有人都去看那些宝石了，眼下的情形显然不同。{w}自从进来，Atsuki 连腿都没挪过一下。我本想和他说话，却没料到他会是这副样子。进塔之前，他和我说的话少得可怜。这一天里，这种情况才渐渐有了改观，可坐在我身边的 Atsuki，那副模样和在他家里时一模一样。',
        "...So Naomi hasn't shown up. Did she not say anything when she locked herself inside the top floor?": '「……Naomi 还是没露面。{w} 她把自己关在顶层的时候，什么都没说吗？」',
        "No, she didn't... I don't know what got into her, but I assume she wanted to do whatever she did to the elevator. I guess while we're here, there's nothing she can do anymore.": '「没有，她什么都没说……我不知道她是怎么了，不过我猜，她大概还想把对电梯做过的事再来一遍。{w} 既然我们待在这儿，她应该也翻不出什么花样了。」',
        "...Oh. I'm very sorry. I can't imagine what that would be like at your age. I thought earlier that something about you two looked off. I'm really sorry for bringing it up.": '「……哦。{w} 实在抱歉。{w} 你们这个年纪经历这种事，我实在想象不出有多难受。刚才我就觉得你们俩有点不对劲。真不该提这事，对不起。」',
        "Atsuki said what I'd been about to. Then, Akaro gave us a look of pity. I could only wonder why he'd said any of that.": '我正要开口，Atsuki 却先说了出来。{w}随后，Akaro 投来怜悯的目光。我实在不明白他为什么要说那些话。',
        "I did lose someone very close to me a long time ago too. I don't imagine this is something you want to hear from a person you don't know, but all I wish now is that I hadn't thought that much about it. At the time, I thought I'd be disrespecting the dead if I tried to get over it, but that nearly ate me alive. I guess you're already doing much better than me if you're here. Thinking too hard about these things when they just happened can be pure torture.": '我很久以前也失去过一个很亲近的人。我知道这话从一个素不相识的人嘴里说出来，你们可能不爱听，但我现在只希望自己当初没有想那么多。{w}当时我觉得，如果试着放下，就是对死者的不敬，可那种想法差点把我整个人吞掉。{w}你们现在能来到这里，已经比我强多了。事情刚发生时想太多，纯粹是折磨。',
        "Uh... almost two hours. It's 11:00.": '呃……快两个小时了。现在是 {time=11.}。',
        "Uh... almost two hours. It's 11 a.m.": '呃……快两个小时了。现在是 {time=11.}。',
        "Of course, nobody but Akaro. The way he had held it hadn't been a coincidence. ...I didn't know why, but aware of its powers, his intention was to keep us shut in a room while the Sekimeiya was with us. Did he know about the twelve hour limit? ...Or was the reason tied to the other Sekimeiya that I'd seen? I still potentially had one hidden in the attic.": '当然，除了 Akaro。他握着它的方式绝非偶然。……我不知道原因，但他既然知道它的力量，那他的意图就是趁 Sekimeiya 还在我们这里时，把我们关在房间里。{w}他知道十二小时的时限吗？……还是说，原因与我见到的另一个 Sekimeiya 有关？阁楼里我可能还藏着一个。',
        "He was the killer who'd hidden his victims' bodies. He had conjured the illusion that Naomi was still alive thanks to the Sekimeiya. ...Next to me, he hadn't opened his mouth again. He knew that I was lying and must've seen me as a threat, but his brief conversation with us had left me dazed.": '他就是那个藏匿受害者尸体的凶手。他借 Sekimeiya 之力，制造出 Naomi 还活着的假象。{w}……坐在我身旁的他再没开过口。他知道我在撒谎，一定也把我视作威胁，可他方才那几句简短的交谈，却让我心神恍惚。',
        "...It's 13:00.": '……现在是 {time=13.}。',
        "...It's 1 p.m.": '……现在是 {time=13.}。',
        "*sigh* ...I'm going to the bathroom.": '唉……{w}{w=0.7}我去趟洗手间。',
        'My mind jumped to the other Atsuki. ...Was he still there? We listened with rapt attention, but there was nothing else to hear.': '我脑中立刻闪过另一个 Atsuki。……他还在那里吗？{w} 我们屏息凝神地听着，却再没听到别的动静。',
        "Don't think about leaving. Whatever they're doing won't matter as long as we're here. It's not our business either. They're the ones who could be committing a crime.": '别想着出去。只要我们还待在这儿，他们想干什么都成不了。{w} 这也不关我们的事。真要说犯法，那也是他们。',
        "Then who was the other person? With everything seemingly unchanging, my need to know had only grown larger. Could it have been Atsuki? I didn't think so. Had Katei been there the whole time? I didn't think so either. ...Was it someone who'd traveled through time?": '那么另一个人是谁？周围的一切看起来毫无变化，我想知道答案的念头反而越来越强。会是 Atsuki 吗？我觉得不像。Katei 会不会一直就在那里？我也不这么认为。{w} ……难道是某个穿越时间而来的人？',
        '...I have to go to the bathroom. Do you need to go too, Isla?': '……我得去趟洗手间。{w} Isla，你也要去吗？',
        'She shook her head. At the same time, the rest of us looked on with skepticism after what had happened with Sai.': '她摇了摇头。{w}与此同时，因为 Sai 之前的事，我们其余人都怀疑地看向 Aki。',
        "...But she wasn't. After a little while, we realized the same thing had occurred.": '……可她并没有回来。{w} 过了一会儿，我们意识到同样的事又发生了。',
        "Before he could object, I walked to the door. I didn't exactly want to leave Atsuki behind, but I had no choice. I hadn't missed Akaro's sudden frown, but he kept his mouth shut as I passed by Isla.": '没等他出言反对，我已经走向门口。我并不想丢下 Atsuki，但别无选择。{w}Akaro 骤然皱眉，我并没有漏看；可我从 Isla 身旁经过时，他始终没有开口。',
        "Both bodies were there, near the hallway A door. Like before, my own looked at the ceiling with empty eyes, while drops of blood had stained the floor beneath Naomi's head. In addition, all the ceiling lights were on, even the ones that the alarm had disabled and weren't working in the morning.": '两具尸体都在，就在 A走廊门口附近。和先前一样，我自己的那具尸体睁着空洞的双眼望着天花板，Naomi 头下的地板则被滴落的血染红了。{w}此外，天花板上的灯全亮着，连早晨因警报而失效、本该不亮的那些也亮了。',
        'Someone was far ahead, next to the staircase. A pool of blood extended around a third fallen body, lying in the illuminated zone.': '前方远处有个人影，就在楼梯旁。{w}第三具尸体倒在灯光照亮的区域，身下漫开一摊血。',
        "Had the killer been outside all along? It was too overwhelming—I couldn't bear it anymore. But the next thing I heard was footsteps from hallway B, causing my heart to drop even further.": '难道凶手一直就在外面？{w}这一切太沉重，我再也承受不住。可紧接着，B走廊传来的脚步声让我的心又往下沉了一截。',
        "Could the door have been preventing the sound from reaching me? No. I'd heard Atsuki going up the stairs.": '难道是门挡住了声音，才传不到我耳中？{w}不，我连 Atsuki 上楼的声音都听见了。',
        "She's not here. Oh... I was right.": '她不在这里。{w} 哦……我猜对了。',
        "It's cold. ...They must've traveled, though. That's why the sounds stopped.": '好冰。{w} ……不过，他们一定是穿越走了，所以声音才停下。',
        '...But where were they? I was clueless. Why had the Sekimeiya been touched, and why had it allowed someone to travel? The temperature in the cabinet was frigid.': '……可他们去了哪里？我毫无头绪。{w} Sekimeiya 为什么会被人碰过，又为什么会让人穿越？展示柜里冷得刺骨。',
        "I left the storeroom. If what had been in the lobby was a pool, near the staircase, Erina's body lay on a sea of blood. ...That Erina, below the broken elevator... We had never spoken to her. That was because she had died.": '我离开储藏室。如果说大厅里那摊血只算一小滩，那么楼梯附近就是一片血海——Erina 的尸体就躺在那里。{w}……那个倒在坏掉的电梯下方的 Erina……我们始终没能和她说上话。因为她早就死了。',
        "It's gotta be later than {time=15.} That fits perfectly. And... the drop of blood that Atsuki and I saw in the lobby... It was exactly where Naomi's body left it before vanishing.": '现在肯定已经过了 {time=15.}。这样就全对上了。{w} 还有……我和 Atsuki 在大厅看到的那滴血……正好就在 Naomi 的尸体消失前留下它的地方。',
        "It's gotta be later than 15:00. That fits perfectly.{w} And... the drop of blood that Atsuki and I saw in the lobby... It was exactly where Naomi's body left it before vanishing.": '现在肯定已经过了 {time=15.}。这样就全对上了。{w} 还有……我和 Atsuki 在大厅看到的那滴血……正好就在 Naomi 的尸体消失前留下它的地方。',
        "It's gotta be later than 15:00. That fits perfectly. And... the drop of blood that Atsuki and I saw in the lobby... It was exactly where Naomi's body left it before vanishing.": '现在肯定已经过了 {time=15.}。这样就全对上了。{w} 还有……我和 Atsuki 在大厅看到的那滴血……正好就在 Naomi 的尸体消失前留下它的地方。',
        "It's gotta be later than 3 p.m. That fits perfectly.{w} And... the drop of blood that Atsuki and I saw in the lobby... It was exactly where Naomi's body left it before vanishing.": '现在肯定已经过了 {time=15.}。这样就全对上了。{w} 还有……我和 Atsuki 在大厅看到的那滴血……正好就在 Naomi 的尸体消失前留下它的地方。',
        "It's gotta be later than 3 p.m. That fits perfectly. And... the drop of blood that Atsuki and I saw in the lobby... It was exactly where Naomi's body left it before vanishing.": '现在肯定已经过了 {time=15.}。这样就全对上了。{w} 还有……我和 Atsuki 在大厅看到的那滴血……正好就在 Naomi 的尸体消失前留下它的地方。',
        'Another Sekimeiya...? Could this be the one I hid?': '另一个 Sekimeiya……？{w} 难道是我藏起来的那个？',
        "It was open, so I could see the narrow staircase ahead. Why? Why wasn't the door locked anymore? Furthermore, the key was inserted in the outer keyhole.": '门开着，前方的窄梯一览无余。{w}为什么？门为什么不再上锁了？不仅如此，外侧的锁孔里还插着钥匙。',
        "Many footprints were pressed into the carpet. It didn't make any sense, but I didn't care. I also saw that the suitcase was no longer on the sofa. As soon as I stepped into the living room, I heard a noise coming from one of the bedrooms.": '地毯上印着许多脚印。这说不通，可我已经不在乎了。我还发现沙发上的行李箱不见了。{w}刚踏进客厅，我便听见某间卧室里传来响动。',
        'He had seen the dead bodies—my own death. I was still alive, though.': '他看见了那些尸体——也看见了我的尸体。{w}可我还活着。',
        "I recalled what Sai had told us a long time in the past. According to him, the drop of blood in the lobby was mine. He'd been wrong, hadn't he? It was Naomi's. In that case, why had he said that? And why had he been both right and wrong about my fate?": '我想起很久以前 Sai 对我们说过的话。据他所说，大厅里那滴血是我的。{w}他弄错了，不是吗？那是 Naomi 的。{w}既然如此，他为什么要那么说？而对于我的命运，他又为何既说对了，又说错了？',
        'The answer to that question was one I already knew. They were in my world. They were the proof that going back was possible.': '这个问题的答案，我其实早已知道。{w}他们在我那个世界里。他们就是能回去的证明。',
        "It had taken me a while to process it, but everything he said had started to make sense. The events he described were the ones I'd just lived through. He'd sympathized with us, and he'd been surprised to hear we'd found Naomi's body but not that she'd died. After all, he had killed her in the world I was in, hadn't he?": '我花了一阵子才想明白，但他说的话渐渐都说得通了。他描述的，正是我刚刚经历过的事。{w}他很同情我们。听说我们找到了 Naomi 的尸体，他很惊讶；但听说她死了，他却不意外。毕竟，在我所在的那个世界里，杀死她的人正是他，不是吗？',
        'And Isla... What the hell happened to her? At the same time that Akaro appeared, Erina swore she heard Isla just outside the bedroom.': '还有 Isla……她到底出了什么事？{w}就在 Akaro 出现的同时，Erina 坚称听见 Isla 就在卧室门外。',
        'The Sai who chased us with a knife... Who was he? ...The one who left the crystal room a while ago is the one who had the chance to see my body in the lobby. Is that where he made a mistake?': '那个拿着刀追我们的 Sai……他到底是谁？{w}……刚才离开水晶展室的那个人，才有可能在大厅看见我的尸体。他是不是就在那儿搞错了？',
        "That's what brought them there. It has to be. How did I even get here in the first place? It was by touching the Sekimeiya. ...And why did Atsuki disappear from this world? I'd bet it happened when Naomi touched the Sekimeiya.": '就是它把他们送到了那里。一定是这样。{w}那我自己最初又是怎么来到这里的？是因为碰了 Sekimeiya。……还有，Atsuki 为什么会从这个世界上消失？我猜，是在 Naomi 碰 Sekimeiya 的时候。',
        "Hm... I'm pretty sure someone should be here, no matter what time it is.": '唔……{w}不管是什么时候，这里按理都该有人才对。',
        '...Hallway A. Immediately, I noticed something that differed.': '……A走廊。{w}我立刻察觉到了异样。',
        '...I put on my boots and closed the door.': '……{w}我穿上靴子，关上了门。',
        "Hold on. That's it. ...That's what happened!": '等等。{w}我知道了。……原来是这么回事！',
        "The identity of Isla's friend... I had finally figured it out.": 'Isla 那位朋友的身份……{w}我终于想通了。',
        "There were many things I had learned. Vaisude revealed that there was a large travel at around 16:00. That was how he had appeared on the 24th of November, and it happened to fit with the approximate date Isla's friend had appeared.": '我已经弄清了许多事。Vaisude 透露，{time=16.} 前后曾发生过一次大规模的穿越。正因如此，他才会在 11 月 24 日出现，而这也恰好与 Isla 的朋友出现的大致日期相符。',
        "There were many things I had learned. Vaisude revealed that there was a large travel at around 4 p.m. That was how he had appeared on the 24th of November, and it happened to fit with the approximate date Isla's friend had appeared.": '我已经弄清了许多事。Vaisude 透露，{time=16.} 前后曾发生过一次大规模的穿越。正因如此，他才会在 11 月 24 日出现，而这也恰好与 Isla 的朋友出现的大致日期相符。',
        'At 16:00, there was a very large travel, and everyone who got caught up in it appeared on the 24th of November. Three people who traveled were Vaisude, Isla, and Akaro.': '在{time=16}，发生过一次规模极大的时间穿越，所有被卷入其中的人都在 11 月 24 日出现。穿越的三人是 Vaisude、Isla 和 Akaro。',
        'At 4 p.m., there was a very large travel, and everyone who got caught up in it appeared on the 24th of November. Three people who traveled were Vaisude, Isla, and Akaro.': '在{time=16}，发生过一次规模极大的时间穿越，所有被卷入其中的人都在 11 月 24 日出现。穿越的三人是 Vaisude、Isla 和 Akaro。',
        "The Akaro who appeared in the cell wasn't the same Akaro we originally met in the morning. In a way, that explains some of the questions I had. Didn't Atsuki say that he'd seen Akaro once again? That was the version of him who escaped the bedroom with Sai. Why did he appear in prison, and what did he do later? I don't know, but at this point I have no doubt Akaro was the Xyn member trapped with us.": '出现在牢房里的 Akaro，并不是我们早上刚见到的那个 Akaro。从某种意义上说，这解释了我心里的几个疑问。{w} Atsuki 不是说过，他又见到过 Akaro 一次吗？那应该就是和 Sai 一起逃出卧室的那个 Akaro。{w} 可他为什么出现在牢房，之后又做了什么？我不知道，但到这一步，我已经毫不怀疑——和我们一起被困住的 Xyn 成员就是 Akaro。',
        'And that\'s how both Islas met. ...Earlier, when we were in the bedroom, Erina\'s and Isla\'s behavior seemed different. That\'s because in that world, her "friend" never appeared. This is the solution to Atsuki\'s problem. After going to the past, she didn\'t recreate what she had lived through. For her, that was happening for the first time.': '两个 Isla 就是这样相遇的。……先前在卧室时，Erina 和 Isla 的举止有些反常。那是因为在那个世界里，她的「朋友」始终没有出现。{w} 这也解开了 Atsuki 的疑问。回到过去之后，她并没有重演自己经历过的一切。对她来说，那些事都是第一次发生。',
        '"She said that if we stayed calm in one place, nobody would be hurt." That\'s exactly what we did. We stayed in a crystal room, and Isla never saw any of the dead bodies.': '「她说，只要我们安静地待在一个地方，就不会有人受伤。」{w} 我们也确实这么做了。我们一直待在某个水晶展室里，Isla 从未见过任何尸体。',
        '"She said that even though she didn\'t know how it would end or how long we\'d stay here for, she\'d wait for me at home." I see. The reason she didn\'t know how it would end was because she traveled to the past in the middle of the day, and she didn\'t know how long we\'d stay because Katei hadn\'t been there to explain the alarm.': '「她说，虽然她不知道事情会怎样结束，也不知道我们要在这里待多久，但她会在家里等我。」{w} 原来如此。她不知道事情会怎样结束，是因为她在白天就穿越回了过去；她不知道我们要待多久，是因为当时 Katei 不在，没人解释那阵警报。',
        "There was one last thing Isla had told us. Her friend assured her that she would get to touch the Sekimeiya. The Isla I'd just been with had touched it. In the crystal room, she asked about it, but Akaro told her not to. When he left Isla alone, I'm sure she took advantage of it. That was why the cabinet was open and why both of them appeared in the world I was in.": 'Isla 还告诉过我们最后一件事。她的朋友向她保证，她一定能亲手碰触 Sekimeiya。{w} 我刚才见到的那个 Isla 就碰过它。在水晶展室里，她问起过它，Akaro 却不许她碰。等 Akaro 留下她一个人时，她一定抓住了机会。所以展示柜才会开着，两人也才会出现在我所在的世界。',
        'Whoa, what the hell...? Did this happen again?': '哇，怎么回事……？{w} 又来了吗？',
        'Just what the hell is happening? The Sekimeiya I have right now is the one we touched in that crystal room, right...?': '到底发生什么事了？{w}我现在手里这个 Sekimeiya，就是我们在那间水晶展室里碰过的那个，对吧……？',
        "I just took it, so that's why we didn't find it later. ...Instead, we found it in a drawer. That must not have been the same one. ...Is that it?": '是我刚刚把它拿走了，所以后来才找不到。……结果，我们却在抽屉里发现了一个。{w}那一定不是同一个。……是这样吗？',
        "It's the same cabinet we saw that day. ...Actually, I should keep the Sekimeiya here. I was thinking of bringing it to the storeroom, but that could be risky depending on what happened.": '这就是我们那天看到的那个展示柜。{w}……说起来，我还是把 Sekimeiya 留在这里吧。我本来想把它带到储藏室，但万一出了什么状况，那样做可能很危险。',
        "The elevator was another key detail to those events. After leaving the attic's bedroom for the first time, we had heard the elevator twice on the office floors.": '电梯也是这些事件中的另一个关键细节。{w}第一次离开阁楼的卧室后，我们在办公楼层听到了两次电梯声。',
        "That was the reason why I was skeptical about my surroundings. I was in that world, but there had to be something I was mistaken about. If it was the time of day, everything made sense. If the sounds I'd heard in the attic hadn't belonged to our past selves, there was no contradiction.": '正因如此，我才对周围的环境心存怀疑。我确实身处那个世界，但一定有什么地方被我弄错了。{w}如果错的是时间，一切就都说得通。如果我在阁楼听到的声响并非来自过去的我们，那就不存在矛盾。',
        "Before I could finish, she fell to the floor. Her clothes were soaked in blood, and her expression was vacant. I moved to shake her shoulder, but she didn't respond.": '话还没说完，她便瘫倒在地。{w} 衣服浸透了血，神情空洞。我伸手去摇她的肩膀，她却毫无反应。',
        "I doubted what to do. Sai and Akaro could've been very close by. In the other world, Akaro had killed me, and in the one I was in, Sai would soon chase us with a knife. No matter what, I couldn't let myself be seen, so going to the storeroom was dangerous.": '我一时拿不定主意。Sai 和 Akaro 很可能就在附近。{w} 在另一个世界里，Akaro 杀了我；而在我所处的这个世界，Sai 很快就会拿刀来追我们。无论如何，我都不能被人看见，所以去储藏室太冒险了。',
        "Wait, no. I don't have to.": '等等，不对。{w} 我没必要去。',
        "I didn't get it. Was I not properly remembering what had happened...? I looked up at the camera. Was I being recorded in two different places simultaneously?": '我不明白。难道是我记错了当时的情形……？{w} 我抬头望向摄像头。难道我在两个不同的地方同时被拍到了？',
        "What...? The green light still isn't there. That's odd...": '什么……？{w} 绿灯还是没亮。真奇怪……',
        "They did. Then, another door was opened. ...I knew it was the staff room's.": '果然如此。{w} 接着，又有一扇门打开了。……我知道，那是员工室的门。',
        '...et the Se— ...has to be—': '……拿到 Sekimeiya——{w} ……一定得——',
        "In the event room, I had fallen asleep very quickly. I'd been dead tired that day. I felt a similar exhaustion at that moment. I'd been in the tower for many hours already, but they'd fortunately been much less dense.": '在活动室里，我很快就睡着了。那天我实在疲惫不堪。{w}此刻我也感到相似的倦意。我已经在塔里待了好几个小时，好在比起那天，这几个小时要松散得多。',
        "There was yet another reason—it would've caused a problem that I was finally sure existed. I couldn't interact with my old self. It was the same thing we'd considered with Isla. If my past self met the future me and tried to keep everything exactly the same, she'd have to replicate precisely what she'd seen me do. Every word, every movement. No human was capable of that. It was crucial not to be seen by both her and Atsuki.": '还有一个原因：那样做会引发一个问题，而我现在终于确信这个问题确实存在。{w}我不能和过去的自己接触。这和当初我们与 Isla 讨论过的是同一回事。如果过去的我遇见了未来的我，还想让一切保持原样，她就必须把看见我做的每件事都分毫不差地复现出来——每一句话、每一个动作。没有人能做到这一点。{w}绝不能让过去的我和 Atsuki 同时看见我。',
        'On that mountain, I made a decision... To change the past and save everyone. Miiya, Isla, Erina, Katei, Naomi...': '在那座山上，我下定了决心……{w}要改变过去，救下所有人。Miiya、Isla、Erina、Katei、Naomi……',
        "And yet... I didn't know what to do. Hadn't I also decided that going to the past was a mistake?": '然而……我却不知道自己该做什么。{w}我不是也认定过，回到过去是个错误吗？',
        "The Atsuki from this morning said that the recording was real. We won't simply leave at 21:00.": '今早的 Atsuki 说那段录音是真的。到了 {time=21.}，我们不会就这么离开。',
        "The Atsuki from this morning said that the recording was real. We won't simply leave at 9 p.m.": '今早的 Atsuki 说那段录音是真的。到了 {time=21.}，我们不会就这么离开。',
        "And that wasn't all. He was suspicious of me and asked if I was the real Shiroya. ...Why? What happened after I went back in time?": '而且还不止如此。他起了疑心，问我是不是真的 Shiroya。{w}……为什么？我回到过去之后，到底发生了什么？',
        "I looked down. When the Sekimeiya had begun to get too hot, I'd left it on the floor. It was a bit difficult to decide what to do with it.": '我低下头。Sekimeiya 开始烫得厉害时，我把它放在了地板上。{w}要怎么处置它，我还有些拿不定主意。',
        "...That was what seemed odd. Up until that point, everything I'd done that had matched with what I'd already lived through contained a purpose. The clothes, showing myself, the elevator... I hadn't repeated anything without a reason. So then, what was going on? Would I leave the Sekimeiya there to give Sai a way to escape? ...Simply to avoid changing the past?": '……{w}奇怪的地方就在这里。在那之前，我做的每一件事，凡是与已经经历过的过去吻合的，都有它的目的。衣服、现身、电梯……我重复任何一件事都有理由。{w}那么，到底是怎么回事？我难道会把 Sekimeiya 留在那里，只为了给 Sai 一条脱身之路？……仅仅为了不改变过去？',
        "It was weird. Because I had realized it, I had no reason to leave the Sekimeiya in that cabinet. Even though I wanted to hide it far from me, it didn't have to be in hallway B. I didn't want to leave the Sekimeiya there. Aside from the fact that it would be consistent with my experiences, it would only bring negative consequences.": '这很奇怪。既然我已经意识到了这一点，就没有理由再把 Sekimeiya 留在那个展示柜里。我固然想把它藏到离自己远点的地方，但未必非要放在 B走廊。{w}我不想把 Sekimeiya 留在那里。除了能和我的经历对得上之外，这么做只会带来坏处。',
        "But didn't that mean Sai would still manage to hide anyway? After all, I wouldn't {i}not{/i} be doing it to change the past; disregarding my own interests purely to be consistent with what I'd already experienced wasn't how everything had worked so far. That was what I was curious about and what I wanted to observe from a distance. How was Sai going to escape detection?": '可这不就说明，Sai 到头来还是会藏起来吗？毕竟，我做这件事并不是为了{i}不{/i}改变过去；一味为了和已经经历过的事保持一致，就不顾自己的利益——到目前为止，事情并不是这样运作的。{w}这正是我好奇、也想从远处观察的地方。Sai 究竟要怎么逃过搜查？',
        "Oh. Don't tell me it's already gonna be gone. ...Is this how Sai managed to disappear?": '哦。别告诉我它已经不见了。{w}……Sai 就是这样消失的吗？',
        "I retreated immediately. ...In hallway A, I'd just seen Sai. He hadn't seen me in return, but something was very odd. He'd been exiting the storeroom with a knife in his hand and was visibly shocked after looking at the stairs, where there was nothing.": '我立刻退了回去。{w}……刚才在 A走廊，我看见了 Sai。他没有看到我，可有件事很不对劲。{w}他手里握着刀，正从储藏室里出来，朝楼梯那边看了一眼——那里什么都没有，他却明显吃了一惊。',
        'The sound got louder until it was coming from right behind the door. However, the steps kept going.': '声音越来越近，最后已经到了门后。{w}然而那脚步没有停，继续往前走了。',
        "...It didn't sound like he'd looked into all the rooms again, so I didn't understand.": '……{w}听这动静，他不像是又把每个房间都看了一遍。我不明白为什么。',
        "Our past selves are in the attic, and they'll try to come back here soon. ...I guess I get how the chase started. I think Sai was searching for someone while holding that knife. I don't know why, but it's very possible he wanted to find Atsuki.": '过去的我们还待在阁楼，很快就会设法回到这里。……我大概明白那场追捕是怎么开始的了。{w} Sai 当时握着那把刀，像是在找什么人。原因我不清楚，但他很可能是在找我。',
        "The elevator's on this floor, and Sai went up to search for Atsuki. When we called the elevator from the attic, he was on the third floor and heard it. He probably figured it was empty, especially if he knew it was on the crystal floor. From his perspective, someone called it from the attic and was about to go back down.": '电梯停在这一层，而 Sai 上楼去找我了。我们从阁楼叫电梯的时候，他正在三楼，听见了动静。{w}他大概以为电梯里没人——毕竟他知道电梯停在水晶层。在他看来，是有人从阁楼叫了电梯，正要坐它下去。',
        "...How did the chase go down, though? We locked ourselves in the attic, but somehow he had another key to open it. We thought we couldn't try to lock ourselves in a bedroom because he took the key, but it was still in the drawer when he and I teleported in there later. But that's not all. I found out Sai had the keys to both bedrooms in his pocket, and he even frowned when he saw one was in the drawer. That must be why he didn't take it to trap us... Did he think it wouldn't be there because he'd already taken it?": '……可那场追捕到底是怎么回事？我们把自己锁进了阁楼，他却不知从哪弄到另一把钥匙，把门打开了。{w} 我们以为没法躲进卧室上锁，是因为钥匙被他拿走了，可后来他和我传送到那里时，那把钥匙还躺在抽屉里。{w} 不止如此。我发现 Sai 口袋里两间卧室的钥匙都在，而且他看到抽屉里那把时还皱了皱眉。所以他没把钥匙拿走、用来困住我们，多半就是这个原因……他是不是以为那钥匙早被自己拿走了，不该还留在那儿？',
        "It was late into the day. 21:00 was close to two hours away, and I'd touched the Sekimeiya in the bathroom a while before that.": '天色已经晚了。距离 {time=21} 还有将近两个小时，而我在此前不久刚在洗手间碰过 Sekimeiya。',
        "It was late into the day. 9 p.m. was close to two hours away, and I'd touched the Sekimeiya in the bathroom a while before that.": '天色已经晚了。距离 {time=21} 还有将近两个小时，而我在此前不久刚在洗手间碰过 Sekimeiya。',
        'Shortly after they faded, the same sound repeated, and it quickly approached me. It was Sai. He had appeared from hallway B, running into Atsuki.': '脚步声刚远去不久，同样的声音又响了起来，并且迅速朝我逼近。{w} 是 Sai。他从 B走廊出现，撞上了 Atsuki。',
        'Confused, I hid myself before Atsuki saw me. Then, I glanced at the Sekimeiya. ...I still had it.': '我一头雾水，趁 Atsuki 还没看见我，先藏了起来。随后我瞥了一眼 Sekimeiya。{w} ……它还在我手上。',
        "Sai had sprinted straight ahead, shutting himself inside room B4, where I'd just been. Could there have been a third Sekimeiya? If not, his disappearance couldn't be explained.": 'Sai 一路直冲，把自己关进了水晶展室 B4——那正是我刚才待的地方。{w} 难道还有第三个 Sekimeiya？若非如此，他的消失就无法解释。',
        '...Ah, no. I think I know what he did.': '……啊，不对。{w} 我想我知道他做了什么。',
        "...It was absurd, but given his grin, I was sure it was the right answer. Something we'd told him had allowed him to pull it off.": '……{w}这太荒唐了，可一想到他那个笑容，我就确信答案正是如此。是我们告诉他的某件事，让他办成了这件事。',
        "We told him Erina died, but he knew the truth. Before, when he was looking through the floor, he came across Erina. After that, she woke up and left the room. When I was in the cleaning room, Sai walked through the hallway again. Maybe he was drawn to the sound and saw Erina was gone. In short, he knew she hadn't died and that she wasn't in that room anymore.": '我们告诉他 Erina 死了，可他知道真相。{w} 之前他在这一层搜寻时，撞见了 Erina。之后她醒了过来，离开了房间。我待在清洁间的时候，Sai 又从走廊经过。也许他是被声音引过去，发现 Erina 不见了。{w} 总之，他知道她没有死，也知道她已经不在那个房间了。',
        "...Did it cool down a little? It's still pretty hot, so it's not like I put it in the cold cabinets. That's weird.": '……它好像凉了一点？{w} 可还是挺烫的，我又没把它放进冰冷的展示柜里。真奇怪。',
        "Next to Naomi's body, the red curtain lay by itself. Without wasting time, I did what I'd planned earlier and left the Sekimeiya sealed away in the very first cabinet where we'd found it. When I closed it, a sound indicated it had locked automatically. The wheel appeared damaged, but it still worked, so I was able to set the temperature to 0 °C.": 'Naomi 的尸体旁，红色遮布孤零零地落在地上。我没有耽搁，按先前想好的做法，把 Sekimeiya 封进我们最初发现它的那个展示柜里。关上柜门时，一声轻响表明它已自动上锁。{w} 转盘看上去有损坏，但还能用，我便把温度设成了 0 °C。',
        "Technically, I was guaranteed to be seen again—it was what I'd been told. Not knowing what would happen was a little nerve-wracking, but Sai had been one person to see me. There was a bit of time left until that could happen, as he'd been in the attic for a while.": '严格来说，我注定还会被人看见——这是别人告诉过我的。{w} 不知道会发生什么，多少让人心里发紧，不过 Sai 就是会看见我的人之一。距离那一刻还有些时间，毕竟他在阁楼里待了好一阵子。',
        "...Where the hell are Erina and Akaro? It's been so long since anyone saw Akaro. The one who came to the bedroom wasn't the same one who left with Sai. ...I know he's here, though.": '……Erina 和 Akaro 到底跑哪去了？{w} 已经这么久没人见过 Akaro 了。来卧室的那个，并不是跟 Sai 一起离开的那个。……可我知道他就在这里。',
        "...! I didn't imagine it this time. There's someone in hallway A.": '……！{w} 这次不是错觉。A走廊里有人。',
        "...My only move was to wait. When I thought about it, I realized that being found wasn't so bad.": '……{w}我能做的只有等。仔细想想，被人发现其实也不算太糟。',
        'The Atsuki from this morning... where is he? Will I ever find him again? ...He was a future version of the Atsuki here, but how will everything lead into what happened? How will he end up at the beginning of this day?': '今天早晨的 Atsuki……他在哪里？{w} 我还能再见到他吗？……他是这里那个 Atsuki 的未来版本，可这一切究竟是怎样一步步变成后来那样的？他又怎么会在这一天刚开始时出现？',
        "...It didn't seem like anything was happening. I'd been expecting either door to open, but a few still minutes had already passed.": '……{w}似乎什么都没发生。我一直等着哪扇门被打开，可寂静的几分钟已经过去了。',
        "Hm... could it be that I have already been seen? What if I didn't know about it, but it already happened?": '嗯……{w} 会不会其实我已经被看见了？也许我并不知道，但那件事早已发生？',
        '...roya! Hey! Wher— ...you!?': '……roya！{w=0.7} 喂！{w=0.5} 你在哪—— ……你！？',
        'Wh— Atsuki?': '什——{w} Atsuki？',
        "...My hoarse voice didn't reach him. Gently, and trying not to stagger, I took a step forward.": '……我沙哑的声音没能传到他耳中。{w}我尽量不让自己踉跄，轻轻向前迈了一步。',
        "...I didn't know what to say. When his eyes pierced into mine, any words I could have prepared flew out of my mind.": '……{w}我不知道该说什么。他的目光直直刺过来，我事先想好的话全都想不起来了。',
        '...It was Erina. The look in her eyes and her way of walking had cut me off. When Atsuki turned around, he hardly reacted, so I was unsure if he already knew what had happened to her.': '……是 Erina。她的眼神和走路的姿态让我把话咽了回去。{w}Atsuki 回过头，却几乎没什么反应，我拿不准他是否已经知道她出了什么事。',
        "...Is he not? Who has the Sekimeiya Sai and I traveled with? ...If he does, I understand why he'd lie. Right now, he believes the past can't be changed.": '……{w}真的没在说谎吗？Sai 和我一起穿越时用的那个 Sekimeiya，如今在谁手上？{w}……如果在他那儿，我明白他为什么要说谎。眼下他相信过去是无法改变的。',
        "Out of nowhere, Erina took out a piece of paper from her purse and handed it to Atsuki. I saw some black letters on it, but I didn't recognize what it was. Immediately, he stashed it in his pocket.": 'Erina 冷不防从手提包里抽出一张纸，递给 Atsuki。纸上写着些黑色的字，可我认不出那是什么。{w}他立刻把它塞进了口袋。',
        "...A personal paper? I didn't think I'd seen it before. When I glanced at him, he immediately looked away, leaving me a little surprised.": '……私人纸条？我印象里从没见过。{w}我朝他瞥了一眼，他立刻把视线移开，让我有些意外。',
        "That was the biggest blow I'd been dealt in a long time. I'd grown to think I partially understood what had happened, but a few words were enough to shatter everything. What did it mean? Could it have been another prediction from the world? Had my own decision been handed to me, confirming that I would save Miiya? There was no way—that didn't make sense. If I'd changed the past, many more things would've differed as well.": '这是很久以来我受到的最重的一击。我原以为自己已经大致弄懂了发生的事，可几句话就足以把这一切击得粉碎。{w}那到底意味着什么？难道又是世界给出的某种预示？还是说，我自己的决定已经被提前摆在了我面前，等于确认我会去救 Miiya？{w}不可能——这说不通。如果我真改变了过去，该有更多事情随之不同才对。',
        "She told me her name, but she didn't look lost or anything. She knew me, too... She just suddenly ran away, and I haven't seen her again. I definitely thought I hadn't seen her before, but I honestly wasn't sure.": '她告诉了我她的名字，可她看上去一点也不茫然。她还认得我……{w}后来她突然就跑掉了，我再也没见过她。我本来一直认定自己从没见过她，可说实话，我也拿不准。',
        '...There was no way to make sense of what she was saying. It seemed the structure of the world had been warped beyond comprehension.': '……{w}她说的这些话根本无从理解。就好像这个世界的结构已经被扭曲到无法想象的地步。',
        "Sai had kept lying to Erina, claiming fifteen minutes was long enough to go hours back. However, I couldn't be entirely sure that was impossible. As she got her hand closer to her purse, the three of us stepped back. Given what we knew about the range, we were outside of it.": 'Sai 一直对 Erina 撒谎，说十五分钟就足以回到好几个小时之前。可我也不能完全确定那一定不可能。{w}Erina 把手一点点伸向手提包，我们三人齐齐后退。按我们所知的作用范围，我们已经在范围之外了。',
        'Wait, what...? The Sekimeiya disappeared?': '等等，什么……？{w} Sekimeiya不见了？',
        "Well, you get what I mean. You don't remember when you got attacked or where you came from very well, right? Of course, Erina and Isla have been here the whole time, but not you.": '总之，你明白我的意思。你不太记得自己什么时候遭到袭击、又是从哪里来的，对吧？{w}当然，Erina 和 Isla 一直在这里，可你不是。',
        "And the green light isn't there. It's... that world. The one from this morning.": '而且绿灯也没有亮。{w}这是……那个世界。今天早上的那个。',
        "Going by myself, I could find him. He was the future version of the Atsuki I'd just been with. I'd just told him I was going there, so if his future self was in that world, I knew he would be waiting.": '一个人去，我才找得到他。他是刚才那个 Atsuki 的未来之身。{w}我刚跟他说过我要去阁楼，所以只要他的未来之身在这个世界，他就一定在等我。',
        'Once it had come, I stepped inside. The "7" button wasn\'t available, but I still had the key to the attic. After getting it out of my purse, I enabled the button and pressed it to start ascending.': '电梯到了，我走进去。「7」楼的按钮无法按下，可阁楼的钥匙还在我手上。{w}我从手提包里取出钥匙，解除了按钮的锁定，按下它，电梯开始上行。',
        'And finally, it opened. The person behind it... Were they the one I wanted to see?': '终于，门开了。{w}门后的人……是我想见的人吗？',
        "There you are... You did come. I'd forgotten you had the key to the attic.": '你来了……你真的来了。{w}我都忘了，阁楼的钥匙在你手上。',
        "He nodded. That was it. I'd finally found him. We just had to stay together from that point on.": '他点了点头。{w}就是这样。我终于找到他了。从今往后，我们只要待在一起就好。',
        "What had happened after I'd traveled didn't matter anymore. As long as I stayed with Atsuki, we would be together at 21:00, which he had lived through once already.": '我穿越之后发生了什么，已经不重要了。只要和 Atsuki 待在一起，到了 {time=21}，我们就会在一起——那个时刻，他已经经历过一次。',
        "What had happened after I'd traveled didn't matter anymore. As long as I stayed with Atsuki, we would be together at 9 p.m., which he had lived through once already.": '我穿越之后发生了什么，已经不重要了。只要和 Atsuki 待在一起，到了 {time=21}，我们就会在一起——那个时刻，他已经经历过一次。',
        'What do you mean? You said the recording was real, right? What happened at 21:00? And why did both of us appear at the start of today?': '什么意思？你说过那段录音是真的，对吧？{time=21} 到底发生了什么？还有，为什么我们两个都出现在今天刚开始的时候？',
        'What do you mean? You said the recording was real, right? What happened at 9 p.m.? And why did both of us appear at the start of today?': '什么意思？你说过那段录音是真的，对吧？{time=21} 到底发生了什么？还有，为什么我们两个都出现在今天刚开始的时候？',
        '...Why did we travel to this morning? I know the answer now.': '……我们为什么会穿越到今天早上？{w}现在我知道答案了。',
        "I don't know why you think that, but I believe you went to the future. You said that you entered the tower in early December. I believe that was the 5th of January instead.": '我不知道你为什么会这么想，但我相信你去的是未来。{w}你说过，你是在 12 月初进入塔里的。我认为那其实是 1 月 5 日。',
        "It didn't... make any sense. ...Did it? The days I'd spent in my apartment. That had been in December, hadn't it?": '这根本……说不通。……对吧？{w}我在公寓里度过的那几天——那些天明明是在十二月，不是吗？',
        "I was at a loss for words. That couldn't be the truth; it didn't make sense. But... if it had happened before... Earlier, when our past selves had traveled to the attic... I'd pressed the elevator button two times, and only one of them could've caused the sound we'd heard. If we'd appeared in the future instead, that solved it. We'd immediately thought we'd traveled just a few minutes to the past because the handle in the bedroom had been reattached and our footprints were still visible in the living room, but that would've been the case a few minutes into the future too. Was that really possible, though? Wouldn't we have noticed a ton of contradictions?": '我一时说不出话来。这不可能是真的，根本说不通。{w}可是……如果以前真的发生过……{w}先前，过去的我们穿越到阁楼的时候……我按了两次电梯按钮，但只有一次可能造成了我们听到的声响。如果我们其实是出现在未来，那就说得通了。{w}我们之所以当即认定自己只回到了几分钟前，是因为卧室的门把手已经装了回去，客厅里也还留着我们的脚印；可如果是去了几分钟后的未来，这些同样成立。然而，这真的可能吗？那么多矛盾，我们怎么会毫无察觉？',
        "Every mystery has been accompanied by the key to unlock it. Shiroya went to the future. That's why the days of the week didn't match December, when the 15th was a Thursday. That's why it wasn't snowing when she stepped out of the drainage channel. That's why, as soon as she got home, she heard fireworks celebrating the new year.": '每一个谜团都伴随着解开它的钥匙。Shiroya 去的是未来。正因如此，星期几才和十二月对不上——那个月的十五日是星期四。{w}正因如此，她走出排水渠时天上没有下雪。也正因如此，她一回到家，就听见了庆祝新年的烟花声。',
        'In the living room, Shiroya thought to herself.': '{cps=80}客厅里，{w=0.4}Shiroya 独自想着心事。{nw}',
        "Everything she'd experienced... How could it have happened in January?": '{cps=80}她经历的一切……{w=0.4}怎么会发生在一月呢？{nw}',
        "It seemed impossible at first, but she soon realized it wasn't. Even if that was the case, though, there were many questions to answer.": '{cps=80}起初看来不可能，{w=0.3}但她很快明白并非如此。{w=0.7}不过，{w=0.2}即便如此，{w=0.2}仍有很多疑问需要解答。{nw}',
        '...So... what now? What will happen at {time=21}?': '{cps=80}那么……{w=0.4}接下来呢？{w=0.7}{time=21}会发生什么？{nw}',
        '{cps=80}...So...{w=0.4} what now?{w=0.7} What will happen at 21:00?{nw}': '{cps=80}那么……{w=0.4}接下来呢？{w=0.7}{time=21}会发生什么？{nw}',
        '...So... what now? What will happen at 21:00?': '{cps=80}那么……{w=0.4}接下来呢？{w=0.7}{time=21}会发生什么？{nw}',
        '{cps=80}...So...{w=0.4} what now?{w=0.7} What will happen at 9 p.m.?{nw}': '{cps=80}那么……{w=0.4}接下来呢？{w=0.7}{time=21}会发生什么？{nw}',
        '...So... what now? What will happen at 9 p.m.?': '{cps=80}那么……{w=0.4}接下来呢？{w=0.7}{time=21}会发生什么？{nw}',
        "It'll be fine. We'll be able to leave.": '{cps=80}没事的。{w=0.4}我们能出去的。{nw}',
        "Finally, Shiroya breathed a sigh of relief, but it was cut short by words she didn't expect.": '{cps=80}终于，{w=0.3}Shiroya 松了口气，{w=0.4}却被一句意料之外的话打断了。{nw}',
        "This isn't over yet, though. We have to do one more thing.": '{cps=80}不过，{w=0.2}这事还没完。{w=0.5}我们还得再做一件事。{nw}',
        'Shiroya peered at him, wondering just what he meant.': '{cps=80}Shiroya 打量着他，{w=0.4}不明白他究竟是什么意思。{nw}',
        '...We are going to save Miiya.': '……我们{w=0.6}要去救 Miiya。',
        'Puzzled, he stepped into hallway B. ...What had just happened? Out of nowhere, the Sekimeiya had disappeared.': '他满腹疑惑，走进了 B走廊。……刚才究竟发生了什么？{w} Sekimeiya 竟凭空消失了。',
        "Sai saw something else. There was no longer a green light on the security cameras. Did that mean they weren't recording? Without a doubt, he wasn't where he'd been a minute ago.": 'Sai 还注意到了另一件事。监控摄像头上的绿灯不亮了。这意味着摄像头没在录像吗？{w}毫无疑问，他已经不在刚才那个地方了。',
        "When he looked at the lobby, he was met with Shiroya's immobile body. Next to her was a puddle of blood, and her eyes showed that no life remained within them. Shiroya had been killed... By who, though? ...Sai didn't find anything important among her belongings.": '他望向大厅，映入眼帘的是 Shiroya 一动不动的身体。她身旁积着一摊血，双眼已经毫无生气。{w}Shiroya 是被杀的……可凶手是谁？……Sai 也没从她的随身物品里找到任何要紧的东西。',
        "Again, he wondered. Where was he...? The corpses he knew of had vanished, while Shiroya and Erina, who should've been in the attic, had been killed. What did the silence mean? Where was Atsuki and everyone else...? His wristwatch wouldn't help him figure any of that out, so he headed to the security room.": '他又一次问自己：这里到底是哪儿……？他所知道的那些尸体都不见了，本该待在阁楼的 Shiroya 和 Erina，反倒被人杀死。{w}这片寂静意味着什么？Atsuki 和其他人都在哪里……？光看手表也想不明白这些，于是他朝监控室走去。',
        "Had Katei locked it? That seemed strange. Sai wanted to know the time. The bodies vanishing indicated that he was in the past, but the truth couldn't have been so simple. The future, perhaps? Had the earlier crimes been covered up? ...Sai wasn't sure what to think.": '是 Katei 锁的吗？这未免奇怪。{w}Sai 想知道现在几点。尸体消失，说明他回到了过去，可真相不可能这么简单。{w}也许是未来？先前那些命案都被掩盖了？……Sai 想不明白。',
        'Then, he looked at the elevator, frowning in consternation. The button was gone... Nonetheless, when he tried to open the door, it budged.': '随后，他望向电梯，困惑地皱起眉。按钮不见了……{w}可他试着开门，门却动了。',
        "Sai noticed that one of the bed sheets was gone. When Atsuki heard him, his head immediately turned and he saw him approaching through his bleary vision. Then, Atsuki's fist flew. If Sai hadn't reacted fast enough, the blow would've broken his jaw.": 'Sai 注意到床上少了一条被单。Atsuki 听见他的声音，猛地转过头，透过模糊的泪眼看见他走近。{w}紧接着，Atsuki 的拳头挥了过来。若不是 Sai 反应够快，这一拳会打断他的下巴。',
        "Before he could process it, Atsuki struck again. When Sai saw Atsuki's fist had barely missed its full impact, he realized it could've easily just killed him. ...After all, from Atsuki's perspective, Sai had to be the murderer.": '他还没反应过来，Atsuki 又打了一拳。Sai 看出这一拳并未完全打实，否则轻易就能要了他的命。{w}……毕竟在 Atsuki 眼里，凶手只能是 Sai。',
        "Everyone had stayed in a crystal room, and Sai had been the first to leave. Only Naomi should've been outside, but she had been one of the victims. Then, Erina had left, and she had been killed as well. Lastly, after Shiroya's departure, she'd instantly been met with the same fate. It was only Sai who could've done that; the one still alive, who had willingly not returned.": '所有人都待在各自的水晶展室里，而 Sai 是第一个出去的。外面本该只有 Naomi 一人，她却成了死者之一。{w}接着 Erina 也出去了，同样被杀。最后，Shiroya 一出去，立刻遭遇了相同的命运。{w}能做到这些的只有 Sai——只有他还活着，并且有意没有回去。',
        "He felt a chill up his spine. He couldn't die there, not after Shiroya's death, but he wasn't a match against Sai's knife. Before he could swing again, Atsuki ran out of the room.": '后背窜起一阵寒意。Shiroya 已经死了，他绝不能也死在这里——可他敌不过 Sai 手里的刀。{w} 没等对方再次挥刀，Atsuki 便逃出了房间。',
        "Sai wouldn't let him go—not after he'd tried to kill him out of nowhere. On top of that, he was aware of a few things. Nobody else was in the tower. Murders had occurred. The cameras didn't seem to be working. He had a knife. ...He had been handed the perfect circumstances to finally know what killing a person was like.": '刚才对方毫无征兆地对他痛下杀手，Sai 怎么可能放他走。更何况，他清楚几件事。{w} 塔里没有其他人。已经出了命案。摄像头似乎没在工作。而他手里有刀。{w} ……一切都为他备好了，只等他亲手弄清楚杀人是什么滋味。',
        "When he'd cut his shirt, Sai had discerned fear within Atsuki's eyes. He had run away, but there weren't many places where he could hide. Sai had enjoyed Atsuki's presence in the tower, and he was poised to enjoy it even more. Thanks to the knife he had, he could hunt him down.": '刚才划破 Atsuki 衬衫时，Sai 从他眼里看出了恐惧。Atsuki 虽然跑了，能藏身的地方却不多。{w} 塔里有 Atsuki 作伴，Sai 原本就乐在其中，如今更是兴味盎然。有这把刀在手，他大可以像追捕猎物一样把他找出来。',
        "And at the same time, he felt enraged. Atsuki had almost killed him; he'd almost suffered a sudden, clueless, and pathetic death. His confusion toward the world was gone. In the blink of an eye, Sai's thoughts had shifted drastically.": '与此同时，他也怒不可遏。Atsuki 差点杀了他；他险些就这样不明不白地突然送命，死得既荒唐又窝囊。{w} 他原本对这个世界的困惑已经一扫而空。眨眼之间，Sai 的想法已经彻底转向。',
        "He began to search for him, aware that Atsuki could attack first. In the living room, he saw footprints running out, yet he cautiously looked through the whole floor to confirm Atsuki wasn't still there.": '他开始搜寻 Atsuki，心里清楚对方可能先一步动手。{w} 客厅里有一串向外跑去的脚印，但他仍旧谨慎地把整层楼查了一遍，确认 Atsuki 没有藏在这里。',
        'Atsuki! I bet you want to know what happened to Shiroya. Open, you stupid moron!': 'Atsuki！{w} 你八成想知道 Shiroya 出了什么事吧。快开门，你这个白痴！',
        "...Oh, I see. You're not answering... because you're already dead.": '……哦，我明白了。{w} 你不回答……{w} 是因为你已经死了。',
        "Sai grinned. In the storeroom on the crystal floor, he had found both Sekimeiya. He'd had a reason to hide one while leaving the other there, but what mattered was that he had access to both. That bathroom was where Atsuki had hidden. If Sai went to the past, he could wait for him inside. Hence, on the other side of the door, Atsuki must've already been dead, and a future version of Sai must've been waiting for his past self to leave.": 'Sai 咧嘴一笑。在水晶层的储藏室里，他找到了两个 Sekimeiya。{w} 他藏起一个、把另一个留在原处，是有原因的；但真正重要的是，两个 Sekimeiya 他都能拿到。{w} Atsuki 就藏在那个浴室里。只要 Sai 回到过去，就能先一步进去等他。所以，门后的 Atsuki 肯定已经死了，而未来的 Sai 一定正等着过去的 Sai 离开。',
        "How long had it been...? Perhaps two hours. No matter the time, for Atsuki, it had felt like a still instant; Atsuki's mind had been consumed by the persistent image of Shiroya's corpse.": '到底过了多久……？也许两个小时。{w} 但不管是多久，在 Atsuki 的感受里都只像一瞬；Shiroya 的尸体一直在脑海中挥之不去。',
        "...Why had Sai not come back? Had he killed everyone else...? Atsuki was incapable of shedding more tears. He'd been in the tower almost the entire day, and he didn't know if the exit would ever unlock.": '……Sai 为什么还没回来？他是不是把其他人都杀了……？{w} Atsuki 已经流不出眼泪了。他在这座塔里待了将近一整天，也不知道出口究竟还会不会解锁。',
        "He stepped back to the wall that had closed. It didn't seem to have a handle either, and he couldn't get it to open. For an instant, Atsuki thought he'd been trapped, but he soon felt the area that allowed him to open the hidden wall.": '他退回到那面已经合上的墙前。它似乎也没有把手，他怎么也打不开。{w} 有那么一瞬，Atsuki 以为自己被困住了，但很快摸到了能打开这面暗墙的地方。',
        "In the hallway, Atsuki stared at the stairs in fright. What was happening to him? Erina had just been there, hadn't she? Yet she no longer was, and the sea of blood there had been reduced to a single droplet.": '走廊里，Atsuki 惊恐地盯着楼梯。{w} 他到底怎么了？Erina 刚才明明还在那里，不是吗？可她现在不见了，那片血海也只剩下一滴血。',
        'Carefully, he reached out to it with his left hand. Again, as soon as he contacted it, the gemstone disappeared and he felt a painful burn.': '他小心翼翼地伸出左手，探向它。{w} 可刚一碰到，宝石又消失不见，随即一阵灼痛袭来。',
        "He pressed it softly, causing the burn on his fingertip to prickle painfully. Long seconds later, the button's outline flashed orange.": '他轻轻按下按钮，指尖的烫伤处立刻一阵刺痛。{w} 过了好几秒，按钮的轮廓才闪起橙光。',
        'At {time=21:04}, the shutter opened. A group of policemen had been in front of it, awaiting that time. As soon as the glass came into view, they saw the figure of a young girl lying next to a puddle of blood.': '{time=21:04}，卷帘门升了起来。{w} 一队警察早已守在门外，等的就是这一刻。玻璃一露出来，他们便看见一个少女倒在血泊旁。',
        'At 21:04, the shutter opened.{w} A group of policemen had been in front of it, awaiting that time. As soon as the glass came into view, they saw the figure of a young girl lying next to a puddle of blood.': '{time=21:04}，卷帘门升了起来。{w} 一队警察早已守在门外，等的就是这一刻。玻璃一露出来，他们便看见一个少女倒在血泊旁。',
        'At 21:04, the shutter opened. A group of policemen had been in front of it, awaiting that time. As soon as the glass came into view, they saw the figure of a young girl lying next to a puddle of blood.': '{time=21:04}，卷帘门升了起来。{w} 一队警察早已守在门外，等的就是这一刻。玻璃一露出来，他们便看见一个少女倒在血泊旁。',
        'At 9:04 p.m., the shutter opened.{w} A group of policemen had been in front of it, awaiting that time. As soon as the glass came into view, they saw the figure of a young girl lying next to a puddle of blood.': '{time=21:04}，卷帘门升了起来。{w} 一队警察早已守在门外，等的就是这一刻。玻璃一露出来，他们便看见一个少女倒在血泊旁。',
        'At 9:04 p.m., the shutter opened. A group of policemen had been in front of it, awaiting that time. As soon as the glass came into view, they saw the figure of a young girl lying next to a puddle of blood.': '{time=21:04}，卷帘门升了起来。{w} 一队警察早已守在门外，等的就是这一刻。玻璃一露出来，他们便看见一个少女倒在血泊旁。',
        "When they were prepared, the team raided Ashiya Tower. The girl in the lobby was young and had blue hair. She didn't have an open wound, so the blood next to her was strange.": '准备妥当后，队伍冲进了芦屋塔。{w} 大厅里的少女年纪尚轻，一头蓝发。她身上没有外伤，身旁那摊血便显得蹊跷。',
        'What exactly had happened during the twelve hours when the tower had been sealed off? The officers were speechless as they stared at the corpses. However, that was nothing compared to what awaited in hallway B.': '塔被封锁的这十二个小时里，究竟发生了什么？警官们盯着那些尸体，说不出话来。{w} 然而，和 B走廊里等着他们的景象相比，这根本不算什么。',
        "Dimly lit, its entire floor was red. It took a moment for the first officer to realize that it was blood, not lighting. Then, when he saw its source, the wind was knocked out of him. He froze, knowing that would be the most gruesome image he'd ever see—the sad remains of what had once been a human being.": '走廊光线昏暗，整片地面却是红的。走在前头的警官愣了一瞬，才明白那是血，不是灯光。{w} 等他看清血的源头，胸口猛地一窒，气都提不上来。{w} 他僵在原地，知道那会是他这辈子见过最惨烈的画面——曾经活生生的一个人，如今只剩凄惨的残骸。',
        "In the middle of the hallway, by the door of a crystal room in the right wall, was the origin of the blood. It wasn't a body. It was only half of one.": '血迹的源头在走廊中央——右侧墙上一间水晶展室的门口。{w} 那不是一具完整的尸体，只有半具。',
        "While the citizens learned the tragic events that had transpired, the bodies were identified. The girl in the lobby was Shiroya Mirana. The woman beside the stairs was Erina Majutsu. And the body split in two was Sai Yomiya's.": '就在市民们得知这场惨剧的同时，尸体也完成了身份确认。{w} 大厅里的少女是 Shiroya Mirana。{w} 楼梯旁的女性是 Erina Majutsu。{w} 而那具被劈成两半的尸体，是 Sai Yomiya。',
        'When he pulled his head up through it, he saw a face before his eyes. It was that of a young, unconscious boy. Blood issued from his mouth in a thin stream.': '他把头探进去，一张脸便出现在眼前。{w} 那是个昏迷的少年。血从他嘴里细细地流出来。',
        "Atsuki Hakutoki. That was the name of the person who'd been found above the elevator. Hours after his rescue, he regained consciousness. At first, he sounded devastated due to the death of his close friend. However, as he continued to be questioned, his answers only grew stranger.": '在电梯上方被发现的人名叫 Atsuki Hakutoki。{w} 获救数小时后，他恢复了意识。起初，他因挚友的死而显得悲痛欲绝。然而随着问话继续，他的回答却越来越离奇。',
        "He didn't have a valid explanation for any of the deaths. No clues at the crime scenes pointed to their truth, and no video footage had been recorded. Quickly, the possibility that Atsuki was lying was presented—only he could've committed those murders. He must've been lying: none of what he'd said could be the truth. However, nobody could be completely sure. Sai's death... It hadn't been natural. How would Atsuki have killed him? How would anyone have killed him like that? And how would Atsuki have ended up unconscious above the elevator?": '对于任何一桩死亡，他都给不出合理的解释。现场没有任何线索能印证他的说法，也没有录下任何影像。很快，有人提出了 Atsuki 在说谎的可能——那些命案只可能是他做的。{w} 他一定在撒谎：他说的话不可能有半句是真的。然而，谁也无法完全确定。Sai 的死……绝非寻常。{w} Atsuki 怎么可能杀得了他？又有谁能用那种方式杀他？而 Atsuki 又怎么会昏迷在电梯上方？',
        "And, admittedly, there was a point of truth to Atsuki's words: the blood in the lobby. Next to Shiroya's body, there'd been a puddle of blood, which was confirmed not to match with any of the bodies present. Could it really have been... Naomi's? The corpse Atsuki swore had disappeared...?": '而且，不得不承认，Atsuki 的话里有一点是真的：大厅里的血。{w} Shiroya 的尸体旁有一摊血，经确认，并不属于在场的任何一具尸体。{w} 那真的会是……Naomi 的血吗？那具 Atsuki 坚称已经消失的尸体……？',
        'Through the glass of a window, the cloudy sky could be seen. However, no one was there to see it.': '透过窗玻璃，能望见阴云密布的天空。{w} 然而，已经没有人站在那里看它了。',
        'Around the country, some people had the opportunity to witness the disappearance of countless citizens. Speechless, they walked to where everyone had been... In the blink of an eye, the streets had become desolate, and even some cars had disappeared.': '在全国各地，有些人亲眼看见了无数市民的消失。{w} 他们说不出话，走向众人原本所在的地方……眨眼之间，街道已变得空荡荒凉，连一些汽车也不见了。',
        'An entrance to a vast field of grass, enclosed by the trees that hid it from view. However, what truly stood out was farther ahead.': '那是一片开阔草地的入口，四周的树木将它遮得严严实实。{w}然而，真正惹眼的还在更远处。',
        "Speechless, he was drawn to it. The grass was tall, and it had almost been concealed by the snow. Slowly making his way inward, Gan didn't take his eyes off the cabin.": '他说不出话，脚步却不由自主地朝那里挪去。{w}草长得很高，几乎被雪盖住。Gan 缓缓向里走，目光始终没有离开那座木屋。',
        'The door was open, so he took a look inside. A few spiders had set up shop there. Most of them had died out during the winter, but their webs still decorated the room.': '门开着，他便探头往里看。{w}几只蜘蛛在此安了家。它们大多没能熬过冬天，蛛网却仍装点着屋子。',
        'He stepped into his shop, Musashi Gemstones. He left his discovery on a stand and hurried to turn on the heater. Then, he grabbed the phone and dialed a number he had memorized.': '他走进自己的店——武藏宝石。{w}他把发现的东西搁在展台上，赶紧去打开取暖器，随后抓起电话，拨了一个记熟的号码。',
        "...Is that so? If you're not exaggerating, you might be in luck.": '……是吗？{w}要是你没夸大其词，说不定你走运了。',
        "Thank you! I'll be waiting. Good night.": '谢谢！我等你。{w}晚安。',
        "The call cut off. Gan pumped his fist in relief. It had been a while since he'd struck a deal with Ashiya.": '电话挂断了。{w}Gan 松了口气，挥了挥拳头。他已经很久没和芦屋谈成一笔生意了。',
        "A while later, he raised his head. He had noticed something. A smell he hadn't perceived before was in his shop.": '过了一会儿，他抬起头，察觉到了异样。{w}店里弥漫着一股先前没有的气味。',
        '...It was hot. Very hot. Why? It had been cold before. Why had its temperature changed?': '……{w}很烫。烫得厉害。{w}怎么会？之前明明还是凉的。温度为什么会变？',
        "Concerned, he grabbed it. He examined it closely, but there was no explanation for the temperature change. What could've caused that? And most importantly, would it ward Ashiya off from buying it?": '他心里不安，把宝石拿了起来。{w}他仔细端详，却找不出温度变化的原因。究竟是什么让它变热的？更要紧的是，芦屋会不会因此不肯买下它？',
        'And when it had, he touched the gemstone one more time. All warmth was long gone, and the smell had also faded.': '等温度稳住了，他又碰了一次那颗宝石。{w}温热早已散尽，那股气味也淡了。',
        'Lei silently nodded. Gan took a deep breath. If Ashiya did what he had instructed, there would be no problem.': 'Lei 默默点了点头。{w}Gan 深吸一口气。只要芦屋照他说的做，就不会出问题。',
        "We'll deal with the paperwork, then. You know the usual. We'll be here this Wednesday. Is {time=21} a good time? Sorry if it's too late, we're pretty overloaded.": '那手续就由我们来办。老规矩，你知道的。{w}我们这周三过来。{time=21}方便吗？要是太晚了很抱歉，我们实在忙不过来。',
        "We'll deal with the paperwork, then. You know the usual.{w} We'll be here this Wednesday. Is 21:00 a good time? Sorry if it's too late, we're pretty overloaded.": '那手续就由我们来办。老规矩，你知道的。{w}我们这周三过来。{time=21}方便吗？要是太晚了很抱歉，我们实在忙不过来。',
        "We'll deal with the paperwork, then. You know the usual. We'll be here this Wednesday. Is 21:00 a good time? Sorry if it's too late, we're pretty overloaded.": '那手续就由我们来办。老规矩，你知道的。{w}我们这周三过来。{time=21}方便吗？要是太晚了很抱歉，我们实在忙不过来。',
        "We'll deal with the paperwork, then. You know the usual.{w} We'll be here this Wednesday. Is 9 p.m. a good time? Sorry if it's too late, we're pretty overloaded.": '那手续就由我们来办。老规矩，你知道的。{w}我们这周三过来。{time=21}方便吗？要是太晚了很抱歉，我们实在忙不过来。',
        "We'll deal with the paperwork, then. You know the usual. We'll be here this Wednesday. Is 9 p.m. a good time? Sorry if it's too late, we're pretty overloaded.": '那手续就由我们来办。老规矩，你知道的。{w}我们这周三过来。{time=21}方便吗？要是太晚了很抱歉，我们实在忙不过来。',
        "The gemstone he'd found... Why had it been there? Snow had fallen days prior, so why had none been on it? Had someone dropped it there? Someone who knew about that place?": '他找到的那颗宝石……为什么会出现在那里？几天前下过雪，它上面为什么一点雪也没沾？{w}是有人把它掉在那里的吗？一个知道那个地方的人？',
        "You know what? This might be great. You remember what I told you, don't you? We're keeping the details of the Sekimeiya a secret, and this could be something perfect to reveal on the day of the event. We'll buy both of them.": '你知道吗？这也许是件大好事。{w}你还记得我跟你说过的吧？{w}Sekimeiya 的细节我们一直保密，而这件事正好可以在活动当天公布。我们两颗都要了。',
        'Nobody truly knew the family who lived in it, but the numerous nasty rumors about them were known by all. For a long time, they were believed to be secretly authoritarian. However, crimes had recently started to be linked back to them.': '住在里面的是怎样一家人，没人真正了解，但关于他们的种种恶毒传言却无人不知。{w}长久以来，人们都认为他们暗地里独断专横。可近来，开始有案件被追查到他们头上。',
        "He'd learned the girl's name: Anora. It made no difference. Regardless of her name, she was locked in the same room as always. Soon, he heard plaintive cries coming from above.": '他知道了那名少女的名字：Anora。这并没有什么不同。不管她叫什么，都还是像往常一样被锁在那个房间里。{w} 不久，楼上传来凄楚的哭喊声。',
        "He didn't like it. He knew that girl was suffering, and he didn't want that. However, he wouldn't talk his brother out of it, and he didn't want to annoy him. Furthermore, the room upstairs was always locked, and he couldn't bring himself to let anybody know.": '他不喜欢这样。他知道那个女孩正在受苦，他并不想看到这种事。{w} 可他不会去劝哥哥收手，也不想惹他心烦。再说，楼上的房间总是锁着，他实在没法鼓起勇气告诉别人。',
        "It was a key. When his brother had gone up loaded with what he'd bought, he'd left his keys in the keyhole.": '是一把钥匙。{w} 哥哥抱着一堆买回来的东西上楼时，把钥匙忘在了锁孔里。',
        "The phone was there. Quietly, he dialed the police's number. When they picked up, he anonymously revealed Anora's whereabouts, claiming to have heard yells coming from the house. Then, before his brother could hear him, he slipped back to his sofa.": '电话就在那里。他悄悄拨了报警电话。{w} 接通后，他匿名说出了Anora的下落，只说自己听见那栋房子里传出喊叫声。随后，趁哥哥还没察觉，他又溜回了沙发上。',
        "The rumors about the mansion were known by the whole town. The first time that someone had disappeared, the police had quickly shown up. Yet, thanks to that well-hidden exit, Kyuuka's brother had avoided being caught.": '这栋宅子的传闻，全镇无人不知。第一次有人失踪时，警察很快就赶来了。{w} 可凭着那处藏得极深的出口，Kyuuka的哥哥躲过了抓捕。',
        "...I called the police. They're on their way right now.": '……{w}我报警了。他们正在赶来的路上。',
        'He had believed that even if she was just like everyone else, not worth caring about, it would be a good thing to put a stop to what his brother was doing to people. And it could have ended up costing him. All Kyuuka had accomplished was getting him killed and putting himself in a dangerous position.': '他原以为，哪怕她和旁人没什么两样、不值得在意，能阻止哥哥再害人，总归是件好事。可这念头本可能让他自己付出性命。{w}到头来，Kyuuka 做到的，不过是害得哥哥丢了命，也把自己推入了险境。',
        'That day, he came back home and realized that his parents were there. As usual, he had no idea what they would say.': '那天他回到家，才发现父母也在。{w}和往常一样，他完全猜不到他们会说些什么。',
        'The lights turned on in the tower. The lobby door opened, and a man stepped into the hallway.': '塔内亮起了灯。{w}大厅的门打开，一名男子走进走廊。',
        "Over the phone, he'd learned Xyn had attacked again. It had happened on the 24th, and it had started during his own shift. On that Thursday, there had been an event in the tower where many gemstones had been replaced. The next night, they had all been taken.": '他在电话里得知，Xyn 又动手了。事情发生在 24 号，而且一开始就发生在他当班期间。{w}那个星期四，塔里办过一场活动，许多宝石被替换。第二天夜里，它们全被劫走了。',
        "Long ago, his job had started to exclusively revolve around Xyn. Ashiya had been outsmarted repeatedly, and every countermeasure they designed was continually bypassed. It was Katei's job to put an end to those incidents. However, his thoughts on Ashiya were far from positive. He'd worked in the tower for years, and he knew information that eluded public knowledge.": '很久以前，他的工作就开始只围着 Xyn 打转。芦屋一次次被人算计，他们设计的每一项对策也一次次被绕开。{w}Katei 的职责就是制止这类事件。但他对芦屋的评价绝谈不上正面。他在塔里工作多年，知道许多外界无从得知的内情。',
        "The computer's webcam, tucked behind one of the monitors. It spent most of the time turned off, but that time, it had been recording the hallway through the open door. Katei had pressed a button behind the camera to begin the recording, and it wasn't a new device in the tower. There was no way Xyn had learned of his plan.": '那是电脑的摄像头，藏在其中一台显示器后面。它平时大多关着，可那一次，它正透过敞开的门，录下走廊里的情形。{w} Katei 按下了摄像头背后的按钮开始录像，而这并不是塔里新添的设备。Xyn 不可能得知他的计划。',
        'The time was before {time=9.} When Katei saw his face disappearing from the video, he let go of the mouse. Then, he saw all he needed to see. Through hallway A, someone he knew passed by. They were pushing a cleaning cart.': '时间停在 {time=9.} 之前。看到自己的脸从画面中消失，Katei 松开了鼠标。{w} 随后，该看的他都看到了。{w} 一个他认识的人推着清洁推车，从 A走廊经过。',
        'The time was before 9:00. When Katei saw his face disappearing from the video, he let go of the mouse.{w} Then, he saw all he needed to see.{w} Through hallway A, someone he knew passed by. They were pushing a cleaning cart.': '时间停在 {time=9.} 之前。看到自己的脸从画面中消失，Katei 松开了鼠标。{w} 随后，该看的他都看到了。{w} 一个他认识的人推着清洁推车，从 A走廊经过。',
        'The time was before 9:00. When Katei saw his face disappearing from the video, he let go of the mouse. Then, he saw all he needed to see. Through hallway A, someone he knew passed by. They were pushing a cleaning cart.': '时间停在 {time=9.} 之前。看到自己的脸从画面中消失，Katei 松开了鼠标。{w} 随后，该看的他都看到了。{w} 一个他认识的人推着清洁推车，从 A走廊经过。',
        'The time was before 9 a.m. When Katei saw his face disappearing from the video, he let go of the mouse.{w} Then, he saw all he needed to see.{w} Through hallway A, someone he knew passed by. They were pushing a cleaning cart.': '时间停在 {time=9.} 之前。看到自己的脸从画面中消失，Katei 松开了鼠标。{w} 随后，该看的他都看到了。{w} 一个他认识的人推着清洁推车，从 A走廊经过。',
        'The time was before 9 a.m. When Katei saw his face disappearing from the video, he let go of the mouse. Then, he saw all he needed to see. Through hallway A, someone he knew passed by. They were pushing a cleaning cart.': '时间停在 {time=9.} 之前。看到自己的脸从画面中消失，Katei 松开了鼠标。{w} 随后，该看的他都看到了。{w} 一个他认识的人推着清洁推车，从 A走廊经过。',
        'That was what Xyn had wanted to hide. Finally, he knew the identity of the infiltrator. Ido, the janitor.': 'Xyn 想遮掩的就是这个。他终于知道了潜入者的身份。{w} 清洁工 Ido。',
        "But that was too dangerous. Xyn seemed to know everything that happened in that place. What if they exposed Katei as being responsible? Would they dislike being impersonated? He was worried they would threaten him too. And even if none of that happened, Katei didn't know what he'd do with those gems.": '但那太危险了。那地方发生的任何事，Xyn 似乎都了如指掌。万一他们揭穿这件事是 Katei 干的呢？他们会介意有人冒充自己吗？他也担心自己会遭到他们的威胁。{w} 就算这些都没发生，Katei 也不知道自己拿到那些宝石后能怎么办。',
        "After everything, Katei didn't think it was fair that he had to keep working there; he couldn't bear the thought of staying in that place for much longer. His parents had died, and he wouldn't be able to support himself for too long if he left his job. ...It wasn't fair. After Xyn's first attack, his mind had produced various scenarios that gave him what he wanted.": '事到如今，Katei 觉得继续留在那里工作，对他并不公平；一想到还要在那地方待很久，他就无法忍受。父母已经去世，他若辞了工作，也撑不了多久。……这不公平。{w} Xyn 第一次袭击之后，他脑中就冒出过种种设想，每一种都能让他得偿所愿。',
        "When the morning came, Katei had slept very little. He'd wanted to find a Xyn member for so long, and he was confident he finally had. Months ago, he'd come up with a tempting plan. However, it was fairly large scale, so he'd been very hesitant to set it into motion.": '天亮时，Katei 几乎没怎么睡。他找 Xyn 成员已经很久了，如今终于确信自己找到了一个。{w} 几个月前，他想出一个诱人的计划。可那计划规模不小，他一直迟迟不敢动手。',
        "No. Access to our computer can't be all they have. If we change it, they'll immediately know they lost that information, which could be bad. I would also not be able to protect the new computer at all times. I have an idea. If I develop the mechanism behind a new alarm at home, it's possible they won't be able to bypass it. I think this is what we should do so that they don't think we're suspicious of anything involving our computer setup. Once I set up the software for this at home, I'll bring it to the tower's computer. If I do it well, it's unlikely they'll notice it.": '不行。他们不可能只靠入侵我们的电脑。要是把电脑换掉，他们立刻就会知道自己失去了那条情报渠道，那可能会坏事；而且我也没法时时刻刻守着新电脑。{w} 我有个主意。要是我在家先把新警报的装置做出来，他们说不定就绕不过去了。{w} 我觉得就该这么做，这样他们也不会想到我们对电脑相关的布置起了疑心。{w} 等我在家把配套软件准备好，再装到塔里的电脑上。只要做得够稳妥，他们不太可能发现。',
        "Me too, but we have to be smart. If this works, we have to catch them. We can't screw this up. If they really activate the alarm, they might still have a method of escape. We have to make sure that won't be possible.": '我也这么想，但必须做得巧妙。若计划奏效，我们就一定要抓住他们。{w} 绝不能搞砸。就算他们真的触发了警报，也还可能有逃跑的办法。我们得确保他们无路可逃。',
        "I can build it so that when the alarm is activated, any exits will close. As soon as they open a cabinet, they will be stuck in the tower. I have thought a lot about this. They have attacked during times I was in the security room, so we'll make sure one of us is always there. If the mechanism also locks that door, we will trap the attacker.": '我可以把它做成这样：警报一触发，所有出口都会关闭。他们只要打开展示柜，就会被困在塔里。{w} 这件事我想了很久。他们之前几次动手时，我都待在监控室，所以我们得保证总有一人守在那里。如果机关也能把那扇门锁上，就能把袭击者困住。',
        "That's what I can't handle. If I use the old system, I can have the mechanism ready for tomorrow. The installation would have to be done during the night, though, when no one else is here. It will be independent of the computer, so Xyn shouldn't learn about it. I believe it's possible they're receiving the camera's feed, but the lobby isn't recorded, so they won't see it.": '难就难在这里。若沿用旧系统，我明天就能把机关准备好。不过安装只能安排在夜里、楼里没别人的时候。{w} 它会独立于电脑，Xyn 应该不会知道。他们可能收得到摄像头的画面，但大厅没有录像，所以他们看不到。',
        "...You're right—that would be seen. I wouldn't like to disable the camera system because they could learn something is being done under their noses. Nothing happens on the higher floors during the night. I can modify the system from home as well to disable those cameras and loop a still image of the floors, then quickly install the modification on the tower's computer. I doubt Xyn will look at that footage, but if they do, they shouldn't notice the cameras were stopped.": '……你说得对，关窗会被看见。我不想关掉摄像系统，那样他们可能会察觉有人就在他们眼皮底下动手脚。{w} 夜里楼上不会有什么事。我也可以在家里改系统，关掉那些摄像头，让楼层的静止画面循环播放，然后尽快把改动装到塔里的电脑上。Xyn 未必会去看那段录像，就算看了，应该也看不出摄像头已经停了。',
        "We can draw them to a specific cabinet. Do you remember when we obtained the Nomdaid? It was targeted by Xyn immediately. If we procure something of that caliber, Xyn won't be able to resist a repeat. That will be the cabinet we'll need to alter, and since it won't be one currently displayed, we can modify it before they know it exists.": '我们可以把他们引到某个特定的展示柜。还记得我们拿到诺姆达伊德的时候吗？Xyn 立刻就盯上了它。{w} 若再弄到一件那种级别的东西，Xyn 一定忍不住故技重施。要改的就是那个展示柜；既然它现在还不会展出，我们就能在他们知道它存在之前先动手改好。',
        "Perfect. We should hurry up before they attack again. If I'm not mistaken, the event for the 15th of next month was hindered. It was going to be a guided tour to cover the last wave of gems, but that can't be done anymore.": '很好。得赶在他们下次动手之前抓紧时间。{w}如果我没记错，下个月15号的活动已经出了状况。原定要办一场导览，介绍最后一批宝石，现在办不成了。',
        "Katei nodded slowly. That was what he'd needed the most. The 15th was a Thursday, and also the middle point of the month. That meant that it was the day his work shift would change. In the first half of the month, Katei worked during the night, and in the second half, he worked during the morning. Up until the 15th, he'd be in the tower all night, ready for Xyn's attack. However, he'd also learned Xyn made daylight moves. So, if the attack didn't happen before the 15th, Katei would be present during the event.": 'Katei缓缓点头。这正是他最需要的。{w}15号是周四，也正好是月中，也就是说，那天他的班次会调换。上半月Katei值夜班，下半月值早班。{w}15号之前，他整夜都会守在塔里，等着Xyn来袭。不过他也已经知道，Xyn会在白天动手。所以，如果袭击没在15号前发生，Katei也会在活动当天在场。',
        "All right, we'll talk about it further. I will let Cou know about this when he leaves, and I'll speak to Wis. Is that fine?": '好，我们再详谈。{w}Cou走的时候我会把这件事告诉他，也会跟Wis说一声。这样可以吗？',
        "Katei nodded after a pause. Cou and Wis were the first people he'd personally investigated, as they shared his job. He couldn't be completely certain, but he really didn't think they were part of Xyn. Katei's shift was about to start, so he bowed and stepped into the tower. As he walked to the security room, he sighed, relieved Lei hadn't put more pressure on him. That would've prevented what he had in mind. It was something only he could do, and it was thanks to a key that had once saved him.": 'Katei停顿了一下，才点了点头。Cou和Wis跟他做着同样的工作，是他最先亲自调查的两个人。他无法完全确定，但他实在不觉得他们是Xyn的人。{w}Katei的值班时间快到了，他鞠了一躬，走进塔里。走向监控室时，他松了口气——幸好Lei没有进一步向他施压。{w}否则他心里盘算的事就行不通了。那件事只有他能做到，靠的是一把曾经救过他的钥匙。',
        "Suddenly, an alarm blared. Immediately, he knew they were in the building. But he didn't understand how that could be. Through the monitors, he couldn't see anyone anywhere.": '忽然，警报大作。他立刻明白，他们已经进楼了。{w}可他不懂这怎么可能。他把监控画面全看了一遍，哪里都不见人影。',
        "Now you understand your position. When the alarm played, Ashiya were notified. They will be here in less than ten minutes. Before that, there's something I want to tell you.": '现在你明白自己的处境了。{w}警报响起时，芦屋那边已经收到通知。不出十分钟他们就会赶到。{w}在那之前，我有件事要告诉你。',
        "It is not possible for me to unlock the exit. For that, Ashiya's input is needed. However, I know of a secret way out.": '出口不是我一个人能解锁的，那需要芦屋那边介入。{w}不过，我知道一条秘密的出路。',
        "In this building, there's a hidden door. I have also hidden the key you'll need to unlock it somewhere here. If you don't waste time, you can leave before Ashiya comes. This alarm has never been activated before. I will tell them that a malfunction set it off. If nobody's found when the building is unlocked, they will believe my word. If you want that, there are two conditions you must agree on. You have stolen from us countless times—it is undeniable that Xyn must be a wealthy group. For your liberty, you will provide me with 50 million yen. I believe that is a fair sum. Secondly, you must reveal your identity in front of the cameras. I know you, Xyn. I know a lot more than you think. Ido is the mole; I know where you gather, and I've investigated many of you. Just like I know you, you know me. For that reason, if anything were to happen to me, this recording and all the information I have will be immediately exposed. Do you agree to these conditions?": '这栋楼里有一扇暗门。开这扇门要用的钥匙，我也藏在了这里的某处。{w}只要你抓紧时间，就能在芦屋赶到之前离开。{w}这道警报以前从未响过。我会告诉他们，是设备故障触发了它。解锁之后若没找到人，他们会信我的话。{w}如果你想这样，就得答应我两个条件。{w}你们从我们这里偷过无数次东西——不可否认，Xyn必定是个财力雄厚的组织。为了你的自由，给我五千万日元。我认为这个数目很公道。{w}第二，你必须在镜头前露脸。{w}我了解你，Xyn。我掌握的比你想象的多得多。{w}Ido是内鬼；我知道你们在哪儿聚集，也调查过你们中的不少人。{w}就像我了解你一样，你也了解我。正因如此，若我出了什么事，这段录音和我手上的所有情报都会立刻公开。{w}这些条件，你答应吗？',
        'The loud voice faded with static. Before the silence could grow uncomfortable, the man nodded. Then, he slowly took off his mask.': '洪亮的声音在杂音中渐渐消失。还没等沉默变得尴尬，男人就点了点头。{w}然后，他缓缓摘下面罩。',
        'B-Brother?': '哥……{w=0.2}哥？',
        'All staff members were often checked despite their positions, and they had to leave their phones behind before beginning their work. That was the reason Katei had set an alarm so early.': '无论职位高低，员工都常被抽查，上班前还必须把手机留在外面。{w}正因如此，Katei才把闹钟定得那么早。',
        'Once hours had passed, he left the security room and walked down the hallway. He entered the storeroom, leaving it shortly after.': '几个小时过去，他离开监控室，沿着走廊走去。{w}他进了储藏室，没多久又出来了。',
        'He had seen Ido cleaning those hallways countless times. He knew Ido was given multiple keys, which he often had at the front of the cleaning cart. Katei waited for Ido to exit the building. Snow had just stopped falling, and Ashiya always wanted to keep the plaza outside the tower free of any buildup.': '他无数次见过Ido打扫那几条走廊。他知道Ido手上有好几把钥匙，平时总放在清洁车的前头。{w}Katei等到Ido离开大楼。雪刚停，而芦屋一向要求塔外的广场保持整洁，不留积雪。',
        "The next day, he listened to what had been recorded. The waveform highlighted the noisy moments, but after minutes of perusing, he realized nothing of importance was there. After Ido's job had ended, he'd walked home and hadn't left again until the next morning.": '第二天，他听了录下的内容。波形图上标出了几处嘈杂的片段，可他仔细查看了几分钟，终于确认其中没有任何要紧的东西。{w} Ido 下班后便走回了家，直到第二天早上都没有再出门。',
        "On Monday the 28th, he stepped into the building. Very few days of his morning shift remained. He listened to what the bug had recorded, and yet again, he hadn't obtained anything valuable. It appeared Ido was always at home.": '28 日星期一，他走进大楼。他上早班的日子已经所剩无几。{w} 他听了窃听器录下的内容，还是没能得到任何有价值的线索。看来 Ido 一直待在家里。',
        "Could he have been mistaken? What if Ido wasn't with Xyn? Perhaps that wasn't it. Maybe they were too careful, and spying on them like that was never going to work.": '难道是他搞错了？万一 Ido 和 Xyn 没有关系呢？{w}也许并不是这个原因。也可能只是对方太谨慎，靠这种办法监视根本行不通。',
        'Yes. I just went to see it, and I think it\'ll fit what we need. Apparently, Gan found it yesterday on Airun. It\'s a white, egg-shaped stone, bright and smooth, that he called the "Sekimeiya".': '是的。我刚去看过，应该正合我们的需要。{w} 听说 Gan 昨天在艾伦山找到了它。那是一块白色的蛋形石头，光洁明亮，他把它叫作「Sekimeiya」。',
        'Good. Anything should work as long as we advertise it like the last time. I have finished doing my part, by the way.': '很好。只要像上次那样宣传，什么都行。{w} 顺便说一句，我这边已经做完了。',
        '...Thank you. I have to go now. *sigh*': '……谢谢。{w} 我得走了。*叹气*',
        'Yes, me too. How was it?': '嗯，我也一样。{w} 事情办得怎么样？',
        "How? It was simple, of course. I had to spend a long time in the tower, but it went as we'd expected.": '怎么样？当然很简单。{w} 我在塔里耗了很久，但一切都如我们所料。',
        "Atase's boss stared into his eyes. Why? Why was he being tested like that?": 'Atase 的上司直直盯着他的眼睛。{w} 为什么？为什么要这样试探他？',
        '...Is this why you called me?': '……{w} 你叫我来就是为了这个？',
        "...That they're working very hard to catch us before that day, handling the situation with utmost care and having a lot of trouble with it. The gemstone was found yesterday on Airun, and it's called the Sekimeiya.": '……说他们正全力争取在那天之前抓住我们，对这件事处理得极为谨慎，也为此颇费周折。{w}那颗宝石是昨天在艾伦山找到的，名字叫 Sekimeiya。',
        'Thank you for letting us know immediately, and do so again in the future. You may go now.': '多谢你立刻来告知，今后也照这样办。{w}你可以走了。',
        "After Ido left the room, Atase's boss looked pensive for some time before inquiring what Atase's thoughts were. Atase had been the most involved in Ashiya-related manners; as such, his superior was curious to know his thoughts on what they'd heard.": 'Ido 离开房间后，Atase 的上司沉思了片刻，才问他有什么想法。{w}与芦屋相关的事务，Atase 一向参与最多，因此上司很想听听他对刚才那番话的看法。',
        "Of course. Three days ago, our access to the tower's computer was terminated. It's unlikely we were detected, though, so they're repeating the same preemptive actions. Infecting the computer again is not a priority. They must be paying close attention to it, and if they found out a way to identify us, we can't risk notifying them of the moment we regained access.": '当然。{w}三天前，我们对塔内电脑的访问被切断了。不过我们不太可能已经暴露，他们只是在重复同样的防范措施。{w}再次入侵电脑不是当务之急。他们现在一定盯得很紧，万一他们已经找到锁定我们的办法，我们一恢复访问就等于通知了他们，这个险不能冒。',
        "...I have a thought. The computer was cleaned, so they're evidently preparing something in the tower. However, we have very early information about the event they're preparing. If we want to make a move, it might be a good call to do it before they actually retrieve the gem on the 30th.": '……{w}我有个想法。{w}电脑被清理过，说明他们显然在塔里准备着什么。不过那场正在筹备的活动，我们早就拿到了情报。如果要动手，赶在他们 30 号真正取回宝石之前，也许是个好时机。',
        "What? That would be disastrous. Did you not listen to Ido? He was told they're handling the situation extremely carefully. And he was told about a few key details. Ashiya are hunting for a spy. If we take advantage of the information Ido was given, we're handing them his identity.": '什么？那会闯下大祸。{w}你没听 Ido 说吗？对方告诉过他，这件事他们处理得极为谨慎，还透了几处关键细节。{w}芦屋正在清查内鬼。我们要是利用 Ido 得到的情报，就等于把他的身份拱手送出去。',
        "...You're right. That's a bad idea.": '……{w}你说得对。这主意不妥。',
        "...You can leave now. I'll think about this.": '……{w}你先出去吧。这件事我再想想。',
        'Yes. They have revealed the existence of the Sekimeiya, and the details match what Ido was told. I think your idea is now worth considering.': '对。他们公开了 Sekimeiya 的存在，细节与 Ido 听到的完全吻合。{w}我看你那个主意，现在值得考虑了。',
        "They think we'll attack the tower as usual. As you said, they cleaned up their computer, so what they're preparing has to entail the building. We know Ashiya will obtain the Sekimeiya tomorrow, but we could've investigated for this information after the announcement.": '他们认为我们会照旧袭击那座塔。正如你所说，他们清理了电脑，那么他们准备的事必然与这栋楼有关。{w}芦屋明天就会拿到 Sekimeiya，其实这些信息，等公告出来后再查也能查到。',
        "Ashiya said they will pick it up tomorrow as opposed to having it brought. We know that means the source is established and from Yushibana. It was found on the 27th, so that Ashiya will already have it tomorrow confirms it's currently here. There are a few established points in contact with Ashiya, but not many. There are a couple of amateur collectors that try to sell all their findings to them. If it was found on the 27th and Ashiya already knew they would obtain it yesterday, it's likely they were immediately called about it in hopes they'd buy it. The 27th is a Sunday, the day Gan closes his shop to go to the caves. It's highly possible it was him who found it. It was also given a name before Ashiya obtained it, which is something he has done in the past.": '芦屋那边说，明天会自己来取，而不是让人送过去。这就说明货源已经确定，而且出自丰花。东西是27号被发现的，芦屋明天就能拿到手，可见它眼下就在这里。{w} 与芦屋有往来的固定卖家不多，只有几位业余收藏家，挖到什么都会想卖给他们。如果东西是27号发现的，而芦屋昨天就已经知道能拿到，那多半是有人发现后立刻打电话通知，指望他们买下。{w} 27号是周日，正是 Gan 关店去山洞的日子。发现它的人极有可能就是他。而且这东西在芦屋拿到之前就已经有了名字——这种事他以前也干过。',
        "...I understand. We don't know how it looks, though. Should Ido try to obtain that information?": '……我明白了。不过，我们还不知道它长什么样。{w} 要不要让 Ido 去打听一下？',
        "Glad to speak with you. I'm Zane, from Ashiya. I'm calling you to confirm that I'll come tomorrow at {time=14.}": '很高兴和你通话。我是芦屋的 Zane。{w} 打电话来是想确认一下，我明天 {time=14.} 过去。',
        "Glad to speak with you. I'm Zane, from Ashiya.{w} I'm calling you to confirm that I'll come tomorrow at 14:00.": '很高兴和你通话。我是芦屋的 Zane。{w} 打电话来是想确认一下，我明天 {time=14.} 过去。',
        "Glad to speak with you. I'm Zane, from Ashiya. I'm calling you to confirm that I'll come tomorrow at 14:00.": '很高兴和你通话。我是芦屋的 Zane。{w} 打电话来是想确认一下，我明天 {time=14.} 过去。',
        "Glad to speak with you. I'm Zane, from Ashiya.{w} I'm calling you to confirm that I'll come tomorrow at 2 p.m.": '很高兴和你通话。我是芦屋的 Zane。{w} 打电话来是想确认一下，我明天 {time=14.} 过去。',
        "Glad to speak with you. I'm Zane, from Ashiya. I'm calling you to confirm that I'll come tomorrow at 2 p.m.": '很高兴和你通话。我是芦屋的 Zane。{w} 打电话来是想确认一下，我明天 {time=14.} 过去。',
        "...14:00? I was told it'd be at 21:00.": '……{time=14}？我听到的说法是 {time=21.}。',
        "...2 p.m.? I was told it'd be at 9 p.m.": '……{time=14}？我听到的说法是 {time=21.}。',
        "...Oh, really? My mistake, I was looking at the wrong page. You're right, it'll be at {time=21.} Is that still all right?": '……啊，{w}是吗？{w} 抱歉，是我看错了页面。{w} 你说得对，是 {time=21.}。这样安排还方便吗？',
        "...Oh,{w} really?{w} My mistake, I was looking at the wrong page.{w} You're right, it'll be at 21:00. Is that still all right?": '……啊，{w}是吗？{w} 抱歉，是我看错了页面。{w} 你说得对，是 {time=21.}。这样安排还方便吗？',
        "...Oh, really? My mistake, I was looking at the wrong page. You're right, it'll be at 21:00. Is that still all right?": '……啊，{w}是吗？{w} 抱歉，是我看错了页面。{w} 你说得对，是 {time=21.}。这样安排还方便吗？',
        "...Oh,{w} really?{w} My mistake, I was looking at the wrong page.{w} You're right, it'll be at 9 p.m. Is that still all right?": '……啊，{w}是吗？{w} 抱歉，是我看错了页面。{w} 你说得对，是 {time=21.}。这样安排还方便吗？',
        "...Oh, really? My mistake, I was looking at the wrong page. You're right, it'll be at 9 p.m. Is that still all right?": '……啊，{w}是吗？{w} 抱歉，是我看错了页面。{w} 你说得对，是 {time=21.}。这样安排还方便吗？',
        'The plan was simple. Atase had to pass himself off as an Ashiya member. In order to not be easily recognizable in the future, his figure had to be slightly disguised, and he knew how to change his voice.': '计划很简单。{w} Atase 要冒充芦屋的人。为了以后不容易被认出来，他的外形得稍微伪装一下；声音方面，他也有办法改变。',
        'Minutes before {time=21}, a car parked outside Musashi Gemstones. Atase emerged from inside it, wearing a long coat. Stepping into the snow, he approached the bright window, leaving the prints of a new pair of shoes behind.': '{time=21} 前几分钟，一辆车停在武藏宝石门外。Atase 穿着长外套，从车里下来。{w} 他踏进雪中，朝那扇明亮的橱窗走去，身后留下一串新鞋的脚印。',
        'Minutes before 21:00, a car parked outside Musashi Gemstones. Atase emerged from inside it, wearing a long coat.{w} Stepping into the snow, he approached the bright window, leaving the prints of a new pair of shoes behind.': '{time=21} 前几分钟，一辆车停在武藏宝石门外。Atase 穿着长外套，从车里下来。{w} 他踏进雪中，朝那扇明亮的橱窗走去，身后留下一串新鞋的脚印。',
