        'Minutes before 9 p.m., a car parked outside Musashi Gemstones. Atase emerged from inside it, wearing a long coat.{w} Stepping into the snow, he approached the bright window, leaving the prints of a new pair of shoes behind.': '{time=21} 前几分钟，一辆车停在武藏宝石门外。Atase 穿着长外套，从车里下来。{w} 他踏进雪中，朝那扇明亮的橱窗走去，身后留下一串新鞋的脚印。',
        'Minutes before 9 p.m., a car parked outside Musashi Gemstones. Atase emerged from inside it, wearing a long coat. Stepping into the snow, he approached the bright window, leaving the prints of a new pair of shoes behind.': '{time=21} 前几分钟，一辆车停在武藏宝石门外。Atase 穿着长外套，从车里下来。{w} 他踏进雪中，朝那扇明亮的橱窗走去，身后留下一串新鞋的脚印。',
        'Inside the shop, he saw a young man near the entrance, who only glanced at him emptily. Avoiding eye contact, Atase stared behind his shoulders. Gan rushed over to the door after hearing the sound.': '店里靠近门口的地方有个年轻人，只淡淡地瞥了他一眼。Atase 避开视线，把目光投向那人身后。{w} Gan 听到动静，匆匆赶到门边。',
        "That was his time—he had it. As he'd discussed with his boss, Gan had to be paid before leaving, so Atase couldn't simply step out of the shop. If he ran away, Gan would try to chase him and would immediately call Ashiya and the police, and it was possible he'd see their car. Atase slowly took something out of his large pocket.": '这就是机会——东西已经到手。{w} 按他和上司说好的，离开前必须先付钱，所以 Atase 不能就这么走出店门。要是他跑了，Gan 会追出来，还会立刻通知芦屋和警察，说不定还会看见他们的车。Atase 慢慢从大衣口袋里取出一样东西。',
        'When she laid eyes inside the shop, a thin darkness hindered her sight. Confused, she placed a finger on the light switch next to the door, but that turned off all remaining light. Immediately, she flipped it back.': '她朝店里望去，视线被一层薄薄的黑暗挡住了。{w} 她有些困惑，伸手按向门旁的电灯开关，却把仅剩的光也关掉了。{w} 她立刻又按了回去。',
        "It had been Xyn. As Lei stared at the scene, she found no other option. They had never taken their attacks to such an extent before, but she knew they were responsible. How? How had they learned about the time and place of the Sekimeiya's tradeoff? Had her phone been hijacked?": '是 Xyn 干的。Lei 盯着眼前的景象，想不出别的可能。{w} 他们以前从没把袭击闹到这种地步，但她知道是他们干的。{w} 可他们是怎么知道的？怎么会知道 Sekimeiya 交易的时间和地点？她的手机被人动了手脚吗？',
        'The man beside Lei began to shake both bodies. Soon, Gan, who had inhaled a lesser amount of the smoke thanks to the shelves, opened his eyes, obstructing the blood from flowing down. In disbelief, he told Lei about what had happened, stuttering as he stared at the broken floor.': 'Lei 身旁的男人开始摇晃地上的两人。{w} 没过多久，Gan 睁开了眼睛——多亏有货架挡着，他吸入的烟较少——血也没再往下淌。{w} 他难以置信地把发生的事讲给 Lei 听，一边盯着破碎的地板，一边结结巴巴地说着。',
        "I'm telling you they just escaped! They're in a vehicle—I see their tire marks outside the shop! They must be found immediately! They just stole an incredibly valuable gemstone!": '我说了，他们刚跑掉！他们开着车——店外还有轮胎印！{w} 必须马上找到他们！他们刚抢走了一颗极其贵重的宝石！',
        "The dim streets of Yushibana were empty, but the snow prevented them from going as fast as they wanted to. They had to be careful not to let the wheel marks show their destination. When he had calmed down, Atase lifted the box's lid.": '丰花昏暗的街道上空无一人，积雪却让他们没法把车开得像预想中那么快。他们得小心，别让车轮印暴露目的地。{w} 等心绪平复下来，Atase 掀开了盒盖。',
        'Out of the blue, they heard a siren behind them. Through the rearview mirror, they could see a police car approaching.': '突然，身后传来警笛声。{w} 他们从后视镜里看见一辆警车正逼近。',
        "Wh-What!? Stop! Don't keep going!": '「什、什么！？{w} 停车！别再开了！」',
        "Pale, Faiten pulled over to the right. He couldn't muster a word—he slowly looked at the box on Atase's lap. Had Ashiya set a trap for them?": 'Faiten 脸色发白，把车靠向右侧。他一句话也说不出来，只是缓缓看向 Atase 膝上的盒子。{w} 是芦屋设下的圈套吗？',
        'The officer paused as he smelled the air. ...Inside the vehicle, both men frowned. What was he doing?': '警察停了下来，嗅了嗅空气。{w}……车内，两个男人都皱起了眉。他在做什么？',
        'After a minute, the officer looked at the result. It said "zero".': '一分钟后，警察看了看结果。{w} 上面显示「零」。',
        "...You can get back in the vehicle. Please, make sure you don't drive over the speed limit.": '「……{w}你可以回车里了。{w} 请务必不要超速。」',
        'Faiten stepped into the car. As he did so, the officer received a radio call. Trying to hide his haste, Faiten asked if he could get going.': 'Faiten 坐回车里。就在这时，警察接到了无线电呼叫。{w} Faiten 掩饰着自己的急切，问他能不能走了。',
        "Suddenly, the officer's look changed. Both men noticed he was staring at the brown box. Then, the officer saw something else. On Atase's attire, there was an Ashiya logo.": '忽然，警察的神色变了。{w} 两人都注意到，他正盯着那个棕色盒子。{w} 紧接着，警察又发现 Atase 的衣服上印着芦屋的标志。',
        "Slowly, Faiten took it and handed it to the officer. He lifted the lid, and his eyes didn't waver.": 'Faiten 缓缓拿起盒子，递给警察。{w} 警察掀开盒盖，目光没有丝毫动摇。',
        "Faiten and Atase looked at each other. Then, after a pause, Faiten extricated his lower body from below the dashboard. The officer never expected the car to accelerate as he did. It was Atase's foot that pressed down the accelerator. Immediately, the officer ran to his car as he yelled for them to stop.": 'Faiten 和 Atase 对视一眼。停顿片刻后，Faiten 把腿从仪表盘下方抽了出来。{w} 警察完全没料到车子会突然加速。{w} 是 Atase 踩下了油门。警察立刻奔向自己的车，一边大喊让他们停车。',
        'Later into the night, a handful of men were in Musashi Gemstones. Everyone had been ordered to leave, and the scene had been preserved as well as possible.': '夜深之后，武藏宝石店里还留着几个人。{w} 所有人都被命令离开，现场也尽可能保持原样。',
        'Shiroya Mirana had hit her head after falling from high up and entered a coma. As soon as the paramedics had reached that place, she had been taken to the hospital too. A few people were scattered around where her body had fallen.': 'Shiroya Mirana 从高处摔下时撞到了头，陷入昏迷。急救人员赶到后，她也被送往医院。{w} 在她坠落的位置周围，零散地站着几个人。',
        'Something else had fallen with the rubble. An open box, identical to the one Atase had received. Its lid had burst open on impact, and its contents had rolled away. A handful of people had seen the shining, egg-shaped stone within the darkness, but nobody had been allowed to touch anything. Its faint shine highlighted the drop of blood that had arced across its surface.': '还有一样东西和瓦砾一同坠落——一只盒子，和 Atase 收到的那只一模一样。{w} 盒盖在撞击中弹开，里面的东西滚了出去。有几个人在黑暗中看见了那颗发亮的蛋形石头，但谁都不准碰任何东西。它幽微的光映照着溅在表面的一道血痕。',
        'When a woman from the forensic team felt the gem for the first time, she was taken aback. ...It was very hot. Ashiya had quickly learned that only one of the Sekimeiya had been taken and asked the investigation team to return the fallen one. However, as it was related to the incident, it had to be inspected by them first.': '鉴识小组的一名女成员第一次摸到那颗宝石时，吃了一惊。……它烫得厉害。{w}芦屋很快得知只有一颗 Sekimeiya 被拿走，便要求调查组归还掉落的那颗。可由于它与案件有关，必须先由调查组检查。',
        "How had Xyn learned about the location? Katei didn't know, but it didn't matter. The preparations for his plan had been completed, so he needed Xyn to attack again. It wasn't in Ashiya's interests to pursue the attack of the 30th any further. As if nothing had happened, the Sekimeiya plan needed to continue as devised.": 'Xyn 是怎么查到那个地点的？Katei 不得而知，但这已无关紧要。{w}他计划的准备工作已经就绪，所以他需要 Xyn 再动一次手。继续追查 30 日那起袭击，对芦屋没有好处。要像什么都没发生过一样，让 Sekimeiya 计划按原定方案继续推进下去。',
        'When the stillness had gone on for a while, Katei listened to the latest recording. Nothing related to Xyn was there. Since Ido had told them about the Sekimeiya, the recordings had been nothing but uneventful.': '静默持续了一阵，Katei 听了最新的录音。{w}里面没有半点与 Xyn 相关的内容。自从 Ido 向他们提起 Sekimeiya 之后，录音就一直平淡无奇。',
        "The SD card behind the device had been swapped out. If the device was ever found in the tower, Katei didn't want the information he had to be revealed; he needed it for himself. It was a small card that wouldn't be questioned, so he could easily leave the building with it. After listening to Xyn's brief meeting, he had saved the recording on his own computer, inserting a new, empty card in the recording device.": '装置背面的 SD 卡已经换过了。万一这装置在塔里被人发现，Katei 不希望自己掌握的情报暴露出去；那份情报他还有用。{w}那不过是张小卡，不会有人起疑，他能轻易带着它离开大楼。听完 Xyn 那场简短会议的录音后，他把录音存进了自己的电脑，再往录音装置里换上一张空白的卡。',
        'Absolutely. The car is parked quite a ways away, but the police will find it soon. We have to give it up.': '确定。{w}车停在很远的地方，但警察很快就能找到。那辆车只能放弃了。',
        '...Have you learned what happened?': '……{w}出的事，你们听说了吗？',
        "...I don't think I'll be recognized.": '……{w}我想不会有人认出我吧。',
        "You say that, but we erased those records. I don't know what the fuck is going on with you, but what just happened isn't acceptable. Now you're being hunted for causing a death, and the police pulled you over. Both of you are basically sacrificial lambs at this point.": '你嘴上这么说，可那些记录已经被我们抹掉了。{w}我不知道你那边到底在搞什么鬼，但刚才发生的事不能就这么算了。现在你因为闹出人命被追捕，警察还拦了你们的车。到这一步，你们两个基本上就是弃子。',
        'I did. I was surprised by how it looked. It honestly looks like an egg made of marble, and I think it was shining a little.': '见到了。它的样子让我吃了一惊。{w}说实话，看着就像一颗大理石做的蛋，好像还微微发着光。',
        'Go home for now. Atase, I want you here tomorrow at {time=14.}': '先回家去吧。{w}Atase，明天{time=14.}我要你到这里来。',
        'Go home for now.{w} Atase, I want you here tomorrow at 14:00.': '先回家去吧。{w}Atase，明天{time=14.}我要你到这里来。',
        'Go home for now. Atase, I want you here tomorrow at 14:00.': '先回家去吧。{w}Atase，明天{time=14.}我要你到这里来。',
        'Go home for now.{w} Atase, I want you here tomorrow at 2 p.m.': '先回家去吧。{w}Atase，明天{time=14.}我要你到这里来。',
        'Go home for now. Atase, I want you here tomorrow at 2 p.m.': '先回家去吧。{w}Atase，明天{time=14.}我要你到这里来。',
        "Atase got home late into the night. He'd lived alone for years, so he had nobody to wake up. The first thing he did was look up the recent news.": 'Atase 回到家时已是深夜。他独居多年，不必担心吵醒谁。{w}他做的第一件事，就是查看最近的新闻。',
        "As he'd been told, he came across an article from the 24th of November. Someone had escaped from a prison cell, but the story was enigmatic. It hadn't been him; as he'd said, he had been in Ashiya Tower at the time. However, he couldn't help but feel that the man in the attached picture did strangely resemble him.": '他按吩咐去查，翻到了一篇11月24日的报道。有人从牢房里逃了出来，但报道写得语焉不详。{w}那并不是他；正如他所说，当时他人在芦屋塔。然而，他忍不住觉得，报道所附照片里的那个男人，竟和他莫名地相似。',
        "His eyes locked onto the headline painfully, and he was unable to clear his suddenly clogged throat. It was the first time his actions had killed someone. When he read that two friends of the girl had been there, a cold hollow expanded within his chest. He vividly remembered how he'd received the death of a close friend of his years ago. It hadn't been his intention, but he had created that pain for someone else, and a friend of the girl he'd killed was in grave danger as well. It was the last thing he'd ever wanted to happen. However, his mind kept going to what his boss had said. It was true—his situation was volatile.": '他痛苦地盯着那行标题，喉咙突然堵得厉害，怎么清嗓子也清不开。这是他第一次因为自己的行动害死人。{w}读到少女的两位朋友当时也在场，一股冰冷的空洞感在胸口蔓延开来。他清楚地记得，多年前得知挚友死讯时，自己是什么感受。他并非有意，却让别人承受了同样的痛苦；而他害死的那个少女的朋友，如今也身陷险境。{w}这是他最不愿发生的事。可是，上司的话一次次在他脑中响起。的确——他的处境随时可能生变。',
        "He frowned as he finished reading the article. He went over it again to confirm he hadn't been mistaken, but there was no mention of Xyn or their plan.": '读完报道，他皱起了眉。{w}他又从头看了一遍，确认自己没有看错，可文中只字未提 Xyn，也没提到他们的计划。',
        '"Enter." Ido stepped in, sensing the tense atmosphere. Then, he sat beside Atase.': '「进来。」{w}Ido 推门而入，察觉到了屋内的紧张气氛，随后在 Atase 身旁坐下。',
        "The tower's janitor put his hand in his pocket and slowly took out a rectangular piece of paper. It was a photograph. He handed it to his boss, who stared at it intensely.": '这位塔里的清洁工把手伸进口袋，缓缓取出一张长方形的纸。{w}那是一张照片。他把它递给上司，上司目不转睛地盯着它。',
        "Xyn had figured out a way to sneak tiny devices into the tower. That was the reason they'd chosen Ido as their associate. Staff members were frequently inspected upon arrival, especially after Xyn's first attacks. However, the janitor's job entailed the maintenance of the tower's plaza. By bringing the cleaning cart outside of the building and using a different Xyn member to drop the desired device in it, they had managed to slip a small camera into the tower.": 'Xyn 摸索出了一套把微型装置带进塔里的办法。他们也正因此才选中 Ido 做内应。{w}员工每次进塔都要接受频繁的检查，Xyn 最初的几次袭击之后更是如此。不过清洁工的工作包括维护塔前的广场。他们先把清洁车推到楼外，再由另一名 Xyn 成员把需要的装置丢进车里，就这样把小巧的摄像头带进了塔。',
        "The Sekimeiya was brought to the event room, and it was inside a cabinet. I hoped it would be out of all the security cameras' sight at some point, but that wasn't the case. I wanted to use the cart to cover my hands so that I wouldn't be seen taking the picture, but it was easier than that. Entering the event room was forbidden to the public, but I stepped in to clean it. As soon as I did, Katei Kuiji entered too—his night shift was about to end. It was very fortunate because a long curtain covered the Sekimeiya. He asked if I was curious about it and offered to let me see it.": 'Sekimeiya 被送进了水晶展室，放在展示柜里。我原本指望它总有一刻会避开所有监控摄像头的视野，可并没有。{w}我本想用清洁车挡住双手，免得被人看见我在拍照，但实际比这还容易。{w}水晶展室不向公众开放，不过我是进去打扫的。我刚进去，Katei Kuiji 也跟着进来了——他的夜班快结束了。运气实在好，因为有一块长遮布盖着 Sekimeiya。他问我好不好奇，还说可以让我看看。',
        '...Is that so? What did he say this time?': '……{w}是这样吗？{w}他这次都说了些什么？',
        "He seemed to want to make small talk. I believe he doesn't suspect me. He had a key for the cabinet, and he said they'd only made one for the event so that Xyn wouldn't be able to unlock it. He even used it to open the cabinet and let me touch the Sekimeiya. It was pretty smooth and felt like cold marble. It was kept refrigerated because it can apparently get damaged otherwise. He didn't say much else of importance, but he kept reiterating that they're hard at work upgrading their security measures to catch us.": '他似乎只是想闲聊几句。我看他并不怀疑我。{w}他有一把展示柜的钥匙，说为了这次活动只配了一把，好让 Xyn 打不开柜子。{w}他甚至用那把钥匙打开柜子，让我摸了摸 Sekimeiya。它相当光滑，摸起来像冰凉的大理石。{w}它一直冷藏保存，据说否则会受损。别的要紧话他没多说，只是一再强调他们正加紧升级安保措施，好抓住我们。',
        "It's strange. You said the cabinet where the Sekimeiya is can be locked and unlocked with a single key. When they did that in the past, we broke them open, so they must've accounted for that. When they linked an alarm to the cabinets, we disabled it remotely thanks to our access to their computer. Given what you've said, it's likely they're doing something similar, and that's why they cleaned their entire system. However, infecting it again to intercept what they're doing might be what they're waiting for.": '奇怪。你说过，放 Sekimeiya 的那个展示柜只用一把钥匙就能开关。以前他们也是这么做的，结果被我们撬开了，所以他们肯定考虑过这一点。{w}后来他们给展示柜连上警报，我们通过侵入他们的电脑远程关掉了。照你说的来看，他们很可能在做类似的事，所以才清理了整个系统。不过，如果我们为了掌握他们的动向再次感染系统，说不定正是他们等着我们做的。',
        "Despite Xyn's knowledge in the field, creating an undetectable malicious program wasn't simple. Because of that, the application they placed on the computer was a harmless one. That allowed it to stay hidden, only booting up for instants at a time. Its purpose was to check a path on the cloud owned by Xyn. If it contained a file, it would be downloaded and executed. However, if the file had already been downloaded once, the process wouldn't be repeated. That remote method allowed Xyn to gain access to Ashiya's computer. They knew about their security system, but a malicious file couldn't remain undetectable for long. By shuffling it every few days, however, they had kept their connection to the computer for months.": '尽管 Xyn 在这方面颇有本事，要写出一个无法被检测的恶意程序却并不简单。因此，他们装在电脑上的程序是无害的。正因如此，它才能一直隐藏，每次只启动一瞬。{w}它的用途是检查 Xyn 名下云端的一个路径。若那里有文件，它就会下载并执行。不过，若该文件已经下载过一次，这个过程就不会重复。{w}靠这种远程手段，Xyn 得以访问芦屋的电脑。他们了解对方的安保系统，可恶意文件瞒不了太久。于是他们每隔几天就换一次文件，就这样让与那台电脑的连接维持了数月。',
        "It entailed a risk. If the server file was found at any given time, reverse tracking Xyn could've been feasible. To prevent that, they had made sure their file wouldn't ever be automatically detected, but their connection to Ashiya had been cut a few days previously. They knew the computer had undergone a thorough cleanup that had managed to erase Xyn's file in the process. However, what about the application that had been manually installed months ago? Had it been erased too?": '这其中也有风险。只要服务器上的文件在某一刻被发现，顺藤摸瓜追查 Xyn 并非不可能。为防万一，他们确保自己的文件永远不会被自动检测到，但几天前，他们与芦屋电脑的连接还是断了。他们知道那台电脑经过了彻底清理，Xyn 的文件也在过程中被抹去。{w}可是，几个月前手动安装的那个程序呢？它是否也被一并清除了？',
        "Jiro feared the reason behind the computer's cleanup. If their original application was still present within the computer, they could infect it again by putting up a new file on the path. What Jiro didn't like was the thought that Ashiya were monitoring every change. While the file itself couldn't be detected as malicious, they might've committed a manual cleanup to assure it or anything similar would be deleted. Then, if Xyn remotely downloaded a new one, its appearance would be noticed, and although it wouldn't be detected as malicious, Ashiya could be sure Xyn had sent it.": 'Jiro 担心的是电脑被清理背后的原因。假如他们原先的程序还留在电脑里，只要在云端路径上放一个新文件，就能再次感染它。让 Jiro 不安的是，芦屋或许正在监视每一次变动。{w}文件本身虽不会被判定为恶意，他们却可能特意做了一次人工清理，以确保它或类似的东西被删掉。这样一来，如果 Xyn 远程下载了新文件，文件的出现就会被察觉；即便不被判为恶意，芦屋也能确定是 Xyn 送进来的。',
        "He had come up with a test. To know if their original application was still there, he put up a different file on the path. Upon execution, it would send a request to a web server before deleting itself. The request had been received, so Jiro knew infecting Ashiya's computer again was possible. However, he was considerably hesitant about doing it.": '他想出了一个试探的办法。为了确认原先的程序是否还在，他在那个路径上放了一个不同的文件。它一旦被执行，就会向一台网络服务器发送请求，然后自行删除。{w}请求已经收到，Jiro 由此知道再次感染芦屋的电脑是可行的。然而，他迟迟下不了决心。',
        "The event will be on the 15th, but until then, it seems the Sekimeiya will be in the event room, merely locked inside a cabinet. Nothing we can do should involve breaking it open. It'll be there for two weeks; they definitely expect our attack, and they think it'll happen during any night. You said the cabinet looks different than all the others, right? It was prepared specifically for this, and the computer was cleaned up. I'll repeat that Katei Kuiji said their intent is to catch us before the 15th. There's one more thing that caught my attention. You were told that they'd only made one key for the day of the event. This means the key will be used on the 15th.": '活动在15号举行。在那之前，Sekimeiya 似乎会一直放在活动室，就锁在展示柜里。我们无论做什么，都不该走撬柜子这条路。{w}它要在那里放两个星期；他们显然料到我们会动手，而且认为会在某一个夜里发生。{w}你说过，那个展示柜和别的都不一样，对吧？它是为这次活动专门准备的，电脑也清理过了。我再重复一遍，Katei Kuiji 说他们的打算是在15号之前抓住我们。{w}还有一点让我在意。你听说他们只为活动当天配了一把钥匙。这意味着那把钥匙会在15号用上。',
        "If we're going to attack, there are many reasons why it should be on the very day of the event. Now that Ashiya are putting so much effort into this, we can't follow along with their expectations. ...And there's another important reason why we shouldn't try to steal the Sekimeiya any day before the 15th. Since the announcement, Ashiya haven't stopped building excitement for this mysterious gemstone; they're likely being excessive on purpose. Today, the Sekimeiya's value is already greater than yesterday's. Every day it's kept as a mystery, Ashiya are artificially inflating its value. On the 15th, the Sekimeiya's value will be the highest it can be. That is when we want it.": '既然要动手，就有很多理由说明该选在活动当天。芦屋现在投入了这么多心力，我们偏不能顺着他们的预想来。{w}……而且还有一个重要的理由，说明我们不该在15号之前的任何一天去偷 Sekimeiya。{w}自公布以来，芦屋一直在为这块神秘宝石造势，恐怕是故意做得过头。今天 Sekimeiya 的价值已经超过昨天。它每多神秘一天，芦屋就在人为地抬高它的价值。{w}到15号，Sekimeiya 的价值会达到顶点。那才是我们下手的时候。',
        "Ashiya are supposedly raising the scale of their measures. So should we. You're right. When the cabinet is unlocked, we won't easily be able to access the Sekimeiya. But when it's locked, there's no way we will. It is possible we could acquire the single key they have, but that's not exactly likely, and it would pretty much reveal Ido. This is why I'm willing to prioritize my first idea. I asked you to bring a picture of the Sekimeiya because I found Atase's description of it interesting. It was supposedly found on Airun, that derelict mountain. I find that very hard to believe. Where did Gan find it? There are no caves there, and like Ashiya are saying, this is far from a typical gemstone. Doesn't it look too good to you? Its shape isn't natural if it's supposed to be a stone formed over the years. There's something about this story that is off.": '听说芦屋正在扩大戒备规模。我们也得跟上。{w} 你说得对。展示柜解锁时，我们没法轻易接近 Sekimeiya；可它锁着的时候，我们更无从下手。{w} 拿到他们那把唯一的钥匙并非不可能，但希望不大，而且几乎等于把 Ido 暴露出去。所以我愿意优先考虑最初那个方案。{w} 我让你带 Sekimeiya 的照片来，是因为 Atase 对它的描述让我很感兴趣。据说它是在艾伦山那座荒山上被发现的。我很难相信这种说法。{w} Gan 究竟是在哪里找到它的？那里根本没有洞穴，而且正如芦屋所说，这远不是寻常宝石。{w} 你不觉得它好得过分了吗？如果它真是经年累月形成的石头，这个形状就太不自然了。这个故事里总有什么地方不对劲。',
        "It was found right after our latest attack, and right as the computer was cleaned up. What I believe is that the emergence of this gemstone is directly related to us. Both of you compared it to marble, and it glows faintly. Added to its shape, vague origin, and the lack of details Ashiya are providing, I can't help but feel this was deliberately organized... As if the Sekimeiya was handcrafted to draw us to the focus of their upgraded security.": '它是在我们最近一次袭击之后、电脑刚被清理干净时被发现的。我认为，这颗宝石的出现与我们直接相关。{w} 你们两个都把它比作大理石，而且它会发出微弱的光。再加上它的形状、含糊的来历，以及芦屋提供的信息少得可怜，我忍不住觉得这一切是刻意安排的……就好像 Sekimeiya 是被人手工做出来，专门把我们引向他们加强戒备的核心。',
        "That is irrelevant. However, if they did, it would've been simple. They crafted a material of a single color into a simple shape. There are some that glow like this, and luminous paint would achieve the same effect. It doesn't matter if the gemstone in this picture was fabricated. Ashiya are giving it real value. However, what I've said could be of immense use to us. Ido, it felt like marble, right? We can have its dimensions, and the color and form aren't an issue. Do you know that molding marble is fairly simple?": '那无关紧要。不过，如果真是他们做的，那做起来也简单。把单一颜色的材料做成一个简单的形状就是了。确实有些东西会这样发光，用夜光涂料也能达到同样的效果。{w} 照片里这颗宝石是不是伪造的并不重要。芦屋赋予了它真实的价值。不过，我刚才说的那些，对我们可能大有用途。{w} Ido，它摸起来像大理石，对吧？我们能拿到它的尺寸，颜色和形状也不成问题。你知道大理石塑形其实相当简单吗？',
        "Of course not. That would eliminate all our credibility. I said this as a solution to Ido's question—how to obtain the real Sekimeiya. On the 15th, if we take it while the cabinet's unlocked, it will be noticed immediately. The real problem is taking it out of the building. We replace it with ours, and Ido takes it out with the cleaning cart.": '当然不是。那会把我们的信誉彻底毁掉。{w} 我这么说，是为了回答 Ido 的问题——如何拿到真正的 Sekimeiya。{w} 15 日那天，如果趁展示柜解锁时取走它，立刻就会被发现。真正的问题在于怎么把它带出大楼。{w} 我们用仿制品把它换掉，再由 Ido 用清洁推车运出去。',
        "Do you really think we could swap them? How would that not be noticed? Also, doesn't this create the same problem? If we managed to replace it with a similar-looking stone, how would we demonstrate we have the real one? If we sold it, Ashiya would claim to still have it.": '你真觉得我们能把它们换掉？怎么可能不被发现？{w} 而且，这不会带来同样的问题吗？就算我们成功换上一颗外观相近的石头，又怎么证明真品在我们手上？如果我们把它卖了，芦屋照样会宣称 Sekimeiya 还在他们那里。',
        "We could easily demonstrate it. And not only to assert our credibility, but also to let Ashiya know their measures have failed again. I know who could do this for us: my good friend Cevin Neneco. I have an idea of how to account for this, but I'll need to think more about it. Your other question, how the swap wouldn't be noticed... That has an easier answer.": '证明起来并不难。而且不只是为了保住我们的信誉，也要让芦屋知道，他们的防范又一次没能奏效。{w} 我知道谁能替我们办这件事：我的好朋友 Cevin Neneco。至于怎么解释这件事，我有个想法，但还得再仔细想想。{w} 你另一个问题——掉包怎么会不被发现……这个答案比较简单。',
        "We'd have to do it when the cabinet is open. However, we can't be seen either in person or from the security room. There is a way. The same thing we used last time, a smoke grenade.": '必须趁展示柜打开时动手。可我们既不能被人亲眼看到，也不能被监控室的人看见。{w} 有办法。和上次一样，用烟雾弹。',
        "The event will consist of guided visits for three people at once, and it will start at {time=9.} Like always, at that time, the floor will be almost empty. That's when we make our move—before anyone knows what the Sekimeiya is. We know the people who show up earliest get in earliest. Atase, you will be there first.": '活动会以导览形式进行，每次三人，从 {time=9.} 开始。{w} 和往常一样，那个时段楼层里几乎没人。我们就趁那时候动手——赶在任何人知道 Sekimeiya 是什么之前。我们知道最早到的人会先进去。Atase，你会第一个进去。',
        "The event will consist of guided visits for three people at once, and it will start at 9:00.{w} Like always, at that time, the floor will be almost empty. That's when we make our move—before anyone knows what the Sekimeiya is. We know the people who show up earliest get in earliest. Atase, you will be there first.": '活动会以导览形式进行，每次三人，从 {time=9.} 开始。{w} 和往常一样，那个时段楼层里几乎没人。我们就趁那时候动手——赶在任何人知道 Sekimeiya 是什么之前。我们知道最早到的人会先进去。Atase，你会第一个进去。',
        "The event will consist of guided visits for three people at once, and it will start at 9:00. Like always, at that time, the floor will be almost empty. That's when we make our move—before anyone knows what the Sekimeiya is. We know the people who show up earliest get in earliest. Atase, you will be there first.": '活动会以导览形式进行，每次三人，从 {time=9.} 开始。{w} 和往常一样，那个时段楼层里几乎没人。我们就趁那时候动手——赶在任何人知道 Sekimeiya 是什么之前。我们知道最早到的人会先进去。Atase，你会第一个进去。',
        "The event will consist of guided visits for three people at once, and it will start at 9 a.m.{w} Like always, at that time, the floor will be almost empty. That's when we make our move—before anyone knows what the Sekimeiya is. We know the people who show up earliest get in earliest. Atase, you will be there first.": '活动会以导览形式进行，每次三人，从 {time=9.} 开始。{w} 和往常一样，那个时段楼层里几乎没人。我们就趁那时候动手——赶在任何人知道 Sekimeiya 是什么之前。我们知道最早到的人会先进去。Atase，你会第一个进去。',
        "The event will consist of guided visits for three people at once, and it will start at 9 a.m. Like always, at that time, the floor will be almost empty. That's when we make our move—before anyone knows what the Sekimeiya is. We know the people who show up earliest get in earliest. Atase, you will be there first.": '活动会以导览形式进行，每次三人，从 {time=9.} 开始。{w} 和往常一样，那个时段楼层里几乎没人。我们就趁那时候动手——赶在任何人知道 Sekimeiya 是什么之前。我们知道最早到的人会先进去。Atase，你会第一个进去。',
        "Ido will be there too. Once you're inside, he will secretly give you a small grenade that he'll bring in the previous day with the cleaning cart. When the event begins, it'll go off in front of the Sekimeiya, and it'll knock everyone out. The smoke will rapidly rise up, so to avoid inhaling any, you'll immediately throw yourself to the floor. The cabinet will be unlocked, which will give you the chance to swap the Sekimeiya. Ours will be in the cleaning cart, and so that you don't have to go back to the lobby, Ido will leave it in the cleaning room. After that, you'll keep acting as if you fell unconscious. In the end, despite the attack, Ashiya will think they still have the Sekimeiya, so, the following day, Ido will be able to take the real one out.": 'Ido 也会在那里。你一进去，他就会悄悄把一枚小烟雾弹交给你——那是他前一天用清洁推车带进来的。活动开始时，它会在 Sekimeiya 前引爆，把所有人熏得昏过去。烟雾会迅速上升，所以为了不吸入，你要立刻扑倒在地。{w} 展示柜那时会解锁，你就有机会掉包 Sekimeiya。我们的仿制品会放在清洁推车里；为了不让你再跑回大厅，Ido 会把推车留在清洁间。之后，你要继续装作昏倒。{w} 最后，尽管遭受袭击，芦屋仍会以为 Sekimeiya 还在自己手里，于是第二天，Ido 就能把真品带出去。',
        "No. At the time of the event, Ido has no reason to be in the event room. Furthermore, it's likely the people present will be investigated, which could lead Ashiya to find the real Sekimeiya in the cart before we can obtain it. This could go wrong, sure, but it can work. However, see it as a chance I'm giving you. You screwed up badly. Not only should you redeem yourself to us, but to yourself. If you're found, you will be seen as a killer. Make sure this plan works before you think of asking for our help again.": '不行。活动开始后，Ido 没有理由待在活动室里。而且，在场的人很可能会被调查，那样芦屋说不定会在我们拿到真品之前，就从推车里找到真正的 Sekimeiya。{w} 这事确实可能出岔子，但也能成功。不过，把它当成我给你的机会。{w} 你犯下大错。你不仅该向我们、也该向你自己赎罪。一旦被发现，你就会被当成杀人犯。先确保这个计划成功，再考虑向我们求助。',
        "...I don't even get what you said, though. I'll still be recorded if I do this.": '……{w}可我还是没听懂你刚才说的。我这么做，不还是会被拍下来吗？',
        "That is one reason why smoke should also be released there. Like in every guided visit, everyone else will be in the lobby. If smoke appears in both hallways, everyone will quickly evacuate, as they'll be worried about it being poisonous or there being a fire. Then, the exit will be guarded to make sure nobody runs out with stolen gems. Katei Kuiji will be in the security room, so due to the smoke, he won't be able to leave it without falling unconscious, and he won't see what's happening in the building. When everyone is knocked out, you will go to the cleaning room and obtain our fake. It is essential that you do this first to make sure no one sees you. You will leave your smoke grenade in the cart and subsequently go back to swap the gemstones.": '这也是为什么那里也得释放烟雾。{w} 每次导览参观时，其他人都会待在大厅。如果两条走廊都出现烟雾，大家都会赶紧撤出去，因为他们会担心烟雾有毒，或者发生了火灾。随后，出口会有人把守，确保没人带着偷来的宝石跑出去。{w} Katei Kuiji 会在监控室，所以烟雾一出现，他只要离开监控室就会昏倒，也就看不到楼里发生了什么。{w} 等所有人都昏过去，你就去清洁间取出我们的赝品。你必须先做这件事，确保没人看见你。把你的烟雾弹留在推车里，然后再回去掉包宝石。',
        'Nobody will. Setting up a timer is the easiest thing in the world. We know when they have to go off: at 9:04.': '不需要人。装个定时器再简单不过。我们知道它们该在什么时候启动：{time=9:04.}',
        'Nobody will. Setting up a timer is the easiest thing in the world. We know when they have to go off: at 9:04 a.m.': '不需要人。装个定时器再简单不过。我们知道它们该在什么时候启动：{time=9:04.}',
        "No, we don't...! The event will begin at 9:00, but we don't know when the cabinet will be unlocked!": '不，我们不知道……！活动确实在 {time=9} 开始，可我们不知道展示柜什么时候才会解锁！',
        "No, we don't...! The event will begin at 9 a.m., but we don't know when the cabinet will be unlocked!": '不，我们不知道……！活动确实在 {time=9} 开始，可我们不知道展示柜什么时候才会解锁！',
        "Don't you remember? We can use the handrails. Behind them, the small grenades will be hidden, and it works perfectly for us. The cameras in the hallways are placed to focus on the doors, so there are parts of the handrails that aren't visible. When Ido is cleaning, he can secretly place a grenade and slide it toward a point of the handrail that's being recorded. We will need two per hallway, and it'll seem like anyone could've placed them the previous day.": '不记得了吗？我们可以利用扶手。{w} 小烟雾弹藏在扶手后面，对我们来说正合适。走廊的摄像头都对着门，因此扶手有些位置拍不到。{w} Ido 打扫时，可以悄悄放下一枚烟雾弹，再把它滑到会被摄像头拍到的扶手位置。每条走廊需要两枚，看上去就像前一天谁都有可能放进去。',
        "...And that's not all. There's something else we'll do that will divert suspicion from Ido. After all, if this works, we still wouldn't be in the clear. After suffering such a major attack, will Ashiya really believe nothing was stolen? If they're careful, they might not believe it and end up finding the real Sekimeiya. So, we will give them a reason to believe it. Their focus will be on the Sekimeiya; that's what they expect to be targeted, and the measures they're taking clearly involve it, as proven by the new cabinet and it only having one key. Targeting a different room will be much less problematic. In the morning, before the event, the cameras will be monitored. However, there are more cameras than monitors, and only the hallways and a few crystal rooms are displayed at once, correct, Ido?": '……还不止这些。我们还要做一件事，把怀疑从 Ido 身上引开。{w} 毕竟，就算计划成功，我们也还没完全脱身。遭到这么大规模的袭击后，芦屋真的会相信什么都没丢吗？如果他们谨慎些，或许不会信，最后还是会找到真正的 Sekimeiya。{w} 所以，我们要给他们一个相信的理由。{w} 他们的注意力会放在 Sekimeiya 上；那才是他们预期会被下手的目标，而他们采取的戒备显然也围绕着它——新的展示柜和只有一把钥匙就是证明。相比之下，去针对另一个展室，麻烦会小得多。{w} 早上活动开始前，监控会有人盯着。但摄像头比监视器多，同一时间只会显示走廊和少数几个水晶展室，对吧，Ido？',
        "Exactly. This means that if you put all the gems there into a case, you won't be seen. We would usually never do this, as it makes you the only suspect, but this isn't an issue this time. The curtains aren't raised until {time=9:10}, so you'll leave all of them down. You'll also leave the case in the room, in the corner beneath the camera, so that we can have a visitor be there when the smoke is released, crouching right as it happens. If they keep their head near the floor as they exit the tower with the case, they won't fall unconscious. Two minutes after the smoke has been released, he will attempt to flee. This will make Ashiya think their expectations were subverted and that the failed attack had that room as its final target. ...I doubt Faiten will be willing to take this job under any circumstances, but I'll find the right person without telling them the full extent of the plan.": '正是如此。也就是说，只要你把那里的宝石全装进箱子，就不会被拍到。平时我们绝不会这么做，因为那样你就成了唯一的嫌疑人，但这次没关系。{w} 遮布要到 {time=9:10} 才会拉起，所以你要让它们一直垂着。你还要把箱子留在那个房间里，放在摄像头下方的角落。这样烟雾释放时，我们可以安排一名访客正好在场，并在那一刻蹲下。只要他带着箱子离开塔时把头贴近地面，就不会昏过去。{w} 烟雾释放两分钟后，他会尝试逃走。这会让芦屋以为他们的预想落空了，以为那场失败的袭击最终针对的其实是那个房间。{w} ……我怀疑 Faiten 无论如何都不肯接这活，但我会找到合适的人，并且不把计划的全部内容告诉他。',
