        'Slowly, the time kept passing. After Ido was done with the little plaza, he entered again, mopping the new snowy footprints and the already shining floor.': '时间缓缓流逝。{w} Ido 把小广场拖完后，又走了进来，擦掉新留下的雪水脚印，把本就发亮的地面又拖了一遍。',
        "Atase's head slowly turned to the girl. She wasn't Shiroya. That was the name of the girl whose memory pressed down on his shoulders.": 'Atase 缓缓转头看向那个少女。{w} 她不是 Shiroya。Shiroya 是另一个少女的名字，关于她的记忆一直沉沉压在他肩上。',
        'Who was that, then? Atase would soon learn.': '那么，她是谁？{w} Atase 很快就会知道。',
        'At {time=9}, the door to hallway B opened. Through it came Naomi Cabca, who gave a brief explanation of the event. It was time. Only four minutes were left.': '到了{time=9}，B走廊的门打开了。Naomi Cabca 从门里走出来，简短地说明了活动内容。{w} 时候到了。只剩四分钟。',
        'At 9:00, the door to hallway B opened. Through it came Naomi Cabca, who gave a brief explanation of the event.{w} It was time. Only four minutes were left.': '到了{time=9}，B走廊的门打开了。Naomi Cabca 从门里走出来，简短地说明了活动内容。{w} 时候到了。只剩四分钟。',
        'At 9:00, the door to hallway B opened. Through it came Naomi Cabca, who gave a brief explanation of the event. It was time. Only four minutes were left.': '到了{time=9}，B走廊的门打开了。Naomi Cabca 从门里走出来，简短地说明了活动内容。{w} 时候到了。只剩四分钟。',
        'At 9 a.m., the door to hallway B opened. Through it came Naomi Cabca, who gave a brief explanation of the event.{w} It was time. Only four minutes were left.': '到了{time=9}，B走廊的门打开了。Naomi Cabca 从门里走出来，简短地说明了活动内容。{w} 时候到了。只剩四分钟。',
        'At 9 a.m., the door to hallway B opened. Through it came Naomi Cabca, who gave a brief explanation of the event. It was time. Only four minutes were left.': '到了{time=9}，B走廊的门打开了。Naomi Cabca 从门里走出来，简短地说明了活动内容。{w} 时候到了。只剩四分钟。',
        'Atase suppressed his nervousness as best he could. The cabinet had been unlocked, so the plan was very close to succeeding. However, a few seconds still remained until 9:04.': 'Atase 竭力压住紧张。展示柜已经解锁，计划离成功只差一步。可距离 {time=9:04.} 还剩几秒。',
        'Atase suppressed his nervousness as best he could. The cabinet had been unlocked, so the plan was very close to succeeding. However, a few seconds still remained until 9:04 a.m.': 'Atase 竭力压住紧张。展示柜已经解锁，计划离成功只差一步。可距离 {time=9:04.} 还剩几秒。',
        'Once everyone plummeted down, a sudden, unsettling silence consumed the room. What was happening outside? Had everyone evacuated? Had the gems been brought out in the suitcase? For a few seconds, Atase had to wait to make sure nobody remained conscious.': '众人相继倒下后，一阵令人不安的死寂笼罩了房间。{w}外面究竟发生了什么？人都撤走了吗？宝石已经装进手提箱带出去了吗？Atase 不得不等上几秒，确认没有一个人还醒着。',
        'Again, it was hard to believe it was the same place as before. However, nobody was there. Covering his face, Atase dashed to the cleaning room.': '和刚才一样，他几乎无法相信这里还是同一个地方。可这里一个人也没有。{w}Atase 捂住脸，冲进清洁间。',
        'There was light; almost no smoke had gone through the door. Occupying most of the space, the cart sat in the room. Without hesitating, he dropped the smoke grenade inside it.': '里面亮着灯，几乎没有烟从门缝里透进来。{w}那辆推车占去了大半个房间。他没有犹豫，把烟雾弹丢进了推车。',
        '...H-Huh?': '……{w}怎、怎么回事？',
        "Why? He couldn't comprehend what he was seeing. Had there been two Sekimeiya?": '怎么会？他无法理解眼前的景象。{w}难道 Sekimeiya 有两个？',
        "Atase had to rush, but he didn't know what to do. If he took both gemstones, Xyn's plan would never work. Dumbfounded, he reached for one of the two; he could only replace a single one.": 'Atase 必须抓紧时间，却不知该怎么办。若把两颗宝石都拿走，Xyn 的计划就绝不可能成功。{w}他怔怔地伸手去拿其中一颗——他只能换掉一颗。',
        'He felt a screen of glass that he was able to slide open. Then, without placing his fingers on it, he took a gemstone out, swapping it with his. Still in awe, he closed the glass and dropped the curtain down.': '他摸到一块可以滑开的玻璃。随后，他尽量不让手指碰到宝石，把其中一颗取出来，换成了自己带来的那颗。{w}他仍满心惊愕，合上玻璃，放下遮布。',
        'However, the darkness prevented him from noticing something. Naomi was no longer there.': '然而黑暗让他没能察觉到一件事。{w}Naomi 已经不在了。',
        "...But he couldn't make sense of it. Why weren't they being rescued?": '……{w}可他怎么也想不通。为什么没人来救他们？',
        'Wh— *cough*': '什——{w=0.4}*咳*',
        "The boy woke up. That was the start of a very long day. During the previous weeks, Atase had come up with countless outcomes. However, the real one was far from any he'd devised.": '那个少年醒了。{w}漫长的一天由此开始。{w}在此之前的几周里，Atase 设想过无数种结果。可真正发生的那一种，与他所设想的任何一种都相去甚远。',
        "They were trapped. The alarm he'd heard had removed all methods of escape. When he learned Naomi had left the event room before his return, he had to hide his fear. ...Could she have noticed Atase's absence upon awakening?": '他们被困住了。他听到的那阵警报封锁了所有逃生的手段。{w}得知 Naomi 在他回来之前就已离开活动室时，他只能把恐惧藏起来。……她会不会一醒来就发现 Atase 不见了？',
        "He didn't know how worried he had to be or what had triggered the alarm. Even though the building was full of cameras, he knew not to be afraid of them. He was told the internet connection had been cut by the alarm. In the meantime, Xyn couldn't remotely access the computer. However, he knew his group well. According to Katei, at {time=21}, the connection would come back, and Xyn would immediately erase all the recorded footage.": '他不知道自己该有多担心，也不知道是什么触发了警报。楼里到处都是摄像头，可他清楚不必怕它们。{w} 他听说警报切断了网络连接，Xyn 一时无法远程访问电脑。不过，他很了解自己的同伴。按 Katei 的说法，到了 {time=21}，连接就会恢复，Xyn 会立刻抹掉所有录像。',
        "He didn't know how worried he had to be or what had triggered the alarm. Even though the building was full of cameras, he knew not to be afraid of them.{w} He was told the internet connection had been cut by the alarm. In the meantime, Xyn couldn't remotely access the computer. However, he knew his group well. According to Katei, at 21:00, the connection would come back, and Xyn would immediately erase all the recorded footage.": '他不知道自己该有多担心，也不知道是什么触发了警报。楼里到处都是摄像头，可他清楚不必怕它们。{w} 他听说警报切断了网络连接，Xyn 一时无法远程访问电脑。不过，他很了解自己的同伴。按 Katei 的说法，到了 {time=21}，连接就会恢复，Xyn 会立刻抹掉所有录像。',
