        "He didn't know how worried he had to be or what had triggered the alarm. Even though the building was full of cameras, he knew not to be afraid of them.{w} He was told the internet connection had been cut by the alarm. In the meantime, Xyn couldn't remotely access the computer. However, he knew his group well. According to Katei, at 9 p.m., the connection would come back, and Xyn would immediately erase all the recorded footage.": '他不知道自己该有多担心，也不知道是什么触发了警报。楼里到处都是摄像头，可他清楚不必怕它们。{w} 他听说警报切断了网络连接，Xyn 一时无法远程访问电脑。不过，他很了解自己的同伴。按 Katei 的说法，到了 {time=21}，连接就会恢复，Xyn 会立刻抹掉所有录像。',
        "He didn't know how worried he had to be or what had triggered the alarm. Even though the building was full of cameras, he knew not to be afraid of them. He was told the internet connection had been cut by the alarm. In the meantime, Xyn couldn't remotely access the computer. However, he knew his group well. According to Katei, at 9 p.m., the connection would come back, and Xyn would immediately erase all the recorded footage.": '他不知道自己该有多担心，也不知道是什么触发了警报。楼里到处都是摄像头，可他清楚不必怕它们。{w} 他听说警报切断了网络连接，Xyn 一时无法远程访问电脑。不过，他很了解自己的同伴。按 Katei 的说法，到了 {time=21}，连接就会恢复，Xyn 会立刻抹掉所有录像。',
        "He recalled the conversation he'd had with his boss word by word; he knew how important it was for him not to fail. Therefore, despite the unforeseen alarm, Atase had only one priority: to make the plan a success.": '他逐字回想与上司的那番对话，清楚自己绝不能失手。{w} 所以，尽管警报来得意外，Atase 也只有一个目标：让计划成功。',
        "Upon arriving at the tower, Katei had listened to the latest recording. As he'd hoped, Ido and his boss had talked one last time and gone over their movements. Katei took out the SD card—he couldn't allow that audio to be heard by anyone else. As he didn't want the card on his person either, he hid it in the security room.": '一到芦屋塔，Katei 就先听了最新那段录音。正如他所期望的，Ido 和他的上司最后谈了一次，把行动安排过了一遍。{w} Katei 取出 SD 卡——那段音频绝不能让其他人听到。他也不愿把卡带在身上，便把它藏进了监控室。',
        "The time was rapidly approaching, and he didn't have the opportunity to go back to the staff room. While he tried to remain calm, he hid the voice recorder as well. Although the large device could've been found if Ashiya searched, he knew the SD card wouldn't be, which was all that mattered. Through the monitors, Katei saw the first group approaching the event room. He had to act.": '时间越来越近，他已经没机会回员工室了。他竭力保持镇定，把录音笔也藏了起来。那东西个头不小，芦屋那边若仔细搜查，或许能找到，但 SD 卡不会——这才是关键。{w} 透过监视器，Katei 看见第一批人正走向活动室。他必须行动了。',
        "Hallway A was empty, but as soon as Katei entered it, so did someone else. From the lobby came a man with long hair who he'd never seen before. Paying no attention to Katei, he walked forward.": 'A走廊空无一人，可 Katei 刚走进去，另一个人也跟着进来了。那是个从大厅走来的长发男人，Katei 从没见过他。{w} 那人看都没看 Katei，径直向前走去。',
        "The room was full of people. All the visitors formed a line behind hallway B, while police officers conversed with Ashiya's guard. Dote and Asfu, Katei's co-workers, greeted him with a smile. Their job was to uncover the cabinets in most of the crystal rooms, but they knew very few people there that day wanted to see those.": '大厅里挤满了人。参观者都在B走廊后面排队，警察则与芦屋的警卫交谈。{w} Katei 的同事 Dote 和 Asfu 笑着向他打招呼。他们的职责是掀开大部分水晶展室里展示柜的遮布，但他们知道，今天在场的人里几乎没有谁想看那些东西。',
        "...Nobody was looking at him, and he didn't want to walk away from the door. As if waiting for the conversation to end, he stared at the police as they talked.": '……{w}没有人看着他，他也不想离开门边。他盯着交谈中的警察，像是在等那番对话结束。',
        "Katei's plan wasn't guaranteed to work, but he wasn't at risk. Once the smoke was released, the chance to step back into the hallway might not have existed. If someone gestured at Katei to evacuate, he couldn't turn around. However, it didn't matter; he wouldn't be blamed for the attack, and Xyn's plan would still fail. Furthermore, he could attempt to sneak away outside and then reenter the building through the storeroom anyway.": 'Katei 的计划未必成功，但他本人不会有危险。烟雾一旦释放，他也许就再没机会回到走廊里了。要是有人示意他撤离，他就不能回头。{w} 不过这无所谓；袭击不会算到他头上，Xyn 的计划照样会失败。再说，他大可以先悄悄溜到外面，再从储藏室绕回楼里。',
        'Katei felt a shock going through his body: that was the moment. In the blink of an eye, everyone had turned around toward the exit, while both police officers were alerting their superiors. As quickly as he could, Katei dashed into the hallway and dropped to his hands and knees.': 'Katei 浑身一震：就是现在。眨眼间，所有人都转身朝出口看去，两名警察则在向上级报告。{w} Katei 用最快的速度冲进走廊，双手双膝着地趴了下来。',
        "Through the gap, he stared. He knew the darkness would prevent Atase from noticing him, and there was something he had to see. Days earlier, he had uncovered the cabinet's curtain. ...He had seen two identical Sekimeiya lying atop the cushion. Although he'd gotten scared at first, Xyn hadn't planted a fake yet—he knew Ashiya had two identical gemstones.": '他透过门缝盯着里面。他知道黑暗里 Atase 不会察觉到他，而且有件事他必须看清。{w} 几天前，他曾掀开展示柜的遮布。……他看见两个一模一样的 Sekimeiya 躺在垫子上。{w} 起初他确实吓了一跳，但 Xyn 还没有把赝品放进去——他知道芦屋手上有两块一样的宝石。',
        'He was completely still until he reached for one of them. After taking out the rightmost one, Atase placed his own inside. He ran back without wasting even a second.': '他僵立不动，直到伸手去拿其中一个。Atase 取出右边那个，把自己带来的放了进去。{w} 他一秒都没耽搁，转身跑了回去。',
        'The other Sekimeiya would be in the cleaning cart. Katei only had to be in the tower for a few more seconds. Hallway C was still being recorded, so he skittered to the lobby. However, on the way, he abruptly stopped himself.': '另一个 Sekimeiya 应该在清洁推车里。Katei 只需在塔里再待几秒。{w} C走廊仍在录像范围之内，于是他快步溜向大厅。可走到半路，他猛地停住了。',
        "He stared at his hands in confusion. ...What had happened? There was no glow there. It didn't make any sense: he could feel the Sekimeiya's touch, but it didn't look like it was there.": '他困惑地盯着自己的双手。……怎么回事？那里没有光芒。{w} 这说不通：他分明能感觉到 Sekimeiya 的触感，却看不出它就在手里。',
        'Bewildered, he stepped toward the light in the lobby, and once it illuminated his hands, he saw what had happened: the Sekimeiya was no longer white. Puzzled, he looked around him. A metal shutter was covering the exit, but somehow the gemstone in his hands was more bizarre.': '他满心惶惑，朝大厅的光亮走去。光线照到手上时，他才看清发生了什么：Sekimeiya 不再是白色的了。{w} 他困惑地环顾四周。出口被一道金属卷帘门封住了，可不知为何，手里的宝石更让他觉得诡异。',
        "He reached his right arm inside and took out the other Sekimeiya without touching it directly. Amazed, Katei stared at it. He couldn't know if the cloth of his shirt had made a difference, but its glow hadn't vanished that time.": '他伸出右臂探进去，没有直接触碰就取出了另一个 Sekimeiya。{w} Katei 惊讶地盯着它。他无从判断是不是衬衫的布料起了作用，但这一次，它的光芒没有消失。',
        '...Wh-What? Wh-Where is it!?': '...{w}什、什么？{w}在、在哪儿！？',
        "Petrified, Katei kept going through all his pockets. The key wasn't there. There was no way out for him without it. Desperately, he looked at all the keys he had, but none of them had the particular rust he most wanted to feel.": 'Katei 僵在原地，把全身上下的口袋翻了个遍。{w}钥匙不在。{w}没有那把钥匙，他根本无路可逃。他急切地翻看手里所有的钥匙，却没有一把带着他最想摸到的那种锈迹。',
        "He realized that he must have dropped it. He didn't keep it with the others, and he'd verified that he had it in the security room. Therefore, he'd dropped it in hallway A, when he'd been crawling toward the event room. Since his pocket had been so close to the floor, he hadn't noticed the sound of it falling out.": '他意识到钥匙一定是掉在路上了。{w}那把钥匙他从不与其他钥匙放在一起，而且在监控室里还确认过自己带着它。那么，就是在他爬向活动室时掉在了A走廊。{w}口袋离地面那么近，钥匙滑出去的声音他自然没能听见。',
        'He stopped before the secret exit. A bright, grassy field was outside it, and he was so close to seeing it. He located the keyhole and inserted the chilly key into it.': '他在暗门前停下。门外是一片明亮青翠的草地，只差一步就能看见。{w}他摸到锁孔，把冰凉的钥匙插了进去。',
        "Subsumed by the darkness, Katei fell to his knees in defeat. The last method of escape, which he'd held as a trump card for years, had betrayed him. The situation only became worse for him when he turned around. There was nothing there.": '黑暗吞没了 Katei，他绝望地跪倒在地。他多年来一直当作最后王牌的退路，到头来背叛了他。{w}可当他转过身时，情况更糟。{w}那里什么都没有。',
        'H-Huh? Where are... the Sekimeiya?': '咦、咦？{w}Sekimeiya 呢……？',
        'Someone was in the hallway. Slowly, he rose and stepped out of the secret corridor, then gripped the doorknob.': '走廊里有人。{w}他缓缓起身，走出秘密通道，握住了门把手。',
        'In an instant, he ran up behind her. He had to talk to her before everyone woke up. However, as soon as she heard his movements, Naomi sprinted away to escape him.': '他立刻追到她身后。必须赶在所有人醒来之前和她谈一谈。{w}然而 Naomi 一听到他的动静，便猛地跑起来，想要甩开他。',
        'He peered into the hallway, but the dark cloud prevented a clear line of sight. Despite that, he was able to see that someone was there, and they began to go up the stairs. He ran without thinking. He had to stop Naomi no matter how much panic assaulted him.': '他朝走廊里张望，烟雾却挡住了视线。尽管如此，他还是看出那边有人，而且正往楼上走。{w}他想都没想就跑了过去。无论心里多么慌乱，他都必须拦下 Naomi。',
        "His hands trembled as he walked back down. He balled them into fists and slowly released them. The trembling stopped, but he was internally collapsing. Attempting a calming breath, he walked to the crystal floor, where he began to look around as if he'd been innocently imprisoned.": '下楼时他的双手一直在抖。他握紧拳头，又缓缓松开。{w}颤抖止住了，心里却已经崩溃。他深吸一口气让自己镇定，然后走向水晶展室，装出一副无辜被困的模样四处张望。',
        "A sharp sound refocused all of her senses. She was in the event room, and there had just been an attack in the tower. After getting that far, she almost gasped. Those shoes belonged to Katei, and what she'd heard was the cabinet opening.": '一声锐响，让她猛然回过神来。{w}她在活动室，塔里刚刚发生过一场袭击。{w}想到这里，她差点倒吸一口凉气。那双鞋是 Katei 的，而她听见的，是展示柜打开的声音。',
        'While she was still processing that information, the steps began to depart. She had to stop him. At once, Naomi considered the possibility that Katei had been responsible for the smoke. Her head hurt, and her limbs took a few seconds to respond. However, she was able to force her body up.': '她还来不及理清这些，脚步声已经要远去了。{w}她必须拦住他。几乎同时，Naomi 想到烟雾也许正是 Katei 放的。{w}她的头很痛，四肢过了好几秒才听使唤，但她还是硬撑起了身体。',
        "Speechless, she saw two people who she'd just met on the floor. Their names were Atsuki and Shiroya. But what about the third person...? Another man had been with them, and Naomi couldn't find him.": '她一时说不出话，只看见地上躺着刚认识不久的两个人——Atsuki 和 Shiroya。{w}可第三个人呢……？他们身边本来还有个男人，Naomi 却找不到他。',
        "Six people had fallen unconscious. When the smoke was released, Naomi had been looking at the cabinet; out of all of them, she'd been the farthest from the source, as everyone else had been next to a grenade. Atase had faked his unconsciousness, meaning that in the event room, Naomi's was the only adult body to be knocked out. Added to the lesser quantity of smoke that she inhaled, she would've been the first to awaken. Because of that, when Katei stepped next to her ears, she was brought back to reality minutes before everyone else.": '昏过去的一共六个人。烟雾释放时，Naomi 正在看展示柜；所有人里她离源头最远，因为其他人身边都有一颗烟雾弹。{w}Atase 是装昏的，也就是说，活动室里真正被放倒的成年人只有 Naomi 一个。再加上她吸入的烟雾更少，她本该是最先醒来的。{w}正因如此，当 Katei 的脚步声在她耳边响起时，她比其他人早了几分钟清醒过来。',
        "Approaching the storeroom, Naomi hoped she'd been mistaken. Katei should've been in the security room, so perhaps he was acting against the attack by protecting the target. Outside the door, she heard a noise.": 'Naomi 走向储藏室，希望是自己看错了。Katei 本该待在监控室，也许他正在应对袭击、保护目标。{w}走到门外，她听见了动静。',
        'As soon as Naomi peeked inside the vacant room, her mouth dropped. What the hell was she seeing? The wall was open...': 'Naomi 往空无一人的屋里一探头，顿时目瞪口呆。{w}她到底看见了什么？墙竟然敞开着……',
        "Although she couldn't see anyone, she was able to perceive Katei nearby. He was there, in the hallway. Wishing not to be seen, she sprinted toward hallway C.": '她看不见任何人，却能感觉到 Katei 就在附近。他就在走廊里。{w}为了不被他发现，她朝 C走廊奔去。',
        "Her eyes went wider than ever before. A metal shutter was in front of the door. It didn't make any sense, but she didn't have time to think. She had to keep running.": '她的眼睛睁得比以往任何时候都大。门前是一道金属卷帘。{w}这根本说不通，但她没有时间思考，只能继续跑。',
        "She tried to open the elevator, but it wasn't on that floor. She couldn't wait for it, so she took out her keys and dashed up the stairs.": '她试着打开电梯，可电梯不在这一层。{w}她等不起，便掏出钥匙，冲上楼梯。',
        "Naomi stepped to the sofa, where she dropped her keys and the suitcase. Exhausted, she took a moment to catch her breath. The bright living room looked nothing like the lowest floor. When she opened the case, she saw both identical gemstones. Even though she'd brought them to safety, she'd been told the cabinet's temperature was essential for their well-being.": 'Naomi 走到沙发前，把钥匙和手提箱放下。她筋疲力尽，缓了好一会儿才把气喘匀。明亮的客厅和最底层看起来完全不像同一个地方。{w}她打开箱子，两颗一模一样的宝石都在。尽管她已经把它们带到了安全之处，但有人告诉过她，展示柜的温度对宝石至关重要。',
        'Out of nowhere, both of the Sekimeiya vanished. Astonished, Naomi stared at the empty suitcase. She had felt one of their white surfaces for an instant before both had disappeared.': '两颗 Sekimeiya 凭空消失了。{w}Naomi 惊愕地盯着空荡荡的箱子。就在它们消失的前一瞬，她还摸到过其中一颗白色宝石的表面。',
        "She couldn't comprehend what had occurred; it wasn't possible. They couldn't have disappeared. ...However, they weren't there anymore.": '她无法理解发生了什么；这不可能。它们不可能凭空消失。{w}……可它们确实已经不在了。',
        "She questioned her own memories. She had just left the keyring there, hadn't she...? Or had she left it in the keyhole? Speechless, she peeked down the stairs.": '她开始怀疑自己的记忆。自己刚才明明把钥匙串放在那儿了……？{w}还是说，插在锁孔里了？{w}她哑然无语，探头朝楼梯下张望。',
        "It... wasn't there. But it wasn't on the sofa either. She couldn't understand. How could her keys have disappeared with the Sekimeiya? It was utterly nonsensical. She'd looked through the sofa, the suitcase, and all her pockets; they really weren't anywhere.": '钥匙……不在那儿。可沙发上也没有。{w}她想不通。钥匙怎么会跟 Sekimeiya 一起消失？这根本说不通。{w}沙发、行李箱、所有口袋她都翻遍了，就是哪儿都找不到。',
        "She'd intended to keep the Sekimeiya in a safe place, but somehow, she'd failed. Completely lost, she wondered what to do. More people were on the crystal floor, and they could have already woken up.": '她本想把 Sekimeiya 藏到稳妥的地方，结果却不知怎么没能做到。她茫然无措，不知该如何是好。{w}水晶层上还有不少人，他们或许已经醒了。',
        "However... she couldn't leave. Without the key, she couldn't unlock the door she'd just locked, so she pressed the elevator button. ...But nothing happened.": '可是……她走不了。钥匙不在手上，刚锁上的门就打不开，于是她按下电梯按钮。{w}……然而毫无反应。',
        "My body crumpled down; I couldn't keep going.": '{w=0.6}我双腿一软，再也支撑不住。',
        "I tried to continue yelling her name, but my voice broke. She'd known what would happen and hadn't warned us. She'd kept waiting at our side, bolstering our hope, until she'd run away. Why...!? She would never have done that... I couldn't let a single day change my view of her.": '我还想继续喊她的名字，喉咙却发不出声。她明明知道会发生什么，却什么都没提醒我们。她一直守在我们身边，为我们打气，直到最后独自逃走。{w}为什么……！？她不可能做出这种事……我不能因为这一天就改变对她的看法。',
        'I—Isla? Where...?': '我——{w=0.4}Isla？{w=0.5}这是哪儿……？',
        "I entered the crystal room. Although I knew its walls were stained dark, I couldn't differentiate them from the rest. I stepped to the cabinet where Isla rested and reached my hand inside. ...She wasn't there.": '我走进水晶展室。我知道墙上染着大片暗色，却分不清那些痕迹和周围有什么不同。{w}我走向 Isla 躺着的展示柜，把手伸了进去。{w}……她不在。',
        "Y-You're right... She was here just minutes ago.": '你、你说得对……{w}几分钟前她明明还在这儿。',
        'I followed Sai out. Utterly lost, we went to check the bathrooms.': '我跟着 Sai 走了出去。{w}我们全无头绪，只好去查看洗手间。',
        "We ran to the crystal room where we'd found her first body. It wasn't there. The curtain wasn't on the floor either.": '我们跑到当初发现她那具遗体的水晶展室。{w}遗体不见了。地上的遮布也不见了。',
        "And it wasn't only the bodies. We had thought that if the exit didn't unlock at 21:00, we would let the others listen to the recording. However, that could no longer happen; the recorder itself had certainly vanished alongside Isla.": '而且不见的不只是遗体。我们本来打算，如果到了 {time=21} 出口仍未解锁，就让其他人听那段录音。可这件事已经办不到了——录音笔一定也和 Isla 一起消失了。',
        "And it wasn't only the bodies. We had thought that if the exit didn't unlock at 9 p.m., we would let the others listen to the recording. However, that could no longer happen; the recorder itself had certainly vanished alongside Isla.": '而且不见的不只是遗体。我们本来打算，如果到了 {time=21} 出口仍未解锁，就让其他人听那段录音。可这件事已经办不到了——录音笔一定也和 Isla 一起消失了。',
        'Why was I the only one to not see that...? Could that indicate what happened? Shiroya ran to hallway B and told us to not follow her. Was she going to the Sekimeiya in the cabinet? Then, out of nowhere, the lights went off, and the shutter remained unmoving.': '为什么只有我没看见……？那会不会恰好说明了什么？{w} Shiroya 跑向 B走廊，还叫我们别跟过去。她是要去取展示柜里的 Sekimeiya 吗？{w} 紧接着灯光毫无征兆地熄灭，卷帘门也始终没有动。',
        '...Y-Yes.': '……{w}是、是的。',
        '...The light breakers are there. Did you turn them off? What the hell happened to your finger?': '……{w}照明电闸就在那儿。是你关的吗？你的手指到底怎么了？',
        '"Don\'t forget what I said... I meant all of it." If she\'s not here anymore, then who did this? It can\'t be just a coincidence that Erina left our side minutes before the shutter was going to open.': '「别忘了我说过的话……每一句我都是认真的。」{w} 如果她已经不在了，那这事又是谁做的？卷帘门就要打开的前几分钟，Erina 偏偏离开了我们身边，这不可能只是巧合。',
        '"Now stay here, and don\'t follow me." Why!? Why did I have to stay there!? Leaving the tower with Shiroya was the only thing I wanted—it was the only thing both of us wanted!': '「待在这里，别跟过来。」{w} 为什么！？为什么我非得留在那儿不可！？和 Shiroya 一起离开这座塔，是我唯一的心愿——也是我们两人唯一的心愿！',
        "He found the button on the wall and pressed it. A while later, it still hadn't lit up.": '他摸到墙上的按钮，按了下去。{w} 过了好一会儿，按钮依旧没有亮起。',
        "Unless it's open on another floor, the elevator is disabled too. I didn't want to use it, though. Let's take the stairs.": '除非它停在别的楼层开着门，否则电梯也不能用了。{w} 不过我本来也不想坐它。走楼梯吧。',
        '...Wh-What the...? What happened to the lights?': '……怎、怎么回事？{w} 灯怎么了？',
        'Perhaps you would like to prove yourself as well. You will have the chance to do that. Show that the peak is also awaiting you—that the keys you were given were put to use.': '或许你也想证明自己。你会有这个机会的。{w} 去证明顶峰同样在等着你——证明交到你手上的那些钥匙都已派上用场。',
        "Of course we are, and it's past 21:00! The shutter didn't open!": '我们当然还在，而且现在已经过了{time=21}！卷帘门没有打开！',
        "Of course we are, and it's past 9 p.m.! The shutter didn't open!": '我们当然还在，而且现在已经过了{time=21}！卷帘门没有打开！',
        "You son of a bitch! He punched me in the stomach! I was knocked out, and when I woke up, I couldn't even stand up straight!": '你这王八蛋！他朝我肚子打了一拳！{w}我被打昏过去，醒来后连站都站不直！',
        'Yes, but she was here again! Sai, why did you go quiet!? You saw her as well!': '对，可她又在这里了！{w}Sai，你怎么不说话了！？你也看见她了！',
        "...I don't know what happened. She was alive when we left the attic. We talked to her, but she didn't remember anything about what had happened. After this son of a bitch knocked me out, I wasn't able to find her again.": '……{w}我不知道发生了什么。{w}我们离开阁楼时，她还活着。我们跟她说过话，可她对之前发生的事一点印象都没有。这个王八蛋把我打昏之后，我就再也没找到她。',
        "...Can you please answer me? Why are the lights off!? There's no way it's {time=21.}": '……{w}能不能回答我？灯到底为什么灭了！？现在不可能是{time=21.}吧。',
        "...{w}Can you please answer me? Why are the lights off!? There's no way it's 21:00.": '……{w}能不能回答我？灯到底为什么灭了！？现在不可能是{time=21.}吧。',
        "...Can you please answer me? Why are the lights off!? There's no way it's 21:00.": '……{w}能不能回答我？灯到底为什么灭了！？现在不可能是{time=21.}吧。',
        "...{w}Can you please answer me? Why are the lights off!? There's no way it's 9 p.m.": '……{w}能不能回答我？灯到底为什么灭了！？现在不可能是{time=21.}吧。',
        "...Can you please answer me? Why are the lights off!? There's no way it's 9 p.m.": '……{w}能不能回答我？灯到底为什么灭了！？现在不可能是{time=21.}吧。',
        "It's 21:12, dumbass! And we don't know what happened! The lights went off just minutes before the shutter was gonna open, and we have no idea why!": '现在是{time=21:12}，蠢货！而且我们也不知道发生了什么！卷帘门本来再过几分钟就要打开，灯却灭了，我们根本不知道为什么！',
        "It's 9:12 p.m., dumbass! And we don't know what happened! The lights went off just minutes before the shutter was gonna open, and we have no idea why!": '现在是{time=21:12}，蠢货！而且我们也不知道发生了什么！卷帘门本来再过几分钟就要打开，灯却灭了，我们根本不知道为什么！',
        "That was why Akaro's story was unbelievable. Had he traveled... to the future? Was that possible? Even if it was, his appearance didn't make sense. Something had happened at {time=21} that went against the normal flow of time. I didn't think that Akaro could've simply traveled forward in time to appear where we were.": '所以 Akaro 的话才让人难以置信。他……穿越到了未来？这可能吗？{w}就算可能，他出现在这里也说不通。{time=21}时一定发生了什么违背正常时间流动的事。我不觉得 Akaro 只是单纯穿越到未来，然后出现在我们面前。',
        "That was why Akaro's story was unbelievable. Had he traveled... to the future? Was that possible?{w} Even if it was, his appearance didn't make sense. Something had happened at 21:00 that went against the normal flow of time. I didn't think that Akaro could've simply traveled forward in time to appear where we were.": '所以 Akaro 的话才让人难以置信。他……穿越到了未来？这可能吗？{w}就算可能，他出现在这里也说不通。{time=21}时一定发生了什么违背正常时间流动的事。我不觉得 Akaro 只是单纯穿越到未来，然后出现在我们面前。',
        "That was why Akaro's story was unbelievable. Had he traveled... to the future? Was that possible? Even if it was, his appearance didn't make sense. Something had happened at 21:00 that went against the normal flow of time. I didn't think that Akaro could've simply traveled forward in time to appear where we were.": '所以 Akaro 的话才让人难以置信。他……穿越到了未来？这可能吗？{w}就算可能，他出现在这里也说不通。{time=21}时一定发生了什么违背正常时间流动的事。我不觉得 Akaro 只是单纯穿越到未来，然后出现在我们面前。',
        "That was why Akaro's story was unbelievable. Had he traveled... to the future? Was that possible?{w} Even if it was, his appearance didn't make sense. Something had happened at 9 p.m. that went against the normal flow of time. I didn't think that Akaro could've simply traveled forward in time to appear where we were.": '所以 Akaro 的话才让人难以置信。他……穿越到了未来？这可能吗？{w}就算可能，他出现在这里也说不通。{time=21}时一定发生了什么违背正常时间流动的事。我不觉得 Akaro 只是单纯穿越到未来，然后出现在我们面前。',
        "That was why Akaro's story was unbelievable. Had he traveled... to the future? Was that possible? Even if it was, his appearance didn't make sense. Something had happened at 9 p.m. that went against the normal flow of time. I didn't think that Akaro could've simply traveled forward in time to appear where we were.": '所以 Akaro 的话才让人难以置信。他……穿越到了未来？这可能吗？{w}就算可能，他出现在这里也说不通。{time=21}时一定发生了什么违背正常时间流动的事。我不觉得 Akaro 只是单纯穿越到未来，然后出现在我们面前。',
        'Wait a second! What the fuck are... these clothes?': '等一下！这他妈……{w}是什么衣服？',
        "These clothes...? I... think so. They're not the ones I had on, though!": '这些衣服……？{w}我……应该是吧。可这不是我原来穿的那套！',
        "You're really saying the shutter is still there...? We're in hallway C, right?": '你是说，卷帘门真的还在……？{w}这里是C走廊，对吧？',
        'It is... It really is still here. Is it actually after {time=21}? What the fuck do we do, then!?': '确实……卷帘门确实还在。{w}现在真的过了{time=21}吗？那我们他妈该怎么办！？',
        'It is... It really is still here.{w} Is it actually after 21:00? What the fuck do we do, then!?': '确实……卷帘门确实还在。{w}现在真的过了{time=21}吗？那我们他妈该怎么办！？',
        'It is... It really is still here. Is it actually after 21:00? What the fuck do we do, then!?': '确实……卷帘门确实还在。{w}现在真的过了{time=21}吗？那我们他妈该怎么办！？',
        'It is... It really is still here.{w} Is it actually after 9 p.m.? What the fuck do we do, then!?': '确实……卷帘门确实还在。{w}现在真的过了{time=21}吗？那我们他妈该怎么办！？',
        'It is... It really is still here. Is it actually after 9 p.m.? What the fuck do we do, then!?': '确实……卷帘门确实还在。{w}现在真的过了{time=21}吗？那我们他妈该怎么办！？',
        "Despite being aware of another option for so long, there was another choice. We had the Sekimeiya. We could travel through time. According to Akaro, he had traveled hours forward, so nothing said we couldn't escape the tower with it. The reason I hadn't explored that option yet was what Shiroya had said. Due to her, I wasn't sure that trying to escape from the dark tower was what I had to do. However, Sai and Akaro weren't even discussing the Sekimeiya. Supposedly, Akaro had just appeared, and he hadn't even asked about its whereabouts.": '我明明早就知道还有另一个选择，却一直没去走。我们手里有 Sekimeiya。{w}我们可以穿越时间。据 Akaro 说，他曾穿越到几小时之后，那靠它逃出塔也并非不可能。{w}我之所以迟迟没考虑这条路，是因为 Shiroya 的那番话。因为她，我不确定自己是否该设法逃出这座黑暗的塔。可 Sai 和 Akaro 却连提都没提 Sekimeiya。Akaro 才刚出现，甚至没问过它在哪儿。',
        "You're the one spewing nonsense! Why would the exit not unlock!? One of you killed Katei, right? Who was it!? And what, the bodies disappeared? Have you searched for them? We know the Sekimeiya doesn't make them vanish, right? Is it even in the cabinet?": '说胡话的是你吧！出口怎么会解不开锁！？Katei 是你们当中某个人杀的，对不对？到底是谁！？{w} 还有，尸体消失了？你们找过没有？Sekimeiya 不会让人凭空消失，这我们总该知道吧？它到底在不在展示柜里？',
        "...Yes. And we were planning to search through the higher floors. We don't even know if the lights went off up there, but the elevator doesn't work, and the security room is locked for some reason.": '……是。{w} 况且我们本来就打算搜上面几层。上面灯有没有灭，我们也不清楚，可电梯用不了，监控室不知怎么还锁着。',
        "Shut the fuck up! If you're telling the truth, we've been here twice as long as you! Let's just go up. We can hope there's still light somewhere.": '你他妈闭嘴！如果你说的是真的，我们在这儿待的时间是你的两倍！{w} 先上去再说。只能指望哪儿还亮着灯。',
        "That put the discussion on pause. I couldn't believe my legs were still obeying me, but I proceeded up the stairs. Was there anything to find? ...Shiroya? Maybe Isla...? I had moved beyond taking things for granted.": '争论就此打住。我的腿居然还听使唤，连我自己都不敢相信，可我还是顺着楼梯往上走。{w} 能找到什么吗？……Shiroya？也许是 Isla……？我已经不敢再把任何事当作理所当然。',
        "Gripping the handrail, we went up the stairs step by step. On the third floor, I wondered if we would even be able to step into the attic. Perhaps Sai had a second key, but the original one should've been in the inner keyhole, and it could've already been taken.": '我们抓着扶手，一级一级往上走。{w} 到了三楼，我开始担心我们究竟进不进得了阁楼。也许 Sai 还有另一把钥匙，可原来那把应该插在内侧的锁孔里，说不定已经被人取走了。',
        'Then, he saw that the inner handle of the right bedroom was unattached, like it had been minutes prior. Confused, he stepped out.': '接着，他发现右侧卧室内侧的门把手脱落了，像是几分钟前才掉的。{w} 他满心疑惑，退了出来。',
        "In the right bedroom, Atsuki noticed that the inner handle was unattached, like it had been minutes prior. He had seen that in the living room, the footprints they'd just left had been the only ones. It was very strange; fainter ones should've been there as well.": '在右侧卧室里，Atsuki 发现内侧的门把手脱落了，像是几分钟前才掉的。{w} 他先前在客厅已经看到，地上只有他们刚留下的脚印。这非常奇怪——本该还有更浅的脚印才对。',
        "There was a glass next to the sink. I recognized it—when I'd been with Shiroya, I had tried to drink tap water. It had tasted terrible, and I'd set it aside.": '水槽边放着一只杯子。{w} 我认得它——和 Shiroya 在一起的时候，我曾试着喝自来水。那水难喝得要命，我就把杯子搁到了一边。',
        "...It is, I'm pretty sure.": '……{w}有可能，我很确定。',
        "...But there are no other footprints in the living room. The ones we left just a while ago should be visible. And there's no way we went to the past because the handle in the right bedroom is on the floor.": '……{w}可客厅里没有别的脚印。我们刚才留下的那些，本来应该还看得见才对。{w}而且我们也不可能回到过去——右边卧室的门把手还掉在地上。',
        "There are plenty of things unaccounted for. Who activated this future travel, and why? Why did we go so far into the future? Why are the lights off? What was the flash Erina and I saw? And why did it not feel like we traveled? We didn't change places, did we?": '解释不通的地方还多着呢。{w}是谁启动了这次穿越，目的又是什么？为什么一下子去了那么远的未来？{w}为什么灯是灭的？{w}我和 Erina 看到的那道闪光是什么？还有，为什么我们完全没有穿越的感觉？我们并没有换地方，对吧？',
        'Sai was right. If we were in the future, all of those questions had to be answered. However, others would be resolved. Spending a month in the tower without any source of food was no longer necessarily a problem.': 'Sai 说得对。如果我们真的身处未来，那些问题就都必须有答案。{w}可反过来，另一些问题也会迎刃而解。{w}在没有任何食物来源的塔里待上一个月，也就不一定是死局了。',
        "Yeah, let's go shack up somewhere for a few dozen more hours just in case the shutter opens some day. Who knows if Shiroya is gonna send us another month forward a minute before they unlock, though. I'm starving, by the way. Think I'll pass out any time now.": '是啊，那就找个地方再窝上几十个小时，万一哪天卷帘门开了呢。不过话又说回来，谁知道 Shiroya 会不会在他们开锁前一分钟，又把我们送到一个月之后。{w}顺带一提，我快饿死了。感觉随时都会昏过去。',
        'Before anyone could reply, Sai departed to the living room. He was followed by everyone but me.': '还没等人答话，Sai 已经往客厅去了。{w}除了我，所有人都跟了上去。',
        "If something like that is what happened, Shiroya knew about it... She didn't say anything about it—only that she meant everything she'd said.": '如果真是那样，Shiroya 是知道的……{w}可她一个字也没提，只说她说过的每句话都是认真的。',
        "And the security room is locked, so we can't see the date on the computer. Is this what Shiroya wanted? Did she want this to happen for a reason...? Everything she said in hallway C... She already knew about this.": '而且监控室锁着，看不到电脑上的日期。{w}这就是 Shiroya 想要的结果吗？她希望这种事发生，是有原因的吗……？{w}她在 C走廊说的那些话……她早就知道会这样。',
        'What happened to the real Shiroya...? To the one who went to the bathroom. Did she touch the Sekimeiya in the water tank? If so, where is she now? Could she eventually have become the other Shiroya...?': '真正的 Shiroya 后来怎么样了……？我是说去洗手间的那个。{w}她碰过水箱里的 Sekimeiya 吗？如果碰过，她现在又在哪儿？她会不会最终变成了另一个 Shiroya……？',
        "Is it random, like the replicated location? I suppose it can't be random if someone made us travel forward in time deliberately, but what exactly caused it?": '难道像复制出来的地点一样，是随机的？{w}可如果是有人刻意让我们穿越到未来，那就不该是随机的。那么，究竟是什么触发了它？',
        'Before we even heard the sound, Erina and I turned to the door. Then, it opened further, followed by gasps.': '还没听见声响，我和 Erina 就已转头望向门口。{w}紧接着，门又开大了些，随之响起几声惊呼。',
        'From the door, Isla looked at all of us. She seemed to be searching for something. However, she paid no mind to our perplexed faces and kept scanning the room.': 'Isla 站在门口，目光逐一扫过我们。她像是在找什么。{w}可她对我们的满脸困惑视若无睹，仍旧扫视着房间。',
        'On the floor, both of them wept. The recording... it had always been genuine. I finally understood its context, but even that understanding brought an immense number of questions along with it.': '两人就那样跪坐在地上痛哭。{w}那段录音……从来都是真的。我终于明白了它的来龙去脉，但明白之后，反而冒出了更多疑问。',
        "N-No! Not to me! To Isla! Why isn't she here!?": '不、不是！不是问我！是问 Isla！{w}她为什么不在这里！？',
        'This is the friend we were told about. She\'s searching for the Isla we knew. I have no idea how this came to happen, but this Isla is the person that "my" Isla mentioned.': '她就是别人跟我们提过的那位朋友。她在找我们认识的那个 Isla。{w}我不知道事情怎么会变成这样，但这位 Isla，正是「我那个」Isla 提过的人。',
        'Isla, this is very important. What day is it? Do you know that?': 'Isla，这件事很要紧。{w}今天是几号？你知道吗？',
        "Shiroya...? We don't know where she is. Do you? Should she be here?": 'Shiroya……？我们不知道她在哪儿。{w}你知道吗？她应该在这里吗？',
        "So she did. I actually found that in the security room a while ago. I didn't know what it was for until I found something else, a bug Atsuki hid in a coat pocket in one of the lockers.": '果然如此。{w}其实那东西是我先前在监控室找到的。起初我不知道它有什么用，直到后来在某个储物柜的一件外套口袋里，发现了 Atsuki 藏的窃听器。',
        "...Really? Well, unfortunately, I found the bug late into the day, but I figured the device I'd found earlier could receive its audio. I thought this was a good occasion to use it, what with Akaro's story being questionable as hell. His clothes changed, and he was out of the tower for a long time. That's why I just placed the bug on him and started recording. I wanted to know if he had a way to exit the building.": '……真的？唉，不巧的是，我发现窃听器时这天已经过去大半了。不过我想，之前找到的那台设备应该能接收它的音频。{w}Akaro 的说辞疑点太多，我觉得正好可以借此一用。他的衣服换了，又离开塔很长时间。所以我就把窃听器放到他身上，开始录音。我想知道他有没有离开这栋楼的办法。',
        "Calm down. Did you really not realize it? It's behind your neck. To be honest, I was also curious about something else. I've still got no explanation for a lot of things that occurred, and I've thought for a while that one of us might travel far to the past to carry out their plan. If that person happened to be Akaro, I hoped that when I pressed the play button, two recordings would show up at once. That would've immediately exposed him, but it didn't happen. I suppose that doesn't matter anymore since he's aware of the bug.": '冷静点。你真没察觉到？就在你脖子后面。{w}说实话，我还有另一件事想弄清楚。发生的许多事我至今都解释不了，而且我早就想过，我们之中或许有人会穿越到很久以前去执行自己的计划。如果那个人恰好是 Akaro，我希望按下播放键时能同时出现两段录音，那样就能当场揭穿他——可惜没有。不过既然他已经知道窃听器的事，这些也无所谓了。',
        "Erina's voice sounded concerned, and I knew why. Isla's right hand was a fist; she was holding something. But she shook her head in fear.": 'Erina 的声音里透着担忧，我知道缘由。Isla 的右手握成拳，手里攥着什么。{w}可她却害怕地摇了摇头。',
        'I... I followed her steps.': '我……{w}我是跟着她的脚步来的。',
        'Wait, what!? Is that door open!?': '等等，什么！？{w}那扇门开着吗！？',
        "Wait a second... I might understand our misconception. Somehow, we traveled days into the future, and the shutter was still here. That's what led us to think it never opened.": '等等……{w}我大概明白我们哪里想错了。{w}我们不知怎么穿越到了几天之后，而卷帘门还留在原处。所以我们才以为它从没打开过。',
        "That's not it, though...! It actually opened minutes after we vanished from the 15th. Long after that, it was closed again. That's why the security room is locked and the elevator isn't working. Those are the alarm's effects—we were trapped for a second time. That's why the corpses are gone!": '可并不是这样……！其实，就在我们从 15 日消失几分钟后，它打开过。{w}很久之后，它才再次关闭。所以监控室才锁着，电梯也不动了。这都是警报造成的——我们第二次被困在了里面。尸体不见了也是因为这个！',
        '...Hm. Someone had to be here.': '……{w}唔。当时这里一定有人。',
        "Oh. I know when it happened! I can't believe I didn't realize it, but it happened immediately before our arrival on this day!": '啊。{w}我知道那是什么时候了！真不敢相信我居然没意识到——那件事就发生在我们抵达这一天的前一刻！',
        "Someone had been there right as the group had appeared on January 5th. Atsuki knew that thanks to the last time he'd been in...": '就在一行人 1 月 5 日出现的那一刻，那里已经有人了。{w}Atsuki 之所以知道，是因为他上一次待在里面的时候……',
        "Although it was kept cold, the Sekimeiya was powered off. It had been used moments prior! How can it be that it was powered off within the cabinet? When the cold hit it, it always regained its glow immediately. The glass was partly open, cooling down the whole room. Was it due to that single detail? Or was it something else? If I'm not mistaken, the longer the travel, the longer the Sekimeiya spends powered off...": '虽然一直被冷藏，Sekimeiya 却处于断电状态。它不久前刚被用过！{w}怎么会在展示柜里就断了电？每次一遇冷，它总会立刻重新亮起。{w}玻璃半开着，整个房间都冷了下来。是因为这个吗？{w}还是另有原因？如果我没记错，穿越的时间跨度越长，Sekimeiya 断电的时间就越久……',
        'I walked out of the bedroom. Everyone else had already gone down.': '我走出卧室。{w}其他人都已经下楼了。',
        "Attentively walking through the darkness, I reached the crystal floor. I heard knocks and voices coming from the storeroom; it appeared Isla hadn't thought to keep the door open. Perhaps she hadn't been aware of the missing handle. Without making a sound, I slowly tiptoed to the event room.": '我小心地穿过黑暗，来到水晶层。{w}储藏室那边传来敲击声和人声；看来 Isla 没想到要让门开着。也许她并不知道门把手不见了。{w}我悄无声息，慢慢踮脚走向活动室。',
        'I just want to go a little while back. It should be simple. This room is pretty cold, so it might not be a good idea to stay here if I want the Sekimeiya to gather energy.': '我只想回到不久之前。这应该很简单。{w}这房间太冷了，想让 Sekimeiya 积蓄能量的话，待在这里恐怕不合适。',
        "The lights went off when Sai's watch read {time=21:03.} I need to arrive before that point, and now his watch must say almost {time=21:20.} I need to leave the Sekimeiya here...": 'Sai 的手表显示 {time=21:03.} 时，灯灭了。我必须在那之前抵达，而现在他的表应该快到 {time=21:20.} 了。{w}我得把 Sekimeiya 留在这里……',
        "The lights went off when Sai's watch read 21:03. I need to arrive before that point, and now his watch must say almost 21:20.{w} I need to leave the Sekimeiya here...": 'Sai 的手表显示 {time=21:03.} 时，灯灭了。我必须在那之前抵达，而现在他的表应该快到 {time=21:20.} 了。{w}我得把 Sekimeiya 留在这里……',
        "The lights went off when Sai's watch read 21:03. I need to arrive before that point, and now his watch must say almost 21:20. I need to leave the Sekimeiya here...": 'Sai 的手表显示 {time=21:03.} 时，灯灭了。我必须在那之前抵达，而现在他的表应该快到 {time=21:20.} 了。{w}我得把 Sekimeiya 留在这里……',
        "The lights went off when Sai's watch read 9:03 p.m. I need to arrive before that point, and now his watch must say almost 9:20 p.m.{w} I need to leave the Sekimeiya here...": 'Sai 的手表显示 {time=21:03.} 时，灯灭了。我必须在那之前抵达，而现在他的表应该快到 {time=21:20.} 了。{w}我得把 Sekimeiya 留在这里……',
        "The lights went off when Sai's watch read 9:03 p.m. I need to arrive before that point, and now his watch must say almost 9:20 p.m. I need to leave the Sekimeiya here...": 'Sai 的手表显示 {time=21:03.} 时，灯灭了。我必须在那之前抵达，而现在他的表应该快到 {time=21:20.} 了。{w}我得把 Sekimeiya 留在这里……',
        "If I wait for 10 minutes, I doubt I'll be able to go back 30 minutes at 21:30.": '如果等上 10 分钟，到 {time=21:30.} 时，我恐怕没法回到 30 分钟前。',
        "If I wait for 10 minutes, I doubt I'll be able to go back 30 minutes at 9:30 p.m.": '如果等上 10 分钟，到 {time=21:30.} 时，我恐怕没法回到 30 分钟前。',
        "If I wait for 15 minutes, I doubt I'll be able to go back 35 minutes at 21:35.": '如果等上 15 分钟，到 {time=21:35.} 时，我恐怕没法回到 35 分钟前。',
        "If I wait for 15 minutes, I doubt I'll be able to go back 35 minutes at 9:35 p.m.": '如果等上 15 分钟，到 {time=21:35.} 时，我恐怕没法回到 35 分钟前。',
        "If I wait for 20 minutes, I doubt I'll be able to go back 40 minutes at 21:40.": '如果等上 20 分钟，到 {time=21:40.} 时，我恐怕没法回到 40 分钟前。',
        "If I wait for 20 minutes, I doubt I'll be able to go back 40 minutes at 9:40 p.m.": '如果等上 20 分钟，到 {time=21:40.} 时，我恐怕没法回到 40 分钟前。',
        "I'd say for about 25 minutes, so that at {time=21:45} I can travel 45 minutes back. I think that's it, based on all the travels, and especially everything that I just learned. I don't have a way to measure the time by myself, though.": '我看等 25 分钟左右正好，这样到 {time=21:45} 时，我就能回到 45 分钟前。根据之前所有的穿越，尤其是刚刚弄明白的这些，我想就是这样。{w}只是我没法自己计时。',
        "I'd say for about 25 minutes, so that at 21:45 I can travel 45 minutes back. I think that's it, based on all the travels, and especially everything that I just learned.{w} I don't have a way to measure the time by myself, though.": '我看等 25 分钟左右正好，这样到 {time=21:45} 时，我就能回到 45 分钟前。根据之前所有的穿越，尤其是刚刚弄明白的这些，我想就是这样。{w}只是我没法自己计时。',
        "I'd say for about 25 minutes, so that at 21:45 I can travel 45 minutes back. I think that's it, based on all the travels, and especially everything that I just learned. I don't have a way to measure the time by myself, though.": '我看等 25 分钟左右正好，这样到 {time=21:45} 时，我就能回到 45 分钟前。根据之前所有的穿越，尤其是刚刚弄明白的这些，我想就是这样。{w}只是我没法自己计时。',
        "I'd say for about 25 minutes, so that at 9:45 p.m. I can travel 45 minutes back. I think that's it, based on all the travels, and especially everything that I just learned.{w} I don't have a way to measure the time by myself, though.": '我看等 25 分钟左右正好，这样到 {time=21:45} 时，我就能回到 45 分钟前。根据之前所有的穿越，尤其是刚刚弄明白的这些，我想就是这样。{w}只是我没法自己计时。',
        "I'd say for about 25 minutes, so that at 9:45 p.m. I can travel 45 minutes back. I think that's it, based on all the travels, and especially everything that I just learned. I don't have a way to measure the time by myself, though.": '我看等 25 分钟左右正好，这样到 {time=21:45} 时，我就能回到 45 分钟前。根据之前所有的穿越，尤其是刚刚弄明白的这些，我想就是这样。{w}只是我没法自己计时。',
        "Hm... I can't measure the real time, but I might have a way to measure minutes.": '嗯……{w}我没法知道确切时间，但或许有办法数出过了多少分钟。',
        "The security room is locked, so I don't think there's anything on the crystal floor that isn't Sai's watch. There are a bunch of computers on the office floors, but I need access information to look at the time. I can only think of the kitchen in the attic. The refrigerator was working, so the oven should be too. There's still electricity, so I should be able to count the minutes that pass with that.": '监控室锁着，水晶层上除了 Sai 的手表，我想不出还有什么能看时间。办公楼层倒是有一堆电脑，可要查看时间就得有登录信息。{w}我能想到的就只有阁楼的厨房了。{w}冰箱还在运转，烤箱应该也没问题。电还没断，用它来计时应该可行。',
        'Two floors down, I stopped abruptly. The others were making their way up. I took a step aside and hushed my breathing. Unaware that I was there, they passed me by.': '下了两层，我猛地停住脚步。其他人正往上走。{w}我侧身让到一旁，屏住呼吸。他们没察觉到我，就从我身旁经过。',
        "The Sekimeiya was still behind room B5's door. I felt it through my sleeve and instantly determined that it had built up considerable energy. I had to quickly withdraw my hand to avoid harm.": 'Sekimeiya 还在 B5 展室的门后。{w}我隔着袖子碰了碰它，立刻发觉它已经积蓄了相当多的能量。为了不被伤到，我赶紧把手缩了回来。',
        '...Did I... change places?': '……{w}我……换了个地方？',
        'However, when I tried to open the door, it was still locked. I had also been assaulted by a wave of tiredness and wished to lie down. Suddenly, a sharp sound echoed in my ears. ...Had it come from hallway B?': '然而，我试着开门时，门依旧锁着。同时一阵强烈的倦意袭来，让我只想躺下。{w}忽然，一声尖锐的声响在耳边回荡。……是从 B走廊传来的吗？',
        "...I stopped still. No sound could be heard anymore. I didn't know what to do, and I was more than a little afraid. If that was the person who'd killed everyone, I was finally in real danger—the recording had guaranteed my safety for a long time, but it had become a past event, and the promise of my well-being had expired.": '……{w}我僵在原地。四周再听不到任何声响。{w}我不知所措，心里不止一点害怕。如果那就是杀死了所有人的凶手，我终于真正身处险境了——那段录音曾在很长一段时间里保证我的安全，可它已经成了过去的事，那份保我平安的承诺也早已失效。',
        'Huh? What...?': '咦？{w}什么……？',
        'If this is Shiroya, she came in from the storeroom! Isla seemed like she entered the tower by following her steps. If Isla was able to enter from the outside, the door was open. I might be able to leave right now...!': '如果这是 Shiroya，那她就是从储藏室进来的！Isla 似乎就是顺着她的踪迹进了塔。{w} 既然 Isla 能从外面进来，说明那扇门开着。我现在说不定就能出去……！',
        'One, two, three, four, five.': '一，{w=0.6}二，{w=0.6}三，{w=0.6}四，{w=0.6}五。',
        'Could we have been back at the beginning? Before asking anything else, I got closer to the hallway. A sound from the other side caused me to stop; a door had closed.': '难道我们回到了起点？我还没来得及多问，便朝走廊走近。{w} 对面传来一声响，我立刻停住——有扇门关上了。',
        "I couldn't believe it. I'd been so close to escaping, but it hadn't been permitted. I had no idea what was ahead of me anymore, but the tower held me in its grip like a python. I lowered my head and saw my own hand. Exposed to the light, I could see the injury was still gone. Then, I noticed something else—I wasn't hungry or tired anymore. Those sensations had also disappeared.": '我简直无法相信。明明只差一步就能逃出去，却终究没能如愿。前方还会发生什么，我全然不知，而这座塔像蟒蛇一样死死缠住我。{w} 我低下头，看见自己的手。借着光，我看出那道伤依然不见踪影。{w} 接着我又发现了一件事——我不再饥饿，也不再疲惫。那些感觉同样消失了。',
        "It had to be that one, then. That's where Naomi died and where I traveled for the first time. If the smoke was just released, someone might have just been there because it's where the temperature regulation cabinets are.": '那就只能是那扇门了。{w}Naomi 就是在那儿死的，我也是在那儿第一次穿越的。如果烟雾才刚放出来，那说不定有人刚去过那里——毕竟控温展示柜就放在那儿。',
        "Were we really at the beginning, just like that? It didn't make any sense; if we had always been present, we would've been found on many occasions. Were we going to change the past? I really wanted Shiroya to be telling the truth. If she was, we would get through everything, but I knew she had withheld the truth from me before.": '我们真的就这么回到了最初？这说不通——如果我们一直都在，早就该被人撞见很多次了。{w}我们是要改变过去吗？我真心希望 Shiroya 说的是实话。如果她说的是真的，我们就能挺过一切；可我知道，她以前也瞒过我。',
        "I couldn't hesitate. The real culprit, the person who had removed the storeroom's handle, could have been present. Low to the ground, I scurried to the crystal room. I turned to Shiroya, who was following me. At that point, I noticed something intriguing, but I couldn't stop there.": '我不能犹豫。真正的犯人——那个卸下储藏室门把手的人——可能就在那里。我压低身子，快步溜向水晶展室。{w}我回头看向跟在身后的 Shiroya。那一刻，我注意到一件耐人寻味的事，却没法停下脚步。',
        "But it was impossible for me to think she was lying; her voice sounded as sincere as always. When I'd activated the Sekimeiya from room B5... had I perhaps traveled to the first days of December? I was stumped. If she was telling the truth, I couldn't explain what had happened to me.": '可要我认定她在说谎，我做不到——她的声音一如既往地真诚。{w}当我在水晶展室 B5 启动 Sekimeiya 时……莫非我穿越到了 12 月初？{w}我陷入了困惑。如果她说的是真的，那我就无法解释自己身上发生的事。',
        "Yes, it did happen. It wasn't a trick. It still doesn't make any sense, though. I can't wrap my head around what happened.": '对，那确实发生了。不是障眼法。{w}可我还是想不通。这件事我怎么想也想不明白。',
        'I nodded and got close to her. Slowly, my hand reached for the Sekimeiya in defiance of the burning aura around it. However, the instant I contacted the gemstone, it vanished.': '我点点头，凑近她，顶着那股灼人的热浪，慢慢把手伸向 Sekimeiya。{w} 可就在指尖触到宝石的一瞬间，它消失了。',
        "She denied it; the cabinet had closed without making a sound. Could we have traveled back in time to a point before I'd unlocked it? In that case, why hadn't we teleported?": '她摇头否认。展示柜无声无息地合上了。{w} 难道我们穿越到了我打开它之前？可那样的话，为什么没有被传送？',
        'However, those rapid footsteps were still audible in the distance. It had to be the person responsible for our imprisonment...! We ran behind the sound, covering our faces.': '可是远处仍能听见那急促的脚步声。那一定就是把我们关在这里的人……！{w} 我们掩住脸，循着声音追了上去。',
        'As expected, the attic door was locked. Had it been Naomi? She was the one with the key.': '果然，阁楼的门锁上了。{w} 是 Naomi 吗？钥匙在她手上。',
        'When she reached the top, Shiroya peeked through the small gap between the door and wall. Then, she turned to me.': '到了顶端，Shiroya 从门与墙之间的细缝往里窥看。{w} 随后，她转向我。',
        "But something was on the sofa that left me dazed. Two Sekimeiya were there, and one of them was powered off. Next to them, I saw a set of keys. ...It was Naomi's.": '可沙发上的东西让我怔住了。那里放着两个 Sekimeiya，其中一个已经关闭。{w} 旁边还有一串钥匙。……是 Naomi 的。',
        "Wait, no... Shiroya couldn't have gone to the past. If she had, she would've shown up immediately after her disappearance, right? Could she have gone to the future...? Is that really possible?": '等等，不对……Shiroya 不可能回到过去。{w} 如果去了过去，她应该刚一消失就立刻出现，不是吗？{w} 难道她去了未来……？那种事真的可能吗？',
        "...And Naomi was definitely here. Why did she run up to the attic with the Sekimeiya, just to travel through time? She didn't know we'd unlocked the way in, so she might think she locked the Sekimeiya in here. ...Which is strange. After all, the attic was locked when we first came across the door.": '……而且 Naomi 确实来过这里。她带着 Sekimeiya 跑上阁楼，难道就是为了穿越时间？{w}她不知道我们已经打开了入口，说不定以为把 Sekimeiya 锁在这里就安全了。{w}……可这说不通。毕竟我们第一次撞见那扇门时，阁楼还是锁着的。',
        "I don't get it...! The Sekimeiya disappeared from the crystal room, and immediately, Naomi was bringing two of them up. At the same time, another one must've been in its original cabinet. What the hell happened before we woke up? How many Sekimeiya are there...?": '我完全想不通……！Sekimeiya 刚从水晶展室消失，Naomi 转眼就搬了两个上去。而与此同时，原本的展示柜里应该还有一个。{w}我们醒来之前究竟发生了什么？Sekimeiya 到底有几个……？',
        '...Wait, is that right? Will the culprit really come in here...?': '……{w}等等，真是这样吗？{w}那个人真的会进这里来……？',
        "When we found the secret wall, a single set of fingerprints was on it, meaning that it had been opened one time in the recent past. I swear I just saw those same fingerprints right now... Does that mean that nobody will come until our past selves find the mechanism? Alternatively, what if they come from outside and won't touch the other side of the wall? ...This doesn't make any sense, though. How is it possible we only saw one set of fingerprints? What about the ones I left just now?": '我们发现暗墙的时候，上面只有一组指纹，说明前不久它被人打开过一次。可我刚才分明看见了同一组指纹……这是不是说，要等过去的我们找到机关，才会有人来？{w}又或者，对方是从外面进来的，根本不会碰到墙的另一面？{w}……可这说不通。怎么可能只有一组指纹？我刚才留下的那些又算什么？',
        "...And where in the world is Shiroya? If she somehow went to the future, she'll definitely come here when she appears. Is it possible she's outside and won't tell the police just so she can avoid changing the past...?": '……还有，Shiroya 究竟在哪里？如果她去了未来，那她出现时一定会来这里。{w}会不会她就在外面，只是为了不改变过去，才不去告诉警察……？',
        "So what exactly is going to happen? Is everything gonna be different? What about our past selves? If the past was changed somewhere, I'm no longer the other Atsuki who's currently here.": '那么接下来到底会发生什么？一切都会变得不一样吗？{w}过去的我们又该怎么办？如果过去在某处被改变，我就不再是此刻待在这里的另一个我了。',
        "If she grabbed it days ago, it wouldn't be in hallway A now. And if the world changed independent of her actions, could the key currently be in the security room? I can't try to find it before everyone wakes up because the alarm locked the room...": '如果几天前她就拿走了钥匙，那现在它就不会在 A走廊。{w}可要是世界的改变与她的行动无关，钥匙此刻会不会就在监控室里？警报把监控室锁上了，我没法赶在大家醒来之前去找……',
        "It was earlier than I'd anticipated when sound came from the hallway. From the lobby side, a group of people approached where I was.": '走廊里传来动静，比我预想的要早。{w}一群人从大厅那边朝我这边走来。',
        "Huh...? Is that everyone? This isn't what we did. We went to the security room the first time we stepped into this hallway.": '咦……？所有人都来了？{w}我们可不是这么做的。第一次踏进这条走廊时，我们是先去了监控室。',
        "If the past has already changed, no matter what I do, I'll have no direct relation to the Atsuki who just went up. ...That means my priority should be to find Shiroya, who's in the same position as me. Where could she be? If she traveled through time and another deviation occurred, she might not exist in this world anymore.": '如果过去已经被改变，那无论我再做什么，都和刚才上楼的那个 Atsuki 没有直接关系了。……也就是说，我该优先去找和我处境相同的 Shiroya。{w}她会在哪儿？如果她穿越了时间，之后又发生了一次偏差，她或许已经不存在于这个世界了。',
        "Following them, another person came from the stairs, crossing in front of the storeroom. A few seconds later, someone else did too, but they didn't enter hallway A.": '紧跟着，又有一个人从楼梯过来，从储藏室门前走过。{w}几秒后，另一个人也一样走过，却没有进 A走廊。',
        '...What the fuck just happened!? Is everyone gone again?': '……{w}刚才到底发生什么了！？所有人又都不见了吗？',
        'Oh... all the screens are off. It looks like the same thing that happened to us, where they all shut down at the same time. It seems it occurred again despite all the differences.': '哦……所有屏幕都黑着。{w}看起来和我们那时一样，全部同时熄掉了。看来尽管情况处处不同，这件事还是照样发生了。',
        "I doubt it's still here. What's most likely is that Katei has—": '我看它多半已经不在了。{w}最有可能的是，Katei 已经——',
        'This is absurd. What the fuck am I supposed to do!? Do I wait half a day here, hoping Shiroya will just appear and the exit will open? And then what? Two versions of us remain forever? ...This is insane! There has to be something we can do.': '这太荒唐了。我到底该怎么办！？{w}难道我要在这里等上半天，指望 Shiroya 自己出现、出口自己打开？{w}然后呢？我们两个就永远这样并存下去？……简直疯了！总该有我们能做的事。',
        '...I had the rusty key, so an old thought came back to me.': '……{w}手里握着那把生锈的钥匙，一个旧的念头又浮了上来。',
        '"Unless I go back to thinking about thought-up loops, I suppose. There could be something that would work. The person who killed Katei took that rusty key and walked out of the tower through the storeroom door, which was open. That created a location outside the tower where they were holding the key that could be replicated. Then, they reentered and used the Sekimeiya to go back in time. In the past, they appeared outside the tower holding the key, so they were able to unlock the door and reenter with something they\'d obtained outside—like a knife. They left the door open so that their past self could exit with the key and create the replicated location."': '「除非我又回头去琢磨那种假想出来的循环。说不定真有什么办法行得通。{w}杀死 Katei 的人拿起那把生锈的钥匙，从敞开的储藏室门走出了塔。于是，塔外就有了一个他持着钥匙的地点，而这个地点可以被复制。接着，他重新进塔，用 Sekimeiya 回到过去。在过去，他拿着钥匙出现在塔外，因此能打开门，带着从外面弄到的东西——比如一把刀——重新进来。他故意让门开着，好让过去的自己带着钥匙出去，造出那个复制地点。」',
        'I stayed on the cold floor, waiting for the door to open. It seemed the last hope that remained entailed being able to leave at {time=21.} Was that going to happen, or was I going to wait another twelve hours just to be faked out again?': '我坐在冰冷的地板上，等着门打开。仅剩的最后一点指望，似乎就是能在 {time=21.} 出去。{w}那会成真吗？还是说我又要再等上十二个小时，到头来再一次空等一场？',
        'I stayed on the cold floor, waiting for the door to open. It seemed the last hope that remained entailed being able to leave at 21:00.{w} Was that going to happen, or was I going to wait another twelve hours just to be faked out again?': '我坐在冰冷的地板上，等着门打开。仅剩的最后一点指望，似乎就是能在 {time=21.} 出去。{w}那会成真吗？还是说我又要再等上十二个小时，到头来再一次空等一场？',
        'I stayed on the cold floor, waiting for the door to open. It seemed the last hope that remained entailed being able to leave at 21:00. Was that going to happen, or was I going to wait another twelve hours just to be faked out again?': '我坐在冰冷的地板上，等着门打开。仅剩的最后一点指望，似乎就是能在 {time=21.} 出去。{w}那会成真吗？还是说我又要再等上十二个小时，到头来再一次空等一场？',
        'I stayed on the cold floor, waiting for the door to open. It seemed the last hope that remained entailed being able to leave at 9 p.m.{w} Was that going to happen, or was I going to wait another twelve hours just to be faked out again?': '我坐在冰冷的地板上，等着门打开。仅剩的最后一点指望，似乎就是能在 {time=21.} 出去。{w}那会成真吗？还是说我又要再等上十二个小时，到头来再一次空等一场？',
        'I stayed on the cold floor, waiting for the door to open. It seemed the last hope that remained entailed being able to leave at 9 p.m. Was that going to happen, or was I going to wait another twelve hours just to be faked out again?': '我坐在冰冷的地板上，等着门打开。仅剩的最后一点指望，似乎就是能在 {time=21.} 出去。{w}那会成真吗？还是说我又要再等上十二个小时，到头来再一次空等一场？',
        "When I stashed the key in my pocket, I noticed something else: another key had disappeared. ...The one that opened the locker that wasn't Naomi's. When had it disappeared? I had only just realized it, but it was a result of one of my last two travels.": '我把钥匙塞进口袋时，又注意到一件事：另一把钥匙不见了。……就是那把能打开另一个储物柜的钥匙——那个柜子不是 Naomi 的。{w}它是什么时候不见的？我直到现在才发现，但这一定是我最近两次穿越中的某一次造成的。',
        "...What about the Sekimeiya? During the prolonged silence, I considered trying to find it. Assuming two existed, obtaining a single one wasn't too hard. Nobody knew about the hidden section I was in, so I could conceal it there.": '……{w}那 Sekimeiya 呢？漫长的沉默里，我也动过找找看的念头。如果存在两个，弄到一个并不算难。没人知道我藏身的这处暗间，正好可以把它藏在那里。',
        "But I knew that would only complicate things further. Escaping the building by touching the Sekimeiya couldn't be possible; when that was supposed to occur, the Sekimeiya vanished instead. What the hell had happened at that time? Why had the cabinet's state reverted? Without a thorough understanding of the Sekimeiya's powers, I couldn't begin to use it.": '但我知道，那只会让事情更复杂。想靠触碰 Sekimeiya 逃出这栋楼根本行不通——真到了那一刻，Sekimeiya 却消失了。{w}那时候究竟发生了什么？展示柜的状态为什么会恢复原样？不把 Sekimeiya 的力量彻底弄清楚，我根本无从使用它。',
        'So I stayed there, ignorant to the actual time. ...However, I could tell that a few hours had passed.': '于是我待在那里，不知道实际过了多久。{w}……不过，我大致能判断已经过了几个小时。',
        '...What?': '……{w}什么？',
        'Suddenly, the storeroom door opened, and I had to fight to contain my panic. It appeared my past self was looking for something, as he quickly moved on to the next crystal room.': '突然，储藏室的门开了，我拼命压住心里的惊慌。{w}看来过去的我正在找什么，很快又转向了下一间水晶展室。',
        'Stay the— ...look at the mechani—': '待在那儿——{w=0.4}……你看机械室——',
        'I emerged from the hidden area so that I could hear a little bit better. It seemed everyone was walking up the stairs. Had I actually heard Miiya? If she was there, I had to see her.': '我从藏身处走出来，好听得更清楚些。看来所有人都上楼了。{w}我真的听到Miiya了吗？如果她就在那里，我一定要见到她。',
        "...What about Miiya? Is she not here? My past self isn't either...": '……Miiya呢？她不在这里吗？{w}过去的我也不在……',
        'I looked around in desperation. I could never hide in a bathroom, as Katei would unlock it. I saw the elevator was open; it was working, and the others had definitely been in the process of searching the whole building.': '我绝望地环顾四周。洗手间根本藏不了——Katei 会把门打开。{w} 我看到电梯开着，还能运行，而其他人显然正在搜查整栋楼。',
        "Did I really mishear that? Was that not Miiya...? Where is my other self, then? What about the past Shiroya? She isn't here either.": '难道我真的听错了？那不是 Miiya……？{w} 那另一个我在哪里？过去的 Shiroya 呢？她也不在这里。',
        "Yeah, they're not there anymore. Where did they go? There's no way they opened the door out, is there?": '嗯，人已经不在了。{w} 到底去了哪里？总不可能把通向外面的门打开了吧？',
        "...It's not hot at all. That means it's not currently working, but it should be.": '……一点都不烫。{w} 也就是说它现在没在运作，可它本该在运作才对。',
        "That sounded like a plausible idea, but it was denied by the time a Sekimeiya had appeared inactive in Sai's hip pack. It was useless, and I didn't want to give myself another headache trying to resolve it. I put it back where I'd found it.": '这猜测看似合理，但 Sai 腰包里也出现过毫无反应的 Sekimeiya，这个说法便站不住脚了。{w} 它反正没用，我也不想再为弄清它头疼一次。我把它放回了原处。',
        "Was that voice really Miiya's? I need to know that. It couldn't have been anyone else. If it wasn't my imagination, it was the real Miiya.": '那真的是 Miiya 的声音吗？我必须确认这一点。{w} 不可能是别人。如果不是我的错觉，那就是真正的 Miiya。',
        "It's likely they'll all come back down. If she's here, I'll be able to see her. She wasn't with the others in the storeroom, though. My past self and Shiroya were missing too...": '他们多半都会下来。如果她在这里，我就能看见她。{w} 可她并不在储藏室那群人里。过去的我和 Shiroya 也不见了……',
        "I decided that if nobody came after a while, I would quietly go up to see if I could find everyone. But soon after that resolution, I thought I might've heard someone just outside the bathroom, separated from the rest.": '我决定，如果过了一会儿还没人来，就悄悄上楼看看能不能找到大家。{w} 可刚下定决心，我好像听见洗手间外有人，而且和其余人分开了。',
        'What the hell is he doing now? And what the hell is everyone else doing, letting him roam around freely?': '他他妈在干什么？{w} 其他人又是怎么回事，竟然让他自由行动？',
        "Was he the person who came out of that crystal room? If he traveled through time, he could've been there and in the storeroom at the same time. But everyone had to see that person when they left A1. They would've reacted at seeing two of one person, and I guess it would've been a paradox...": '他是不是那个从水晶展室出来的人？如果他穿越了时间，就可能同时出现在那边和储藏室。{w} 但那人离开 A1 时，大家肯定都看见了。要是看到同一个人同时出现两个，他们不可能没有反应——我想那会形成悖论……',
        'The sound grew clearer: a group of people was coming down. Once they went down the stairs, I slowly opened the door.': '声音渐渐清晰：一群人正往下走。{w}等他们下了楼梯，我才慢慢推开门。',
        '...any of the— Can you he—': '……这些里面有没有——{w}你听得见——',
        "And that's me. My past self is with them this time. ...Where the hell is Sai, though?": '那是我。这次和他们在一起的是过去的我。{w}……可 Sai 到底跑哪去了？',
        'Keeping myself hidden, I peeked into hallway B. Nobody was there, but I saw what had hit the floor next to the event room.': '我藏起身形，朝 B走廊里张望。{w}那里空无一人，但我看见了掉在活动室旁地上的东西。',
        "Its color... It's white. If they had touched it, it would be gray.": '颜色……是白的。{w}要是被他们碰过，就该是灰色了。',
        "...What happened? They touched this one instead? Hang on, is this the one I found in the cabinet? If it's not working now, that means it was previously working.": '……怎么回事？他们碰的是这一个？{w}等等，这是我在展示柜里找到的那个吗？它现在失效，说明之前是能用的。',
        "I thought that maybe the past changed at some point. This would've led into the countless deviations I've noticed. ...But there's something about this world that I recognize.": '我原以为，是过去在某个时刻被改变了。我察觉到的那些数不清的偏差，大概就由此而来。{w}……可这个世界里，有一点让我觉得熟悉。',
        "Even though I haven't been able to see her, what I heard was her voice. I can't doubt that. When that happened, everyone was there. In other words, Miiya's existence wasn't something anyone found strange—not even my past self.": '虽然我没能看见她，但我听到的是她的声音，这一点毋庸置疑。{w}那时所有人都在场。也就是说，Miiya 的存在对谁来说都不奇怪——包括过去的我。',
        "Sai and Akaro acted as if Miiya's existence was normal. And that's not all. Akaro disappeared after that point, and when he appeared with different clothes after {time=21}, he said he hadn't been present at the last time I'd seen him.": 'Sai 和 Akaro 的表现，就好像 Miiya 的存在理所当然。{w}不仅如此。那之后 Akaro 就消失了，过了 {time=21}，他换了身衣服出现，还说我最后一次见到他时，他并不在场。',
        "Sai and Akaro acted as if Miiya's existence was normal.{w} And that's not all. Akaro disappeared after that point, and when he appeared with different clothes after 21:00, he said he hadn't been present at the last time I'd seen him.": 'Sai 和 Akaro 的表现，就好像 Miiya 的存在理所当然。{w}不仅如此。那之后 Akaro 就消失了，过了 {time=21}，他换了身衣服出现，还说我最后一次见到他时，他并不在场。',
        "Sai and Akaro acted as if Miiya's existence was normal. And that's not all. Akaro disappeared after that point, and when he appeared with different clothes after 21:00, he said he hadn't been present at the last time I'd seen him.": 'Sai 和 Akaro 的表现，就好像 Miiya 的存在理所当然。{w}不仅如此。那之后 Akaro 就消失了，过了 {time=21}，他换了身衣服出现，还说我最后一次见到他时，他并不在场。',
        "Sai and Akaro acted as if Miiya's existence was normal.{w} And that's not all. Akaro disappeared after that point, and when he appeared with different clothes after 9 p.m., he said he hadn't been present at the last time I'd seen him.": 'Sai 和 Akaro 的表现，就好像 Miiya 的存在理所当然。{w}不仅如此。那之后 Akaro 就消失了，过了 {time=21}，他换了身衣服出现，还说我最后一次见到他时，他并不在场。',
        "Sai and Akaro acted as if Miiya's existence was normal. And that's not all. Akaro disappeared after that point, and when he appeared with different clothes after 9 p.m., he said he hadn't been present at the last time I'd seen him.": 'Sai 和 Akaro 的表现，就好像 Miiya 的存在理所当然。{w}不仅如此。那之后 Akaro 就消失了，过了 {time=21}，他换了身衣服出现，还说我最后一次见到他时，他并不在场。',
        "Three major questions arose: why did Erina, Shiroya, and I not travel, but Sai did? Why did the Sekimeiya teleport instantly back to its cabinet? Why was the range bigger than it should've been?": '三个疑问随之浮现：为什么 Erina、Shiroya 和我没有穿越，Sai 却穿越了？{w}为什么 Sekimeiya 会瞬间传送回展示柜？{w}为什么范围比应有的更大？',
        "Before Erina touched the Sekimeiya, when we entered the event room, Shiroya and I were confused to see the Sekimeiya in the cabinet. In my case, it was because I'd recently hidden it. ...Specifically, in a locker in the staff room.": 'Erina 触碰 Sekimeiya 之前，我们走进活动室时，Shiroya 和我看到展示柜里的 Sekimeiya，都感到困惑。{w} 我之所以困惑，是因为我不久前才把它藏起来。{w}……准确地说，是藏进了员工室的一个储物柜里。',
        'When I saw it in the cabinet, I thought it must\'ve teleported to its "original place", or where the cold temperature was. The reality was...': '看到它出现在展示柜里时，我以为它一定是传送回了“原本的位置”，也就是温度较低的地方。{w} 可事实却是……',
        "The one in the event room spent fifteen minutes outside the cabinet. Meanwhile, as I had touched the one in the staff room at around 18:30, it should've gathered power there for almost half an hour.": '活动室里的那个在展示柜外待了十五分钟。而我大约在 {time=18:30} 碰过员工室里的那个，所以它应该已经在那里蓄能将近半小时了。',
        "The one in the event room spent fifteen minutes outside the cabinet. Meanwhile, as I had touched the one in the staff room at around 6:30 p.m., it should've gathered power there for almost half an hour.": '活动室里的那个在展示柜外待了十五分钟。而我大约在 {time=18:30} 碰过员工室里的那个，所以它应该已经在那里蓄能将近半小时了。',
        "The range of the Sekimeiya Erina touched probably looked like this. However, the hidden factor that I didn't account for...": 'Erina 碰过的那个 Sekimeiya，范围大概是这样。{w} 然而，还有一个我当时没考虑到的隐藏因素……',
        '...Was the Sekimeiya in the staff room. It was in the rightmost set of lockers, and given the time it had been there, I imagine its range extended halfway through the event room.': '……就是员工室里的那个 Sekimeiya。{w} 它在最右侧的那排储物柜里；按它在那儿放的时间来算，它的范围应该已经覆盖到活动室的一半了。',
        "...If this is what was special about that travel, then what happened to us? Sai did travel because he was only within range of Erina's Sekimeiya. However, the rest of us didn't teleport through space or time.": '……{w}如果那次穿越的特殊之处就在这，那我们又经历了什么？{w} Sai 确实穿越了，因为他只在 Erina 那个 Sekimeiya 的范围内。可我们其余人并没有在空间或时间上传送。',
        "Instead, what changed was the world around us. The Sekimeiya didn't teleport back to the cabinet—that was a mere illusion.": '真正改变的，是我们周围的世界。{w} Sekimeiya 并没有传送回展示柜——那不过是错觉。',
        "I might be mistaken somewhere, but I don't think that was still the same world. However, what happened later? We did reunite with the Sai who'd traveled in the event room, didn't we? Similarly, Akaro and the other Sai weren't found again. It was as if we'd gone back to our world.": '也许我在某处弄错了，但我觉得那已经不是同一个世界。{w} 可是后来呢？我们确实和那位在活动室里穿越的 Sai 重逢了，不是吗？{w} 而 Akaro 和另一个 Sai 也再没被找到。就好像我们回到了自己的世界。',
        "I wonder... Does that hypothesis solve every mystery surrounding that travel? What about the range? It was bigger than previous fifteen-minute travels, wasn't it? ...Two functional Sekimeiya existed. If their ranges overlapped, the Sekimeiya's effect wouldn't just be time travel. I think that could be right. It's not an idea that can only be applied in that instance.": '我在想……那个假设能解开围绕那次穿越的所有谜团吗？{w} 范围又该怎么解释？它比以往十五分钟的穿越更大，不是吗？{w}……当时有两个能运作的 Sekimeiya。{w} 如果它们的范围发生重叠，Sekimeiya 的效果就不只是时间穿越了。{w} 我觉得这有可能。这个想法不只适用于那一次。',
        "Where is everyone? The Sekimeiya was just activated when both of them were close to each other on the crystal floor, and it doesn't seem like the others are still in this tower. How did I get to this world? Could it really be the same one we briefly visited? This morning, Shiroya and I witnessed the Sekimeiya teleport. But that isn't what's been going on—the Sekimeiya isn't teleporting. It only appears that way because the entire world is changing.": '大家都去哪了？两个 Sekimeiya 在水晶层上彼此靠近时，其中一个刚被启动，而其他人似乎已经不在这座塔里了。{w} 我是怎么来到这个世界的？难道这真的是我们短暂造访过的那个世界？{w} 今天早晨，Shiroya 和我亲眼看见 Sekimeiya 传送。可事情并不是这样——Sekimeiya 并没有在传送。它看起来是这样，只是因为整个世界都在改变。',
        "When it happened, we found the Sekimeiya inside a cabinet in room B4. It's very possible the other one was hidden nearby. That's why Naomi was running to the attic with both Sekimeiya immediately after it disappeared. We chased her up, but in the attic's staircase, Shiroya disappeared. When I looked at the living room, both Sekimeiya were next to each other, and one of them was gray. As a result, neither Naomi nor Shiroya are here.": '那件事发生时，我们在 B4房间的展示柜里发现了 Sekimeiya。另一个很可能就藏在附近。{w} 所以它一消失，Naomi 就带着两个 Sekimeiya 跑向阁楼。{w} 我们追了上去，可就在阁楼的楼梯上，Shiroya 消失了。{w} 我看向客厅时，两个 Sekimeiya 并排放在一起，其中一个已经变成灰色。结果，Naomi 和 Shiroya 都不在这里了。',
        "Lastly, though... this would answer the question of how Naomi's corpse appeared two times. If Naomi touched the Sekimeiya and the world around her changed, she would've appeared in the attic. Her keys had been left behind, so she had no way to leave. That's what happened. That's what we saw on the floor of the living room. That's why we found Naomi dead twice. The Naomi that Shiroya disappeared with was one of the two bodies that we found dead. ...Does this mean that version of Shiroya was there since the beginning?": '最后……这也能解释 Naomi 的尸体为何会出现两次。{w} 如果 Naomi 触碰了 Sekimeiya，周围的世界随之改变，她就会出现在阁楼里。她的钥匙被留在了原地，所以她没法离开。{w} 事情就是这样。那就是我们在客厅地板上看到的情景。也正因如此，我们才会两次发现 Naomi 死去。{w} 和 Shiroya 一起消失的那个 Naomi，就是我们发现的两具尸体之一。……这是否意味着，那个 Shiroya 从一开始就在那里？',
        "Where are they, though? Am I really correct in what I'm thinking? Everyone who was in hallway B is no longer in this world. If that is the case, are they in the world I came from?": '可是，他们去哪了？我的想法真的正确吗？{w} 原本在B走廊的所有人都不在这个世界了。如果是这样，他们是在我来的那个世界吗？',
        'What exactly were the body double mysteries? I can\'t understand Shiroya\'s case at all, and I\'m not sure about Sai\'s. Isla\'s, though... Could her "friend" have been the Isla from this world?': '那些替身之谜究竟是怎么回事？Shiroya 的情况我完全想不通，Sai 的我也说不准。{w} 但 Isla 的……她那位“朋友”会不会就是这个世界的 Isla？',
        '"From this world"... I don\'t know what the hell to think, and that\'s mostly due to the most blatant example: the second Akaro. The Akaro who had different memories and disappeared from the bedroom. Did he come from a different world in the way that I\'m thinking? If so, he couldn\'t have been the Akaro from this world because he didn\'t know who Katei was, but he did know Shiroya.': '“来自这个世界”……我根本不知道该怎么想，而最明显的例子就是第二个 Akaro。{w} 那个记忆和我们不同、从卧室里消失的 Akaro。他会不会就像我想的那样，来自另一个世界？{w} 若是如此，他就不可能是这个世界的 Akaro，因为他不认识 Katei，却认识 Shiroya。',
        "Correct. A world beyond Atsuki's knowledge.": '正确。{w} 那是 Atsuki 认知之外的世界。',
        "So, where did that Akaro come from? Could he have come from a world without Katei? If that's it, though, this is too fucking confusing! Could changing worlds bring me to any kind of world? There could be infinite worlds, and the Sekimeiya could act as random bridges between them!": '那么，那个 Akaro 是从哪来的？{w} 他会不会来自一个没有 Katei 的世界？{w} 可要真是这样，这也太他妈让人糊涂了！世界切换会把我带到任何一种世界吗？世界也许有无数个，而 Sekimeiya 可能在它们之间随机架起桥梁！',
        "It is because the three worlds loop. That is the essential core of the universe you've witnessed. Through the Sekimeiya, the link between three worlds looped. The three sides of the mountain spun around, leading to a single peak.": '因为三个世界构成了循环。这就是你所见证的宇宙的核心本质。{w} 借助 Sekimeiya，三个世界之间的联结形成了循环。山的三个侧面旋转交汇，最终归于同一座峰顶。',
        "Atsuki correctly figured out the Sekimeiya's core secret. In each world, two Sekimeiya existed. When one was activated, the active range sent anyone encompassed in it through time. However, if both ranges overlapped, whoever found themselves present within both were not transported through time and space, but through worlds.": 'Atsuki 准确解开了 Sekimeiya 的核心秘密。{w} 每个世界里都存在两个 Sekimeiya。激活其中一个时，生效范围会将范围内的人送往另一段时间。{w} 然而，若两个范围发生重叠，同时处在两者之中的人便不会被送往另一个时间，而是会被送往另一个世界。',
        'This effect is called a world switch, although the full extent of the name might not make a lot of sense to you yet. Like everything about the Sekimeiya, the world switch hid many secrets of its own. Of course, you may have figured some of them out with the tools you were given.': '这种现象被称为世界切换，不过这个名称的全部含义，你现在或许还无法完全理解。{w} 如同 Sekimeiya 的一切，世界切换本身也藏着许多秘密。当然，凭借手中的工具，你可能已经解开了其中一些。',
        '"B" is the world in which the recorder was present. At 21:00, Atsuki, Sai, and Erina weren\'t able to escape.': '“B”是录音笔所在的世界。到了 {time=21}，Atsuki、Sai 和 Erina 没能逃出去。',
        '"B" is the world in which the recorder was present. At 9 p.m., Atsuki, Sai, and Erina weren\'t able to escape.': '“B”是录音笔所在的世界。到了 {time=21}，Atsuki、Sai 和 Erina 没能逃出去。',
        'Then, "B" is the world in which the recorder was present. At 21:00, Atsuki, Sai, and Erina weren\'t able to escape.': '那么，“B”就是录音笔所在的世界。到了 {time=21}，Atsuki、Sai 和 Erina 没能逃出去。',
        'Then, "B" is the world in which the recorder was present. At 9 p.m., Atsuki, Sai, and Erina weren\'t able to escape.': '那么，“B”就是录音笔所在的世界。到了 {time=21}，Atsuki、Sai 和 Erina 没能逃出去。',
        "You've seen a few instances of full loops. Miiya's group went from their own world, C, to world A. From world A they went to world B, and then from world B they went back to world C. Shiroya, after traveling from January 5th to December 15th, went from world B to world C with Atsuki. In the attic, she went from world C to world A with Naomi, and she finally returned alone to world B. The order is A - B - C - A.": '你已经见过几次完整的循环。Miiya 一行人从自己所在的 C世界前往 A世界。接着从 A世界到 B世界，再从 B世界回到 C世界。{w} Shiroya 从1月5日穿越到12月15日后，与 Atsuki 一同从 B世界来到 C世界。在阁楼里，她又和 Naomi 从 C世界到了 A世界，最后独自返回 B世界。顺序是 A - B - C - A。',
        "You don't think so? Can you not find any instances that didn't follow that order? They do exist. If you find them, perhaps you'll notice what they had in common.": '你不这么认为？难道找不到不按这个顺序发生的例子吗？{w} 那样的例子确实存在。只要找出来，或许你就会注意到它们的共同点。',
        'The incident at the tower happened in all three worlds, but the outcome was vastly different. Why?': '塔中的事件在三个世界里都发生过，结果却大相径庭。{w} 为什么？',
        "That isn't right. Katei didn't have that key. He dropped the security room's.": '不对。Katei 没有那把钥匙。{w} 他掉的是监控室的钥匙。',
        "You remember that Atsuki found it there, but that didn't happen in world A, did it? That was in world C. You might know who found the key in world A. It was Akaro. Although many things were different, Atsuki only came across it in world C because Katei had been staring at the floor, and he wasn't there in world A.": '你记得 Atsuki 是在那里发现钥匙的，但这件事并没有发生在 A 世界，对吧？那是在 C 世界。{w} 你也许知道 A 世界里是谁发现了钥匙：Akaro。虽然许多事情都不一样，但 Atsuki 在 C 世界之所以会偶然发现那把钥匙，是因为 Katei 当时一直盯着地板看；而在 A 世界里，Katei 并不在场。',
        "He left through the storeroom before the others woke up. Outside, he was fast enough to meet up with everyone else who'd evacuated. He knew the floor 2 cameras had recorded him, but he was confident he could take care of that at 21:00.": '其他人醒来之前，他从储藏室离开了。到了外面，他跑得够快，追上了其他已经疏散出来的人。他知道二楼的监控拍到了自己，但有把握在 {time=21.} 处理好。',
        "He left through the storeroom before the others woke up. Outside, he was fast enough to meet up with everyone else who'd evacuated. He knew the floor 2 cameras had recorded him, but he was confident he could take care of that at 9 p.m.": '其他人醒来之前，他从储藏室离开了。到了外面，他跑得够快，追上了其他已经疏散出来的人。他知道二楼的监控拍到了自己，但有把握在 {time=21.} 处理好。',
        "Meanwhile, in world C, everything happened similarly. However, when Katei attempted to unlock the storeroom door, he couldn't. Something prevented him from doing so. Like in world A, he heard Naomi's movements and chased her up, dropping the key in the same staircase.": '与此同时，C 世界里的一切也大致相同。然而，Katei 试图打开储藏室的门时却没能成功。有什么东西阻碍了他。{w} 就像在 A 世界一样，他听见 Naomi 的动静后追了上去，又在那段楼梯上掉了钥匙。',
        "...It was the handle's removal. In world B, Katei went to the secret door, ready to leave. However, he immediately felt it with his hand: the handle wasn't there.": '……问题出在门把手上。{w} 在 B 世界，Katei 来到暗门前，准备离开。然而他伸手一摸，立刻察觉：门把手不见了。',
        "He understood that he would have to stay in the tower, but he didn't immediately give up. Xyn's Sekimeiya was still in the event room, and perhaps he could make use of it. Katei sighed deeply, trying to figure out who could've known about the storeroom's secret.": '他明白自己只能留在塔里，却没有就此放弃。Xyn 的 Sekimeiya 还在活动室，或许还能派上用场。{w}Katei 深深叹了口气，思索着究竟有谁会知道储藏室的秘密。',
        "Yet, one of the cabinets was open... It was impossible anyone had been there, and the cabinet's temperature hadn't even cooled off yet. He hurriedly put the Sekimeiya back in, still trying to process what could've happened.": '然而，有一个展示柜敞开着……{w}刚才不可能有人在那里，柜里的温度甚至还没降下来。他匆匆把 Sekimeiya 放回去，脑中仍在琢磨究竟发生了什么。',
        "When he left the room, he saw Erina's group on the floor of the hallway. She was moving slightly, so Katei felt trapped. He didn't want her to wake up and see him leaving. Slowly, he walked over and crouched beside the three incapacitated people.": '他走出展室，看见 Erina 一行人倒在走廊的地上。她微微动着，Katei 顿时觉得自己被困住了。他不愿她醒来时撞见自己离开。{w}他缓缓走过去，在那三个失去意识的人身旁蹲下。',
        "That's not right. The person who removed the secret door's handle in world B was Akaro A.": '不对。{w}在B世界卸下暗门把手的人，是 Akaro A。',
        "He was the main person behind the attack. In his world, however, Xyn were outsmarted. The alarm Xyn didn't know about went off, and the Sekimeiya Akaro had hidden in the cleaning cart was taken.": '他是这次袭击的主谋。然而在他的世界里，Xyn 却反遭算计。{w}Xyn 并不知道的警报响了，Akaro 藏在清洁车里的 Sekimeiya 也被人拿走。',
        "In that world, he was surprised to find out the attic was unlocked, and even more so to see that everyone was taking shelter inside a bedroom. There, he learned about two things: Katei's presence in the tower and the existence of the storeroom's secret. Naturally, he knew who Katei Kuiji was, but he shouldn't have been there. Akaro had suspected someone from Ashiya had hindered their plan, so he was internally taken aback when he heard details about that world's events.": '在那个世界，他惊讶地发现阁楼没有上锁，更惊讶的是所有人都在一间卧室里避难。{w}在那里，他得知了两件事：Katei 就在塔里，以及储藏室藏有一道暗门。{w}他自然知道 Katei Kuiji 是什么人，但那人本不该出现在那里。Akaro 一直怀疑是芦屋的人妨碍了他们的计划，所以听到那个世界里那场事件的细节时，他心里暗暗一惊。',
        "Out of nowhere, he appeared in a detention cell, but he was able to leave it. Then, he realized he was in the far past. He recalled the times Katei had chosen to speak to Ido: he must've been who had interfered with Xyn's plan.": '他毫无征兆地出现在一间拘留室里，却顺利离开了。随后他意识到，自己身处遥远的过去。{w}他回想起 Katei 几次主动找 Ido 说话的情形：干扰 Xyn 计划的人，一定就是他。',
        "Katei hadn't been in the tower, yet everyone had eventually claimed he'd been there since the start. It wasn't hard to suspect the truth. However, Akaro still couldn't believe what he'd done. In the tower, desperate to fulfill Xyn's plan...": 'Katei 本不在塔里，可到头来所有人都说他从一开始就在。要猜到真相并不难。{w}然而，Akaro 仍不敢相信自己做了什么。在塔里，他为了完成 Xyn 的计划不惜一切……',
        "How had Shiroya come back to life? ...And she had clearly been aware of what he'd done. Why had she not said anything, then? Akaro had no idea why she had come back, but he had been next to her and Atsuki for hours; he'd seen how they'd turned out after he'd caused the death of their friend.": 'Shiroya 是怎么死而复生的？……而且她显然知道他做过什么。{w}那她为什么一句都没说？Akaro 完全不明白她为何会回来，但他曾在 Shiroya 和 Atsuki 身边待了好几个小时；他亲眼看到，在自己害死他们的朋友之后，两人变成了什么样子。',
        'At first, when he appeared in November, Akaro thought of what to do. He could take advantage of it—he knew what would happen. Yet his remorse soon overcame him. His greatest wish was to walk away, and he had the opportunity to do so. The plan was going to be a failure, but he was no longer in his world. Perhaps he could let his other self take the blame while he tried to atone for his actions...': '刚出现在11月时，Akaro 还在盘算该怎么办。他本可以利用这一切——他知道接下来会发生什么。{w}可愧疚很快压过了这个念头。他最大的心愿就是一走了之，而现在他正好有这样的机会。计划注定要失败，但他已不在自己的世界里。或许他可以让另一个自己去背这个罪责，而自己设法赎罪……',
        'In worlds A and C, however, the same thing occurred. In the attic, Naomi touched the Sekimeiya and world switched. When Naomi A touched it, she appeared in world B. Her keys remained in world A, and the elevator was disabled. Until that changed, she was trapped up there. From her point of view, both Sekimeiya disappeared, as she brought the suitcase along as one of her possessions.': '然而在A世界和C世界，发生的是同一件事。Naomi 在阁楼触碰到 Sekimeiya，世界切换了。{w}Naomi A 触碰它时，出现在B世界。Naomi A 的钥匙留在了A世界，电梯也无法使用。在情况改变之前，她一直被困在上面。{w}在她看来，两个 Sekimeiya 都消失了，因为她是把手提箱当作随身物品一起带过来的。',
        "However, Naomi C's outcome was different. She world switched to world A, and the range encompassed Shiroya as well. Even though the attic was locked, they weren't trapped. Not only did Shiroya have the key, but so did Naomi: although she'd changed worlds, she grabbed the keys Naomi A had left behind, unaware they were no longer hers.": '但 Naomi C 的结果不同。{w}她世界切换到了A世界，Shiroya 也在重叠范围内。{w}尽管阁楼上了锁，她们却没有被困住。Shiroya 有钥匙，Naomi 也有：她虽已换了世界，却顺手拿上了 Naomi A 留下的钥匙，并不知道那已不属于她。',
        "In addition, she brought the suitcase along too, but the Sekimeiya Naomi A had used were both still there. As both Naomis world switched at exactly the same time, for Naomi C, it only seemed as though the Sekimeiya she'd touched turned gray, even though it was the one Naomi A had activated. Instinctively, what she did was touch the other Sekimeiya, unable to believe her finger had changed a gem's color. When she did, she traveled through time: since one of the Sekimeiya was powered off, there was no world switch.": '此外，她也把手提箱带了过来，但 Naomi A 用过的两个 Sekimeiya 都还在原处。由于两个 Naomi 是在同一瞬间切换世界的，所以在 Naomi C 看来，仿佛只有自己碰过的那个 Sekimeiya 变成了灰色——尽管那其实是 Naomi A 激活的那一个。{w}她无法相信自己的手指能让宝石变色，便本能地去碰了另一个 Sekimeiya。这一碰，她穿越了时间：因为其中一个 Sekimeiya 已经断电，所以没有发生世界切换。',
        "In world A, Akaro couldn't see Katei as his enemy, so his attitude toward the others was rougher and sterner. In addition, the article detailing his escape from prison only existed in world B.": '在A世界，Akaro 无法把 Katei 视为敌人，所以他对待其他人的态度更加粗暴严厉。{w}此外，详细报道他越狱的那篇文章只存在于B世界。',
        'Up to the 24th of November, all the worlds were identical. You might be familiar with the many-worlds interpretation. According to it, every choice splits the world, leading into infinite worlds which are infinitely different.': '在11月24日之前，所有世界都完全相同。{w}你或许听说过多重世界诠释。照这种说法，每一个选择都会分裂世界，衍生出无穷多个彼此千差万别的世界。',
        "In these three worlds, the initial difference came in November of 2011, and it was caused due to someone who had world switched from another world. In other words, there was no change that wasn't influenced by another world—if zero world switches had occurred, each of the three worlds would've remained identical.": '在这三个世界中，最初的差异出现在2011年11月，起因是有人从另一个世界切换而来。{w}换句话说，任何变化都受到另一个世界的影响——假如一次世界切换都不曾发生，这三个世界至今仍会完全相同。',
        "There are numerous enigmas around the world switch. Perhaps you have some lingering questions. When Akaro A appeared in world B, the storeroom had been sealed by his future self. However, in part, that helped him go back in time and seal it. Doesn't that seem contradictory? If he had appeared in a world without a sealed storeroom, he wouldn't have been able to go back and seal it... You might find a number of similar cases. For that, you can look at the people who world switched and the way they shaped their new world. If the answer escapes you, that's where you will find it, alongside the real form of the world switch.": '围绕世界切换，还有许多谜团。你或许仍有疑问。{w}当 Akaro A 出现在B世界时，储藏室已经被他未来的自己封上了。可在某种程度上，正是这一点帮了他，让他能回到过去把储藏室封上。这不是自相矛盾吗？如果他出现的那个世界里储藏室没有被封，他就无法回去把它封上……类似的情形你或许还能找出不少。{w}为此，你可以去看看那些发生过世界切换的人，以及他们如何塑造自己的新世界。想不出答案的话，答案就在那里，世界切换的真实面貌也在那里。',
        "I couldn't just think that infinite worlds existed. After all, it was possible I was going back and forth between two. The first time, Erina had brought us to a different world, but we had eventually returned. When we'd later traveled back to that morning, Shiroya and I had changed worlds, but I suspected that we'd appeared in the same one again. That was why thinking that infinite worlds existed was a bit of a leap.": '我不能就此认定存在无穷多个世界。毕竟，我也可能只是在两个世界之间来回。{w}第一次，Erina 把我们带到了另一个世界，但最后我们还是回去了。后来我们穿越回那天早晨时，Shiroya 和我切换了世界，可我怀疑我们又一次落在了同一个世界。所以说，断言存在无穷多个世界，还是有些操之过急。',
        'I shut a Sekimeiya inside the refrigerator for a few seconds. When I took it out, I felt it through my shirt.': '我在冰箱里放了一个 Sekimeiya，关上门，等了几秒。{w}取出来时，我隔着衬衫感受它的温度。',
        '...Hm? What just happened?': '……{w}嗯？刚才怎么回事？',
        "And the location where I appeared... Why was it right next to where I touched the Sekimeiya? It's as if I only moved a tiny bit because I only went a few seconds to the future.": '还有我出现的位置……为什么恰好就在我碰 Sekimeiya 的位置旁边？{w}就好像我只往未来走了几秒，所以位置也只挪了一点点。',
        "Hm... I have an idea, but I don't think I can test it.": '嗯……{w}我有个想法，不过恐怕没法验证。',
        "That wasn't strange. After all, the recorder in Isla's purse had to have traveled from the future, while the one in the security room was the original one. However, my intention wasn't to record anything. I wanted to use the device as a timer that I could hold.": '这并不奇怪。毕竟 Isla 包里的那支是从未来穿越而来的，监控室里的这一支才是原本的那支。{w}可我要的并不是录音。我只想把它当作可以随身带着的计时器。',
        'Immediately, I looked at the oven. Its timer indicated that four minutes and fifteen seconds still remained. Right after that, I glanced at my own hand, eager to look at my timer. The device was there.': '我立刻去看烤箱，计时显示还剩四分十五秒。{w}紧接着，我低头看向自己的手，急着看自己的计时器。{w}录音笔还在手里。',
        "But while the device's screen changed to 4:16, the oven's timer went to 4:14. Like before, the recorder kept counting up, whereas the oven counted down.": '可录音笔的屏幕跳到 4:16 时，烤箱的计时却变成了 4:14。{w}和刚才一样，录音笔在递增，烤箱在倒数。',
        "I had to do it again. I turned off the oven and erased the recording. Next, I set the oven to five minutes and pressed the device's record button at the same time. I left the Sekimeiya in the refrigerator until two minutes had elapsed. Then, thirty seconds later, when the recorder displayed 2:30, I touched the gem again.": '我得再来一次。{w}我关掉烤箱，删除了录音。接着，我把烤箱设成五分钟，同时按下录音笔的录音键。{w}我让 Sekimeiya 在冰箱里放了两分钟。等过了三十秒，录音笔显示 2:30 时，我再次碰了它。',
        'The immediate result was the same: I appeared in the kitchen, pretty much where I\'d already been standing. I looked at both timers at once. The two of them showed "2:21", yet the device\'s timer kept ticking up while the oven\'s counted down.': '眼前的结果还是一样：我出现在厨房，差不多就在原先站立的地方。我同时看了一眼两个计时器。{w}两边都显示「2:21」，可录音笔的计时仍在递增，烤箱的却在倒数。',
        "What the fuck? Again, I went nine seconds to the future, but the location I appeared in was from nine seconds before touching the Sekimeiya. Is this it? Does traveling to the future X amount of time replicate the location in space you were at X amount of time in the past? What about traveling back, though? I've gone to the future three times in a row!": '这他妈是怎么回事？又是这样——我向未来跳了九秒，落点却是我触碰 Sekimeiya 之前九秒所在的位置。{w}难道说，向未来跳 X 秒，复制出的地点就是你在 X 秒前所在的位置？{w}可要是向过去跳呢？我都已经连着三次跳往未来了！',
        "I see... I just traveled through time, and the Sekimeiya's range was so small that it didn't pick me up again. It does seem like I went nine seconds to the past. It's probably due to the Sekimeiya I used: this one makes you travel to the past, while the other sends you to the future.": '原来如此……我刚刚经历了一次时间穿越，而 Sekimeiya 的范围太小，没能再次把我卷进去。看来我确实回到了九秒前。{w}原因大概出在我用的这个 Sekimeiya 上：这个会让人回到过去，另一个则把人送往未来。',
        "The oven's timer was at 2:25, so I hurried to look at the voice recorder as I thought about it. I had gone nine seconds to the past, so upon appearing, the oven's timer would've been at 2:39. Then, I had waited out the nine seconds needed for my past self to disappear, and five extra seconds had elapsed since. Before the oven's timer counted down to 2:24, I looked at the device between my hands.": '烤箱定时器显示 2:25，我一边琢磨，一边急忙去看录音笔。{w}我是回到了九秒前，所以刚出现时，烤箱定时器应该停在 2:39。之后我等了九秒，直到过去的自己消失；那之后又过了五秒。趁烤箱定时器还没跳到 2:24，我看向手中的录音笔。',
        "The screen is blank! What the hell!? Why? I can't know where this location is from!": '屏幕一片空白！搞什么鬼！？{w}为什么？这样一来，我根本没法知道这个位置是从哪儿来的！',
        "Traveling nine seconds to the future put me where I'd been nine seconds in the past! Wouldn't traveling to the past put me— ...where I'd be nine seconds in the future. And I'm still here, exactly where I appeared.": '向未来跳九秒，会把我送到九秒前我所在的地方！{w}那向过去跳，不就会把我送到——{w}……{w}九秒后我会在的地方吗？{w}而我还在这里，就在我出现的位置上，一动没动。',
        'Wait, no. It might make sense.': '等等，{w}不对，{w}也许说得通。',
        "Let's say the Sekimeiya is touched at time {b}t{/b}. In this case, {b}t{/b} is 2:30. {b}X{/b} will refer to the travel time, which is nine seconds.": '假设在时刻 {b}t{/b} 触碰 Sekimeiya。这里 {b}t{/b} 是 2:30。{w}再设 {b}X{/b} 为穿越时间，也就是九秒。',
        '{b}t+X{/b}, or 2:39. Then {b}2X{/b} seconds would pass to reach the future state.': '应是 {b}t+X{/b}，也就是 2:39。{w}可要抵达那个未来状态，还得再经过 {b}2X{/b} 秒。',
        'The timer would read {b}t+3X{/b}, or 2:57, but that contradicts the past position.  The timer at arrival would have to be {b}t+3X{/b}.': '定时器会显示 {b}t+3X{/b}，也就是 2:57，可这与过去的位置不符。{w}照此推算，抵达时定时器的读数只可能是 {b}t+3X{/b}。',
        "This can't make sense, though. If the replicated location is one that occurs after touching the Sekimeiya, we would die.": '可这样根本说不通。{w}如果复制出的位置是触碰 Sekimeiya 之后才会出现的，那我们不就死定了。',
        "However, isn't this what happened... to Sai's watch? Not only to Sai, but to a Sai who I have to assume traveled to the past. When I saw him, he should've been in the attic, so he'd come from the future. Later, I learned his watch had stopped working again.": '然而……Sai 的手表，不正是这样吗？{w}而且不只是 Sai，而是那个我不得不认定曾穿越到过去的 Sai。我见到他时，他本该待在阁楼，可见他是从未来回来的。后来我得知，他的手表又停了。',
        "If he appeared five minutes in the past where he would be ten minutes after his appearance... the time on his watch would've increased by ten minutes infinitely, and the battery would've eventually stopped working. There's no way it would've lasted thousands of years, though, so what the hell? And why would the watch's inner mechanism add up the looped time while its outer appearance wasn't affected?": '如果他出现在五分钟前，而那个位置正是他出现十分钟后会在的地方……那手表上的时间就会以十分钟为单位无限累加，电池迟早撑不住。{w}可它绝不可能撑上几千年，这到底是怎么回事？{w}况且，为什么只有手表的内部机件在累加循环的时间，外表却毫无变化？',
        "Wait, no. I can make it work again if what I've concluded is correct. After all, just minutes ago, I was holding it when it worked. I just have to replicate that location, which should be easy. I only have to travel a couple minutes to the future.": '等等，不对。只要我的推论没错，我就能让它重新工作。{w}毕竟就在几分钟前，我拿着它的时候它还是好的。我只要复制出那个位置就行，这应该不难。我只需要向未来跳几分钟。',
        'So, twenty minutes after the point I touched the Sekimeiya... I was in the lobby, right in front of the hallway A door. I was watching the hallway while the others looked through every room.': '也就是说，在我触碰 Sekimeiya 之后二十分钟……{w}我就在大厅里，站在 A走廊门前。当时其他人逐个房间搜查，我则守着走廊。',
        'Forty minutes after the time we touched the Sekimeiya... I really was in the security room, looking at the computer. Sai had just run away from me, and I even looked at the time. I was there from 12:18 to 12:31.': '在我们触碰 Sekimeiya 之后四十分钟……我确实待在监控室里，盯着电脑。那时 Sai 刚从我这逃走，我还看过时间。从 {time=12:18} 到 {time=12:31.}，我一直都在那里。',
        'Forty minutes after the time we touched the Sekimeiya... I really was in the security room, looking at the computer. Sai had just run away from me, and I even looked at the time. I was there from 12:18 p.m. to 12:31 p.m.': '在我们触碰 Sekimeiya 之后四十分钟……我确实待在监控室里，盯着电脑。那时 Sai 刚从我这逃走，我还看过时间。从 {time=12:18} 到 {time=12:31.}，我一直都在那里。',
        "It's nonsense! What's actually determining where we appear? Something must be. We appeared inside the tower every single time.": '荒唐！到底是什么决定了我们出现的位置？{w}肯定有什么在起作用。每一次，我们都出现在塔内。',
        "A knife was buried in Atsuki's chest. She looked directly into his eyes, but only silence filled the elevator—neither of them could bring themselves to utter a word.": '一把刀插在 Atsuki 的胸口。{w}她直直望进他的眼睛，电梯里却只有沉默——两人谁都说不出一句话来。',
        "Then, Shiroya looked at the hand gripping the knife. She followed it up to an arm and then a shoulder. Finally, she traced it to Sai's face.": '随后，Shiroya 看向握着刀的那只手。她的目光顺着手臂上移，越过肩膀，{w}最后落到 Sai 的脸上。',
        "But what the hell would happen now if I travel to the past? Let's say I travel two minutes back and appear in the kitchen. Will it be guaranteed that I'll be in the kitchen four minutes later?": '可如果我穿越回过去，现在到底会怎样？{w}假设我回到两分钟前，出现在厨房。那么四分钟后，我是否就一定会待在厨房？',
        "What if I don't want to? What if I decide to leave? Does the location where I appear force me to be somewhere in the future? That makes even less sense!": '要是我不愿意呢？要是我决定离开呢？{w}难道我出现的地点，还能强迫我未来必须待在某个地方？这更说不通！',
        "I mean, if I do appear in the kitchen, can I refuse to be there in the future? Can I risk doing that just out of curiosity? What if it's the universe's rule? Would I end up not trying to go against it out of fear of what might happen, which would confirm the impossibility of being in a paradoxical location?": '我是说，假如我真出现在厨房，难道我能在未来拒绝待在那里吗？只因为好奇，我就敢冒这个险吗？{w}万一这是宇宙定下的规律呢？我会不会因为害怕后果而不敢违逆，结果反倒坐实了「不可能待在悖论地点」这件事？',
        "And so I waited. I had traveled nine seconds to the past, so the only mandatory rule was that I had to be there after eighteen seconds. ...But I didn't wait there because the universe had forced me to—I did it so that my request could be fulfilled.": '于是我就在那里等着。我回到了九秒之前，唯一必须满足的规则，就是十八秒后我得待在那里。{w}……不过我留在那里，并非宇宙强迫，而是为了让自己的请求得以实现。',
        "Before touching the Sekimeiya, I had thought of what would happen. I had thought that eighteen seconds after appearing in the past, I would be in the living room. Of course, if that was the case, it implied I would appear in the living room, so it was what had happened. Then, to make it possible, I'd remained there, exactly where I'd imagined myself appearing.": '在碰Sekimeiya之前，我已经想过会发生什么。我心想，回到过去后，过十八秒，我会待在客厅。{w}如果真是这样，那就说明我会出现在客厅——而事实也确实如此。为了让这一切成立，我就一直待在自己想象中的出现地点。',
        'It\'s like the thought-up loops that I came up with. As long as the loop is in my head before touching the Sekimeiya, and as long as it can be executed, it will work. "As long as it can be executed". Didn\'t I just travel from the 5th of January to the 15th of December?': '这就像我自己设想出来的那些循环。只要在碰Sekimeiya之前，循环已经在我脑中成形，而且它能够被执行，就会成立。{w}「只要能够被执行」——我不就刚从1月5日穿越到了12月15日吗？',
        "I went 21 days into the past, and my knowledge of the replicated location came after the travel but before the location is replicated in the future. What the hell happens now? I appeared in the lobby; does that confirm that I'll be alive in the future?": '我回到了二十一天前。复现地点的事，我是在穿越之后才知道的，而那个地点要到未来才会复现。现在到底会怎样？{w}我出现在了大厅——这是否就能确认，未来我还活着？',
        '...I went 21 days to the past. 21 days after January 5th is a Thursday, January 26th...': '……{w}我回到了二十一天前。{w}1月5日往后二十一天，是1月26日，星期四……',
        "There was something there. That wasn't some random day. Shiroya and I had talked with Miiya about it. We had said that we would go back to the tower on the 26th if we liked it the first time.": '那天确实有些特别。那并不是随便哪一天。{w}我和Shiroya曾经跟Miiya聊起过。我们说过，如果第一次玩得尽兴，26号就再去一次塔里。',
        "Miiya had died because of the Sekimeiya—without the Sekimeiya's existence, the explosion wouldn't have occurred, and Miiya would've kept on living. Ashiya held an event in the tower every Thursday, and on January 26th, a Thursday, an event that had grabbed our attention would take place. If the Sekimeiya hadn't existed, we would've been in the tower on January 26th. Even after Miiya's death, if no travels had taken place, it was feasible that Shiroya and I would've returned to continue healing and moving forward. But from what I understood, our reason for returning would be different—to satisfy a travel that had already happened.": 'Miiya是因Sekimeiya而死的——若Sekimeiya不曾存在，那场爆炸就不会发生，Miiya也会继续活下去。芦屋每周四都会在塔里举办活动，而1月26日正是星期四，那天会有一场引起我们注意的活动。{w}若Sekimeiya不存在，1月26日我们本就会在塔里。即便Miiya死后、没有任何穿越发生，我和Shiroya也很有可能回到那里，继续疗伤、继续向前走。但据我所知，我们回去的理由会不一样——为了让一次已经发生过的穿越成立。',
        "This means that I can pretty much teleport anywhere I want, doesn't it? I just have to think about where I'll be in the future. The limit is that the location has to be possible to reach in a set time. Is that it?": '也就是说，我几乎能传送到任何想去的地方，对吧？{w}我只要想好自己未来会在哪里就行。限制只在于，那个地点必须能在规定时间内抵达。是这样吗？',
        "Once more, I appeared in the living room, where I'd wanted to appear. I looked at my hands, but they were empty.": '我再一次出现在客厅，也就是我想出现的地方。{w}我看了看自己的手，手上空无一物。',
        "Before touching the Sekimeiya, I had thought that I'd be in the living room with a chocolate bar in my hands. By appearing there with the chocolate, I would be able to have it in the future so that it could appear in the past. Presumably, that hadn't worked because I could never have obtained that chocolate in the span of those seconds, so I went back to the kitchen after I waited the proper amount of time.": '在碰Sekimeiya之前，我想的是：我会出现在客厅，手里拿着一块巧克力。只要我带着巧克力出现在那里，未来我就能拥有它，好让它出现在过去。{w}大概正因为在那几秒之内我根本不可能拿到那块巧克力，这招才没有奏效。于是等够时间后，我又回到厨房。',
        'After I appeared in the living room, I looked at my hands. I was holding a pen.': '出现在客厅后，我看了看自己的手。{w}手里握着一支笔。',
        "Before touching the Sekimeiya, I'd thought that I would appear in the living room, and that during those eighteen seconds, I would go grab the pen. That was why I had appeared with it. However, I already had the pen. I didn't have to go get it; I could simply stay where I'd appeared so that I could appear with it.": '在触碰 Sekimeiya 之前，我以为自己会出现在客厅，然后在那十八秒里去拿笔——正因为这样，我才会带着笔出现。{w} 可笔本来就已经在我手上了。我根本不必去拿，只要一直待在自己出现的位置不动，就能带着它出现。',
        "Why? She appeared in the lobby of the tower, and the future coordinate was January 26th. I'm sure you haven't forgotten that phones are strictly prohibited in the tower: she couldn't have been there with it in the future, so she appeared without it in the past.": '为什么？{w} 她出现在塔的大厅，而未来坐标是1月26日。想必你还记得，塔内严禁携带手机：在未来，她不可能带着手机待在那里，所以她在过去出现时，手机也就不在了。',
        "How much can I figure out with what I know? Was Sai aware of all this? He had a wristwatch, so I bet it would've been a lot easier for him to learn some of it. There were two Sekimeiya since this morning, but what about the third one? Does that one never work...?": '凭我现在知道的东西，能推出多少？Sai 清楚这些吗？他有一只手表，要弄明白其中几件事，想必比我容易得多。{w} 从今天早上起就有两个 Sekimeiya，那第三个呢？它难道永远不会启动……？',
        "And one made us travel back in time, while the other sent us forward. If I know the time someone appeared in the future, I can know that's where they were in the past—there are many ways to apply all of this. I wonder... When someone travels to the past, if I think that I'll bring them somewhere in the future, would I make them appear there in the past? Could the origin be in my mind even though I'm not the one traveling?": '而且，一个让我们回到过去，另一个把我们送往未来。{w} 只要知道某人出现在未来的时刻，就能知道他在过去身处何处——这些信息能派上很多用场。{w} 我在想……如果有人要穿越到过去，而我认定自己会在未来把他带到某个地方，那他在过去是不是就会出现在那里？即便穿越的人不是我，原点也可能出在我的意识里？',
        "Maybe he appeared with it. An important detail is that it was inactive. If he hid a powered-off Sekimeiya in his hip pack in the future, it's possible he appeared with it in the past.": '也许他是带着它一起出现的。关键的一点是，它当时处于关闭状态。{w} 如果他在未来把一个关掉的 Sekimeiya 藏进腰包，那他穿越回过去时就有可能带着它出现。',
        'I took the Future Sekimeiya out of the refrigerator and grabbed the disabled Past Sekimeiya. Half a minute later, I left it on the countertop and touched the Future Sekimeiya.': '我从冰箱里取出 未来Sekimeiya，再拿起那个已经无法使用的 过去Sekimeiya。{w} 半分钟后，我把它放在台面上，触碰了 未来Sekimeiya。',
        "What the hell? Can the Sekimeiya not be duplicated? It seems like the original one disappeared when I appeared with it in the future and disallowed the duplication. There's no way anyone came and took it during the nine seconds I wasn't here, right?": '搞什么？难道 Sekimeiya 不能被复制？{w} 看来，我带着它在未来出现之后，复制就没能成立，原本那一个也跟着消失了。总不可能有人趁我不在的那九秒里把它拿走吧？',
        "It's still working. I wonder if the fact that it was powered off mattered at all.": '它还能用。{w} 不知道它当时关着到底有没有影响。',
        'I repeated the same process but held the powered Past Sekimeiya with my sleeves for half a minute. Then, I left it in the refrigerator to avoid overlapping ranges and went nine seconds to the future.': '我又按同样的步骤做了一遍，只是这次隔着袖子，把启动中的过去Sekimeiya握了半分钟。{w} 然后，为了避免范围重叠，我把它放进冰箱，再穿越到九秒后。',
        "...I didn't appear with the Sekimeiya. My hands looked to be holding something that wasn't there.": '……{w}我没有带着 Sekimeiya 出现。两手还保持着握东西的姿势，可手里空无一物。',
        'What would happen if I did the reverse of this? Wouldn\'t the past change? If I go to the past holding the powered-off Future Sekimeiya, I would appear with it in the past, so the "original" one would disappear. That means that I couldn\'t hold it anymore when I\'m traveling to the past, thereby changing it.': '如果把顺序反过来，会怎么样？过去不就会被改变吗？{w} 如果我拿着关闭状态的 未来Sekimeiya 回到过去，我就会带着它在过去出现，那么「原本」那一个就会消失。也就是说，我穿越回过去时不可能还拿着它——过去就这样被改写了。',
        'Suddenly, I heard a sound coming from the kitchen. It scared me at first, but I immediately understood what it was. Nine seconds later, I entered through the door.': '忽然，厨房里传来一阵声响。我起初被吓了一跳，但马上就明白那是什么了。{w} 九秒后，我从门口走了进来。',
        "Why, though? I don't get it. ...Wait, no, I might have an idea.": '可是为什么？我想不通。{w}……等等，不对，我或许有点头绪。',
        "I think it's due to the infinite loop concept I thought of. If I had appeared with the powered-off Future Sekimeiya in the past, eighteen seconds later, it would've been closer to powering on. Once the infinite loop is applied, the Sekimeiya could've never appeared powered off, and when it's powered on, it doesn't count as a normal object. I believe that's why it didn't travel.": '我想，这跟先前设想的无限循环有关。{w}如果关掉的未来Sekimeiya随我一起出现在过去，那么十八秒后，它就更接近启动状态。套用无限循环后，Sekimeiya 就绝不可能以关闭状态出现；而启动状态下，它又不算普通物体。我认为这就是它没有跟着我穿越的原因。',
        "I've been figuring all of this out, but I still don't fully understand the most important aspect: the amount of time traveled. I've been repeatedly traveling nine seconds through time, so it has to be consistent as well.": '这些我已经一点点理清了，可最关键的一点仍没弄明白：穿越的时间长度。{w}我反复穿越的都是九秒，那它也应该是一致的才对。',
        "Thirty seconds stored equals nine seconds traveled. Two minutes stored equals 45 seconds traveled. There's already an indication here: each stored second turns into more amount of time traveled than the previous. In the first case, each second stored added 0.3 seconds traveled. In the second case, each second stored added 0.37 seconds traveled.": '蓄能三十秒，穿越九秒；蓄能两分钟，穿越 45 秒。{w}这里已经有迹象了：每多蓄一秒，换算出的穿越时间都比前一秒更多。第一种情况，每蓄一秒增加 0.3 秒；第二种情况，每蓄一秒增加 0.37 秒。',
        "And it's evident this keeps going—fifteen minutes stored led into twenty minutes traveled. In that case, each second stored added 1.3 seconds. Earlier, keeping the Sekimeiya out of the cabinet for 25 minutes made me travel about 45 minutes to the past. That's a pretty noticeable increase. Each stored second would've counted for 1.8 seconds traveled.": '而且很明显，这个趋势还在延续——蓄能十五分钟，穿越二十分钟。这样算下来，每蓄一秒等于 1.3 秒。{w}之前我把 Sekimeiya 放在展示柜外二十五分钟，结果穿越到了约四十五分钟前。增幅相当明显，每蓄一秒已经相当于 1.8 秒的穿越时间。',
        "So the more time it's gathered, the larger the increase is. It's exponential. The difference between five and ten minutes is very little compared to the difference between twenty and 25. For a while, the numbers will be low, but there'll be a point where they suddenly become immense. Once the Sekimeiya has been out of the cabinet for 35 minutes, how much will one stored second equal to? ...What about after an hour?": '也就是说，蓄能越久，增幅越大。这是指数级的。{w}五分钟到十分钟的差距，跟二十分钟到二十五分钟的差距相比微不足道。起初数值会很低，但总有一刻会突然变得极其庞大。{w}Sekimeiya 离开展示柜三十五分钟后，蓄一秒会等于多少？{w}……那一小时之后呢？',
        "There's an indication that I'm correct about this: Akaro and Shiroya. They traveled days through time, and so did I. Akaro said he touched the Sekimeiya while we were in the attic's bedroom, so it's very possible it stored energy for a long time.": '有件事可以证明我猜得没错：Akaro 和 Shiroya。{w}他们穿越了数日之久，我也是。Akaro 说，我们还在阁楼卧室时他碰过 Sekimeiya，所以它很可能已经蓄能了很长时间。',
        'There is something else that could follow a similar progression, which is the time it spends recovering. No matter the amount of time traveled, the Sekimeiya always spends a while gray. However, the amount of time stored seems to gradually add to the guaranteed amount.': '还有另一样东西也可能呈现类似的渐进变化，那就是它的恢复时间。{w}无论穿越多久，Sekimeiya 总会维持一段灰色状态。不过，蓄能的时长似乎会一点点累加到那段保底时间上。',
        'What could it be? A formula that increases the amount each second adds as more seconds have passed... If I could figure it out, I could use the Sekimeiya to appear at any point in time.': '会是什么公式？蓄能秒数越多，每秒换算出的时长也跟着增加的公式……{w}如果能解出来，我就能用 Sekimeiya 出现在任何时间点。',
        "Why was I so preoccupied with the idea? Was it due to mere curiosity? No. That wasn't all. At some point, I had realized it.": '我为什么对这件事如此执着？只是出于好奇吗？{w}不，不只是这样。在某个时候，我已经意识到了这一点。',
        "While locked in the tower for twelve hours, I'd spent a long time trying to figure out if saving Miiya was possible. And I knew, at that moment, that it was. However, those thoughts had all faded from my mind some time previously. Shiroya had caused me to abandon the idea of saving her. But I'd learned that wasn't the real Shiroya, and it made a lot of sense—she would never have said that. She had wanted to save Miiya just like me and had been prepared to do it once I'd told her it was possible.": '被困在塔里的那十二个小时里，我花了很长时间思考救下 Miiya 是否可行。而在那一刻，我就已经知道这是可行的。{w}可那些念头，之前不知什么时候已经从我心里淡去了。是 Shiroya 让我放弃了救 Miiya 的念头。{w}但我后来知道，那不是真正的 Shiroya——这就说得通了，她绝不会说出那种话。她和我一样想救 Miiya，只要我告诉她这是可行的，她早就准备好了。',
        "Before traveling the 45 seconds, I'll read the note with the formula. Then, 45 seconds in the past, I'll write it down so that my original self can see it. Would this allow me to spend two hours finding the formula without actually having to waste that time?": '在穿越那 45 秒之前，我会先读那张写着公式的纸条。然后回到 45 秒前，把它写下来，好让原本的我能看到。{w}这样一来，我岂不是能花两个小时找出公式，却又不必真的耗掉那两个小时？',
        'There was no point in assuming an answer because it was easy to test. I readied myself to perform the loop and started to store time with the Past Sekimeiya. However, when I looked at the drawer where I wanted the note to be hidden, it was empty.': '凭空假定答案没有意义，因为这件事一试便知。我做好准备，要执行这个循环，便用过去Sekimeiya开始蓄能。{w}然而，当我看向那个准备用来藏纸条的抽屉时，里面空无一物。',
        "Am I mistaken, then? Is this concept just unworkable? That can't be. It's the same thing as the recorder powering off when I go to the past: the hypothetical realities in which it progressively loses battery need to exist in order for it to appear without power in the real one.": '那么是我想错了？这套思路根本行不通？{w}不可能。这跟我回到过去时录音笔会断电是一个道理：它只有在那些假想世界里一点点耗尽电量，才会在真正的现实里以没电的状态出现。',
        "The tower will open at 21:00, so assuming no one else comes, even in a hypothetical world, I would only have until 21:00 to experiment... Actually, probably way less than that, because to travel to the past and appear in the tower, I'd have to be inside it hours after 21:00.": '塔在 {time=21} 开放，所以假设没有别人来，即便在假想世界里，我也只能在 {time=21} 之前做实验……不，实际能用的时间恐怕还要短得多：要回到过去并出现在塔里，我得在 {time=21.} 之后还在塔里待上好几个小时。',
        "The tower will open at 9 p.m., so assuming no one else comes, even in a hypothetical world, I would only have until 9 p.m. to experiment... Actually, probably way less than that, because to travel to the past and appear in the tower, I'd have to be inside it hours after 9 p.m.": '塔在 {time=21} 开放，所以假设没有别人来，即便在假想世界里，我也只能在 {time=21} 之前做实验……不，实际能用的时间恐怕还要短得多：要回到过去并出现在塔里，我得在 {time=21.} 之后还在塔里待上好几个小时。',
        "...But assuming I had all the time I needed, would I be able to use a hypothetical world to my advantage? Could I make use of countless hours without actually spending any? ...I considered that there might've been a way to test it.": '……不过，假如时间充裕，我能不能把假想世界利用起来？能不能用掉无数个小时，而现实中一个小时都不必花？{w}……我想，或许有办法验证这一点。',
        "...If I touch the Sekimeiya when fifteen minutes have passed, I'll go twenty minutes to the past. But before I touch it, I'll open the door to the hallway and find a notepad from the bedrooms on the floor. Depending on what it says, I'll do one of three things.": '……{w}等过了十五分钟，我再去碰 Sekimeiya，就会回到二十分钟前。{w}不过在碰它之前，我要先打开通往走廊的门，看看地上有没有从卧室拿来的笔记本。看上面写着什么，我再决定做三件事中的哪一件。',
        "3: If I find a notepad that doesn't contain the formula, it will have my current progress along with a number in the top left corner of the first page, which will indicate the amount of iterations that have occurred so far. I'll go back to the past, and using the information I read in the notepad, I'll start working to find the formula. Before the twenty minutes pass, I'll write down the updated progress in a notepad from the bedrooms, increase the number I saw in the top left corner by one, and then leave the notepad in the hallway.": '三：如果找到的笔记本上没有公式，那上面会写着我当前的进展，第一页左上角还有一个数字，代表到目前为止已经重复了多少轮。{w}我就回到过去，依据笔记本上读到的内容继续推算公式。二十分钟结束前，我把更新后的进展写进一本从卧室拿来的笔记本，再把左上角的数字加一，然后把笔记本留在走廊。',
        '...I realized the plan had a small flaw.': '……{w}我意识到，这个计划有一个小小的漏洞。',
        "But if in the real world, I open the hallway door and find no notepad, I'll think that the plan hasn't worked and won't go through with the first loop. In the same way, the first hypothetical version of me, instead of assuming that he's about to start the first iteration, would assume that the plan is flawed and wouldn't start the sequence. If I want this to work, I'll have to execute the first loop in the instance that I don't find a notepad in the hallway right now. This is okay, because even though the plan wouldn't work for me, I'd have to resort to trying to find the formula manually in the real world. Executing the first loop would work toward that, and it would make the plan succeed if the concept is valid.": '可如果我在现实世界里打开走廊的门，什么笔记本都没找到，我就会认定计划失败，也不会去走第一轮。同样，第一个假想中的我也不会认为自己正要开始第一轮，而会断定计划有破绽，从而不肯启动这一连串循环。要让计划成立，我必须在此时此刻——在走廊里没有找到笔记本的这一刻——照样执行第一轮。{w}这没关系，因为即便这套计划对我无效，我在现实中也只能靠手工去推公式。执行第一轮正是在为此铺路；而只要那个构想成立，计划就会因此成功。',
        "I appeared in the kitchen and immediately saw the disabled Future Sekimeiya under the water. Then I looked at the oven and saw the amount of time I'd gone to the future. The timer was at 4:31, immediately ticking down to 4:30.": '我出现在厨房，立刻看见水里那个已经停摆的未来Sekimeiya。接着我看向烤箱，看看自己往未来跳了多久。{w}计时器显示 4:31，转眼就跳成了 4:30。',
        "29 seconds. I have gone 29 seconds forward. So I was right. There's another factor: the temperature.": '29 秒。我向前跳了 29 秒。{w}果然，我没猜错。还有一个因素：{w}温度。',
        "But the heat capacity of water is four times the air's, meaning that it heats up four times slower. It appears a temperature higher than the cabinet lets the Sekimeiya store energy and become hot. Of course, that heats up the air around it. Then, that same air makes the Sekimeiya even hotter, leading into the infinite increase of energy.": '可水的比热是空气的四倍，升温速度也就慢四倍。{w}看来，只要周围温度高于展示柜内部，Sekimeiya 就能蓄能并升温。它当然也会把周围的空气加热。{w}而这些空气又让它更热，如此循环，能量便无止境地增长。',
        "That's why. For those fifteen minutes, the Sekimeiya was in her purse. That led to the opposite situation as the water. The air inside the purse couldn't easily escape, so it heated up faster than outside it. That is the reason why the range was bigger. And Sai, the only person who actually traveled through time, would have been sent more than twenty minutes.": '原来如此。那十五分钟里，Sekimeiya 一直在她的手提包里。{w}这就和水里的情形正好相反。包里的空气不易散出，升温比包外更快。范围之所以更大，原因就在这里。{w}而真正穿越了时间的只有 Sai，他应该被送去了二十多分钟之外。',
        "At 9:00, the smoke was released in the tower, beginning the attack that trapped us inside. What triggered the alarm? Was anyone aware of the Sekimeiya's powers? I'm still not sure about the details behind it, but it's a lot clearer now.": '{time=9}，塔内释放了烟雾，那场把我们困在里面的袭击就此开始。警报是谁触发的？有人知道 Sekimeiya 的力量吗？背后的细节我仍不清楚，但现在已经明朗了许多。',
        "At 9 a.m., the smoke was released in the tower, beginning the attack that trapped us inside. What triggered the alarm? Was anyone aware of the Sekimeiya's powers? I'm still not sure about the details behind it, but it's a lot clearer now.": '{time=9}，塔内释放了烟雾，那场把我们困在里面的袭击就此开始。警报是谁触发的？有人知道 Sekimeiya 的力量吗？背后的细节我仍不清楚，但现在已经明朗了许多。',
        'While we were asleep, someone hid the Sekimeiya in room B4 and turned on the temperature regulation. Was it Naomi? In this world, she ran up to the attic with them.': '我们睡着的时候，有人把 Sekimeiya 藏进了 B4房间，还打开了温度调节。{w}是 Naomi 吗？在这个世界里，是她带着它们跑上了阁楼。',
        "There's also Katei. He wasn't in the security room, and he has to be who dropped the rusty key in hallway A. Beyond the truth of the attack, the third Sekimeiya, the one that doesn't work, was the only one inside the cabinet when we woke up. When Isla touched it, nothing happened to her.": '还有 Katei。他不在监控室，A走廊里那把生锈的钥匙一定是他掉的。{w}除了袭击的真相之外，还有一点：我们醒来时，展示柜里只剩下第三个 Sekimeiya，也就是那个失效的。Isla 碰了它，却什么也没有发生。',
        "I think it was Katei. The person who was sitting in front of the computer. When it happened, we were about to look at the recorded footage. That would've revealed that he hadn't been in the security room and who knows what else.": '我想是 Katei。就是坐在电脑前的那个人。{w}当时我们正要查看录下的画面。那会揭穿他根本不在监控室，天知道还会带出什么别的东西。',
        'And even that wasn\'t all. We tried to communicate with the outside a second time, but upon inputting his credentials, an "Access Denied" message appeared. Why? I\'m not completely sure why he would\'ve done that, but he could\'ve purposely entered an incorrect password to prompt that message. Perhaps there was a reason why he couldn\'t allow a second call, but he must\'ve done that. After all, there\'s no way Ashiya would\'ve been the ones to cut our single method of communication.': '而且事情还不止这些。我们第二次尝试与外界联络，输入他的账号信息后，却弹出了「拒绝访问」的提示。{w}为什么？我并不完全确定他为什么要这样做，但他很可能故意输错密码，好让那行提示出现。也许出于某种原因，他不能让第二次通话打通，而这事一定是他做的。毕竟，芦屋那边绝不可能自己切断我们唯一的联络方式。',
        "...He wasn't in the security room when the smoke went off, but one of the things he said was that he'd tried to do his part of removing the shutter and that the system hadn't let him. That didn't actually happen, but Suripo told us that a similar error was affecting Ashiya. Since Katei knew or lied about it without experiencing it, it follows he was probably the cause behind it. He didn't want the exit to open before the time limit. Therefore, there was something he had to do before the time expired, and deleting the saved footage was likely part of that. When we were done, we left him alone in the security room. That was the time we later learned footage had been erased; he used it to briefly reconnect the system and delete what he didn't want us to see.": '……烟雾弥漫的时候，他并不在监控室，但他说过一句话：他试过拆下自己负责的那部分卷帘门，系统却没让他操作。{w}这件事其实并没有发生，可 Suripo 告诉过我们，芦屋那边也出现了类似的故障。既然 Katei 没亲身经历却能知道这件事，或者干脆是在撒谎，那么他很可能就是造成这起故障的人。他不想让出口在时限之前打开。{w}也就是说，在时限结束前，他有非做不可的事，而删除已存的录像多半就是其中一环。{w}我们办完事之后，把他一个人留在了监控室。后来我们才知道，录像正是在那段时间被抹掉的——他利用那段时间短暂地接回系统，删掉了他不想让我们看到的东西。',
        "From the sixth floor, the elevator went to the attic. Of course, we didn't hear that. Then, that Naomi used it to go all the way down.": '电梯从六楼开到了阁楼。当然，我们并没有听见。{w}随后，那个 Naomi 又乘着它一路下到了底层。',
        "If she was still down there, we couldn't let her keep escaping. Shiroya and I waited in front of the elevator while the others went down to make sure we'd find her. Suddenly, we heard the elevator going up.": '如果她还在下面，我们就不能再让她这样一次次脱身。Shiroya 和我守在电梯前，其他人则下楼去，确保能找到她。{w}忽然，我们听见电梯升了上来。',
        "Someone coming from the future could've killed her, but I'm inclined to think it was actually Katei. It happened in the room where the Sekimeiya were hidden, and in this world, Naomi didn't bring them there. That makes me think it was Katei who did.": '从未来过来的人也可能杀了她，但我更倾向于认为动手的就是 Katei。{w}事情发生在藏匿 Sekimeiya 的那间房里，而在这一世界，把 Sekimeiya 带过去的人并不是 Naomi。所以我才会认为是 Katei 干的。',
        "The truth was out, so Katei attempted a bribe. If they obtained the Sekimeiya, both of them could work together to trade it off. Immediately, Naomi refused—she was Ashiya's most trusted employee. The third step was a threat. With a calm voice, Katei let her pick between Ashiya or her own safety. He needed her to stay quiet, and starting immediately; she knew two real Sekimeiya existed. However, as Katei's words were dismissed again, he finally wavered. He had been acting stern, but that was far from reality. Inwardly, Katei burned with rage toward Naomi.": '真相已经败露，Katei 便试着收买她。要是拿到 Sekimeiya，两人就能联手把它转手卖掉。{w}Naomi 当即拒绝——她可是芦屋最受信任的员工。{w}第三步，他改用威胁。Katei 用平静的语气让她在芦屋和自己的安危之间做选择。他必须让她立刻保持沉默；她已经知道有两块真正的 Sekimeiya。{w}然而，她再次拒绝，他终于动摇了。他一直摆出强硬的样子，其实那全是装出来的。内心深处，Katei 对 Naomi 已是怒火中烧。',
        'After a sudden step forward, Katei dashed at her. She had enough time to react and defend herself, but she was no match for him. After an abrupt scuffle, Katei dragged her to the wall and knocked her out. Before her death, Naomi let out a yell that only reached a single pair of ears outside the room: her own.': 'Katei 猛然踏前一步，朝她扑了过去。{w}她有足够的时间反应，也出手自卫，但根本不是他的对手。一阵短促的扭打之后，Katei 把她拖到墙边，打昏了她。临死之前，Naomi 发出了一声喊叫，而门外听见这声音的只有一双耳朵——她自己的。',
        "From above, Katei stared at Naomi's body, unaware that a cabinet's temperature wheel had been damaged. Seconds later, he finally checked her breathing. ...There was none. But all wasn't lost. Earlier, he had turned off that room's camera. He had known that he would have to take one of the Sekimeiya away eventually, so he had preemptively disabled the video. But although he hadn't been recorded, he knew he was the only possible suspect.": 'Katei 居高临下地望着 Naomi 的尸体，没有察觉展示柜的温度转盘已被撞坏。几秒之后，他才去探她的呼吸。……已经没有了。{w}但事情还没有到山穷水尽的地步。早些时候，他已经关掉了那间房的摄像头。他早就知道自己迟早要带走一个 Sekimeiya，因此提前让监控失效了。{w}可是，尽管没有被拍下来，他也清楚自己是唯一可能的嫌疑人。',
        "...That was until he heard a sudden sound that forced him out of the room. Outside, he saw Atsuki's lone figure. Katei rapidly stepped aside; he couldn't afford to be seen. However, Atsuki had just been recorded by the cameras, so there was another potential culprit to build a narrative against. Before he walked back up, Katei thought about what he had to say. He had killed someone else after all those years, and he could find another way out.": '……直到一阵突如其来的声响把他逼出了房间。到了外面，他看见了 Atsuki 孤零零的身影。{w}Katei 迅速闪到一旁，绝不能让人看见自己。不过，Atsuki 刚刚被摄像头拍了下来，也就是说，还有一个可以拿来做文章的可疑对象。{w}在往回走之前，Katei 盘算着该说些什么。时隔这么多年，他又杀了人，而他还能另寻出路。',
        "The Sekimeiya turned gray, so we brought it to its cabinet in the event room, where it became white again. We heard a sound coming from outside. After all, someone else was still lurking within the tower—the Naomi who took the elevator down. The corpse had stopped our search, and we'd never looked into every room.": '那个 Sekimeiya 变成了灰色，我们便把它送回活动室里它原本的展示柜，它在那里又变回了白色。{w}我们听见外面传来声响。毕竟，塔里还藏着另一个人——乘电梯下楼的 Naomi。那具尸体让我们中断了搜索，我们始终没有把每一间房都查遍。',
        'Had it been taken already? We went to the event room, and it was in fact gone from the cabinet. Who hid it in the storeroom? That question ate at me.': '难道它已经被人拿走了？我们赶到活动室，展示柜里果然空了。{w} 是谁把它藏进了储藏室？这个问题始终缠着我不放。',
        "I believe I now understand what happened. To get the Sekimeiya out of the event room's cabinet, the key was necessary, and it was with Naomi's corpse in room B4. That means someone who investigated hallway B must have taken it to unlock the cabinet. However, none of them had the chance to hide it in the storeroom without being seen by the people who'd investigated hallway A. That's why it didn't make sense.": '我想，我现在明白是怎么回事了。{w} 要把 Sekimeiya 从活动室的展示柜里取出来，就必须用到钥匙；而钥匙就在 B4 房间里 Naomi 的尸体旁。也就是说，搜查 B走廊的人当中，必定有人取走钥匙打开了展示柜。{w} 但搜查 A走廊的人一直看在眼里，B走廊那几个人谁都没机会把 Sekimeiya 藏进储藏室而不被发现。所以那件事才说不通。',
        "It wasn't the same Sekimeiya. The first mystery regarding its whereabouts already pointed at the truth that more than one Sekimeiya existed. ...After all, when Sai left the storeroom, he made me touch it, and nothing happened. It was definitely the third Sekimeiya—the one that had disappeared from the event room the first time. The Past Sekimeiya was in room B4 since we'd regained consciousness, so we never actually found the one that disappeared first.": '那不是同一个 Sekimeiya。最初关于它下落的谜团，其实早已指向一个事实：Sekimeiya 不止一块。{w} ……毕竟，Sai 离开储藏室时让我碰过它，却什么也没发生。{w} 那肯定就是第三个 Sekimeiya——最初从活动室消失的那一块。自我们醒来后，过去Sekimeiya 就一直在 B4 房间里；也就是说，我们从未真正找到最初消失的那一块。',
        "Who hid the third Sekimeiya in the storeroom? That happened before Shiroya, Akaro, and I walked down from the sixth floor. I don't believe it was Katei because he's likely the one who hid the two working Sekimeiya. If he wanted to also hide the third, which was originally in the event room, he would have done so while we were asleep. I don't believe the other Naomi would have wanted to leave it there either.": '是谁把第三个 Sekimeiya 藏进了储藏室？那是发生在我、Shiroya 和 Akaro 从六楼下来之前的事。{w} 我不认为是 Katei。藏起那两块还能用的 Sekimeiya 的人，多半就是他。若他还想连原本放在活动室的第三块也一并藏起来，趁我们睡着时动手就行了。{w} 我也不认为另一个 Naomi 会愿意把它留在那里。',
        "Sai guarded hallway A from the stairs while Katei guarded hallway B and the lobby. As the hallway B rooms were inspected, Sai could've gone to the event room to take the gemstone and hide it in the storeroom.": 'Sai 守住楼梯口，负责盯 A走廊；Katei 则守着 B走廊和大厅。{w} 在 B走廊的房间被逐一检查时，Sai 本有机会去活动室取走宝石，再把它藏进储藏室。',
        "Why would he have done that? ...At that point, we hadn't learned about the Sekimeiya's powers yet. During the morning, Sai's attitude was different from how it was later. He often talked with me about what he thought and was visibly enjoying what was happening around him. When did that change, exactly? I believe it was when we found out about time travel. He became a lot more reserved and hard to read. If he hid the Sekimeiya so early, his motive likely aligned to his original attitude.": '他为什么要那么做？{w} ……那时我们还没弄清 Sekimeiya 的力量。{w} 那天早上，Sai 的态度和后来截然不同。他常跟我谈起自己的想法，也看得出他很享受身边发生的事。他究竟是什么时候变的？{w} 我想，是在我们得知时间穿越之后。他变得沉默许多，让人看不透。若他在那么早的时候就藏起了 Sekimeiya，动机多半与他最初的态度有关。',
        "The event room and hallway A weren't being recorded. He chose the storeroom, another place without cameras. Later on, he acted as if he'd found it there, so I don't think his intention was to keep it. Did he do it for fun, or did he have a better reason? In any case, it's likely he already knew that he would point the finger at Katei, who he immediately accused.": '活动室和 A走廊都没有监控。他选了同样没有摄像头的储藏室。后来他又装出是在那里发现它的样子，所以我觉得，他并不打算把它留在手里。{w} 是出于好玩，还是另有更充分的理由？无论如何，他恐怕早就知道自己会把矛头指向 Katei——毕竟他一开口便指控了 Katei。',
        "I was told Shiroya and Akaro looked through the rooms while Sai watched the hallway like I did. We had to make sure the person we were searching for was found, so the search took a while. During the time Shiroya and Akaro were inside the crystal rooms, Sai had the chance to pick up the key in room B4, take the Sekimeiya from the event room, and then hide it somewhere in hallway B. After that, he slipped the cabinet key into Shiroya's purse as soon as possible.": '我听说，Shiroya 和 Akaro 逐个查看房间时，Sai 像我一样守在走廊里。为了确保能找到那个人，搜查花了不少时间。在 Shiroya 和 Akaro 进入水晶展室期间，Sai 有机会去 B4 房间取走钥匙，从活动室拿走 Sekimeiya，再把它藏到 B走廊的某处。{w} 之后，他又尽快把展示柜的钥匙塞进了 Shiroya 的手袋。',
        "By acting like he'd found the Sekimeiya in the storeroom, he removed any potential blame from himself. I didn't really think about it, but he said we couldn't trust Katei's search and never ended up looking at all the other rooms Katei went through.": '他装出在储藏室里发现 Sekimeiya 的样子，让自己摆脱了可能受到的怀疑。{w} 我当时没怎么细想，但他说过不能相信 Katei 的搜查，最后也没有把 Katei 查过的其余房间逐一查看。',
        "And still, I'm sure there's another reason Sai did that. I don't know why, but everyone thought only one Sekimeiya existed. By finding the one that didn't work, he made sure we wouldn't search for the one he had hidden.": '不过，我确信 Sai 那么做还有另一个理由。{w} 不知为何，所有人都以为只存在一个 Sekimeiya。他找到那个不能用的，正是为了让我们不去寻找他藏起来的那个。',
        'I see... That must be the answer to that question. "Why is the Sekimeiya being hidden when it can easily be found?" I wonder who knew the truth. I wonder who knew that three Sekimeiya existed. The people who did kept hiding them because leaving the third one in the event room cabinet meant no one would look for others. The quality of their hiding spots hardly mattered—we just found one Sekimeiya and thought that was it. Maybe they were often poorly hidden precisely so that we\'d find one and stop the search before coming across another.': '原来如此……那个问题的答案一定就是这个。{w} 「为什么 Sekimeiya 明明很容易就能找到，却总被人藏起来？」{w} 我想知道，究竟是谁知道真相。是谁知道存在三个 Sekimeiya。{w} 知情者之所以一再把它们藏起来，是因为只要把第三个留在活动室展示柜里，我们便不会再去寻找其他 Sekimeiya。藏得是否妥当并不重要——我们只要找到一个 Sekimeiya，就会以为只有这一个。说不定它们之所以常常被藏得很草率，正是为了让我们找到一个后就此收手，不会撞见另一个。',
        "We still hadn't found the Naomi who'd made the sound, which meant that she had successfully escaped upstairs. That's why we searched through the higher floors. Shiroya and I stayed on the fifth, and although we didn't hear anything, something strange happened with the elevator.": '我们始终没找到那个发出声响的 Naomi，这说明她已经成功逃到楼上。所以我们才去搜查更高的楼层。{w} 我和 Shiroya 留在五楼，虽然我们什么声音都没听见，电梯却出了怪事。',
        "Then, inside it, we found Naomi's second body. However, I later traveled forty minutes to the past and appeared on the crystal floor before we'd all come back down.": '随后，我们在里面发现了 Naomi 的第二具尸体。{w} 可后来，我却穿越回四十分钟前，出现在水晶层——那时我们所有人都还没下楼。',
        "Somehow, the search failed to find her. A different person stayed on each floor, so it's possible one wasn't investigated—the floor the person who used the elevator was supposed to guard. ...Erina and Isla were on the second floor. Sai was on the third floor. Akaro was on the fourth floor. Shiroya and I were on the fifth floor. Katei was on the sixth floor.": '不知为何，搜查没能找到她。{w} 每一层都安排了不同的人留守，所以也许有一层根本没被搜查——就是本该由乘电梯的人守着的那一层。{w} ……Erina 和 Isla 在二楼。Sai 在三楼。Akaro 在四楼。我和 Shiroya 在五楼。Katei 在六楼。',
        "Then, he used it to go to the crystal floor... Why, though? I can't help but remember that it was him who proposed this arrangement. He wanted us to stay separated between different floors, leaving the crystal floor vacant.": '然后，他乘电梯去了水晶层……可他为什么要这么做？{w} 我不由得想起，提出这种安排的人正是他。他希望我们分散在不同楼层，好让水晶层空着。',
        "Later, he would've gone back to the fourth floor, and finally, he would've sent it to the fifth, where it was supposed to be. Shiroya and I wouldn't have noticed that. It definitely ended up there: Sai confirmed it when he called it from the crystal floor.": '之后，他再返回四楼，最后把电梯送回它本该停在的五楼。我和 Shiroya 不会察觉。{w} 电梯确实回到了那里：Sai 从水晶层叫电梯时，就确认了这一点。',
        "I don't get it, though. Why would Akaro do that? He knew his trips up and down could be heard, didn't he? And Erina and Isla didn't hear the elevator even once. I suppose it's possible Akaro stopped on floor 2 and then used the elevator to the crystal floor if he knew that wouldn't be heard, but if that happened, surely he would've done the same on floor 3 so that Sai wouldn't hear him either...": '可我还是不明白。Akaro 为什么要那么做？他明知道自己乘电梯上下会被人听见，不是吗？{w} 而且 Erina 和 Isla 一次也没听见电梯声。我也想过，如果 Akaro 知道这样不会被听见，他或许会先停在二楼，再乘电梯去水晶层；可如果真是这样，他在三楼时也该照做，免得被 Sai 听见才对……',
        "Who had taken it? Not only the one in the cart, but also one of the two Akaro had left in the event room before lying on the floor. Silently, Akaro continued watching Katei, but it could've been Naomi as well. Katei was acting like only one Sekimeiya existed, and Akaro didn't know the reason. It was rational to conclude that one of them being in a cold cabinet indicated the other was as well.": '是谁拿走的？不只是推车里的那一块，就连 Akaro 躺到地上之前留在活动室的两块中也少了一块。Akaro 默不作声地继续观察 Katei，但拿走它的也可能是 Naomi。{w} Katei 的举动仿佛只存在一个 Sekimeiya，而 Akaro 不知道其中缘由。既然有一块被放进了低温展示柜，那另一块很可能也在同样的地方，这么想才说得通。',
        "During the previous search, he had looked through that room. He knew there was another cabinet that had been set to 0 °C. The other real Sekimeiya was there, and it was all he needed. He only had to keep one hidden, but there weren't many places he could think of.": '在先前那次搜查中，他查看过那个房间。他知道那里还有另一个设定为 0 °C 的展示柜。{w} 另一块真正的 Sekimeiya 就在里面，而这正是他需要的。他只要藏起一块就够了，可一时也想不出多少合适的地方。',
        "When I was staring at the bathroom door, Naomi appeared from the other side of hallway C. She likely came from above. She was the Naomi who'd appeared in the attic, but her actions differed from the Naomi who'd been killed. Why? Why didn't she ask to talk to Katei? What was she doing, exactly, moving around through the building?": '我正盯着洗手间的门时，Naomi 从 C走廊的另一头走了出来。她多半是从楼上下来的。{w} 她就是那个出现在阁楼里的 Naomi，可她的举动却和被杀死的那个 Naomi 不同。为什么？她为什么没有要求见 Katei？她在楼里四处走动，究竟是在做什么？',
        "They traveled to the future. After all, I'm pretty sure the Past Sekimeiya was in one of hallway B's crystal rooms, which is where Shiroya and I later traveled from. Maybe I should've pieced together the reason why no Sekimeiya was found in the bathroom...": '凶手穿越到了未来。毕竟，我很确定 过去Sekimeiya 就在 B走廊的某间水晶展室里，而我和 Shiroya 后来正是从那里出发穿越的。{w}或许我早该想到，为什么洗手间里找不到任何 Sekimeiya……',
        'So, the person who traveled to the future... who was it? Who killed Naomi? Knowing all of that, the answer has to be Akaro...': '那么，那个穿越到未来的人……究竟是谁？是谁杀了 Naomi？{w}既然已经知道这些，答案只能是 Akaro……',
        "And it never happened. I watched from a distance for minutes, and when the group came from the attic, Akaro was already there. I can only think he teleported inside. Why didn't he leave, though?": '而那种情况始终没有出现。我在远处观察了好几分钟，等众人从阁楼下来时，Akaro 已经在那里了。我只能想到，他是传送进去的。{w}可他为什么没有离开？',
        "That's gotta be due to the mental state we found him in. He looked out of it and unresponsive, likely because he had just killed a second Naomi who couldn't have existed. After locking the door, he touched the Sekimeiya in the bathroom and went some amount of minutes into the future. Seeing as he appeared in the bathroom, it makes me think it was him who hid the Sekimeiya there in the past. That's why he knew where it was and why he rapidly activated it in an attempt to escape.": '那一定跟他被发现时的精神状态有关。他看上去神志恍惚、毫无反应，大概是因为他刚刚杀死了本不该存在的第二个 Naomi。{w}锁上门后，他碰了洗手间里的 Sekimeiya，穿越到了若干分钟之后。既然他出现在洗手间里，我就觉得，之前把 Sekimeiya 藏在那里的人就是他。所以他才知道它在哪里，也才会为了逃跑而迅速启动它。',
        "The only explanation for all of this is that he traveled to the past. Later, he even admitted to having touched the Sekimeiya. That makes a lot of sense. If Sai hid it in the crystal room that Shiroya and I later traveled from, we would've gone much more than forty minutes into the past.": '这一切唯一的解释，就是他穿越回到了过去。后来他甚至承认自己碰过 Sekimeiya。{w}这样就说得通了。如果 Sai 把它藏在了那间水晶展室——我和 Shiroya 后来就是从那里出发穿越的——那我们就会回到比四十分钟前更早的时间。',
        "That makes me think that Akaro saw through Sai. Maybe he was aware that more than one Sekimeiya existed. If that was the case, from his point of view, only Sai could've hidden the Past Sekimeiya. He knew the one we found in the storeroom wasn't the same one, so it wouldn't have been too hard to find out where it was. I remember that Shiroya found it quickly because she noticed a slight bump in one of the gem cabinets.": '这让我觉得，Akaro 看穿了 Sai。也许他知道 Sekimeiya 不止一个。{w}若果真如此，在他看来，能藏起过去Sekimeiya 的人就只有 Sai。他知道我们在储藏室找到的那个并不是同一个，因此要查出它藏在哪里并不算难。我记得 Shiroya 很快就找到了它，因为她注意到其中一个宝石展示柜有轻微的凸起。',
        "Later, Akaro said that upon touching the Sekimeiya, he teleported. However, he assured us he hadn't traveled through time. He said he'd seen us searching through the floor, but he was probably referring to the search from minutes prior.": '后来，Akaro 说他一碰到 Sekimeiya 就传送了。但他向我们保证自己并没有时间穿越。{w}他说看见我们在楼层里搜寻，可他指的应该是几分钟前的那次搜查。',
        "I don't know why he killed Naomi, but this has to be the truth. ...Was murdering her the cause of the state we found him in? When we saw him, the first thing he did was ask Sai for the time, and when he heard it, he said that he hadn't traveled through time—that he'd only teleported.": '我不知道他为什么要杀 Naomi，但真相一定就是这样。……杀害她，是不是就是我们发现他时那副状态的原因？{w}我们见到他时，他做的第一件事就是向 Sai 询问时间；听到答案后，他说自己并没有时间穿越——只是传送了而已。',
        "Wouldn't this explain it? He went minutes to the past. I could probably calculate the exact amount, but that seems unnecessary. There, he killed Naomi and immediately went to the future when he heard me approaching the bathroom. If both travels were similar in length, upon being told the current time, he would've thought that he hadn't traveled through time at all, especially because he appeared in the bathroom when he went to the future. He barely moved, so there was no way he'd earlier gone to the past... But there seemed to be more to it than that. Akaro's voice seemed deeper in denial.": '这样不就解释得通了吗？{w}他穿越到了几分钟前。具体是几分钟，我大概算得出来，但似乎没这个必要。{w}他在那里杀了 Naomi，随后一听见我走近洗手间，就立刻穿越到了未来。{w}如果两次穿越的时长差不多，那么当他被告知当前时间时，就会以为自己根本没有穿越过——尤其因为他穿越到未来后又出现在了洗手间里。他几乎没挪动过位置，所以怎么也想不到自己先前竟去了过去……{w}但事情似乎不止如此。Akaro 的声音里，那种否认的意味更深。',
        "In the bathroom, when the door opened, what Akaro last expected was to see Naomi lying on the floor again. He had been incredibly worried that she'd seen him missing in the event room. If that had happened, she was a massive threat.": '洗手间的门打开时，Akaro 最不愿看到的，就是 Naomi 又一次躺在地上。{w}他一直极为担心她发现他不在活动室。若真如此，她便是极大的威胁。',
        "Yet, for some reason, it hadn't ended there. Once he had progressed to different worries, Naomi had appeared dead a second time. Akaro had no idea what was happening inside the tower. He only wanted his plan to succeed in order to have a future ahead of him.": '可不知为何，事情并没有就此结束。当他开始操心别的事情时，Naomi 又一次死在了他眼前。{w}Akaro 完全不知道塔里正在发生什么。他只想让计划成功，好让自己还有未来。',
        "The third time he saw Naomi's face, her eyes were staring into his. It couldn't be real; he doubted the stability of his own mind. When her mouth opened, the words Akaro had been dreading entered his ears. She knew he had left the event room, and she knew that he'd been concealing it.": '第三次看见 Naomi 的脸时，她的双眼正死死盯着他。那不可能是真的；他开始怀疑自己的神志是否还清醒。{w}当她开口时，Akaro 最害怕听到的话钻进了耳朵。她知道他离开过活动室，也知道他一直在隐瞒这件事。',
        'And now that I think about it, someone reacted differently to both suitcases. Katei.': '现在回想起来，有个人对两只行李箱的反应并不一样。{w}Katei。',
        "Thinking about it, it's very unlikely the device traveled to December 15th. Isla said it was impossible someone dropped it in her purse, which means it was there when she entered the tower.": '仔细想想，这支录音笔几乎不可能是穿越到十二月十五日的。{w}Isla 说过，不可能有人把它丢进她的手提包，也就是说，她进塔时它就已经在里面了。',
        'I think... I know the answer. It has to be due to her "friend".': '我想……我知道答案了。{w}一定和她的「朋友」有关。',
        'Apparently, when Sai and Akaro escaped from the attic, they met with "Isla". Even Erina heard her from the bedroom. She was dead at that point, so she probably wasn\'t the same Isla we\'d been with. Despite that, we never found her after we left the bedroom, so one explanation is that she traveled to the past at around that time.': '听说 Sai 和 Akaro 从阁楼逃出来时，遇见了「Isla」。连 Erina 都在卧室里听见了她的声音。可她当时已经死了，所以那多半不是与我们待在一起的那个 Isla。{w} 尽管如此，我们离开卧室后始终没再找到她，所以有一种解释是：她大约在那个时候穿越回了过去。',
        "So, what happened to the device after it recorded the audio? Isla saw Sai hiding it, and she ended up with it. If the replicated location was from a time where she still had it in the future, she would've appeared with it in the past.": '那么，那支录音笔录下音频之后，又发生了什么？Isla 看见 Sai 把它藏了起来，最后东西落到了她手上。{w} 如果复制的地点对应的是她未来仍然持有录音笔的那个时间，那么她回到过去时就会随身带着它。',
        'I can\'t know that, but it\'s likely the recorder appeared inside her friend\'s purse. Then, both Islas tried to hide the existence of the "friend" from Erina. Two identical purses were in the past. There was probably a mix-up at some point, like the original Isla mistakenly taking the wrong purse on the day of the event for some reason.': '这一点我无法确定，但录音笔很可能就是出现在她朋友的手提包里。随后，两个 Isla 都试图向 Erina 隐瞒「朋友」的存在。{w} 过去有两只一模一样的手提包。中途大概发生过一次拿错，比如原本的 Isla 因为某种缘故，在事件当天误拿了另一只包。',
        "After we listened to it, Shiroya and I left the attic alone. Going down the floors, we came across Akaro, who kept walking up. Then, on the crystal floor, we saw that the Sekimeiya we left in the event room was no longer there. Someone took the third Sekimeiya out of the cabinet. ...Who would've wanted to do that? At first glance, Akaro seemed to be the only candidate. However, I know someone else was there.": '听完之后，我和 Shiroya 独自离开了阁楼。我们逐层往下时，遇到了正往上走的 Akaro。接着，在水晶层，我们发现留在活动室的 Sekimeiya 已经不见了。{w} 有人把第三个 Sekimeiya 从展示柜里取走了。……谁会想这么做？{w} 乍看之下，Akaro 似乎是唯一的人选。可我知道，当时还有另一个人在。',
        "Shiroya and I found the Past Sekimeiya in a hallway B crystal room, unaware that it wasn't the same one that had just disappeared. That's most likely where Sai chose to hide it a while earlier. What stands out to me is that he chose a room with functional cameras after previously leaving it in the storeroom. I wonder if he was forced to or if he had a reason, because it happened when we were searching both hallways...": '我和 Shiroya 在 B走廊的一间水晶展室里找到了过去Sekimeiya，却没意识到它并不是刚刚消失的那一个。那多半是 Sai 早些时候藏东西的地方。{w} 让我在意的是，他之前把东西放在储藏室，这次却选了一间监控还在运作的展室。我猜不透他是迫不得已，还是另有原因——毕竟他这么做的时候，我们正在同时搜索两条走廊……',
        "It had been there since the previous time the Sekimeiya had disappeared, so it's worth noting that it wasn't found when we looked for Akaro, especially since he would've left the glass open after traveling. ...Recalling how that search went, though, I'm pretty sure I get why that happened.": '早在 Sekimeiya 上一次消失时，它就已经在那里了。因此，我们寻找 Akaro 时没有发现它，这一点值得注意——尤其是 Akaro 穿越之后，柜子的玻璃本该敞开着。{w} ……不过回想那次搜索的经过，我大致明白为什么会这样了。',
        "Much later, he admitted to remembering the time I'd seen him, so it was definitely the same Sai who told the people in the attic not to follow us. The way he traveled to the past confused me for a while. That's because he was surprised to see me; he didn't know I'd also traveled. If he traveled after Shiroya and I returned to the attic, he would've had to fake his surprise upon seeing me.": '很久以后，他承认记得我见到他的那一次。所以在阁楼里叫大家不要跟下来的，肯定就是他。{w} 他回到过去的方式让我困惑了一阵：他见到我时很惊讶，因为他不知道我也穿越了。如果他是在我和 Shiroya 回到阁楼之后才穿越的，那他见到我时的惊讶就只能是装出来的。',
        'How did he travel before Shiroya and I returned? The others said he was there the whole time. ...Is that really the case, though? Shiroya told me what she heard when she was listening to them.': '他究竟是怎样在我和 Shiroya 回来之前完成穿越的？其他人说他一直待在那里。{w} ……可真是这样吗？{w} Shiroya 把她旁听他们谈话时听到的内容告诉了我。',
        'That was all Sai needed to trick the others. Everyone went to the bathroom, so when it was his turn, he could\'ve gone to the crystal floor. He had hidden the Past Sekimeiya, so he traveled after us when it had already gathered a lot of energy. There was something curious about Sai\'s behavior. He kept insisting that he hadn\'t traveled to the past, and he was in a rush. He tried to run away from me twice. That\'s probably because he had to be ready to go back to the attic. As soon as his past self "went to the bathroom", he returned as if nothing had happened, which made the others say that he never left the attic.': '对 Sai 来说，骗过其他人只需要做到这一点。{w} 所有人都去洗手间，轮到他时，他就能去水晶展室。他事先藏好了过去Sekimeiya，等它积蓄了足够多的能量，才在我们之后穿越。{w} Sai 的行为有一点奇怪。他一直坚称自己没有回到过去，而且显得很匆忙。他两次想甩开我逃走。{w} 这大概是因为他必须准备好回到阁楼。等他过去的自己一“去洗手间”，他便若无其事地回来了，所以其他人才会说，他从没离开过阁楼。',
        "I don't know about the actual specifics. Shiroya said it was possible she missed him when she was inspecting the office rooms, but when we returned to the attic, we didn't see Sai's footprints in the living room... That's strange, since I don't think he could've taken the elevator back up. The key was in the attic's door, and he wouldn't have appeared with it, so he couldn't have activated the floor 7 button. Furthermore, it should have been disabled in the attic anyway.": '具体经过我并不清楚。Shiroya 说，她在检查办公室时可能漏看了他，可我们回到阁楼后，并没有在客厅里看到 Sai 的脚印……{w} 这很奇怪，因为我不认为他能乘电梯上去。钥匙插在阁楼门上，而他穿越时不可能带着钥匙出现，所以无法按下七楼的按钮。况且，七楼按钮在阁楼里本来就该是禁用状态。',
        "I'm not sure if this is exactly what happened, but maybe when Shiroya was in the attic, Sai, claiming to go to the bathroom, sent the elevator to the crystal floor and called it. Then, he went to the bathroom. Afterward, he took the elevator down. If Shiroya was still in the attic, she wouldn't have heard it. Sai traveled to the past, and that's where I met up with him. Entering the elevator on the crystal floor and waiting for his past self to call it was one route back to the attic.": '我不确定事情是否真是这样。不过，也许 Shiroya 在阁楼时，Sai 借口去洗手间，把电梯送到水晶展室，再把它叫回来。随后，他去了洗手间。{w} 之后，他乘电梯下楼。如果 Shiroya 当时还在阁楼，就不会听见电梯的声音。Sai 穿越到了过去，我就是在那里遇见他的。{w} 回到阁楼的一条路线，就是先在水晶展室进入电梯，等过去的自己把电梯叫上去。',
        "I don't know if his plan went this far or if I'm missing something else... Maybe he did all of this just so he wouldn't be analyzed for what he wanted to do. He set it up so that Shiroya and I would be much easier to suspect.": '我不知道他的计划是否周密到了这一步，还是我漏掉了别的什么……{w} 也许他做这一切，只是为了不让人看穿他真正的目的。他故意布置成这样，让人更容易怀疑我和 Shiroya。',
        "But again, what about the cameras? They would've recorded him going down. Later, he voiced his thoughts regarding that—he didn't think the recorded footage would ever see the light of the day. As far as he and the rest of us knew, the killer had willingly recorded themselves committing crimes.": '可话说回来，监控呢？它们应该拍到了他下楼。{w} 后来他谈到过这一点——他认为那些录像永远不可能公之于众。就他和我们所有人所知，凶手是自愿录下自己犯罪过程的。',
        "What was it he wanted to do? He'd hidden a functional Sekimeiya, so I bet he wanted to know whether he'd really travel through time with it. He took the third Sekimeiya away from the cabinet even though it was him who found it for us...": '他到底想做什么？他藏起了一个还能用的 Sekimeiya，所以我猜，他是想知道自己是否真能靠它穿越时间。{w} 明明是他替我们找到了第三个 Sekimeiya，却把它从展示柜里拿走了……',
        "However, this brings about another issue. Why didn't the watch work in the past? After all, it worked again when we added the new battery. This means that minutes later, during the future location, the watch should've been working. It seems to be an impossibility that it wasn't working in the past, given both locations are supposed to be the same.": '然而，这又引出了另一个问题：为什么表在过去无法运转？{w} 毕竟我们装上新的锂电池后，它就恢复了。这意味着，几分钟后、也就是处于未来那个地点时，表本应正在运转。可既然两个地点理应相同，它在过去却无法运转，这实在说不过去。',
        "Now that I think more about it, it could be due to the lithium battery itself. It was in the attic, a place that's been abandoned for many years. It was, I have to assume, a battery that the Ashiya family had when they lived there.": '再仔细想想，问题也许出在锂电池本身。{w} 它一直放在阁楼里，那地方已经废弃多年。我只能推测，那是芦屋家还住在这里时留下的电池。',
        '...But does this really make sense, or am I missing something crucial? I just remembered... Sai must have synced his watch to the computer after we saw the "9,999" date since it was working when Shiroya and I returned to the attic. The time would always have been set to that specific point before reaching the end of the loop, so it couldn\'t have kept counting up...': '……{w}可这真的说得通吗？还是我漏掉了什么关键之处？我刚刚想起来……{w} 在我们看到「9,999」这个日期之后，Sai 一定把手表跟电脑同步过——毕竟我和 Shiroya 回到阁楼时，它已经能正常显示。循环结束前，时间总会被设回那个特定时刻，所以不可能一直往上累加……',
        "We were fast enough to see him in front of the cleaning room, where he'd hidden a Sekimeiya. I thought something then...": '我们赶得够快，正好看见他站在清洁间前——他把一个 Sekimeiya 藏在了那里。{w} 当时我心里冒出一个念头……',
        "At the time, we thought we'd gone to the past. That's not what happened, though. We recognized our locations—we'd been there half an hour before we'd traveled. That means we went half an hour to the future.": '当时我们以为自己回到了过去，其实并非如此。{w}那些地方我们都认得——正是穿越前半小时我们待过的地方。也就是说，我们往未来跳了半个小时。',
        "The staircase door is open, so this is past the time we unlocked the attic. There are a bunch of footprints next to the door, but I don't see ours. This must mean that you and I haven't gone down yet. These are probably the ones that we left after going back up, when we found Akaro in the bathroom. We're not before that point since there are too many.": '楼梯间的门开着，说明现在已经过了我们打开阁楼的时间。门边有一堆脚印，可我没看到我们的。这么说，我们还没下楼。{w}这些多半是我们重新上楼之后留下的，也就是在洗手间发现 Akaro 那会儿。脚印这么多，说明现在不会早于那一刻。',
        "That was a big misinterpretation. We were told what caused those footprints. It was the search that occurred after Isla went missing; the ones Shiroya and I had left were long buried. They were all slightly faded too. There was no chance we'd just traveled a few seconds back, which led me to be pretty certain of the time.": '那是个天大的误判。{w}后来我们才知道那些脚印是怎么来的——是 Isla 失踪后众人搜索时踩出来的，我和 Shiroya 的脚印早被盖住了。{w}而且所有脚印都略微褪了色。我们不可能只往回穿越了几秒，正因如此，我才对时间相当有把握。',
        "How is that possible, though? We heard a sound coming from the bedroom where we'd been. Who the hell was that? Nobody should've been there, right?": '可这怎么可能？{w}我们听见声音从刚才待过的那间卧室传来。到底是谁？那里不该有人的吧？',
        "And in the second level of the opposite bedroom, both of us fell asleep. When we woke up, we had no idea how long we'd been there for. That's why, when we were told the time, we thought we'd slept for quite a while. In reality, the main reason a lot of time had passed was because we'd gone to the future.": '而在对面卧室的第二层，我们两个都睡着了。{w}醒来后，我们根本不知道已经过了多久。所以后来有人告诉我们时间，我们才以为睡了很久。实际上，时间过去这么久，主要是因为我们跳到了未来。',
        "When we came down, we saw that the cleaning cart had disappeared. What was strange was that the Sekimeiya was in one of the buckets which had been below it. But that wasn't the Future Sekimeiya; it wasn't working. Why was the third Sekimeiya there? Had it also been in the cart when we'd traveled? Shiroya said something else was there, but would the third Sekimeiya not have disappeared with the cart? ...And she said it was a dark object. I'm not sure, but I think I can guess what happened to the Future Sekimeiya.": '下楼时，我们发现清洁车不见了。奇怪的是，Sekimeiya 就在原本位于车下的一个水桶里。{w}可那不是未来Sekimeiya，它没在工作。{w}第三个 Sekimeiya 怎么会在这儿？我们穿越时它也在车上吗？Shiroya 说当时那里还有别的什么，可第三个 Sekimeiya 不是该跟车一起消失吗？……而且她说那是个深色的东西。{w}我没有把握，不过未来Sekimeiya 的去向，我大概猜得到。',
        '"Sai, showing the strongest reaction, approached the room while letting out a conspicuous grunt. He opened the door and stayed still for some time. Then, he entered the small space. Before the others had time to wonder what he was doing, he exited and told them that it was empty."': '反应最大的是 Sai，他闷哼一声，走向那间房。{w} 他推开门，在门口一动不动地站了好一会儿，随后才走进那个狭小的空间。其他人还没来得及琢磨他在做什么，他就已经出来，说里面空无一人。',
        "The powered-off Sekimeiya was there, and he put it in his hip pack. That's why he had appeared with it in the past... In the cleaning room, the others were distracted by the missing cart, and Sai pointed out the third Sekimeiya in the bucket. I'm still having trouble understanding the cause behind some of these details, though. He was only able to obtain the Future Sekimeiya like that because he had appeared with it and had hidden it in the cleaning room... This seems to be an event with no origin, so perhaps it's an indication that something else happened on top of it.": '那个已经断电的 Sekimeiya 就在里面，他把它收进了腰包。所以他才会带着它出现在过去……{w}在清洁间里，其他人都在为不见的清洁车分神，Sai 则指出了水桶里的第三个 Sekimeiya。{w}不过这些细节背后的原因，我到现在还是没想明白。他能那样拿到未来Sekimeiya，是因为他曾带着它出现，并把它藏在了清洁间……这件事似乎没有起因，或许说明还有别的事情叠在它上面。',
        "Akaro saw us enter and never leave the cleaning room—they knew we traveled through time. However, there was another disappearance. Katei's.": 'Akaro 看见我们进了清洁间就再没出来——他们知道我们穿越了时间。可还有另一起失踪。{w}Katei 的失踪。',
        "The remaining people searched through every room on the crystal floor, but they didn't find us. When they were about to go up, Isla walked to room A5. That's when she fell into a cabinet and disappeared.": '剩下的人把水晶层的每个房间都搜了一遍，却没有找到我们。{w}就在他们准备上楼时，Isla 走到了水晶展室 A5。她就是在那里跌进展示柜，消失不见的。',
        "...I wonder what happened. The cabinet she looked into is one that can be seen from the stairs, where she and Erina were waiting. During the period Sai and Akaro investigated the rooms, I'm sure Sai quickly disposed of the Future Sekimeiya. That makes me think Isla saw him do that through the door's gap...": '……她身上到底发生了什么？{w}她看的那台展示柜，从楼梯那边正好看得见，而她和 Erina 当时就在楼梯那儿等着。{w}在 Sai 和 Akaro 查看房间的那段时间里，Sai 肯定很快就把未来Sekimeiya 处理掉了。这么一想，Isla 会不会是透过门缝看见了……',
        "When the others saw Isla disappeared, they were unable to find a Sekimeiya in room A5's cabinet. I'd bet it was powered off, and there was very little light. Since Sai knew the Sekimeiya was there, it wouldn't surprise me if he grabbed it immediately before the others saw it. I'm not sure about that, though.": '其他人看到 Isla 消失后，在水晶展室 A5 的展示柜里找过，却没找到 Sekimeiya。{w}我猜它已经断电，周围光线又很暗。Sai 既然知道 Sekimeiya 在那里，赶在别人看清之前把它拿走，也不奇怪。不过这点我没有把握。',
        "Isla wasn't found. Katei wasn't found. Shiroya and I weren't found. Of course, we weren't found because we were in the process of traveling to the future. What about Katei, though?": 'Isla 没被找到，Katei 没被找到，我和 Shiroya 也没被找到。{w}我们之所以没被找到，自然是因为当时正穿越到未来。可 Katei 呢？',
        "Half an hour earlier, he, Shiroya, and I were in the attic, so that's where we appeared in the future. Katei was in the rightmost bedroom. He suddenly teleported there and left the room, disoriented. He's the one we heard approaching the door when we were in the hallway and who left the newer footprints in the living room.": '半小时前，他、Shiroya 和我都在阁楼，所以我们穿越到未来后就出现在阁楼。Katei 当时在最右边那间卧室。{w}他忽然被传送到那里，神志恍惚地走出房间。我们在走廊里听到的靠近门口的动静就是他，客厅里较新的脚印也是他留下的。',
        'After failing to find anyone, Erina, Akaro, and Sai gave up and moved back to the lobby. There was only silence for a long time until they heard a sound from hallway A.': '找了一圈毫无收获，Erina、Akaro 和 Sai 只好作罢，回到大厅。{w}此后很长一段时间只剩寂静，直到 A走廊那边传来声响。',
        'Then, they looked into the cabinet where Isla had disappeared. She was there, already dead. The Sekimeiya, meanwhile, was nowhere to be found.': '随后，他们去查看 Isla 消失的那个展示柜。{w}她就在里面，人已经死了。而那个 Sekimeiya 却怎么也找不到。',
        "This only made sense from our point of view, but Sai never denied it. Why? There's no way he really didn't look at the upper levels, is there? Perhaps that was the first indication he had that traveling to the future was possible, and he consciously chose not to let us know. Since he should've been in hallway C when Katei disappeared, I wonder if he turned around and realized what had happened to him too.": '这话只有从我们的角度才说得通，可 Sai 始终没有反驳。{w}为什么？他总不可能真的没看卧室上层吧？{w}也许正是那时，他第一次察觉到穿越到未来的可能，于是刻意不让我们知道。Katei 消失时，他应该就在 C走廊；我猜他是不是回过头，也明白 Katei 身上发生了什么。',
        "I don't get it. I don't know what happened to Isla. Is there a whole other factor that I'm missing about this? Did something else occur that I don't know about?": '我不明白。我不知道 Isla 到底出了什么事。{w} 难道那件事里还有我完全没想到的另一层因素？是不是还发生了别的、我一无所知的事？',
        "Isla disappeared from the cabinet, but how? Did she go to the future? ...The Future Sekimeiya should've been powered off since we had just used it. Even if that happened, did she reappear in that same cabinet, where she'd gone to look? Why, though? She wasn't there in the past, was she? And why did she die?": 'Isla 从展示柜里消失了，可这是怎么做到的？她去了未来吗？……未来Sekimeiya 应该已经断电了，因为我们刚用过它。{w} 就算真是那样，她难道会重新出现在她刚才查看的那个展示柜里吗？{w} 可为什么？过去那里并没有她，对吧？而且她为什么会死？',
        "Right, she yelled before falling in. What the hell does that mean? Did she go to the past? Before, Sai had kept walking toward hallway A—perhaps he put the Future Sekimeiya where he had the past one, for whatever reason. Since the future one should've been powered off, Isla would've actually traveled back in time and not changed worlds. I can't know if the search took long enough for it to power back on, though.": '对，她在掉进去之前喊了一声。那到底是什么意思？她去了过去吗？{w} 之前 Sai 一直朝 A走廊走去——也许他不知出于什么原因，把未来Sekimeiya 放到了原本放着过去Sekimeiya 的位置。既然未来Sekimeiya 应该已经断电，那 Isla 应该就是穿越回了过去，而没有触发世界切换。不过，我没法确定那次搜寻是否持续得足够久，让它重新启动。',
        "Most importantly, the Sekimeiya reappeared in that cabinet later. ...Did someone do this? Or was it all an accident that didn't involve a murder?": '最重要的是，后来 Sekimeiya 又出现在了那个展示柜里。……是有人动了手脚吗？{w} 还是说，这一切都只是意外，与谋杀无关？',
        "It's possible someone killed her, but who? Who would've had a motive to do that? Who could've done that? There was a whole search, and the Future Sekimeiya had just been used. It's possible a killer with an elaborate plan carried this out, but that's completely out of place.": '也许有人杀了她，可那个人是谁？谁会有这种动机？又有谁能做到？{w} 当时我们展开了全面搜索，而未来Sekimeiya 也刚被用过。一个精心谋划的凶手或许能办到，但这完全不合常理。',
        "What happened to Isla? Under the right circumstances, touching the Sekimeiya ended her life. It wasn't an instant result, however. The complexity of what occurred might be a bit more involved than what you're imagining, as no world switches factored in.": 'Isla 出了什么事？在特定条件下，触碰 Sekimeiya 结束了她的生命。{w} 不过，这并不是瞬间发生的结果。其中经过也许比你想象的更复杂一些，因为此事并没有涉及世界切换。',
        'This riddle will be left all to you, but know something: when Isla looked into the cabinet for the first time, she saw the body of a young girl. It was her own, but that was far from her interpretation. Inside the cabinet, she saw the image of her friend. Her mind and body both teetered on the edge, and she screamed as she toppled into that sarcophagus of a cabinet.': '这个谜题就全留给你了，但你要知道一件事：{w} 当 Isla 第一次往展示柜里看时，她看见了一具年轻女孩的尸体。那其实是她自己，可她却完全会错了意。{w} 她在展示柜里看见的是自己朋友的影像。她的身心都濒临崩溃，尖叫着跌进了那个宛如石棺的展示柜。',
        "Afterward, we simply stayed in the lobby. It didn't look like any of us had the strength to stand again, but that changed when Katei and Sai left out of the blue.": '之后，我们只是留在大厅里。{w} 我们似乎谁都没有力气再站起来，可 Katei 和 Sai 忽然离开后，情况就变了。',
        "I don't think it was ever used by anyone who didn't want to be seen, though. I saw a single set of fingerprints, identical to the ones I saw this morning. ...Since this morning, no one had opened that door from the hallway.": '不过，我不觉得有谁为了不让人看见而用过那里。{w} 我只看到了一组指纹，和今早见到的那组一模一样。……从今早到现在，没有人从走廊那边打开过那扇门。',
        "What happened outside the bedroom? I only have Akaro's version. He touched the Sekimeiya Sai had hidden, and went to the fu—": '卧室外到底发生了什么？我只有 Akaro 的说法。{w} 他碰了 Sai 藏起来的那个 Sekimeiya，然后去了未——',
        "How did I not think this through? There's no way we went to January 5th. For that, we should've been in the tower 21 days before the 15th.": '我怎么没想通这一点？我们不可能去了一月五日。{w} 若真是那样，我们在 15 日的 21 天前就应该在塔里了。',
        '21 days before the 15th... That was November 24th. I was not in the tower at that time.': '15日往前推21天……就是11月24日。{w}那时我并不在塔里。',
        'I thought about our last minutes in the tower, right before {time=21.} What exactly had caused the travel?': '我回想着我们在塔里的最后几分钟，就在 {time=21.} 之前。{w}究竟是什么引发了那次时间穿越？',
        'I thought about our last minutes in the tower, right before 21:00.{w} What exactly had caused the travel?': '我回想着我们在塔里的最后几分钟，就在 {time=21.} 之前。{w}究竟是什么引发了那次时间穿越？',
        'I thought about our last minutes in the tower, right before 21:00. What exactly had caused the travel?': '我回想着我们在塔里的最后几分钟，就在 {time=21.} 之前。{w}究竟是什么引发了那次时间穿越？',
        'I thought about our last minutes in the tower, right before 9 p.m.{w} What exactly had caused the travel?': '我回想着我们在塔里的最后几分钟，就在 {time=21.} 之前。{w}究竟是什么引发了那次时间穿越？',
        'I thought about our last minutes in the tower, right before 9 p.m. What exactly had caused the travel?': '我回想着我们在塔里的最后几分钟，就在 {time=21.} 之前。{w}究竟是什么引发了那次时间穿越？',
        'I had to think about everything that had happened during the last segment of the day. When I did, a possibility came to mind.': '我不得不把那天最后一段时间里发生的一切重新想一遍。{w}想着想着，一个可能性浮上心头。',
        'A bit after 20:30, we found the powered-off Sekimeiya in the water tank, and we left it in the cold cabinet.': '过了 {time=20:30} 不久，我们在水箱里找到了那个断电的 Sekimeiya，并把它留在了冷藏展示柜里。',
        'A bit after 8:30 p.m., we found the powered-off Sekimeiya in the water tank, and we left it in the cold cabinet.': '过了 {time=20:30} 不久，我们在水箱里找到了那个断电的 Sekimeiya，并把它留在了冷藏展示柜里。',
        "What's strange is that the Sekimeiya was scalding; it didn't make sense for Erina to have recently used it. That makes me think it wasn't the same Sekimeiya that had just disappeared from the cabinet.": '奇怪的是，那个 Sekimeiya 烫得灼手；如果 Erina 前不久刚用过它，实在说不通。{w}这让我觉得，它并不是刚从展示柜里消失的那一个。',
        "If the Future Sekimeiya was put in a hot place during those minutes, it could've gathered enough energy. However, that wouldn't explain the replicated location: I wasn't in the tower on November 24th. So there is necessarily an answer that explains both mysteries at once.": '如果 未来Sekimeiya 在那几分钟里被放到高温处，它或许能积攒足够的能量。可那解释不了被复制的地点：11月24日我并不在塔里。{w}因此，一定存在一个能同时解释这两个谜团的答案。',
        "Could it really be what I'm imagining...? Before the exit unlocked, the Future Sekimeiya was activated. I believe the location where that happened is a very important detail.": '难道真如我所想……？{w}出口解锁前，未来Sekimeiya 被启动了。我认为，它被启动的地点是个非常关键的细节。',
        "It was in the mechanical room. That's where the Future Sekimeiya was at {time=21.} And it was Erina who activated it. She was in the mechanical room when the lights went off.": '它就在机械室。{time=21.} 时，未来Sekimeiya 正是在那里。{w}而启动它的正是 Erina。灯灭的时候，她就在机械室里。',
        "It was in the mechanical room. That's where the Future Sekimeiya was at 21:00.{w} And it was Erina who activated it. She was in the mechanical room when the lights went off.": '它就在机械室。{time=21.} 时，未来Sekimeiya 正是在那里。{w}而启动它的正是 Erina。灯灭的时候，她就在机械室里。',
        "It was in the mechanical room. That's where the Future Sekimeiya was at 21:00. And it was Erina who activated it. She was in the mechanical room when the lights went off.": '它就在机械室。{time=21.} 时，未来Sekimeiya 正是在那里。{w}而启动它的正是 Erina。灯灭的时候，她就在机械室里。',
        "It was in the mechanical room. That's where the Future Sekimeiya was at 9 p.m.{w} And it was Erina who activated it. She was in the mechanical room when the lights went off.": '它就在机械室。{time=21.} 时，未来Sekimeiya 正是在那里。{w}而启动它的正是 Erina。灯灭的时候，她就在机械室里。',
        "It was in the mechanical room. That's where the Future Sekimeiya was at 9 p.m. And it was Erina who activated it. She was in the mechanical room when the lights went off.": '它就在机械室。{time=21.} 时，未来Sekimeiya 正是在那里。{w}而启动它的正是 Erina。灯灭的时候，她就在机械室里。',
        'She still wanted to go to the past; she never stopped saying that. It was her last chance to do so. Before then, she used the Sekimeiya we left in the cabinet. However, when she came back to the lobby and asked us the time, she had gone to the future instead. Based on what happened later, that had to be the Future Sekimeiya.': '她仍想回到过去，这话她一直挂在嘴边。那是她最后的机会。{w}在此之前，她用过了我们留在展示柜里的那个 Sekimeiya。可当她回到大厅、问我们时间时，她其实是去了未来。结合后来发生的事，那个必定是未来Sekimeiya。',
        "But that's not all. Before, Erina noticed the mechanical room had been opened. That makes me think Sai was down there and came out when we went to the event room. He knew I'd purposely left the cabinet unlocked. If he later hid the Sekimeiya in the mechanical room, he was probably scoping it out ahead of time.": '「但不止如此。Erina 之前就注意到机械室被人打开过。这让我觉得，Sai 当时就在下面，趁我们去活动室时溜了出来。{w}他知道我故意没锁展示柜。若他后来把 Sekimeiya 藏进机械室，那他多半事先就踩过点了。」',
        "Why did we go to January 5th, though? If that was the case, the range should've picked up everyone who'd been waiting outside the tower. ...Somehow, Shiroya knew the travel would occur, and she ran away from us to avoid being involved...": '「可我们为什么会跑到1月5日？如果是这样，那范围理应把等在塔外的所有人都卷进来才对。{w}……Shiroya 不知怎么预知到会发生时间穿越，为了不被牵扯进来，才从我们身边逃开了……」',
        "But why? Why 21 days into the future? On the surface, it seems like Erina activating the Sekimeiya would never result in that. However... I think I can tell what the answer is by simply running through what would've happened after she touched it.": '「可为什么？为什么会是二十一天之后的未来？{w}乍看之下，Erina 启动 Sekimeiya 无论如何都不会造成那样的结果。不过……只要顺着她触碰之后会发生什么推演一遍，我想我就能看出答案。」',
        'So, we traveled twenty minutes to the future. What would the locations have been?': '「于是，我们穿越到了二十分钟后的未来。{w}那么，出现的位置又会是哪里？」',
        "What occurred relied on Sai's location upon appearing. By that point, I had also learned that fifteen minutes stored resulted in five minutes of the Sekimeiya's recovery phase. After Erina touched the Sekimeiya, it spent five minutes off and then gathered energy for fifteen more minutes until we appeared.": '「接下来会发生什么，取决于 Sai 出现时所在的位置。{w}到那时我也已经明白：蓄能十五分钟，换来的是 Sekimeiya 五分钟的恢复期。Erina 触碰 Sekimeiya 之后，它先停摆了五分钟，随后又蓄能十五分钟，直到我们出现。」',
        "When we appeared, Sai was in the mechanical room, where he would hide the Sekimeiya. So the instant we appeared, he activated it again. ...I'm not sure how that happened fluidly, but I can think of a couple things that make a lot of sense. Immediately, we went twenty more minutes to the future, and when we appeared, the Sekimeiya had gathered energy for another fifteen minutes.": '「我们出现时，Sai 正在机械室——他后来藏 Sekimeiya 的地方。于是就在我们出现的瞬间，他又一次启动了它。{w}……我不知道这一切为何能衔接得如此顺畅，不过我能想到几种说得通的解释。{w}紧接着，我们又穿越到了二十分钟后的未来，而我们出现时，Sekimeiya 已经又蓄能了十五分钟。」',
        'That time, the locations were from the time Erina had touched the Sekimeiya. In other words, she was in the mechanical room while Sai and I were in the lobby. So, we went twenty more minutes to the future.': '「那一次，出现的位置是根据 Erina 触碰 Sekimeiya 时的情况来定的。也就是说，她在机械室，而 Sai 和我在大厅。{w}于是，我们又穿越到了二十分钟后的未来。」',
        "Only two locations alternated: the one in which Sai was in the mechanical room, and the one in which Erina was. Meanwhile, I was in the lobby regardless. This explains why I didn't see the sudden, instant flashing they talked about.": '交替的只有两个位置：一个是 Sai 在机械室，另一个是 Erina 在机械室。而不管哪种情况，我都在大厅。{w}这就解释了为什么我没看见他们说的那道突如其来的闪光。',
        'For some reason, on January 5th, the tower was empty. Katei told us once that the lights turn off every night and are manually turned on in the morning. So, if nobody was in the tower in the morning, the lights would\'ve remained off. However, before all the lights turned off permanently, every twenty minutes, Sai and Erina alternated between being in the lobby and in the mechanical room. Although it lasted an instant each time, due to the darkness in the mechanical room and the light in the lobby, they perceived a "flashing light".': '不知为何，1月5日那天，塔里空无一人。Katei 曾告诉我们，灯每晚都会熄灭，早上再手动打开。所以如果早上塔里没有人，灯就会一直关着。{w}然而，在所有灯彻底熄灭之前，每隔二十分钟，Sai 和 Erina 就会在大厅与机械室之间交替。尽管每次只有一瞬，但机械室一片漆黑、大厅亮着灯，于是他们看到了一道「闪光」。',
        'Akaro traveled to the future after he and Sai escaped, but since Isla was still there, she went to the past afterward. Would there have been enough time to store the needed energy to go so far back?': 'Akaro 和 Sai 逃脱之后，Akaro 穿越到了未来；而 Isla 当时仍在原地，随后便去了过去。{w}要回到那么远的过去，所需能量来得及蓄够吗？',
        "Actually, yes. It was due to a bed sheet that the world C group had obtained in world A. When it was brought to world B, they wrapped it around the Past Sekimeiya and world switched back to world C. However, the sheet remained around the Sekimeiya in world B. When it powered back on, the sheet was still very hot. That's why it took a short time to reach the needed amount of energy.": '没错，那是因为 C世界那组人在 A世界拿到了一条床单。他们把床单带到 B世界，裹在 过去Sekimeiya 上，然后世界切换回 C世界。然而，那条床单留在了 B世界的 Sekimeiya 上。{w}当它重新启动时，床单还很烫。所以它才在很短的时间里蓄够了所需的能量。',
        "That's wrong. It was due to a bed sheet that the world C group had obtained in world A. When it was brought to world B, they wrapped it around the Past Sekimeiya and world switched back to world C. However, the sheet remained around the Sekimeiya in world B. When it powered back on, the sheet was still very hot. That's why it took a short time to reach the needed amount of energy.": '不对。那是因为 C世界那组人在 A世界拿到了一条床单。他们把床单带到 B世界，裹在 过去Sekimeiya 上，然后世界切换回 C世界。然而，那条床单留在了 B世界的 Sekimeiya 上。{w}当它重新启动时，床单还很烫。所以它才在很短的时间里蓄够了所需的能量。',
        'Someone else disappeared as well: Akaro A. The bedroom where everyone stayed was directly above the event room, so the range reached him. From a locked bedroom, he appeared in an unlocked prison cell. That was when a policeman outside the building suddenly appeared 21 days in the past.': '同时消失的还有另一个人：Akaro A。{w}大家住的卧室就在活动室正上方，所以他也被卷了进去。他从上锁的卧室，出现在没上锁的牢房里。也就在那时，楼外的一名警察突然穿越到了二十一天前。',
        "Who the hell did that? There's no way it teleported out. ...Did anyone else have the key after all?": '到底是谁干的？它绝不可能自己传送出去。{w}……难道还有别人也有钥匙？',
        "One was Shiroya. She was naturally encompassed by the range when Atsuki touched the Sekimeiya. However, she didn't appear in the lobby with him. Strangely, she appeared in a bathroom on the crystal floor, and when she left, she was seen from the security room and addressed through the microphone.": '其中一人是 Shiroya。Atsuki 触碰 Sekimeiya 时，她自然也被纳入了范围。{w} 然而，她并没有和他一起出现在大厅。奇怪的是，她出现在水晶层的一间洗手间里；她出来之后，有人在监控室看见她，用麦克风对她喊话。',
        "When Katei walked out of the bedroom, Erina followed close behind. She didn't believe Atsuki and Shiroya had killed Isla. ...Sai and Akaro had been with her the entire time.": 'Katei 走出卧室时，Erina 紧跟在后。{w} 她不相信是 Atsuki 和 Shiroya 杀了 Isla。……毕竟 Sai 和 Akaro 一直和她在一起。',
        "However, Katei had been missing during that time, and he hadn't explained himself. She didn't trust him at all; he'd been lying all day. ...He had faked going to the bathroom to take advantage of Isla's death.": '然而，那段时间 Katei 一直不见踪影，也从没解释过自己的去向。{w} 她完全无法信任他；他整天都在撒谎。……他借口去洗手间，正是为了利用 Isla 的死。',
        "Katei realized the meaning behind that. Erina suspected him of causing Isla's death. He sighed quietly and then spoke.": 'Katei 明白这句话背后的意思。Erina 怀疑 Isla 的死是他造成的。{w} 他轻轻叹了口气，然后开口。',
        'I said I experienced the teleportation, and I am telling you the truth. I was beyond confused when I appeared there. When I came down, the three of you were in the lobby.': '我说过，我经历了传送，我说的都是实话。我出现在那里时，完全不知所措。{w} 我下楼时，你们三个人都在大厅里。',
        "Katei saw nothing but hostility in Erina's face. Enough to appear as a threat. Did she really think he had killed Isla? He didn't know anything about what had happened to her, but there was a way he could prove his innocence.": 'Katei 在 Erina 脸上只看到敌意，那几乎已经算是一种威胁。{w} 她真的以为是他杀了 Isla 吗？他对 Isla 的遭遇一无所知，不过，他有一个办法能证明自己的清白。',
        '...After a brief pause, Katei moved the cursor to a different camera. He was calm. He knew very little incriminating footage was located in those folders.': '……{w}短暂停顿后，Katei 把光标移到了另一个摄像头上。{w}他很镇定。那些文件夹里几乎没有对他不利的录像，这一点他再清楚不过。',
        'Once he clicked on room B4\'s camera, a message appeared on the screen. "{time=10:04}: Camera(s) disabled and associated footage erased".': '他刚点开 B4 房间的摄像头，屏幕上就弹出一行字。{w}「{time=10:04}：摄像头已停用，相关录像已删除」。',
        'Once he clicked on room B4\'s camera, a message appeared on the screen.{w} "10:04: Camera(s) disabled and associated footage erased".': '他刚点开 B4 房间的摄像头，屏幕上就弹出一行字。{w}「{time=10:04}：摄像头已停用，相关录像已删除」。',
        'Once he clicked on room B4\'s camera, a message appeared on the screen. "10:04: Camera(s) disabled and associated footage erased".': '他刚点开 B4 房间的摄像头，屏幕上就弹出一行字。{w}「{time=10:04}：摄像头已停用，相关录像已删除」。',
        'Once he clicked on room B4\'s camera, a message appeared on the screen.{w} "10:04 a.m.: Camera(s) disabled and associated footage erased".': '他刚点开 B4 房间的摄像头，屏幕上就弹出一行字。{w}「{time=10:04}：摄像头已停用，相关录像已删除」。',
        'Once he clicked on room B4\'s camera, a message appeared on the screen. "10:04 a.m.: Camera(s) disabled and associated footage erased".': '他刚点开 B4 房间的摄像头，屏幕上就弹出一行字。{w}「{time=10:04}：摄像头已停用，相关录像已删除」。',
        'Wh-What!? The killer erased it! H-How!?': '什、什么！？{w}是凶手删掉的！他、他怎么办到的！？',
        "...{time=10:04}? Isn't that when we left you here?": '……{w}{time=10:04}？那不就是我们把你留在这儿的时候吗？',
        "...{w}10:04? Isn't that when we left you here?": '……{w}{time=10:04}？那不就是我们把你留在这儿的时候吗？',
        "...10:04? Isn't that when we left you here?": '……{w}{time=10:04}？那不就是我们把你留在这儿的时候吗？',
        "...{w}10:04 a.m.? Isn't that when we left you here?": '……{w}{time=10:04}？那不就是我们把你留在这儿的时候吗？',
        "...10:04 a.m.? Isn't that when we left you here?": '……{w}{time=10:04}？那不就是我们把你留在这儿的时候吗？',
        "...I think I can imagine what happened. We then found Erina's body, but she was still alive, and after we were in the event room for a while, the other Shiroya woke me up.": '……我大概能想象出经过。{w}之后我们发现了 Erina，但她还活着；我们在活动室待了一阵，另一个 Shiroya 把我叫醒了。',
        "We couldn't find her, but suddenly, Sai attacked us. I don't get that either...! Why did he want to kill us, and where did he even get that knife from!?": '我们没找到她，Sai 却突然袭击了我们。{w}这一点我也想不通……！他为什么想杀我们？那把刀又是从哪儿来的！？',
        "He realized Atsuki B didn't seem to know what had occurred and that he hadn't been crying, but it was the camera's green light that stopped him, as it otherwise would've been possible for that Atsuki to be a future version of the one who'd punched him. In world A, Sai had noticed the green lights were gone; the cameras hadn't been recording. When he unknowingly returned to world B, he even saw the message on the computer that matched with the lack of green lights.": '他意识到，Atsuki B 似乎并不知道发生了什么，而且也没有哭过；但真正让他停下的是摄像头的绿灯——否则，那个 Atsuki 也可能是打过他的那个人的未来版本。{w}在 A世界，Sai 注意到绿灯已经熄灭，摄像头并没有在录像。后来他在不知不觉中回到 B世界时，甚至看到了电脑上的那条消息，正好与绿灯熄灭的情况吻合。',
        "Sai had seen a dead body in the lobby near a pool of blood: Shiroya's. Why was it not there anymore? Why had the pool of blood diminished?": 'Sai 曾在大厅里看见 Shiroya 的尸体倒在血泊旁。{w}为什么尸体现在不见了？为什么血泊也变少了？',
        "When he touched it, he and Shiroya appeared in the attic, which was inaccessible for me. I'm not sure what happened there, but Shiroya told me Sai locked her in a bedroom.": '他一碰到它，就和 Shiroya 一起出现在了我进不去的阁楼里。{w}我不清楚那里发生了什么，但 Shiroya 告诉我，Sai 把她锁在了一间卧室里。',
        '...From the staff room, I used the Sekimeiya and appeared twenty minutes in the past, in the event room. I used that time to search through the upper floors, but I had locked myself out of the attic. I ended up in the security room without finding anyone, but Erina had to be somewhere, likely with Miiya...': '……我从员工室使用了 Sekimeiya，出现在二十分钟前的活动室。我利用那段时间搜遍了楼上几层，却把自己锁在了阁楼外。{w}最后我到了监控室，谁也没找到；但 Erina 一定在某个地方，很可能和 Miiya 在一起……',
        "I never wrote it. What the fuck was it doing in my pocket? I don't believe anyone else left it on the floor. Wait, no. This doesn't even make sense. Nobody could've put it in my pocket, so what I must assume is that I appeared with it when I traveled to the past.": '我从没写过它。它他妈怎么会在我口袋里？我不相信是别人把它丢在地上的。{w}等等，不对。这根本说不通。{w}没人能把它塞进我的口袋，所以我只能认为，是我回到过去时把它一起带过去的。',
        "However, this is illogical. Where is its origin? I appeared with it and I threw it away. Then, Erina found it and gave it to me, which is why I appeared with it. ...It doesn't have a beginning.": '可是，这不合逻辑。它到底是从哪来的？{w}我带着它出现，又把它丢掉。后来 Erina 捡到它，交给我，所以我才带着它出现。……它根本没有源头。',
        'Hm... I assumed Erina found the note where I\'d discarded it, behind the handrail in hallway B. But she only said "I found this just now."': '嗯……我以为 Erina 是在我丢掉纸条的地方——B走廊的栏杆后面——捡到它的。{w}可她只说了「这是我刚才找到的」。',
        "Right. The next time I traveled to the past, I didn't appear with it. But... why? I should have.": '对了。下一次我回到过去时，并没有带着它出现。{w}可是……为什么？我明明该带着它的。',
        "Oh, it's like I thought earlier. I had the note when I traveled to the past. From the staff room, I appeared in hallway B and then slammed the storeroom door to create a new noise. After that, I waited in the bathroom on the second floor. There, I put my hand in my pocket because I wanted to flush the note away. However, it wasn't there. That's why I didn't appear with it. I wanted to flush it away, so if I had, I wouldn't have held the note in the future, and I never could've appeared with it.": '哦，就像我之前想的那样。我回到过去时，身上带着那张纸条。我从员工室出发，出现在 B走廊，然后用力摔上储藏室的门，制造出新的响声。之后，我在二楼的洗手间里等着。{w}在那里，我把手伸进口袋，因为我想把纸条冲掉。可是它不在。{w}所以它才没有跟着我出现。我想把它冲掉；要是我真那么做了，未来的我手上就不会有那张纸条，我也就不可能带着它出现。',
        'These details... I wonder how many I missed. Now that I think about it, something similar happened that very same travel. When I touched the Sekimeiya, I had the locker key in my hand. However, when I returned to the staff room with Shiroya, I had it in my pocket. I still appeared with it in the past, but it was in my pocket.': '这些细节……不知道我漏掉了多少。{w}现在回想起来，就在那一次穿越里，也发生过类似的事。{w}我碰到 Sekimeiya 时，手里拿着储物柜钥匙。可是当我和 Shiroya 回到员工室时，钥匙却在我的口袋里。我回到过去时还是带着它，只是它已经在口袋里了。',
        "...That's because if I'd appeared with it in my hand, I would've then put it in my pocket. That redundant action was canceled, and I simply appeared with it already inside. Along the same line of thought, I didn't go to the bathroom many times, did I? I didn't feel the need to. Maybe that happened due to my travels—if I'd felt that urge upon going back, I would've gone to the bathroom. Then, in the replicated location, that wouldn't have been needed anymore. My bladder just automatically emptied without me noticing.": '……因为如果我出现时手里拿着它，之后也会把它放进口袋。结果这个多余的动作被省掉了，我出现时它已经在口袋里。{w}同理，我去洗手间的次数其实并不多，对吧？因为我没觉得有必要。{w}也许这也是穿越造成的——如果我在回去时产生了尿意，就会去洗手间。可到了复制出的地点，就已经不需要再去了。我的膀胱只是在我没注意的时候自己排空了。',
        'That location was exactly where she was on November 30th. The only way for her to appear there is if she went fifteen days into the future. ...To December 30th.': '那个地方，正是她11月30日所在之处。{w} 她要出现在那里，唯一的可能就是穿越到了十五天后的未来。{w}……也就是12月30日。',
        "...Could she really have gone to the future? Did that occur without her realizing it? Right, I didn't think about it earlier, but the Sekimeiya that sent us repeatedly to January 5th at {time=21:00} was the one that Shiroya activated in the bathroom.": '……她真的去了未来吗？难道连她自己都没有察觉？{w} 对了，我之前一直没想到——那个在{time=21:00}一次次把我们送往1月5日的 Sekimeiya，正是 Shiroya 在浴室里启动的。',
        "...Could she really have gone to the future? Did that occur without her realizing it?{w} Right, I didn't think about it earlier, but the Sekimeiya that sent us repeatedly to January 5th at 21:00 was the one that Shiroya activated in the bathroom.": '……她真的去了未来吗？难道连她自己都没有察觉？{w} 对了，我之前一直没想到——那个在{time=21:00}一次次把我们送往1月5日的 Sekimeiya，正是 Shiroya 在浴室里启动的。',
        "...Could she really have gone to the future? Did that occur without her realizing it? Right, I didn't think about it earlier, but the Sekimeiya that sent us repeatedly to January 5th at 21:00 was the one that Shiroya activated in the bathroom.": '……她真的去了未来吗？难道连她自己都没有察觉？{w} 对了，我之前一直没想到——那个在{time=21:00}一次次把我们送往1月5日的 Sekimeiya，正是 Shiroya 在浴室里启动的。',
        "...Could she really have gone to the future? Did that occur without her realizing it?{w} Right, I didn't think about it earlier, but the Sekimeiya that sent us repeatedly to January 5th at 9:00 p.m. was the one that Shiroya activated in the bathroom.": '……她真的去了未来吗？难道连她自己都没有察觉？{w} 对了，我之前一直没想到——那个在{time=21:00}一次次把我们送往1月5日的 Sekimeiya，正是 Shiroya 在浴室里启动的。',
        "...Could she really have gone to the future? Did that occur without her realizing it? Right, I didn't think about it earlier, but the Sekimeiya that sent us repeatedly to January 5th at 9:00 p.m. was the one that Shiroya activated in the bathroom.": '……她真的去了未来吗？难道连她自己都没有察觉？{w} 对了，我之前一直没想到——那个在{time=21:00}一次次把我们送往1月5日的 Sekimeiya，正是 Shiroya 在浴室里启动的。',
        "She didn't tell me exactly what she did, but I know she was in the mechanical room. She told me that she found the attic key there. So she was looking for something, and without realizing it, she moved the Future Sekimeiya in the mechanical room. The next time that all of us appeared, nobody instantly activated the next travel, so we stopped on the 5th. That has to be it!": '她没细说自己做了什么，但我知道她去过机械室。她说过，阁楼的钥匙就是在那儿找到的。{w} 也就是说，她当时在找东西，却无意间挪动了机械室里的未来Sekimeiya。等我们所有人下一次现身时，没有人立刻启动下一段穿越，所以我们才停在了5日。一定是这样！',
        "...Although it once seemed impossible, saving Miiya from the explosion should be simple. Very soon, if I touch the Sekimeiya, I'll be sent back to a point before she died. ...Then, I could stop it. I could change the past.": '……把 Miiya 从爆炸中救下，曾经看来毫无可能，如今却应该很简单。再过不久，只要我触碰 Sekimeiya，就会被送回她死去之前的时间点。{w}……那样，我就能阻止它。我就能改变过去。',
        "If I'm right, and touching the Sekimeiya when both ranges overlap will send me to the other world, I could do that after saving Miiya. If it worked, although I'd end up in my original world, I would've at least facilitated the best one's existence.": '如果我的推测没错，在两个范围重叠时触碰 Sekimeiya 就能被送往另一个世界，那我大可在救下 Miiya 之后这么做。{w} 若真能成功，纵然我最后会回到原本的世界，至少也能让那个最好的世界存在下去。',
        "But I don't get what's happening right now. Why was Miiya in the tower? If I did what I'm thinking, I would make sure our past selves don't go to the event, as that would put them in danger again. So, then, why is Miiya here? ...And why have I not seen Shiroya anywhere?": '可眼前的一切，我仍旧想不通。Miiya 为什么会在塔里？{w} 若我按计划行事，一定会设法让过去的我们不去参加那场活动，免得他们再次陷入危险。既然如此，Miiya 又怎会在这里？……还有，为什么我到处都见不到 Shiroya？',
        "...That time before 21:00, why did Shiroya say that she didn't want to save Miiya? It couldn't have been the real Shiroya, but I can't figure out a reason.": '……{time=21}之前的那一次，Shiroya 为什么说不想救 Miiya？那不可能是真正的 Shiroya，可我想不出其中的缘由。',
        "...That time before 9 p.m., why did Shiroya say that she didn't want to save Miiya? It couldn't have been the real Shiroya, but I can't figure out a reason.": '……{time=21}之前的那一次，Shiroya 为什么说不想救 Miiya？那不可能是真正的 Shiroya，可我想不出其中的缘由。',
        "...However, as I'd thought, doing what I'd proposed myself was simple. I only had to touch the Sekimeiya when the device displayed 65 minutes and 20 seconds. As I could plan out the loop before executing it, there was a best-case scenario that I'd thought up.": '……不过，正如我所料，执行自己的方案并不难。只要在装置显示65分20秒时触碰 Sekimeiya 即可。{w} 我可以在执行之前把循环安排妥当，也想好了一套最理想的情形。',
        "After November 30th, once everything is done, I could touch the Sekimeiya to go to our previous world. There, I know I'll be able to use the Sekimeiya on January 5th after we break free from the chain of travels. ...If I plan this out so I obtain both Sekimeiya on the 5th, I can appear with them on November 24th, which will allow me to use them immediately after the 30th.": '等到11月30日之后、一切尘埃落定，我可以触碰 Sekimeiya，回到我们原先的世界。在那里，等我们挣脱穿越的连锁，我知道自己能在1月5日使用 Sekimeiya。{w}……只要我事先安排妥当，让自己在5日那天拿到两个 Sekimeiya，就能带着它们出现在11月24日，这样在30日之后便能立刻动用。',
        "...Was it a flawed plan? I went over it again, and I didn't think so. I intended to change history. There was no option to check a note a future self of mine would leave behind to assure my success. Saving Miiya was achievable. I'd dearly wished for that, hoped it was possible, been denied, and arrived at a real chance for it. It was a surreal thought, but there was no longer a reason to doubt it.": '……{w}这个计划有破绽吗？我又推敲了一遍，不觉得有。我本来就打算改写历史。我也无法靠未来自己留下的字条来确认这次行动能否成功。{w} 救下 Miiya 是可以做到的。我曾那样殷切地盼望、相信它有可能实现，也曾被现实否定，如今终于等到了真正的机会。这念头仿佛不真实，却再没有理由怀疑。',
        "Once it was created, I would let that world continue to exist by leaving it. Would it be possible to find the Shiroya I'd been with? If so, would we be able to return to our world? Assuming we could do that, there would be nothing else to wish for.": '一旦那个世界被创造出来，我会离开那里，让它继续存在下去。{w} 我能找到曾与我相伴的那个 Shiroya 吗？若能找到，我们还能回到原本的世界吗？倘若这一切都能实现，那便再无所求了。',
        "But I still can't wrap my head around Miiya's existence in the tower. Does that conflict with what I'm aiming for? How was she here? If I save her, I know I'll make sure none of us go to the tower. How is it possible that she was here all day?": '可我怎么也想不明白，Miiya 为什么会在塔里。这和我打算做的事有冲突吗？{w} 她怎么会在这里？如果我救了她，我一定会确保我们谁都不去那座塔。既然如此，她又怎么可能一整天都待在这里？',
        "I don't understand it, but it shouldn't be an issue regardless. On top of that, I can't be content with just knowing that she was in the tower. I still need to act.": '我不明白，但无论如何，这应该都不成问题。{w} 再说，光是知道她曾在塔里，并不能让我安心。我还得动手去做。',
        "The note I found in my pocket could've come from Miiya. Erina said that she saw her minutes before we traveled to the world where she existed... That note implied only one thing: Shiroya's death. If that world was this very same one I'm in, and Miiya came from it, could that be why I haven't seen Shiroya...? Is it because she's not here at all?": '我口袋里那张字条，或许是 Miiya 写的。Erina 说过，就在我们穿越到那个有她存在的世界之前几分钟，她还见过 Miiya……{w} 那张字条只暗示了一件事：Shiroya 的死。如果那个世界正是我现在身处的世界，而 Miiya 也来自那里，这会不会就是我一直没见到 Shiroya 的原因……？她根本就不在这里？',
        "I can do it, can't I? I can easily appear on November 24th. It has to be that day because it's proportional to January 5th. I don't think anyone's still in the tower right now, so the range should only affect me.": '我能做到的，不是吗？让我出现在11月24日并不难。必须是那一天，它与1月5日正好对应。{w} 现在塔里应该没有别人了，波及范围也只会影响我一个人。',
        "In November, I could very easily obtain the money my past self has saved. However, I'd like to avoid doing that so I don't cause any issues. Instead, I can just duplicate it. I can take that money, which will allow me to have it on January 5th. Then, I'll appear with it on November 24th, so it won't be necessary to obtain it from my past self.": '到了十一月，想拿到过去的自己存下的那笔钱很容易。但我不想节外生枝，所以还是别那么干。{w} 不如直接复制一份。我拿走复制出来的钱，就能在一月五日拥有它；再带着它出现在十一月二十四日，就不用从过去的自己手里取了。',
        '65:15, 16, 17, 18...': '65:15，{w=1} 16，{w=1}17，{w=1} 18……',
        "It worked...! The Sekimeiya are here! This is everything I need to confirm this'll work! I'll go back to my world, and on January 5th, I'll be able to get both Sekimeiya!": '成功了……！Sekimeiya 就在这里！{w} 有这些，就够我确认这计划行得通了！{w} 我回到自己的世界，到了一月五日，就能把两个 Sekimeiya 都拿到手！',
        "I placed my hand on the handle and gently pushed. The door didn't open. As I'd expected, it was locked. I couldn't go to the storeroom because the hallway cameras would record me...": '我把手放在门把上，轻轻一推。{w} 门没有开。果然锁着。{w} 我不能去储藏室，走廊的摄像头会拍到我……',
        'My attention was immediately grabbed by a digital clock on the table. It was 22:54 on November 24th, a Thursday.': '桌上的电子钟立刻吸引了我的目光。上面显示着 11 月 24 日，星期四，{time=22:54}。',
        'My attention was immediately grabbed by a digital clock on the table. It was 10:54 p.m. on November 24th, a Thursday.': '桌上的电子钟立刻吸引了我的目光。上面显示着 11 月 24 日，星期四，{time=22:54}。',
        'Wait! The money... I have to duplicate it.': '等等！{w}钱……我得把钱复制出来。',
        "They've been outside for so long, I'm sure they don't have a lot of energy. I should be able to touch one without the range reaching anyone else here. I wonder which is the future one. If I touch the past one, I'll just appear in the bathroom and stay there until my past self leaves.": '它们在外面放了这么久，能量肯定不多了。我碰其中一个，影响范围应该不会波及这里的其他人。{w}不知道哪个才是通往未来的。要是碰到过去那个，我只会出现在浴室里，一直待到过去的我离开为止。',
        "I'd undressed before getting in bed since the room was warm. If I replicated my past location, the money I'd been holding would duplicate. I placed the suitcase on the bed and separated both gemstones. Then, I touched one of them in the center of the room.": '房间很暖和，我上床前就把衣服脱了。只要重现我过去所在的位置，我手里的钱就会复制出来。{w}我把手提箱放到床上，把两颗宝石分开，然后在房间中央碰了其中一个。',
        'The Sekimeiya was still on the bed. There was no doubt it was the future one, as the clock showed 23:29.': 'Sekimeiya 还在床上。钟上显示着 {time=23:29.}，毫无疑问是通往未来的那个。',
        'The Sekimeiya was still on the bed. There was no doubt it was the future one, as the clock showed 11:29 p.m.': 'Sekimeiya 还在床上。钟上显示着 {time=23:29.}，毫无疑问是通往未来的那个。',
        'My old clothes were beside the bed, but I had to reset the Sekimeiya before attempting it again. I sat up and walked to the kitchen.': '原先的衣服就在床边，不过我得先把 Sekimeiya 重置，才能再试一次。{w}我坐起身，走向厨房。',
        'I looked at the clock, trying to remember where I was. {time=10:09}, November 25th. It all came back to me when I saw those blurry numbers.': '我看向时钟，努力回想自己身在何处。{w} {time=10:09}，11 月 25 日。看清那串模糊的数字，一切才重新涌回脑海。',
        'I looked at the clock, trying to remember where I was.{w} 10:09, November 25th. It all came back to me when I saw those blurry numbers.': '我看向时钟，努力回想自己身在何处。{w} {time=10:09}，11 月 25 日。看清那串模糊的数字，一切才重新涌回脑海。',
        'I looked at the clock, trying to remember where I was. 10:09, November 25th. It all came back to me when I saw those blurry numbers.': '我看向时钟，努力回想自己身在何处。{w} {time=10:09}，11 月 25 日。看清那串模糊的数字，一切才重新涌回脑海。',
        'I looked at the clock, trying to remember where I was.{w} 10:09 a.m., November 25th. It all came back to me when I saw those blurry numbers.': '我看向时钟，努力回想自己身在何处。{w} {time=10:09}，11 月 25 日。看清那串模糊的数字，一切才重新涌回脑海。',
        'I looked at the clock, trying to remember where I was. 10:09 a.m., November 25th. It all came back to me when I saw those blurry numbers.': '我看向时钟，努力回想自己身在何处。{w} {time=10:09}，11 月 25 日。看清那串模糊的数字，一切才重新涌回脑海。',
        'Fortunately, I had enough money to cover all the days I needed. Once I felt rested, I went back up.': '幸好身上的钱足够付清这些天的房费。{w}歇够了，我才回到楼上。',
        "I couldn't bring myself to do that. ...I had already accepted Miiya's death once. Even if I was able to bring her to our world, would that truly be better? I would just create avoidable pain in another.": '可我做不到。……Miiya 的死，我已经接受过一次。{w} 就算我能把她带回我们的世界，那真的更好吗？我不过是在另一个世界里制造本可避免的痛苦罢了。',
        "He didn't take his eyes off the clock. At 21:00, he could hardly breathe, remembering what had once happened.": '他的视线一刻也没离开时钟。到了 {time=21}，回想起曾经发生过的事，他几乎无法呼吸。',
        "He didn't take his eyes off the clock. At 9 p.m., he could hardly breathe, remembering what had once happened.": '他的视线一刻也没离开时钟。到了 {time=21}，回想起曾经发生过的事，他几乎无法呼吸。',
        "...He didn't see it. None of them had been about a gas explosion in Yushibana.": '……{w}他没有看到。没有一条是关于丰花煤气爆炸的。',
        "When he reached the street, he was able to see it in the distance: there was light in Musashi Gemstones. He didn't stop running. He burst through the door and gaped at the owner in disbelief.": '跑到那条街上时，他远远就看见了：武藏宝石里亮着灯。{w} 他没有停下脚步，一把推开门，难以置信地瞪着店主。',
        "No... What am I thinking? ...I didn't change the past at all.": '不……我在胡思乱想什么？{w}……我根本没有改变过去。',
        "And in that world, I ended up taking the elevator up to follow Shiroya. That had to be when we came back. For some reason, we went back to our world. That's what that injury signified—the elevator stopped abruptly because it wasn't moving in our world, and I cut myself with the handrail as my body overlapped with it.": '而在那个世界里，我为了追 Shiroya，坐上了电梯。{w}我们一定就是在那时回来的。不知为何，我们回到了自己的世界。{w}那道伤就是这个意思——电梯在我们这个世界里本就没有运行，所以骤然停住；我的身体和扶手重叠在一起，手被割伤了。',
        "And that was the exact world we'd been in before: the Past Sekimeiya was back in the staff room, where I'd hidden it. It didn't teleport back there. Akaro was gone, and Sai was once again the person we'd been with in the event room. Also, the blood I would leave on the staircase was surely already there.": '而那正是我们先前待过的世界：过去Sekimeiya回到了员工室，就在我藏它的地方。它不是被传送回去的。{w}Akaro不见了，活动室里和我们在一起的又变回了Sai。还有，我之后会留在楼梯上的血迹，那时想必已经在那里了。',
        '...So, when I went back in time and produced that "new" sound... I didn\'t actually change anything. When I slammed the door, the event room was already empty. And then, despite the difference I would\'ve caused, Erina and I still got out of the elevator on the third floor.': '……{w}也就是说，我穿越回过去，弄出那声「新」的响动……其实什么都没改变。我摔门的时候，活动室已经空了。{w}而后来，尽管我本该改变些什么，Erina和我还是在三楼走出了电梯。',
        "Now what!? Technically, I could never die after traveling to the past, or else there'd be no future location to replicate. Would I die by touching the Sekimeiya, then? There's no way to verify any of this...!": '那又该怎么办！？严格说来，穿越回过去之后，我根本不可能死，否则就没有未来的位置可供复制了。{w}那么，我会因为触碰Sekimeiya而死吗？这些根本无从验证……！',
        'I appeared in the bathroom. Silently, I glanced at the bedroom.': '我出现在浴室里。{w}我默默朝卧室瞥了一眼。',
        '12:43. November 28th...': '{time=12:43.}11月28日……',
        '12:43 p.m. November 28th...': '{time=12:43.}11月28日……',
        "Wait. This is wrong... That can't be the case...!": '等等。{w}不对……{w}不可能是这样……！',
        "But I had the Sekimeiya. If that had removed the ones on the mountain, the butterfly effect would surely be immense. That was why I had to consider a certain question and why I hadn't opened the refrigerator. ...Was there a way for the Sekimeiya to have been found the day before?": '但我手里有 Sekimeiya。如果这会让山上的那些消失，蝴蝶效应必然巨大。{w}正因如此，我才必须先想清楚一个问题，才没有打开冰箱。……有没有可能，Sekimeiya 确实在前一天就被发现了？',
        "...Is there any chance? If they were found, they can't be here anymore. Similarly, if they're here, they couldn't have been found. Is it impossible...? That can't be...": '……有这种可能吗？若它们被发现了，就不可能还在这里。同样，若它们还在这里，就不可能被发现过。{w}难道真的不可能……？不会的……',
        "It's... not possible. They couldn't have been found yesterday! But the past can't change, can it? Does that mean they're not in the refrigerator anymore? If I never open it, should I assume that they made it to the mountain somehow?": '这……不可能。它们不可能昨天就被发现了！{w}可过去是无法改变的，不是吗？那是不是说，它们已经不在冰箱里了？如果我永远不打开，是不是就该认为，它们以某种方式到了山上？',
        "This is where the Sekimeiya were found. I can't believe it. How is that even possible? This was our special place...": '那几个 Sekimeiya 就是在这里被发现的。真不敢相信。{w}这怎么可能？这里明明是我们最特别的地方……',
        '...I stepped back out, opened the suitcase, and looked at the clock. It was 14:03.': '……我重新走到屋外，打开箱子，看了看时钟。时间是 {time=14:03.}',
        '...I stepped back out, opened the suitcase, and looked at the clock. It was 2:03 p.m.': '……我重新走到屋外，打开箱子，看了看时钟。时间是 {time=14:03.}',
        'I appeared inside the cabin, next to the door. When I looked outside, I saw myself in the middle of the field. 35 seconds later, I disappeared.': '我出现在木屋里，就在门边。朝外望去，我看见自己站在空地中央。{w}三十五秒后，那个我便消失了。',
        'The Sekimeiya was on the grass, next to the suitcase and the clock. I put it inside at 14:05.': 'Sekimeiya 当时在草地上，旁边是箱子和时钟。我在 {time=14:05.} 把它放了进去。',
        'The Sekimeiya was on the grass, next to the suitcase and the clock. I put it inside at 2:05 p.m.': 'Sekimeiya 当时在草地上，旁边是箱子和时钟。我在 {time=14:05.} 把它放了进去。',
        'I spent the last stretch sitting on a bed. I could see the suitcase through the window, and at 14:43, I stood up.': '最后那段时间，我一直坐在床上。透过窗户能看见那只箱子。到了 {time=14:43}，我站起身来。',
        'I spent the last stretch sitting on a bed. I could see the suitcase through the window, and at 2:43 p.m., I stood up.': '最后那段时间，我一直坐在床上。透过窗户能看见那只箱子。到了 {time=14:43}，我站起身来。',
        'I locked my eyes on those numbers. As soon as 14:45 appeared, I opened it.': '我死死盯着那些数字。{time=14:45} 一出现，我便打开了箱子。',
        'I locked my eyes on those numbers. As soon as 2:45 p.m. appeared, I opened it.': '我死死盯着那些数字。{time=14:45} 一出现，我便打开了箱子。',
        "It was my own self sleeping. When I glanced at the clock, I saw the red numbers I'd expected: 7:01. November 27th.": '睡在那里的正是我自己。我瞥了一眼时钟，红色数字正如我所料：{time=7:01.}11月27日。',
        "It was my own self sleeping. When I glanced at the clock, I saw the red numbers I'd expected: 7:01 a.m. November 27th.": '睡在那里的正是我自己。我瞥了一眼时钟，红色数字正如我所料：{time=7:01.}11月27日。',
        "Oh, it's a lot dustier in here... I suppose that makes sense; I have to stay until I can return to the motel.": '哦，这里的灰可真多……{w}也难怪，我得在这儿待到能回旅馆为止。',
        "Yawning, I put the clock in the suitcase and drowsily moved through the rows of trees. The sun was well past the mountains, so I'd slept for a long time. I entered the streets of Yushibana and walked to Eagle Motel.": '我打着哈欠把时钟放进箱子，昏昏沉沉地穿过一排排树。太阳早已越过山头，看来我睡了很久。{w}我走进丰花的街道，朝鹰旅馆走去。',
        'I quickly looked at the time: it was 10:29.': '我赶紧看了一眼时间：{time=10:29.}',
        'I quickly looked at the time: it was 10:29 a.m.': '我赶紧看了一眼时间：{time=10:29.}',
        "I'd had them sitting in the refrigerator for so long without using them. It was undeniable that I could've obtained anything with them; Sai had once talked about winning the lottery with ease. But I hadn't worried about that because of the single guarantee I possessed: on January 5th, I would have both Sekimeiya.": '它们就那么一直放在冰箱里，这么久我都没用过。不可否认，有它们在，我什么都弄得到；Sai 还说过，用它们中彩票轻而易举。{w}可我并不为此担心，因为我握着一个绝对的保证：1月5日，两个 Sekimeiya 都会在我手上。',
        "{time=7:11.} December 1st. I'd gotten new batteries for the clock and confirmed it was accurate. I gingerly rubbed my eyes, grateful that I'd at least been able to sleep a little.": '{time=7:11.}12月1日。{w}我给时钟换了新电池，确认它走得准。我轻轻揉了揉眼睛，庆幸自己至少还睡了一会儿。',
        "7:11. December 1st.{w} I'd gotten new batteries for the clock and confirmed it was accurate. I gingerly rubbed my eyes, grateful that I'd at least been able to sleep a little.": '{time=7:11.}12月1日。{w}我给时钟换了新电池，确认它走得准。我轻轻揉了揉眼睛，庆幸自己至少还睡了一会儿。',
        "7:11. December 1st. I'd gotten new batteries for the clock and confirmed it was accurate. I gingerly rubbed my eyes, grateful that I'd at least been able to sleep a little.": '{time=7:11.}12月1日。{w}我给时钟换了新电池，确认它走得准。我轻轻揉了揉眼睛，庆幸自己至少还睡了一会儿。',
        "7:11 a.m. December 1st.{w} I'd gotten new batteries for the clock and confirmed it was accurate. I gingerly rubbed my eyes, grateful that I'd at least been able to sleep a little.": '{time=7:11.}12月1日。{w}我给时钟换了新电池，确认它走得准。我轻轻揉了揉眼睛，庆幸自己至少还睡了一会儿。',
        "7:11 a.m. December 1st. I'd gotten new batteries for the clock and confirmed it was accurate. I gingerly rubbed my eyes, grateful that I'd at least been able to sleep a little.": '{time=7:11.}12月1日。{w}我给时钟换了新电池，确认它走得准。我轻轻揉了揉眼睛，庆幸自己至少还睡了一会儿。',
        '"Gas explosion in Yushibana". At a low volume, a reporter began to talk about it.': '「丰花发生瓦斯爆炸。」{w} 记者压低了声音，开始播报这条新闻。',
        "Last night, a gas explosion occurred at a gem shop in Yushibana. An unknown individual released smoke that knocked four people unconscious, and some time later, the explosion occurred due to a gas heater that had depleted its surrounding oxygen. Given the size of the explosion, the flame had been out before the smoke's release. Since everyone present was unconscious, nobody was able to recognize the artificial smell of the gas, which had no way to leave the enclosed space. At {time=21}, when the lights were turned on, the presence of smoke and gas caused a dust explosion.": '昨晚，丰花的一家宝石店发生瓦斯爆炸。一名不明身份者释放烟雾，导致四人昏迷；其后，一台耗尽了周围氧气的瓦斯暖炉引发了爆炸。{w} 从爆炸的规模来看，在烟雾释放之前，火焰便已熄灭。由于在场者全部昏迷，没人能察觉出瓦斯那股人工气味，而封闭的空间又让瓦斯无处散去。{time=21}，灯光亮起时，积聚的烟雾与瓦斯引发了粉尘爆炸。',
        "Last night, a gas explosion occurred at a gem shop in Yushibana. An unknown individual released smoke that knocked four people unconscious, and some time later, the explosion occurred due to a gas heater that had depleted its surrounding oxygen.{w} Given the size of the explosion, the flame had been out before the smoke's release. Since everyone present was unconscious, nobody was able to recognize the artificial smell of the gas, which had no way to leave the enclosed space. At 21:00, when the lights were turned on, the presence of smoke and gas caused a dust explosion.": '昨晚，丰花的一家宝石店发生瓦斯爆炸。一名不明身份者释放烟雾，导致四人昏迷；其后，一台耗尽了周围氧气的瓦斯暖炉引发了爆炸。{w} 从爆炸的规模来看，在烟雾释放之前，火焰便已熄灭。由于在场者全部昏迷，没人能察觉出瓦斯那股人工气味，而封闭的空间又让瓦斯无处散去。{time=21}，灯光亮起时，积聚的烟雾与瓦斯引发了粉尘爆炸。',
        "Last night, a gas explosion occurred at a gem shop in Yushibana. An unknown individual released smoke that knocked four people unconscious, and some time later, the explosion occurred due to a gas heater that had depleted its surrounding oxygen. Given the size of the explosion, the flame had been out before the smoke's release. Since everyone present was unconscious, nobody was able to recognize the artificial smell of the gas, which had no way to leave the enclosed space. At 21:00, when the lights were turned on, the presence of smoke and gas caused a dust explosion.": '昨晚，丰花的一家宝石店发生瓦斯爆炸。一名不明身份者释放烟雾，导致四人昏迷；其后，一台耗尽了周围氧气的瓦斯暖炉引发了爆炸。{w} 从爆炸的规模来看，在烟雾释放之前，火焰便已熄灭。由于在场者全部昏迷，没人能察觉出瓦斯那股人工气味，而封闭的空间又让瓦斯无处散去。{time=21}，灯光亮起时，积聚的烟雾与瓦斯引发了粉尘爆炸。',
        "Last night, a gas explosion occurred at a gem shop in Yushibana. An unknown individual released smoke that knocked four people unconscious, and some time later, the explosion occurred due to a gas heater that had depleted its surrounding oxygen.{w} Given the size of the explosion, the flame had been out before the smoke's release. Since everyone present was unconscious, nobody was able to recognize the artificial smell of the gas, which had no way to leave the enclosed space. At 9 p.m., when the lights were turned on, the presence of smoke and gas caused a dust explosion.": '昨晚，丰花的一家宝石店发生瓦斯爆炸。一名不明身份者释放烟雾，导致四人昏迷；其后，一台耗尽了周围氧气的瓦斯暖炉引发了爆炸。{w} 从爆炸的规模来看，在烟雾释放之前，火焰便已熄灭。由于在场者全部昏迷，没人能察觉出瓦斯那股人工气味，而封闭的空间又让瓦斯无处散去。{time=21}，灯光亮起时，积聚的烟雾与瓦斯引发了粉尘爆炸。',
        "Last night, a gas explosion occurred at a gem shop in Yushibana. An unknown individual released smoke that knocked four people unconscious, and some time later, the explosion occurred due to a gas heater that had depleted its surrounding oxygen. Given the size of the explosion, the flame had been out before the smoke's release. Since everyone present was unconscious, nobody was able to recognize the artificial smell of the gas, which had no way to leave the enclosed space. At 9 p.m., when the lights were turned on, the presence of smoke and gas caused a dust explosion.": '昨晚，丰花的一家宝石店发生瓦斯爆炸。一名不明身份者释放烟雾，导致四人昏迷；其后，一台耗尽了周围氧气的瓦斯暖炉引发了爆炸。{w} 从爆炸的规模来看，在烟雾释放之前，火焰便已熄灭。由于在场者全部昏迷，没人能察觉出瓦斯那股人工气味，而封闭的空间又让瓦斯无处散去。{time=21}，灯光亮起时，积聚的烟雾与瓦斯引发了粉尘爆炸。',
        'The other two people, a nineteen-year-old boy and the owner of the shop, were far enough from the heater that they avoided major damage. The identity of the person who released the smoke is being investigated, as is their motive. Despite the outcome, it is unlikely that the explosion was intentional, and nothing has been reported as stolen.': '另外两人——一名十九岁的少年和店主——离暖炉较远，避开了严重的伤害。{w} 释放烟雾者的身份与动机仍在调查。尽管结果如此，爆炸多半并非蓄意为之，也没有任何失窃的报告。',
        "...I see. This is before they found her jaw. I don't even know why I thought I could expect anything else.": '……{w}原来如此。这是在她下颌骨被发现之前。我都不知道自己凭什么觉得会有别的结果。',
        "After hearing everything again, my heart dropped into a black abyss. It almost felt like I'd been told the news for the first time again. ...I really was powerless. The immense power I'd been able to wield meant nothing.": '再次听完这一切，我的心沉入了漆黑的深渊。几乎又像是头一次听到这个消息。{w}……我果然无能为力。我曾能驾驭的那股庞大力量，此刻毫无意义。',
        "As expected, they're being kept in here. I shouldn't bother checking inside. That could bring me problems, and there's no way only one was found anyway...": '果然，它们被收在这里。{w} 我不该多此一举进去查看。那只会给我惹麻烦，而且怎么可能只找到一件……',
        'I was about to step out when a voice called for me. It was the receptionist, who held out a green paper that I recognized.': '我正要出门，有人叫住了我。{w} 是前台的那位，她递来一张我认得的绿色传单。',
        '...Our sleep schedule was all over the place. I spent most nights awake.': '……{w}我们的作息彻底乱了。大部分夜晚我都醒着。',
        '...I was right. I changed my past, but not the past of the Atsuki from this world. In my memories, the snow piled on the gate never fell.': '……{w}我猜对了。我改变的是自己的过去，不是这个世界的 Atsuki 的过去。在我的记忆里，门上那堆积雪从没被抖掉过。',
        "The reason why I hadn't been able to unlock that door from the inside... I had thought that if an identical key was on the opposite side, I might not have been able to turn it from the inside. I wanted it to be there. I needed it to remain outside so that the door wouldn't be unlocked from the inside... so that Katei couldn't escape and so that the others couldn't leave when they found the door. But... why was that key there? If it was just there because I'd known it would be there, that didn't really satisfy me.": '我一直没能从内侧打开那扇门，原因就在这里……我原先猜想，如果对面插着一把一模一样的钥匙，从里面或许就拧不动了。{w} 我希望那把钥匙在那里。我需要它留在门外，这样门就无法从内侧打开……Katei 便逃不出去，其他人发现那扇门时也走不了。{w} 可是……那把钥匙为什么会插在那里？如果只是因为我早就知道它会在那儿，这个理由并不能让我满意。',
        'I got closer to the hallway. It would very soon be 9:00.': '我朝走廊靠近。马上就要到{time=9.}了。',
        'I got closer to the hallway. It would very soon be 9 a.m.': '我朝走廊靠近。马上就要到{time=9.}了。',
        "Katei won't be in the security room... Nobody will see me getting out of here. I'll be recorded. Maybe the footage will actually be seen by the police. ...That doesn't matter, though.": 'Katei 不在监控室……没人会看见我从这里出去。{w} 不过我会被拍下来。也许那段录像真会落到警察手里。……那也无所谓了。',
        'I made it just in time to see the event room closing. The first group was there. I had very little time; the second group would appear at any moment.': '我赶得及时，看见活动室的门正在合上。第一批人已经进去了。{w} 我的时间所剩无几，第二批随时都会出现。',
        'I knew the alarm would lock it. If that happened, Katei could be fast enough to erase the footage I wanted to preserve. However, I could avoid that by staying inside. He had told us once that the door could be unlocked from the inside without the need for the key.': '我知道警报一响，那扇门就会自动上锁。若真如此，只要 Katei 手脚够快，就能把我想要保住的录像抹掉。{w} 不过，只要我待在里面，就能避免这一点。他曾经告诉过我们，那扇门从内侧打开并不需要钥匙。',
        "She and I were in the event room with Akaro. And... Shiroya was nowhere to be seen. I couldn't believe it. No matter how much I stared at the footage, I couldn't believe that she was really a room away. And the cabinet covered by that crimson curtain... Which Sekimeiya were there?": '我和她，还有 Akaro，都在活动室里。而……Shiroya 却不见踪影。{w} 我不敢相信。无论盯着画面看多久，都不敢相信她就在一室之隔的地方。{w} 还有那个罩着深红遮布的展示柜……里面放的是哪几个 Sekimeiya？',
        'Every monitor displayed different locations on the crystal floor except for one. One of the screens was covered by tape. I kept my eyes peeled with anticipation. It was about to happen again. I would see that dense smoke appearing out of nowhere, and my vision would blacken.': '只有一块屏幕例外，其余每块都显示着水晶层上的不同位置。那块屏幕被胶带贴住了。{w} 我屏息凝神，紧盯着屏幕。那件事又要发生了。我会看见浓烟凭空涌出，随后眼前一黑。',
        "When Shiroya and I had appeared on that morning after traveling from January 5th, we'd been able to avoid falling unconscious by looking down as we'd run through the smoke. Akaro had to have thrown himself to the ground immediately to avoid inhaling it, as it had quickly risen to the ceiling. I had to act again while I still could, but I waited a few seconds so that the exit to the outside would close.": '从 1 月 5 日穿越过来的那个早上，Shiroya 和我一出现，就一边跑过烟雾一边低头，才没有晕过去。烟雾很快升到了天花板，Akaro 想必是立刻趴到了地上，才没吸进去。{w} 我必须趁自己还能行动时再动手，可我还是等了几秒，好让通往外面的出口关上。',
        'Is someone here...? Is it Katei?': '有人吗……？{w} 是 Katei 吗？',
        'On the screen, the culprits finally came to light. Akaro came out of the event room and looked both ways.': '屏幕上，罪魁祸首终于显露出来。{w} Akaro 从活动室里走出，左右张望。',
        "What the hell...? Is that a Sekimeiya? No, I know what that must be. ...The third Sekimeiya. That's what the plan was about.": '搞什么……？那是 Sekimeiya？{w} 不，我知道那是什么。……第三个 Sekimeiya。原来那个计划打的是这个主意。',
        '...This is why only the third Sekimeiya was there when we woke up. When does Katei come into the picture, though?': '……难怪我们醒来时，那里只剩第三个 Sekimeiya。{w} 可 Katei 又是什么时候插进来的？',
        "I didn't have to wait very long to find out. After Akaro had returned to the event room, Katei appeared from the lobby. Keeping his head down, he stepped to the cleaning room.": '我没等多久就知道了。Akaro 回到活动室之后，Katei 从大厅那边出现了。{w} 他低着头，走进了清洁间。',
        "It was Naomi. She ran all the way down holding Katei's suitcase, and as she disappeared, another door opened. From room B4, Shiroya and I appeared—Naomi had drawn us out. Then, Shiroya stared at the camera intensely, as if she was looking directly at me. Before I could even process it, they ran behind the sound, quickly vanishing from the frame.": '那是 Naomi。她提着 Katei 的手提箱一路跑下楼，就在她消失时，另一扇门开了。{w} Shiroya 和我从 B4房间走出来——是 Naomi 把我们引出来的。随后，Shiroya 死死盯着摄像头，仿佛正透过镜头看着我。还没等我理清头绪，他们便循着声响跑向后方，转眼消失在画面里。',
        "I couldn't travel forward in time to speed up the process because I hadn't been in the tower in the proportional past. However, I doubted I would have been willing to do that anyway. ...To skip that last time I had... where Miiya existed. When I heard her voice, I couldn't stop myself from getting closer to the door.": '我无法穿越到未来去加快进度，因为在对应的那段过去里，我并没有待在塔里。不过，就算能这么做，我大概也不会愿意。{w}……毕竟，那会跳过我所拥有的最后一段……有 Miiya 在的时光。听到她的声音时，我还是忍不住朝门口靠近。',
        "Oh, huh. The suitcase isn't here this time. Naomi ran up to the attic with it, and I didn't see it. But the Sekimeiya were on the sofa. It has to be that the suitcase was brought to our world as well, which is why we saw two.": '哦，咦？这次手提箱不在这里。{w} Naomi 提着它跑上了阁楼，可我没看到那箱子。不过 Sekimeiya 在沙发上。一定是手提箱也被带到了我们的世界，所以我们才会看到两个。',
        '...Was that it? No one else seemed to be coming. Why had they gone down alone? As I wondered that, a fifth person came from the upper floor.': '……就这些？似乎不会再有别人下来了。{w} 他们为什么独自下楼？我正想着，第五个人从楼上走了下来。',
        'Akaro. He looked deep in thought as he walked. While I was still fazed, the sixth person appeared. Sai trailed behind Akaro as he disappeared beyond the glass.': 'Akaro。他边走边沉思。{w} 我还没回过神，第六个人出现了。Sai 跟在 Akaro 身后，后者消失在了玻璃那头。',
        '...What the hell are they doing? I remember this. When I was in the storeroom, everyone came back on their own. I heard different footsteps walking beyond the wall.': '……他们到底在干什么？{w} 这一幕我记得。我待在储藏室的时候，所有人都是自己回来的。我听见墙外传来不同的脚步声。',
        'People came from below. It sounded like it was the group of four: my other self, Miiya, Erina, and Isla. Ignoring the three partitions, they walked up. I could hear their steps above me, but they rapidly faded. ...Their destination was likely the attic.': '楼下有人上来了。听动静是那四个人：另一个我、Miiya、Erina 和 Isla。他们没理会那三处隔间，径直往上走。{w} 我能听见头顶的脚步声，可很快就远去了。……他们多半是去阁楼了。',
        'Oh...! I left the duct tape in the security room! It sounds like Katei found it.': '啊……！我把那卷胶带落在监控室了！{w} 听这意思，是 Katei 找到了。',
        'He had the keys. That means he got the keyring that Naomi left behind. Since the attic was locked just now, he definitely locked it while he was up here before.': '钥匙在他手上。也就是说，他拿到了 Naomi 落下的那串钥匙。{w} 刚才阁楼还是锁着的，那就肯定是他先前待在上面时锁上的。',
        "...What? Is it working? They just tried it on this floor, and it wasn't...": '……什么？电梯能用了？{w} 他们刚刚在这层试过，明明还不行……',
        'From there, I saw the people who were walking down. Myself, Miiya, and Katei.': '我从那里看见了往下走的几个人。{w} 我自己、Miiya，还有 Katei。',
        "...What is my other self thinking? What is he thinking now that he's witnessed time travel for the first time? The events of November 30th... Did they occur as I imagine? If so, I don't have to wonder.": '……另一个我在想什么？{w}第一次亲眼见到时间穿越，他现在会怎么想？11月30日发生的事……是不是和我设想的一样？如果是，那我就不用再猜了。',
        '...What? Did the other Atsuki just touch the Sekimeiya?': '……什么？{w}另一个 Atsuki 刚才是不是碰了 Sekimeiya？',
        "I kept looking at the staircase, wondering where the other Atsuki was. I was sure he had appeared in the past with Sai, but it was unusual that he hadn't shown himself yet. The door to the lobby was open. As it was likely he was on a higher floor, I wanted to leave as soon as I saw him returning.": '我一直望着楼梯，心里想着另一个我在哪儿。我确信他早已和 Sai 一起出现在了过去，却迟迟不露面，这很反常。{w}通往大厅的门开着。他多半在更高的楼层，我打算一看到他回来就立刻离开。',
        "Wait a second. Am I falling for it again? Katei touched the Sekimeiya and appeared in hallway A. He had just been there, as he'd walked from the security room to the event room. He appeared in a past location! He could've gone to the future.": '等等。我是不是又上当了？{w}Katei 碰了 Sekimeiya，然后出现在 A走廊。他刚刚才经过那里——从监控室走到活动室。{w}他出现在了过去的地点！可他也可能是去了未来啊。',
        "Why the hell did he say that!? He was carefully holding the Sekimeiya without touching it with his skin, so he knew about its powers... If he had traveled to the past before, it's very likely that's what he assumed just happened again. He went a couple seconds to the future, so he couldn't notice his own misinterpretation. Unless he lied on purpose, I guess.": '他到底为什么要那么说！？他小心地捧着 Sekimeiya，不让皮肤碰到它，可见他知道它的力量……{w}如果他以前有过穿越到过去的经历，那他很可能会以为这次也是如此。可他其实是去了几秒后的未来，所以察觉不到自己判断错了。除非——他是故意撒谎。',
        "So it was placed on the lens of that camera, which prevented the smoke from hitting it. Afterward, it was removed... I'm confused about a few things. Why would someone do that? They had to already know the smoke attack would happen.": '所以它是被贴在那台摄像头的镜头上，挡住了烟。之后又被取下来……{w}有几件事我想不通。谁会这么做？他一定事先就知道会有人放烟。',
        "The other Atsuki and Miiya were back. I saw them in the security room. I didn't understand what they'd been doing. ...Why would they have locked themselves in the attic? And why had they returned? Suddenly, a sound drew them to the lobby.": '另一个 Atsuki 和 Miiya 回来了。我看见他们进了监控室。{w}我不明白他们此前在做什么。……他们为什么要把自己关在阁楼里？又为什么回来了？{w}忽然，一个声响把他们引向了大厅。',
        "I was instantly alarmed. If they looked at the hallway, I would be seen. I couldn't go to the lobby, and walking back could lead to me being noticed.": '我顿时警觉起来。只要他们往走廊这边看一眼，就会发现我。{w}我不能去大厅，往回走也可能被人注意到。',
        'What? ...Who is that?': '什么？{w}……那是谁？',
        "I turned my head abruptly. ...Had someone just come out of the security room? I was fairly sure I'd sensed that, but I kept paying attention to the lobby.": '我猛地转过头。……刚刚是有人从监控室出来了吗？{w}我几乎确定自己察觉到了动静，却还是继续留意着大厅。',
        'Someone ran. That was all I could make out. Then, a noise like someone collapsing.': '有人跑了起来。我只分辨得出这些。{w}紧接着，传来一声像是有人倒下的响动。',
        '...What? Is he gone?': '……{w}怎么回事？他不见了？',
        'Did he enter through the storeroom? No. What am I thinking? My past self is currently there.': '难道是从储藏室进来的？{w}不对。我在想什么？过去的我此刻就在那里。',
        'Oh...! D-Did I just appear out of nowhere?': '啊……！{w}我、我是刚刚凭空出现的吗？',
        "...It teleported you as well? How come that didn't happen the other times?": '……{w}连你也一起传送了？为什么之前几次没发生这种事？',
        "They were in the event room, but I couldn't pick up anything. That was until Sai yelled.": '他们就在活动室，可我什么也听不清。{w}直到 Sai 大吼了一声。',
        "...Right. Katei went to the future a while ago. The range was large, so I bet it barely reached outside the tower. It reached far enough to include Suripo, and they went far forward in time. The locations match. Before the attack, Suripo was in the lobby, near the front door. At the time, Katei was still in the security room. That's where they appeared just now. Those locations are from a time before the smoke was released; Katei's clothes should have no smoke on them. They were pretty clean anyway, so I doubt anyone would notice that.": '……没错。Katei 刚才去了未来。范围很大，我猜它勉强够到了塔外。{w}但已经远到把 Suripo 也包了进去，于是他们一起跳到了很久之后。{w}位置也对得上。袭击发生前，Suripo 就在大厅靠近正门的地方；而当时 Katei 还在监控室。Katei 刚才正是在那里出现的。{w}这两处位置的时间都在烟雾释放之前，所以 Katei 的衣服上不该沾到烟。再说那身衣服本来就挺干净的，我想没人会注意到。',
        '...This is a knife wound.': '……{w}这是刀伤。',
        "Listening to the conversation, I grew a bit more confused. According to the other me, Suripo hadn't been dead six minutes previously, so nobody could've killed him.": '听着他们的对话，我越发糊涂了。{w}按另一个我的说法，六分钟前 Suripo 还没死，那就不可能有人杀他。',
        "But that's wrong. He was dead six minutes ago. Why is he saying that? ...Six minutes ago, I bet that version of me was already traveling to the future. There's no way he saw the lobby. Miiya's agreeing with him, though.": '可那不对。六分钟前他就已经死了。{w}他为什么这么说？……六分钟前，那个我那时应该已经在往未来穿越了，根本不可能看到大厅。可 Miiya 却附和他。',
        "This doesn't make sense, though. Sai just said it's 13:23.": '可这说不通。Sai 刚才说现在是 {time=13:23.}',
        "This doesn't make sense, though. Sai just said it's 1:23 p.m.": '可这说不通。Sai 刚才说现在是 {time=13:23.}',
        "That's what led Atsuki to say that Suripo was alive six minutes ago. At 13:17, they'd seen the lobby was empty.": '正因如此，Atsuki 才会说六分钟前 Suripo 还活着。{time=13:17} 的时候，他们看到大厅空无一人。',
        "That's what led Atsuki to say that Suripo was alive six minutes ago. At 1:17 p.m., they'd seen the lobby was empty.": '正因如此，Atsuki 才会说六分钟前 Suripo 还活着。{time=13:17} 的时候，他们看到大厅空无一人。',
        "...Oh! That's not actually right!": '……{w}啊！{w}不对，其实不是这样！',
        'At 13:17, the lobby was empty. That was before they traveled to the future, and somehow, they knew what the time was. They just said that they touched the Sekimeiya in the mechanical room.': '在 {time=13:17}，大厅还是空的。那是在他们穿越到未来之前，而他们不知怎么就知道了当时的时刻。他们刚才说，他们在机械室碰了 Sekimeiya。',
        'At 1:17 p.m., the lobby was empty. That was before they traveled to the future, and somehow, they knew what the time was. They just said that they touched the Sekimeiya in the mechanical room.': '在 {time=13:17}，大厅还是空的。那是在他们穿越到未来之前，而他们不知怎么就知道了当时的时刻。他们刚才说，他们在机械室碰了 Sekimeiya。',
        "Atsuki and Miiya appeared at around 13:37. The key to this is Sai's wristwatch.": 'Atsuki 和 Miiya 大约在 {time=13:37.} 现身。关键就在 Sai 的手表上。',
        "Atsuki and Miiya appeared at around 1:37 p.m. The key to this is Sai's wristwatch.": 'Atsuki 和 Miiya 大约在 {time=13:37.} 现身。关键就在 Sai 的手表上。',
        "Sai just said it's {time=13:23}, but his watch is still behind. The computer isn't on, so he's not going to recognize that. That's what's making Atsuki and Miiya think they've gone to the past again. They think they appeared back at {time=13:23} and that Suripo has just been killed.": 'Sai 刚才说现在是 {time=13:23}，可他的表还是慢的。电脑没开，他也没法察觉。{w}正因为这样，Atsuki 和 Miiya 才以为又回到了过去——他们以为自己回到了 {time=13:23}，而 Suripo 刚刚遇害。',
        "Sai just said it's 13:23, but his watch is still behind. The computer isn't on, so he's not going to recognize that.{w} That's what's making Atsuki and Miiya think they've gone to the past again. They think they appeared back at 13:23 and that Suripo has just been killed.": 'Sai 刚才说现在是 {time=13:23}，可他的表还是慢的。电脑没开，他也没法察觉。{w}正因为这样，Atsuki 和 Miiya 才以为又回到了过去——他们以为自己回到了 {time=13:23}，而 Suripo 刚刚遇害。',
        "Sai just said it's 13:23, but his watch is still behind. The computer isn't on, so he's not going to recognize that. That's what's making Atsuki and Miiya think they've gone to the past again. They think they appeared back at 13:23 and that Suripo has just been killed.": 'Sai 刚才说现在是 {time=13:23}，可他的表还是慢的。电脑没开，他也没法察觉。{w}正因为这样，Atsuki 和 Miiya 才以为又回到了过去——他们以为自己回到了 {time=13:23}，而 Suripo 刚刚遇害。',
        "Sai just said it's 1:23 p.m., but his watch is still behind. The computer isn't on, so he's not going to recognize that.{w} That's what's making Atsuki and Miiya think they've gone to the past again. They think they appeared back at 1:23 p.m. and that Suripo has just been killed.": 'Sai 刚才说现在是 {time=13:23}，可他的表还是慢的。电脑没开，他也没法察觉。{w}正因为这样，Atsuki 和 Miiya 才以为又回到了过去——他们以为自己回到了 {time=13:23}，而 Suripo 刚刚遇害。',
        "Sai just said it's 1:23 p.m., but his watch is still behind. The computer isn't on, so he's not going to recognize that. That's what's making Atsuki and Miiya think they've gone to the past again. They think they appeared back at 1:23 p.m. and that Suripo has just been killed.": 'Sai 刚才说现在是 {time=13:23}，可他的表还是慢的。电脑没开，他也没法察觉。{w}正因为这样，Atsuki 和 Miiya 才以为又回到了过去——他们以为自己回到了 {time=13:23}，而 Suripo 刚刚遇害。',
        "If it's neither of those, there's still an answer with the Sekimeiya. This policeman could've come from the future if he touched the Sekimeiya after 21:00, and Naomi could've left the tower by going far to the past. We found the Seki— ...where it is now.": '如果这两者都不是，那还可以用 Sekimeiya 来解释。要是这名警察在 {time=21} 之后碰过 Sekimeiya，他可能是从未来来的；Naomi 也可能穿越到遥远的过去，就此离开了这座塔。我们在阁楼找到了 Sekimeiya，如今却不知道它在哪儿。',
        "If it's neither of those, there's still an answer with the Sekimeiya. This policeman could've come from the future if he touched the Sekimeiya after 9 p.m., and Naomi could've left the tower by going far to the past. We found the Seki— ...where it is now.": '如果这两者都不是，那还可以用 Sekimeiya 来解释。要是这名警察在 {time=21} 之后碰过 Sekimeiya，他可能是从未来来的；Naomi 也可能穿越到遥远的过去，就此离开了这座塔。我们在阁楼找到了 Sekimeiya，如今却不知道它在哪儿。',
        'I could hear cabinets being opened. Then, footsteps came toward me. The doorknob shook slightly, and the door slowly opened.': '我听见展示柜一个接一个打开，接着脚步声朝我这边来了。{w}门把手轻轻一晃，门缓缓开了。',
        'Wh-What!? Who are you!? Are you... me?': '什、什么！？你是谁！？{w=0.7}你是……我？',
        "...He nodded. It was the same thing I would've done.": '……{w}他点了点头。换成我也会这么做。',
        "Right, the third Sekimeiya's here. I'd forgotten that it was brought here before Erina and Isla came to this room. This is the cabinet where my past self will see it. That means that the person who left this room was the Atsuki from this world.": '对了，第三个 Sekimeiya 就在这儿。我忘了它是在 Erina 和 Isla 来这个房间之前就被搬过来的。{w}过去的我会在这个展示柜里看到它。也就是说，离开这个房间的人，是这个世界的 Atsuki。',
        "I'd been able to camouflage myself in addition to something else. If I hadn't been there, the Sekimeiya would've been found, but I could prevent that.": '除了另一件事，我还成功隐藏了自己的行踪。{w}如果我不在场，Sekimeiya 就会被人发现，而我能阻止这件事发生。',
        'This is the Future Sekimeiya. When I was in the other crystal room, I heard someone here. After killing Suripo, this is where his killer left the Future Sekimeiya.': '这是未来Sekimeiya。{w}我在另一间水晶展室时，听见这边有人。杀了 Suripo 之后，凶手就把未来Sekimeiya 留在了这里。',
        "But I'd been able to see that she was suffering too. The world we were in wasn't yet what it could be. I dug my fingernails into my palm, telling myself that the result would be worth everything.": '可我也看得出来，她同样在痛苦。我们所处的世界，还不是它应有的样子。{w} 我把指甲掐进掌心，告诉自己，只要结果如愿，一切就都值得。',
        "...I don't really expect Naomi to be in these, but it all gets weirder every time we move on. Could a secret place that Katei doesn't know about exist...? There's no way, right? If the answer is somehow a hidden spot, he must've made use of it as well.": '……我其实并不指望 Naomi 会藏在这些地方，可我们每往前走一步，事情就越是古怪。会不会有一处连 Katei 都不知道的秘密地点……？{w} 这不可能吧？如果答案真是某处隐蔽的地点，那他没道理不利用。',
        "No recent footprints... It'll be fine if you stay here. If I don't find anyone, I'm gonna be pretty confused.": '最近没有脚印……{w} 你留在这儿就好。要是我连一个人都找不到，可就真搞不懂了。',
        "I had to leave. The real Atsuki would soon reappear. But it was hard to turn around. Miiya was right there in front of me—a friend who I'd thought I'd never see again, and who I might have been looking at for the very last time.": '我必须离开。很快，真正的我就要回来了。{w} 可要我转身走开，实在太难了。Miiya 就站在我面前——这个我以为再也见不到的朋友，也许这就是我最后一次看她了。',
        "It happened even sooner than I recalled. Evidently discontent with my search, he walked from room to room. He didn't care about the third Sekimeiya; he'd been the one to leave it there. When he came to hallway B, I was already in a room in hallway A.": '一切来得比我记忆中的更早。他显然对我先前那番搜寻并不满意，一间一间地走了过去。{w}他并不在意第三个 Sekimeiya——把它留在那里的正是他自己。等他来到 B走廊时，我已经待在 A走廊的一间房里了。',
        'I just had to wait. Sai would find the Future Sekimeiya and bring it to the event room. Then, the others would find the Past Sekimeiya and walk to the event room.': '我只需要等着。{w}Sai 会找到未来Sekimeiya，把它带到活动室。随后，其他人会找到过去Sekimeiya，走进活动室。',
        'Two people waited in the lobby. 9:00 was approaching.': '大厅里有两个人等着。快到 {time=9:00} 了。',
        'Two people waited in the lobby. 9:00 a.m. was approaching.': '大厅里有两个人等着。快到 {time=9:00} 了。',
        "At that point, you may have realized something was wrong. Shiroya wasn't there; Miiya was occupying her place. However, her name was spoken before the doors opened.": '那时，你或许已经察觉到有什么不对。Shiroya 并不在那里，占据她位置的是 Miiya。{w}然而，在门打开之前，有人叫出了她的名字。',
        "Miiya was there with her own purse, which contained three tickets. When she stretched, one fell out, meaning that her purse hadn't been closed. In world B, when Shiroya opened her purse, she unzipped it—the tickets couldn't have fallen from her purse, as it was closed since long before 9:00.": 'Miiya 也在场，她的包里装着三张票。她一活动身体，就有一张掉了出来，说明她的包当时没合上。而在 B 世界，Shiroya 打开包时是先拉开拉链的——票不可能从她的包里掉出来，因为那只包早在 {time=9.} 之前就一直合着。',
        "Miiya was there with her own purse, which contained three tickets. When she stretched, one fell out, meaning that her purse hadn't been closed. In world B, when Shiroya opened her purse, she unzipped it—the tickets couldn't have fallen from her purse, as it was closed since long before 9 a.m.": 'Miiya 也在场，她的包里装着三张票。她一活动身体，就有一张掉了出来，说明她的包当时没合上。而在 B 世界，Shiroya 打开包时是先拉开拉链的——票不可能从她的包里掉出来，因为那只包早在 {time=9.} 之前就一直合着。',
        "At that point, Katei had traveled to the past one time. Upon appearing, he hadn't realized that the keyring Naomi had left behind suddenly appeared in his pocket. Then, when he came across it, he put it inside. In that way, he came into possession of two copies.": '那时，Katei 已经穿越到过去一次。他出现时，没有察觉 Naomi 遗落的那串钥匙忽然出现在自己口袋里。{w}后来他偶然摸到它，便把它收了起来。就这样，他手上有了两串。',
        "Before they got there, he decided to test if something else Katei had said was invalid too. On the sixth floor, he attempted to call the elevator, which should've been disabled. They waited, but it never came.": '到达那里之前，他决定再验证 Katei 的另一句话是否同样站不住脚。在六楼，他试着呼叫本该被停用的电梯。{w}他们等了许久，电梯始终没有上来。',
        "At the same time, the Sekimeiya had disappeared from the cabinet. From their perspective, it had been brought to the attic. However, Sai knew the truth. Just like in worlds A and B, he had quickly hidden the fake Sekimeiya when everyone had split up, so the one they'd retrieved from the attic was different.": '与此同时，展示柜里的 Sekimeiya 不见了。大家以为它被搬到了阁楼。{w}可 Sai 知道真相。和在 A世界、B世界一样，他在众人分头行动时迅速藏起了赝品 Sekimeiya，所以他们从阁楼取回的那一个，已经换成了别的东西。',
        "Atsuki appeared in the attic, which was locked. The elevator had been left open on the crystal floor, so he couldn't leave through it either. However, Sai appeared on the crystal floor since his group had left the attic earlier. He realized the elevator was open and allowed Atsuki to leave.": 'Atsuki 出现在上了锁的阁楼里。电梯被留在水晶层，门还开着，所以他也无法借电梯离开。{w}而 Sai 则出现在水晶层，因为他的同伴们早些时候已经离开了阁楼。他发现电梯是开着的，便让 Atsuki 得以脱身。',
        "When they met, they thought they'd gone minutes to the past, although neither of them spoke about it. Atsuki recalled Sai had gone missing, so finding him in the past wasn't strange. His misinterpretation arose due to Sai's watch, which had ended up minutes behind. When they returned to the others, they saw that everyone was in the security room.": '两人相遇时，都以为自己回到了几分钟前，尽管谁也没有说出口。Atsuki 记得 Sai 曾经失踪，所以在过去遇见他并不奇怪。{w}他之所以判断错误，是因为 Sai 的手表慢了整整几分钟。等他们回到其他人身边，才发现众人都在监控室里。',
        'Indeed, your choice made Miiya become Shiroya. The world changed drastically. The butterfly effect amplifies even a single unwitting change.': '的确，正是你的选择让 Miiya 变成了 Shiroya。{w} 世界因此发生了剧变。蝴蝶效应会把哪怕一处无心造成的改变无限放大。',
        '"Six pairs of eyes saw the identical scene." Exactly, it was Katei\'s absence. The storeroom\'s door hadn\'t been locked, so he\'d been able to leave before everyone awakened. In that world, nobody had told the group about keeping the Sekimeiya cold.': '「六双眼睛看到了同一幕景象。」{w} 没错，问题就出在 Katei 不在场。储藏室的门没有上锁，他才能在众人醒来前离开。那个世界里，没人告诉过他们得让 Sekimeiya 保持低温。',
        '"Six pairs of eyes saw the identical scene." It was Katei\'s absence. The storeroom\'s door hadn\'t been locked, so he\'d been able to leave before everyone awakened. In that world, nobody had told the group about keeping the Sekimeiya cold.': '「六双眼睛看到了同一幕景象。」{w} 问题正是 Katei 不在场。储藏室的门没有上锁，他才能在众人醒来前离开。那个世界里，没人告诉过他们得让 Sekimeiya 保持低温。',
        'In reality, Atsuki and Miiya brought everyone to the crystal floor in an attempt to find Sai. Before he was seen, the Past Sekimeiya was found in room B6. Sai was in the event room, and he suddenly heard people approaching. Hoping it would let him escape, he touched the Future Sekimeiya.': '实际上，Atsuki 和 Miiya 为了找 Sai，把大家带到了水晶层。还没人看见他，过去Sekimeiya 就已经在水晶展室 B6 被发现了。{w} 当时 Sai 正在活动室，忽然听见有人靠近。他指望靠这个脱身，便碰了未来Sekimeiya。',
        'Atsuki and Miiya brought everyone to the crystal floor in an attempt to find him. Before he was seen, the Past Sekimeiya was found in room B6. Sai was in the event room, and he suddenly heard people approaching. Hoping it would let him escape, he touched the Future Sekimeiya.': 'Atsuki 和 Miiya 为了找他，把大家带到了水晶层。还没人看见他，过去Sekimeiya 就已经在水晶展室 B6 被发现了。{w} Sai 当时在活动室，忽然听见有人靠近。他指望靠这个脱身，便碰了未来Sekimeiya。',
        'The panel to call the elevator was gone. ...All of them were. They had been ripped off on every floor.': '呼叫电梯的面板不见了。{w} ……所有面板都不见了，每一层的都被拆掉了。',
        "He'd left the key inserted in the door because he knew what had happened with the elevator: it was in the attic despite the panel having vanished. Inside, he'd found that world's attic key. He could keep everyone from entering the highest floor by locking the door in. He left it by bringing the elevator to the sixth floor; he could keep it there as a hidden way up. Since he had his set of keys, he could always access the attic through the elevator he'd prepared.": '他把钥匙插在门上没有拔走，因为他知道电梯出了什么状况：面板明明已经消失，电梯却仍停在阁楼。{w} 在阁楼里，他找到了那个世界的阁楼钥匙。只要把门反锁，就能让众人无法进入顶层。{w} 他离开时把电梯叫到六楼停住，留作一条隐藏的上楼通道。由于他带着自己的那串钥匙，他随时都能通过准备好的电梯进入阁楼。',
        'But... it was found when Atsuki attempted to open it. Inside, there were the bodies of Naomi C and Shiroya A.': '可是……Atsuki 试着打开阁楼时，秘密还是暴露了。{w} 里面躺着 Naomi C 和 Shiroya A 的尸体。',
        "Everyone saw Erina's body atop a pool of blood. Someone had just killed her, and Atsuki had heard her words before dying. ...She had confronted who she'd thought was the killer. However, it quickly became clear that nobody could've easily committed the crime. Everyone stated what they'd been doing.": '所有人都看见了躺在血泊中的 Erina 的尸体。有人刚刚杀了她，而 Atsuki 死前听到过她说的话。……她曾当面质问那个她认定的凶手。{w} 然而，很快就查清，没有人能轻易犯下这桩罪行。众人也纷纷说出了自己当时在做什么。',
        "Atsuki said that after being the first to leave the attic, he'd spent a few minutes on the second floor. He said that at one point, he heard the elevator once. Miiya said that she'd left second and remained on the third floor until Atsuki ran up from below, letting her know what had happened. Sai and Katei claimed to have been above them, and their versions of events seemed to confirm each other. Akaro claimed to have left the attic last when Erina and Isla had still been sitting on the sofa, and that afterward, he'd stayed on the sixth floor alone.": 'Atsuki 说，他最先离开阁楼，之后在二楼待了几分钟。他说其间听到过一次电梯的动静。{w}Miiya 说自己是第二个离开的，一直待在三楼，直到 Atsuki 从楼下跑上来，告诉她出了事。{w}Sai 和 Katei 则说自己当时在他们上面，两人的说法似乎互相印证。{w}Akaro 说自己是最后离开阁楼的，那时 Erina 和 Isla 还坐在沙发上，之后他便独自留在六楼。',
        'The elevator was on the crystal floor. Since the panels hadn\'t been reattached, the "1" button must\'ve been pressed from the attic. It seemed like nobody could\'ve performed a murder simply. The only way to get to the crystal floor after Atsuki\'s departure would\'ve been by riding in the elevator with Erina and Isla. However, if that had happened, they couldn\'t have ended up above Atsuki when he\'d gone to find everyone; nobody had seen them walking up, and the elevator hadn\'t been heard again.': '电梯停在水晶展室。既然面板还没装回去，那个「1」按钮只能是从阁楼按的。{w}看来没人能轻松犯下这桩谋杀。Atsuki 离开之后，想上水晶展室，唯一的办法就是和 Erina、Isla 一同乘电梯。可若是那样，等 Atsuki 去找大家时，他们就不可能出现在他上方——没人看见他们走上去，也没人再听到电梯响过。',
        "You know what happened in that world. The Past Sekimeiya was in room B4 with the world A group. It was in the cabinet where Akaro had put it, and it wasn't activated until he and Isla world switched to world B.": '你知道那个世界发生了什么。过去Sekimeiya 和 A世界那组人一起留在了 B4 房间。{w}它就在 Akaro 放进去的那个展示柜里，直到他和 Isla 一起世界切换到了 B世界，它才被启动。',
        'After that, what happened to it? Shiroya B found it and was able to world switch to world B. Later on, Sai B found it was well and world switched back to world B. Lastly, Atsuki A found it and also world switched to world B.': '那之后它又怎样了？Shiroya B 找到了它，借此世界切换到了 B世界。后来，Sai B 也找到了它，随后世界切换回了 B世界。{w}最后，Atsuki A 找到它，同样世界切换到了 B世界。',
        "Erina had seen the bodies in the lobby. Shiroya had died, but she'd just been in the crystal room. Sai hadn't come back. ...Naomi was dead, and earlier in the day, what had happened with the elevator buttons convinced Erina that the killer was someone they'd been unable to find.": 'Erina 见过大厅里的尸体。Shiroya 死了，可她刚刚还在水晶展室；Sai 没有回来。{w}……Naomi 也死了。而那天早些时候，电梯按钮的事让 Erina 认定，凶手是一个他们始终找不到的人。',
        "She attempted to hide her future knowledge. At that point in time, the elevator hadn't been opened yet; nobody knew it was usable despite the broken panels. And despite the fact that they should have been together recently, Atsuki had told her he'd been alone. ...Did that mean that she'd overwritten her past self?": '她想隐瞒自己知道未来的事。那时电梯还没被人打开过；面板虽已破损，却没人知道它还能用。{w} 而不久前他们本该待在一起，Atsuki 却说自己一直独自一人。……这是不是意味着，她覆盖了过去的自己？',
        "Everyone stated that the elevator had been heard once, so she'd been forced to go along with it. However, if she'd really heard it, she should've known that the elevator had ended up on one of the first two floors.": '所有人都说只听到过一次电梯的声音，她也只能顺着这么说。{w} 可是，倘若她真的听见了，就该知道电梯最后停在了一楼或二楼。',
        "It was the Future Sekimeiya that Miiya had activated. Within the sheet, it gathered energy very quickly. The killer could've been hiding somewhere, so starting with the attic, they searched every floor. Since they had the Sekimeiya, they figured nobody could use it to hide from them.": '那是 Miiya 启动过的未来Sekimeiya。它在床单里蓄能极快。{w} 凶手可能藏在某处，于是他们从阁楼开始，逐层搜查。既然 Sekimeiya 在他们手上，他们便认为谁也没法借它躲过搜查。',
        "...Which was right above the lobby. This is why Shiroya and Atsuki were the only two who didn't world switch—they were in hallway C.": '……而那里就在大厅的正上方。{w} 正因如此，只有 Shiroya 和 Atsuki 两人没有发生世界切换——他们当时在 C走廊。',
        "...I-Is this what you're implying? That it was taken out of the cabinet since the thread is gone and then brought to the attic? Then, at some point, it teleported inside again? I have another idea. Let me take the Sekimeiya. Akaro and Katei, you watch the stairs.": '……你、你是说，线不见了，所以有人把它从展示柜里拿出来带去了阁楼？然后它又在某个时刻传送回柜子里？{w} 我有个别的想法。Sekimeiya 我来拿。Akaro、Katei，你们盯住楼梯。',
        "...It is getting hot—definitely. All right, I'm sure there's someone on this floor. Don't take your eyes off the stairs. I'm not sure we'll find them, though.": '……热起来了——确实是热了。{w}好，这一层肯定有人。盯紧楼梯。不过能不能找到，就不好说了。',
        "They inspected the crystal floor, but nobody was found. Akaro and Isla A had remained in world B. However, there were many things they noticed: Suripo's body had reappeared, and Shiroya's had disappeared. But Naomi was still there—she had returned to her world too, and the blood that had pooled below her had vanished.": '他们查过水晶层，却一个人也没找到。Akaro 和 Isla A 留在了 B世界。{w}不过，他们注意到了不少变化：Suripo 的尸体重新出现，Shiroya 的却不见了。可 Naomi 还在——她也回到了自己的世界，身下积的那摊血却已经消失了。',
        "They'd all returned to world C, but during the brief time they'd been in world B, Naomi's had been the only body in the lobby. She'd been bleeding from her head, so she'd left a large spot of blood on the polished floor. That blood confused many people, but the person most thoroughly deceived by it was Sai B. When he world switched to world A, only Shiroya's corpse was in the lobby, and there was blood next to her. Of course, he naturally assumed that it was hers, not Naomi's. However, when he returned to world B, not only had the pool shrunk, but Shiroya's corpse had disappeared—she was still alive in that world.": '所有人都回到了 C世界。但他们在 B世界待的那一小段时间里，大厅里的尸体只有 Naomi 一具。血从她头部流出，在光洁的地板上留下一大片血迹。{w}那片血迹让不少人产生了误解，被它骗得最彻底的正是 Sai B。{w}当他切换到 A世界时，大厅里只有 Shiroya 的尸体，旁边还有一摊血。他自然以为那是她的血，而不是 Naomi 的。{w}可当他回到 B世界，血迹不仅缩小了，Shiroya 的尸体也不见了——在那个世界里，她还活着。',
        '"Puzzled, he stepped into hallway B. ...What had just happened? Out of nowhere, the Sekimeiya had disappeared. He wondered if he\'d traveled through time. Even though he hadn\'t touched the Sekimeiya, something peculiar had occurred."': '「他满腹疑惑，走进了 B走廊。……刚才究竟发生了什么？{w}Sekimeiya 忽然不见了。{w}他怀疑自己是不是经历了时间穿越。明明没有碰过 Sekimeiya，却出了怪事。」',
        'When Sai world switched from world B to world A, someone world switched from world A to world B. ...Shiroya.': '当 Sai 从 B世界切换到 A世界时，也有人从 A世界切换到了 B世界。{w}……是 Shiroya。',
        '...He was only there momentarily. After allowing Erina and his world B self to return to world B, he took the elevator up.': '……他只在那里停留了片刻。{w} 等 Erina 和 B世界的自己回到 B世界后，他便乘电梯上去了。',
        'After what had happened with Erina, Miiya had learned that traveling to the future with the Sekimeiya was possible. She wanted to be brought to {time=21}, out of the tower. Through the slits in the locker, she activated it, and as Erina had just triggered the world switch, the Future Sekimeiya was powered off. Miiya went more than half an hour to the past and reset the Sekimeiya. When Atsuki B, who had originally hidden it there, later activated it, he only went forty minutes back in time.': '经历了 Erina 那件事后，Miiya 明白用 Sekimeiya 穿越到未来是可行的。她希望自己被送到 {time=21} 的塔外。{w} 她透过储物柜的缝隙启动了它；由于 Erina 刚触发过世界切换，未来Sekimeiya 已处于关闭状态。Miiya 回到了半个多小时前，并重置了 Sekimeiya。后来，原本把它藏在那里的 Atsuki B 再次启动它时，只回到了四十分钟前。',
        'After what had happened with Erina, Miiya had learned that traveling to the future with the Sekimeiya was possible. She wanted to be brought to 21:00, out of the tower.{w} Through the slits in the locker, she activated it, and as Erina had just triggered the world switch, the Future Sekimeiya was powered off. Miiya went more than half an hour to the past and reset the Sekimeiya. When Atsuki B, who had originally hidden it there, later activated it, he only went forty minutes back in time.': '经历了 Erina 那件事后，Miiya 明白用 Sekimeiya 穿越到未来是可行的。她希望自己被送到 {time=21} 的塔外。{w} 她透过储物柜的缝隙启动了它；由于 Erina 刚触发过世界切换，未来Sekimeiya 已处于关闭状态。Miiya 回到了半个多小时前，并重置了 Sekimeiya。后来，原本把它藏在那里的 Atsuki B 再次启动它时，只回到了四十分钟前。',
        'After what had happened with Erina, Miiya had learned that traveling to the future with the Sekimeiya was possible. She wanted to be brought to 21:00, out of the tower. Through the slits in the locker, she activated it, and as Erina had just triggered the world switch, the Future Sekimeiya was powered off. Miiya went more than half an hour to the past and reset the Sekimeiya. When Atsuki B, who had originally hidden it there, later activated it, he only went forty minutes back in time.': '经历了 Erina 那件事后，Miiya 明白用 Sekimeiya 穿越到未来是可行的。她希望自己被送到 {time=21} 的塔外。{w} 她透过储物柜的缝隙启动了它；由于 Erina 刚触发过世界切换，未来Sekimeiya 已处于关闭状态。Miiya 回到了半个多小时前，并重置了 Sekimeiya。后来，原本把它藏在那里的 Atsuki B 再次启动它时，只回到了四十分钟前。',
        'After what had happened with Erina, Miiya had learned that traveling to the future with the Sekimeiya was possible. She wanted to be brought to 9 p.m., out of the tower.{w} Through the slits in the locker, she activated it, and as Erina had just triggered the world switch, the Future Sekimeiya was powered off. Miiya went more than half an hour to the past and reset the Sekimeiya. When Atsuki B, who had originally hidden it there, later activated it, he only went forty minutes back in time.': '经历了 Erina 那件事后，Miiya 明白用 Sekimeiya 穿越到未来是可行的。她希望自己被送到 {time=21} 的塔外。{w} 她透过储物柜的缝隙启动了它；由于 Erina 刚触发过世界切换，未来Sekimeiya 已处于关闭状态。Miiya 回到了半个多小时前，并重置了 Sekimeiya。后来，原本把它藏在那里的 Atsuki B 再次启动它时，只回到了四十分钟前。',
        'After what had happened with Erina, Miiya had learned that traveling to the future with the Sekimeiya was possible. She wanted to be brought to 9 p.m., out of the tower. Through the slits in the locker, she activated it, and as Erina had just triggered the world switch, the Future Sekimeiya was powered off. Miiya went more than half an hour to the past and reset the Sekimeiya. When Atsuki B, who had originally hidden it there, later activated it, he only went forty minutes back in time.': '经历了 Erina 那件事后，Miiya 明白用 Sekimeiya 穿越到未来是可行的。她希望自己被送到 {time=21} 的塔外。{w} 她透过储物柜的缝隙启动了它；由于 Erina 刚触发过世界切换，未来Sekimeiya 已处于关闭状态。Miiya 回到了半个多小时前，并重置了 Sekimeiya。后来，原本把它藏在那里的 Atsuki B 再次启动它时，只回到了四十分钟前。',
        'Miiya appeared in hallway A and immediately fell down. An interesting location. After all, forty minutes after the point she traveled, she was back in world C. She and Atsuki were running to the event room, which was what had made her fall in the past. ...The replicated location was from world C, but it was applied in the past of world B.': 'Miiya 出现在 A走廊，随即摔倒在地。这个地点很有意思。{w} 毕竟，在她穿越到的那个时间点的四十分钟后，她就回到了 C世界。她之所以会在过去摔倒，正是因为那时的她和 Atsuki 正跑向活动室。……那个被复制的地点来自 C世界，却被套用在了 B世界的过去。',
        'At 18:21, Miiya found Katei dead. Following that, she noticed the flickering green lights of the security cameras.': '在 {time=18:21}，Miiya 发现 Katei 已经死了。紧接着，她注意到监控摄像头的绿色指示灯在闪烁。',
        'At 6:21 p.m., Miiya found Katei dead. Following that, she noticed the flickering green lights of the security cameras.': '在 {time=18:21}，Miiya 发现 Katei 已经死了。紧接着，她注意到监控摄像头的绿色指示灯在闪烁。',
        '"It was possible"... She wasn\'t sure if she had gone to the past. She couldn\'t know if she had gone to the future because she had slept for an unknown period of time. The computer\'s clock couldn\'t confirm anything for her.': '「有可能」……她不确定自己是否回到了过去。{w} 她不知道自己睡了多久，也就无法判断是否去了未来。电脑上的时钟同样无法为她证实什么。',
        'Two hours remained until 21:00.': '距离 {time=21.} 还有两个小时。',
        'Two hours remained until 9 p.m.': '距离 {time=21.} 还有两个小时。',
        'They were yells that, in reality, nobody ever heard. At {time=21:04}, the police entered the building. Even though everyone was alive, Suripo was dead on the floor. The officers could hardly believe their eyes while the survivors emerged.': '那些喊声，现实中谁也没有听见。在 {time=21:04}，警察进入了大楼。{w} 尽管所有人都还活着，Suripo 却已倒在地板上，没了气息。幸存者一个个走出来时，警官们几乎不敢相信自己的眼睛。',
        'They were yells that, in reality, nobody ever heard. At 21:04, the police entered the building.{w} Even though everyone was alive, Suripo was dead on the floor. The officers could hardly believe their eyes while the survivors emerged.': '那些喊声，现实中谁也没有听见。在 {time=21:04}，警察进入了大楼。{w} 尽管所有人都还活着，Suripo 却已倒在地板上，没了气息。幸存者一个个走出来时，警官们几乎不敢相信自己的眼睛。',
