        "You'll be able to stay in the third partition on the fourth floor. I know that'll work, because after 2 p.m., you'll go to the sixth floor and leave some kind of indication for me under one of the drawers. The fifth desk from the left, in the first partition.{w} After that, you'll only need to leave momentarily at 3:30 p.m. If you're in the floor 2 and 3 staircase, you'll avoid being inside the range of a travel. The range might actually reach the crystal floor, but if you're in a corner of the building a floor above, you'll avoid it. Just not in the crystal floor staircase since that's where I was at the time.": '你可以待在四楼的第三个隔间。我知道那样行得通：过了 {time=14} 之后，你会去六楼，在某个抽屉底下给我留个记号。也就是第一个隔间里从左数第五张桌子的抽屉。{w}之后，你只要在 {time=15:30.} 暂时离开一下就行。只要你在二楼和三楼之间的楼梯上，就不会落在某次穿越的范围内。范围说不定会延伸到水晶展室，但只要你待在这栋楼比水晶展室高一层的角落，就能避开。只是别待在通往水晶展室的楼梯上——那个时间点我正在那里。',
        "You'll be able to stay in the third partition on the fourth floor. I know that'll work, because after 2 p.m., you'll go to the sixth floor and leave some kind of indication for me under one of the drawers. The fifth desk from the left, in the first partition. After that, you'll only need to leave momentarily at 3:30 p.m. If you're in the floor 2 and 3 staircase, you'll avoid being inside the range of a travel. The range might actually reach the crystal floor, but if you're in a corner of the building a floor above, you'll avoid it. Just not in the crystal floor staircase since that's where I was at the time.": '你可以待在四楼的第三个隔间。我知道那样行得通：过了 {time=14} 之后，你会去六楼，在某个抽屉底下给我留个记号。也就是第一个隔间里从左数第五张桌子的抽屉。{w}之后，你只要在 {time=15:30.} 暂时离开一下就行。只要你在二楼和三楼之间的楼梯上，就不会落在某次穿越的范围内。范围说不定会延伸到水晶展室，但只要你待在这栋楼比水晶展室高一层的角落，就能避开。只是别待在通往水晶展室的楼梯上——那个时间点我正在那里。',
        "No, but you will on January 26th. If I don't take it now, you won't be able to have it. Because, at {time=21} today, the police will find you, and they'll take this key from you if you have it. I need to keep it.": '我不需要，但1月26日的你会需要。如果我现在不把它拿走，你就拿不到它了。{w}因为今天 {time=21} 的时候，警察会找到你，钥匙要是还在你身上，就会被他们收走。我得留着它。',
        "No, but you will on January 26th. If I don't take it now, you won't be able to have it.{w} Because, at 21:00 today, the police will find you, and they'll take this key from you if you have it. I need to keep it.": '我不需要，但1月26日的你会需要。如果我现在不把它拿走，你就拿不到它了。{w}因为今天 {time=21} 的时候，警察会找到你，钥匙要是还在你身上，就会被他们收走。我得留着它。',
        "No, but you will on January 26th. If I don't take it now, you won't be able to have it. Because, at 21:00 today, the police will find you, and they'll take this key from you if you have it. I need to keep it.": '我不需要，但1月26日的你会需要。如果我现在不把它拿走，你就拿不到它了。{w}因为今天 {time=21} 的时候，警察会找到你，钥匙要是还在你身上，就会被他们收走。我得留着它。',
        "No, but you will on January 26th. If I don't take it now, you won't be able to have it.{w} Because, at 9 p.m. today, the police will find you, and they'll take this key from you if you have it. I need to keep it.": '我不需要，但1月26日的你会需要。如果我现在不把它拿走，你就拿不到它了。{w}因为今天 {time=21} 的时候，警察会找到你，钥匙要是还在你身上，就会被他们收走。我得留着它。',
        "No, but you will on January 26th. If I don't take it now, you won't be able to have it. Because, at 9 p.m. today, the police will find you, and they'll take this key from you if you have it. I need to keep it.": '我不需要，但1月26日的你会需要。如果我现在不把它拿走，你就拿不到它了。{w}因为今天 {time=21} 的时候，警察会找到你，钥匙要是还在你身上，就会被他们收走。我得留着它。',
        "...No. I'd tell you why, but there's not enough time right now.": '……不会。{w}原因我可以告诉你，但现在时间不够。',
        "...I should go. I'm sure your future self is currently on the fourth floor. She's been there for hours. You understand everything I said, right?": '……{w}我该走了。未来的你此刻一定就在四楼，已经待了好几个小时。{w}我说的话，你都明白了吧？',
        "You'll appear on the 30th, next to that gem shop. I have to go now, but I guess I'm about to see you again. I'm sorry that there wasn't more time to explain.": '你会在30日出现在那家宝石店旁边。{w}我现在得走了，不过看来我很快就会再见到你。抱歉，没能有更多时间解释。',
        "She hadn't traveled to the past, but she was about to. She stared firmly at the numbers on the screen and gradually moved her hand deeper into the heat. After fourteen more seconds had gone by, she felt the hard touch.": '她还没有穿越回过去，但马上就要。她定定地盯着屏幕上的数字，把手一点点探入那团灼热之中。{w}又过了十四秒，她的指尖触到了坚硬的表面。',
        'She picked herself up by her shoulders and began to retreat. However, a slight sound caused her to spin around, and her heart skipped a beat.': '她抓住另一个自己的肩膀，把她扶起来，随后开始后退。{w}然而，一点轻微的响动让她猛地转过身，心头骤然一紧。',
        'Before she could answer, we heard a noise. It sounded like the elevator had opened.': '她还没来得及回答，我们就听见了响动。{w}听起来像是电梯门开了。',
        'I looked at Shiroya. We were back. It had really worked. That was happening on the third floor, near the staircase. Our past selves had returned too, although they were unaware of it. Their voices hardly reached us, but I could understand them since I knew what they were saying.': '我看向 Shiroya。我们回来了。真的成功了。{w}那声音来自三楼，就在楼梯附近。过去的我们也回来了，只是他们自己并不知道。他们的声音几乎传不到这里，但我听得懂——因为我知道他们在说什么。',
        '...A-Ats— ...not bleedi—': '……A-Ats——{w}……没在流——',
        "...Um, everything did go well, but... I saw Miiya earlier. She came in here once, and I'm pretty sure she saw me. She didn't say anything, though. I almost froze from the shock, but before I could react, she had already left.": '……嗯，事情确实都顺利，只是……{w}我刚才见到 Miiya 了。她进来过一次，而且我敢肯定她看见我了。{w}不过她什么也没说。我吓得几乎僵住，还没等我反应过来，她就已经走了。',
        "She nodded, still puzzled. So, it really had been like that. It had happened as I'd imagined it. I didn't get it. I'd known that she wouldn't be found thanks to the drawing under the drawer. Before seeing it, I hadn't come up with a reason to explain why Miiya hadn't found her, but at that point, I had realized that one wasn't needed. If she simply stayed there, she wouldn't be found. ...I still couldn't understand what had happened.": '她点了点头，仍是一脸困惑。{w}原来，事情真的就是这样。一切正如我想象的那样发生了。{w}我不明白。多亏抽屉下面那张画，我早就知道她不会被找到。在看到它之前，我一直想不出理由解释 Miiya 为什么没找到她；可那一刻我明白，根本不需要什么理由。只要她就那样待在那里，就不会被找到。……可我还是不懂，到底发生了什么。',
        "Yes. She wasn't found at the site of the explosion, but she wasn't harmed. ...Why couldn't she be found?": '嗯。爆炸现场没有找到她，不过她没有受伤。{w}……为什么就是找不到她呢？',
        "You were there? By the way, what keeps happening to your clothes? They're the ones you entered the tower with again, but you didn't have them when you went to the past.": '你在那儿？{w}话说回来，你的衣服到底是怎么回事？又变回你进塔时穿的那身了，可你回到过去的时候穿的并不是这身。',
        "...Ah. That time, right before 21:00, I did think that something about her looked strange. It was so late into the day that I didn't realize it was the complete lack of smoke on her clothes. ...And her pendant is gone too—the thing that tied her with Miiya disappeared when she went to the future.": '……啊。那一次，就在 {time=21} 之前，我确实觉得她哪里有些不对劲。可当时天色已晚，我没意识到那是因为她衣服上一点烟味都没有。……还有她的吊坠也不见了——那个把她和 Miiya 联系在一起的东西，在她去往未来时消失了。',
        "...Ah. That time, right before 9 p.m., I did think that something about her looked strange. It was so late into the day that I didn't realize it was the complete lack of smoke on her clothes. ...And her pendant is gone too—the thing that tied her with Miiya disappeared when she went to the future.": '……啊。那一次，就在 {time=21} 之前，我确实觉得她哪里有些不对劲。可当时天色已晚，我没意识到那是因为她衣服上一点烟味都没有。……还有她的吊坠也不见了——那个把她和 Miiya 联系在一起的东西，在她去往未来时消失了。',
        "It's 19:37.": '现在是 {time=19:37.}',
        "It's 7:37 p.m.": '现在是 {time=19:37.}',
        "Actually... I bet I know why. Only Sai could have used the computer, and not too long ago, he traveled to the past from the event room with Shiroya. That would've disabled his watch, but the next time we saw him, it was working. Every time that happened, he came here to sync it with the computer's time. There was a drawer with a bunch of batteries.": '其实……我想我知道原因。能用那台电脑的只有 Sai，而就在不久前，他还和 Shiroya 一起从活动室穿越回过去。{w}那会让他的手表失效，可我们下一次见到他时，手表又在走了。每次出现这种情况，他都会来这里，把手表与电脑的时间同步。这里有个抽屉，里面放着一堆电池。',
        "That's what I thought. Not completely sure how much sense it makes yet, but there's nothing I can do to fight it. I have the rusty key right here too, by the way, but there's a slight problem. I'll need it on January 5th, and since you gave up yours, you'll also need this one on December 30th.": '我就知道。这其中的道理我还没完全弄明白，但也没法违逆。{w}顺便说一句，生锈的钥匙现在也在我手上，不过有个小问题。一月五日我需要用它，而你既然把自己的那把交了出去，十二月三十日你也得用这一把。',
        "...She didn't seem to know why that was the case.": '……{w}她似乎并不明白为什么会这样。',
        'Yes. As soon as I leave, open the door.': '行。{w} 我一走，你就开门。',
        "It's {time=19:45.} I'll travel to the past soon. ...Sorry, to the future.": '现在是 {time=19:45.} 我很快就要穿越到过去了。{w} ……抱歉，是未来。',
        "It's 19:45. I'll travel to the past soon.{w} ...Sorry, to the future.": '现在是 {time=19:45.} 我很快就要穿越到过去了。{w} ……抱歉，是未来。',
        "It's 19:45. I'll travel to the past soon. ...Sorry, to the future.": '现在是 {time=19:45.} 我很快就要穿越到过去了。{w} ……抱歉，是未来。',
        "It's 7:45 p.m. I'll travel to the past soon.{w} ...Sorry, to the future.": '现在是 {time=19:45.} 我很快就要穿越到过去了。{w} ……抱歉，是未来。',
        "It's 7:45 p.m. I'll travel to the past soon. ...Sorry, to the future.": '现在是 {time=19:45.} 我很快就要穿越到过去了。{w} ……抱歉，是未来。',
        "...Hm... Not quite. Once you leave for the bathroom, they'll search everywhere for you.": '……唔……不太行。{w} 你一去洗手间，他们就会四处找你。',
        "No. If my past self saw me, that'd be a paradox. But there's no simple way out of this. The Future Sekimeiya will be powered off and Sai will stay next to it when it repowers, and the Past Sekimeiya will send us too far to hide us since it'll build up energy until your past self leaves. I doubt touching it twice would work due to the powered-off time.": '不会。如果过去的我看到我，就会形成悖论。{w}但这事没那么容易解决。未来Sekimeiya 会处于断电状态，等它重新通电时，Sai 会守在旁边；过去Sekimeiya 则会一直蓄能，直到过去的你离开，再把我们送到太远的地方，根本没法藏身。考虑到它断电的那段时间，再碰一次恐怕行不通。',
        "But what about at 21:00? The shutter won't move, will it?": '可 {time=21} 的时候呢？卷帘门不会动，对吧？',
        "But what about at 9 p.m.? The shutter won't move, will it?": '可 {time=21} 的时候呢？卷帘门不会动，对吧？',
        "Yes, but before the exit opened, we went to the future. We appeared on January 5th, where the recording occurred. So, if you're out of that range, you'll stay here and be able to leave.": '是，但在出口打开之前，我们去了未来。我们出现在 1 月 5 日，录音就是那天留下的。{w}所以，只要你不在那个范围里，就会留在这里，也就能离开。',
        "Oh... that's what happened. Where will the range be?": '哦……原来是这么回事。{w}那范围会在哪里？',
        "Here. Just before {time=21:05}, Erina is going to activate it. The Future Sekimeiya has yet to be brought here. It won't be a normal travel, though. When she touches it, she'll trigger a chain reaction that will bring us to January 5th. We'll go twenty minutes to the future repeatedly. Akaro will appear a bit later because he traveled directly from today to January 5th after escaping from the bedroom with Sai.": '就在这里。就在 {time=21:05} 之前，Erina 会启动它。那时未来Sekimeiya 还没被带到这里。{w}不过，那不会是一次普通的穿越。她一碰它，就会引发连锁反应，把我们带到 1 月 5 日。我们会一次又一次地向未来跳二十分钟。Akaro 会稍晚出现，因为他是和 Sai 一起逃出卧室后，直接从今天穿越到了 1 月 5 日。',
        "Here. Just before 21:05, Erina is going to activate it. The Future Sekimeiya has yet to be brought here.{w} It won't be a normal travel, though. When she touches it, she'll trigger a chain reaction that will bring us to January 5th. We'll go twenty minutes to the future repeatedly. Akaro will appear a bit later because he traveled directly from today to January 5th after escaping from the bedroom with Sai.": '就在这里。就在 {time=21:05} 之前，Erina 会启动它。那时未来Sekimeiya 还没被带到这里。{w}不过，那不会是一次普通的穿越。她一碰它，就会引发连锁反应，把我们带到 1 月 5 日。我们会一次又一次地向未来跳二十分钟。Akaro 会稍晚出现，因为他是和 Sai 一起逃出卧室后，直接从今天穿越到了 1 月 5 日。',
        "Here. Just before 21:05, Erina is going to activate it. The Future Sekimeiya has yet to be brought here. It won't be a normal travel, though. When she touches it, she'll trigger a chain reaction that will bring us to January 5th. We'll go twenty minutes to the future repeatedly. Akaro will appear a bit later because he traveled directly from today to January 5th after escaping from the bedroom with Sai.": '就在这里。就在 {time=21:05} 之前，Erina 会启动它。那时未来Sekimeiya 还没被带到这里。{w}不过，那不会是一次普通的穿越。她一碰它，就会引发连锁反应，把我们带到 1 月 5 日。我们会一次又一次地向未来跳二十分钟。Akaro 会稍晚出现，因为他是和 Sai 一起逃出卧室后，直接从今天穿越到了 1 月 5 日。',
        "Here. Just before 9:05 p.m., Erina is going to activate it. The Future Sekimeiya has yet to be brought here.{w} It won't be a normal travel, though. When she touches it, she'll trigger a chain reaction that will bring us to January 5th. We'll go twenty minutes to the future repeatedly. Akaro will appear a bit later because he traveled directly from today to January 5th after escaping from the bedroom with Sai.": '就在这里。就在 {time=21:05} 之前，Erina 会启动它。那时未来Sekimeiya 还没被带到这里。{w}不过，那不会是一次普通的穿越。她一碰它，就会引发连锁反应，把我们带到 1 月 5 日。我们会一次又一次地向未来跳二十分钟。Akaro 会稍晚出现，因为他是和 Sai 一起逃出卧室后，直接从今天穿越到了 1 月 5 日。',
        "Here. Just before 9:05 p.m., Erina is going to activate it. The Future Sekimeiya has yet to be brought here. It won't be a normal travel, though. When she touches it, she'll trigger a chain reaction that will bring us to January 5th. We'll go twenty minutes to the future repeatedly. Akaro will appear a bit later because he traveled directly from today to January 5th after escaping from the bedroom with Sai.": '就在这里。就在 {time=21:05} 之前，Erina 会启动它。那时未来Sekimeiya 还没被带到这里。{w}不过，那不会是一次普通的穿越。她一碰它，就会引发连锁反应，把我们带到 1 月 5 日。我们会一次又一次地向未来跳二十分钟。Akaro 会稍晚出现，因为他是和 Sai 一起逃出卧室后，直接从今天穿越到了 1 月 5 日。',
        "...Not being here twenty minutes before it's activated would also avoid it. It won't be so simple, though... Only you will be able to do that.": '……{w}只要在它启动前二十分钟不待在这里，就能避开。{w}不过没那么简单……{w}能做到这一点的，只有你。',
        "The people above us will search for you soon. They'll find you, and then the shutter will open. You can leave this place. I can't do that, though. There's something very important that still has to happen. On January 5th, I'll have to be in the tower in order to appear on November 24th with the Sekimeiya. If I stay here, I'll travel to the future one more time. That's when I'll finally be able to leave.": '楼上那些人很快就会来找你。他们会找到你，然后卷帘门就会打开。你就能离开这里。{w}可我不行。还有一件非常重要的事必须发生。{w}1 月 5 日，我必须待在塔里，才能在 11 月 24 日带着 Sekimeiya 出现。如果我留在这里，就会再向未来穿越一次。到那时，我才能真正离开。',
        "No... there are a few reasons why I can't. The 5th is 21 days away. It's possible that getting out today will prevent me from being in the tower in the future. I don't know what the police will do. If they find any evidence that incriminates me, being here on the 5th might not be possible. I'm sure my parents will keep trying to make me leave with them too. ...Staying here is the only way to guarantee it, and it's what I thought I'd do before I touched the Sekimeiya.": '不行……有几个原因。{w}距离 5 日还有 21 天。今天出去的话，我之后可能就没法待在塔里了。{w}我不知道警方会怎么做。如果他们找到任何对我不利的证据，5 日那天也许就没法待在这里了。我父母肯定也会一直想办法让我跟他们走。……留在这里是唯一能保证的办法，也是我在碰 Sekimeiya 之前就打算做的事。',
        "The cabinet key? If the police found you with it, they would take it, so the only way to get it to the 26th would be by doing the same thing as with the attic's. Did you ever need to unlock the cabinet?": '展示柜钥匙？如果警方发现你带着它，就会收走。要把它带到 26 日，唯一的办法就是像阁楼钥匙那样处理。{w}你之前有需要打开展示柜的时候吗？',
        "You can stay at my house too. At least you'll be with Maxi and Umi. You were on January 5th once already, right? Was the tower not open?": '你也可以住在我家。至少还有 Maxi 和 Umi 陪着你。{w}你已经去过一次 1 月 5 日，对吧？那时塔没有开放吗？',
        "Yeah. They'll go to the attic and come back down. By the way, can I borrow your watch? It'll be useful to have it.": '嗯。他们会去阁楼，然后再下来。{w}对了，能借你的手表用用吗？带着会方便些。',
        "Her shadowy figure slowly faded up the stairs. I recalled the time we'd found her drowsy in room A1 and the words she'd told me in hallway C... They were words I'd hated before, but they had grown to bring me happiness.": '她的身影渐渐隐没在楼梯上。{w}我想起我们在 A1 房间发现她昏昏欲睡时的情形，还有她在 C走廊对我说过的那番话……那些话我从前很讨厌，后来却渐渐给我带来了幸福。',
        "I couldn't see who they were, but it had to be Sai. He seemed to be looking around in the dark. I feared he would find me until his movements slowed down. He kneeled under a table and stopped.": '我看不清来人的脸，但一定是 Sai。他似乎正在黑暗里四下摸索。{w}我生怕他发现我，直到他的动作慢了下来。他在一张桌子下面跪了下来，停住不动了。',
        'I hardly had time to exhale before he was back. There was a glaring difference—the area between his hands was glowing. Once more, he kneeled under the table and ran back up the stairs as soon as he was finished.': '我还没来得及松口气，他就回来了。这次有明显不同——他两手之间正发着光。{w}他又一次在桌下跪下，刚弄完就立刻跑上了楼梯。',
        "...Now, my past self will find the Past Sekimeiya in the security room, and we'll all wait out the last few minutes in the lobby.": '……{w}接下来，过去的我会在监控室找到过去Sekimeiya，然后我们所有人就在大厅里熬过最后这几分钟。',
        'I stared at the glowing numbers on the watch until 21:01 came. At that point, someone began to carefully descend the stairs.': '我一直盯着表上发光的数字，直到 {time=21:01} 来临。就在这时，有人小心翼翼地走下楼梯。',
        'I stared at the glowing numbers on the watch until 9:01 p.m. came. At that point, someone began to carefully descend the stairs.': '我一直盯着表上发光的数字，直到 {time=21:01} 来临。就在这时，有人小心翼翼地走下楼梯。',
        "However, Erina was still there. Her outline had disappeared because the light had moved. The faint ceiling light had turned off, and the Sekimeiya's glow couldn't be seen.": '然而，Erina 还留在原处。消失的是她的轮廓，因为光源移开了。{w}天花板上那盏微弱的灯熄灭了，Sekimeiya 的光也看不见了。',
        "The watch still showed 21:03, but that was far from the real time. I could hear the others shouting above me. The shutter wasn't opening.": '表上仍显示 {time=21:03}，可那离真正的时间还差得远。我能听见头顶上其他人在喊。卷帘门没有打开。',
        "The watch still showed 9:03 p.m., but that was far from the real time. I could hear the others shouting above me. The shutter wasn't opening.": '表上仍显示 {time=21:03}，可那离真正的时间还差得远。我能听见头顶上其他人在喊。卷帘门没有打开。',
        "I can't get out yet. I'll need to have both Sekimeiya after the watch shows 22:30.": '我还出不去。得等到表上的时间过了 {time=22:30.}，并且两个 Sekimeiya 都到手才行。',
        "I can't get out yet. I'll need to have both Sekimeiya after the watch shows 10:30 p.m.": '我还出不去。得等到表上的时间过了 {time=22:30.}，并且两个 Sekimeiya 都到手才行。',
        'I was forcing Shiroya to wait, but I had to stay there for a little while longer. When {time=21:50} came, I approached the stairs.': '我让 Shiroya 干等着，自己却还得在那里多待一会儿。{w}等到 {time=21:50}，我走向楼梯。',
        'I was forcing Shiroya to wait, but I had to stay there for a little while longer.{w} When 21:50 came, I approached the stairs.': '我让 Shiroya 干等着，自己却还得在那里多待一会儿。{w}等到 {time=21:50}，我走向楼梯。',
        'I was forcing Shiroya to wait, but I had to stay there for a little while longer. When 21:50 came, I approached the stairs.': '我让 Shiroya 干等着，自己却还得在那里多待一会儿。{w}等到 {time=21:50}，我走向楼梯。',
        'I was forcing Shiroya to wait, but I had to stay there for a little while longer.{w} When 9:50 p.m. came, I approached the stairs.': '我让 Shiroya 干等着，自己却还得在那里多待一会儿。{w}等到 {time=21:50}，我走向楼梯。',
        'I was forcing Shiroya to wait, but I had to stay there for a little while longer. When 9:50 p.m. came, I approached the stairs.': '我让 Shiroya 干等着，自己却还得在那里多待一会儿。{w}等到 {time=21:50}，我走向楼梯。',
        'I walked to the crystal room the past me had traveled from, B5. After feeling the floor, I realized that the powered-off Past Sekimeiya was there. For the time being, I went to the crystal room at my right and put both inside a temperature regulation cabinet, setting it to where I believed 0 °C was. It seemed the curtains were all still raised.': '我走向过去的我穿越离开的那间水晶展室 B5。伸手一探地板，便发现断电的过去Sekimeiya就在那儿。{w}我暂且走进右边那间水晶展室，把两个都放进带温控的展示柜，把温度调到我估计是 0 °C 的位置。看来所有遮布都仍然卷着。',
        'I kept looking down. It was already past 22:00.': '我一直低着头。时间已经过了 {time=22.}',
        'I kept looking down. It was already past 10 p.m.': '我一直低着头。时间已经过了 {time=22.}',
        "What? No. That's the third one.": '什么？{w}不对。那是第三个。',
        "He went to the mechanical room. Maybe he noticed the Sekimeiya he'd hidden was no longer there, but he didn't say anything. Afterward, he walked back with the others. Akaro was there. Hopefully, the recording of him had been obtained by the police. Erina and Isla were the last two. Their stories had been tragic in different ways. They were together again, but it was possible that Erina would never understand that the Isla she'd entered the tower with was gone.": '他去了机械室。也许他发现自己藏起来的 Sekimeiya 不见了，可他什么也没说。之后，他和其他人一起走了回去。{w}Akaro 也在。但愿警方已经拿到了录有他的那段录音。{w}最后两个是 Erina 和 Isla。她们两人的遭遇都很悲惨，只是方式不同。她们又在一起了，但 Erina 也许永远无法明白，当初和她一起走进这座塔的那个 Isla 已经不在了。',
        'Now that I think about it, it was when I traveled to 21:00 that my hand injury disappeared. Even though I only went 45 minutes to the past, it took me many days to reach the proportional future.': '说起来，我的手伤是在我穿越到 {time=21:00} 的时候消失的。虽然我只回到了 45 分钟前，可要到达对应的未来时间点，却花了我好几天。',
        'Now that I think about it, it was when I traveled to 9:00 p.m. that my hand injury disappeared. Even though I only went 45 minutes to the past, it took me many days to reach the proportional future.': '说起来，我的手伤是在我穿越到 {time=21:00} 的时候消失的。虽然我只回到了 45 分钟前，可要到达对应的未来时间点，却花了我好几天。',
        "Right now, I have Shiroya's watch and the rusty key. When I was briefly at {time=21:00}, I might not have realized that. However, after Shiroya made me travel to the 15th, there's no way I had them. I suppose that makes sense since that location was based on a point much farther into the future. That's still a little strange, though, because Shiroya did have the rusty key.": '现在，我手里有 Shiroya 的表和生锈的钥匙。我短暂停留在 {time=21:00} 的时候，也许还没意识到这一点。可是，在 Shiroya 让我穿越到 15 日之后，我绝不可能带着这两样东西。{w}想想也合理，毕竟那个位置对应的，是未来更远处的一个时间点。不过还是有点奇怪——毕竟当时 Shiroya 确实拿着生锈的钥匙。',
